"passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME5","text":"Der Gegensatz von Abhängigkeit und Unabhängigkeit zerfällt zugunsten verschiedener Formen der Bindung, Verlagerung, Dämpfung und Realitätsdistanz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME6","text":"Neurose, Intoxikation, Psychose und Religion werden auf einem Kontinuum kompensatorischer Reaktionen auf gescheiterte Glücksanpassung angeordnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7","text":"Religion wird von einer privilegierten Wahrheits- und Heilsordnung zu einer kollektiv standardisierten psychischen Technik mit begrenzter Entlastungsleistung umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Untersucht werden menschliche Wege zur Lustgewinnung und Leidabwehr sowie die Stellung der Religion unter diesen Wegen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die Verfahren beruhen auf Lustprinzip, Realitätsprinzip, organismischer Empfindung, Triebregulierung, Libidoverschiebung und Objektbindung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Universale Lebensregeln werden durch eine vergleichende Strategie individueller Anpassung, Verteilung und Risikobegrenzung ersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Die vorausgesetzte Realität ist nicht teleologisch auf menschliches Glück eingerichtet; Lust ist kontrastabhängig und episodisch, Leiden dagegen dauerhaft möglich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von der Religionsfrage über die Glücksökonomie zur Diagnose religiöser Uniformierung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben der chemische Mechanismus der Intoxikation, die metapsychologische Qualität sublimierter Lust und die Herkunft der Schönheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist kohärent, sofern alle Lebensziele als Varianten von Lustgewinnung und Leidvermeidung rekonstruierbar sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Generativität liegt in der Verbindung von Lust-Leid-Asymmetrie, dreifacher Leidensquelle und kostenförmiger Pluralität der Abwehrtechniken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT5","text":"Der Übergang vom zurückgewiesenen objektiven Lebenszweck zum aus Verhalten erschlossenen subjektiven Lebensziel beruht auf einer nicht vollständig formalisierten Bedeutungsverschiebung von Zweck.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT6","text":"Die Reduktion allen Leidens auf Empfindung lässt organismische Eingriffe prinzipiell vorrangig erscheinen, ohne das fortgesetzte Gewicht äußerer und sozialer Kausalität vollständig zu erklären.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT7","text":"Die Religion wird zugleich als Massenwahn und als Schutz vor individueller Neurose bestimmt; die Grenze zwischen kollektiv normalisierter und individueller Pathologie bleibt funktional, nicht nosologisch geklärt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT8","text":"Die Zurückweisung allgemeiner Glücksrezepte steht in Spannung zur allgemeinen Empfehlung von Anpassung, Diversifikation und Vermeidung extremer Festlegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT9","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Argumentbewegung, hängt aber bei der Totalisierung des Lustprinzips und der Klassifikation von Religion als Massenwahn von komprimierten diagnostischen Setzungen ab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171344350513Z_53178f35","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter II","source_sha256":"2dc2f2c6467a1619459066d9b712c8d9d796d1132af973c2f8c5ea34d365abd3","sha256":"1f22d848f101e6223a0587770c8f876cb6cb448bab088ca0f8925e10475c7d0c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:13:44.353466+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumentative Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS1","text":"The text determines the position of religion among the psychical means through which human beings endure a life experienced as unbearable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS2","text":"The unanswerable question of a predetermined purpose of life is replaced by the question of what purpose human behaviour actually reveals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS3","text":"Human behaviour is reconstructed from the dual aim of happiness: the gain of pleasure and the avoidance of suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS4","text":"The pleasure principle establishes this aim of happiness, while psychical constitution, the body, the external world, and social relations prevent its complete realization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","text":"The argument proceeds diagnostically, comparatively, and in terms of libido economy, by ordering techniques of life according to point of intervention, achievement, and cost.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS6","text":"Every technique of life reduces certain risks of suffering, but produces losses of enjoyment, new dependencies, distance from reality, or particular vulnerabilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS7","text":"Attainable happiness is therefore determined as a contingent result of individual libido economy, psychical constitution, and adaptation to the environment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS8","text":"The movement ends with the diagnosis that religion replaces this individual selection with a uniform infantile and delusional solution, without being able to fulfil its promise of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A1","text":"The religion of the common man combines an explanation of the world with the promise of paternal providence and otherworldly compensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A2","text":"The notion of a predetermined purpose of life stands or falls with the religious system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A3","text":"Following the disappearance of a tenable teleology, the purpose of human life must be inferred from behaviour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A4","text":"Human behaviour manifests a striving for happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A5","text":"The striving for happiness divides into the absence of pain and the attainment of intense pleasure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A6","text":"The pleasure principle sets the programme of happiness for the psychical apparatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A7","text":"Intense pleasure presupposes contrast and the sudden satisfaction of accumulated needs and therefore remains episodic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","text":"The text posits the body, the external world, and human relations as three fundamentally non-eliminable sources of suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","text":"The pressure of the external world transforms the pleasure principle into the more modest reality principle and shifts priority from the gain of pleasure to the avoidance of suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A10","text":"Suffering becomes psychically effective only as an organically conditioned sensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","text":"The psychical apparatus enables instinctual regulation, displacement of libido, sublimation, phantasy satisfaction, and object-cathexis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","text":"Every technique of acquiring happiness alters the distribution of pleasure, suffering, reality-binding, and dependency, without optimizing all four magnitudes simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","text":"The usefulness of a technique of life depends on environmental conditions, the power to effect change, and the psychical constitution of the individual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14","text":"Exclusive attachment to one technique of life intensifies its specific inadequacy, whereas distribution may reduce risk.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","text":"No path to attainable happiness is universally valid or assured of success.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16","text":"The unfulfillable programme of happiness remains effective in action and cannot be abandoned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","text":"Religion prevents individual selection and adaptation by combining devaluation of life, distortion of reality, intellectual intimidation, infantilism, and mass delusion into a unified technique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18","text":"The limited success of religion consists in replacing individual neurosis with collective fixation, not in fulfilling its promise of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX1","text":"The deepest sources of religious feeling are not the immediate object of investigation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX2","text":"Within the framework of inquiry, an impersonal abstract principle does not count as religion in the proper sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX3","text":"A predetermined purpose of life is not a fact secured independently of religion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX4","text":"Enduring intense happiness is neither consonant with psychical constitution nor provided for in the order of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX5","text":"Unrestricted instinctual satisfaction is not a sustainably viable way of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX6","text":"An illusion is not psychically ineffective merely because it deviates from reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX7","text":"No single technique simultaneously offers complete protection against suffering, intense pleasure, general accessibility, and secure duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX8","text":"The wish-conforming replacement of reality is not a successful mastery of reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX9","text":"Collective sharing does not annul the delusional character of a distortion of reality and does not make religion a secure path to happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D1","text":"The text replaces objective teleology with a functional reconstruction of the human aim that is actually effective.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D2","text":"The avoidance of suffering receives structural priority over the gain of pleasure because suffering is more readily available and intense pleasure only episodic.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D3","text":"Techniques of life can be classified according to their site of intervention as modifications of the environment, relations, organism, instincts, libido, or relation to reality.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D4","text":"Mastery of instincts reduces the painfulness of frustration, but at the same time lowers the intensity of possible satisfaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5","text":"Independence from the external world is purchased through displacement or attenuation of dependency, not through its abolition.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D6","text":"Scientific-technical activity and work bind one to reality and community, whereas intoxication, phantasy, and withdrawal seek satisfaction through reduced dependence on reality.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D7","text":"Love approaches the positive aim of happiness more closely than resigned protective techniques, but increases vulnerability through the loss of object and love.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D8","text":"Practical wisdom of life becomes the contingent distribution of cathexes rather than obedience to a universal recipe for happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D9","text":"If the adaptation of libido economy fails, neurosis, chronic intoxication, or psychosis may arise as remaining substitute techniques.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:D10","text":"Following its failure, the religious promise ends not in the securing of happiness, but in the pleasure and consolation function of unconditional submission.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD1","text":"The human economy of happiness is temporally asymmetrical: pleasure culminates at particular moments, while suffering remains present as a permanent possibility.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD2","text":"Asceticism, work, art, love, intoxication, neurosis, psychosis, and religion appear as differently organized responses of the same libido economy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3","text":"Psychical autonomy denotes not freedom from dependency, but the capacity to redistribute dependencies among body, world, phantasy, and objects.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD4","text":"Collective mastery of nature and religious mass delusion constitute opposed collectivizations of the defence against suffering: reality is either altered or distorted in conformity with wishes.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD5","text":"The universality of religious prescription contradicts the constitutional and situational individuality of every viable technique of happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD6","text":"Attainable happiness is not a stable final state, but a precarious and revisable achievement of adaptation without any guarantee of success.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX1","text":"The system presupposes that the world is neither arranged for human happiness nor legitimized by an objective human purpose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a sovereign subject capable of arbitrarily choosing or reshaping its instincts, its constitution, and its environment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the general accessibility and functional equivalence of all techniques of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX4","text":"Within the system, collective assent, historical authority, and psychical efficacy cannot establish the truth of religious ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX5","text":"Independent life aims outside the economy of pleasure and suffering receive no irreducible status, but are recoded as forms of satisfaction, protection, or substitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX1","text":"The terminally barred possibility is an enduring reconciliation of the pleasure principle, psychical constitution, and reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX2","text":"Unavailable is a technique that simultaneously guarantees intense pleasure, complete protection against suffering, preservation of reality, general accessibility, and duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX3","text":"The system lacks a positive criterion outside libido economy according to which competing forms of life could be ordered independently of their value for satisfaction and protection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX4","text":"The religiously promised guarantee remains structurally absent; after failure, only submission to an inscrutable decree remains in its place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS1","text":"Paternal providence and otherworldly compensation → religious purposiveness → functional question of religion as a means of alleviation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS2","text":"Rejection of predetermined teleology → observation of human behaviour → happiness as the actual aim of life.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS3","text":"Aim of happiness → gain of pleasure plus avoidance of suffering → pleasure principle as psychical generator.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS4","text":"Episodic pleasure plus threefold source of suffering → unfulfillability of the programme of happiness → transformation into the reality principle.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS5","text":"Reality principle → interventions in world, organism, instincts, libido, and object relations → partial relief plus specific cost.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS6","text":"Varying environment and constitution plus incomplete techniques → individual selection → diversification without guarantee of success.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:FGS7","text":"Religious uniformization → infantile fixation and mass delusion → limited neurotic relief → failure of the promise → submission.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AF1","text":"Religious answer to the purpose of life → rejection of teleology → reconstruction of the behavioural aim → pleasure principle → structural unfulfillability → priority of defence against suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:AF2","text":"Comparison of techniques of life → demonstration of their costs → individualization of libido economy → rejection of universal recipes → diagnosis of religion as a uniform technique of delusion and submission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME1","text":"The purpose of life is remapped from a cosmic determination to a psychical function inferred from behaviour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME2","text":"Happiness is reclassified from a lasting state to an asymmetrical relation between episodic pleasure and continuous danger of suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME3","text":"Suffering is mapped both according to external sources and according to its organic mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME4","text":"Asceticism, technology, work, art, intoxication, love, and religion become visible as comparable interventions in the same psychical economy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME5","text":"The opposition between dependency and independence disintegrates in favour of different forms of attachment, displacement, attenuation, and distance from reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME6","text":"Neurosis, intoxication, psychosis, and religion are arranged on a continuum of compensatory reactions to failed adaptation to happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7","text":"Religion is reclassified from a privileged order of truth and salvation to a collectively standardized psychical technique with limited capacity for relief.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Human paths to the gain of pleasure and defence against suffering, as well as the position of religion among these paths, are examined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT2","text":"Structural — The procedures are based on the pleasure principle, reality principle, organic sensation, instinctual regulation, displacement of libido, and object attachment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Universal rules of life are replaced by a comparative strategy of individual adaptation, distribution, and limitation of risk.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The presupposed reality is not teleologically arranged for human happiness; pleasure depends on contrast and is episodic, whereas suffering remains permanently possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the question of religion through the economy of happiness to the diagnosis of religious uniformization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT2","text":"The chemical mechanism of intoxication, the metapsychological quality of sublimated pleasure, and the origin of beauty remain underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT3","text":"The structure is coherent insofar as all aims of life can be reconstructed as variants of the gain of pleasure and the avoidance of suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT4","text":"The strongest generativity lies in the connection between pleasure-suffering asymmetry, the threefold source of suffering, and the cost-shaped plurality of techniques of defence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT5","text":"The transition from the rejected objective purpose of life to the subjective aim of life inferred from behaviour rests on a not fully formalized shift in the meaning of purpose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT6","text":"The reduction of all suffering to sensation makes organic interventions appear in principle primary, without fully explaining the continuing weight of external and social causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT7","text":"Religion is determined both as mass delusion and as protection against individual neurosis; the boundary between collectively normalized and individual pathology remains clarified functionally, not nosologically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT8","text":"The rejection of general recipes for happiness stands in tension with the general recommendation of adaptation, diversification, and avoidance of extreme fixation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the argument, but in the totalization of the pleasure principle and the classification of religion as mass delusion it depends on compressed diagnostic posits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_2:P0097","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_2@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KA_2:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 02","title":"Chapter II","context":"Chapter 02","original_title":"Kapitel II","original_context":"Chapter 02"},"original_title":"Kapitel II","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3","layer":"CH","title":"Chapter III","order":3,"parents":["RAW_R2TV_KA_3"],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_3@R001","sha256":"009c58d25162b33ebeb6a963d01023fe0660106f487477d18d125f985cdf9330","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS1","text":"Die Sonderstellung der sozialen Leidensquelle bildet das Problem, weil Menschen selbstgeschaffene Einrichtungen nicht wie Naturübermacht und Körperverfall als unvermeidlich anerkennen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2","text":"Kultur ist zugleich das Schutzsystem gegen Leiden und durch ihre Versagungen eine Quelle neuen Leidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3","text":"Das Argument verfährt diagnostisch, genealogisch und psychoanalytisch-rekonstruktiv.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS4","text":"Langdauernde Unzufriedenheit wird durch religiöse Entwertung des Lebens, Projektionen primitiven Glücks, Neurosendiagnostik und technische Enttäuschung zur Kulturfeindlichkeit verdichtet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS5","text":"Weder technische Fortschritte noch Vergleiche mit früheren Lebensformen entscheiden den Glückswert der Kultur, weil Naturbeherrschung nicht hinreicht und Glück subjektiv bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS6","text":"Die Untersuchung ersetzt das globale Glücksurteil durch eine funktionale Rekonstruktion der Kultur als Naturschutz, Beziehungsregelung und Pflege nützlicher wie nichtnützlicher Leistungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS7","text":"Soziale Kultur entsteht durch die Ersetzung individueller Gewalt durch Gemeinschaftsmacht, erzeugt Recht und Gerechtigkeit und verschärft zugleich den Konflikt mit individueller Freiheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS8","text":"Die abschließende Neurahmung bestimmt Kulturentwicklung als Bearbeitung menschlicher Triebe durch Charakterbildung, Sublimierung und Versagung und öffnet damit die Frage nach Ursprung, Verlauf und Kompensation dieses Prozesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","text":"Menschliches Leiden entspringt der Übermacht der Natur, der Hinfälligkeit des Körpers und der Unzulänglichkeit sozialer Einrichtungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A2","text":"Natur und Körper bleiben grundsätzlich unvollständig beherrschbar, obwohl einzelne Leiden aufgehoben oder gemildert werden können.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A3","text":"Hinter der Unzulänglichkeit sozialer Einrichtungen steht der Verdacht einer Grenze in der psychischen Beschaffenheit des Menschen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","text":"Kultur umfasst die Leistungen und Einrichtungen zum Schutz gegen die Natur und zur Regelung menschlicher Beziehungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","text":"Kultur vermindert Leiden durch Schutz und erzeugt Leiden durch die Einschränkung von Befriedigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A6","text":"Naturbeherrschung ist weder die einzige Bedingung menschlichen Glücks noch das einzige Ziel der Kultur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","text":"Glück ist grundsätzlich subjektiv und von der jeweiligen psychischen Empfindlichkeit abhängig.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8","text":"Kulturelle Wertung wird durch Nutzen nicht erschöpft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A9","text":"Menschliches Zusammenleben wird erst durch eine Gemeinschaftsmacht ermöglicht, die jedem Einzelnen überlegen ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10","text":"Gerechtigkeit verlangt, dass die gesetzte Rechtsordnung nicht zugunsten Einzelner durchbrochen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","text":"Individuelle Freiheit ist kein Kulturgut und wird durch Kultur eingeschränkt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A12","text":"Der fortbestehende Freiheitsdrang kann sich entweder gegen Ungerechtigkeit oder gegen Kultur als solche richten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13","text":"Kulturentwicklung ist ein Prozess der Veränderung menschlicher Triebanlagen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A14","text":"Einzelne Triebregungen können in dauerhafte Charaktereigenschaften umgewandelt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A15","text":"Triebsublimierung ermöglicht die kulturelle Bedeutung wissenschaftlicher, künstlerischer und ideologischer Tätigkeiten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","text":"Kultur beruht in erheblichem Maß auf der Nichtbefriedigung mächtiger Triebe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","text":"Triebversagung erzeugt ohne ökonomische Kompensation ernste Störungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX1","text":"Vollständige Naturbeherrschung und Aufhebung körperlicher Endlichkeit sind ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX2","text":"Aus kulturell erzeugtem Leiden folgt keine gesicherte Rückkehrmöglichkeit zu einem glücklicheren primitiven Zustand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX3","text":"Aus dem fehlenden Zuwachs an Gesamtglück folgt nicht die Wertlosigkeit technischer Fortschritte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX4","text":"Das Glück früherer Menschen ist nicht durch Projektion gegenwärtiger Ansprüche objektiv messbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX5","text":"Kultur ist nicht auf technische Nützlichkeit reduzierbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX6","text":"Kulturentwicklung ist nicht mit menschlicher Vervollkommnung gleichzusetzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX7","text":"Die Entstehung von Recht aus Gemeinschaftsmacht begründet noch keinen ethischen Wert dieses Rechts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX8","text":"Freiheitsdrang ist weder eindeutig kulturfördernd noch eindeutig kulturfeindlich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX9","text":"Sublimierung wird nicht abschließend als ausschließlich kulturzwanghaftes Schicksal aller Triebe festgelegt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D1","text":"Die soziale Leidensquelle bleibt institutionell veränderbar, ohne deshalb von psychischen Grenzen unabhängig zu sein.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D2","text":"Kulturfeindlichkeit wird endogen erzeugt, weil dasselbe System Schutz gewährt und Befriedigungen versagt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D3","text":"Technischer Fortschritt kann reale Einzelbefriedigungen hervorbringen, ohne ein zuverlässiges Maß des Gesamtglücks zu liefern.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D4","text":"Der Kulturbegriff verbindet instrumentelle Naturbeherrschung mit ästhetischen, ordnenden und ideellen Leistungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","text":"Recht beseitigt Macht nicht, sondern überführt individuelle Macht in dauerhafte Gemeinschaftsmacht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6","text":"Freiheitskampf erweitert Kultur, wenn er ungleiche Einschränkungen beseitigt, und bekämpft Kultur, wenn er Einschränkung überhaupt zurückweist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D7","text":"Kulturelle Eigenschaften und höhere Leistungen sind Resultate unterschiedlicher Umformungen der Triebökonomie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D8","text":"Kulturfeindseligkeit und psychische Störung sind erwartbare Folgen unzureichend kompensierter Kulturversagung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1","text":"Kultur operiert rekursiv: Sie bearbeitet vorgefundenes Leiden durch Mechanismen, die eine neue soziale Form des Leidens erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","text":"Die Steigerung menschlicher Verfügungsmacht verändert Lebensbedingungen, ohne die subjektive Glücksökonomie proportional zu verbessern.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD3","text":"Politische Ordnung bleibt strukturell zwangsförmig, weil Recht auf kollektivierter Macht und gleichmäßig verlangtem Triebopfer beruht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4","text":"Kulturfortschritt bezeichnet keine lineare Zunahme von Glück oder Vollkommenheit, sondern eine fortgesetzte Reorganisation von Triebzielen, Befriedigungen und Charakterformen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD5","text":"Der Gesamtwert einer Kultur für das Glück bleibt epistemisch unentscheidbar, während ihre Mechanismen der Unzufriedenheit strukturell diagnostizierbar bleiben.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX1","text":"Soziale Institutionen können nicht als von menschlicher Triebstruktur unabhängige Konstruktionen behandelt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX2","text":"Ein lineares Verhältnis zwischen technischer Macht und Glückszuwachs ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX3","text":"Nützlichkeit kann die Entstehung und Geltung kultureller Formen nicht vollständig erklären.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX4","text":"Recht kann nicht als machtfreier Gegensatz zur Gewalt begriffen werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX5","text":"Dauerhafte Gemeinschaft ist nicht mit unbeschränkter individueller Triebbefriedigung vereinbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX6","text":"Die menschliche Natur ist nicht so vollständig formbar, dass der individuelle Freiheitsanspruch restlos in den Willen der Masse überführt werden könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX1","text":"Eine Kultur ohne Triebopfer, Feindseligkeit und psychische Kosten steht dem System nicht als Möglichkeit zur Verfügung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX2","text":"Ein empirisch gesicherter außerkultureller Glückszustand steht nicht als Alternative zur Kultur bereit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX3","text":"Eine endgültige Versöhnung von individueller Freiheit und kulturellem Massenanspruch bleibt ungesichert und möglicherweise unerreichbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX4","text":"Ein bestimmbares Äquivalent zwischen gefordertem Triebopfer und gewährtem Kulturgewinn fehlt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5","text":"Eine terminale Erklärung des Ursprungs und des Verlaufsgesetzes der Kulturentwicklung wird nicht erreicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS1","text":"Leiden → Naturübermacht + Körperhinfälligkeit + soziale Unzulänglichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS2","text":"Natur und Körper → Anerkennung irreduzibler Grenze → partielle Milderung; Sozialordnung → Zurückweisung der Grenze → Verdacht auf psychische Vermittlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS3","text":"Langdauernde Unzufriedenheit + historische Auslöser → Kulturanklage; Kulturanklage + Schutzfunktion der Kultur → innerer Kulturwiderspruch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS4","text":"Technische Macht ohne proportionalen Glückszuwachs + subjektive Inkommensurabilität des Glücks → Suspendierung des globalen Glücksurteils.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS5","text":"Suspendiertes Werturteil → funktionale Kulturdefinition → Naturschutz + Regelung sozialer Beziehungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS6","text":"Kulturdefinition → Organerweiterung + Schönheit, Reinlichkeit und Ordnung + höhere psychische Tätigkeiten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS7","text":"Individuelle Gewalt → überlegene Mehrheit → Gemeinschaftsmacht → Recht → Gerechtigkeit als allgemeine Einschränkung → Freiheitskonflikt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS8","text":"Triebveränderung → Charakterbildung oder Sublimierung oder Versagung → Kulturleistung und Kulturfeindseligkeit → Kompensationsproblem → offene Ursprungsfrage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AF1","text":"Dreifache Leidensdiagnose → Sonderstellung der sozialen Leidensquelle → Kulturanklage → Genealogie der Kulturfeindlichkeit → Entkopplung von Fortschritt und Glück → funktionale Kulturdefinition → Recht-Freiheits-Konflikt → psychoanalytische Prozessbestimmung → offene Frage nach Ursprung und Kompensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME1","text":"Die soziale Leidensquelle wird von einem bloßen Institutionenfehler zu einer Vermittlungszone zwischen Einrichtung und psychischer Beschaffenheit umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME2","text":"Kultur wird zugleich als Schutzapparat und als endogene Leidensproduktion klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME3","text":"Technik erscheint nicht mehr als Glücksmaß, sondern als prothetische Erweiterung begrenzter menschlicher Organe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME4","text":"Die kulturelle Landschaft wird von einer reinen Nutzenordnung zu einem Verbund instrumenteller, ästhetischer, hygienischer, intellektueller und ideeller Leistungen erweitert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME5","text":"Der Gegensatz von Recht und Gewalt wird durch die Unterscheidung individueller Gewalt und kollektiv organisierter Macht ersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME6","text":"Freiheit wird von einem eindeutigen Kulturwert zu einer ambivalenten Kraft zwischen Gerechtigkeitskorrektur und Kulturfeindlichkeit umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME7","text":"Kulturfortschritt wird von Vervollkommnung auf Triebverarbeitung umgestellt; Kulturfeindseligkeit erscheint dadurch als internes Prozessprodukt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — Der explizite Gegenstand ist der zweifelhafte Glückswert der Kultur und die Bestimmung ihrer erkennbaren Merkmale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Kultur organisiert Naturbeherrschung, Gemeinschaftsmacht, Recht, Gerechtigkeit und die Einschränkung individueller Befriedigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Das Argument ersetzt Kulturverwerfung und Fortschrittsapologie durch die Analyse jener Mechanismen, die Schutzleistung und Unbehagen gleichzeitig erzeugen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Der Mensch bleibt endlicher Naturkörper, Kultur bleibt unabgeschlossener Triebprozess, und Glückszustände bleiben zwischen psychisch verschiedenen Subjekten und Zeiten inkommensurabel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von der Leidensdiagnose zur triebdynamischen Kulturtheorie zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die historische Kausalkette der Kulturfeindlichkeit sowie Ursprung und Verlaufsgesetz der Kulturentwicklung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT3","text":"Die Doppelbestimmung der Kultur als Schutz und Versagung ist intern kohärent, weil beide Wirkungen auf verschiedenen Funktionsachsen liegen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste generative Verbindung liegt zwischen Befriedigungseinschränkung, Kulturfeindseligkeit und Kompensationsbedarf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT5","text":"Die Analogie zwischen Kulturprozess und individueller Libidoentwicklung bleibt mechanistisch unvollständig; die Triebverwandlung wird behauptet, ihr Vollzug aber als ungeklärt markiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT6","text":"Zwischen der deskriptiven Herleitung des Rechts aus Gemeinschaftsmacht und dem Entwicklungsziel allgemeinen Rechts bleibt eine normative Bruchlinie bestehen, obwohl der ethische Wert ausdrücklich suspendiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT7","text":"Der Merkmalskatalog der Kultur stützt sich auf Sprachgebrauch und Sprachgefühl; seine operative Brauchbarkeit ersetzt keinen Vollständigkeitsbeweis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT8","text":"Die Subjektivität des Glücks verhindert einen vergleichenden Gesamtbeweis für die Schuld der Kultur; die Gegenüberstellung technischer Wohltaten und Folgekosten bleibt daher ohne gemeinsame Bilanzgröße.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT9","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung: Kulturkritik wird weder bestätigt noch verworfen, sondern in eine Theorie von Macht, Triebverarbeitung und unvermeidbaren Kosten überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171411407721Z_8352106b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter III","source_sha256":"009c58d25162b33ebeb6a963d01023fe0660106f487477d18d125f985cdf9330","sha256":"febd3094507c1f5afbce0177ee2dcbe11498d697abc8bb88473d76e3c59d0422","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:14:11.410653+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS1","text":"The special status of the social source of suffering constitutes the problem, because human beings do not acknowledge self-created institutions as unavoidable in the way they acknowledge the overpowering force of nature and bodily decay.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2","text":"Culture is at once the system of protection against suffering and, through its denials, a source of new suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds diagnostically, genealogically, and psychoanalytically-reconstructively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS4","text":"Persistent dissatisfaction is condensed into hostility to culture through religious devaluation of life, projections of primitive happiness, the diagnosis of neurosis, and technical disappointment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS5","text":"Neither technical advances nor comparisons with earlier forms of life determine the happiness-value of culture, because mastery of nature does not suffice and happiness remains subjective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS6","text":"The inquiry replaces the global judgment on happiness with a functional reconstruction of culture as protection against nature, regulation of relationships, and cultivation of useful as well as non-useful achievements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS7","text":"Social culture arises through the replacement of individual violence by communal power, produces law and justice, and simultaneously intensifies the conflict with individual freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS8","text":"The concluding reframing defines cultural development as the working-over of human drives through character formation, sublimation, and denial, thereby opening the question of the origin, course, and compensation of this process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","text":"Human suffering springs from the overpowering force of nature, the frailty of the body, and the inadequacy of social institutions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A2","text":"Nature and the body remain fundamentally incompletely controllable, although individual sufferings can be removed or alleviated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A3","text":"Behind the inadequacy of social institutions lies the suspicion of a limit in the human being's psychical constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","text":"Culture encompasses the achievements and institutions for protection against nature and for the regulation of human relationships.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","text":"Culture reduces suffering through protection and produces suffering through the restriction of satisfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A6","text":"Mastery of nature is neither the sole condition of human happiness nor the sole aim of culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","text":"Happiness is fundamentally subjective and dependent on the respective psychical sensitivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8","text":"Cultural valuation is not exhausted by utility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A9","text":"Human coexistence first becomes possible through a communal power superior to each individual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10","text":"Justice demands that the established legal order not be breached in favor of individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","text":"Individual freedom is not a cultural asset and is restricted by culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A12","text":"The persisting urge for freedom can be directed either against injustice or against culture as such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13","text":"Cultural development is a process of transforming human drive-dispositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A14","text":"Individual drive impulses can be transformed into enduring character traits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A15","text":"Drive sublimation enables the cultural significance of scientific, artistic, and ideological activities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","text":"Culture rests to a considerable extent on the non-satisfaction of powerful drives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","text":"Drive denial produces serious disturbances without economic compensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX1","text":"Complete mastery of nature and abolition of bodily finitude are excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX2","text":"Culturally produced suffering does not entail any assured possibility of return to a happier primitive state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX3","text":"The absence of an increase in overall happiness does not entail the worthlessness of technical advances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX4","text":"The happiness of earlier human beings cannot be objectively measured by projecting present-day demands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX5","text":"Culture is not reducible to technical utility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX6","text":"Cultural development is not to be equated with human perfectibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX7","text":"The emergence of law from communal power does not yet establish the ethical value of this law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX8","text":"The urge for freedom is neither unambiguously culture-promoting nor unambiguously hostile to culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX9","text":"Sublimation is not conclusively fixed as the exclusively culture-compelled fate of all drives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D1","text":"The social source of suffering remains institutionally alterable without thereby being independent of psychical limits.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D2","text":"Hostility to culture is generated endogenously because the same system grants protection and denies satisfactions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D3","text":"Technical progress can produce real individual satisfactions without providing a reliable measure of overall happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D4","text":"The concept of culture joins instrumental mastery of nature with aesthetic, ordering, and ideational achievements.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","text":"Law does not abolish power but rather transforms individual power into enduring communal power.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6","text":"The struggle for freedom expands culture when it abolishes unequal restrictions, and combats culture when it rejects restriction altogether.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D7","text":"Cultural characteristics and higher achievements are results of different transformations of the drive economy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:D8","text":"Hostility to culture and psychical disturbance are expectable consequences of insufficiently compensated cultural denial.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1","text":"Culture operates recursively: it works upon pre-existing suffering through mechanisms that produce a new social form of suffering.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","text":"The increase of human power of disposal alters conditions of life without proportionally improving the subjective economy of happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD3","text":"Political order remains structurally coercive, because law rests upon collectivized power and sacrifice of drives demanded equally of all.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4","text":"Cultural progress denotes no linear increase in happiness or perfection, but a continuing reorganization of drive aims, satisfactions, and character forms.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD5","text":"The overall value of a culture for happiness remains epistemically undecidable, while its mechanisms of dissatisfaction remain structurally diagnosable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX1","text":"Social institutions cannot be treated as constructions independent of human drive structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX2","text":"A linear relation between technical power and an increase in happiness is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX3","text":"Utility cannot fully explain the emergence and validity of cultural forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX4","text":"Law cannot be understood as a power-free opposite to violence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX5","text":"Enduring community is not compatible with unrestricted individual drive satisfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX6","text":"Human nature is not so completely malleable that the individual claim to freedom could be transferred without remainder into the will of the mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX1","text":"A culture without drive sacrifice, hostility, and psychical costs is not available to the system as a possibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX2","text":"An empirically secured extra-cultural state of happiness is not available as an alternative to culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX3","text":"A final reconciliation of individual freedom and the cultural claim of the masses remains unassured and perhaps unattainable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0079","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX4","text":"A determinable equivalent between the required sacrifice of drives and the cultural gain granted is lacking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5","text":"A terminal explanation of the origin and law of development of cultural development is not attained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS1","text":"Suffering → overpowering force of nature + bodily frailty + social inadequacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS2","text":"Nature and body → acknowledgment of irreducible limit → partial alleviation; social order → rejection of the limit → suspicion of psychical mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS3","text":"Persistent dissatisfaction + historical triggers → indictment of culture; indictment of culture + protective function of culture → inner contradiction of culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS4","text":"Technical power without proportional increase in happiness + subjective incommensurability of happiness → suspension of the global judgment on happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS5","text":"Suspended value judgment → functional definition of culture → protection against nature + regulation of social relationships.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS6","text":"Definition of culture → extension of organs + beauty, cleanliness, and order + higher psychical activities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS7","text":"Individual violence → superior majority → communal power → law → justice as general restriction → conflict over freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:FGS8","text":"Transformation of drives → character formation or sublimation or denial → cultural achievement and hostility to culture → problem of compensation → open question of origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:AF1","text":"Threefold diagnosis of suffering → special status of the social source of suffering → indictment of culture → genealogy of hostility to culture → decoupling of progress and happiness → functional definition of culture → conflict between law and freedom → psychoanalytic determination of process → open question of origin and compensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME1","text":"The social source of suffering is remapped from a mere institutional defect into a mediating zone between institution and psychical constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME2","text":"Culture is classified at once as a protective apparatus and as endogenous production of suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME3","text":"Technology no longer appears as a measure of happiness, but as a prosthetic extension of limited human organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME4","text":"The cultural landscape is expanded from a pure order of utility into a complex of instrumental, aesthetic, hygienic, intellectual, and ideational achievements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME5","text":"The opposition of law and violence is replaced by the distinction between individual violence and collectively organized power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME6","text":"Freedom is reclassified from an unambiguous cultural value into an ambivalent force between correction of injustice and hostility to culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME7","text":"Cultural progress is shifted from perfection to drive processing; hostility to culture thereby appears as an internal product of the process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — The explicit subject is the questionable happiness-value of culture and the determination of its recognizable features.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Culture organizes mastery of nature, communal power, law, justice, and the restriction of individual satisfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — The argument replaces rejection of culture and apologetics for progress with the analysis of those mechanisms that simultaneously generate protective achievement and discontent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — The human being remains a finite natural body, culture remains an unfinished drive process, and states of happiness remain incommensurable between psychically different subjects and times.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the diagnosis of suffering to a drive-dynamic theory of culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT2","text":"The historical causal chain of hostility to culture, as well as the origin and law of development of cultural development, remain underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT3","text":"The dual determination of culture as protection and denial is internally coherent because both effects lie on different functional axes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4","text":"The strongest generative connection lies between restriction of satisfaction, hostility to culture, and the need for compensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT5","text":"The analogy between the cultural process and individual libido development remains mechanistically incomplete; the transformation of drives is asserted, but its execution is marked as unexplained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT6","text":"Between the descriptive derivation of law from communal power and the developmental aim of universal law, a normative fault line remains, although the ethical value is explicitly suspended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT7","text":"The catalogue of features of culture relies on linguistic usage and linguistic feeling; its operational usefulness does not replace proof of completeness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT8","text":"The subjectivity of happiness prevents a comparative overall proof of culture's guilt; the juxtaposition of technical benefits and consequential costs therefore remains without a common unit of accounting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: cultural criticism is neither confirmed nor rejected, but transformed into a theory of power, drive processing, and unavoidable costs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_3:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_3@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KA_3:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 03","title":"Chapter III","context":"Chapter 03","original_title":"Kapitel III","original_context":"Chapter 03"},"original_title":"Kapitel III","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4","layer":"CH","title":"Chapter IV","order":4,"parents":["RAW_R2TV_KA_4"],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_4@R001","sha256":"65bc39497e890ffede41efdb247eb5840acbe3950d428c5708a43fdea69f6920","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS1","text":"Der Text rekonstruiert Kultur als Antwort auf die Verbindung von äußerer Arbeitsnotwendigkeit und dauerhafter libidinöser Bindung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS2","text":"Die Familie entsteht als frühe Bindungsform, genügt jedoch nicht als Kultur, solange väterliche Willkür uneingeschränkt bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS3","text":"Die Ablösung der patriarchalen Familie durch Brüderbünde erzeugt wechselseitige Verbote, Tabu und Recht als Bedingungen stabiler Vergesellschaftung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","text":"Liebe ermöglicht intensivere Bindung als Arbeitsinteresse, erzeugt aber zugleich exklusive Familienbindungen, die der kulturellen Ausdehnung widerstehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS5","text":"Kultur verlangt für ihre Expansion psychische Energie und entzieht sie dem Sexualleben, wodurch sie ihre eigene libidinöse Grundlage beschädigt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS6","text":"Die kulturelle Universalisierung sexueller Normen missachtet unterschiedliche sexuelle Konstitutionen, bleibt praktisch unvollständig und erzeugt dennoch Leid, Ungleichheit und Funktionsschädigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A1","text":"Äußere Notwendigkeit zwingt Menschen zur Arbeit und macht Kooperation lebenspraktisch vorteilhaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","text":"Dauerhafte sexuelle Erregung wird hypothetisch als Bedingung dafür gesetzt, Sexualobjekte und Kinder dauerhaft in einer Familienbindung festzuhalten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A3","text":"Die patriarchale Urfamilie ist noch keine voll entwickelte Kultur, weil sie auf uneingeschränkter väterlicher Willkür beruht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A4","text":"Die Erfahrung gemeinsamer Stärke ermöglicht den Übergang von individueller Unterordnung zu Brüderbünden mit gegenseitigen Einschränkungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","text":"Tabuvorschriften bilden als wechselseitig auferlegte Einschränkungen die erste Rechtsform kulturellen Zusammenlebens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","text":"Eros und Ananke begründen Kultur gemeinsam, weil Liebe bindet und Notwendigkeit zur Kooperation zwingt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","text":"Die psychische Energie des Menschen ist begrenzt und muss zwischen kultureller Arbeit, Sexualität und Familienbindung verteilt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","text":"Kultur strebt nach Erweiterung ihrer sozialen Einheiten und verlangt deshalb Einschränkungen exklusiver sexueller und familialer Bindungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9","text":"Standardisierte sexuelle Verbote ignorieren angeborene und erworbene Unterschiede sexueller Konstitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10","text":"Eine kulturelle Sexualordnung kann ihre Verbote faktisch nicht vollständig durchsetzen und schädigt das Sexualleben dennoch nachhaltig.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX1","text":"Kultur ist nicht identisch mit der Familie, weil familiale Bindung unter patriarchaler Willkür und exklusiver Selbstabschließung bestehen kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX2","text":"Kulturentwicklung ist nicht automatisch Glücksentwicklung, obwohl Eros und Ananke zunächst eine harmonische Steigerung von Beherrschung und Gemeinschaft erwarten lassen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX3","text":"Allgemeine Menschenliebe ist nicht schlechthin die höchste Liebesform, weil sie Selektivität und Objektwert nivelliert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX4","text":"Genitale Liebe ist nicht bloß eine sichere Glückstechnik, weil sie Abhängigkeit vom Liebesobjekt und Verlustleid erzeugt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX5","text":"Sexuelle Einschränkung ist nicht harmlos, auch wenn kulturelle Verbote faktisch vielfach überschritten werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX6","text":"Heterosexuelle, genitale und monogame Ehebindung ist nicht als neutrale natürliche Norm gesetzt, sondern als kulturell erzwungene Beschränkung der Sexualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX7","text":"Die organische Genealogie von Aufrichtung, Geruchsverdrängung, Scham, Sexualkontinuität und Familie wird nicht als gesicherte Erklärung behauptet, sondern ausdrücklich als theoretische Spekulation begrenzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D1","text":"Arbeitsteilung allein erzeugt keine hinreichend intensive und dauerhafte Gemeinschaft; Liebe übernimmt eine stärkere Bindungsfunktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D2","text":"Recht erscheint nicht als ursprüngliche moralische Ordnung, sondern als institutionalisierte Selbstbeschränkung ehemals rivalisierender Einzelner.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","text":"Die Familie ist zugleich Keimform der Kultur und Widerstandszentrum gegen ihre Ausdehnung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D4","text":"Die kulturelle Ausweitung sozialer Einheiten verlangt eine partielle Ablösung des Individuums von seinen primären Familienbindungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D5","text":"Kulturelle Arbeit verwandelt Libido nicht verlustfrei, sondern konkurriert mit Ehe, Elternschaft und direkter Sexualbefriedigung um dieselbe psychische Energie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D6","text":"Die Unterdrückung kindlicher Sexualität fungiert im Text als Vorarbeit für die spätere Disziplinierung erwachsener Sexualität.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D7","text":"Die Gleichförmigkeit der sexuellen Norm produziert Ungerechtigkeit, weil sie unterschiedliche sexuelle Dispositionen zugleich reguliert, ausschließt und pathologisiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","text":"Kultur reproduziert sich durch die Umleitung jener Libido, aus der ihre ersten Bindungsformen hervorgegangen sind, und erzeugt dadurch einen Konflikt mit ihrer eigenen Voraussetzung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD2","text":"Die kulturelle Vergrößerung der Gemeinschaft erfolgt nicht durch bloße Addition von Familien, sondern durch Begrenzung familialer Ausschließlichkeit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD3","text":"Kultur produziert einen strukturellen Zielkonflikt zwischen intensiver, selektiver Bindung und extensiver, universalisierten Vergesellschaftung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD4","text":"Das Sexualleben wird kulturell zugleich als notwendige Reproduktionsquelle geduldet und als autonome Lustquelle eingeschränkt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD5","text":"Die kulturelle Ordnung bleibt von der Sexualität abhängig, obwohl sie Sexualität als potentiell widerständige und zu kontrollierende Energie behandelt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX1","text":"Das System setzt voraus, dass keine konfliktfreie Kontinuität zwischen privatem Glück, erotischer Exklusivität und kultureller Universalität besteht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX2","text":"Das System schließt aus, dass psychische Energie unbegrenzt oder ohne Verlust von Sexualität in Kulturarbeit überführbar ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX3","text":"Das System disqualifiziert die Annahme, soziale Ordnung könne ohne Triebverzicht, Tabu oder wechselseitige Beschränkung stabilisiert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX4","text":"Das System schließt aus, dass eine einheitliche Sexualnorm den verschiedenen sexuellen Konstitutionen gerecht werden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX5","text":"Das System verneint implizit, dass der kulturelle Fortschritt als lineare Steigerung von Freiheit, Glück und sexueller Befriedigung begriffen werden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt eine gesellschaftliche Form, in der die Ausdehnung des Kollektivs und die Unversehrtheit exklusiver Liebe vollständig vereinbar wären.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt eine Kultur, die ihre libidinöse Grundlage bewahrt, ohne sie zugleich institutionell zu regulieren und zu beschneiden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt eine abschließende Versöhnung von individueller sexueller Vielfalt und allgemeingültiger sozialer Normierung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt eine sichere teleologische Erzählung, nach der Kultur notwendig zu zunehmendem Glück führt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS1","text":"Äußere Notwendigkeit → Arbeit → Kooperation → Nutzen gemeinschaftlichen Zusammenlebens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS2","text":"Dauerhafte Sexualbindung → Familienbildung → intensive exklusive Bindung → frühe soziale Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS3","text":"Patriarchale Willkür → kollektive Überwältigung des Vaters → Brüderbund → gegenseitige Verbote → Tabu und Recht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS4","text":"Eros + Ananke → kulturelle Bindungskapazität → Vergrößerung der Gemeinschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS5","text":"Gemeinschaftsausdehnung + endliche Libido → Entzug psychischer Energie aus Sexualität und Familie → kulturelle Sexualbeschränkung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS6","text":"Universalisierte Sexualnorm + heterogene Konstitutionen → Ausschluss, Ungerechtigkeit, Übertretung und Schädigung des Sexuallebens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS7","text":"Kulturelle Abhängigkeit von Liebe + kulturelle Einschränkung der Liebe → dauerhafte Entzweiung von Kultur und Erotik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF1","text":"Arbeitsnot und dauerhafte Sexualbindung → Familie als erste nützliche Bindungsform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF2","text":"Familie unter väterlicher Willkür → Brüderbund und gegenseitige Restriktion → Tabu und Recht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF3","text":"Eros und Ananke → Möglichkeit größerer Gemeinschaften → Erwartung kulturellen Glücks.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF4","text":"Familiäre und genitale Exklusivität → Widerstand gegen Gemeinschaftsausdehnung → Konflikt von Liebe und Kultur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF5","text":"Kultureller Energiebedarf → sexuelle Einschränkung → Beschädigung der Glücksquelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF6","text":"Einheitliche sexuelle Normierung → Ungleichheit und faktische Überschreitung → unaufgelöste kulturelle Schädigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME1","text":"Kultur wird von einem Fortschrittsraum zu einem Konfliktfeld umverteilter Libido umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME2","text":"Liebe wird zugleich als Ursprung sozialer Bindung, als Technik individuellen Glücks und als Hindernis kultureller Expansion klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME3","text":"Recht wird als sedimentierte Einschränkung konkurrierender Triebansprüche statt als voraussetzungsloser moralischer Ursprung sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME4","text":"Die Familie erscheint nicht als private Vorstufe außerhalb der Kultur, sondern als kulturelle Grundlage und strukturelle Gegenkraft zugleich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME5","text":"Sexuelle Normen erscheinen nicht als bloße Sittenregeln, sondern als Mechanismen zur Umlenkung psychischer Energie in Kulturarbeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME6","text":"Faktische Regelverletzung widerlegt kulturelle Repression nicht, sondern zeigt ihre Durchsetzungslimits bei fortbestehender Schädigungswirkung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der Text behandelt Familie, Liebe, Sexualität, Tabu, Monogamie und die kulturelle Einschränkung des Sexuallebens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT2","text":"Structural — Kultur stabilisiert größere soziale Einheiten durch Arbeit, Recht, Tabu und die Umlenkung begrenzter Libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Das Problem wird von einer moralischen Bewertung sexueller Normen in eine Analyse kultureller Energieverwaltung verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Kultur erscheint als nichtlinearer Prozess, in dem ihre Grundlage, die libidinöse Bindung, zur dauerhaften Quelle ihrer inneren Störung wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT5","text":"Genealogical — Die Ordnung der Gegenwart wird auf eine Abfolge hypothetischer somatischer, familialer, rechtlicher und ökonomischer Umformungen zurückgeführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die doppelte kulturelle Herkunft aus Notwendigkeit und Liebe sowie den Übergang von Familie zu Recht zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT2","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um den späteren Konflikt zwischen kultureller Expansion und sexueller beziehungsweise familialer Bindung herzuleiten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT3","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt die empirische Tragfähigkeit der organischen Genealogie von Aufrichtung, Geruchsverdrängung, Scham und Familiengründung, da sie als Spekulation markiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT4","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt die Begründung, weshalb Kultur notwendig gerade die dargestellten Formen sexueller Einschränkung wählen muss und keine weniger schädlichen Vermittlungen hervorbringen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT5","text":"Die Struktur ist kohärent, sofern Kultur als auf begrenzte Libido angewiesenes und diese zugleich umleitendes System begriffen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT6","text":"Die stärkste Spannung liegt darin, dass Liebe Kultur zugleich begründet, verdichtet, begrenzt und durch kulturelle Anforderungen beschädigt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die argumentative Bewegung, sofern die historische Genealogie nicht als gesicherter Ursprung, sondern als teilweise hypothetische Trägerschicht behandelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171442676921Z_199de6e4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter IV","source_sha256":"65bc39497e890ffede41efdb247eb5840acbe3950d428c5708a43fdea69f6920","sha256":"297ef9bd9f942669f82059cc41cecd1161a087cf653203d61ea2d1a955f05619","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:14:42.678152+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS1","text":"The text reconstructs civilization as a response to the conjunction of external necessity of labor and enduring libidinal attachment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS2","text":"The family emerges as an early form of attachment, but does not suffice as civilization so long as paternal arbitrariness remains unrestricted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS3","text":"The replacement of the patriarchal family by bands of brothers generates reciprocal prohibitions, taboo, and law as conditions of stable social association.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","text":"Love enables a more intensive attachment than an interest in labor, but at the same time produces exclusive family attachments that resist civilizational expansion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS5","text":"Civilization requires psychic energy for its expansion and withdraws it from sexual life, thereby damaging its own libidinal foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS6","text":"The civilizational universalization of sexual norms disregards differing sexual constitutions, remains practically incomplete, and nevertheless produces suffering, inequality, and impairment of functioning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A1","text":"External necessity compels human beings to work and makes cooperation advantageous in practical life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","text":"Permanent sexual excitation is hypothetically posited as the condition for retaining sexual objects and children enduringly within a family bond.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A3","text":"The patriarchal primal family is not yet a fully developed civilization because it rests upon unrestricted paternal arbitrariness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A4","text":"The experience of collective strength enables the transition from individual subordination to bands of brothers with mutual restrictions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","text":"Taboo prescriptions, as mutually imposed restrictions, constitute the first legal form of civilized coexistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","text":"Eros and Ananke jointly ground civilization, because love binds and necessity compels cooperation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","text":"Human psychic energy is limited and must be distributed among civilizational work, sexuality, and family attachment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","text":"Civilization strives to enlarge its social units and therefore requires restrictions upon exclusive sexual and familial attachments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9","text":"Standardized sexual prohibitions ignore innate and acquired differences in sexual constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10","text":"A civilizational sexual order cannot in fact fully enforce its prohibitions and nevertheless damages sexual life enduringly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX1","text":"Civilization is not identical with the family, because familial attachment can persist under patriarchal arbitrariness and exclusive self-enclosure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX2","text":"Civilizational development is not automatically the development of happiness, although Eros and Ananke initially suggest a harmonious increase in mastery and community.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX3","text":"Universal love of humankind is not simply the highest form of love, because it levels selectivity and the value of the object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX4","text":"Genital love is not merely a secure technique of happiness, because it produces dependence on the love object and suffering from loss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX5","text":"Sexual restriction is not harmless, even when civilizational prohibitions are in fact frequently transgressed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX6","text":"Heterosexual, genital, and monogamous marital attachment is not posited as a neutral natural norm, but as a culturally enforced restriction of sexuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX7","text":"The organic genealogy of upright posture, repression of smell, shame, sexual continuity, and family is not asserted as a secure explanation, but is expressly limited as theoretical speculation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D1","text":"The division of labor alone does not produce a sufficiently intensive and enduring community; love assumes a stronger binding function.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D2","text":"Law appears not as an original moral order, but as the institutionalized self-restraint of formerly rival individuals.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","text":"The family is at once the germinal form of civilization and a center of resistance against its expansion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D4","text":"The civilizational expansion of social units requires a partial detachment of the individual from primary family attachments.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D5","text":"Civilizational work does not transform libido without loss, but competes with marriage, parenthood, and direct sexual satisfaction for the same psychic energy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D6","text":"In the text, the suppression of infantile sexuality functions as preparatory work for the later disciplining of adult sexuality.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:D7","text":"The uniformity of the sexual norm produces injustice because it simultaneously regulates, excludes, and pathologizes differing sexual dispositions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","text":"Civilization reproduces itself through the diversion of the libido from which its first forms of attachment arose, thereby generating a conflict with its own precondition.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD2","text":"The civilizational enlargement of the community does not occur through the mere addition of families, but through the limitation of familial exclusivity.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD3","text":"Civilization produces a structural conflict of ends between intensive, selective attachment and extensive, universalized social association.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD4","text":"Sexual life is culturally tolerated both as a necessary source of reproduction and restricted as an autonomous source of pleasure.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD5","text":"Civilizational order remains dependent on sexuality, although it treats sexuality as a potentially resistant energy to be controlled.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX1","text":"The system presupposes that no conflict-free continuity exists between private happiness, erotic exclusivity, and civilizational universality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that psychic energy is unlimited or can be transferred from sexuality into civilizational work without loss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX3","text":"The system disqualifies the assumption that social order could be stabilized without instinctual renunciation, taboo, or mutual restriction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a uniform sexual norm can do justice to different sexual constitutions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX5","text":"The system implicitly denies that civilizational progress can be understood as a linear increase in freedom, happiness, and sexual satisfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX1","text":"Excluded remains a social form in which the expansion of the collective and the intactness of exclusive love would be fully compatible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX2","text":"Excluded remains a civilization that preserves its libidinal foundation without at the same time institutionally regulating and curtailing it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX3","text":"Excluded remains a final reconciliation of individual sexual diversity and universally valid social normativity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX4","text":"Excluded remains a secure teleological narrative according to which civilization necessarily leads to increasing happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS1","text":"External necessity → work → cooperation → benefit of communal coexistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS2","text":"Enduring sexual attachment → family formation → intensive exclusive attachment → early social unit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS3","text":"Patriarchal arbitrariness → collective overpowering of the father → band of brothers → mutual prohibitions → taboo and law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS4","text":"Eros + Ananke → civilizational capacity for attachment → enlargement of the community.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS5","text":"Expansion of the community + finite libido → withdrawal of psychic energy from sexuality and family → civilizational sexual restriction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS6","text":"Universalized sexual norm + heterogeneous constitutions → exclusion, injustice, transgression, and impairment of sexual life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS7","text":"Civilizational dependence on love + civilizational restriction of love → enduring division between civilization and eroticism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF1","text":"Necessity of labor and enduring sexual attachment → family as the first useful form of attachment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF2","text":"Family under paternal arbitrariness → band of brothers and mutual restriction → taboo and law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF3","text":"Eros and Ananke → possibility of larger communities → expectation of civilizational happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF4","text":"Familial and genital exclusivity → resistance to the expansion of the community → conflict between love and civilization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF5","text":"Civilizational energy demand → sexual restriction → damage to the source of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF6","text":"Uniform sexual normativity → inequality and factual transgression → unresolved civilizational damage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME1","text":"Civilization is remapped from a space of progress into a field of conflict of redistributed libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME2","text":"Love is classified at once as the origin of social attachment, as a technique of individual happiness, and as an obstacle to civilizational expansion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME3","text":"Law becomes visible as the sedimented restriction of competing instinctual claims rather than as a presuppositionless moral origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME4","text":"The family appears not as a private preliminary stage outside civilization, but as both a civilizational foundation and a structural counterforce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME5","text":"Sexual norms appear not as mere rules of custom, but as mechanisms for redirecting psychic energy into civilizational work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME6","text":"Factual rule-breaking does not refute civilizational repression, but shows its limits of enforcement while its damaging effect persists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text addresses family, love, sexuality, taboo, monogamy, and the civilizational restriction of sexual life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT2","text":"Structural — Civilization stabilizes larger social units through labor, law, taboo, and the redirection of limited libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The problem is shifted from a moral evaluation of sexual norms to an analysis of civilizational energy management.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Civilization appears as a nonlinear process in which its foundation, libidinal attachment, becomes the enduring source of its internal disturbance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT5","text":"Genealogical — The order of the present is traced back to a sequence of hypothetical somatic, familial, legal, and economic transformations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the dual civilizational origin in necessity and love, as well as the transition from family to law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT2","text":"The axioms suffice to derive the later conflict between civilizational expansion and sexual or familial attachment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT3","text":"The empirical viability of the organic genealogy of upright posture, repression of smell, shame, and family formation remains underdetermined, since it is marked as speculation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT4","text":"Underdetermined remains the justification for why civilization must necessarily choose precisely the depicted forms of sexual restriction and could not produce less damaging mediations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT5","text":"The structure is coherent insofar as civilization is understood as a system dependent on limited libido and simultaneously redirecting it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT6","text":"The strongest tension lies in the fact that love simultaneously grounds, intensifies, limits civilization, and is damaged by civilizational demands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the argumentative movement insofar as the historical genealogy is treated not as a secure origin, but as a partially hypothetical supporting layer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_4:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_4@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KA_4:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 04","title":"Chapter IV","context":"Chapter 04","original_title":"Kapitel IV","original_context":"Chapter 04"},"original_title":"Kapitel IV","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV","layer":"CH","title":"Chapter V","order":5,"parents":["RAW_R2TV_KAPV"],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KAPV@R001","sha256":"90b8c88d6542a59a161f3e235718066bf22f209ac26fdc7b04587ed05dea1543","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS1","text":"Das Kapitel bestimmt das kulturelle Unbehagen als Folge von Triebverzicht, der Sexualität und Aggression zugleich betrifft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS2","text":"Der Gegensatz von Kultur und Sexualität wird aus der Spannung zwischen dyadischer erotischer Bindung und der Ausdehnung sozialer Bindungen auf viele Personen entwickelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","text":"Das Gebot der Nächstenliebe fungiert als diagnostischer Zugang zu einer primären menschlichen Feindseligkeit, die moralisch überdeckt werden soll.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS4","text":"Die Kultur erscheint als Zwangsapparat zur Begrenzung, Umlenkung und Bindung von Aggression, weil Arbeitsinteressen allein keine dauerhafte Gemeinschaft sichern.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","text":"Die kommunistische Eigentumskritik wird zurückgewiesen, soweit sie Eigentum als Ursache statt als Werkzeug menschlicher Aggression behandelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS6","text":"Die Argumentbewegung endet bei einer Grenze der Reform: Kultur kann vermeidbares Leid mindern, aber nicht notwendig die triebhaften Bedingungen aufheben, durch die sie selbst erforderlich wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A1","text":"Versagungen sexueller Befriedigung können Ersatzbefriedigungen erzeugen, die neues Leiden und soziale Schwierigkeiten hervorbringen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2","text":"Die Libido widersteht der Aufgabe älterer Besetzungen zugunsten neuer Positionen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","text":"Erotische Liebe ist wesentlich eine Bindung zwischen zwei Personen, in der ein Dritter überflüssig oder störend wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","text":"Kultur beruht auf Beziehungen zwischen einer größeren Anzahl von Menschen und kann nicht allein durch Arbeits- und Interessengemeinschaft stabilisiert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","text":"Die Herstellung umfassender Gemeinschaftsbindungen verlangt die Umlenkung libidinöser Energie in Identifizierungen und zielgehemmte Liebesbeziehungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","text":"Die kulturelle Umlenkung der Libido macht Einschränkungen des unmittelbaren Sexuallebens unvermeidlich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","text":"Der Mensch verfügt neben seinen Bindungs- und Liebesfähigkeiten über eine mächtige, unter günstigen Bedingungen spontan hervortretende Aggressionsneigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","text":"Primäre wechselseitige Feindseligkeit bedroht den Bestand der Kultur, weil triebhafte Leidenschaften stärker sein können als vernünftige Arbeitsinteressen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","text":"Kultur begrenzt Aggression durch Verbote, psychische Reaktionsbildungen, Identifizierung und zielgehemmte Liebesbindungen, ohne sie vollständig kontrollieren zu können.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","text":"Privateigentum ist ein Mittel der Aggression, nicht deren Ursprung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","text":"Innere Gemeinschaftsbindung kann durch die gegen Außenstehende gerichtete Befriedigung von Aggression erleichtert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","text":"Kultur erkauft Sicherheit durch Einschränkung von Sexualität und Aggression und vermindert dadurch Möglichkeiten unmittelbarer Triebbefriedigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13","text":"Manche Schwierigkeiten der Kultur können ihrem Wesen anhaften und daher keinem Reformversuch vollständig weichen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14","text":"Eine vorwiegend durch gegenseitige Identifizierung erzeugte Gemeinschaft kann psychologisches Massenelend hervorbringen, wenn Führerindividualitäten keine entsprechende Bedeutung erhalten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX1","text":"Kultur ist nicht notwendig mit jeder sexuellen Befriedigung unvereinbar; eine bloß arbeits- und interessenverbundene Gemeinschaft libidinös gesättigter Paare bleibt jedoch ein nicht verwirklichter Grenzfall.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX2","text":"Erotische Liebe ist keine unmittelbar verallgemeinerbare Grundlage für eine große Gemeinschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX3","text":"Der Fremde ist nicht von sich aus ein Gegenstand gleicher Liebe, weil Liebe an Ähnlichkeit, Idealisierung, Bindung oder Gegenseitigkeit geknüpft sein kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX4","text":"Der Mensch ist nicht ursprünglich ein sanftes, nur bei Angriff zur Verteidigung bereites Wesen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX5","text":"Aggression ist nicht bloß eine Reaktion auf Eigentumsungleichheit oder materielle Not.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX6","text":"Rechtliche Gewalt verhindert nicht die feineren und vorsichtigeren Ausdrucksformen menschlicher Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX7","text":"Streit und Wettkampf sind nicht notwendig mit Feindschaft identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX8","text":"Die vermeintlich triebfreie vormoderne oder primitive Lebensform ist kein tragfähiges Gegenbild kultureller Einschränkung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D1","text":"Sexuelle Einschränkung erzeugt nicht nur Entbehrung, sondern kann bei ihrer symptomatischen Verarbeitung zusätzliche individuelle und soziale Leidensformen hervorbringen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D2","text":"Die Spannung zwischen Kultur und Sexualität entsteht, weil Kultur Libido aus exklusiven Zweierbindungen in breit verteilte, weniger unmittelbar sexuelle Bindungen überführen muss.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D3","text":"Das Gebot der Nächstenliebe wird als kulturelle Gegenmaßnahme gegen menschliche Aggression lesbar, gerade weil seine Erfüllung der spontanen Disposition widerspricht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D4","text":"Eine unterschiedslose ethische Liebe kann kulturelle Zwecke schädigen, wenn sie Ausbeutung und Böswilligkeit ohne Veränderung ihrer Bedingungen gleich behandelt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D5","text":"Die Abschaffung des Privateigentums entzieht Aggression ein wichtiges Werkzeug, lässt aber Machtunterschiede, sexuelle Rivalität und den aggressiven Trieb selbst bestehen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D6","text":"Gruppen können innere Liebe und Identifizierung dadurch stabilisieren, dass Aggression auf außenstehende Gruppen abgeleitet wird.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D7","text":"Die Kultur kann rohe Gewalt begrenzen, bleibt aber gegenüber verdeckter, sozial angepasster oder institutionell nicht erfassbarer Aggression strukturell unzureichend.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D8","text":"Reformen können vermeidbares Kulturleid reduzieren, können aber die aus notwendiger Triebeinschränkung hervorgehenden Konflikte nicht notwendig abschaffen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D9","text":"Die Bindungsform der Identifizierung kann selbst zum kulturellen Risiko werden, wenn sie die psychische Struktur einer Masse ohne hinreichende Führerfunktion organisiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","text":"Kultur operiert als System der Umverteilung von Libido und Aggression: unmittelbare Sexualität wird eingeschränkt, Libido wird sozial gebunden, Aggression wird gehemmt, umgeleitet oder externalisiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD2","text":"Universale Liebesethik enthält eine strukturelle Umkehrung, weil die Herstellung innerer Solidarität gerade die Ausgrenzung oder Befeindung eines Außen begünstigen kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3","text":"Eine politische Ordnung kann Aggression in ihren Mitteln verändern, aber nicht dadurch aufheben, dass sie Eigentumsverhältnisse allein reorganisiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD4","text":"Das Verhältnis von Freiheit, Glück und Sicherheit ist keine einfache historische Fortschrittsformel, weil Triebfreiheit ungleich verteilt und auch außerhalb der modernen Kultur durch andere Beschränkungen begrenzt war.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","text":"Die Instrumente, durch die Kultur Aggression eindämmt, können selbst neue Pathologien erzeugen: äußere Feindbilder im Fall der Gemeinschaftsbildung und Massenelend im Fall dominanter Identifizierung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen wird die Annahme, dass rationale Interessen und Arbeitsteilung von selbst eine dauerhafte friedliche Gesellschaft erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen wird die Annahme, dass menschliche Feindseligkeit historisch aus Eigentum hervorgehe und mit dessen Abschaffung verschwinde.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen wird die Annahme, dass Sexualität vollständig privat und uneingeschränkt bleiben könne, während Kultur zugleich intensive affektive Bindungen zwischen vielen Menschen herstellt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen wird die Annahme, dass ein moralisches Gebot seine eigenen psychischen Vollzugsbedingungen erzeugen könne.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX5","text":"Ausgeschlossen wird die Annahme, dass Kulturkritik in eine vollständige Befreiung von Triebeinschränkung überführt werden könne.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX1","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine dauerhafte Großgemeinschaft, deren innere Bindung keine Einschränkung der Sexualität und keine Umlenkung von Aggression erfordert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX2","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine universale Liebe, die alle Menschen gleichermaßen bindet, ohne einen Rest von Feindschaft, Ausschluss oder aggressiver Ersatzbefriedigung zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX3","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine politische Reform, die Sicherheit, freie Triebbefriedigung und konfliktfreie Gleichheit endgültig zur Deckung bringt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX4","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine reine Identifikationsgemeinschaft, die weder äußere Feindbilder noch psychologisches Massenelend hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS1","text":"Sexuelle Versagung und Libidoträgheit erzeugen eine Ausgangslage, in der der Wechsel von exklusiver Besetzung zu neuen sozialen Bindungen Widerstand auslöst.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS2","text":"Dyadische erotische Liebe kollidiert mit der Ausdehnung von Beziehungen auf eine größere Zahl von Menschen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS3","text":"Kultur beantwortet diesen Konflikt durch die Umleitung von Libido in Identifizierung und zielgehemmte Liebe und setzt damit Sexualeinschränkung voraus.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS4","text":"Die Prüfung des Gebots der Nächstenliebe legt offen, dass der Fremde nicht spontan als Liebesobjekt erscheint.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS5","text":"Die fehlende spontane Nächstenliebe wird als Ausdruck primärer Aggression bestimmt, die den kulturellen Verband gefährdet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS6","text":"Kultur reagiert auf diese Gefahr durch Hemmung, psychische Umformung und Umlenkung der Aggression, ohne deren vollständige Beseitigung zu erreichen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS7","text":"Die Eigentumsaufhebung wird als institutioneller Testfall behandelt und verworfen, weil sie das aggressive Substrat nicht entfernt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8","text":"Die Externalisierung von Aggression stabilisiert partielle Gemeinschaften, verwandelt universale Bindungsansprüche jedoch in ein Problem von Ausschluss und Intoleranz.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9","text":"Kultur bleibt deshalb ein Sicherheitsgewinn unter Kosten von Glück, Triebbefriedigung und möglicher psychischer Selbstschädigung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF1","text":"Sexuelle Versagung → Ersatzbefriedigung und Leiden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF2","text":"Dyadische Liebe → Unverträglichkeit mit der Ausweitung affektiver Bindung auf die Kulturgruppe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF3","text":"Kulturelle Bindungsforderung → Identifizierung, zielgehemmte Liebe und Einschränkung unmittelbarer Sexualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF4","text":"Prüfung der Nächstenliebe → Diagnose der primären Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF5","text":"Primäre Aggression → kulturelle Hemmungs-, Umlenkungs- und Gewaltapparate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF6","text":"Eigentumskritik → Trennung von aggressivem Werkzeug und aggressivem Ursprung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF7","text":"Innere Bindung durch äußere Feindseligkeit → Entlarvung der Ausschlussseite universaler Liebe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF8","text":"Triebverzicht und unvollständige Kontrolle → Grenze kultureller Reform und Risiko des psychologischen Massenelends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME1","text":"Kultur wird von einer Ordnung vernünftiger Kooperation in ein System der libidinösen Bindungsproduktion und Aggressionsverwaltung überführt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2","text":"Nächstenliebe wird von einer autonomen ethischen Forderung in ein Symptom und Instrument kultureller Aggressionsabwehr umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME3","text":"Eigentum wird als historisch und politisch bedeutsames Medium der Aggression sichtbar, ohne als deren psychische Quelle gelten zu können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME4","text":"Gruppenidentität und Außenfeindschaft erscheinen nicht als entgegengesetzte, sondern als funktional miteinander verschränkte Prozesse.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME5","text":"Kulturkritik wird in vermeidbare institutionelle Mängel und möglicherweise unreformierbare Triebkosten der Kultur geteilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME6","text":"Identifizierung erscheint zugleich als kulturelles Bindungsmittel und als mögliche Ursache psychologischen Massenelends.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT1","text":"Surface — Das Kapitel behandelt sexuelle Versagung, Nächstenliebe, Aggression, Eigentum, Gruppenfeindschaft und kulturelles Unbehagen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT2","text":"Structural — Kultur stabilisiert sich durch die Verteilung von Libido auf soziale Bindungen und durch die Begrenzung einer fortbestehenden Aggressionsneigung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Ethische Gebote und politische Erlösungsmodelle werden nicht an ihren Idealen, sondern an den psychischen Bedingungen ihrer Durchsetzbarkeit geprüft.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Menschliche Kultur wird als dauerhaftes Konfliktverhältnis zwischen Triebanspruch, sozialer Bindung, Sicherheit und nicht abschließbarer Aggression gefasst.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von sexueller Einschränkung über die Diagnose der Aggression bis zur Grenze politischer und kultureller Reform zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT2","text":"Die Herkunft der angenommenen Aggressionsneigung bleibt innerhalb des Kapitels unterbestimmt; sie wird durch Erfahrung und Geschichte gestützt, aber nicht metapsychologisch hergeleitet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT3","text":"Die biologische Vermutung einer organischen Grundlage fortschreitender Sexualverdrängung bleibt ausdrücklich ungesichert und trägt die Hauptarchitektur nicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste argumentative Verbindung liegt in der Überführung des Liebesgebots in einen Hinweis auf jene Aggression, deren kulturelle Eindämmung es zugleich leisten soll.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT5","text":"Die zentrale Bruchlinie besteht darin, dass Kultur Identifizierung und Liebe zur Überwindung von Aggression benötigt, dieselben Bindungen aber durch äußere Feindbilder stabilisieren kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT6","text":"Eine zweite Bruchlinie liegt darin, dass Kultur Gewalt eindämmen soll, zugleich aber selbst Gewalt gegen Gewalttäter beansprucht und feinere Aggression nicht erfassen kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT7","text":"Die Grenze zwischen reformierbarem Kulturleid und wesensnotwendiger Triebeinschränkung wird behauptet, aber nicht durch ein Kriterium bestimmt, das beide eindeutig trennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT8","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung des Kapitels, sofern die Aggressionsannahme als Bedingung der gesamten Maschine und nicht als nachträgliches Beispiel behandelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171315039879Z_248e6b75","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter V","source_sha256":"90b8c88d6542a59a161f3e235718066bf22f209ac26fdc7b04587ed05dea1543","sha256":"34dbb54271d7f0b7fdb37d2f9cf9cb19d860162d86acc36ef2357f75027a83f7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:13:15.040769+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS1","text":"The chapter determines cultural discontent as a consequence of instinctual renunciation, which affects sexuality and aggression simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS2","text":"The opposition between culture and sexuality is developed from the tension between dyadic erotic attachment and the extension of social ties to many persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","text":"The commandment of love of one's neighbor functions as a diagnostic approach to a primary human hostility that is to be morally covered over.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS4","text":"Culture appears as an apparatus of compulsion for limiting, redirecting, and binding aggression, because work interests alone do not secure a lasting community.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","text":"The communist critique of property is rejected insofar as it treats property as the cause rather than the instrument of human aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument ends at a limit of reform: culture can reduce avoidable suffering, but cannot necessarily abolish the instinctual conditions through which it itself becomes necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A1","text":"Frustrations of sexual satisfaction can produce substitute satisfactions that bring forth new suffering and social difficulties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2","text":"Libido resists the relinquishment of older cathexes in favor of new positions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","text":"Erotic love is essentially a bond between two persons, in which a third becomes superfluous or disruptive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","text":"Culture rests on relations among a larger number of human beings and cannot be stabilized by communities of work and interest alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","text":"The production of comprehensive communal bonds requires the redirection of libidinal energy into identifications and aim-inhibited love relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","text":"The cultural redirection of libido renders restrictions on immediate sexual life unavoidable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","text":"Alongside his capacities for attachment and love, the human being possesses a powerful inclination to aggression that emerges spontaneously under favorable conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","text":"Primary mutual hostility threatens the persistence of culture because instinctual passions can be stronger than rational work interests.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","text":"Culture limits aggression through prohibitions, psychological reaction-formations, identification, and aim-inhibited love bonds, without being able to control it completely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","text":"Private property is a means of aggression, not its origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","text":"Internal communal attachment can be facilitated through the satisfaction of aggression directed against outsiders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","text":"Culture purchases security through the restriction of sexuality and aggression and thereby diminishes possibilities of immediate instinctual satisfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13","text":"Some difficulties of culture may adhere to its essence and therefore not fully yield to any attempt at reform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14","text":"A community produced predominantly through mutual identification can bring forth psychological mass misery if leader individualities are not accorded corresponding significance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX1","text":"Culture is not necessarily incompatible with every sexual satisfaction; yet a community of libidinally satiated couples connected merely by work and interests remains an unrealized limiting case.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX2","text":"Erotic love is not an immediately generalizable foundation for a large community.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX3","text":"The stranger is not inherently an object of equal love, because love may be bound to similarity, idealization, attachment, or reciprocity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX4","text":"The human being is not originally a gentle creature prepared for defense only when attacked.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX5","text":"Aggression is not merely a reaction to inequality of property or material hardship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX6","text":"Legal violence does not prevent the subtler and more cautious forms of expression of human aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX7","text":"Dispute and competition are not necessarily identical with hostility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX8","text":"The purportedly instinct-free premodern or primitive form of life is not a viable counterimage to cultural restriction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D1","text":"Sexual restriction produces not only deprivation, but can, in its symptomatic processing, give rise to additional individual and social forms of suffering.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D2","text":"The tension between culture and sexuality arises because culture must transfer libido from exclusive dyadic bonds into widely distributed, less immediately sexual bonds.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D3","text":"The commandment of love of one's neighbor becomes legible as a cultural countermeasure against human aggression, precisely because its fulfillment contradicts the spontaneous disposition.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D4","text":"An indiscriminate ethical love can harm cultural purposes when it treats exploitation and malice equally without altering their conditions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D5","text":"The abolition of private property deprives aggression of an important instrument, but leaves differences of power, sexual rivalry, and the aggressive instinct itself intact.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D6","text":"Groups can stabilize internal love and identification by diverting aggression onto groups standing outside.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D7","text":"Culture can limit crude violence, but remains structurally inadequate in relation to concealed, socially adapted, or institutionally ungraspable aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D8","text":"Reforms can reduce avoidable cultural suffering, but cannot necessarily abolish the conflicts arising from necessary instinctual restriction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:D9","text":"The bonding form of identification can itself become a cultural risk when it organizes the psychological structure of a mass without a sufficient leadership function.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","text":"Culture operates as a system for the redistribution of libido and aggression: immediate sexuality is restricted, libido is socially bound, and aggression is inhibited, redirected, or externalized.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD2","text":"Universal ethics of love contains a structural reversal, because the production of internal solidarity can precisely favor the exclusion or enmity of an outside.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3","text":"A political order can alter aggression in its means, but cannot abolish it by reorganizing property relations alone.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD4","text":"The relation of freedom, happiness, and security is not a simple formula of historical progress, because instinctual freedom was unequally distributed and was also limited outside modern culture by other restrictions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0072","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","text":"The instruments through which culture curbs aggression can themselves produce new pathologies: external enemy-images in the case of community formation and mass misery in the case of dominant identification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX1","text":"Excluded is the assumption that rational interests and the division of labor by themselves produce a lasting peaceful society.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX2","text":"Excluded is the assumption that human hostility historically arises from property and disappears with its abolition.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX3","text":"Excluded is the assumption that sexuality can remain entirely private and unrestricted while culture simultaneously produces intensive affective bonds among many people.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX4","text":"Excluded is the assumption that a moral commandment can produce its own psychic conditions of enactment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX5","text":"Excluded is the assumption that cultural critique can be transformed into a complete liberation from instinctual restriction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX1","text":"Unavailable is a lasting large community whose internal bond requires neither a restriction of sexuality nor a redirection of aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX2","text":"Unavailable is a universal love that binds all human beings equally without producing a remnant of hostility, exclusion, or aggressive substitute satisfaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX3","text":"Unavailable is a political reform that definitively brings security, free instinctual satisfaction, and conflict-free equality into coincidence.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX4","text":"Unavailable is a pure community of identification that produces neither external enemy-images nor psychological mass misery.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS1","text":"Sexual frustration and the inertia of libido produce an initial situation in which the shift from exclusive cathexis to new social bonds provokes resistance.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS2","text":"Dyadic erotic love collides with the extension of relations to a larger number of people.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS3","text":"Culture answers this conflict by redirecting libido into identification and aim-inhibited love and thereby presupposes sexual restriction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS4","text":"Examination of the commandment of love of one's neighbor reveals that the stranger does not spontaneously appear as an object of love.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS5","text":"The absence of spontaneous neighborly love is determined as the expression of primary aggression, which endangers the cultural association.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS6","text":"Culture responds to this danger through inhibition, psychic transformation, and redirection of aggression, without achieving its complete elimination.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS7","text":"The abolition of property is treated as an institutional test case and rejected because it does not remove the aggressive substrate.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8","text":"The externalization of aggression stabilizes partial communities, but transforms universal claims of attachment into a problem of exclusion and intolerance.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9","text":"Culture therefore remains a gain in security at the cost of happiness, instinctual satisfaction, and possible psychic self-injury.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF1","text":"Sexual frustration → substitute satisfaction and suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF2","text":"Dyadic love → incompatibility with the extension of affective attachment to the cultural group.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF3","text":"Cultural demand for attachment → identification, aim-inhibited love, and restriction of immediate sexuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF4","text":"Examination of neighborly love → diagnosis of primary aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF5","text":"Primary aggression → cultural apparatuses of inhibition, redirection, and violence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF6","text":"Critique of property → separation of aggressive instrument and aggressive origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF7","text":"Internal attachment through external hostility → unmasking of the exclusionary side of universal love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:AF8","text":"Instinctual renunciation and incomplete control → limit of cultural reform and risk of psychological mass misery.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME1","text":"Culture is transformed from an order of rational cooperation into a system of libidinal bond production and aggression management.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2","text":"Love of one's neighbor is reclassified from an autonomous ethical demand into a symptom and instrument of cultural defense against aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME3","text":"Property becomes visible as a historically and politically significant medium of aggression, without being able to count as its psychic source.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME4","text":"Group identity and hostility toward outsiders appear not as opposed, but as functionally interwoven processes.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME5","text":"Cultural critique is divided into avoidable institutional deficiencies and possibly irreformable instinctual costs of culture.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME6","text":"Identification appears simultaneously as a cultural means of attachment and as a possible cause of psychological mass misery.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0074","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT1","text":"Surface — The chapter addresses sexual frustration, love of one's neighbor, aggression, property, group hostility, and cultural discontent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT2","text":"Structural — Culture stabilizes itself through the distribution of libido onto social bonds and through the limitation of a persisting inclination to aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Ethical commandments and political models of redemption are examined not according to their ideals, but according to the psychic conditions of their enforceability.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Human culture is conceived as an enduring relation of conflict between instinctual claim, social attachment, security, and non-finalizable aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from sexual restriction through the diagnosis of aggression to the limit of political and cultural reform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT2","text":"The origin of the assumed inclination to aggression remains underdetermined within the chapter; it is supported by experience and history, but not metapsychologically derived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT3","text":"The biological conjecture of an organic basis for progressive sexual repression remains expressly unsecured and does not bear the main architecture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT4","text":"The strongest argumentative connection lies in transforming the commandment of love into an indication of that aggression whose cultural containment it is simultaneously meant to accomplish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT5","text":"The central fault line consists in the fact that culture requires identification and love to overcome aggression, but can stabilize these same bonds through external enemy-images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT6","text":"A second fault line lies in the fact that culture is meant to curb violence, yet simultaneously claims violence against violent offenders and cannot grasp subtler aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT7","text":"The boundary between reformable cultural suffering and instinctual restriction necessary to its essence is asserted, but not determined by a criterion that clearly distinguishes the two.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the chapter insofar as the assumption of aggression is treated as the condition of the entire machine and not as a retrospective example.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KAPV:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KAPV@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KAPV:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 05","title":"Chapter V","context":"Chapter 05","original_title":"Kapitel V","original_context":"Chapter 05"},"original_title":"Kapitel V","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5","layer":"CH","title":"Chapter VI","order":6,"parents":["RAW_R2TV_KA_5"],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_5@R001","sha256":"628d035cb30851ad698b902c3a63416457cc675bf0c84323178d4ee5216a33d0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS1","text":"Der Text behandelt die Anerkennung eines selbständigen Aggressionstriebes als Präzisierung einer bereits vollzogenen Umformung der Trieblehre, nicht als deren Bruch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS2","text":"Die narzißtische Besetzung des Ichs hebt die ursprüngliche Gegenüberstellung von Ichtrieben und Objekttrieben als hinreichende Grundordnung auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS3","text":"Der verbleibende Unterschied zwischen Triebarten erzwingt eine Dualisierung in verbindenden Eros und auflösenden Todestrieb.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4","text":"Aggression wird als nach außen gewandte Erscheinungsform des Todestriebs bestimmt, während ihre Rückwendung die Selbstzerstörung verstärkt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS5","text":"Kultur wird als erotischer Einigungsprozeß bestimmt, dessen Programm durch die ursprüngliche menschliche Aggressionsneigung konstitutiv widerstanden wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","text":"Die Kulturentwicklung wird als geschichtliche Vollzugsform des allgemeinen Kampfes zwischen Eros und Todestrieb gefaßt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A1","text":"Eine Trieblehre muß die Grundkräfte bestimmen, durch welche Leben erhalten, organisiert und verändert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","text":"Das Ich ist ursprünglich mit Libido besetzt und kann Libido auf Objekte richten oder von ihnen wieder zu sich zurückziehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A3","text":"Die Libidinisierung des Ichs erlaubt keine vollständige Gleichsetzung aller Triebenergie mit Libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","text":"Eros erhält lebende Substanz und faßt sie zu immer größeren Einheiten zusammen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","text":"Neben Eros wirkt ein Todestrieb, der Einheiten auflöst und auf den anorganischen Zustand zurückführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A6","text":"Eros und Todestrieb treten gewöhnlich nur in wechselnden Mischungsverhältnissen auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","text":"Aggression und Destruktion sind die gegen die Außenwelt gewendete Tätigkeit des Todestriebs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8","text":"Die Rückwendung der Aggression nach innen steigert die Selbstzerstörung des Lebewesens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","text":"Die menschliche Aggressionsneigung ist eine ursprüngliche und selbständige Triebanlage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","text":"Kultur ist ein im Dienst des Eros stehender Prozeß zur libidinösen Bindung einzelner Menschen zu einer Menschheitseinheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11","text":"Arbeitsnotwendigkeit und Arbeitsvorteil genügen nicht, um menschliche Mengen dauerhaft zusammenzuhalten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12","text":"Der natürliche Aggressionstrieb widersetzt sich dem kulturellen Einigungsprogramm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","text":"Der Todestrieb ist theoretisch notwendig, bleibt aber ohne seine Mischung mit Eros nur schwer empirisch faßbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX1","text":"Aggression ist nicht bloß eine gefährliche oder feindselige Seite der Liebe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX2","text":"Destruktion ist nicht restlos als Libido oder Sexualität erklärbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX3","text":"Der Todestrieb ist nicht unmittelbar durch seine isolierte Beobachtung nachweisbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX4","text":"Sadismus und Masochismus sind nicht einfache Sexualphänomene, sondern Mischformen erotischer und destruktiver Strebungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX5","text":"Kultur ist nicht durch Nutzen, Zwang oder Arbeitsgemeinschaft allein begründbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX6","text":"Der Mensch ist nicht von einer ursprünglich harmonischen oder ausschließlich sittlichen Natur bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX7","text":"Kulturentwicklung ist nicht als fortschreitende Aufhebung des Konflikts zwischen Bindung und Zerstörung bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D1","text":"Die Unterscheidung zwischen Ichtrieben und Objekttrieben verliert ihren Status als grundlegende Triebdifferenz, weil beide libidinös besetzt sein können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D2","text":"Sadismus und Masochismus werden zu privilegierten Indikatoren der sonst schwer sichtbaren Mischung von Eros und Todestrieb.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D3","text":"Die nach außen gerichtete Destruktion entlastet das Individuum teilweise von der gegen sich selbst gerichteten Auflösungstendenz.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D4","text":"Die Befriedigung destruktiver Aggression kann narzißtischen Gewinn erzeugen, weil sie dem Ich Allmachtswünsche erfüllt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D5","text":"Die kulturelle Bindung der Menschen verlangt libidinöse Beziehungen, weil bloße Zweckgemeinschaften der Aggression nicht standhalten.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D6","text":"Aggression ist zugleich Voraussetzung individueller Naturbeherrschung und Hindernis kollektiver Einigung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7","text":"Die Kulturentwicklung ist keine autonome soziale Dynamik, sondern die artspezifische Austragung eines vorausgesetzten Triebdualismus.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1","text":"Das Soziale wird als sekundäre Erscheinung einer ontologischen Triebantinomie kartiert: kulturelle Institutionen bearbeiten einen Konflikt, den sie nicht erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD2","text":"Kultur kann Aggression weder durch moralische Aufklärung noch durch Nutzenkalkül endgültig beseitigen, weil ihre Widerstandskraft triebhaft und ursprünglich bestimmt ist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3","text":"Jede kulturelle Bindung bleibt ambivalent, weil dieselbe Triebökonomie, die äußere Destruktion hemmen kann, Destruktion nach innen verlagern kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4","text":"Die Theorie gewinnt Erklärungsreichweite durch einen nicht direkt sichtbaren Rest: Der Todestrieb fungiert als notwendige Ursache gerade dort, wo die Erscheinungen nicht libidinös aufgehen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD5","text":"Der Begriff des Lebens wird nicht als Einheit, sondern als dauerhafte Konfliktform bestimmt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX1","text":"Das System setzt voraus, daß eine monistische Theorie des Begehrens oder der Liebe die destruktive Realität nicht zureichend erklären kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX2","text":"Das System schließt aus, daß gesellschaftliche Feindseligkeit primär aus äußeren Umständen, Knappheit oder fehlerhafter Organisation hervorgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX3","text":"Das System verwirft implizit die Annahme, Kultur könne auf einem natürlichen Einklang zwischen individueller Selbsterhaltung und kollektiver Vereinigung beruhen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","text":"Das System setzt voraus, daß direkte Sichtbarkeit kein Kriterium theoretischer Wirklichkeit ist, weil das maßgebliche Destruktive meist nur in Mischformen erscheint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Verfügbarkeit eines konfliktfreien Endzustands, in dem menschliche Bindung nicht mehr gegen Destruktion errungen werden müßte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein kulturelles Außen gegenüber dem Triebkonflikt; Kultur bleibt dessen Vollzugsform und nicht seine Überwindung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine vollständig positive Erkenntnis des Todestriebs; er ist nur indirekt, residual und über seine Legierungen zugänglich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS1","text":"Ich-/Objekttrieb-Dualismus → Narzißmus → Libidinisierung des Ichs → Verlust der ursprünglichen Trennlinie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS2","text":"Rest nichtlibidinöser Triebqualität → Wiederholungszwang und Konservatismus → Eros/Todestrieb-Dualismus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS3","text":"Todestrieb → Außenwendung → Aggression und Destruktion; Innenwendung → gesteigerte Selbstzerstörung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS4","text":"Triebmischung → eingeschränkte Beobachtbarkeit → Sadismus und Masochismus als Erscheinungsformen der Legierung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS5","text":"Eros als Einigungsprinzip → Kultur als libidinöse Bindungsarbeit → Aggression als struktureller Widerstand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS6","text":"Triebdualismus auf Ebene des Individuums → Übertragung auf die Menschheitsgeschichte → Kulturentwicklung als Lebenskampf der Art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF1","text":"Unzureichender Ich-/Objekttrieb-Gegensatz → Narzißmus → Krise des Libidobegriffs → Annahme qualitativer Triebverschiedenheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF2","text":"Qualitative Triebverschiedenheit → Eros/Todestrieb-Dualismus → Aggression als externalisierte Destruktion → Selbstzerstörung als internalisierte Destruktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF3","text":"Aggression als ursprüngliche Anlage → Kultur als erosgeleitete Einigung → antagonistische Gegenkraft → Kulturentwicklung als unabschließbarer Kampf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME1","text":"Die Differenz zwischen Selbst- und Objektbezug wird von einer Unterscheidung der Triebziele zu einer Bewegungsform derselben Libido umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME2","text":"Aggression wird von einer akzidentiellen Reaktion oder moralischen Abweichung zu einer ursprünglichen Triebfunktion umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME3","text":"Sadismus und Masochismus werden nicht länger als Randphänomene der Sexualität behandelt, sondern als diagnostische Knotenpunkte des Triebdualismus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4","text":"Kultur wird nicht als Gegenpol der Natur, sondern als spezifische Organisation eines naturhaften Triebkonflikts sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME5","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen individueller Zerstörung und sozialer Ordnung wird durch die Einsicht ersetzt, daß beide durch Umleitung derselben destruktiven Energie verbunden sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der Text begründet die Annahme eines selbständigen Aggressions- und Destruktionstriebs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT2","text":"Structural — Kultur erscheint als libidinöse Integrationsarbeit unter permanentem Widerstand einer ursprünglichen destruktiven Anlage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Die Analyse verschiebt die Erklärung sozialer Konflikte von Nutzen-, Moral- und Organisationsmodellen auf die Verwaltung unaufhebbarer Triebambivalenz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Leben und Geschichte werden als fortdauernde Auseinandersetzung zwischen Einheitsbildung und Rückführung ins Anorganische bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von der Krise des frühen Triebd Dualismus zur Kulturtheorie des Eros-Todestrieb-Konflikts zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wie der Todestrieb unabhängig von seinen Legierungen empirisch identifiziert werden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT3","text":"Die interne Kohärenz ist konditional: Sie besteht, wenn die theoretische Notwendigkeit eines nichtlibidinösen Restes als zureichender Grund für den Todestrieb akzeptiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Schließung liegt in der Verbindung von Triebdualismus, Aggressionsbegriff und Kulturprozeß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5","text":"Die stärkste Bruchlinie liegt zwischen der behaupteten Ursprünglichkeit der Aggression und der nur indirekten, gemischten Beobachtbarkeit ihres Triebgrundes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT6","text":"Eine weitere Spannung besteht darin, daß Aggression zugleich als destruktive Gegenmacht der Kultur und als für Selbsterhaltung und Naturbeherrschung nutzbar bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung, sofern Kultur nicht als eigenständige Sozialtheorie, sondern als artspezifische Projektion des allgemeinen Triebkonflikts gelesen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171509605732Z_8553112d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter VI","source_sha256":"628d035cb30851ad698b902c3a63416457cc675bf0c84323178d4ee5216a33d0","sha256":"196b94441d567e4cdffdb26a31312e5d1a9ca0ed88e92b926b7b591ebe3158fb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:15:09.607654+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS1","text":"The text treats the recognition of an independent aggressive drive as a specification of an already accomplished transformation of drive theory, not as a rupture with it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS2","text":"The narcissistic cathexis of the ego abolishes the original opposition between ego drives and object drives as a sufficient basic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS3","text":"The remaining difference between types of drives necessitates a dualization into binding Eros and the dissolving death drive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4","text":"Aggression is determined as the outwardly directed manifestation of the death drive, while its turning back intensifies self-destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS5","text":"Civilization is determined as an erotic process of unification whose program is constitutively resisted by the original human inclination to aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","text":"The development of civilization is conceived as the historical mode of enactment of the general struggle between Eros and the death drive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A1","text":"A theory of drives must determine the fundamental forces through which life is preserved, organized, and transformed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","text":"The ego is originally cathected with libido and can direct libido toward objects or withdraw it from them back to itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A3","text":"The libidinization of the ego does not permit a complete identification of all drive energy with libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","text":"Eros preserves living substance and combines it into ever larger units.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","text":"Alongside Eros operates a death drive that dissolves units and leads back to the inorganic state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A6","text":"Eros and the death drive ordinarily occur only in changing proportions of mixture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","text":"Aggression and destruction are the activity of the death drive directed against the external world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8","text":"The turning of aggression inward increases the self-destruction of the living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","text":"The human inclination to aggression is an original and independent drive disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","text":"Civilization is a process in the service of Eros, aimed at the libidinal binding of individual human beings into a unity of humanity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11","text":"The necessity of work and the advantage of work do not suffice to hold human multitudes together permanently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12","text":"The natural aggressive drive resists the civilizational program of unification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","text":"The death drive is theoretically necessary, but without its mixture with Eros it remains difficult to grasp empirically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX1","text":"Aggression is not merely a dangerous or hostile side of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX2","text":"Destruction cannot be explained exhaustively as libido or sexuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX3","text":"The death drive cannot be demonstrated directly through its isolated observation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX4","text":"Sadism and masochism are not simple sexual phenomena, but mixed forms of erotic and destructive strivings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX5","text":"Civilization cannot be grounded in utility, compulsion, or the work community alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX6","text":"The human being is not determined by an originally harmonious or exclusively moral nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX7","text":"The development of civilization is not determined as a progressive abolition of the conflict between binding and destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D1","text":"The distinction between ego drives and object drives loses its status as a fundamental drive difference because both can be libidinally cathected.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D2","text":"Sadism and masochism become privileged indicators of the otherwise difficult-to-see mixture of Eros and the death drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D3","text":"Destruction directed outward partially relieves the individual of the tendency toward dissolution directed against itself.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D4","text":"The satisfaction of destructive aggression can produce narcissistic gain because it fulfills wishes for omnipotence in the ego.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D5","text":"The civilizational binding of human beings requires libidinal relationships because mere communities of purpose cannot withstand aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D6","text":"Aggression is at once a precondition of individual mastery over nature and an obstacle to collective unification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7","text":"The development of civilization is not an autonomous social dynamic, but the species-specific enactment of a presupposed drive dualism.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1","text":"The social is mapped as a secondary manifestation of an ontological antinomy of drives: civilizational institutions work upon a conflict that they do not produce.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD2","text":"Civilization can definitively eliminate aggression neither through moral enlightenment nor through calculations of utility, because its force of resistance is determined instinctually and originally.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3","text":"Every civilizational bond remains ambivalent because the same drive economy that can inhibit external destruction can displace destruction inward.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4","text":"The theory gains explanatory scope through a residue not directly visible: the death drive functions as a necessary cause precisely where phenomena cannot be exhausted by the libidinal.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD5","text":"The concept of life is determined not as unity, but as an enduring form of conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX1","text":"The system presupposes that a monistic theory of desire or love cannot adequately explain destructive reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that social hostility arises primarily from external circumstances, scarcity, or defective organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX3","text":"The system implicitly rejects the assumption that civilization could rest upon a natural harmony between individual self-preservation and collective unification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","text":"The system presupposes that direct visibility is not a criterion of theoretical reality, because the decisive destructive element usually appears only in mixed forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1","text":"Excluded is the availability of a conflict-free final state in which human binding would no longer have to be wrested from destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX2","text":"Excluded is a cultural outside in relation to the drive conflict; civilization remains its mode of enactment and not its overcoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3","text":"Excluded is a fully positive cognition of the death drive; it is accessible only indirectly, residually, and through its alloys.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS1","text":"Ego-/object-drive dualism → narcissism → libidinization of the ego → loss of the original line of separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS2","text":"Residue of non-libidinal drive quality → compulsion to repeat and conservatism → Eros/death-drive dualism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS3","text":"Death drive → outward direction → aggression and destruction; inward direction → intensified self-destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS4","text":"Mixture of drives → restricted observability → sadism and masochism as manifestations of the alloy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS5","text":"Eros as principle of unification → civilization as libidinal work of binding → aggression as structural resistance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS6","text":"Drive dualism at the level of the individual → transfer to the history of humanity → development of civilization as the life-struggle of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF1","text":"Inadequate ego-/object-drive opposition → narcissism → crisis of the concept of libido → assumption of qualitative drive difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF2","text":"Qualitative drive difference → Eros/death-drive dualism → aggression as externalized destruction → self-destruction as internalized destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF3","text":"Aggression as original disposition → civilization as Eros-guided unification → antagonistic counterforce → development of civilization as an unfinishable struggle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME1","text":"The difference between self-reference and object-reference is reclassified from a distinction of drive aims into a mode of movement of the same libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME2","text":"Aggression is reclassified from an accidental reaction or moral deviation into an original drive function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME3","text":"Sadism and masochism are no longer treated as marginal phenomena of sexuality, but as diagnostic nodes of drive dualism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4","text":"Civilization becomes visible not as the opposite pole of nature, but as a specific organization of a natural drive conflict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME5","text":"The opposition between individual destruction and social order is replaced by the insight that both are connected through the diversion of the same destructive energy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text grounds the assumption of an independent drive of aggression and destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT2","text":"Structural — Civilization appears as libidinal work of integration under the permanent resistance of an original destructive disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The analysis shifts the explanation of social conflicts from models of utility, morality, and organization to the management of irreducible drive ambivalence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Life and history are determined as an enduring confrontation between the formation of unity and return to the inorganic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the crisis of early drive dualism to the theory of civilization of the Eros-death-drive conflict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT2","text":"It remains underdetermined how the death drive can be empirically identified independently of its alloys.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT3","text":"The internal coherence is conditional: it obtains if the theoretical necessity of a non-libidinal residue is accepted as sufficient ground for the death drive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4","text":"The strongest closure lies in the connection between drive dualism, the concept of aggression, and the process of civilization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5","text":"The strongest line of fracture lies between the asserted originality of aggression and the merely indirect, mixed observability of its drive ground.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT6","text":"A further tension consists in the fact that aggression is determined both as a destructive counterforce to civilization and as usable for self-preservation and mastery over nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement insofar as civilization is read not as an independent social theory, but as a species-specific projection of the general drive conflict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_5:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_5@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KA_5:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 06","title":"Chapter VI","context":"Chapter 06","original_title":"Kapitel VI","original_context":"Chapter 06"},"original_title":"Kapitel VI","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6","layer":"CH","title":"Chapter VII","order":7,"parents":["RAW_R2TV_KA_6"],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_6@R001","sha256":"bbfbf7c576290a1a3bfffd2af9e506b69d656d10cc4e08610f1fd5092ddded3a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1","text":"Das Kapitel untersucht diagnostisch, wie Kultur die für das Zusammenleben gefährliche individuelle Aggression nicht beseitigt, sondern psychisch umleitet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","text":"Die Umleitung wird als Introjektion der Aggression rekonstruiert: Aus äußerer Autorität entsteht eine innere Überwachungsinstanz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS3","text":"Die Genealogie des Schuldgefühls bewegt sich von äußerer Liebesverlustangst über die Verinnerlichung der Autorität zur Gewissensangst des Über-Ichs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","text":"Der Text kehrt die anfängliche Kausalordnung um, indem Triebverzicht nicht nur als Folge des Gewissens, sondern als dessen fortlaufende Verstärkungsquelle bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS5","text":"Die Spannung zwischen unterdrückter und ausgeführter Aggression wird durch den Ambivalenzkonflikt von Liebe und Hass gegen die Vaterinstanz vermittelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS6","text":"Die Ausweitung der Gemeinschaft von der Familie zur Menschheit wird als Prozess bestimmt, der kulturelle Bindung nur durch eine zunehmende Steigerung des Schuldgefühls erzeugen kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","text":"Kultur muss individuelle Aggression hemmen, um menschliches Zusammenleben zu sichern.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","text":"Gehemmte Aggression wird introjiziert, gegen das Ich zurückgewendet und vom Über-Ich übernommen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","text":"Die Spannung zwischen dem strafenden Über-Ich und dem unterworfenen Ich ist Schuldgefühl und äußert sich als Strafbedürfnis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","text":"Gut und Böse entstehen anfänglich nicht aus natürlicher moralischer Einsicht, sondern aus der Abhängigkeit von einer liebgewährenden oder liebentziehenden Autorität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","text":"Nach der Verinnerlichung der Autorität bleibt kein verbotener Wunsch vor dem Über-Ich verborgen; böse Absicht und böse Tat werden daher gleichwertig.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6","text":"Der erste Triebverzicht folgt der Angst vor der strafenden Aggression äußerer Autorität, die psychisch als Angst vor Liebesverlust wirksam wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","text":"Die ursprüngliche Strenge des Über-Ichs repräsentiert wesentlich die gegen die Autorität gerichtete, jedoch unterdrückte eigene Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A8","text":"Die Strenge des Über-Ichs wird weder allein durch erfahrene Erziehungsstrenge noch allein durch innere Disposition bestimmt, sondern durch deren Zusammenwirken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","text":"Triebverzicht befreit nach der Über-Ich-Bildung nicht vom Schuldgefühl, weil der verbotene Wunsch fortbesteht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","text":"Jeder weitere Triebverzicht überträgt zusätzliche Aggression auf das Über-Ich und steigert dessen Strenge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","text":"Schuldgefühl entspringt dem Ambivalenzkonflikt von Liebe und destruktiver Aggression gegen dieselbe Autoritätsfigur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12","text":"Die Theorie setzt für die Menschheitsgeschichte hypothetisch voraus, dass das Schuldgefühl am Odipuskomplex und an der Tötung des Urvaters durch die Brüdervereinigung erworben wurde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","text":"Kultur folgt einem erotischen Vereinigungsantrieb und kann wachsende soziale Bindung nur durch wachsende Verstärkung des Schuldgefühls herstellen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX1","text":"Gut und Böse beruhen nicht auf einem ursprünglichen natürlichen Unterscheidungsvermögen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX2","text":"Angst vor Entdeckung und Liebesverlust ist noch kein Schuldgefühl im strengen Sinn, sondern soziale Angst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX3","text":"Das verinnerlichte Gewissen unterscheidet nicht mehr entlastend zwischen vollzogener Tat und bloßer böser Absicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX4","text":"Triebverzicht stellt nach der Aufrichtung des Über-Ichs keine voll befreiende moralische Leistung dar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX5","text":"Tugendhaftes Verhalten vermindert nicht notwendig die Strenge des Gewissens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX6","text":"Die Strenge des Über-Ichs ist nicht einfach die psychische Kopie erfahrener elterlicher Strenge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX7","text":"Reue nach einer tatsächlich begangenen Tat erklärt weder den Ursprung des Gewissens noch den Ursprung des Schuldgefühls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX8","text":"Schuldgefühl hängt innerhalb des Ambivalenzmodells nicht entscheidend davon ab, ob die Aggression gegen den Vater ausgeführt oder unterlassen wurde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D1","text":"Die erste moralische Ordnung erscheint als Abhängigkeitsordnung: Das Verbotene ist zunächst dasjenige, dessen Entdeckung Liebesverlust und Strafe auslöst.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D2","text":"Mit der Über-Ich-Bildung wird die äußere Kontrollfrage durch eine innere Totalüberwachung ersetzt, in der auch Wünsche strafrelevant werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D3","text":"Der Wegfall realer äußerer Gefahr beendet die Strafangst nicht, weil das Über-Ich die Strafbereitschaft der Autorität im Inneren fortsetzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D4","text":"Tugend, Enthaltsamkeit und von außen auferlegte Versagung können das Gewissen verschärfen, weil sie zusätzliche Aggression in die innere Strafinstanz überführen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D5","text":"Ein strenges Gewissen entsteht aus der Verbindung von Triebversagung, die Aggression freisetzt, und Liebeserfahrung, die diese Aggression nach innen wendet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","text":"Die anfängliche Kausalrichtung wird rekursiv: Autoritätsangst erzeugt Triebverzicht, während späterer Triebverzicht die Autoritätsinstanz im Inneren verstärkt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D7","text":"Die phylogenetische Hypothese kann ausgeführte Vateraggression und unterdrückte Vateraggression nur über die nachträgliche Wiederkehr der Liebe und Identifizierung in einer gemeinsamen Schuldlogik verbinden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D8","text":"Die kulturelle Ausweitung sozialer Bindung verwandelt den familiären Autoritätskonflikt in eine allgemeine und wachsende Last des Schuldgefühls.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD1","text":"Kultur stabilisiert sich nicht durch die Aufhebung von Aggression, sondern durch ihre Umwandlung von möglicher Außenaggression in dauerhafte innere Herrschaft über das Ich.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD2","text":"Kulturelle Integration und individuelles Leiden wachsen innerhalb des Systems nicht gegeneinander austauschbar, sondern gemeinsam: Das Mittel der Bindung produziert die Last, die es aufrechterhält.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD3","text":"Moralische Selbstdisziplin besitzt eine paradoxe Struktur, weil sie nicht als Tilgung von Schuld fungiert, sondern den Mechanismus ihrer Verstärkung speist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD4","text":"Schuld wird vom objektiven Schadensereignis abgelöst und an die unaufhebbare psychische Koexistenz von Liebe, Hass, Wunsch und Identifizierung gebunden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX1","text":"Das System schließt eine autonome Moral aus, die unabhängig von Abhängigkeit, Autorität und Liebesverlust entstehen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX2","text":"Das psychische Innere ist kein Rückzugsraum vor sozialer Kontrolle, weil die verinnerlichte Autorität auch nicht ausgeführte Wünsche erfasst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","text":"Aggression kann nicht folgenlos unterdrückt werden; ihre Hemmung setzt sie als Strafgewalt gegen das Ich wieder ein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX4","text":"Familie und Kultur bilden keine getrennten Ordnungen, weil die kulturelle Schuldökonomie die familiäre Vater- und Autoritätsstruktur in verallgemeinerter Form fortsetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX1","text":"Eine Kultur ohne kumulative Schuldsteigerung ist innerhalb des Systems nicht verfügbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX2","text":"Ein durch Enthaltsamkeit vollständig entlastetes oder durch moralische Leistung endgültig unschuldiges Subjekt ist innerhalb des Systems nicht verfügbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX3","text":"Eine endgültige Versöhnung von erotischer Bindung und destruktiver Aggression ist ausgeschlossen, weil ihr Konflikt als dauerhaft und kulturkonstitutiv bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS1","text":"Abhängigkeit von äußerer Autorität → Angst vor Liebesverlust und Strafe → erster Triebverzicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS2","text":"Versagung durch Autorität → feindselige Aggression gegen Autorität → Unterdrückung dieser Aggression → Identifizierung mit Autorität → Über-Ich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS3","text":"Über-Ich + fortbestehender verbotener Wunsch → Gleichsetzung von Absicht und Tat → Schuldgefühl + Strafbedürfnis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS4","text":"Neuer Triebverzicht → Aggressionsübertragung auf das Über-Ich → größere Gewissensstrenge → weiterer Triebverzicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS5","text":"Ambivalenzkonflikt der Vaterbeziehung → familiäres Schuldmodell → Ausweitung der Gemeinschaft → kulturelle Verstärkung des Schuldgefühls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AF1","text":"Kulturelle Aggressionsgefahr → Introjektion der Aggression → Über-Ich als innere Besatzungsinstanz → Schuldgefühl als Spannung zwischen Über-Ich und Ich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AF2","text":"Äußere Autoritätsangst → soziale Angst → Verinnerlichung der Autorität → Gleichstellung von Wunsch und Tat → unauflösbare innere Strafbarkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AF3","text":"Paradox der Gewissensverschärfung durch Verzicht → Rückführung auf unterdrückte Eigenaggression → Ambivalenzmodell → kulturelle Steigerung des Schuldgefühls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME1","text":"Moral wird von einer natürlichen Wertordnung in eine Abhängigkeits- und Autoritätsökonomie umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME2","text":"Gewissen wird nicht als neutrale innere Norminstanz, sondern als gegen das Ich gewendete Form unterdrückter Aggression sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3","text":"Triebverzicht wechselt seinen Status von moralischer Entlastung zu einem rekursiven Verstärker der Schuldproduktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME4","text":"Kultur erscheint nicht als Gegenwelt zur familiären Autorität, sondern als deren Erweiterung in eine massenhafte Schuldordnung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT1","text":"Surface — Das Kapitel erklärt Gewissen, Schuldgefühl, Reue, Triebverzicht und Strafbedürfnis als verschiedene psychische Vorgänge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT2","text":"Structural — Äußere Autorität, Liebesabhängigkeit, Verinnerlichung, Über-Ich und Triebverzicht bilden einen Kreislauf der Aggressionsverwaltung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Die kulturelle Lösung des Aggressionsproblems wird als Verschiebung ihres Ortes rekonstruiert: von zwischenmenschlicher Gewalt zu innerpsychischer Strafgewalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Die Kulturgeschichte wird als Fortsetzung eines dauerhaften Konflikts von Eros und Destruktionsstreben gedacht, dessen phylogenetischer Ursprung hypothetisch in der Vateraggression lokalisiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Hauptbewegung von äußerer Autoritätsangst über Introjektion und Über-Ich zur kulturellen Schuldsteigerung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT2","text":"Die interne Kohärenz beruht auf der Verbindung zweier zunächst konkurrierender Erklärungen der Über-Ich-Strenge: fortgesetzte äußere Autorität und nach innen gewendete Eigenaggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT3","text":"Die Gewichtung von konstitutionellen Faktoren, realer Erziehung und unterdrückter Aggression bleibt unterbestimmt, obwohl alle drei als wirksam gesetzt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT4","text":"Der Übergang von individueller Gewissensbildung zu einer Menschheitsgeschichte der Urvatertötung bleibt hypothetisch, weil der Text selbst über die Annahme eines solchen Ereignisses nicht hinausgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT5","text":"Die Differenz zwischen Schuld nach unterdrückter Aggression und Reue nach ausgeführter Aggression wird durch Ambivalenz vermittelt, aber nicht unabhängig von der phylogenetischen Konstruktion begründet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT6","text":"Die stärkste Rekonstruktionsleistung liegt in der rekursiven Umkehrung, dass das Gewissen Triebverzicht fordert und derselbe Verzicht das Gewissen verschärft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT7","text":"Die eröffnende Frage nach dem Ausbleiben eines entsprechenden Kulturkampfs bei Tieren bleibt als Vergleichsproblem bestehen und wird von der Schuldgenealogie nicht aufgelöst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171534450316Z_2b9d29e3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter VII","source_sha256":"bbfbf7c576290a1a3bfffd2af9e506b69d656d10cc4e08610f1fd5092ddded3a","sha256":"9bdbcc388569e44b7c269dd0f121d40b5fb67f3be21a7cc753b7f6e84a7319be","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:15:34.453094+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1","text":"The chapter examines diagnostically how culture does not eliminate individual aggression, which is dangerous for communal life, but psychically redirects it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","text":"The redirection is reconstructed as the introjection of aggression: external authority gives rise to an internal monitoring agency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS3","text":"The genealogy of the feeling of guilt moves from the external fear of loss of love, through the internalization of authority, to the Super-ego's anxiety of conscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","text":"The text reverses the initial causal order by determining instinctual renunciation not only as a consequence of conscience, but as its ongoing source of intensification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS5","text":"The tension between suppressed and enacted aggression is mediated through the ambivalence conflict of love and hatred toward the paternal agency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS6","text":"The expansion of the community from the family to humanity is determined as a process that can produce cultural bonding only through an increasing intensification of the feeling of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","text":"Culture must inhibit individual aggression in order to secure human communal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","text":"Inhibited aggression is introjected, turned back against the ego, and taken over by the Super-ego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","text":"The tension between the punishing Super-ego and the subjected ego is the feeling of guilt and manifests itself as a need for punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","text":"Good and evil initially arise not from natural moral insight, but from dependence on an authority that grants or withdraws love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","text":"After the internalization of authority, no prohibited wish remains hidden from the Super-ego; evil intention and evil deed therefore become equivalent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6","text":"The first instinctual renunciation follows from fear of the punishing aggression of external authority, which becomes psychically effective as fear of loss of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","text":"The original severity of the Super-ego essentially represents one's own aggression directed against authority but suppressed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A8","text":"The severity of the Super-ego is determined neither solely by experienced educational severity nor solely by inner disposition, but by their interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","text":"After the formation of the Super-ego, instinctual renunciation does not free one from the feeling of guilt because the prohibited wish persists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","text":"Every further instinctual renunciation transfers additional aggression onto the Super-ego and increases its severity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","text":"The feeling of guilt springs from the ambivalence conflict of love and destructive aggression toward the same authority figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12","text":"For the history of humanity, the theory hypothetically presupposes that the feeling of guilt was acquired through the Oedipus complex and the killing of the primal father by the fraternal union.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","text":"Culture follows an erotic drive toward unification and can establish growing social bonds only through growing intensification of the feeling of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX1","text":"Good and evil do not rest on an original natural capacity for distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX2","text":"Fear of discovery and loss of love is not yet a feeling of guilt in the strict sense, but social anxiety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX3","text":"Internalized conscience no longer exculpatorily distinguishes between an enacted deed and mere evil intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX4","text":"After the establishment of the Super-ego, instinctual renunciation does not constitute a fully liberating moral achievement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX5","text":"Virtuous behavior does not necessarily diminish the severity of conscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX6","text":"The severity of the Super-ego is not simply the psychic copy of experienced parental severity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX7","text":"Remorse after an actually committed deed explains neither the origin of conscience nor the origin of the feeling of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX8","text":"Within the ambivalence model, the feeling of guilt does not depend decisively on whether aggression against the father was enacted or omitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D1","text":"The first moral order appears as an order of dependency: what is forbidden is initially that whose discovery triggers loss of love and punishment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D2","text":"With the formation of the Super-ego, the external question of control is replaced by an internal total surveillance in which wishes too become relevant to punishment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D3","text":"The disappearance of real external danger does not end fear of punishment, because the Super-ego continues internally the authority's readiness to punish.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D4","text":"Virtue, abstinence, and externally imposed frustration can sharpen conscience because they transfer additional aggression into the internal punitive agency.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D5","text":"A strict conscience arises from the conjunction of instinctual frustration, which releases aggression, and the experience of love, which turns this aggression inward.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","text":"The initial causal direction becomes recursive: fear of authority produces instinctual renunciation, while later instinctual renunciation strengthens the agency of authority within.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D7","text":"The phylogenetic hypothesis can connect enacted paternal aggression and suppressed paternal aggression only through the subsequent return of love and identification in a shared logic of guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:D8","text":"The cultural expansion of social bonding transforms the familial conflict of authority into a general and growing burden of the feeling of guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD1","text":"Culture stabilizes itself not through the abolition of aggression, but through its transformation from possible outward aggression into enduring internal domination over the ego.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD2","text":"Cultural integration and individual suffering do not grow in the system as mutually exchangeable opposites, but together: the means of bonding produces the burden that sustains it.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD3","text":"Moral self-discipline has a paradoxical structure because it does not function as the cancellation of guilt, but feeds the mechanism of its intensification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD4","text":"Guilt is detached from the objective event of harm and bound to the irreducible psychic coexistence of love, hatred, wish, and identification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an autonomous morality that could arise independently of dependency, authority, and loss of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX2","text":"The psychic interior is not a refuge from social control, because internalized authority also apprehends wishes that are not enacted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","text":"Aggression cannot be suppressed without consequence; its inhibition reinstates it as punitive force against the ego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX4","text":"Family and culture do not form separate orders, because the cultural economy of guilt continues the familial structure of father and authority in generalized form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX1","text":"A culture without cumulative intensification of guilt is unavailable within the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX2","text":"A subject fully relieved through abstinence or definitively innocent through moral achievement is unavailable within the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX3","text":"A final reconciliation of erotic bonding and destructive aggression is excluded, because their conflict is determined as enduring and constitutive of culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS1","text":"Dependence on external authority → fear of loss of love and punishment → first instinctual renunciation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS2","text":"Frustration by authority → hostile aggression against authority → suppression of this aggression → identification with authority → Super-ego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS3","text":"Super-ego + persisting prohibited wish → equation of intention and deed → feeling of guilt + need for punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS4","text":"New instinctual renunciation → transfer of aggression onto the Super-ego → greater severity of conscience → further instinctual renunciation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:FGS5","text":"Ambivalence conflict of the father relationship → familial model of guilt → expansion of the community → cultural intensification of the feeling of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AF1","text":"Cultural danger of aggression → introjection of aggression → Super-ego as internal occupying agency → feeling of guilt as tension between Super-ego and ego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AF2","text":"External fear of authority → social anxiety → internalization of authority → equation of wish and deed → irresolvable internal punishability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:AF3","text":"Paradox of the sharpening of conscience through renunciation → reduction to suppressed self-aggression → ambivalence model → cultural intensification of the feeling of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME1","text":"Morality is reclassified from a natural order of value into an economy of dependency and authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME2","text":"Conscience becomes visible not as a neutral internal normative agency, but as a form of suppressed aggression turned against the ego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3","text":"Instinctual renunciation changes its status from moral relief to a recursive intensifier of guilt production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME4","text":"Culture appears not as a counterworld to familial authority, but as its extension into a mass order of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT1","text":"Surface — The chapter explains conscience, the feeling of guilt, remorse, instinctual renunciation, and the need for punishment as distinct psychic processes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT2","text":"Structural — External authority, dependence on love, internalization, Super-ego, and instinctual renunciation form a cycle of aggression management.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The cultural solution to the problem of aggression is reconstructed as a displacement of its site: from interpersonal violence to intrapsychic punitive force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Cultural history is conceived as the continuation of an enduring conflict between Eros and the destructive drive, whose phylogenetic origin is hypothetically located in paternal aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement from external fear of authority through introjection and Super-ego to the cultural intensification of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT2","text":"Internal coherence rests on the connection between two initially competing explanations of the severity of the Super-ego: continued external authority and self-aggression turned inward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0056","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT3","text":"The weighting of constitutional factors, actual upbringing, and suppressed aggression remains underdetermined, although all three are posited as effective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0060","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT4","text":"The transition from individual formation of conscience to a history of humanity involving the killing of the primal father remains hypothetical, because the text itself does not go beyond the assumption of such an event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT5","text":"The difference between guilt after suppressed aggression and remorse after enacted aggression is mediated through ambivalence, but is not grounded independently of the phylogenetic construction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT6","text":"The strongest reconstructive achievement lies in the recursive reversal that conscience demands instinctual renunciation and that the same renunciation sharpens conscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT7","text":"The opening question concerning the absence of a corresponding cultural struggle among animals remains as a comparative problem and is not resolved by the genealogy of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_6:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_6@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KA_6:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 07","title":"Chapter VII","context":"Chapter 07","original_title":"Kapitel VII","original_context":"Chapter 07"},"original_title":"Kapitel VII","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7","layer":"CH","title":"Chapter VIII","order":8,"parents":["RAW_R2TV_KA_7"],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_7@R001","sha256":"a77adb053d406586b66af32417d77e0778617140177e0c4fbf4b97d598bd62fa","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS1","text":"Das zentrale Problem ist, wie Kultur Aggression bindet und dabei ein teils unbewusstes Schuldgefühl erzeugt, das individuelles Glück mindert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS2","text":"Kulturfortschritt wird durch eine Glückseinbuße bezahlt, deren psychischer Träger die Steigerung des Schuldgefühls ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS3","text":"Schuld wird aus der moralischen Tatbewertung in eine Dynamik von Angst, Aggressionshemmung, Verinnerlichung und Über-Ich-Bildung überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS4","text":"Das Argument verfährt metapsychologisch-rekonstruktiv, klinisch-analogisch und endet in einer bedingten Kulturdiagnostik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS5","text":"Die Bewegung führt von begrifflicher Differenzierung über die aggressive Genese des Schuldgefühls zur Triebökonomie von Individuum und Kultur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6","text":"Die Individualpsychologie wird unter Wahrung einer Zielasymmetrie auf den Kulturprozess übertragen und erzeugt das Modell eines Kultur-Über-Ichs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS7","text":"Die Kritik überfordernder Ethik mündet in die offene Frage, ob Eros die technologisch gesteigerte Selbstvernichtungsmacht der Aggression begrenzen kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","text":"Kulturfortschritt wird durch Glückseinbuße infolge gesteigerten Schuldgefühls bezahlt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","text":"Die Wirksamkeit des Schuldgefühls ist von seiner bewussten Wahrnehmung unabhängig.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3","text":"Schuldgefühl ist eine topische Abart der Angst und fällt in seiner späteren Form mit der Angst vor dem Über-Ich zusammen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A4","text":"Über-Ich, Gewissen, Schuldgefühl, Strafbedürfnis und Reue sind nicht austauschbare Bestimmungen desselben Autoritätsverhältnisses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A5","text":"Das vor dem Über-Ich bestehende Schuldgefühl entspringt der Angst vor äußerer Autorität und dem Konflikt zwischen Liebesbedürfnis und Triebbefriedigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6","text":"Die Verinnerlichung der Autorität hebt für die Schuldproduktion den Unterschied zwischen ausgeführter und bloß beabsichtigter Aggression auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","text":"Die Aggressivität des Über-Ichs ist nach innen verschobene Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8","text":"Die Aggressivität des Über-Ichs speist sich aus fortgesetzter äußerer Strafgewalt und aus eigener gehemmter Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9","text":"Die leitende, klinisch nicht eindeutig bestätigte Hypothese beschränkt die unmittelbare Genese des Schuldgefühls auf den Verzicht auf Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","text":"Der Kulturprozess ist ein vom Konflikt zwischen Eros und Todestrieb bestimmter Lebensprozess, den Eros unter dem Druck der Ananke auf libidinöse Gemeinschaftsbildung ausrichtet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","text":"Individualentwicklung und Kulturentwicklung sind analoge Integrationsprozesse an verschiedenartigen Objekten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12","text":"Individualentwicklung priorisiert Glück, während Kulturentwicklung die Herstellung einer menschlichen Einheit priorisiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","text":"Der Konflikt zwischen Individuum und Gemeinschaft ist ein Konflikt der Libidoverteilung und lässt deshalb einen endlichen Ausgleich grundsätzlich zu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","text":"Eine Gemeinschaft bildet ein Kultur-Über-Ich, das Ideale setzt, Forderungen erhebt und Abweichung durch Gewissensangst sanktioniert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","text":"Ethik ist der therapeutische Versuch des Kultur-Über-Ichs, die konstitutionelle Aggression durch Gebote zu beherrschen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16","text":"Forderungen jenseits psychischer Beherrschbarkeit erzeugen Auflehnung, Neurose oder Unglück, statt Aggression zuverlässig aufzuheben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17","text":"Die Diagnose einer Gemeinschaftsneurose bleibt durch das Fehlen eines externen Normalitätsmaßstabs und einer therapiefähigen Autorität begrenzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","text":"Die technologische Beherrschung der Natur macht die kulturelle Beherrschung des Aggressions- und Selbstvernichtungstriebs zur offenen Schicksalsfrage der Menschheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1","text":"Schuldgefühl ist nicht mit bewusstem Schuldbewusstsein identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX2","text":"Über-Ich, Gewissen, Schuldgefühl, Strafbedürfnis und Reue sind keine Synonyme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3","text":"Reue ist nicht die allgemeine Form des Schuldgefühls, sondern die Reaktion auf tatsächlich ausgeführte Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX4","text":"Nicht jede Versagung oder verhinderte Triebbefriedigung steigert unmittelbar das Schuldgefühl.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX5","text":"Unerfüllte erotische Ansprüche erzeugen Schuld nicht ohne die Vermittlung einer hervorgerufenen und erneut unterdrückten Aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX6","text":"Die allgemeine Formel vom Kampf zwischen Eros und Todestrieb besitzt ohne besondere Bedingungen keine unterscheidende Erklärungskraft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7","text":"Die Analogie zwischen Individual- und Kulturentwicklung begründet keine vollständige Identität beider Prozesse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX8","text":"Der Konflikt zwischen Individuum und Gesellschaft ist nicht unmittelbar der unversöhnliche Gegensatz von Eros und Todestrieb.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX9","text":"Das Ich besitzt keine unbeschränkte Herrschaft über das Es.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10","text":"Die moralische Forderung beweist weder ihre psychische Durchführbarkeit noch ihre aggressive Wirksamkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX11","text":"Natürliche Ethik und religiöse Jenseitsvergütung ersetzen keine diesseitige Struktur, in der sich Tugend praktisch auszahlt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX12","text":"Eine Veränderung der Besitzverhältnisse beseitigt Aggression nicht, wenn sie mit einer idealistischen Verkennung der menschlichen Triebkonstitution verbunden wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX13","text":"Kultur ist weder notwendig das höchste Gut noch ein gesicherter Weg zu fortschreitender Vollkommenheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX14","text":"Kulturelle Entwicklungstendenzen sind nicht als unabänderliche Naturnotwendigkeiten erwiesen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX15","text":"Aus einer Analogie zwischen individueller und kollektiver Neurose folgt keine unmittelbar anwendbare Massentherapie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1","text":"Kulturell erzeugte Schuld kann als unbestimmtes Unbehagen oder als Unzufriedenheit erscheinen und nach fremden Motivierungen suchen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D2","text":"Die Überlagerung äußerer und innerer Autoritätsangst erklärt die wechselnde Beziehung des Schuldgefühls zum Bewusstsein.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D3","text":"Nach der Über-Ich-Bildung kann ein aggressiver Impuls Schuld erzeugen, ohne in eine Handlung überzugehen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D4","text":"Die konkurrierenden Herkunftsmodelle der Über-Ich-Aggression werden durch die gemeinsame Kategorie der nach innen verschobenen Aggression verbunden, ohne ihre unterschiedliche Gewichtung aufzuheben.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D5","text":"Erotische Versagung erhöht das Schuldgefühl nur über die Erzeugung und nachfolgende Unterdrückung einer Aggression gegen die versagende Instanz.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D6","text":"Unter Verdrängung werden in durchschnittlicher Annäherung libidinöse Anteile in Symptome und aggressive Anteile in Schuldgefühl umgesetzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D7","text":"Die strukturelle Ähnlichkeit von Individual- und Kulturentwicklung erklärt gemeinsame Mittel, nicht aber eine gemeinsame Rangordnung ihrer Ziele.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D8","text":"Das individuelle Glück wird im Kulturprozess systematisch zur nachgeordneten Größe der Gemeinschaftsbildung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9","text":"Je stärker das Kultur-Über-Ich psychisch undurchführbare Aggressionsabwehr verlangt, desto eher reproduziert seine Ethik Schuld und Unglück.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D10","text":"Die Pathologisierung einer Kultur ist analogisch möglich, bleibt aber diagnostisch und therapeutisch ungesichert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11","text":"Technischer Fortschritt steigert die Reichweite der Aggression und damit Unruhe, Angst und die Möglichkeit vollständiger Selbstvernichtung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12","text":"Eros fungiert als notwendige Gegenkraft zur Selbstvernichtung, nicht als Garantie ihres Scheiterns.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1","text":"Kultur bildet eine rekursive Schuldschleife: Aggressionshemmung erzeugt Verinnerlichung, Verinnerlichung erzeugt Schuld, Schuld mindert Glück, und das fortbestehende Aggressionsproblem erzeugt verschärfte Forderungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD2","text":"Das einigende Werk des Eros erzeugt kulturelle Pathologie, soweit es Aggression nicht beseitigt, sondern zu ihrer Verlagerung gegen das Subjekt zwingt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD3","text":"Individuelles und kulturelles Über-Ich bilden gekoppelte Normierungskreisläufe, weil kulturelle Forderungen zu individuellen Gewissensforderungen werden und individuelle Triebkonflikte kollektiv reproduziert werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD4","text":"Ein unerfüllbares ethisches Ideal sanktioniert die Unfähigkeit zu seiner Befolgung zuverlässiger, als es die Aggression beseitigt, gegen die es gerichtet ist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5","text":"Die Beherrschung äußerer Naturkräfte verschärft die kulturelle Krise, wenn die Verfügung über Vernichtungsmittel schneller wächst als die Fähigkeit zur Bindung innerer Aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6","text":"Psychoanalytische Kulturdiagnostik kann Pathologie sichtbar machen, erzeugt aber weder einen kulturäußeren Normalitätsmaßstab noch ein legitimes Subjekt kollektiver Therapie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD7","text":"Ein möglicher Ausgleich zwischen Individuum und Gemeinschaft beendet nicht den übergeordneten Konflikt zwischen Eros und Todestrieb.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX1","text":"Psychische Wirksamkeit setzt keine transparente Selbstwahrnehmung voraus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX2","text":"Vernünftige Einsicht oder moralischer Wille verleihen dem Ich keine souveräne Verfügung über seine Triebe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX3","text":"Schuld lässt sich nicht aus Entbehrung als solcher ableiten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX4","text":"Gemeinschaftsbildung und individuelles Glück konvergieren nicht von selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX5","text":"Aggression ist weder ausschließlich ein Produkt falscher Erziehung noch vollständig auf Besitzverhältnisse reduzierbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX6","text":"Die Übertragung individualpsychologischer Begriffe auf Kollektive ist keine maßstabsneutrale Operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX7","text":"Für eine gleichartig affizierte Menschheit steht keine unbetroffene Normalität als Vergleichshintergrund bereit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX8","text":"Geschichte enthält keine gesicherte Teleologie, die Kulturfortschritt, Glück und den Sieg des Eros miteinander verbürgt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX1","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Form kultureller Einheit, deren Aggressionsbindung ohne Schuldsteigerung und Glücksverlust auskommt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX2","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein kulturäußerer Standpunkt, von dem aus die gesamte Menschheit eindeutig als normal oder neurotisch bestimmt werden könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX3","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine anerkannte Autorität, die eine diagnostizierte soziale Neurose gegen den Widerstand der Masse therapieren könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX4","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein Trost, der die kulturellen Opfer als notwendig, sinnvoll oder endgültig kompensiert ausweist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine terminale Versöhnung von Eros und Todestrieb; der Schluss kann nur eine Gegenanstrengung des Eros erwarten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS1","text":"Eros + Ananke → Gemeinschaftsbildung → Einschränkung individueller Triebbefriedigung → Konflikt zwischen Glück und Anschluss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS2","text":"Äußere Autorität + Liebesabhängigkeit → Aggressionshemmung → Autoritätsangst → frühes Schuldgefühl.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS3","text":"Verinnerlichung der Autorität → Über-Ich → Gleichstellung von Aggressionsabsicht und Aggressionstat → dauerhafte Schuldproduktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS4","text":"Gehemmte Aggression → Verschiebung nach innen → Über-Ich-Aggression → Schuld, Strafbedürfnis oder unbestimmtes Unbehagen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS5","text":"Gemischte Triebstrebung + Verdrängung → libidinöser Symptomanteil / aggressiver Schuldanteil → symptomatische Strafbindung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS6","text":"Individualpsychologische Struktur → kontrollierte Skalierung → Kultur-Über-Ich → Ethik als institutionalisierte Aggressionsabwehr.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS7","text":"Überforderndes Gebot + begrenzte Ich-Herrschaft → Nichtbefolgung → Schuld, Auflehnung, Neurose oder Unglück → therapeutisches Scheitern des Gebots.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS8","text":"Technische Naturbeherrschung + fortbestehender Selbstvernichtungstrieb → globale Ausrottungsfähigkeit → offene Entscheidung zwischen kultureller Bindung und Destruktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AF1","text":"Unverständliche Beziehung von Schuld und Bewusstsein → begriffliche Differenzierung → Schichtung äußerer und innerer Autoritätsangst → aggressive Genese des Schuldgefühls → Einordnung in Eros und Todestrieb → Analogie von Individual- und Kulturentwicklung → Kultur-Über-Ich → Ethik als überforderte Aggressionsabwehr → begrenzte Gemeinschaftsdiagnose → technologische Selbstvernichtungsfrage → erwartete, nicht garantierte Gegenanstrengung des Eros.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME1","text":"Schuld wird von einer moralischen Tatkategorie in eine psychische Topik von Angst, Spannung und Aggressionsverschiebung überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME2","text":"Bewusstsein verliert den Status eines zuverlässigen Maßes psychischer Wirksamkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME3","text":"Triebstörung wird in libidinöse und aggressive Komponenten zerlegt; nur die aggressive Komponente erhält unmittelbare schuldgenerierende Funktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME4","text":"Kulturfortschritt wird von einer Gewinnlogik in eine Tauschstruktur aus Gemeinschaftsbildung, Schuldsteigerung und Glücksverlust überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME5","text":"Individualentwicklung und Kulturentwicklung werden als analoge Prozesse mit entgegengesetzter Zielgewichtung kartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME6","text":"Der Gegensatz Individuum/Gesellschaft wird vom Gegensatz Eros/Todestrieb getrennt und als Konflikt der Libidoverteilung neu klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME7","text":"Ethik wird von einer autonomen Normordnung zu einer therapeutischen Technik des Kultur-Über-Ichs umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME8","text":"Die strategische Landschaft spaltet sich in moralisches Gebot, materielle Beziehungsordnung und triebkonstitutionelle Grenze.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME9","text":"Neurose wird unter Vorbehalt von einer individuellen Pathologie zu einem möglichen Diagnosemodell ganzer Kulturen erweitert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10","text":"Technischer Fortschritt wird nicht mehr nur als Naturbeherrschung, sondern als Verstärker ungebundener Selbstvernichtungsmacht sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT1","text":"Oberflächenebene: Schuldgefühl, Gewissen, Ethik, Kulturfortschritt und gegenwärtige Vernichtungsfähigkeit bilden die expliziten Gegenstände.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2","text":"Strukturelle Ebene: Autoritätsverinnerlichung verschiebt gehemmte Aggression nach innen und institutionalisiert sie als individuelles oder kulturelles Über-Ich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT3","text":"Metastrategische Ebene: Moralische Forderung wird durch eine Prüfung psychischer Durchführbarkeit, materieller Anreizstruktur und diagnostischer Reichweite ersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT4","text":"Ontologische und zeitliche Ebene: Leben und Kultur bleiben im nicht teleologisch entschiedenen Konflikt zwischen Eros und Todestrieb; technische Entwicklung verändert dessen Vernichtungspotential, nicht seine Grundstruktur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen zur Rekonstruktion der Hauptbewegung von der Schuldtopik über das Kultur-Über-Ich bis zur Selbstvernichtungsfrage aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT2","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern Trieblehre, Aggressionsverinnerlichung und kontrollierte Individual-Kultur-Analogie akzeptiert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT3","text":"Die ausschließliche Ableitung des Schuldgefühls aus Aggressionsverzicht bleibt empirisch unterbestimmt und wird selbst nur als theoretisch vereinfachende Hypothese gesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT4","text":"Die zwei Quellen der Über-Ich-Aggression werden durch den Oberbegriff der nach innen verschobenen Aggression verbunden, aber nicht kausal gegeneinander gewichtet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT5","text":"Die Übertragung auf Kulturen bleibt durch fehlenden Normalitätsvergleich, ungesicherte Skalierung und das Fehlen einer therapeutischen Autorität begrenzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT6","text":"Die behauptete Überlegenheit veränderter Besitzbeziehungen gegenüber ethischem Gebot bleibt ohne ausgearbeiteten Vermittlungsmechanismus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT7","text":"Die höchste inferentielle Dichte liegt in der Kette Aggressionshemmung → Verinnerlichung → Über-Ich → Schuld → Glücksverlust.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT8","text":"Die Urschuld, die historische Genese des Über-Ichs und die Herkunft kultureller Ideale hängen von vorausgesetzten früheren Konstruktionen und analogischer Kompression ab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT9","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung des Arguments; ihr Endpunkt bleibt prognostisch offen und wird nicht deduktiv entschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171608766750Z_eb50e02e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapter VIII","source_sha256":"a77adb053d406586b66af32417d77e0778617140177e0c4fbf4b97d598bd62fa","sha256":"c6f4454efca1d0dcffe3c2938cf6e3de0dc9f5140cb074c7c97028b16f098dae","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:16:08.769966+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS1","text":"The central problem is how culture binds aggression while generating a partly unconscious sense of guilt that diminishes individual happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS2","text":"Cultural progress is paid for by a loss of happiness, whose psychic bearer is the intensification of the sense of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS3","text":"Guilt is transferred from moral evaluation of the deed into a dynamic of anxiety, inhibition of aggression, internalization, and formation of the superego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS4","text":"The argument proceeds metapsychologically-reconstructively and clinically-analogically, and concludes in a conditional diagnosis of culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS5","text":"The movement leads from conceptual differentiation, via the aggressive genesis of the sense of guilt, to the drive economy of the individual and culture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6","text":"Individual psychology is transferred to the cultural process while preserving an asymmetry of aims, and produces the model of a cultural superego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS7","text":"The critique of overburdening ethics culminates in the open question of whether Eros can limit the technologically enhanced power of aggression to self-annihilate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","text":"Cultural progress is paid for by a loss of happiness resulting from an intensified sense of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","text":"The efficacy of the sense of guilt is independent of its conscious perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3","text":"The sense of guilt is a topical variant of anxiety and, in its later form, coincides with anxiety before the superego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A4","text":"Superego, conscience, sense of guilt, need for punishment, and remorse are non-interchangeable determinations of the same relation to authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A5","text":"The sense of guilt existing prior to the superego springs from anxiety before external authority and from the conflict between the need for love and drive satisfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6","text":"For the production of guilt, the internalization of authority abolishes the difference between carried-out and merely intended aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","text":"The aggressiveness of the superego is aggression shifted inward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8","text":"The aggressiveness of the superego is nourished by continued external punitive force and by one's own inhibited aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9","text":"The guiding hypothesis, not unambiguously confirmed clinically, restricts the immediate genesis of the sense of guilt to the renunciation of aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","text":"The cultural process is a life process determined by the conflict between Eros and the death drive, which Eros, under the pressure of Ananke, directs toward libidinal community formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","text":"Individual development and cultural development are analogous processes of integration directed at heterogeneous objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12","text":"Individual development prioritizes happiness, whereas cultural development prioritizes the creation of a human unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","text":"The conflict between individual and community is a conflict over the distribution of libido and therefore fundamentally permits a finite accommodation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","text":"A community forms a cultural superego that establishes ideals, makes demands, and sanctions deviation through anxiety of conscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","text":"Ethics is the therapeutic attempt of the cultural superego to master constitutional aggression through commandments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16","text":"Demands beyond psychic manageability produce rebellion, neurosis, or unhappiness, rather than reliably abolishing aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17","text":"The diagnosis of a communal neurosis remains limited by the absence of an external standard of normality and of an authority capable of therapy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","text":"The technological mastery of nature makes the cultural mastery of the drive toward aggression and self-annihilation the open question of humanity's fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1","text":"The sense of guilt is not identical with conscious awareness of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX2","text":"Superego, conscience, sense of guilt, need for punishment, and remorse are not synonyms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3","text":"Remorse is not the general form of the sense of guilt, but the reaction to aggression actually carried out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX4","text":"Not every frustration or prevented drive satisfaction immediately intensifies the sense of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX5","text":"Unfulfilled erotic claims do not generate guilt without the mediation of an aggression that is evoked and then repressed anew.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX6","text":"Without particular conditions, the general formula of the struggle between Eros and the death drive possesses no discriminating explanatory force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7","text":"The analogy between individual and cultural development does not establish a complete identity of the two processes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX8","text":"The conflict between individual and society is not directly the irreconcilable opposition of Eros and the death drive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX9","text":"The ego possesses no unrestricted mastery over the id.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10","text":"The moral demand proves neither its psychic feasibility nor its efficacy against aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX11","text":"Natural ethics and religious compensation in the beyond do not replace an earthly structure in which virtue pays off in practice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX12","text":"A change in property relations does not eliminate aggression if it is joined to an idealistic misrecognition of the human drive constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX13","text":"Culture is neither necessarily the highest good nor a secure path to progressive perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX14","text":"Tendencies of cultural development are not proven to be immutable natural necessities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX15","text":"No directly applicable mass therapy follows from an analogy between individual and collective neurosis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1","text":"Culturally produced guilt can appear as indeterminate malaise or dissatisfaction and seek other motivations.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D2","text":"The superimposition of anxiety before external and internal authority explains the changing relation of the sense of guilt to consciousness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D3","text":"After formation of the superego, an aggressive impulse can generate guilt without passing into an action.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D4","text":"The competing models of the origin of superego aggression are connected by the common category of aggression shifted inward, without abolishing their differing weighting.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D5","text":"Erotic frustration increases the sense of guilt only through the generation and subsequent repression of an aggression against the frustrating agency.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D6","text":"Under repression, libidinal components are, in approximate average, converted into symptoms and aggressive components into a sense of guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D7","text":"The structural similarity of individual and cultural development explains shared means, but not a shared hierarchy of their aims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D8","text":"In the cultural process, individual happiness systematically becomes subordinate to community formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9","text":"The more the cultural superego demands psychically unfeasible defense against aggression, the more its ethics reproduces guilt and unhappiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D10","text":"The pathologization of a culture is analogically possible, but remains diagnostically and therapeutically unsecured.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11","text":"Technical progress increases the scope of aggression and thus unrest, anxiety, and the possibility of complete self-annihilation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12","text":"Eros functions as a necessary counterforce to self-annihilation, not as a guarantee of its failure.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1","text":"Culture forms a recursive guilt loop: inhibition of aggression produces internalization, internalization produces guilt, guilt diminishes happiness, and the persisting problem of aggression produces intensified demands.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD2","text":"The unifying work of Eros produces cultural pathology insofar as it does not eliminate aggression, but compels its displacement against the subject.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD3","text":"Individual and cultural superego form coupled cycles of norm-setting, because cultural demands become individual demands of conscience and individual drive conflicts are collectively reproduced.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD4","text":"An unfulfillable ethical ideal sanctions the inability to follow it more reliably than it eliminates the aggression against which it is directed.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5","text":"The mastery of external natural forces intensifies the cultural crisis when control over means of destruction grows more rapidly than the capacity to bind internal aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6","text":"Psychoanalytic cultural diagnostics can make pathology visible, but produces neither an extra-cultural standard of normality nor a legitimate subject of collective therapy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD7","text":"A possible accommodation between individual and community does not end the superordinate conflict between Eros and the death drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX1","text":"Psychic efficacy does not presuppose transparent self-perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX2","text":"Rational insight or moral will grants the ego no sovereign control over its drives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX3","text":"Guilt cannot be derived from deprivation as such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX4","text":"Community formation and individual happiness do not converge of themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX5","text":"Aggression is neither exclusively a product of false education nor wholly reducible to property relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX6","text":"The transfer of individual-psychological concepts to collectives is not an operation neutral with respect to standards.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX7","text":"For a humanity affected in like manner, no unaffected normality is available as a background for comparison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX8","text":"History contains no secure teleology that vouches for cultural progress, happiness, and the victory of Eros together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX1","text":"Unavailable is a form of cultural unity whose binding of aggression manages without intensified guilt and loss of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX2","text":"Unavailable is an extra-cultural standpoint from which humanity as a whole could be determined unequivocally as normal or neurotic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX3","text":"Unavailable is a recognized authority that could treat a diagnosed social neurosis against the resistance of the masses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX4","text":"Unavailable is a consolation that demonstrates cultural sacrifices to be necessary, meaningful, or definitively compensated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5","text":"Unavailable is a terminal reconciliation of Eros and the death drive; the conclusion can only expect a counter-effort of Eros.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS1","text":"Eros + Ananke → community formation → restriction of individual drive satisfaction → conflict between happiness and affiliation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS2","text":"External authority + dependence on love → inhibition of aggression → anxiety before authority → early sense of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS3","text":"Internalization of authority → superego → equivalence of aggressive intention and aggressive deed → permanent production of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS4","text":"Inhibited aggression → displacement inward → superego aggression → guilt, need for punishment, or indeterminate malaise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS5","text":"Mixed drive tendency + repression → libidinal symptom component / aggressive guilt component → symptomatic binding to punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS6","text":"Individual-psychological structure → controlled scaling → cultural superego → ethics as institutionalized defense against aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS7","text":"Overburdening commandment + limited mastery of the ego → noncompliance → guilt, rebellion, neurosis, or unhappiness → therapeutic failure of the commandment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:FGS8","text":"Technical mastery of nature + persisting drive toward self-annihilation → global capacity for extermination → open decision between cultural binding and destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:AF1","text":"Incomprehensible relation between guilt and consciousness → conceptual differentiation → stratification of anxiety before external and internal authority → aggressive genesis of the sense of guilt → placement within Eros and the death drive → analogy of individual and cultural development → cultural superego → ethics as overburdened defense against aggression → limited diagnosis of community → question of technological self-annihilation → expected, not guaranteed, counter-effort of Eros.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME1","text":"Guilt is transferred from a moral category of deed into a psychic topic of anxiety, tension, and displacement of aggression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME2","text":"Consciousness loses the status of a reliable measure of psychic efficacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME3","text":"Drive disturbance is divided into libidinal and aggressive components; only the aggressive component receives an immediate guilt-generating function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME4","text":"Cultural progress is transferred from a logic of gain into an exchange structure of community formation, intensified guilt, and loss of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME5","text":"Individual development and cultural development are mapped as analogous processes with opposed weighting of aims.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME6","text":"The opposition individual/society is separated from the opposition Eros/death drive and reclassified as a conflict over the distribution of libido.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME7","text":"Ethics is reclassified from an autonomous normative order into a therapeutic technique of the cultural superego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME8","text":"The strategic landscape divides into moral commandment, material order of relations, and constitutional limit of drives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME9","text":"Under reservation, neurosis is extended from an individual pathology to a possible diagnostic model of entire cultures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10","text":"Technical progress becomes visible no longer merely as mastery of nature, but as an amplifier of unbound power of self-annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT1","text":"Surface level: sense of guilt, conscience, ethics, cultural progress, and present capacity for annihilation constitute the explicit objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2","text":"Structural level: internalization of authority shifts inhibited aggression inward and institutionalizes it as an individual or cultural superego.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic level: moral demand is replaced by an examination of psychic feasibility, material incentive structure, and diagnostic scope.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT4","text":"Ontological and temporal level: life and culture remain in the conflict between Eros and the death drive, not decided teleologically; technical development changes its potential for destruction, not its basic structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement from the topic of guilt through the cultural superego to the question of self-annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent provided that drive theory, the internalization of aggression, and the controlled individual-culture analogy are accepted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT3","text":"The exclusive derivation of the sense of guilt from renunciation of aggression remains empirically underdetermined and is itself posited only as a theoretically simplifying hypothesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT4","text":"The two sources of superego aggression are connected by the superordinate concept of aggression shifted inward, but are not causally weighted against one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT5","text":"The transfer to cultures remains limited by the absence of a comparison with normality, unsecured scaling, and the absence of a therapeutic authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT6","text":"The asserted superiority of altered property relations over ethical commandment remains without an elaborated mechanism of mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT7","text":"The highest inferential density lies in the chain inhibition of aggression → internalization → superego → guilt → loss of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT8","text":"Primal guilt, the historical genesis of the superego, and the origin of cultural ideals depend on presupposed earlier constructions and analogical compression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the argument; its endpoint remains prognostically open and is not decided deductively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_R2TV_KA_7:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_R2TV_KA_7@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_R2TV_KA_7:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 08","title":"Chapter VIII","context":"Chapter 08","original_title":"Kapitel VIII","original_context":"Chapter 08"},"original_title":"Kapitel VIII","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 01–03","order":1,"parents":["CH_R2TV_KAPI","CH_R2TV_KA_2","CH_R2TV_KA_3"],"revision":"CL_R2TV_01@R001","sha256":"e10b31da18b73cd6bddb7ef3c58339c59f833dc175e0ca49542e7bf5119e6ac2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-01","text":"Das System untersucht, wie religiöse Gewissheit, menschliche Glückserwartung und kulturelles Unbehagen aus psychischer Abhängigkeit und Leiden hervorgehen, ohne als Beweise einer transzendenten Ordnung gelten zu können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-02","text":"Ichbildung, Realitätsanpassung und Kulturentwicklung werden als verschachtelte Grenzbildungsprozesse rekonstruiert, die Schutz ermöglichen, indem sie Befriedigung beschränken.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-03","text":"Das Argument wird auf dieser Ebene zu einer diagnostischen, genetischen und libidoökonomischen Rekonstruktion subjektiver Erlebnisse, individueller Lebenstechniken und kollektiver Institutionen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","text":"Die Bewegung führt von behaupteter Wahrheit über genetische Umdeutung und funktionalen Vergleich zur Analyse der Kosten, die psychische und soziale Schutzordnungen selbst erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-05","text":"Die Grenze zwischen Selbst und Außen mutiert von einer entwickelten Abwehrleistung zur allgemeinen Form, in der Abhängigkeiten individuell verteilt und gesellschaftlich geregelt werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-06","text":"Das unerfüllbare Glücksprogramm erzeugt pluralisierte Lebenstechniken; Religion vereinheitlicht sie illusionär, während Kultur ihre Schutz- und Versagungsfunktionen institutionell generalisiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-07","text":"Die Bewegung ist kumulativ und rekursiv, weil jede Abwehrform bestimmte Leiden mindert, dabei jedoch neue Abhängigkeiten, Versagungen und Konflikte hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-08","text":"Die Schließung bleibt offen: Kultur erweist sich als notwendige, aber kompensationsbedürftige Triebverarbeitung, deren Ursprung und endgültige Vereinbarkeit mit Freiheit und Glück ungeklärt bleiben.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Weder subjektive Intensität noch kollektive Zustimmung legitimieren einen psychischen Inhalt als ontologische oder religiöse Wahrheit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Das Subjekt ist kein souveräner Ausgangspunkt, sondern eine geschichtete, begrenzte und von Körper, Außenwelt, Objekten und Trieben abhängige Formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Das Lustprinzip setzt ein unerfüllbares Glücksprogramm, das unter dem Druck der Realität in eine Vorrangordnung der Leidvermeidung überführt wird.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Infantile Hilflosigkeit wird von einer Quelle religiöser Energie zur Grundlage eines kollektiv standardisierten Schutz- und Vorsehungsmodells erweitert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Psychische Techniken und kulturelle Einrichtungen beseitigen Abhängigkeit nicht, sondern verteilen Lust, Leiden, Realitätsbindung und Verwundbarkeit neu.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Körper, Außenwelt und soziale Beziehungen bilden irreduzible Leidensfelder, wobei nur das soziale Feld institutionell veränderbar und zugleich psychisch rückgebunden ist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Das Realitätsprinzip erweitert sich von der Korrektur früher Ichgrenzen zur übergreifenden Logik individueller Anpassung und kultureller Regelung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Eine dauerhafte, allgemein gültige Versöhnung von Lust, Leidensschutz, Freiheit, psychischer Konstitution und Realität ist nicht verfügbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Religion transformiert ein Schutzbedürfnis in eine uniforme Technik, die individuelle Anpassung durch kollektive Fixierung und Wirklichkeitsentstellung ersetzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Kultur ist zugleich Schutzapparat und endogene Leidensproduktion, weil dieselben Einrichtungen, die Natur und soziale Gewalt begrenzen, Triebverzicht erzwingen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Recht hebt Gewalt nicht auf, sondern transformiert individuelle Gewalt in überlegene Gemeinschaftsmacht und bindet deren Stabilität an allgemeine Einschränkung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Triebverzicht bleibt nur begrenzt stabil, wenn die entzogene Befriedigung ökonomisch kompensiert wird; ausbleibende Kompensation erzeugt Störung und Kulturfeindseligkeit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Technische Verfügungsmacht und Kulturfortschritt bezeichnen keine proportionale Zunahme von Glück oder Vervollkommnung, sondern eine Reorganisation von Lebensbedingungen und Triebzielen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-14","text":"[Persistent] Vorgegebene Teleologie wird durch genetische und funktionale Rekonstruktion ersetzt: Zwecke gelten nur insoweit, als sie sich in psychischen und sozialen Operationen nachweisen lassen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","text":"Die Ichgrenze kehrt funktional als soziale Grenze wieder: Was zunächst Innen und Außen trennt, mutiert später zur rechtlichen und kulturellen Ordnung individueller Ansprüche.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-02","text":"Das Schutzbedürfnis behält seine Funktion, wechselt aber seinen Träger: Aus infantiler Abhängigkeit wird religiöse Vorsehung und schließlich institutionalisierte Uniformierung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-03","text":"Realitätsprüfung wandert aus der Ichgenese in die Glücksökonomie und von dort in die Kulturtheorie, ohne ihre Funktion der Begrenzung wunschbestimmter Ansprüche zu verlieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-04","text":"Soziales Leiden mutiert von einer äußeren Leidensquelle zum rekursiven Produkt des kulturellen Apparats, der andere Leiden vermindern soll.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-05","text":"Glück verschiebt sich vom vermeintlichen Lebenszweck über ein episodisches Lustgeschehen zu einer subjektiv inkommensurablen Größe, die keinen Kulturfortschritt messen kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-06","text":"Freiheit erscheint erst auf der sozialen Ebene und trägt eine umgekehrte Valenz: Sie kann ungerechte Einschränkung korrigieren oder die für Gemeinschaft erforderliche Einschränkung selbst angreifen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-07","text":"Psychische Erhaltung wird in eine nichtlineare Geschichtsform absorbiert: Frühere Formationen verschwinden nicht notwendig, während kulturelle Entwicklung Ziele und Charaktere reorganisiert, ohne sie zu vervollkommnen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-08","text":"Religion wechselt vom möglichen Gefühlsursprung zur vergleichbaren Lebenstechnik und schließlich zur kollektiven Fixierungsordnung; ihr Wahrheitsstatus verschwindet, nachdem er die genetische Analyse ausgelöst hat.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-01","text":"Ob das ozeanische Gefühl tatsächlich vorkommt, bleibt lokal unterbestimmt; nach oben skaliert allein die Trennung von phänomenalem Auftreten, genetischer Herkunft und kausaler Funktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-02","text":"Die einzelnen Lebenstechniken verbleiben als lokale Typologie; auf Clusterebene trägt die allgemeine Struktur, dass jeder Eingriff eine spezifische Kosten- und Abhängigkeitsverteilung erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-03","text":"Schönheit, Reinlichkeit, Ordnung und andere Kulturmerkmale bleiben lokale Bestimmungen; global werden die Nichterschöpfbarkeit der Kultur durch Nutzen und ihre Verankerung in Triebumbildung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-04","text":"Die konkrete Säuglingsrekonstruktion bleibt ein lokales genetisches Modell; global trägt sie die Proposition, dass Grenzen und Autonomie hervorgebrachte, störbare Leistungen sind.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:D1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-05","text":"Die Diagnose der Religion als Massenwahn bleibt eine zugespitzte lokale Klassifikation; auf Clusterebene skaliert die strukturell belastbarere Bestimmung religiöser Uniformierung und kollektiver Fixierung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-06","text":"Die Fortdauer psychischer Vergangenheit legitimiert keine Theorie kulturellen Gedächtnisses; sie skaliert nur als Modell nichtlinearer Persistenz unter fortgesetzter Transformation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-01","text":"Das System verwirft die Selbstbeglaubigung religiöser Erfahrung: Ein Gefühl ist weder Glaubenssatz noch unmittelbarer Erkenntniszugang.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:NX1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-02","text":"Es verwirft eine unabhängig gesicherte Teleologie und damit die Annahme, Welt oder Kultur seien auf menschliches Glück eingerichtet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-03","text":"Es verwirft das souveräne, von Bedürftigkeit, Trieb und Außenwelt unabhängige Subjekt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-04","text":"Es verwirft dauerhaft intensives Glück und jede Technik, die Lust, Leidensschutz, Realitätswahrung, Dauer und Allgemeingültigkeit zugleich gewährleisten soll.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-05","text":"Es verwirft Religion als privilegierte Wahrheits- und Glücksgarantie, ohne ihre psychische Trost- und Fixierungswirksamkeit zu leugnen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-06","text":"Es verwirft die Gleichsetzung technischer Macht mit Glückszuwachs und kultureller Entwicklung mit menschlicher Vervollkommnung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-07","text":"Es verwirft sowohl ein machtfreies Recht als auch die empirisch ungesicherte Flucht in einen glücklichen außerkulturellen Zustand.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-01","text":"Damit das System trägt, dürfen Lebensziele keinen irreduziblen Status außerhalb der Lust-, Schutz- und Ersatzökonomie besitzen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-02","text":"Vollständige Unabhängigkeit muss unmöglich sein; Autonomie darf nur als Verteilung, Dämpfung oder Verlagerung von Bindungen erscheinen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-03","text":"Soziale Institutionen dürfen weder von Triebstruktur noch von Machtverhältnissen unabhängig gedacht werden, ohne die Kulturtheorie in eine äußerliche Organisationslehre zurückfallen zu lassen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-04","text":"Kostenloser Schutz muss ausgeschlossen bleiben: Jede Abwehr- oder Kulturleistung muss neue Abhängigkeiten, Realitätsverluste oder Befriedigungsbeschränkungen erzeugen können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-05","text":"Eine vollständige Bilanzierung psychischer Vergangenheit und kulturellen Glücks muss unmöglich bleiben, weil weder innere Geschichte noch subjektive Glückswerte vollständig verfügbar oder kommensurabel sind.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-06","text":"Dauerhafte Triebversagung ohne Ersatz darf nicht stabilisierbar sein; andernfalls verlöre das Kompensationsproblem seine generative Funktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste versperrte Möglichkeit ist eine endgültige Versöhnung von Lustprinzip, Realität, individueller Freiheit und kultureller Ordnung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-02","text":"Abwesend bleibt ein vollständig souveränes Subjekt, das seine Grenzen, Bedürfnisse, Objekte und sozialen Bindungen aus eigener Macht setzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-03","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Kultur ohne Triebopfer, Feindseligkeit und psychische Kosten; gerade diese Abwesenheit treibt die Kulturdiagnose an.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-04","text":"Das System besitzt weder ein terminales Verlaufsgesetz der Kultur noch ein bestimmbares Äquivalent zwischen gefordertem Opfer und gewährtem Gewinn.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-05","text":"Ein unvermittelter Zugang zur unendlichen Selbst-Welt-Einheit bleibt ausgeschlossen; seine Nichtverfügbarkeit strukturiert die Umdeutung religiöser Erfahrung in psychische Genese.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-01","text":"Psychische und soziale Ordnung erweisen sich als homologe Grenzmaschinen: Unlust erzeugt Ausschließung, während Recht individuelle Macht in eine kollektiv stabilisierte Begrenzung überführt. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","CL_R2TV_01:GA-07","CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KAPI:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-02","text":"Religion institutionalisiert infantile Hilflosigkeit, indem sie ein individuelles Schutzbedürfnis in eine uniforme kollektive Anpassungsordnung transformiert. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","CL_R2TV_01:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-03","text":"Individuelle Lebenstechniken und Kultur sind Operationen derselben Kostenökonomie auf verschiedenen Skalen: Beide lindern Leiden durch Eingriffe, die neue Versagungen und Abhängigkeiten erzeugen. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-04","text":"Die soziale Leidensquelle ist kein bloßer dritter Außenfaktor, sondern das rekursive Nebenprodukt jener Kultur, die Naturübermacht und individuelle Gewalt begrenzen soll. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-06","CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-05","text":"Technische Verfügungsmacht kann Glück nicht proportional steigern, weil Lust episodisch, Leiden dauerhaft möglich und kultureller Schutz selbst kostenförmig bleibt. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-03","CL_R2TV_01:GA-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-06","text":"Recht stabilisiert Gemeinschaft durch kollektivierte Macht und allgemeine Einschränkung, erzeugt aber im fortbestehenden Freiheitsdrang zugleich seine Reformkraft und seinen möglichen Gegner. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","CL_R2TV_01:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-07","text":"Psychische und kulturelle Geschichte folgen derselben nichtlinearen Form: Frühere Strukturen können fortwirken, während ihre Ziele, Funktionen und Valenzen reorganisiert werden. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-08","text":"Praktische Anpassung und kulturelle Stabilität konvergieren im Kompensationsprinzip: Verteilung kann Risiken mindern, aber keine versagte Befriedigung ohne psychischen Preis neutralisieren. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_01:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-01","text":"Realität erscheint als verschachteltes Regulationssystem, in dem psychische Grenzen, individuelle Techniken und kulturelle Institutionen Druck in Bindung, Verzicht und Ersatzleistung umwandeln.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird zu einem endlichen Verteilungsknoten der Libidoökonomie, dessen Charakter, Autonomie und Handlungsspielraum aus fortgesetzter Trieb- und Umweltbearbeitung hervorgehen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-03","text":"Religion wird zu einer politischen Psychotechnik: Sie bindet Schutzbedürftigkeit an kollektiv verbindliche Deutung, Fixierung und Unterwerfung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-04","text":"Geschichte verliert die Form linearen Fortschritts und wird zur Persistenz unter Mutation, in der frühere psychische Formationen und neue kulturelle Ordnungen gleichzeitig wirksam bleiben können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-05","text":"Handlungsmacht besteht nicht in Unabhängigkeit, sondern in der revidierbaren Auswahl von Bindungen, der Verteilung von Risiken und der institutionellen Korrektur ungleicher Einschränkungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnis wird methodisch von Intensität, Tradition und Zweckbehauptung auf Genese, Funktion, Kosten und Transformationspfade umgestellt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-01","text":"Unlust erzeugt Grenzbildung; Grenzbildung erzeugt Abhängigkeit von ihren Schutzmechanismen; diese Abhängigkeit erzeugt neue Verwundbarkeit und erneute Unlust.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-02","text":"Hilflosigkeit erzeugt Schutzsehnsucht; Schutzsehnsucht erzeugt religiöse Uniformierung; deren enttäuschtes Versprechen endet in Unterwerfung und reproduziert Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-03","text":"Das unerfüllbare Glücksprogramm erzeugt Lebenstechniken; deren spezifische Kosten erzeugen Diversifikation; ausschließliche Festlegung steigert erneut das Scheiternsrisiko.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-04","text":"Kultur lindert Natur- und Sozialgefahren, erzeugt durch Versagung Kulturfeindlichkeit und beantwortet diese Feindseligkeit mit weiterer Regelung und Triebverarbeitung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-05","text":"Individuelle Gewalt wird kollektiviert, als Recht stabilisiert, durch Freiheit herausgefordert und entweder gerechter reorganisiert oder als kulturelle Einschränkung insgesamt bekämpft.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-06","text":"Technischer Fortschritt steigert Erwartungen, ohne Glück proportional zu erhöhen; die daraus entstehende Enttäuschung intensiviert Kulturkritik und weitere Verfügungstechniken.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-07","text":"Der begriffliche Attraktor ist Kompensation: Alle Pfade konvergieren auf die ungelöste Frage, welche Ersatzbefriedigung den für Schutz und Gemeinschaft verlangten Verzicht tragfähig machen kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B01","text":"Religiöser Ursprungsanspruch → Analyse des Vorstellungsinhalts → genetische Rekonstruktion → Entzug ontologischer Selbstbeglaubigung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B02","text":"Frühe Selbst-Welt-Ungetrenntheit → Unlustabwehr → Grenzbildung → Realitätsprüfung → begrenztes und störbares Ich.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS3","CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B03","text":"Psychische Erhaltung → mögliche Erklärung des Einheitserlebens → Trennung von Zustandsgenese und religionskausaler Energie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS4","CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B04","text":"Hilflosigkeit → Vatersehnsucht → Schutzbedürfnis → religiöse Vorsehung → kollektive Fixierung und Unterwerfung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B05","text":"Entzug vorgegebener Teleologie → Rekonstruktion beobachtbaren Verhaltens → Glücksstreben → Unerfüllbarkeit → Vorrang der Leidabwehr.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:D1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B06","text":"Leidensdruck → Eingriffe in Organismus, Trieb, Objekt und Umwelt → partielle Entlastung → spezifischer Preis → kontingente Diversifikation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B07","text":"Individuelle Abwehr → kollektiver Naturschutz und Beziehungsregelung → Gemeinschaftsmacht → Recht → allgemeine Einschränkung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B08","text":"Triebumbildung → Charakter, Sublimierung und Versagung → Kulturleistung plus Kulturfeindseligkeit → Kompensationsproblem → offene Ursprungserklärung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AFM-B01","text":"Behauptete Allverbundenheit → Psychogenese der Ichgrenze → Hilflosigkeit als religiöse Energie → Entzug der Teleologie → unerfüllbares Glücksprogramm → pluralisierte Lebenstechniken → religiöse Uniformierung → soziale Leidensfrage → Kultur als Schutz und Versagung → Recht-Freiheits-Konflikt → Kompensationsproblem.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AFM-B02","text":"Individuelle Grenzbildung → individuelle Leidabwehr → kollektive Grenzbildung → kulturelle Leidproduktion → Triebumbildung ohne endgültige Versöhnung oder terminales Verlaufsgesetz.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-01","text":"Religion wird vom möglichen Zeugnis transzendenter Einheit zur psychogenetisch erklärbaren und institutionell standardisierten Schutztechnik umkartiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-02","text":"Psychische Grenze und soziale Ordnung werden als verwandte Hervorbringungen sichtbar; dadurch zerfällt der Gegensatz zwischen natürlichem Innen-Außen-Schnitt und bloß äußerer Rechtsregel.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-03","text":"Glück wird von einem stabilen Zielzustand zu einer episodischen, subjektiven und für Fortschrittsbilanzen ungeeigneten Größe umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-04","text":"Individuelle Lebensführung und Kulturordnung werden als verschiedene Maßstäbe derselben Abwehr- und Kostenökonomie lesbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-05","text":"Der Gegensatz von Recht und Gewalt kollabiert zugunsten der Unterscheidung zwischen individueller Gewalt und kollektiv organisierter Macht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-06","text":"Freiheit und Fortschritt verlieren ihre eindeutig positive Valenz: Freiheit kann reformieren oder desintegrieren, Fortschritt kann Macht steigern, ohne Glück oder Vervollkommnung zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene werden religiöse Ursprungserfahrung, menschliche Glückstechniken und der zweifelhafte Glückswert der Kultur untersucht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene operieren Ichgrenze, Lust- und Realitätsprinzip, Libidoverschiebung, Triebumbildung, Gemeinschaftsmacht und Recht als gekoppelte Regulationsmechanismen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene werden subjektive Gewissheit, universale Lebensregel und pauschales Kultururteil durch genetische Prüfung, Kostenvergleich und rekursive Funktionsanalyse ersetzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-temporalen Ebene ist Realität nicht auf Glück eingerichtet, das Subjekt bleibt endlicher Naturkörper und Vergangenheit wirkt unter Mutation fort, ohne linearen Fortschritt zu garantieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollzieht die Argumentform selbst die behauptete Entprivilegierung, indem sie intensive Ansprüche seriell in Genesen, Funktionen, Kosten und offene Spannungen zerlegt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-01","text":"Die Reduktion aller Lebensziele auf Lust, Schutz oder Ersatz steht in Spannung zur Anerkennung kultureller Werte, die sich durch Nützlichkeit nicht erschöpfen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-02","text":"Die genetische Erklärung des ozeanischen Gefühls bleibt eine Möglichkeit, während ihre systemische Verwendung leicht den Eindruck einer nachgewiesenen tatsächlichen Regression erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-03","text":"Die Zurückweisung allgemeiner Glücksrezepte steht in produktiver Spannung zur verallgemeinerten Empfehlung von Anpassung, Diversifikation und Vermeidung ausschließlicher Festlegung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-04","text":"Zwischen der deskriptiven Herleitung des Rechts aus Gemeinschaftsmacht und dem Ziel allgemeiner Gerechtigkeit bleibt eine nicht aufgelöste normative Brücke.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-05","text":"Die soziale Leidensquelle gilt zugleich als institutionell veränderbar und als Ausdruck einer psychischen Grenze; diese Doppelbestimmung ermöglicht Kritik, droht aber soziale Kontingenz zu naturalisieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-06","text":"Religion wird zugleich als kollektive Pathologie und als Schutz vor individueller Neurose bestimmt, ohne dass die Grenze zwischen normalisierter Fixierung und Störung abschließend geklärt wird.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-01","text":"Das ozeanische Gefühl mutiert vom beanspruchten Transzendenzzeugnis zum möglichen Rest einer frühen psychischen Formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD2","CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-02","text":"Religion mutiert von der Frage nach ihrer Gefühlsquelle über eine individuelle Trosttechnik zu einer kollektiv verbindlichen Fixierungs- und Unterwerfungsordnung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-03","text":"Das Realitätsprinzip mutiert von der Korrektur der Ichgrenze zum Auswahlkriterium individueller Lebenstechniken und zur Funktionslogik kultureller Schutzordnungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-04","text":"Kulturfortschritt mutiert von technischer Machtsteigerung zu einer wertneutralen Reorganisation von Triebzielen, Charakterformen und institutionellen Einschränkungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-01","text":"Realität erscheint als verschachtelte Grenz- und Umwandlungsmaschine, die Druck in Abwehr, Bindung, Recht und Triebverzicht überführt und dabei neue Druckformen erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist darin kein Zentrum souveräner Verfügung, sondern ein geschichteter Knoten, der Abhängigkeiten zwischen Körper, Welt, Objekten und Gemeinschaft umverteilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist asymmetrisch und nichtlinear: Lust ist episodisch, Leiden dauerhaft möglich, und frühere Formationen bleiben unter späteren Transformationen wirksam.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-04","text":"Möglich bleibt keine endgültige Flucht, sondern nur die revidierbare Navigation von Bindungen, die politische Korrektur ungleicher Einschränkungen und die Suche nach tragfähiger Kompensation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B01","text":"Die extrahierten Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von der genetischen Entzauberung religiöser Erfahrung über die Glücksökonomie zur rekursiven Kulturtheorie zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B02","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben das tatsächliche Vorkommen des ozeanischen Gefühls, einzelne metapsychologische Mechanismen sowie Ursprung, Verlaufsgesetz und Bilanzgröße der Kulturentwicklung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B03","text":"Das System ist kohärent, sofern phänomenales Vorkommen, genetische Herkunft, psychische Funktion und kulturelle Institutionalisierung getrennt sowie Schutz und Versagung als verschiedene Funktionsachsen behandelt werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B04","text":"Die stärkste Architektur liegt in der skalierbaren Verbindung von Grenzbildung, Lust-Leid-Asymmetrie, kostenförmiger Abwehr und kompensationsbedürftigem Triebverzicht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B05","text":"Einer vollständigen axiomatischen Reduktion widerstehen die singuläre Qualität berichteter Erfahrung, nichtutilitäre Kulturwerte und der normative Überschuss der Gerechtigkeit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:NX2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B06","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung, bleibt aber von serieller Umdeutung, diagnostischer Kompression und der offenen Rückkehr des Kompensationsproblems abhängig.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171653646180Z_4a64bf52","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 01–03","source_sha256":"e10b31da18b73cd6bddb7ef3c58339c59f833dc175e0ca49542e7bf5119e6ac2","sha256":"8bcc42ca3cf45ea6ed188dbaa21b2a3a2581b2ea79e544cb7fcbbcff13ffcfea","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:16:53.647035+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-01","text":"The system examines how religious certainty, human expectations of happiness, and cultural discontent arise from psychic dependency and suffering, without being able to count as proofs of a transcendent order.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-02","text":"Ego formation, adaptation to reality, and cultural development are reconstructed as nested processes of boundary formation that enable protection by restricting satisfaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-03","text":"At this level, the argument becomes a diagnostic, genetic, and libidinal-economic reconstruction of subjective experiences, individual techniques of living, and collective institutions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","text":"The movement leads from asserted truth through genetic reinterpretation and functional comparison to the analysis of the costs that psychic and social protective orders themselves produce.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-05","text":"The boundary between self and outside mutates from a developed defensive achievement into the general form in which dependencies are individually distributed and socially regulated.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-06","text":"The unfulfillable happiness programme produces pluralized techniques of living; religion illusorily unifies them, while culture institutionally generalizes its functions of protection and renunciation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-07","text":"The movement is cumulative and recursive because every form of defense mitigates certain sufferings while thereby producing new dependencies, renunciations, and conflicts.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AS-08","text":"The closure remains open: culture proves to be a necessary but compensation-requiring processing of drives, whose origin and final compatibility with freedom and happiness remain unresolved.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Neither subjective intensity nor collective assent legitimates a psychic content as ontological or religious truth.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The subject is not a sovereign point of departure, but a layered, bounded formation dependent on body, external world, objects, and drives.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The pleasure principle posits an unfulfillable happiness programme that, under the pressure of reality, is transformed into an order prioritizing the avoidance of suffering.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Infantile helplessness is expanded from a source of religious energy into the foundation of a collectively standardized model of protection and providence.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Psychic techniques and cultural institutions do not eliminate dependency, but redistribute pleasure, suffering, reality-bondage, and vulnerability.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Body, external world, and social relations constitute irreducible fields of suffering, whereby only the social field is institutionally alterable and simultaneously psychically tethered.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] The reality principle expands from the correction of early ego boundaries into the overarching logic of individual adaptation and cultural regulation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] A lasting, universally valid reconciliation of pleasure, protection from suffering, freedom, psychic constitution, and reality is unavailable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Religion transforms a need for protection into a uniform technique that replaces individual adaptation with collective fixation and distortion of reality.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Culture is at once a protective apparatus and endogenous production of suffering, because the very institutions that limit nature and social violence enforce instinctual renunciation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Law does not abolish violence, but transforms individual violence into superior communal power and ties its stability to universal restriction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Instinctual renunciation remains stable only to a limited extent when withdrawn satisfaction is economically compensated; absent compensation produces disturbance and hostility to culture.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Technical power of disposal and cultural progress do not denote a proportional increase in happiness or perfection, but a reorganization of conditions of life and instinctual aims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GA-14","text":"[Persistent] Given teleology is replaced by genetic and functional reconstruction: purposes hold only insofar as they can be demonstrated in psychic and social operations.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","text":"The ego boundary recurs functionally as a social boundary: what initially separates inside and outside later mutates into the legal and cultural ordering of individual claims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-02","text":"The need for protection retains its function but changes its bearer: infantile dependency becomes religious providence and finally institutionalized uniformity.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-03","text":"Reality-testing migrates from ego genesis into the economy of happiness and thence into cultural theory, without losing its function of limiting wish-determined claims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-04","text":"Social suffering mutates from an external source of suffering into the recursive product of the cultural apparatus that is supposed to mitigate other sufferings.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-05","text":"Happiness shifts from its presumed status as the purpose of life through an episodic occurrence of pleasure to a subjectively incommensurable magnitude that cannot measure cultural progress.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-06","text":"Freedom appears only at the social level and bears an inverted valence: it can correct unjust restriction or itself attack the restriction required for community.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-07","text":"Psychic preservation is absorbed into a nonlinear form of history: earlier formations do not necessarily disappear, while cultural development reorganizes aims and characters without perfecting them.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RMD-08","text":"Religion shifts from a possible origin in feeling to a comparable technique of living and finally to an order of collective fixation; its truth status disappears after it has triggered genetic analysis.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-01","text":"Whether the oceanic feeling actually occurs remains locally underdetermined; what alone scales upward is the distinction between phenomenal occurrence, genetic origin, and causal function.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-02","text":"The individual techniques of living remain a local typology; at the cluster level, the general structure bears that every intervention produces a specific distribution of costs and dependencies.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-03","text":"Beauty, cleanliness, order, and other cultural features remain local determinations; globally, what holds are the inexhaustibility of culture by utility and its grounding in instinctual transformation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-04","text":"The concrete reconstruction of infancy remains a local genetic model; globally, it bears the proposition that boundaries and autonomy are produced, disruptible achievements.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:D1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-05","text":"The diagnosis of religion as a mass delusion remains a pointed local classification; at the cluster level, the structurally more robust determination of religious uniformity and collective fixation scales.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:CGD-06","text":"The persistence of psychic past does not legitimate a theory of cultural memory; it scales only as a model of nonlinear persistence under continuing transformation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects the self-authentication of religious experience: a feeling is neither a proposition of belief nor immediate access to knowledge.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:NX1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-02","text":"It rejects an independently secured teleology and thus the assumption that world or culture is arranged for human happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-03","text":"It rejects the sovereign subject independent of neediness, drive, and external world.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-04","text":"It rejects enduring intense happiness and every technique meant simultaneously to guarantee pleasure, protection from suffering, preservation of reality, duration, and universal validity.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:NX4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-05","text":"It rejects religion as a privileged guarantee of truth and happiness, without denying its psychic efficacy of consolation and fixation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-06","text":"It rejects the equation of technical power with an increase in happiness and of cultural development with human perfection.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:GNX-07","text":"It rejects both law free of power and the empirically unsecured flight into a happy extra-cultural state.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, life aims must not possess an irreducible status outside the economy of pleasure, protection, and substitution.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-02","text":"Complete independence must be impossible; autonomy may appear only as distribution, attenuation, or displacement of ties.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-03","text":"Social institutions must not be conceived independently of either drive structure or relations of power, lest cultural theory fall back into an external doctrine of organization.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-04","text":"Cost-free protection must remain excluded: every defensive or cultural achievement must be able to produce new dependencies, losses of reality, or restrictions of satisfaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-05","text":"A complete accounting of psychic past and cultural happiness must remain impossible, because neither inner history nor subjective values of happiness are fully available or commensurable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:DBN-06","text":"Enduring instinctual renunciation without substitution must not be stabilizable; otherwise the problem of compensation would lose its generative function.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-01","text":"The deepest barred possibility is a final reconciliation of the pleasure principle, reality, individual freedom, and cultural order.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-02","text":"Absent remains a completely sovereign subject that posits its boundaries, needs, objects, and social ties by its own power.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-03","text":"Unavailable is a culture without instinctual sacrifice, hostility, and psychic costs; precisely this absence drives the diagnosis of culture.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-04","text":"The system possesses neither a terminal law of cultural development nor a determinable equivalent between the sacrifice demanded and the gain granted.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSA-05","text":"Unmediated access to the infinite unity of self and world remains excluded; its unavailability structures the reinterpretation of religious experience into psychic genesis.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-01","text":"Psychic and social order prove to be homologous boundary-machines: unpleasure produces exclusion, while law transforms individual power into a collectively stabilized limitation. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","CL_R2TV_01:GA-07","CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KAPI:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-02","text":"Religion institutionalizes infantile helplessness by transforming an individual need for protection into a uniform collective order of adaptation. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","CL_R2TV_01:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-03","text":"Individual techniques of living and culture are operations of the same economy of costs at different scales: both mitigate suffering through interventions that produce new renunciations and dependencies. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-04","text":"The social source of suffering is not a mere third external factor, but the recursive by-product of that culture which is supposed to limit the power of nature and individual violence. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-06","CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-05","text":"Technical power of disposal cannot increase happiness proportionally, because pleasure is episodic, suffering remains permanently possible, and cultural protection itself retains the form of cost. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-03","CL_R2TV_01:GA-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-06","text":"Law stabilizes community through collectivized power and universal restriction, but in the persisting drive toward freedom it simultaneously produces its reforming force and its possible adversary. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","CL_R2TV_01:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-07","text":"Psychic and cultural history follow the same nonlinear form: earlier structures can continue to operate while their aims, functions, and valences are reorganized. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:XD-08","text":"Practical adaptation and cultural stability converge in the principle of compensation: distribution can mitigate risks, but cannot neutralize denied satisfaction without a psychic price. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_01:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-01","text":"Reality appears as a nested system of regulation in which psychic boundaries, individual techniques, and cultural institutions transform pressure into binding, renunciation, and substitutive achievement.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes a finite node of distribution within the libidinal economy, whose character, autonomy, and scope for action arise from the continuing processing of drives and environment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-03","text":"Religion becomes a political psychotechnique: it binds the need for protection to collectively binding interpretation, fixation, and subjection.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-04","text":"History loses the form of linear progress and becomes persistence under mutation, in which earlier psychic formations and new cultural orders can remain effective simultaneously.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-05","text":"Agency consists not in independence, but in the revisable selection of ties, the distribution of risks, and the institutional correction of unequal restrictions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:BSD-06","text":"Knowledge is methodically shifted from intensity, tradition, and assertions of purpose to genesis, function, costs, and paths of transformation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-01","text":"Unpleasure produces boundary formation; boundary formation produces dependency on its protective mechanisms; this dependency produces new vulnerability and renewed unpleasure.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-02","text":"Helplessness produces longing for protection; longing for protection produces religious uniformity; its disappointed promise ends in subjection and reproduces dependency.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-03","text":"The unfulfillable happiness programme produces techniques of living; their specific costs produce diversification; exclusive commitment again increases the risk of failure.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A16","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-04","text":"Culture mitigates natural and social dangers, produces hostility to culture through renunciation, and answers this hostility with further regulation and processing of drives.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-05","text":"Individual violence is collectivized, stabilized as law, challenged by freedom, and either reorganized more justly or combated as cultural restriction altogether.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-06","text":"Technical progress raises expectations without increasing happiness proportionally; the resulting disappointment intensifies cultural critique and further techniques of disposal.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:RLE-07","text":"The conceptual attractor is compensation: all paths converge upon the unresolved question of which substitute satisfaction can make the renunciation demanded for protection and community sustainable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B01","text":"Religious claim of origin → analysis of representational content → genetic reconstruction → withdrawal of ontological self-authentication.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS1","CH_R2TV_KAPI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B02","text":"Early undifferentiatedness of self and world → defense against unpleasure → boundary formation → reality-testing → bounded and disruptible ego.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS3","CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B03","text":"Psychic preservation → possible explanation of the experience of unity → separation of state genesis and religiously causal energy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS4","CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B04","text":"Helplessness → longing for the father → need for protection → religious providence → collective fixation and subjection.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:FGS6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B05","text":"Withdrawal of given teleology → reconstruction of observable behavior → striving for happiness → unfulfillability → priority of defense against suffering.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:D1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B06","text":"Pressure of suffering → interventions in organism, drive, object, and environment → partial relief → specific price → contingent diversification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B07","text":"Individual defense → collective protection against nature and regulation of relations → communal power → law → universal restriction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FGS-B08","text":"Transformation of drives → character, sublimation, and renunciation → cultural achievement plus hostility to culture → problem of compensation → open explanation of origin.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AFM-B01","text":"Asserted universal connectedness → psychogenesis of the ego boundary → helplessness as religious energy → withdrawal of teleology → unfulfillable happiness programme → pluralized techniques of living → religious uniformity → question of social suffering → culture as protection and renunciation → conflict between law and freedom → problem of compensation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:AFM-B02","text":"Individual boundary formation → individual defense against suffering → collective boundary formation → cultural production of suffering → transformation of drives without final reconciliation or terminal law of development.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-01","text":"Religion is remapped from possible testimony to transcendent unity into a psychogenetically explicable and institutionally standardized technique of protection.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-02","text":"Psychic boundary and social order become visible as related productions; thereby the opposition between the natural cut of inside and outside and a merely external rule of law disintegrates.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-03","text":"Happiness is reclassified from a stable target state into an episodic, subjective magnitude unsuitable for assessments of progress.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-04","text":"Individual conduct of life and cultural order become readable as different scales of the same economy of defense and costs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-05","text":"The opposition between law and violence collapses in favor of the distinction between individual violence and collectively organized power.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MME-06","text":"Freedom and progress lose their unambiguously positive valence: freedom can reform or disintegrate, progress can increase power without producing happiness or perfection.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, religious experience of origin, human techniques of happiness, and the dubious happiness-value of culture are investigated.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, ego boundary, pleasure and reality principles, displacement of libido, transformation of drives, communal power, and law operate as coupled mechanisms of regulation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, subjective certainty, universal rule of life, and blanket judgment of culture are replaced by genetic examination, comparison of costs, and recursive functional analysis.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, reality is not arranged for happiness, the subject remains a finite natural body, and the past continues to operate under mutation without guaranteeing linear progress.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the argument's form itself enacts the asserted deprivileging by serially decomposing intensive claims into geneses, functions, costs, and open tensions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-01","text":"The reduction of all life aims to pleasure, protection, or substitution stands in tension with the recognition of cultural values that are not exhausted by utility.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:DNX5","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-02","text":"The genetic explanation of the oceanic feeling remains a possibility, while its systemic use easily creates the impression of an actually demonstrated regression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-03","text":"The rejection of general recipes for happiness stands in productive tension with the generalized recommendation of adaptation, diversification, and avoidance of exclusive commitment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-04","text":"Between the descriptive derivation of law from communal power and the aim of universal justice, an unresolved normative bridge remains.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:NX7","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-05","text":"The social source of suffering counts both as institutionally alterable and as expression of a psychic boundary; this double determination enables critique but threatens to naturalize social contingency.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:D1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:FL-06","text":"Religion is determined both as collective pathology and as protection against individual neurosis, without the boundary between normalized fixation and disturbance being conclusively clarified.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-01","text":"The oceanic feeling mutates from claimed testimony of transcendence into a possible remnant of an early psychic formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:SD2","CH_R2TV_KAPI:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-02","text":"Religion mutates from the question of its source in feeling through an individual technique of consolation into a collectively binding order of fixation and subjection.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_2:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-03","text":"The reality principle mutates from the correction of the ego boundary into the criterion of selection for individual techniques of living and into the functional logic of cultural protective orders.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_2:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MP-04","text":"Cultural progress mutates from an increase in technical power into a value-neutral reorganization of instinctual aims, forms of character, and institutional restrictions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a nested machine of boundaries and transformations that converts pressure into defense, binding, law, and instinctual renunciation while producing new forms of pressure.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-02","text":"Within it, the subject is not a center of sovereign disposal, but a layered node that redistributes dependencies between body, world, objects, and community.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is asymmetrical and nonlinear: pleasure is episodic, suffering remains permanently possible, and earlier formations remain effective beneath later transformations.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:HSI-04","text":"What remains possible is not a final escape, but only the revisable navigation of ties, the political correction of unequal restrictions, and the search for sustainable compensation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_2:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_3:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the genetic disenchantment of religious experience through the economy of happiness to recursive cultural theory.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B02","text":"What remains underdetermined are the actual occurrence of the oceanic feeling, individual metapsychological mechanisms, and the origin, law of development, and accounting magnitude of cultural development.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B03","text":"The system is coherent insofar as phenomenal occurrence, genetic origin, psychic function, and cultural institutionalization are separated, and protection and renunciation are treated as different functional axes.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B04","text":"The strongest architecture lies in the scalable connection of boundary formation, pleasure-suffering asymmetry, defense in the form of cost, and instinctual renunciation requiring compensation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT4","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT4","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B05","text":"Resisting a complete axiomatic reduction are the singular quality of reported experience, non-utilitarian cultural values, and the normative surplus of justice.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:NX2","CH_R2TV_KA_3:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement, but remains dependent on serial reinterpretation, diagnostic compression, and the open return of the problem of compensation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPI:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_2:MRT9","CH_R2TV_KA_3:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_R2TV_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_R2TV_01:v1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Chapters 01–03"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review","title":"Chapters 01–03","context":"Chapter I · Chapter II · Chapter III","original_title":"Chapters 01–03","original_context":"Kapitel I · Kapitel II · Kapitel III"},"original_title":"Chapters 01–03","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 04–06","order":2,"parents":["CH_R2TV_KA_4","CH_R2TV_KAPV","CH_R2TV_KA_5"],"revision":"CL_R2TV_02@R001","sha256":"7d47a955b43242ec803c73bde556256a552f73db76b0d56873822a38f1854d92","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-01","text":"Das zentrale Problem besteht darin, wie Kultur größere und dauerhaftere Einheiten erzeugen kann, obwohl intensive Bindung zur Exklusivität tendiert und primäre Feindseligkeit jeden erweiterten Verband bedroht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-02","text":"Kultur wird als Triebapparat bestimmt, der Libido in soziale Bindung überführt und Aggression hemmt, umlenkt oder bindet, ohne eine dieser Energien selbst hervorzubringen oder vollständig zu beherrschen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-03","text":"Das Argument steigt von einer Genealogie kultureller Bindungsformen über eine Ökonomie begrenzter Libido zur metapsychologischen Begründung eines selbständigen Aggressions- und Destruktionsprinzips ab.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-04","text":"Die Bewegung führt von Eros und Ananke über Recht, Sexualeinschränkung und Aggressionsverwaltung zur Dualisierung von verbindendem Eros und auflösendem Todestrieb.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-05","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv, weil kulturelle Bindung ihre libidinöse Grundlage beschneidet und jede Aggressionshemmung die destruktive Energie lediglich verlagert oder neu legiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-06","text":"Institutionen wechseln ihren Kausalstatus: Familie, Eigentum, Recht und Moral erscheinen nicht mehr als letzte Ursachen, sondern als historische Medien eines tieferen Triebkonflikts.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-07","text":"Kulturzeit wird nicht als Fortschrittslinie, sondern als fortdauernde und maßstabsabhängig wiederkehrende Auseinandersetzung zwischen Einheitsbildung und Auflösung konstruiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-08","text":"Die Schließung ist terminal, aber nicht versöhnend: Ein konfliktfreier kultureller Endzustand wird ausgeschlossen, während vermeidbares Leiden von strukturell unaufhebbarem Konflikt nur unvollständig getrennt bleibt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Große kulturelle Verbände benötigen libidinöse Bindungen, weil Arbeitsvorteil und Zweckgemeinschaft menschliche Mengen nicht dauerhaft zusammenhalten.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Libido und psychische Energie sind begrenzt und besetzungsträge; jede kulturelle Umverteilung erzeugt deshalb Widerstand, Entzug oder Ersatzbildung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Liebe ist zunächst Keimform intensiver Sozialität, wird dann zum Hindernis ihrer Ausdehnung und schließlich als Eros zum allgemeinen Prinzip wachsender Einheitsbildung erweitert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Die Vergrößerung kultureller Einheiten verlangt eine Transformation exklusiver sexueller und familialer Bindungen in breiter verteilte, zielgehemmte oder identifikatorische Beziehungen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Kultur institutionalisiert wechselseitige Triebeinschränkung als Recht, Norm und Sicherheitsordnung und erkauft dadurch Stabilität mit verminderter unmittelbarer Befriedigung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Aggression wird von einer diagnostizierten menschlichen Feindseligkeit zur ursprünglichen Triebanlage und schließlich zur nach außen gewendeten Erscheinungsform des Todestriebs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Kultur ist ein Doppelapparat, der Libido sozial verteilt und Aggression begrenzt, ohne die von ihm bearbeiteten Kräfte endgültig aufheben zu können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Nach außen gewendete Destruktion kann individuelle Selbsterhaltung und lokale Gruppenkohäsion fördern, widersetzt sich aber der kulturellen Einigung auf größerem Maßstab.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Aggressionshemmung beseitigt Destruktion nicht, sondern erzeugt durch Externalisierung, psychische Umformung oder Rückwendung neue individuelle und kollektive Pathologien.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Reformen können institutionelle Werkzeuge der Aggression verändern und vermeidbares Leiden mindern, nicht aber notwendig den Triebkonflikt beseitigen, der Kultur erforderlich macht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Kulturentwicklung ist die geschichtliche Vollzugsform des unabschließbaren Kampfes zwischen dem einheitsbildenden Eros und der gegen Einigung gerichteten Destruktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Kulturfortschritt garantiert weder Glück noch Befreiung, weil jeder Sicherheitsgewinn Kosten an sexueller Befriedigung, Freiheit und psychischer Integrität erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-01","text":"Ananke und Arbeit bewahren ihre Identität als materielle Kooperationsbedingungen, verlieren aber ihre anfängliche Stellung als hinreichende Erklärung dauerhafter Vergesellschaftung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-02","text":"Liebe kehrt funktional verändert wieder: als familiale Haftung, als umzuleitende Libido und schließlich als überindividuelles Erosprinzip der Einheitsbildung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-03","text":"Die Familie wird nicht unverändert fortgeführt, sondern in die allgemeinere Struktur dyadischer Exklusivität absorbiert; ihre genealogischen Einzelheiten verschwinden, ihre Skalengrenze bleibt wirksam.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-04","text":"Einschränkung eskaliert von standardisierten Sexualverboten über kulturelle Aggressionshemmung zur möglichen Rückwendung destruktiver Energie gegen das Subjekt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-05","text":"Recht mutiert von der genealogisch ersten Form wechselseitiger Selbstbeschränkung zu einem Teilapparat umfassender Triebbegrenzung, der rohe Gewalt eindämmt, aber feinere Aggression nicht erfasst.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","text":"Aggression durchläuft die stärkste ontologische Eskalation: Das Liebesgebot macht sie diagnostisch sichtbar, ihre Ursprünglichkeit verselbständigt sie, und der Todestrieb liefert ihren verborgenen Grund.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-07","text":"Universale Liebe erfährt eine Valenzumkehr, sobald innere Solidarität durch äußere Aggression stabilisiert wird und der Einigungsanspruch selbst Ausschluss produziert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-08","text":"Sicherheit verschiebt den Glücksbegriff von unmittelbarer Befriedigung zu geschützter Koexistenz, widerlegt damit aber jede teleologische Gleichsetzung von Kulturzuwachs und Glückszuwachs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-09","text":"Der Todestrieb ist eine terminale Transformation des Aggressionsbegriffs: Er wird zum Attraktor der Architektur, bleibt jedoch nur indirekt und in Mischungen zugänglich.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-01","text":"Die organische Genealogie von Aufrichtung, Geruchsverdrängung und Scham bleibt lokal und spekulativ; nach oben skaliert nur die Regel, dass die Architektur nicht von dieser ungesicherten Herkunftserzählung abhängt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-02","text":"Vatermord und Brüderbund bleiben lokale genealogische Figuren; global tragend wird die Umcodierung des Rechts als institutionalisierte Selbstbeschränkung konkurrierender Triebansprüche.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-03","text":"Monogamie, Genitalität und Heterosexualität bleiben konkrete Normformen; auf Clusterebene skaliert der Konflikt zwischen universalisierter Regulierung und heterogenen sexuellen Dispositionen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-04","text":"Die kommunistische Eigentumskritik bleibt ein politischer Testfall; nach oben skaliert die Unterscheidung zwischen institutionellen Aggressionsmitteln und dem nicht institutionell erzeugten Aggressionssubstrat.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-05","text":"Die besondere These über Führerindividualitäten bleibt lokal; global fortbesteht die Einsicht, dass kulturelle Bindungstechniken selbst Massenelend, Außenfeindschaft und andere Pathologien hervorbringen können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-06","text":"Die technische Revision des Ich-/Objekttrieb-Gegensatzes bleibt Begründungsschicht; auf Clusterebene skaliert ihr Ergebnis als Dualismus zwischen verbindendem Eros und auflösender Destruktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-07","text":"Sadismus und Masochismus bleiben lokale Indikatoren; global relevant wird die Regel, dass Triebkräfte in Mischungen erscheinen und theoretische Wirklichkeit nicht mit direkter Sichtbarkeit zusammenfällt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:D2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-01","text":"Dauerhafte Kultur wird nicht aus rationalem Eigeninteresse, Arbeitsteilung oder gemeinsamem Nutzen allein erklärbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-02","text":"Erotische Liebe ist keine unverändert universalisierbare Grundlage großer Gemeinschaften, und ein moralisches Liebesgebot erzeugt nicht selbst die psychischen Bedingungen seiner Erfüllung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-03","text":"Psychische Energie ist weder unbegrenzt noch verlustfrei von exklusiver Sexualität in kulturelle Bindung überführbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-04","text":"Aggression ist weder bloße Reaktion auf Eigentum und Knappheit noch vollständig aus fehlerhafter gesellschaftlicher Organisation ableitbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-05","text":"Recht, Moral und Aufklärung können Destruktion nicht vollständig eliminieren, weil sie feinere Ausdrucksformen verfehlen und keine zureichende Gewalt über den Triebgrund besitzen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-06","text":"Kultur ist nicht der Gegenpol einer triebhaften Natur, sondern deren spezifische Organisation auf sozialem und geschichtlichem Maßstab.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-07","text":"Kulturentwicklung ist keine fortschreitende Aufhebung ihres Grundkonflikts und keine automatische Steigerung von Glück.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-01","text":"Falsch sein muss eine monistische Theorie, die Bindung, Aggression und Destruktion restlos aus Libido oder Liebe ableitet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-02","text":"Falsch sein muss die Annahme, exklusive Sexualität könne unangetastet bleiben, während Kultur ihre Bindungsreichweite ohne qualitative Transformation vergrößert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-03","text":"Falsch sein muss ein Modell, in dem Eigentum, Institutionen oder historische Umstände menschliche Feindseligkeit ursprünglich erzeugen statt kanalisieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-04","text":"Falsch sein muss die Gleichsetzung normativer Geltung mit psychischer Vollziehbarkeit; Ideale werden an ihren Triebbedingungen und nicht an ihrer moralischen Reinheit geprüft.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-05","text":"Falsch sein muss ein Empirismus, der nur unmittelbar isolierbare Kräfte als theoretisch wirklich anerkennt, weil Destruktion gerade über Mischungen und Residuen erschlossen wird.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-06","text":"Falsch sein muss die Vorstellung, Kultur könne außerhalb des Triebkonflikts stehen und ihn von einer neutralen Position aus endgültig befrieden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-01","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Großgemeinschaft, die exklusive Liebe vollständig bewahrt und dennoch ohne deren Einschränkung universale kulturelle Bindung erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine universale Liebe, deren innere Solidarität keinen Ausschluss, kein Außen und keine aggressive Ersatzbefriedigung erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-03","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine politische Ordnung, in der Sicherheit, freie Triebbefriedigung und konfliktfreie Gleichheit endgültig zusammenfallen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-04","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein geschichtlicher Endzustand, in dem Einheitsbildung keinen Widerstand der Destruktion mehr bearbeiten muss.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-05","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine vollständig positive und isolierte Erkenntnis des Todestriebs; seine konstitutive Abwesenheit zwingt die Theorie zur residualen Rekonstruktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-01","text":"Kultur kann nicht durch bloße Addition familialer oder dyadischer Einheiten wachsen, sondern muss die Bindungsform, aus der sie hervorgeht, partiell entsexualisieren und umverteilen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-03","CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-02","text":"Weil begrenzte Libido und ursprüngliche Aggression zugleich bearbeitet werden müssen, ist jeder Integrationsgewinn eine Neuverteilung von Befriedigung, Bindung und destruktivem Risiko.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-03","text":"Recht ist eine unvollständige institutionelle Übersetzung von Triebkonflikt in Selbstbeschränkung: Es reduziert offene Gewalt, ohne angepasste oder verdeckte Aggression aufzuheben.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-04","text":"Die aggressive Externalisierung stabilisiert begrenzte Gemeinschaften gerade dadurch, dass sie das erosgeleitete Programm einer umfassenden Menschheitseinheit unterläuft.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-08","CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-05","text":"Die kulturelle Hemmung äußerer Aggression kann Sicherheit erzeugen und zugleich die Selbstzerstörung intensivieren, sodass gesellschaftliche Befriedung psychische Destruktion verlagert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CL_R2TV_02:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-06","text":"Politische Reform kann die Kanäle und Instrumente von Aggression verändern, aber aus der Veränderung ihrer Mittel folgt keine Aufhebung ihres vorausgesetzten Triebgrundes.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-07","text":"Das Gebot universaler Liebe fungiert zugleich als Gegenmittel und diagnostischer Indikator, weil seine psychische Unwahrscheinlichkeit die Aggression sichtbar macht, gegen die es gerichtet ist.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-08","text":"Die indirekte Erschließung des Todestriebs erweitert soziale Aggressionsphänomene zu ontologischen Indizien, erzeugt aber eine zirkuläre Gefährdung, weil die Mischphänomene zugleich Prämisse und Erklärung des verborgenen Triebs werden.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-09","text":"Die universalistische Form kultureller Normierung verteilt Triebverzicht ungleich, weil sie heterogene sexuelle Konstitutionen einer einheitlichen Sicherheits- und Bindungsordnung unterstellt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-01","text":"Soziale Realität wird zur Erscheinungsfläche eines vorsozialen Triebantagonismus; Institutionen organisieren den Konflikt zwischen Bindung und Auflösung, den sie weder erzeugen noch verlassen können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird von einem souveränen Handlungskern zu einem Umschlagpunkt, an dem Libido zwischen Ich und Objekten wandert und Destruktion nach außen oder innen gerichtet wird.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-03","text":"Kausalität wird geschichtet: Triebe liefern das Substrat, Institutionen bestimmen seine Kanäle, und dieselbe destruktive Energie verbindet individuelle, politische und kulturelle Konflikte.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-04","text":"Geschichte erhält eine rekursive Zeitform, in der Einheitsbildung und Auflösung auf wechselnden Maßstäben wiederkehren, ohne einen teleologischen Abschluss zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-05","text":"Ethik wird zur Triebdiagnostik: Ein moralisches Ideal wird danach gelesen, welche psychische Gegenkraft seine übersteigerte Forderung voraussetzt und welche Abwehrfunktion es erfüllt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-06","text":"Politik wird in begrenzte institutionelle Veränderbarkeit und nicht sicher reformierbare Triebkosten geteilt; diese Grenze bleibt operativ notwendig, aber kriteriell unscharf.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-07","text":"Handlungsmacht besteht nicht in der Abschaffung des Antagonismus, sondern in der prekären Umlenkung seiner Energien, wobei jede Bindungsstrategie eigene Pathologien und Ausschlüsse erzeugen kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-08","text":"Kulturelles Unbehagen ist kein bloßer Defekt der Kultur, sondern ein rekursiver Effekt der Operationen, durch die Kultur ihre libidinöse Grundlage beschneidet und Destruktion verlagert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-01","text":"Libidinöse Bindung erzeugt Familie und Kultur; kulturelle Expansion beschränkt exklusive Bindung; diese Beschränkung schwächt die eigene Bindungsquelle und steigert den Bedarf an kultureller Ersatzbindung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-02","text":"Aggression erzeugt kulturelle Hemmung; Hemmung erzeugt Umleitung oder Innenwendung; deren Pathologien provozieren weitere Kontrolle und schließen die Aggressionsverwaltung rekursiv.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-03","text":"Innere Gruppenbindung leitet Aggression nach außen, Außenfeindschaft verdichtet die innere Bindung, und die verdichtete Gruppe reproduziert damit ihre antagonistische Grenze.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-04","text":"Sicherheit verlangt Triebverzicht, Triebverzicht erzeugt Unbehagen und Ersatzbildungen, und deren Gefährdungen legitimieren erneute Sicherheitssteigerung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-05","text":"Der Eskalationspfad führt von der Kooperation durch Eros und Ananke über die Diagnose primärer Feindseligkeit zur ontologischen Bestimmung von Aggression als externalisierter Destruktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-06","text":"Die Wiederkehr der Liebe markiert Phasenwechsel: Bindung wird zunächst sozialer Inhalt, dann kulturell zu verteilende Energie und schließlich ein allgemeines Prinzip der Einheitsbildung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-07","text":"Der Eros-Todestrieb-Gegensatz bildet den begrifflichen Attraktor, auf den Familienkonflikt, Sexualeinschränkung, Gruppenfeindschaft und Kulturgeschichte nachträglich konvergieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-08","text":"Die theoretische Schleife des Todestriebs führt von schwer erklärbaren Mischphänomenen zur Annahme eines verborgenen Triebs und von diesem Trieb zurück zur Erklärung eben jener Mischphänomene.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B01","text":"Äußere Notwendigkeit + dauerhafte erotische Bindung → Kooperation und Familie → lokale, aber noch nicht hinreichend kulturelle Sozialität.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B02","text":"Exklusive Familie + kulturelle Vergrößerung → Skalierungskonflikt zwischen intensiver Zweier- oder Nahbindung und extensiver Vergesellschaftung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B03","text":"Rivalität + kollektive Gegenmacht → wechselseitige Einschränkung → Tabu und Recht als institutionalisierter Triebkompromiss.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B04","text":"Endliche Libido + kultureller Bindungsbedarf → Umlenkung aus unmittelbarer Sexualität → Entbehrung, Ungleichheit und Ersatzbildung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B05","text":"Primäre Feindseligkeit + unzureichende Arbeitsinteressen → moralische und institutionelle Aggressionsabwehr → unvollständige Befriedung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B06","text":"Aggressionshemmung → Externalisierung, Reaktionsbildung oder Innenwendung → Gruppenfeindschaft, Massenpathologie oder Selbstzerstörung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B07","text":"Ursprüngliche Aggression + metapsychologischer Rest → Todestrieb → Kultur als artspezifische Austragung des Konflikts zwischen Einigung und Auflösung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B08","text":"Eros/Todestrieb-Dualismus + geschichtliche Skalierung → rekursive Kulturentwicklung → terminale Schließung ohne versöhnten Endzustand.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B01","text":"Arbeitsnot und erotische Dauerbindung → familiale Exklusivität → wechselseitige Restriktion und Recht → Umverteilung endlicher Libido → Diagnose primärer Aggression → kulturelle Aggressionsverwaltung → Todestrieb als verborgener Grund → Kulturgeschichte als unabschließbarer Eros-Destruktions-Kampf.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B02","text":"Die Endposition kehrt rekursiv zum Ausgang zurück: Kultur benötigt Bindung, beschädigt deren unmittelbare Formen, verlagert die dadurch verschärften Konflikte und benötigt deshalb erneut Bindung und Einschränkung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-01","text":"Kultur wird von einem Fortschrittsraum zu einem Triebmetabolismus umkartiert, der Libido verteilt und Aggression verwaltet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-02","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen Familie und Kultur kollabiert zugunsten einer Skalendifferenz innerhalb derselben Bindungslogik: Was lokal integriert, kann globale Integration blockieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-03","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen Natur und Kultur kollabiert, weil das Soziale als historische Organisation und nicht als Überwindung eines naturhaften Triebkonflikts erscheint.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-04","text":"Liebe und Aggression werden nicht mehr als reine Gegensätze lesbar, weil soziale Bindungen destruktive Legierungen enthalten und innere Solidarität äußere Feindschaft mobilisieren kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-05","text":"Recht und Reform werden von Erlösungsinstanzen zu Kanaltechniken umklassifiziert, die konkurrierende Triebansprüche beschränken und Aggressionsmittel verändern.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-06","text":"Moralische und politische Modelle müssen fortan an ihren psychischen Vollzugsbedingungen, nicht allein an ihren normativen Zielen geprüft werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-07","text":"Gruppenidentität und Außenfeindschaft bilden eine gemeinsame Grenzmaschine; die strategische Landschaft wird daher nach Umlenkungsrichtungen statt nach dem Gegensatz von Integration und Konflikt kartiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-08","text":"Indirekte, residuale und mischungsbezogene Lektüre wird methodisch notwendig, weil die tragende destruktive Kraft nicht als isolierter positiver Gegenstand erscheint.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Surface level erscheinen Familie, Liebe, Sexualität, Tabu, Nächstenliebe, Eigentum, Gruppenfeindschaft sowie die theoretische Anerkennung eines selbständigen Aggressionstriebs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der Structural level stabilisiert Kultur größere Verbände durch Arbeit, Recht, libidinöse Verteilung und permanente Begrenzung einer nicht aufhebbaren destruktiven Anlage.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der Metastrategic level werden sexuelle Normen, Moralgebote und politische Reformmodelle als Verfahren kultureller Energieverwaltung und anhand ihrer psychischen Durchsetzbarkeit gelesen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der Ontological / Temporal level werden Leben, Subjekt und Geschichte als dauerhafte Auseinandersetzung von Bindung, Triebanspruch, Sicherheit, Einheitsbildung und Auflösung bestimmt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der Methodological / Performative level vollzieht die Architektur selbst einen Abstieg von genealogischen Hypothesen über soziale Symptome zu indirekt erschlossenen Grundkräften und macht wiederholte Negation zum Rekonstruktionsverfahren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-01","text":"Die behauptete Ursprünglichkeit und Selbständigkeit der Aggression steht in Spannung zur nur indirekten und gemischten Beobachtbarkeit ihres Todestriebgrundes.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-02","text":"Kultur soll als Erosprozeß Aggression überwinden, beansprucht aber selbst Gewalt und kann ihre innere Bindung durch Aggression gegen Außenstehende stabilisieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-03","text":"Liebe ist zugleich kulturelle Voraussetzung, privilegierte Glücksquelle, exklusive Gegenkraft zur Erweiterung und Objekt kultureller Beschädigung; ihre Mehrdeutigkeit ist konstitutiv statt auflösbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-04","text":"Aggression fungiert zugleich als destruktive Gegenmacht der Kultur und als Mittel von Selbsterhaltung und Naturbeherrschung; ihre Valenz hängt von Richtung und Maßstab ab.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-05","text":"Die Grenze zwischen reformierbarem Kulturleid und wesensnotwendigem Triebverzicht bleibt ohne eindeutiges Kriterium und trägt dennoch die politische Begrenzung der Reformhoffnung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-06","text":"Der universale Triebdualismus erklärt die Wiederkehr kultureller Konflikte, unterbestimmt aber, weshalb sie historisch gerade die Formen von Familie, Eigentum, Sexualnorm und Gruppenordnung annehmen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-01","text":"Der Liebesbegriff mutiert von einer konkreten familialen Bindung über sozial umzuleitende Libido zum kosmologisch erweiterten Erosprinzip.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-02","text":"Aggression mutiert von der durch das Liebesgebot freigelegten Feindseligkeit zur selbständigen Triebanlage und danach zur externalisierten Tätigkeit des Todestriebs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-03","text":"Einschränkung mutiert von wechselseitiger Rechtsbindung über kulturelle Sexualhemmung zur Umlenkung und möglichen Selbstwendung destruktiver Energie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-04","text":"Der Kausalstatus gesellschaftlicher Institutionen kehrt sich um: Sie werden von vermeintlichen Ursprüngen des Konflikts zu Werkzeugen und Erscheinungsformen einer vorausgesetzten Triebantinomie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als Maschine zweier gegenläufiger Ströme: Eros erhält und verdichtet lebende Einheiten, während Destruktion ihre Bindungen löst und sie zum Anorganischen zurückführt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist ein Umschaltknoten, der Libido zwischen Ich und Objekten verteilt und destruktive Energie entweder gegen die Außenwelt oder gegen sich selbst richtet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-03","text":"Zeit ist weder linear noch kumulativ versöhnend, sondern die wiederholte Austragung desselben Antagonismus auf individuellen, institutionellen und menschheitsgeschichtlichen Maßstäben.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-04","text":"Möglich bleibt nur partielle Navigation: Aggression kann gehemmt, Libido umgeleitet und vermeidbares Leid vermindert werden, doch ein Außen oder endgültiger Fluchtpunkt des Triebkonflikts bleibt ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B01","text":"Die Architektur ist rekonstruierbar, wenn endliche Libido, notwendige Sozialbindung, ursprüngliche Aggression und der Eros-Todestrieb-Dualismus als minimale tragende Axiome erhalten bleiben.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B02","text":"Die Kohärenz bleibt konditional, weil sie voraussetzt, dass indirekte Mischphänomene die Annahme eines nicht unmittelbar sichtbaren Todestriebs zureichend begründen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B03","text":"Am stärksten ist die Architektur dort, wo soziale Aggression nicht als nachträgliches Beispiel, sondern als Übergang vom kulturellen Bindungsproblem zum Triebdualismus fungiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B04","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die unabhängige Identifikation des Todestriebs und die Herkunft der vorausgesetzten Aggressionsneigung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B05","text":"Ebenfalls unterbestimmt bleibt, wie notwendiger Triebverzicht von vermeidbarer institutioneller Schädigung abgegrenzt und durch weniger schädliche Vermittlungen ersetzt werden könnte.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B06","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn genealogische Hypothesen als Trägerschichten und Kulturinstitutionen als artspezifische Projektionen eines tieferen Konflikts behandelt werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B07","text":"Der axiomatischen Reduktion widersteht der Todestrieb selbst: Ohne ihn verliert die terminale Schließung ihren Grund, mit ihm überschreitet die Architektur ihre unmittelbar nachweisbare Evidenz.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171741650639Z_cee1acbc","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 04–06","source_sha256":"7d47a955b43242ec803c73bde556256a552f73db76b0d56873822a38f1854d92","sha256":"f885e9b7c0b39ac3a04e655180e39870011d8b420cd29ebea4da57353086c9be","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:17:41.653433+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-01","text":"The central problem consists in how culture can produce larger and more enduring units, although intense attachment tends toward exclusivity and primary hostility threatens every expanded association.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-02","text":"Culture is determined as a drive apparatus that transforms libido into social attachment and inhibits, redirects, or binds aggression, without itself producing or fully mastering any of these energies.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-03","text":"The argument descends from a genealogy of cultural forms of attachment through an economy of limited libido to the metapsychological grounding of an autonomous principle of aggression and destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-04","text":"The movement leads from Eros and Ananke through law, sexual restriction, and the management of aggression to the dualization of binding Eros and dissolving death drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-05","text":"The movement is recursive because cultural attachment curtails its libidinal basis and every inhibition of aggression merely displaces or newly alloys destructive energy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-06","text":"Institutions change their causal status: family, property, law, and morality no longer appear as ultimate causes, but as historical media of a deeper conflict of drives.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-07","text":"Cultural time is constructed not as a line of progress, but as an enduring and scale-dependently recurrent conflict between the formation of unity and dissolution.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AS-08","text":"The closure is terminal but not reconciliatory: a conflict-free cultural end state is excluded, while avoidable suffering remains only incompletely distinguished from structurally unresolvable conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Large cultural associations require libidinal attachments because the advantages of labor and purposive association do not hold human multitudes together permanently.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Libido and psychic energy are limited and inertial in cathexis; every cultural redistribution therefore produces resistance, withdrawal, or substitute formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Love is initially the germinal form of intense sociality, then becomes an obstacle to its expansion, and finally is extended as Eros into the general principle of increasing unity formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The enlargement of cultural units requires a transformation of exclusive sexual and familial attachments into more broadly distributed, aim-inhibited, or identificatory relations.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Culture institutionalizes reciprocal drive restriction as law, norm, and an order of security, thereby purchasing stability at the cost of diminished immediate satisfaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Aggression is transformed from a diagnosed human hostility into an original drive disposition and finally into the outwardly directed manifestation of the death drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Culture is a dual apparatus that distributes libido socially and limits aggression, without being able definitively to abolish the forces it processes.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Outwardly directed destruction can promote individual self-preservation and local group cohesion, but resists cultural unification on a larger scale.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] The inhibition of aggression does not eliminate destruction, but produces new individual and collective pathologies through externalization, psychic transformation, or reversal against the self.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Reforms can alter institutional instruments of aggression and reduce avoidable suffering, but cannot necessarily eliminate the conflict of drives that makes culture necessary.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Cultural development is the historical mode of enactment of the interminable struggle between unifying Eros and destruction directed against unification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Cultural progress guarantees neither happiness nor liberation, because every gain in security incurs costs in sexual satisfaction, freedom, and psychic integrity.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-01","text":"Ananke and labor retain their identity as material conditions of cooperation, but lose their initial status as a sufficient explanation of enduring socialization.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-02","text":"Love recurs with altered function: as familial attachment, as libido to be redirected, and finally as a supra-individual Eros principle of unity formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-03","text":"The family is not carried forward unchanged, but absorbed into the more general structure of dyadic exclusivity; its genealogical particulars disappear, while its scale limit remains effective.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-04","text":"Restriction escalates from standardized sexual prohibitions through cultural inhibition of aggression to the possible reversal of destructive energy against the subject.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-05","text":"Law mutates from the genealogically first form of reciprocal self-restraint into a sub-apparatus of comprehensive drive limitation, which restrains raw violence but does not capture subtler aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","text":"Aggression undergoes the strongest ontological escalation: the commandment of love renders it diagnostically visible, its originality makes it autonomous, and the death drive supplies its hidden ground.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-07","text":"Universal love undergoes a reversal of valence as soon as internal solidarity is stabilized by external aggression and the claim to unification itself produces exclusion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-08","text":"Security shifts the concept of happiness from immediate satisfaction to protected coexistence, but thereby refutes every teleological equation of cultural growth with growth in happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RMD-09","text":"The death drive is a terminal transformation of the concept of aggression: it becomes the attractor of the architecture, yet remains accessible only indirectly and in mixtures.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-01","text":"The organic genealogy of upright posture, repression of smell, and shame remains local and speculative; what scales upward is only the rule that the architecture does not depend on this unsecured narrative of origin.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-02","text":"Parricide and the band of brothers remain local genealogical figures; globally load-bearing is the recoding of law as institutionalized self-restraint of competing drive claims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-03","text":"Monogamy, genitality, and heterosexuality remain concrete normative forms; at the cluster level, the conflict between universalized regulation and heterogeneous sexual dispositions scales.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-04","text":"Communist criticism of property remains a political test case; what scales upward is the distinction between institutional means of aggression and the aggression substrate not produced institutionally.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-05","text":"The special thesis concerning leader individualities remains local; globally enduring is the insight that cultural techniques of attachment can themselves produce mass misery, external hostility, and other pathologies.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A14","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-06","text":"The technical revision of the opposition between ego drives and object drives remains a grounding layer; at the cluster level, its result scales as a dualism between binding Eros and dissolving destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:CGD-07","text":"Sadism and masochism remain local indicators; globally relevant becomes the rule that drive forces appear in mixtures and that theoretical reality does not coincide with direct visibility.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:D2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-01","text":"Enduring culture cannot be explained by rational self-interest, division of labor, or common benefit alone.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-02","text":"Erotic love is not an unchanged, universalizable foundation of large communities, and a moral commandment of love does not itself produce the psychic conditions of its fulfillment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-03","text":"Psychic energy is neither unlimited nor transferable without loss from exclusive sexuality into cultural attachment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:DNX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-04","text":"Aggression is neither a mere reaction to property and scarcity nor fully derivable from defective social organization.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-05","text":"Law, morality, and enlightenment cannot completely eliminate destruction, because they miss subtler forms of expression and possess no sufficient power over the ground of the drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-06","text":"Culture is not the opposite pole of a drive-based nature, but its specific organization on a social and historical scale.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:GNX-07","text":"Cultural development is neither a progressive abolition of its fundamental conflict nor an automatic increase in happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:NX2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-01","text":"A monistic theory that derives attachment, aggression, and destruction exhaustively from libido or love must be false.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-02","text":"The assumption that exclusive sexuality could remain untouched while culture enlarges its range of attachment without qualitative transformation must be false.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-03","text":"A model in which property, institutions, or historical circumstances originally produce rather than channel human hostility must be false.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-04","text":"The equation of normative validity with psychic practicability must be false; ideals are tested by their drive conditions and not by their moral purity.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-05","text":"An empiricism that recognizes as theoretically real only forces immediately isolable must be false, because destruction is inferred precisely through mixtures and residues.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:DBN-06","text":"The notion that culture could stand outside the conflict of drives and definitively pacify it from a neutral position must be false.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-01","text":"Unavailable is a large community that fully preserves exclusive love and nevertheless generates universal cultural attachment without restricting it.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is a universal love whose internal solidarity produces no exclusion, no outside, and no aggressive substitute satisfaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-03","text":"Unavailable is a political order in which security, free drive satisfaction, and conflict-free equality definitively coincide.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-04","text":"Unavailable is a historical end state in which unity formation no longer has to process the resistance of destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSA-05","text":"Unavailable is a fully positive and isolated cognition of the death drive; its constitutive absence compels theory toward residual reconstruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-01","text":"Culture cannot grow through the mere addition of familial or dyadic units, but must partially desexualize and redistribute the form of attachment from which it emerges.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-03","CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-02","text":"Because limited libido and original aggression must be processed simultaneously, every gain in integration is a redistribution of satisfaction, attachment, and destructive risk.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-03","text":"Law is an incomplete institutional translation of conflict of drives into self-restraint: it reduces open violence without abolishing adapted or concealed aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-04","text":"Aggressive externalization stabilizes limited communities precisely by undermining the Eros-guided program of a comprehensive unity of humanity.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-08","CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-05","text":"The cultural inhibition of external aggression can generate security while simultaneously intensifying self-destruction, such that social pacification displaces psychic destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CL_R2TV_02:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-06","text":"Political reform can alter the channels and instruments of aggression, but no abolition of its presupposed drive ground follows from the alteration of its means.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-07","text":"The commandment of universal love functions simultaneously as antidote and diagnostic indicator, because its psychic improbability makes visible the aggression against which it is directed.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-08","text":"The indirect inference of the death drive expands social phenomena of aggression into ontological indications, but generates a circular vulnerability because the mixed phenomena become both premise and explanation of the hidden drive.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:XD-09","text":"The universalist form of cultural norm-setting distributes drive renunciation unequally because it subjects heterogeneous sexual constitutions to a uniform order of security and attachment.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_4:D7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-01","text":"Social reality becomes the surface of appearance of a pre-social antagonism of drives; institutions organize the conflict between attachment and dissolution, which they can neither produce nor leave.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-02","text":"The subject is transformed from a sovereign core of action into a switching point at which libido migrates between ego and objects and destruction is directed outward or inward.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-03","text":"Causality becomes layered: drives supply the substrate, institutions determine its channels, and the same destructive energy connects individual, political, and cultural conflicts.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-04","text":"History acquires a recursive temporal form in which unity formation and dissolution recur at changing scales without producing a teleological closure.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-05","text":"Ethics becomes drive diagnostics: a moral ideal is read according to what psychic counterforce its excessive demand presupposes and what defensive function it fulfills.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-06","text":"Politics is divided into limited institutional modifiability and drive costs not reliably reformable; this boundary remains operationally necessary but criterially indeterminate.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-07","text":"Agency consists not in abolishing antagonism, but in the precarious redirection of its energies, whereby every strategy of attachment can produce its own pathologies and exclusions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:BSD-08","text":"Cultural discontent is not a mere defect of culture, but a recursive effect of the operations through which culture curtails its libidinal basis and displaces destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-01","text":"Libidinal attachment produces family and culture; cultural expansion restricts exclusive attachment; this restriction weakens its own source of attachment and increases the need for cultural substitute attachment.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:FGS7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-02","text":"Aggression produces cultural inhibition; inhibition produces redirection or inward reversal; their pathologies provoke further control and recursively close the management of aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-03","text":"Internal group attachment directs aggression outward, external hostility condenses internal attachment, and the condensed group thereby reproduces its antagonistic boundary.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A11","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-04","text":"Security demands drive renunciation, drive renunciation produces discontent and substitute formations, and their dangers legitimate a renewed increase in security.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A12","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-05","text":"The path of escalation leads from cooperation through Eros and Ananke via the diagnosis of primary hostility to the ontological determination of aggression as externalized destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A6","CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-06","text":"The recurrence of love marks phase changes: attachment initially becomes social content, then culturally distributable energy, and finally a general principle of unity formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-07","text":"The Eros–death drive opposition forms the conceptual attractor to which family conflict, sexual restriction, group hostility, and cultural history subsequently converge.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:RLE-08","text":"The theoretical loop of the death drive leads from difficult-to-explain mixed phenomena to the assumption of a hidden drive and from this drive back to the explanation of precisely those mixed phenomena.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B01","text":"External necessity + enduring erotic attachment → cooperation and family → local, but not yet sufficiently cultural, sociality.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B02","text":"Exclusive family + cultural enlargement → conflict of scale between intense dyadic or close attachment and extensive socialization.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B03","text":"Rivalry + collective counterpower → reciprocal restriction → taboo and law as institutionalized drive compromise.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B04","text":"Finite libido + cultural need for attachment → redirection away from immediate sexuality → deprivation, inequality, and substitute formation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:D5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B05","text":"Primary hostility + insufficient interests of labor → moral and institutional defense against aggression → incomplete pacification.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A8","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B06","text":"Inhibition of aggression → externalization, reaction formation, or inward reversal → group hostility, mass pathology, or self-destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B07","text":"Original aggression + metapsychological remainder → death drive → culture as species-specific enactment of the conflict between unification and dissolution.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FGS-B08","text":"Eros/death drive dualism + historical scaling → recursive cultural development → terminal closure without a reconciled end state.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:FGS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B01","text":"Necessity of labor and enduring erotic attachment → familial exclusivity → reciprocal restriction and law → redistribution of finite libido → diagnosis of primary aggression → cultural management of aggression → death drive as hidden ground → cultural history as interminable Eros–destruction struggle.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AF2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B02","text":"The end position returns recursively to the beginning: culture requires attachment, damages its immediate forms, displaces the conflicts thereby intensified, and therefore again requires attachment and restriction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-01","text":"Culture is remapped from a space of progress into a drive metabolism that distributes libido and manages aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-02","text":"The opposition between family and culture collapses in favor of a difference of scale within the same logic of attachment: what integrates locally can block global integration.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-03","text":"The opposition between nature and culture collapses because the social appears as historical organization and not as the overcoming of a natural conflict of drives.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:ME4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-04","text":"Love and aggression can no longer be read as pure opposites, because social attachments contain destructive alloys and internal solidarity can mobilize external hostility.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-05","text":"Law and reform are reclassified from agencies of redemption into channel techniques that restrict competing drive claims and alter means of aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ME3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-06","text":"Moral and political models must henceforth be tested by their psychic conditions of enactment, not solely by their normative aims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-07","text":"Group identity and external hostility form a common boundary machine; the strategic landscape is therefore mapped according to directions of redirection rather than according to the opposition between integration and conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ME4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MME-08","text":"Indirect, residual, and mixture-related reading becomes methodologically necessary because the load-bearing destructive force does not appear as an isolated positive object.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B01","text":"At the Surface level appear family, love, sexuality, taboo, love of neighbor, property, group hostility, and the theoretical recognition of an autonomous aggression drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT1","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B02","text":"At the Structural level, culture stabilizes larger associations through labor, law, libidinal distribution, and the permanent limitation of a non-abolishable destructive disposition.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B03","text":"At the Metastrategic level, sexual norms, moral commandments, and models of political reform are read as procedures of cultural energy management and in terms of their psychic enforceability.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT3","CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B04","text":"At the Ontological / Temporal level, life, subject, and history are determined as the enduring conflict of attachment, drive claim, security, unity formation, and dissolution.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B05","text":"At the Methodological / Performative level, the architecture itself performs a descent from genealogical hypotheses through social symptoms to indirectly inferred fundamental forces, and makes repeated negation a procedure of reconstruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:ALT5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-01","text":"The asserted originality and autonomy of aggression stand in tension with the only indirect and mixed observability of its death-drive ground.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-02","text":"Culture is supposed to overcome aggression as an Eros process, yet itself lays claim to violence and can stabilize its internal attachment through aggression against outsiders.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A10","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-03","text":"Love is simultaneously a cultural precondition, a privileged source of happiness, an exclusive counterforce to expansion, and an object of cultural damage; its ambiguity is constitutive rather than resolvable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT6","CH_R2TV_KA_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-04","text":"Aggression functions simultaneously as the destructive counterforce of culture and as a means of self-preservation and mastery of nature; its valence depends on direction and scale.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-05","text":"The boundary between culturally reformable suffering and essentially necessary drive renunciation remains without an unequivocal criterion and nevertheless bears the political limitation of hope for reform.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:FL-06","text":"Universal drive dualism explains the recurrence of cultural conflicts, but underdetermines why they historically assume precisely the forms of family, property, sexual norm, and group order.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:D7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-01","text":"The concept of love mutates from a concrete familial attachment through socially redirectable libido into a cosmologically expanded Eros principle.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:AS4","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-02","text":"Aggression mutates from the hostility disclosed by the commandment of love into an autonomous drive disposition and thereafter into the externalized activity of the death drive.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-03","text":"Restriction mutates from reciprocal legal attachment through cultural sexual inhibition into the redirection and possible self-turning of destructive energy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:A5","CH_R2TV_KAPV:A6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MP-04","text":"The causal status of social institutions is reversed: they are transformed from supposed origins of conflict into tools and manifestations of a presupposed antinomy of drives.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:AS5","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a machine of two countervailing currents: Eros preserves and condenses living units, while destruction dissolves their attachments and returns them to the inorganic.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a switching node that distributes libido between ego and objects and directs destructive energy either against the external world or against itself.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-03","text":"Time is neither linear nor cumulatively reconciliatory, but the repeated enactment of the same antagonism on individual, institutional, and human-historical scales.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_5:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:HSI-04","text":"Only partial navigation remains possible: aggression can be inhibited, libido redirected, and avoidable suffering reduced, but an outside or definitive point of escape from the conflict of drives remains excluded.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:A9","CH_R2TV_KAPV:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B01","text":"The architecture is reconstructible if finite libido, necessary social attachment, original aggression, and Eros–death drive dualism are retained as minimal load-bearing axioms.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B02","text":"Coherence remains conditional because it presupposes that indirect mixed phenomena sufficiently ground the assumption of a death drive not immediately visible.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_5:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B03","text":"The architecture is strongest where social aggression functions not as a subsequent example, but as a transition from the problem of cultural attachment to drive dualism.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT8","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B04","text":"The independent identification of the death drive and the origin of the presupposed propensity for aggression remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B05","text":"Likewise underdetermined remains how necessary drive renunciation could be distinguished from avoidable institutional damage and replaced by less damaging mediations.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KAPV:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if genealogical hypotheses are treated as supporting layers and cultural institutions as species-specific projections of a deeper conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_4:MRT7","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B07","text":"The death drive itself resists axiomatic reduction: without it, the terminal closure loses its ground; with it, the architecture exceeds its immediately demonstrable evidence.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_5:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_R2TV_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_R2TV_02:v1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Chapters 04–06"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review","title":"Chapters 04–06","context":"Chapter IV · Chapter V · Chapter VI","original_title":"Chapters 04–06","original_context":"Kapitel IV · Kapitel V · Kapitel VI"},"original_title":"Chapters 04–06","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 07–08","order":3,"parents":["CH_R2TV_KA_6","CH_R2TV_KA_7"],"revision":"CL_R2TV_03@R001","sha256":"57478135f99fc1e74da11db171a50d3e027820df0948ca585871c7a4fe0b9d27","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B01","text":"Das zentrale Problem besteht darin, dass Kultur die für Gemeinschaft gefährliche Aggression binden muss, ohne sie beseitigen zu können, und deshalb ihre Wirkungsrichtung gegen das Subjekt verschiebt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02","text":"Die globale These lautet, dass kulturelle Integration durch die Verwandlung äußerer Aggression in innere Strafgewalt erkauft wird und deshalb Schuldsteigerung sowie Glückseinbuße strukturell miteinander verbindet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B03","text":"Das Argument rekonstruiert Schuld nicht als moralische Bewertung einer Tat, sondern als genealogisch und topisch organisierte Dynamik aus Autoritätsabhängigkeit, Aggressionshemmung, Verinnerlichung und Angst.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B04","text":"Seine gerichtete Bewegung führt von familiärer Autorität über das individuelle Über-Ich zum Kultur-Über-Ich, wobei die Skalierung die Mechanismen bewahrt, ihre Ziele jedoch asymmetrisch neu gewichtet.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B05","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv und eskalatorisch: Der durch Autoritätsangst erzeugte Verzicht verstärkt nach der Verinnerlichung jene Instanz, die weiteren Verzicht und zusätzliche Schuld fordert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B06","text":"Mit der Ausweitung sozialer Bindung wächst die Schuldökonomie von der individuellen Gewissensstruktur zu einer kollektiven Normierungsordnung, die Gemeinschaft durch sanktionierende Ideale stabilisiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07","text":"Die terminale Eskalation entsteht, sobald technische Naturbeherrschung ungebundener Aggression eine globale Vernichtungsreichweite verleiht und Eros nur noch als mögliche, nicht garantierte Gegenkraft verbleibt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B08","text":"Die Schließung bleibt diagnostisch statt therapeutisch: Das System macht die kulturelle Pathologie sichtbar, verweigert aber sowohl einen kulturäußeren Normalitätsmaßstab als auch eine deduktive Entscheidung ihres Ausgangs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Kultur kann Zusammenleben nur sichern, indem sie individuelle Aggression hemmt und deren Energie umverteilt, nicht indem sie Aggression aufhebt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Autorität wandert von äußerer Liebes- und Strafabhängigkeit in das individuelle Über-Ich und von dort in die normsetzende Struktur des Kultur-Über-Ichs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Schuld ist die als Angst, Spannung oder diffuses Unbehagen wirksame Beziehung des Ichs zur internalisierten Autorität und benötigt kein bewusstes Schuldbewusstsein.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","text":"[Attractor] Triebverzicht bildet nach der Über-Ich-Bildung keinen Endpunkt, sondern einen rekursiven Verstärker, der zusätzliche Aggression an die innere Strafinstanz überträgt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Die libidinöse Erweiterung von Gemeinschaft und die Steigerung von Schuld sind gekoppelt, sodass kulturelle Bindungsgewinne systematisch mit individuellem Glücksverlust bezahlt werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Die Aggressivität des Über-Ichs vereinigt fortgesetzte äußere Strafgewalt und die gegen Autorität gerichtete, aber nach innen gewendete Eigenaggression, ohne beide Quellen kausal gleichzusetzen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Nach der Verinnerlichung verliert die Differenz zwischen Aggressionswunsch und Aggressionstat ihre entlastende Funktion, während Reue als Reaktion auf tatsächlich ausgeführte Aggression begrifflich begrenzt bleibt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Individual- und Kulturentwicklung sind analog strukturierte Integrationsprozesse, deren Zielordnungen auseinanderfallen, weil individuelles Glück und kollektive Einheitsbildung verschieden priorisiert werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Ethik wird zur therapeutischen Technik des Kultur-Über-Ichs, schlägt aber bei psychisch undurchführbaren Forderungen in Schuldsteigerung, Auflehnung, Neurose oder Unglück um.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Der Konflikt zwischen Individuum und Gemeinschaft bleibt als veränderbare Libidoverteilung von dem nicht terminal lösbaren Konflikt zwischen Eros und Destruktion unterschieden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Die Skalierung psychischer Diagnostik auf Kulturen bleibt ohne externen Normalitätsmaßstab und ohne therapiefähige kollektive Autorität diagnostisch und praktisch unabschließbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Technische Naturbeherrschung steigert die Reichweite destruktiver Handlungsmacht bis zur möglichen Selbstvernichtung, während die Gegenanstrengung des Eros weder prognostisch noch teleologisch garantiert ist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","text":"Aggression behält ihre strukturelle Identität, wechselt aber ihren Ort: Sie erscheint zunächst als zwischenmenschliche Gefahr, dann als gegen das Ich gewendete Strafgewalt und schließlich als technisch potenzierte Selbstvernichtungsmacht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-02","text":"Autorität kehrt funktional auf drei Ebenen wieder: als äußere Quelle von Liebesverlustangst, als individuelle Überwachungsinstanz und als kollektive Produktion von Idealen und Sanktionen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-03","text":"Schuld mutiert von sozialer Entdeckungsangst zu Gewissensangst und anschließend zu einem möglicherweise unbewussten Unbehagen, das seine Ursachen durch fremde Motivierungen verdecken kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04","text":"Triebverzicht erfährt eine kausale Umkehrung: Er beginnt als Folge der Autoritätsangst und wird nach der Verinnerlichung zum rekursiven Produzenten größerer Gewissensstrenge.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-05","text":"Die familiäre Ambivalenz von Liebe und Destruktion erweitert ihren Geltungsbereich zum kulturgeschichtlichen Konflikt zwischen Eros und Todestrieb, ohne ihre antagonistische Kopplung zu verlieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-06","text":"Die hypothetische Urvatertötung leistet genealogische Übergangsarbeit, wird auf Clusterebene jedoch in eine allgemeinere Architektur von Ambivalenz, Identifizierung und Triebkonflikt absorbiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-07","text":"Moral und Ethik verkehren ihre normative Valenz: Aus einer vermeintlich natürlichen Wertordnung wird eine Autoritätsökonomie, und aus dem Gebot wird eine hinsichtlich ihrer Nebenwirkungen zu prüfende therapeutische Technik.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-08","text":"Kulturfortschritt mutiert von einer Gewinn- und Vervollkommnungsfigur zu einer Tausch- und Risikostruktur, in der Integrationsgewinn, Glücksverlust und technische Vernichtungsfähigkeit gemeinsam wachsen können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-01","text":"Die Urvatertötung bleibt ein hypothetisches genealogisches Gerüst der unteren Ebene; auf Clusterebene trägt nicht das historische Ereignis, sondern die übertragbare Verbindung von Aggression, Liebe, Identifizierung und Schuld.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-02","text":"Das ungelöste Vergleichsproblem eines ausbleibenden Kulturkampfs bei Tieren bleibt lokal und erzeugt keinen tragenden Übergang zur Kulturdiagnose.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-03","text":"Die begriffliche Unterscheidung von Über-Ich, Gewissen, Schuldgefühl, Strafbedürfnis und Reue skaliert nach oben, weil sie verhindert, dass verschiedene Stufen der Autoritätsverinnerlichung zu einer einzigen Moralreaktion eingeebnet werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-04","text":"Die klinische Aufteilung verdrängter Triebstrebungen in Symptom- und Schuldanteile bleibt ein lokales Begründungsmittel; auf Clusterebene fortbestehend ist nur die qualifizierte Vorrangstellung gehemmter Aggression für unmittelbare Schuldproduktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-05","text":"Die Polemik gegen eine bloße Veränderung von Besitzverhältnissen bleibt unterbestimmt und trägt die Clusterarchitektur nur negativ als Ausschluss einer monokausalen Sozialerklärung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-06","text":"Das Kultur-Über-Ich skaliert die individuelle Gewissensstruktur tatsächlich nach oben, doch die Übertragung bleibt durch Zielasymmetrie und fehlende Maßstabsneutralität begrenzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-07","text":"Die technologische Selbstvernichtungsfrage ist kein lokales Beispiel, sondern die terminale Probe darauf, ob kulturelle Aggressionsbindung mit der Reichweite der von ihr freigesetzten Handlungsmacht Schritt halten kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-01","text":"Das System verwirft eine natürliche oder autonome Moral, die Gut und Böse unabhängig von Autoritätsabhängigkeit und Liebesverlust begründen könnte.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-02","text":"Es verwirft die Gleichsetzung psychischer Wirksamkeit mit bewusster Wahrnehmung; Schuld kann wirksam sein, ohne als Schuld erkannt zu werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-03","text":"Es verwirft ein ausschließlich tatbezogenes Schuldmodell, weil das Über-Ich Absicht und Tat gleichstellt, ohne deshalb Reue und Schuld begrifflich zu identifizieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-04","text":"Es verwirft die Annahme, Triebverzicht oder tugendhaftes Verhalten müsse das Subjekt moralisch entlasten und die Gewissensstrenge vermindern.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-05","text":"Es verwirft die Geltung moralischer Forderungen als Beweis ihrer psychischen Durchführbarkeit oder aggressionshemmenden Wirksamkeit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-06","text":"Es verwirft eine maßstabsneutrale Identität von Individual- und Kulturentwicklung sowie den unmittelbaren Übergang von analogischer Diagnose zu kollektiver Therapie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-07","text":"Es verwirft jede gesicherte Teleologie, nach der Kulturfortschritt notwendig Vollkommenheit, Glück oder den endgültigen Sieg des Eros hervorbringen müsste.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-01","text":"Damit die Clusterlogik Bestand hat, muss die Vorstellung falsch sein, Aggression könne ohne Rückkehrwirkung gehemmt werden; jede Hemmung muss als Verschiebung, Speicherung oder erneute Mobilisierung denkbar bleiben.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-02","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein transparentes und souveränes psychisches Inneres, das sozialer Kontrolle entzogen wäre und über seine Triebe nach bewusster Einsicht frei verfügen könnte.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-03","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine natürliche Konvergenz von Gemeinschaftsbildung und individuellem Glück; kulturelle Einheit darf nicht ohne strukturelle Kosten gedacht werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-04","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist jede vollständige Reduktion von Aggression auf Erziehungsstrenge, Eigentumsordnung oder eine einzelne äußere Institution, weil die Triebkonstitution als eigenständige Wirksamkeitsbedingung erhalten bleiben muss.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-05","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein neutraler kulturäußerer Beobachtungsstandpunkt; die diagnostizierende Instanz bleibt in dieselbe Kultur und dieselben Normalitätsprobleme eingelassen wie ihr Gegenstand.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-01","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist innerhalb des Systems eine kulturelle Einheit, die Aggression bindet, ohne Schuld zu steigern und individuelles Glück zu vermindern.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein durch Enthaltsamkeit, Tugend oder innere Transparenz endgültig unschuldig gewordenes Subjekt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-03","text":"Nicht verfügbar sind sowohl eine unbetroffene Normalität außerhalb der Menschheit als auch eine anerkannte Instanz, die eine kollektive Pathologie gegen den Widerstand der Betroffenen therapieren könnte.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-04","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine geschichtliche Rechtfertigung, welche die kulturellen Opfer als notwendig kompensiert und ihren Ausgang durch eine Fortschrittsteleologie verbürgt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-05","text":"Die tiefste unzulässige Möglichkeit ist eine terminale Versöhnung von Eros und Destruktion; der Konflikt muss offen bleiben, damit Kultur zugleich Bindungsprozess und Vernichtungsrisiko sein kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-01","text":"Die individuelle Gewissensrekursion und die überfordernde kollektive Ethik bilden gemeinsam einen Selbstverstärkungskreis, in dem der Versuch, Aggression durch Verzicht zu kontrollieren, neue Aggression und verschärfte Schuldanforderungen erzeugt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-02","text":"Die Ausweitung familiärer Autoritätsbindung und die Bildung eines Kultur-Über-Ichs erzeugen verschachtelte Normierungskreisläufe, in denen kulturelle Gebote individuelles Gewissen formen und individuelle Triebkonflikte kollektiv reproduziert werden.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-03","text":"Weil soziale Erweiterung steigende Schuld verlangt und Kulturentwicklung Gemeinschaftseinheit vor individuelles Glück stellt, ist Glücksverlust kein korrigierbarer Nebeneffekt, sondern der systemische Preis der bevorzugten Zielordnung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-04","text":"Die Gleichstellung von Wunsch und Tat verbindet sich mit der möglichen Unbewusstheit der Schuld zu einer Strafbarkeit ohne identifizierbares Schadensereignis und ohne notwendig verfügbare Selbsterkenntnis.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","CL_R2TV_03:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-05","text":"Die doppelte Herkunft der Über-Ich-Aggression macht Herrschaft weder rein äußerlich noch rein selbstgesetzt; sie entsteht als Kopplung von fortgesetzter Sanktion und gegen sich selbst gewendeter Widerstandsenergie.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-06","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-06","text":"Eine veränderte Libidoverteilung kann den Konflikt zwischen Individuum und Gemeinschaft begrenzen, ohne den umfassenderen Antagonismus von Eros und Destruktion oder dessen Schuldwirkungen aufzuheben.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-07","text":"Die Verbindung konkurrierender Erklärungen der Über-Ich-Strenge mit dem fehlenden kulturäußeren Normalitätsmaßstab macht die Kulturdiagnose strukturell reflexiv: Sie kann Mechanismen bestimmen, aber keine neutrale Gesamtbewertung erzeugen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-06","CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-08","text":"Die innere Aggressionsbindung kann kulturell funktionieren und dennoch strategisch scheitern, wenn technische Vernichtungsmittel schneller wachsen als die Fähigkeit, destruktive Energie psychisch und kollektiv zu binden.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-01","text":"Das Subjekt wird zu einem Übersetzungs- und Rückkopplungsknoten, der äußere Verbote in Selbstbestrafung umsetzt und diese innere Normierung als Träger kultureller Ordnung reproduziert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-02","text":"Kausalität nimmt eine zirkuläre Form an: Autorität erzeugt Verzicht, Verzicht erzeugt und verschärft die innere Autorität, und deren Forderungen erzeugen weiteren Verzicht.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-03","text":"Kulturelle Zeit ist keine Fortschrittslinie, sondern eine Akkumulation ungelöster Aggression, gesteigerter Schuld und wachsender technischer Reichweite, in der spätere Lösungen frühere Konflikte auf höherem Gefahrenniveau wiederholen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-04","text":"Politische Veränderung wird als Eingriff in materielle und libidinöse Verteilungen denkbar, verliert aber den Status einer vollständigen Lösung, sobald Aggression weder auf Familienstruktur noch auf Eigentumsordnung reduzierbar ist.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-05","text":"Ethik muss nach psychischer Beherrschbarkeit und tatsächlichen Aggressionseffekten beurteilt werden; normativer Anspruch allein kann eine schuldproduzierende Fehlsteuerung des Kultur-Über-Ichs verdecken.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnis wird dezentriert, weil weder Bewusstsein ein vollständiges Maß psychischer Wirksamkeit noch kulturelle Distanz einen neutralen Maßstab kollektiver Normalität liefert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-07","text":"Handlungsmacht bleibt begrenzt, aber nicht annulliert: Eros kann der Selbstvernichtung entgegenarbeiten, doch weder die Triebstruktur noch der technologische Gefahrenstand erlauben eine Erfolgsgarantie.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-01","text":"Die primäre Schuldschleife verläuft als Autoritätsangst → Triebverzicht → Aggressionshemmung → Verinnerlichung → größere Über-Ich-Strenge → erneuter Triebverzicht.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-02","text":"Die kulturelle Bindungsschleife verläuft als libidinöse Vereinigung → Erweiterung der Gemeinschaft → größere Einschränkung individueller Befriedigung → steigende Schuld → verstärkter Bedarf an bindender Ordnung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-03","text":"Die ethische Eskalationsschleife verläuft als Aggressionsproblem → verschärftes Gebot → psychische Nichtbefolgbarkeit → Schuld oder Auflehnung → Diagnose moralischen Versagens → weiteres Gebot.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-04","text":"Die Skalierungsbewegung ist spiralförmig: Familienautorität wird zum individuellen Über-Ich, dieses liefert das Modell des Kultur-Über-Ichs, und dessen Gebote kehren als individuelle Gewissensforderungen zurück.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-05","text":"Der technologische Eskalationspfad verbindet fortbestehende Aggression mit wachsender Naturbeherrschung, bis kulturelle Selbstbindung und globale Vernichtungsfähigkeit in ein asymmetrisches Wettrennen treten.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-06","text":"Der übergeordnete Attraktor ist die unabschließbare Spannung von Eros und Destruktion: Jede Bindung reorganisiert die Aggression, ohne den Konflikt terminal aufzulösen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B01","text":"Zusammenlebenszwang + individuelle Aggression → kulturelle Hemmung der Aggression, jedoch keine Aufhebung ihres energetischen Bestands.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B02","text":"Äußere Autorität + Liebesabhängigkeit + gehemmte Gegenaggression → Identifizierung und Verinnerlichung → individuelles Über-Ich.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B03","text":"Über-Ich + fortbestehender Aggressionswunsch → Entwertung der Differenz zwischen Absicht und Tat → Schuld, Strafbedürfnis oder diffuses Unbehagen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B04","text":"Neuer Verzicht → zusätzliche Aggressionsübertragung → größere Gewissensstrenge → verschärfte Forderung → erneuter Verzicht; die kulturelle Lösung reproduziert ihr eigenes Zwangsmittel.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B05","text":"Individuelle Integrationsstruktur + kontrollierte Skalierung + Vorrang kollektiver Einheit → Kultur-Über-Ich → Ethik als institutionalisierte und potenziell überfordernde Aggressionsabwehr.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B06","text":"Technische Naturbeherrschung + ungelöste Destruktivität → globale Selbstvernichtungsfähigkeit; Eros fungiert als notwendige Gegenkraft, ohne eine terminale Lösung zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B01","text":"Kulturelle Aggressionsgefahr → Hemmung statt Beseitigung → Verschiebung der Aggression in das psychische Innere.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B02","text":"Äußere Autoritätsabhängigkeit → Angst vor Liebesverlust → Triebverzicht → Verinnerlichung → Über-Ich und dauerhafte innere Strafbarkeit.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B03","text":"Gewissensforderung → weiterer Verzicht → Übertragung zusätzlicher Aggression → verschärfte Gewissensforderung → rekursive Schuldproduktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B04","text":"Familiäres Ambivalenzmodell → Individualpsychologie → kontrollierte Kulturskalierung → Kultur-Über-Ich → Ethik als riskante Aggressionsabwehr.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B05","text":"Kulturelle Integration → Glückseinbuße → ungesicherte Gemeinschaftsdiagnose → technische Vernichtungseskalation → offene Gegenanstrengung des Eros.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-01","text":"Moral wird von einer natürlichen Wertordnung in eine Genealogie von Abhängigkeit, Liebesverlust, Autorität und verinnerlichter Sanktion überführt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-02","text":"Schuld wird von der Bewertung objektiver Taten in eine psychische Topik von Angst, Aggressionsverschiebung und möglicherweise unbewusster Spannung umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-03","text":"Gewissen wird nicht länger als neutrale Norminstanz, sondern als institutionalisierte Form gegen das Ich gewendeter Aggression lesbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-04","text":"Tugend und Triebverzicht wechseln ihren Status von Entlastungsleistungen zu potenziellen Verstärkern der inneren Strafökonomie.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX5","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-05","text":"Kulturfortschritt wird als Tauschstruktur neu kartiert, in der Gemeinschaftsbildung, Schuldsteigerung und Glücksverlust nicht getrennt bilanziert werden können.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-06","text":"Der Gegensatz Individuum versus Gesellschaft wird vom Konflikt Eros versus Destruktion getrennt; damit werden reformierbare Libidoverteilung und nicht terminal lösbarer Triebantagonismus unterscheidbar.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-07","text":"Technischer Fortschritt wird von bloßer Naturbeherrschung zum Multiplikator einer Aggression umklassifiziert, deren kulturelle Bindung nicht im selben Maßstab gesichert ist.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene verbinden sich Gewissen, Schuldgefühl, Reue, Ethik, Kulturfortschritt und technologische Vernichtungsfähigkeit zu einem gemeinsamen Problem kultureller Aggressionsverwaltung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene bilden Autoritätsabhängigkeit, Introjektion, Über-Ich, Triebverzicht und kulturelle Normsetzung gekoppelte Kreisläufe, die Aggression räumlich verschieben und zeitlich akkumulieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene wird moralische Verurteilung durch die Prüfung ersetzt, ob ein Gebot psychisch ausführbar ist, welche Aggression es bindet und welche Schuld oder Auflehnung es selbst produziert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologischen und zeitlichen Ebene erscheint Kultur als nicht teleologisch entschiedener Lebensprozess, in dem Eros und Destruktion ihre Kräfteverhältnisse verändern, ohne ihren Konflikt aufzulösen.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologischen und performativen Ebene vollzieht die Argumentation ihre These durch wiederholte Rückkehr, begriffliche Differenzierung, Kausalumkehr und Maßstabsskalierung statt durch lineare Deduktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-01","text":"Die relative Gewichtung erfahrener äußerer Strenge, konstitutioneller Disposition und gehemmter Eigenaggression bleibt ungelöst; ihre Zusammenführung bezeichnet eine Funktionsgemeinschaft, aber keine geklärte Kausalverteilung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-02","text":"Die Beschränkung unmittelbarer Schuldgenese auf Aggressionsverzicht organisiert das System, bleibt jedoch klinisch nicht eindeutig bestätigt und empirisch unterbestimmt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-03","text":"Die Analogie zwischen individueller und kultureller Entwicklung ist für das Kultur-Über-Ich unverzichtbar, zugleich aber durch Zielasymmetrie, ungesicherte Skalierung und fehlenden Normalitätsvergleich begrenzt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-04","text":"Die Möglichkeit eines endlichen Ausgleichs zwischen Individuum und Gemeinschaft steht in Spannung zur Behauptung, größere kulturelle Einheit erfordere kumulativ steigende Schuld.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-05","text":"Das Kultur-Über-Ich ist zugleich notwendiges Instrument der Aggressionsbindung und Quelle überfordernder Gebote, sodass seine therapeutische Funktion nicht von seiner pathogenen Wirkung getrennt werden kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-06","text":"Eros ist gleichzeitig Ursprung kultureller Vereinigung, indirekter Produzent schuldhafter Selbstunterwerfung und letzte mögliche Gegenkraft zur Selbstvernichtung; diese Mehrfachfunktion bleibt produktiv uneindeutig.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-01","text":"Der entscheidende Kausalitätswechsel tritt ein, wenn Triebverzicht von einer Wirkung des Gewissens zu dessen eigener Verstärkungsquelle mutiert.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-02","text":"Schuld mutiert von einer bewussten moralischen Tatkategorie zu einer topischen Angst- und Spannungsform, die als unspezifisches Unbehagen erscheinen kann.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-03","text":"Das Über-Ich mutiert von einer individuellen psychischen Instanz zu einer kollektiven Normierungsstruktur, ohne dass die Skalierung vollständige Prozessidentität erzeugt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-04","text":"Der kulturelle Fortschrittsbegriff mutiert von Integrationsgewinn zu einer offenen Risikostruktur, sobald Naturbeherrschung als Steigerung globaler Selbstvernichtungsfähigkeit erscheint.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-05","text":"Der familiäre Vaterkonflikt mutiert von einer genealogischen Ursprungserzählung zu einem allgemeinen Modell der nicht aufhebbaren Kopplung von libidinöser Bindung und destruktiver Aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-01","text":"Realität erscheint implizit als geschichtete Umleitungsmaschine, in der Triebenergien gehemmt, räumlich verschoben, institutionell gespeichert und auf höheren Skalen erneut wirksam werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist kein souveräner Ursprung, sondern ein umkämpfter Umschlagplatz zwischen Es, äußerer Autorität, Über-Ich und kultureller Forderung.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-03","text":"Zeit besitzt die Form rekursiver Akkumulation: Vergangene Autorität bleibt im Über-Ich gegenwärtig, jeder Verzicht verdichtet ihre Gewalt, und technische Beschleunigung vergrößert die Folgen ungelöster Konflikte.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-04","text":"Der verbleibende Kampf ist keine Flucht aus der Triebordnung, sondern eine prekäre Navigation zwischen libidinöser Bindung, begrenzbarer sozialer Verteilung und nicht garantiert beherrschbarer Destruktion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B01","text":"Die extrahierten Axiome reichen aus, um die Clusterbewegung von äußerer Autoritätsangst über Verinnerlichung und rekursive Schuldsteigerung bis zum Kultur-Über-Ich und zur Selbstvernichtungsfrage zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B02","text":"Die Architektur ist am stärksten in der Verbindung von Aggressionshemmung, innerer Verschiebung und rekursiver Gewissensverschärfung; unterbestimmt bleibt die kausale Gewichtung der Quellen des Über-Ichs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B03","text":"Empirisch unterbestimmt bleiben die konstitutionellen Anteile, die ausschließliche Bindung unmittelbarer Schuldgenese an Aggressionsverzicht und der Übergang von individueller Struktur zu kollektiver Diagnose.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B04","text":"Die Clusterkohärenz ist bedingt: Sie setzt Trieblehre, Aggressionsverinnerlichung und eine kontrollierbare, aber nicht identische Skalierung zwischen Individual- und Kulturentwicklung voraus.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B05","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn die Kausalumkehr des Triebverzichts und die anschließende Skalierung zum Kultur-Über-Ich nicht als bloße Wiederholung eingeebnet werden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B06","text":"Der offene Ausgang widersteht axiomatischer Schließung: Weder das Verhältnis von Eros und Destruktion noch die technologische Schicksalsfrage lässt sich aus der rekonstruierten Maschine deduktiv entscheiden.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT9","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171831695362Z_06754158","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 07–08","source_sha256":"57478135f99fc1e74da11db171a50d3e027820df0948ca585871c7a4fe0b9d27","sha256":"d45a72ff68dbdf55fb0703ee008b11933346dc969e50246053e64d13db2f216d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:18:31.696246+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B01","text":"The central problem consists in the fact that culture must bind aggression dangerous to community without being able to eliminate it, and therefore shifts its direction of operation against the subject.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02","text":"The global thesis is that cultural integration is purchased through the transformation of external aggression into internal punitive force and therefore structurally links the increase of guilt and the diminution of happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B03","text":"The argument reconstructs guilt not as a moral evaluation of an act, but as a genealogically and topically organized dynamic of dependence on authority, inhibition of aggression, internalization, and anxiety.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B04","text":"Its directed movement leads from familial authority via the individual superego to the cultural superego, whereby scaling preserves the mechanisms but asymmetrically reweights their aims.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B05","text":"The movement is recursive and escalating: renunciation produced by anxiety before authority strengthens, after internalization, that agency which demands further renunciation and additional guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B06","text":"With the expansion of social bonds, the economy of guilt grows from an individual structure of conscience into a collective order of normalization that stabilizes community through sanctioning ideals.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07","text":"The terminal escalation arises as soon as technical mastery of nature confers upon unbound aggression a global range of destruction, and Eros remains only as a possible, not guaranteed, counterforce.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AS-B08","text":"The conclusion remains diagnostic rather than therapeutic: the system makes cultural pathology visible, but refuses both an extra-cultural standard of normality and a deductive decision concerning its outcome.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Culture can secure coexistence only by inhibiting individual aggression and redistributing its energy, not by abolishing aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Authority migrates from external dependence on love and punishment into the individual superego and from there into the norm-setting structure of the cultural superego.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Guilt is the relation of the ego to internalized authority, effective as anxiety, tension, or diffuse malaise, and requires no conscious sense of guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","text":"[Attractor] After the formation of the superego, instinctual renunciation constitutes not an endpoint but a recursive amplifier that transfers additional aggression to the internal punitive agency.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The libidinal expansion of community and the intensification of guilt are coupled, so that gains in cultural bonding are systematically paid for by losses in individual happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The aggressiveness of the superego combines continuing external punitive force and the subject's own aggression directed against authority but turned inward, without causally equating the two sources.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] After internalization, the difference between the wish for aggression and the act of aggression loses its exculpatory function, while remorse remains conceptually limited to a reaction to aggression actually carried out.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Individual and cultural development are analogously structured processes of integration whose orders of aims diverge because individual happiness and collective unification are differently prioritized.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Ethics becomes the therapeutic technique of the cultural superego, but turns, when demands are psychically infeasible, into intensified guilt, rebellion, neurosis, or unhappiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The conflict between individual and community remains distinct, as a modifiable distribution of libido, from the conflict between Eros and destruction, which is not terminally soluble.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] The scaling of psychic diagnosis to cultures remains diagnostically and practically inconclusive without an external standard of normality and without a collective authority capable of therapy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A17","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Technical mastery of nature increases the range of destructive agency up to possible self-annihilation, while the counter-effort of Eros is guaranteed neither prognostically nor teleologically.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","text":"Aggression retains its structural identity but changes its location: it first appears as an interpersonal danger, then as punitive force turned against the ego, and finally as technologically potentiated power of self-annihilation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-02","text":"Authority recurs functionally on three levels: as an external source of anxiety over loss of love, as an individual supervisory agency, and as collective production of ideals and sanctions.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-03","text":"Guilt mutates from social anxiety over discovery into anxiety of conscience and subsequently into a possibly unconscious malaise that can conceal its causes through alien motivations.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04","text":"Instinctual renunciation undergoes a causal reversal: it begins as a consequence of anxiety before authority and becomes, after internalization, the recursive producer of greater severity of conscience.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-05","text":"The familial ambivalence of love and destruction expands its scope into the cultural-historical conflict between Eros and the death drive, without losing its antagonistic coupling.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-06","text":"The hypothetical killing of the primal father performs genealogical work of transition, but at the cluster level is absorbed into a more general architecture of ambivalence, identification, and instinctual conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-07","text":"Morality and ethics reverse their normative valence: a purportedly natural order of value becomes an economy of authority, and the command becomes a therapeutic technique to be examined with respect to its side effects.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RMD-08","text":"Cultural progress mutates from a figure of gain and perfecting into a structure of exchange and risk, in which gains in integration, losses in happiness, and technological capacity for destruction can grow together.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-01","text":"The killing of the primal father remains a hypothetical genealogical framework of the lower level; at the cluster level, it is not the historical event but the transferable connection of aggression, love, identification, and guilt that bears the argument.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-02","text":"The unresolved comparative problem of the absence of a cultural struggle among animals remains local and generates no load-bearing transition to cultural diagnosis.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-03","text":"The conceptual distinction among superego, conscience, sense of guilt, need for punishment, and remorse scales upward because it prevents different stages of the internalization of authority from being flattened into a single moral reaction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-04","text":"The clinical division of repressed instinctual strivings into symptom and guilt components remains a local means of grounding; at the cluster level, only the qualified priority of inhibited aggression for immediate guilt production persists.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-05","text":"The polemic against a mere alteration of property relations remains underdetermined and supports the cluster architecture only negatively, as the exclusion of a monocausal social explanation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-06","text":"The cultural superego genuinely scales the individual structure of conscience upward, yet the transfer remains limited by asymmetry of aims and lack of neutrality of standards.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:CGD-07","text":"The question of technological self-annihilation is not a local example, but the terminal test of whether cultural binding of aggression can keep pace with the range of agency unleashed by it.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects a natural or autonomous morality that could ground good and evil independently of dependence on authority and loss of love.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-02","text":"It rejects the equation of psychic efficacy with conscious perception; guilt can be effective without being recognized as guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-03","text":"It rejects an exclusively act-related model of guilt because the superego equates intention and act, without thereby conceptually identifying remorse and guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-04","text":"It rejects the assumption that instinctual renunciation or virtuous conduct must morally exculpate the subject and diminish the severity of conscience.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-05","text":"It rejects the validity of moral demands as proof of their psychic feasibility or aggression-inhibiting efficacy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-06","text":"It rejects a standard-neutral identity of individual and cultural development, as well as the immediate transition from analogical diagnosis to collective therapy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:GNX-07","text":"It rejects every assured teleology according to which cultural progress would necessarily bring forth perfection, happiness, or the final victory of Eros.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-01","text":"For the cluster logic to hold, the idea that aggression could be inhibited without rebound effects must be false; every inhibition must remain thinkable as displacement, storage, or renewed mobilization.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-02","text":"Excluded is a transparent and sovereign psychic interior that would be withdrawn from social control and could freely dispose of its instincts on the basis of conscious insight.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-03","text":"Excluded is a natural convergence of community formation and individual happiness; cultural unity must not be conceived without structural costs.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-04","text":"Excluded is every complete reduction of aggression to educational severity, property order, or a single external institution, because instinctual constitution must remain as an independent condition of efficacy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:DBN-05","text":"Excluded is a neutral extra-cultural standpoint of observation; the diagnosing agency remains implicated in the same culture and the same problems of normality as its object.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-01","text":"Unavailable within the system is a cultural unity that binds aggression without increasing guilt and diminishing individual happiness.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is a subject rendered definitively innocent through abstinence, virtue, or inner transparency.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-03","text":"Unavailable are both an unaffected normality outside humanity and a recognized agency capable of therapeutically treating a collective pathology against the resistance of those affected.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-04","text":"Unavailable is a historical justification that compensates the cultural sacrifices as necessary and guarantees their outcome through a teleology of progress.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSA-05","text":"The deepest inadmissible possibility is a terminal reconciliation of Eros and destruction; the conflict must remain open so that culture can be both a process of bonding and a risk of destruction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-01","text":"Individual recursion of conscience and overburdening collective ethics jointly form a self-reinforcing circuit in which the attempt to control aggression through renunciation generates new aggression and intensified demands of guilt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-02","text":"The expansion of familial bonds of authority and the formation of a cultural superego generate nested circuits of normalization in which cultural commands shape individual conscience and individual instinctual conflicts are collectively reproduced.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-03","text":"Because social expansion demands increasing guilt and cultural development gives precedence to communal unity over individual happiness, loss of happiness is not a corrigible side effect but the systemic price of the preferred order of aims.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-04","text":"The equation of wish and act combines with the possible unconsciousness of guilt to yield punishability without an identifiable harmful event and without necessarily available self-knowledge.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","CL_R2TV_03:GA-07","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-05","text":"The dual origin of superego aggression makes domination neither purely external nor purely self-imposed; it arises as the coupling of continuing sanction and resistance energy turned against itself.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-06","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-06","text":"An altered distribution of libido can limit the conflict between individual and community without abolishing the more comprehensive antagonism of Eros and destruction or its effects of guilt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-07","text":"The conjunction of competing explanations of superego severity with the absent extra-cultural standard of normality renders cultural diagnosis structurally reflexive: it can determine mechanisms, but cannot produce a neutral overall evaluation.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-06","CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:XD-08","text":"Internal binding of aggression can function culturally and nevertheless fail strategically if technical means of destruction grow faster than the capacity to bind destructive energy psychically and collectively.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-01","text":"The subject becomes a node of translation and feedback that converts external prohibitions into self-punishment and reproduces this internal normalization as the bearer of cultural order.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-02","text":"Causality assumes a circular form: authority produces renunciation, renunciation produces and intensifies internal authority, and its demands produce further renunciation.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-03","text":"Cultural time is not a line of progress but an accumulation of unresolved aggression, intensified guilt, and increasing technological range, in which later solutions repeat earlier conflicts at a higher level of danger.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-04","text":"Political change becomes conceivable as intervention in material and libidinal distributions, but loses the status of a complete solution as soon as aggression is reducible neither to family structure nor to property order.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-05","text":"Ethics must be judged according to psychic manageability and actual effects on aggression; normative claim alone can conceal a guilt-producing misdirection of the cultural superego.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-09","CH_R2TV_KA_6:D4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-06","text":"Knowledge is decentered because neither consciousness provides a complete measure of psychic efficacy nor cultural distance a neutral standard of collective normality.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-03","CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:BSD-07","text":"Agency remains limited but not annulled: Eros can work against self-annihilation, yet neither instinctual structure nor the state of technological danger permits a guarantee of success.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-10","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-01","text":"The primary guilt loop runs as anxiety before authority → instinctual renunciation → inhibition of aggression → internalization → greater superego severity → renewed instinctual renunciation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:D6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-02","text":"The cultural bonding loop runs as libidinal unification → expansion of community → greater restriction of individual satisfaction → increasing guilt → intensified need for binding order.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-03","text":"The ethical escalation loop runs as problem of aggression → intensified command → psychic noncompliance → guilt or rebellion → diagnosis of moral failure → further command.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-04","text":"The scaling movement is spiral-shaped: familial authority becomes the individual superego, the latter supplies the model of the cultural superego, and its commands return as individual demands of conscience.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:D8","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-05","text":"The technological path of escalation connects continuing aggression with growing mastery of nature until cultural self-binding and global capacity for destruction enter into an asymmetrical race.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:RLE-06","text":"The overarching attractor is the inconclusive tension of Eros and destruction: every bond reorganizes aggression without terminally resolving the conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B01","text":"Compulsion to coexist + individual aggression → cultural inhibition of aggression, but no abolition of its energetic stock.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B02","text":"External authority + dependence on love + inhibited counter-aggression → identification and internalization → individual superego.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B03","text":"Superego + continuing wish for aggression → devaluation of the difference between intention and act → guilt, need for punishment, or diffuse malaise.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B04","text":"New renunciation → additional transfer of aggression → greater severity of conscience → intensified demand → renewed renunciation; the cultural solution reproduces its own means of compulsion.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B05","text":"Individual structure of integration + controlled scaling + priority of collective unity → cultural superego → ethics as institutionalized and potentially overburdening defense against aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B06","text":"Technical mastery of nature + unresolved destructiveness → global capacity for self-annihilation; Eros functions as a necessary counterforce without producing a terminal solution.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A18","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B01","text":"Cultural danger of aggression → inhibition rather than elimination → displacement of aggression into the psychic interior.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B02","text":"External dependence on authority → anxiety over loss of love → instinctual renunciation → internalization → superego and permanent internal punishability.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS3","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B03","text":"Demand of conscience → further renunciation → transfer of additional aggression → intensified demand of conscience → recursive production of guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B04","text":"Familial model of ambivalence → individual psychology → controlled cultural scaling → cultural superego → ethics as risky defense against aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A11","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B05","text":"Cultural integration → loss of happiness → unsecured diagnosis of community → technological escalation of destruction → open counter-effort of Eros.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-01","text":"Morality is transferred from a natural order of value into a genealogy of dependence, loss of love, authority, and internalized sanction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX1","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-02","text":"Guilt is reclassified from the evaluation of objective acts into a psychic topic of anxiety, displacement of aggression, and possibly unconscious tension.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:SD4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-03","text":"Conscience is no longer legible as a neutral normative agency, but as an institutionalized form of aggression turned against the ego.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-04","text":"Virtue and instinctual renunciation change their status from exculpatory achievements to potential amplifiers of the internal punitive economy.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:NX5","CH_R2TV_KA_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-05","text":"Cultural progress is remapped as a structure of exchange in which community formation, intensification of guilt, and loss of happiness cannot be accounted for separately.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-06","text":"The opposition individual versus society is separated from the conflict Eros versus destruction; thereby reformable distribution of libido and instinctual antagonism not terminally soluble become distinguishable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MME-07","text":"Technical progress is reclassified from mere mastery of nature into the multiplier of an aggression whose cultural binding is not secured on the same scale.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, conscience, sense of guilt, remorse, ethics, cultural progress, and technological capacity for destruction are joined into a common problem of cultural administration of aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, dependence on authority, introjection, superego, instinctual renunciation, and cultural norm-setting form coupled circuits that spatially displace and temporally accumulate aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, moral condemnation is replaced by examination of whether a command is psychically executable, what aggression it binds, and what guilt or rebellion it itself produces.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, culture appears as a life process not teleologically decided, in which Eros and destruction alter their relations of force without resolving their conflict.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:ALT4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the argument enacts its thesis through repeated return, conceptual differentiation, causal reversal, and scaling of standards rather than through linear deduction.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_7:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-01","text":"The relative weighting of experienced external severity, constitutional disposition, and inhibited self-aggression remains unresolved; their conjunction designates a functional association but no clarified causal distribution.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A8","CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-02","text":"The restriction of immediate genesis of guilt to renunciation of aggression organizes the system, but remains clinically not unambiguously confirmed and empirically underdetermined.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A9","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-03","text":"The analogy between individual and cultural development is indispensable for the cultural superego, but is at the same time limited by asymmetry of aims, unsecured scaling, and absent comparison of normality.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-04","text":"The possibility of a finite adjustment between individual and community stands in tension with the assertion that greater cultural unity requires cumulatively increasing guilt.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-05","text":"The cultural superego is both a necessary instrument of binding aggression and the source of overburdening commands, so that its therapeutic function cannot be separated from its pathogenic effect.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A15","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:FL-06","text":"Eros is simultaneously the origin of cultural unification, the indirect producer of guilty self-subjection, and the final possible counterforce to self-annihilation; this multiple function remains productively ambiguous.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-01","text":"The decisive shift in causality occurs when instinctual renunciation mutates from an effect of conscience into its own source of reinforcement.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:AS4","CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-02","text":"Guilt mutates from a conscious moral category of action into a topical form of anxiety and tension that can appear as nonspecific malaise.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-03","text":"The superego mutates from an individual psychic agency into a collective structure of normalization, without scaling producing complete identity of process.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A14","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-04","text":"The concept of cultural progress mutates from gain in integration into an open structure of risk as soon as mastery of nature appears as an increase in global capacity for self-annihilation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MP-05","text":"The familial conflict with the father mutates from a genealogical narrative of origin into a general model of the irreducible coupling of libidinal bonding and destructive aggression.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A12","CH_R2TV_KA_7:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as a layered machine of redirection in which instinctual energies are inhibited, spatially displaced, institutionally stored, and become effective again at higher scales.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:DNX3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not a sovereign origin but a contested transfer point among the id, external authority, superego, and cultural demand.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX9","CH_R2TV_KA_6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-03","text":"Time has the form of recursive accumulation: past authority remains present in the superego, every renunciation condenses its force, and technological acceleration enlarges the consequences of unresolved conflicts.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:A10","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:HSI-04","text":"The remaining struggle is not an escape from the instinctual order, but a precarious navigation between libidinal bonding, limitable social distribution, and destruction not guaranteed to be controllable.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:A13","CH_R2TV_KA_7:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the cluster movement from external anxiety before authority through internalization and recursive intensification of guilt to the cultural superego and the question of self-annihilation.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT1","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B02","text":"The architecture is strongest in the connection of inhibition of aggression, internal displacement, and recursive intensification of conscience; the causal weighting of the sources of the superego remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B03","text":"Empirically underdetermined remain the constitutional components, the exclusive binding of immediate genesis of guilt to renunciation of aggression, and the transition from individual structure to collective diagnosis.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT3","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B04","text":"Cluster coherence is conditional: it presupposes instinct theory, internalization of aggression, and a controllable but non-identical scaling between individual and cultural development.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT2","CH_R2TV_KA_7:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if the causal reversal of instinctual renunciation and the subsequent scaling to the cultural superego are not flattened into mere repetition.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_6:MRT6","CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B06","text":"The open outcome resists axiomatic closure: neither the relation between Eros and destruction nor the technological question of fate can be deductively decided from the reconstructed machine.","refs":["CH_R2TV_KA_7:MRT9","CH_R2TV_KA_7:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_R2TV_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_R2TV_03:v1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Chapters 07–08"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review","title":"Chapters 07–08","context":"Chapter VII · Chapter VIII","original_title":"Chapters 07–08","original_context":"Kapitel VII · Kapitel VIII"},"original_title":"Chapters 07–08","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"WB_R2TV","layer":"WB","title":"Civilization and Its Discontents (1930) · OCR review","order":1,"parents":["CL_R2TV_01","CL_R2TV_02","CL_R2TV_03"],"revision":"WB_R2TV@R002","sha256":"5ef2f653bbb088e8456e8275c9d4277b95311c73fbe901f58752cc29b3c2f5d3","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-01","text":"Das System untersucht, warum Kultur zugleich unverzichtbarer Schutz gegen Hilflosigkeit, Naturgewalt und menschliche Aggression sowie eine eigenständige Quelle von Versagung, Schuld und Unglück ist.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-02","text":"Die globale These lautet, dass psychische und kulturelle Ordnungen Triebkräfte nicht beseitigen, sondern durch Grenzbildung, Bindung, Einschränkung, Verlagerung und Verinnerlichung so umverteilen, dass jede Stabilisierung neue Kosten erzeugt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:GA-09","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-03","text":"Das Argument wird zu einer genetischen, funktionalen und metapsychologischen Rekonstruktion, die religiöse Gewissheit, Glücksanspruch, Kulturideal und moralische Schuld von ihrer Selbstbeglaubigung trennt und auf ihre psychischen Operationen zurückführt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","CL_R2TV_02:AS-03","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-04","text":"Die Bewegung führt von psychischer Hilflosigkeit und Schutzsehnsucht über das unerfüllbare Glücksprogramm zur Kultur als Triebökonomie, von dort zur ursprünglichen Aggression und schließlich zur inneren Strafgewalt des Über-Ichs.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-08","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-05","text":"Diese Bewegung ist rekursiv und eskalatorisch, weil Schutz Abhängigkeit, Bindung Verzicht, Aggressionshemmung Innenwendung und Gewissensgehorsam zusätzliche Gewissensstrenge hervorbringt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-07","CL_R2TV_02:AS-05","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-06","text":"Individuelle Psyche, soziale Institution und Kulturgeschichte bilden keine getrennten Bereiche, sondern verschiedene Maßstäbe einer einzigen Umleitungsarchitektur, deren Skalierung Funktionen bewahrt, Ziele jedoch verschiebt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:XD-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-07","text":"Technischer Fortschritt schließt diese Architektur nicht, sondern verschärft sie, weil wachsende Verfügungsmacht weder Glück garantiert noch mit einer proportionalen Steigerung kultureller Aggressionsbindung verbunden ist.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-08","text":"Die Schließung bleibt offen und diagnostisch: Eine endgültige Versöhnung von Lust, Freiheit, Sicherheit, kultureller Einheit, Eros und Destruktion ist ausgeschlossen, während der Ausgang ihres Konflikts unentscheidbar bleibt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-01","CL_R2TV_02:BSA-04","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Subjektive Intensität, kollektive Zustimmung, moralische Geltung und behauptete Zweckmäßigkeit legitimieren keinen Inhalt ohne genetische, funktionale und ökonomische Rekonstruktion.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-01","CL_R2TV_01:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Das Subjekt ist kein souveräner Ursprung, sondern ein geschichteter Umschlagpunkt körperlicher Bedürfnisse, libidinöser Besetzungen, destruktiver Richtungen, äußerer Autorität und internalisierter Forderungen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:BSD-02","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Kultur sichert größere Gemeinschaften durch Schutz, Recht, Bindung und Triebeinschränkung, produziert jedoch gerade durch diese Integrationsmittel eigene Formen des Leidens.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Jede psychische oder kulturelle Schutzleistung ist eine Umverteilung begrenzter Befriedigung, Bindung und Aggression; sie kann Gefahren vermindern, ohne Abhängigkeit oder Triebkosten aufzuheben.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:XD-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-05","text":"[Terminal] Das vom Lustprinzip gesetzte Glücksprogramm ist weder dauerhaft noch universell erfüllbar, und kultureller Fortschritt kann seine Unerfüllbarkeit nicht in eine gesicherte Versöhnung überführen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-03","CL_R2TV_01:GA-08","CL_R2TV_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Liebe mutiert von exklusiver Objekt- und Familienbindung über zielgehemmte Sozialbindung zum Erosprinzip kultureller Einheitsbildung, wobei jede Erweiterung ihre intensiven Ausgangsformen beschneiden muss.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-03","CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Aggression eskaliert von zwischenmenschlicher Feindseligkeit zur Erscheinungsform des Todestriebs, wird kulturell nach außen oder innen umgelenkt und durch technische Macht bis zur möglichen Selbstvernichtung potenziert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Grenzbildung mutiert von der psychischen Unterscheidung zwischen Selbst und Außen über Recht und Triebeinschränkung zur internalisierten Autorität des Über-Ichs.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Triebverzicht wird nach der Verinnerlichung von Autorität zum rekursiven Schuldverstärker, weil jeder neue Verzicht weitere Aggression an die Instanz überträgt, die ihn fordert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Kulturgeschichte ist die unabschließbare Austragung des Konflikts zwischen einheitsbildendem Eros und bindungslösender Destruktion auf psychischen, institutionellen und menschheitsgeschichtlichen Maßstäben.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","CL_R2TV_03:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Kulturelle Zeit ist nichtteleologisch und rekursiv: Frühere Formationen bleiben unter funktionaler Mutation wirksam, während ungelöste Aggression, Schuld und technische Reichweite akkumulieren.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-07","CL_R2TV_02:BSD-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Technische Naturbeherrschung steigert Handlungsmacht ohne proportionale psychische Selbstbindung; deshalb endet die Architektur in einem offenen Überlebenskonflikt, nicht in einer Fortschrittsgarantie.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-01","text":"Religion kehrt nicht als eigenständiger Endgegenstand wieder, sondern wird nach ihrer psychogenetischen Umdeutung in die allgemeinere Architektur von Hilflosigkeit, Schutzabhängigkeit und Autoritätsbindung absorbiert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-02","text":"Die Ichgrenze wandert aus der Individualgenese in Recht und soziale Einschränkung und kehrt schließlich als psychische Innengrenze zwischen Ich und Über-Ich zurück.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-03","text":"Glück verschiebt sich vom vermeintlichen Lebenszweck zur episodischen Befriedigung und danach zum negativen Bilanzposten kultureller Integration und technischer Risikosteigerung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-05","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-04","text":"Liebe behält ihre bindende Funktion, erweitert aber ihren Geltungsbereich von exklusiver Nähe über umverteilte Libido bis zum überindividuellen Eros, der kulturelle Einheit erzeugt und dadurch zusätzliche Einschränkung verlangt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-05","text":"Aggression bewahrt ihre energetische Identität, mutiert jedoch ontologisch und topisch von äußerer Feindseligkeit über Todestrieb und innere Strafgewalt zur technisch verstärkten Selbstvernichtungsmacht.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-06","text":"Einschränkung eskaliert von Realitätsanpassung und Rechtsbindung über Sexual- und Aggressionshemmung zur kausalen Umkehr, in der vollzogener Verzicht die ihn fordernde Gewissensinstanz verstärkt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-04","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-07","text":"Autorität wechselt ihren Ort von äußerer Schutz- und Strafmacht zum individuellen Über-Ich und zum Kultur-Über-Ich; Moral verliert dabei ihre natürliche Valenz und wird zur Technik der Triebverwaltung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:RMD-02","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-08","text":"Fortschritt kehrt mit umgekehrter Valenz wieder: Was zunächst Verfügung und Schutz steigert, wird schließlich zum Multiplikator jener Aggression, deren kulturelle Bindung nicht entsprechend wächst.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-06","CL_R2TV_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-01","text":"Das tatsächliche Vorkommen und die genaue Genese des ozeanischen Gefühls bleiben lokal; auf Gesamtbuchebene skaliert nur die methodische Trennung von Erlebnisintensität, Herkunft, Funktion und Wahrheitsgeltung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-02","text":"Einzelne Glückstechniken und Kulturmerkmale verbleiben als lokale Typologien; global trägt allein die Regel, dass jede Technik eine besondere Verteilung von Entlastung, Abhängigkeit und Kosten erzeugt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:CGD-02","CL_R2TV_01:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-03","text":"Organische Ursprungsspekulationen und die Urvatertötung bleiben genealogische Gerüste der unteren Ebene; nach oben skaliert die Verbindung von Ambivalenz, Identifizierung, Aggression und institutionalisierter Einschränkung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:CGD-01","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-04","text":"Monogamie, Heterosexualität und Eigentumsordnung bleiben konkrete Norm- oder Testfälle; global relevant ist die Differenz zwischen historisch veränderlichen Aggressionskanälen und nicht auf Institutionen reduzierbarer Triebkonstitution.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:CGD-03","CL_R2TV_02:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-05","text":"Sadismus, Masochismus und klinische Symptomaufteilungen bleiben lokale Begründungsmittel; auf Gesamtbuchebene skaliert die indirekte Erschließung gemischter Triebkräfte und gehemmter Aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:CGD-07","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-06","text":"Die technologische Selbstvernichtungsfrage ist kein Schlussbeispiel, sondern die globale Belastungsprobe dafür, ob kulturelle Bindung mit der Reichweite destruktiver Handlungsmacht Schritt halten kann.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-01","text":"Religiöses Gefühl und behauptete Weltzweckmäßigkeit werden als unmittelbare Erkenntnisquellen ausgeschlossen. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GNX-01","CL_R2TV_01:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-02","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein von Bedürftigkeit, Trieb, Objektbindung und Autorität unabhängiges oder sich selbst vollständig transparentes Subjekt. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GNX-03","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-03","text":"Ausgeschlossen sind dauerhaftes Glück, teleologischer Kulturfortschritt und jede fortschreitende Aufhebung des Grundkonflikts. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GNX-04","CL_R2TV_02:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-04","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Kultur, die Schutz, Freiheit und Gemeinschaft ohne Triebopfer, Aggressionsverlagerung oder Schuld erzeugt. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-03","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-05","text":"Rationales Eigeninteresse und moralische Liebesgebote werden als hinreichende Grundlagen dauerhafter Großgemeinschaften verworfen. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GNX-01","CL_R2TV_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-06","text":"Eigentum, Erziehung oder einzelne Institutionen dürfen Aggression weder ursprünglich erzeugen noch restlos erklären. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-07","text":"Normative Geltung beweist weder psychische Vollziehbarkeit noch therapeutische Wirksamkeit, und die Individualdiagnostik lässt sich nicht maßstabsneutral in eine kollektive Therapie überführen. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:DBN-04","CL_R2TV_03:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-01","text":"Damit die Gesamtarchitektur trägt, muss kostenloser Schutz unmöglich sein; jede Abwehr muss neue Bindungen, Versagungen oder Rückkehrwirkungen erzeugen können. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-02","text":"Libido und Destruktion dürfen weder unbegrenzt verfügbar noch durch kulturelle Hemmung vernichtbar sein, weil sonst Umverteilung und Rückwendung ihre generative Funktion verlieren. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-03","text":"Kultur darf nicht außerhalb des Triebkonflikts stehen; eine neutrale Befriedungsinstanz würde die Rekursion von Bindung, Verzicht und Aggressionsverlagerung aufheben. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:DBN-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-04","text":"Natürliche Moral und ein transparentes Inneres müssen ausgeschlossen bleiben, weil Schuld und Autorität sonst nicht als unbewusste, verinnerlichte Trieboperationen rekonstruierbar wären. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GNX-01","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-05","text":"Kulturelle Erweiterung darf exklusive Bindungen nicht unverändert bewahren, und psychische Mechanismen dürfen beim Maßstabswechsel nicht ohne Zielverschiebung identisch bleiben. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:DBN-02","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-06","text":"Ein externer Normalitätsmaßstab und eine therapiefähige kollektive Autorität müssen fehlen; andernfalls würde die Diagnose in eine souveräne Gesamtsteuerung umschlagen. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste versperrte Möglichkeit ist die terminale Versöhnung von Lust, Realität, Freiheit, Eros und Destruktion. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-01","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Großgemeinschaft, die exklusive Liebe bewahrt, Aggression bindet und dennoch weder Ausschluss noch Schuld produziert. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSA-01","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-03","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein vollständig souveränes, tugendhaft entlastetes und innerlich transparentes Subjekt. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-02","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-04","text":"Nicht verfügbar sind eine positive isolierte Erkenntnis des Todestriebs und eine unbetroffene Normalität, von der aus seine kulturellen Wirkungen abschließend bewertet werden könnten. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSA-05","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-05","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Geschichtsteleologie, die Opfer kompensiert, den Kulturverlauf rechtfertigt und den Sieg des Eros garantiert. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-01","text":"Die Kostenförmigkeit individueller Abwehr und die Endlichkeit kulturell verfügbarer Libido machen jeden Schutzgewinn zu einer Neuverteilung von Befriedigung, Bindung und destruktivem Risiko. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-03","WB_R2TV:GA-04","CL_R2TV_01:XD-03","CL_R2TV_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-02","text":"Psychische Grenze, Recht und Über-Ich bilden eine verteilte Grenzmaschine, die äußere Macht in soziale Selbstbeschränkung und schließlich in innere Überwachung transformiert. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-02","WB_R2TV:GA-08","WB_R2TV:GA-09","CL_R2TV_01:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-03","text":"Religiöse Schutzordnung und moralische Gewissensordnung sind homologe Autoritätsformationen: Beide transformieren Abhängigkeit in bindende Deutung, verlieren aber dadurch ihren Anspruch auf transzendente oder natürliche Selbstbegründung. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-01","WB_R2TV:GA-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-04","text":"Kultur beantwortet soziale Aggressionsgefahr, indem sie äußere Destruktion in Schuld und Selbstbestrafung umleitet; ihr Schutzapparat produziert dadurch das Unbehagen, das er regulieren soll. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-03","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-09","CL_R2TV_01:XD-04","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-05","text":"Die Erweiterung kultureller Einheit verlangt zugleich libidinöse Umverteilung und verschärfte innere Einschränkung, sodass Eros nicht nur verbindet, sondern mittelbar die Schuldökonomie vergrößert. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-06","WB_R2TV:GA-09","WB_R2TV:GA-10","CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-06","text":"Die Ortswechsel der Aggression bilden einen Eskalationspfad von zwischenmenschlicher Gefahr über Selbstbestrafung zur technisch potenzierten Vernichtungsfähigkeit der Gattung. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-12","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-07","text":"Politische Reform kann Rechtsformen, Verteilungen und Aggressionsinstrumente verändern, aber keine vollständige Emanzipation vom Triebkonflikt garantieren; Handlungsmacht bleibt kanalbezogen statt souverän. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-03","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","CL_R2TV_02:XD-06","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-08","text":"Die Verbindung von genetischer Kritik, indirekter Todestrieb-Rekonstruktion und fehlendem kulturäußerem Maßstab erzeugt eine reflexive Erkenntnismethode, die starke Diagnosen erlaubt, aber ihre eigenen Voraussetzungen nicht neutralisieren kann. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-01","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-11","CL_R2TV_01:CGD-01","CL_R2TV_02:XD-08","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-09","text":"Universale Liebes- und Moralgebote können ihre Gegenkräfte verstärken, weil äußere Solidarität Aggression verlagert und psychisch undurchführbare Forderungen Schuld, Auflehnung oder Ausschluss erzeugen. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-06","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-09","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-07","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-10","text":"Die Entkopplung technischer Macht von Glück und Triebbeherrschung transformiert das Kulturproblem von einer Verzichtsbilanz in eine Überlebensfrage. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-11","WB_R2TV:GA-12","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CL_R2TV_03:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-01","text":"Realität erscheint als geschichtete Umwandlungsmaschine, die Druck in Grenze, Bindung, Recht, Verzicht, Schuld und technische Macht überführt und dabei neue Druckformen erzeugt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-01","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird zu einem endlichen Relais, an dem Libido zwischen Ich und Objekten, Aggression zwischen Außenwelt und Selbst sowie Autorität zwischen sozialer Sanktion und innerem Gebot zirkuliert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-02","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-02","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-03","text":"Kausalität wird geschichtet und zirkulär: Triebe liefern energetische Bedingungen, Institutionen bestimmen Richtungen, und die Resultate institutioneller Hemmung wirken auf die Triebökonomie zurück.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSD-03","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-04","text":"Zeit wird zur Persistenz unter Mutation und zur Akkumulation ungelöster Konflikte; spätere Ordnungen ersetzen frühere Strukturen nicht, sondern reaktivieren sie auf erhöhtem Gefahrenniveau.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-05","text":"Politik wird als begrenzte, aber reale Veränderung von Bindungen, Machtverteilungen und Aggressionskanälen rekonstruierbar, ohne den Status einer vollständigen Triebtherapie zu erhalten.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-05","CL_R2TV_02:BSD-06","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-06","text":"Ethik wird zur Diagnose ihrer psychischen Vollzugsbedingungen und tatsächlichen Aggressionseffekte; ein Gebot ist nicht allein nach seinem normativen Inhalt, sondern nach seinen Schuld- und Widerstandsproduktionen zu beurteilen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSD-05","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-07","text":"Handlungsmacht besteht in partieller Navigation, Umlenkung und institutioneller Korrektur; sie bleibt wirksam, besitzt aber weder einen triebfreien Außenpunkt noch eine Erfolgsgarantie gegen Selbstvernichtung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:HSI-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-01","text":"Unlust erzeugt Grenze und Schutz; Schutz erzeugt Abhängigkeit und Versagung; diese Kosten erzeugen neue Unlust und legitimieren weitere Schutzleistungen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RLE-01","CL_R2TV_01:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-02","text":"Das unerfüllbare Glücksprogramm erzeugt pluralisierte Lebenstechniken, deren Scheitern Kultur und Kompensation aufruft, ohne eine allgemeine Glückstechnik hervorzubringen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RLE-03","CL_R2TV_01:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-03","text":"Kulturelle Expansion beschränkt exklusive Libido, schwächt damit eine Quelle ihrer eigenen Bindungskraft und steigert den Bedarf an zielgehemmten Ersatzbindungen und zusätzlichen Normen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-01","CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-04","text":"Aggression erzeugt Hemmung; Hemmung erzeugt Innenwendung; Innenwendung verstärkt das Über-Ich; dessen Forderungen erzeugen weiteren Verzicht und zusätzliche Aggressionsübertragung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-05","text":"Innere Gruppenbindung externalisiert Aggression, Außenfeindschaft verdichtet die Gruppe, und die verdichtete Gruppe reproduziert die Grenze, aus der ihre Kohäsion hervorgeht.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-03","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-06","text":"Überfordernde Ethik bildet einen Selbstverstärkungskreis: Verschärfte Gebote erzeugen Nichtbefolgbarkeit, Schuld oder Auflehnung, die als moralisches Defizit gelesen und mit neuen Geboten beantwortet werden.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:XD-01","CL_R2TV_03:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-07","text":"Technische Naturbeherrschung steigert die Reichweite fortbestehender Aggression schneller, als kulturelle Selbstbindung gesichert werden kann, und eskaliert den Triebkonflikt zur Gattungsgefahr.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:RLE-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-08","text":"Der übergeordnete Attraktor verbindet Kompensation mit dem Eros-Todestrieb-Gegensatz: Kultur sucht Ersatz für verlangten Verzicht, während jede Bindung Destruktion lediglich reorganisiert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-07","CL_R2TV_03:RLE-06","CL_R2TV_01:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B01","text":"Behauptete Wahrheit → genetische und funktionale Rekonstruktion → Entzug religiöser, teleologischer oder moralischer Selbstbeglaubigung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","CL_R2TV_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B02","text":"Unerfüllbares Glücksprogramm → pluralisierte Abwehrtechniken → spezifische Kosten → Übergang von individueller Lebensführung zur Kulturökonomie.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-06","CL_R2TV_01:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B03","text":"Hilflosigkeit und Leidensdruck → kollektiver Schutzapparat → Recht und Triebeinschränkung → Kultur als notwendige und endogene Leidensproduktion.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CL_R2TV_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B04","text":"Endliche Libido + kultureller Skalierungsbedarf → Beschneidung exklusiver Bindung → zielgehemmte Umverteilung → Eros als Prinzip extensiver Einheitsbildung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B05","text":"Primäre Feindseligkeit → unvollständige institutionelle Hemmung → metapsychologischer Rest → Todestrieb als verborgener Grund der Destruktion.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B06","text":"Äußere Aggressionshemmung → Innenwendung → Über-Ich → Triebverzicht als Ursache weiterer Gewissensstrenge → rekursive Schuldsteigerung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B07","text":"Individuelle Autoritätsverinnerlichung → kontrollierte Skalierung zum Kultur-Über-Ich → Ethik als bindende, aber potenziell pathogene Aggressionsabwehr.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B08","text":"Technische Naturbeherrschung + unaufgehobene Destruktion → globale Selbstvernichtungsfähigkeit → Eros als notwendige, aber nicht sieggarantierte Gegenkraft.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07","CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:AFM-B01","text":"Religiöser Wahrheitsanspruch → Psychogenese der Schutzsehnsucht → unerfüllbares Glücksprogramm → kostenförmige Lebenstechniken → Kultur als Schutz und Versagung → Kultur als Triebmetabolismus.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","CL_R2TV_01:AS-06","CL_R2TV_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AFM-B02","text":"Endliche Libido → kulturelle Einheitsbildung → primäre Aggression → Todestrieb → Innenwendung → Über-Ich und Schuld → technische Selbstvernichtungsfähigkeit.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-09","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AFM-B03","text":"Kultur benötigt Bindung → beschädigt deren unmittelbare Formen → reproduziert ihr eigenes Zwangsmittel → endet in einer offenen Gegenanstrengung des Eros.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B02","CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B04","CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-01","text":"Religion und Moral werden von privilegierten Wahrheits- oder Wertordnungen zu genealogisch rekonstruierbaren Techniken von Schutz, Abhängigkeit und Autoritätsbindung umkartiert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-01","CL_R2TV_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-02","text":"Der Gegensatz von Natur und Kultur kollabiert: Kultur erscheint als historische Organisation natürlicher Triebkräfte und nicht als deren äußere Überwindung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-03","CL_R2TV_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-03","text":"Individuum und Gesellschaft werden als verschiedene Maßstäbe derselben Regulationsarchitektur lesbar, ohne ihre Zielordnungen oder Prozessformen vollständig gleichzusetzen.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-04","text":"Liebe und Aggression verlieren den Status reiner Gegensätze, weil Bindung destruktive Legierungen enthalten und Eros über Einschränkung, Schuld und Außenfeindschaft vermittelt sein kann.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-04","CL_R2TV_03:FL-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-05","text":"Recht, Reform und Ethik werden von Erlösungsinstanzen zu Kanaltechniken umklassifiziert, deren Wert an psychischer Vollziehbarkeit und tatsächlichen Aggressionseffekten hängt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-05","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-06","text":"Glück und Fortschritt werden entkoppelt: episodische Befriedigung eignet sich nicht als Kulturmaß, während technischer Fortschritt selbst zum Aggressionsmultiplikator werden kann.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-03","CL_R2TV_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-07","text":"Schuld wird von objektiver Tatbewertung in eine psychische Topik umkartiert, und Gewissen erscheint als institutionalisierte Aggression gegen das Ich.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:MME-02","CL_R2TV_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-08","text":"Die angemessene Lektüre wird residual, rekursiv und maßstabssensibel, weil tragende Kräfte indirekt erscheinen und begriffliche Wiederkehr häufig einen Funktions- oder Phasenwechsel bezeichnet.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-08","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Surface level verbinden sich religiöse Erfahrung, Glückstechniken, Familie, Sexualität, Moral, Schuld und technische Vernichtungsmacht zu Erscheinungsformen eines gemeinsamen Kulturproblems.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B01","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B01","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der Structural level operieren Arbeit, Recht, Libidoumleitung, Aggressionshemmung, Über-Ich und Schuld als gekoppelte Mechanismen räumlicher Verschiebung und zeitlicher Akkumulation.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B02","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der Metastrategic level werden Wahrheitsanspruch, Moralgebot und Reformmodell durch genetische Prüfung, Kostenvergleich, Energieverwaltung und Analyse psychischer Durchführbarkeit ersetzt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B03","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B03","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der Ontological / Temporal level ist Realität nicht auf Glück eingerichtet; Leben und Geschichte bestehen als nichtteleologisch entschiedene Auseinandersetzung von Bindung und Auflösung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B04","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B04","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der Methodological / Performative level vollzieht die Argumentform ihre These durch Entprivilegierung, genealogischen Abstieg, wiederholte Rückkehr, Kausalumkehr und Maßstabsskalierung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B05","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B05","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-01","text":"Der Todestrieb ist für die terminale Architektur unverzichtbar, bleibt aber nur indirekt in Mischphänomenen zugänglich; dieselben Phänomene begründen und bestätigen daher den angenommenen Trieb. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:FL-01","CL_R2TV_02:RLE-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-02","text":"Die Unterscheidung zwischen reformierbarem Kulturleid und strukturell notwendigem Triebverzicht bleibt politisch unverzichtbar, besitzt jedoch kein stabiles Kriterium. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:FL-05","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-03","text":"Die Analogie von Individual- und Kulturentwicklung ermöglicht das Kultur-Über-Ich, wird aber durch Zielasymmetrie, ungesicherte Skalierung und fehlende Prozessidentität begrenzt. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:FL-03","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-04","text":"Die Architektur kritisiert ungerechte Einschränkung und pathogene Ethik, obwohl sie einen kulturäußeren Normalitätsmaßstab verwirft; ihre normative Brücke bleibt deshalb operativ, aber unbegründet. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:FL-04","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-05","text":"Liebe und Aggression besitzen richtungs- und maßstabsabhängige Valenzen: Liebe kann binden und Schuld vermitteln, Aggression kann auflösen, Selbsterhaltung fördern oder Gruppen integrieren. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:FL-03","CL_R2TV_02:FL-04","CL_R2TV_03:FL-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-06","text":"Die offene Gegenanstrengung des Eros begründet begrenzte Handlungsmacht, erlaubt aber keine Deduktion des technologischen Ausgangs oder des endgültigen Kräfteverhältnisses. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:BSD-07","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-01","text":"Religiöse Erfahrung mutiert vom möglichen Transzendenzzeugnis zum psychischen Rest früher Grenzlosigkeit und danach zum Modell institutionalisierter Schutzabhängigkeit. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MP-01","CL_R2TV_01:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-02","text":"Grenzbildung mutiert von der Ich-Außen-Unterscheidung zur rechtlichen Selbstbeschränkung und schließlich zur innerpsychischen Teilung zwischen Ich und Über-Ich. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-03","text":"Liebe mutiert von konkreter familialer Bindung über kulturell umgeleitete Libido zum ontologisch erweiterten Erosprinzip. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-04","text":"Aggression mutiert von sozialer Feindseligkeit über externalisierte Todestriebtätigkeit zur inneren Strafgewalt und technisch potenzierten Gattungsgefahr. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MP-02","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-05","text":"Triebverzicht mutiert von einer Wirkung äußerer Autoritätsangst zur Ursache zusätzlicher Über-Ich-Strenge und schließt damit die Schuldrekursion. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:MP-01","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-06","text":"Fortschritt mutiert von Macht- und Integrationsgewinn zu einer offenen Risikostruktur, sobald technische Naturbeherrschung globale Selbstvernichtungsfähigkeit erzeugt. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:MP-04","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-01","text":"Realität erscheint als verschachtelte Grenz-, Strom- und Umleitungsmaschine, in der Eros Einheiten bindet, Destruktion sie löst und Kultur beide Kräfte durch Institutionen und innere Instanzen kanalisiert.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-01","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-01","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist kein verfügungsfähiges Zentrum, sondern ein umkämpfter Umschlagplatz von Körper, Objektlibido, Destruktion, äußerer Autorität und Über-Ich.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-02","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-02","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-03","text":"Zeit ist asymmetrische rekursive Akkumulation: Lust bleibt episodisch, frühere Autorität wirkt im Über-Ich fort, und derselbe Antagonismus kehrt mit wachsender technischer Reichweite wieder.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-03","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-03","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-04","text":"Möglich bleibt keine Flucht aus der Triebordnung, sondern nur revidierbare Navigation zwischen Bindung, Verteilung, institutioneller Korrektur und nicht garantiert beherrschbarer Destruktion.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-04","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-04","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B01","text":"Die extrahierten Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von religiöser Schutzsehnsucht über Glücksökonomie und kulturelle Triebverwaltung bis zu Schuldrekursion und technischer Selbstvernichtungsgefahr zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B01","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B01","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B02","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben das tatsächliche Vorkommen einzelner Ursprungserfahrungen, die unabhängige Identifikation des Todestriebs, die Gewichtung der Über-Ich-Quellen und der Übergang zur kollektiven Diagnose.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B02","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B04","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B03","text":"Das System ist nur konditional kohärent: Es verlangt die Trennung von Erlebnis, Genese und Funktion sowie die Annahme indirekt erschließbarer Triebkräfte und einer kontrollierten, nicht identischen Skalierung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B03","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B02","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B04","text":"Die Architektur ist am stärksten in der skalierbaren Verbindung von Grenzbildung, kostenförmiger Abwehr, endlicher Libido, Aggressionshemmung, Innenwendung und rekursiver Gewissensverschärfung.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B04","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B03","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B05","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn genealogische Hypothesen als Trägerschichten, wiederholte Begriffe als Mutationen und der Triebverzicht als kausal umkehrender Mechanismus behandelt werden.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B06","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B06","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B06","text":"Einer vollständigen axiomatischen Reduktion widerstehen nichtutilitäre Kulturwerte, der normative Überschuss der Gerechtigkeit, die indirekte Evidenz des Todestriebs und der unentscheidbare Ausgang des Eros-Destruktions-Konflikts.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B05","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B07","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261014T171924407672Z_db5664e0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Civilization and Its Discontents (1930) · OCR review","source_sha256":"5ef2f653bbb088e8456e8275c9d4277b95311c73fbe901f58752cc29b3c2f5d3","sha256":"ac699b832b8cf5dcd754eb55d1ceb95868ba6b164567bb889a54325d832fd5a3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-14T17:19:24.408651+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-01","text":"The system examines why culture is at once indispensable protection against helplessness, the force of nature, and human aggression, as well as an independent source of frustration, guilt, and unhappiness.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-02","text":"The global thesis is that psychic and cultural orders do not eliminate drives, but redistribute them through boundary formation, binding, restriction, displacement, and internalization in such a way that every stabilization generates new costs.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:GA-09","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-03","text":"The argument becomes a genetic, functional, and metapsychological reconstruction that separates religious certainty, the claim to happiness, the cultural ideal, and moral guilt from their self-authentication and traces them back to their psychic operations.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","CL_R2TV_02:AS-03","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-04","text":"The movement leads from psychic helplessness and the longing for protection, through the unfulfillable happiness programme, to culture as a drive economy, from there to primary aggression, and finally to the inner punitive force of the superego.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-08","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-05","text":"This movement is recursive and escalating because protection produces dependency, binding renunciation, the inhibition of aggression inward turning, and obedience to conscience additional severity of conscience.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-07","CL_R2TV_02:AS-05","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-06","text":"Individual psyche, social institution, and cultural history do not constitute separate domains, but different scales of a single architecture of redirection, whose scaling preserves functions while shifting aims.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:XD-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-07","text":"Technical progress does not close this architecture but intensifies it, because increasing power of disposal neither guarantees happiness nor is linked to a proportional increase in the cultural binding of aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AS-08","text":"The conclusion remains open and diagnostic: a final reconciliation of pleasure, freedom, security, cultural unity, Eros, and destruction is excluded, while the outcome of their conflict remains undecidable.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-01","CL_R2TV_02:BSA-04","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Subjective intensity, collective assent, moral validity, and asserted purposiveness do not legitimize any content without genetic, functional, and economic reconstruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-01","CL_R2TV_01:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The subject is not a sovereign origin, but a stratified point of conversion of bodily needs, libidinal cathexes, destructive directions, external authority, and internalized demands.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:BSD-02","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Culture secures larger communities through protection, law, binding, and drive restriction, yet produces its own forms of suffering precisely through these means of integration.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CL_R2TV_02:GA-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Every psychic or cultural protective achievement is a redistribution of limited satisfaction, binding, and aggression; it can diminish dangers without abolishing dependency or drive costs.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-05","CL_R2TV_02:XD-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-05","text":"[Terminal] The happiness programme posited by the pleasure principle is neither durably nor universally fulfillable, and cultural progress cannot transform its unfulfillability into a secured reconciliation.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-03","CL_R2TV_01:GA-08","CL_R2TV_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Love mutates from exclusive object- and family-binding, through aim-inhibited social binding, into the Eros principle of cultural unification, whereby every expansion must curtail its intensive initial forms.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-03","CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Aggression escalates from interpersonal hostility to a manifestation of the death drive, is culturally redirected outward or inward, and is potentiated by technical power up to possible self-destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-06","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Boundary formation mutates from the psychic distinction between self and outside, through law and drive restriction, into the internalized authority of the superego.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] After the internalization of authority, drive renunciation becomes a recursive intensifier of guilt, because every new renunciation transfers further aggression to the agency that demands it.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Cultural history is the interminable working-out of the conflict between unifying Eros and binding-dissolving destruction on psychic, institutional, and human-historical scales.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-11","CL_R2TV_03:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Cultural time is non-teleological and recursive: earlier formations remain effective under functional mutation, while unresolved aggression, guilt, and technical reach accumulate.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-07","CL_R2TV_02:BSD-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Technical mastery of nature increases agency without proportional psychic self-binding; therefore, the architecture ends in an open conflict of survival, not in a guarantee of progress.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12","CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-01","text":"Religion does not recur as an autonomous final object, but after its psychogenetic reinterpretation is absorbed into the more general architecture of helplessness, dependency on protection, and attachment to authority.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-02","text":"The ego boundary migrates from individual genesis into law and social restriction and finally returns as a psychic inner boundary between ego and superego.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-03","text":"Happiness shifts from an alleged purpose of life to episodic satisfaction and then to a negative balance-sheet item of cultural integration and increasing technical risk.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-05","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-04","text":"Love retains its binding function, but expands its scope from exclusive proximity, through redistributed libido, to the supra-individual Eros that produces cultural unity and thereby demands additional restriction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-05","text":"Aggression preserves its energetic identity, but mutates ontologically and topically from external hostility, through the death drive and inner punitive force, to technologically intensified power of self-destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-06","text":"Restriction escalates from adaptation to reality and legal binding, through sexual and aggressive inhibition, to causal reversal, in which enacted renunciation strengthens the agency of conscience that demands it.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-04","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-07","text":"Authority changes its place from external protective and punitive power to the individual superego and the cultural superego; morality thereby loses its natural valence and becomes a technique of drive administration.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:RMD-02","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RMD-08","text":"Progress recurs with reversed valence: what initially increases power of disposal and protection ultimately becomes a multiplier of the aggression whose cultural binding does not grow correspondingly.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-06","CL_R2TV_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-01","text":"The actual occurrence and precise genesis of the oceanic feeling remain local; at the whole-book level, only the methodological separation of experiential intensity, origin, function, and truth-validity scales.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-02","text":"Individual techniques of happiness and cultural traits remain local typologies; globally, only the rule carries that every technique produces a particular distribution of relief, dependency, and costs.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:CGD-02","CL_R2TV_01:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-03","text":"Organic speculations about origins and the primal-father murder remain genealogical frameworks of the lower level; what scales upward is the connection of ambivalence, identification, aggression, and institutionalized restriction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:CGD-01","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-04","text":"Monogamy, heterosexuality, and the order of property remain concrete normative or test cases; globally relevant is the difference between historically variable channels of aggression and a drive constitution irreducible to institutions.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:CGD-03","CL_R2TV_02:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-05","text":"Sadism, masochism, and clinical symptom divisions remain local means of justification; at the whole-book level, the indirect apprehension of mixed drive forces and inhibited aggression scales.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:CGD-07","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:CGD-06","text":"The question of technological self-destruction is not a concluding example, but the global stress test of whether cultural binding can keep pace with the reach of destructive agency.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-01","text":"Religious feeling and asserted purposiveness of the world are excluded as immediate sources of knowledge. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GNX-01","CL_R2TV_01:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-02","text":"Excluded is a subject independent of neediness, drive, object-binding, and authority, or one wholly transparent to itself. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GNX-03","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-03","text":"Excluded are lasting happiness, teleological cultural progress, and every progressive overcoming of the fundamental conflict. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GNX-04","CL_R2TV_02:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-04","text":"Excluded is a culture that produces protection, freedom, and community without drive sacrifice, displacement of aggression, or guilt. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-03","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-05","text":"Rational self-interest and moral commandments of love are rejected as sufficient foundations of lasting large communities. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GNX-01","CL_R2TV_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-06","text":"Property, education, or individual institutions may neither originally produce aggression nor exhaustively explain it. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:GNX-07","text":"Normative validity proves neither psychic feasibility nor therapeutic efficacy, and individual diagnosis cannot be transferred into collective therapy in a scale-neutral manner. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:DBN-04","CL_R2TV_03:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-01","text":"For the overall architecture to hold, cost-free protection must be impossible; every defense must be capable of producing new bindings, frustrations, or return effects. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-02","text":"Libido and destruction may be neither infinitely available nor destructible through cultural inhibition, for otherwise redistribution and turning-back lose their generative function. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-03","text":"Culture may not stand outside the drive conflict; a neutral agency of pacification would abolish the recursion of binding, renunciation, and displacement of aggression. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:DBN-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-04","text":"Natural morality and a transparent inner life must remain excluded, because otherwise guilt and authority could not be reconstructed as unconscious, internalized drive operations. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GNX-01","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-05","text":"Cultural expansion may not preserve exclusive bindings unchanged, and psychic mechanisms may not remain identical during a change of scale without a shift of aim. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:DBN-02","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:DBN-06","text":"An external standard of normality and a therapeutically capable collective authority must be absent; otherwise diagnosis would turn into sovereign overall control. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-11","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-01","text":"The deepest barred possibility is the terminal reconciliation of pleasure, reality, freedom, Eros, and destruction. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-01","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is a large community that preserves exclusive love, binds aggression, and nevertheless produces neither exclusion nor guilt. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSA-01","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-03","text":"Unavailable is a wholly sovereign subject, virtuously relieved and inwardly transparent. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-02","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-04","text":"Unavailable are a positive isolated cognition of the death drive and an unaffected normality from which its cultural effects could be conclusively assessed. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSA-05","CL_R2TV_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSA-05","text":"Unavailable is a teleology of history that compensates sacrifices, justifies the course of culture, and guarantees the victory of Eros. ; Trace Type — Negative","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-01","text":"The cost-character of individual defense and the finitude of culturally available libido make every gain in protection a redistribution of satisfaction, binding, and destructive risk. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-03","WB_R2TV:GA-04","CL_R2TV_01:XD-03","CL_R2TV_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-02","text":"Psychic boundary, law, and superego form a distributed boundary machine that transforms external power into social self-restriction and finally into inner surveillance. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-02","WB_R2TV:GA-08","WB_R2TV:GA-09","CL_R2TV_01:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-03","text":"Religious protective order and moral order of conscience are homologous formations of authority: both transform dependency into binding interpretation, but thereby lose their claim to transcendent or natural self-foundation. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-01","WB_R2TV:GA-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-04","text":"Culture responds to the danger of social aggression by redirecting external destruction into guilt and self-punishment; its protective apparatus thereby produces the discontent it is meant to regulate. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-03","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-09","CL_R2TV_01:XD-04","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-05","text":"The expansion of cultural unity simultaneously requires libidinal redistribution and intensified inner restriction, such that Eros not only binds but indirectly enlarges the economy of guilt. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-06","WB_R2TV:GA-09","WB_R2TV:GA-10","CL_R2TV_02:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-06","text":"The changes of place of aggression form a path of escalation from interpersonal danger, through self-punishment, to the technologically potentiated destructive capacity of the species. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-12","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-07","text":"Political reform can alter legal forms, distributions, and instruments of aggression, but cannot guarantee complete emancipation from drive conflict; agency remains channel-specific rather than sovereign. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-03","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-08","CL_R2TV_01:GA-11","CL_R2TV_02:XD-06","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-08","text":"The connection of genetic critique, indirect reconstruction of the death drive, and the absence of a standard external to culture produces a reflexive method of knowledge that permits strong diagnoses but cannot neutralize its own presuppositions. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-01","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-11","CL_R2TV_01:CGD-01","CL_R2TV_02:XD-08","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-09","text":"Universal commandments of love and morality can reinforce their counterforces, because external solidarity displaces aggression and psychically unfulfillable demands produce guilt, rebellion, or exclusion. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-06","WB_R2TV:GA-07","WB_R2TV:GA-09","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-07","CL_R2TV_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:XD-10","text":"The decoupling of technical power from happiness and drive mastery transforms the problem of culture from a balance of renunciation into a question of survival. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["WB_R2TV:GA-11","WB_R2TV:GA-12","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13","CL_R2TV_03:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-01","text":"Reality appears as a stratified machine of transformation that converts pressure into boundary, binding, law, renunciation, guilt, and technical power, while producing new forms of pressure.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-01","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes a finite relay through which libido circulates between ego and objects, aggression between outer world and self, and authority between social sanction and inner command.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-02","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-02","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-03","text":"Causality becomes stratified and circular: drives provide energetic conditions, institutions determine directions, and the results of institutional inhibition act back upon the drive economy.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSD-03","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-04","text":"Time becomes persistence under mutation and the accumulation of unresolved conflicts; later orders do not replace earlier structures, but reactivate them at an elevated level of danger.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-05","text":"Politics becomes reconstructible as limited but real alteration of bindings, distributions of power, and channels of aggression, without receiving the status of a complete therapy of drives.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:BSD-05","CL_R2TV_02:BSD-06","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-06","text":"Ethics becomes diagnosis of its conditions of psychic enactment and actual effects of aggression; a commandment is to be judged not solely by its normative content, but by its productions of guilt and resistance.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:BSD-05","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:BSD-07","text":"Agency consists in partial navigation, redirection, and institutional correction; it remains effective, but possesses neither a drive-free external standpoint nor a guarantee of success against self-destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:HSI-04","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-01","text":"Unpleasure produces boundary and protection; protection produces dependency and frustration; these costs produce new unpleasure and legitimize further protective measures.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RLE-01","CL_R2TV_01:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-02","text":"The unfulfillable happiness programme produces pluralized techniques of life whose failure calls forth culture and compensation without producing a general technique of happiness.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RLE-03","CL_R2TV_01:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-03","text":"Cultural expansion restricts exclusive libido, thereby weakens a source of its own binding force, and increases the need for aim-inhibited substitute bindings and additional norms.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-01","CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-04","text":"Aggression produces inhibition; inhibition produces inward turning; inward turning strengthens the superego; its demands produce further renunciation and additional transfer of aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-04","CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-05","text":"Inner group binding externalizes aggression, hostility toward outsiders condenses the group, and the condensed group reproduces the boundary from which its cohesion arises.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-03","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-06","text":"Overburdening ethics forms a self-reinforcing circle: intensified commandments produce noncompliance, guilt, or rebellion, which are read as moral deficiency and answered with new commandments.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:XD-01","CL_R2TV_03:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-07","text":"Technical mastery of nature increases the reach of persisting aggression faster than cultural self-binding can be secured, and escalates drive conflict into a danger to the species.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:RLE-05","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:RLE-08","text":"The higher-order attractor connects compensation with the Eros–death-drive opposition: culture seeks substitutes for demanded renunciation, while every binding merely reorganizes destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RLE-07","CL_R2TV_03:RLE-06","CL_R2TV_01:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B01","text":"Asserted truth → genetic and functional reconstruction → withdrawal of religious, teleological, or moral self-authentication.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","CL_R2TV_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B02","text":"Unfulfillable happiness programme → pluralized techniques of defense → specific costs → transition from individual conduct of life to cultural economy.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-06","CL_R2TV_01:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B03","text":"Helplessness and pressure of suffering → collective protective apparatus → law and drive restriction → culture as necessary and endogenous production of suffering.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:GA-10","CL_R2TV_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B04","text":"Finite libido + need for cultural scaling → curtailment of exclusive binding → aim-inhibited redistribution → Eros as principle of extensive unification.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:GA-02","CL_R2TV_02:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B05","text":"Primary hostility → incomplete institutional inhibition → metapsychological remainder → death drive as the hidden ground of destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-06","CL_R2TV_02:RMD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B06","text":"External inhibition of aggression → inward turning → superego → drive renunciation as cause of further severity of conscience → recursive intensification of guilt.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B07","text":"Individual internalization of authority → controlled scaling to the cultural superego → ethics as binding, yet potentially pathogenic, defense against aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FGS-B08","text":"Technical mastery of nature + unabolished destruction → global capacity for self-destruction → Eros as a necessary counterforce, but one not guaranteed victory.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07","CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:AFM-B01","text":"Religious claim to truth → psychogenesis of the longing for protection → unfulfillable happiness programme → cost-form techniques of life → culture as protection and frustration → culture as drive metabolism.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:AS-04","CL_R2TV_01:AS-06","CL_R2TV_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AFM-B02","text":"Finite libido → cultural unification → primary aggression → death drive → inward turning → superego and guilt → technical capacity for self-destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:RMD-09","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B02","CL_R2TV_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:AFM-B03","text":"Culture requires binding → damages its immediate forms → reproduces its own means of coercion → ends in an open counter-effort of Eros.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:AFM-B02","CL_R2TV_03:FGS-B04","CL_R2TV_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-01","text":"Religion and morality are remapped from privileged orders of truth or value into genealogically reconstructible techniques of protection, dependency, and attachment to authority.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-01","CL_R2TV_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-02","text":"The opposition between nature and culture collapses: culture appears as the historical organization of natural drive forces and not as their external overcoming.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-03","CL_R2TV_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-03","text":"Individual and society become legible as different scales of the same regulatory architecture, without completely equating their orders of aim or forms of process.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-04","CL_R2TV_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-04","text":"Love and aggression lose the status of pure opposites, because binding can contain destructive alloys and Eros can be mediated through restriction, guilt, and hostility toward outsiders.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-04","CL_R2TV_03:FL-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-05","text":"Law, reform, and ethics are reclassified from agencies of redemption into channel techniques, whose value depends on psychic feasibility and actual effects of aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-05","CL_R2TV_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-06","text":"Happiness and progress are decoupled: episodic satisfaction is unsuitable as a measure of culture, while technical progress itself can become a multiplier of aggression.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MME-03","CL_R2TV_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-07","text":"Guilt is remapped from objective assessment of an act into a psychic topic, and conscience appears as institutionalized aggression against the ego.","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:MME-02","CL_R2TV_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MME-08","text":"The appropriate reading becomes residual, recursive, and scale-sensitive, because supporting forces appear indirectly and conceptual recurrence often denotes a change of function or phase.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MME-08","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B01","text":"At the Surface level, religious experience, techniques of happiness, family, sexuality, morality, guilt, and technical destructive power combine into manifestations of a common problem of culture.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B01","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B01","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B02","text":"At the Structural level, labor, law, libidinal redirection, inhibition of aggression, superego, and guilt operate as coupled mechanisms of spatial displacement and temporal accumulation.","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B02","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B03","text":"At the Metastrategic level, claims to truth, moral commandments, and models of reform are replaced by genetic examination, comparison of costs, energy administration, and analysis of psychic feasibility.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B03","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B03","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B04","text":"At the Ontological / Temporal level, reality is not arranged for happiness; life and history consist as a non-teleologically decided confrontation between binding and dissolution.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B04","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B04","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:ALT-B05","text":"At the Methodological / Performative level, the argumentative form enacts its thesis through deprivileging, genealogical descent, repeated return, causal reversal, and scaling of measure.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:ALT-B05","CL_R2TV_02:ALT-B05","CL_R2TV_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-01","text":"The death drive is indispensable to the terminal architecture, but remains accessible only indirectly in mixed phenomena; the same phenomena therefore ground and confirm the assumed drive. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:FL-01","CL_R2TV_02:RLE-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-02","text":"The distinction between reformable cultural suffering and structurally necessary drive renunciation remains politically indispensable, but possesses no stable criterion. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:FL-05","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-03","text":"The analogy between individual and cultural development enables the cultural superego, but is limited by asymmetry of aims, unsecured scaling, and lack of process identity. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:FL-03","CL_R2TV_03:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-04","text":"The architecture criticizes unjust restriction and pathogenic ethics although it rejects a standard of normality external to culture; its normative bridge therefore remains operative, but ungrounded. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:FL-04","CL_R2TV_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-05","text":"Love and aggression possess direction- and scale-dependent valences: love can bind and mediate guilt, aggression can dissolve, promote self-preservation, or integrate groups. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:FL-03","CL_R2TV_02:FL-04","CL_R2TV_03:FL-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:FL-06","text":"The open counter-effort of Eros grounds limited agency, but permits no deduction of the technological outcome or of the final relation of forces. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:BSD-07","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-01","text":"Religious experience mutates from possible testimony of transcendence into the psychic remnant of earlier boundlessness and then into the model of institutionalized dependency on protection. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MP-01","CL_R2TV_01:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-02","text":"Boundary formation mutates from the ego–outside distinction to legal self-restriction and finally to intrapsychic division between ego and superego. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-03","text":"Love mutates from concrete familial binding, through culturally redirected libido, into the ontologically expanded Eros principle. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-04","text":"Aggression mutates from social hostility, through externalized death-drive activity, into inner punitive force and technologically potentiated danger to the species. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_02:MP-02","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-01","CL_R2TV_03:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-05","text":"Drive renunciation mutates from an effect of fear of external authority into the cause of additional superego severity and thereby closes the recursion of guilt. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:MP-01","CL_R2TV_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MP-06","text":"Progress mutates from a gain in power and integration into an open risk structure once technical mastery of nature produces global capacity for self-destruction. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_R2TV_03:MP-04","CL_R2TV_01:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a nested machine of boundaries, flows, and redirections, in which Eros binds unities, destruction dissolves them, and culture channels both forces through institutions and inner agencies.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-01","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-01","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not a center capable of disposal, but a contested switching point of body, object-libido, destruction, external authority, and superego.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-02","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-02","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-03","text":"Time is asymmetric recursive accumulation: pleasure remains episodic, earlier authority persists in the superego, and the same antagonism recurs with increasing technical reach.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-03","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-03","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:HSI-04","text":"What remains possible is not escape from the order of drives, but only revisable navigation between binding, distribution, institutional correction, and destruction not guaranteed to be controllable.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:HSI-04","CL_R2TV_02:HSI-04","CL_R2TV_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from religious longing for protection, through the economy of happiness and cultural drive administration, to the recursion of guilt and the danger of technical self-destruction.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B01","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B01","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B02","text":"What remains underdetermined are the actual occurrence of individual experiences of origin, the independent identification of the death drive, the weighting of the sources of the superego, and the transition to collective diagnosis.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B02","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B04","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B03","text":"The system is only conditionally coherent: it requires the separation of experience, genesis, and function, as well as the assumption of indirectly apprehensible drive forces and controlled, non-identical scaling.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B03","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B02","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B04","text":"The architecture is strongest in the scalable connection of boundary formation, cost-form defense, finite libido, inhibition of aggression, inward turning, and recursive intensification of conscience.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B04","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B03","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if genealogical hypotheses are treated as supporting layers, repeated concepts as mutations, and drive renunciation as a causally reversing mechanism.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B06","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B06","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_R2TV:MRT-B06","text":"Resisting complete axiomatic reduction are non-utilitarian cultural values, the normative surplus of justice, the indirect evidence of the death drive, and the undecidable outcome of the Eros–destruction conflict.","refs":["CL_R2TV_01:MRT-B05","CL_R2TV_02:MRT-B07","CL_R2TV_03:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"WB_R2TV@R002","source_variant_id":"canonical:WB_R2TV:WB_R2TV@R002","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review"}],"identity":{"layer":"WB","kicker":"Whole book","title":"Civilization and Its Discontents (1930) · OCR review","context":"","original_title":"Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review"},"original_title":"Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review","title_language_code":"en"}],"seal":"SEAL_R2TV_141903BB4E1B85BBB0A4","version_work_id":"WORK_STORE_HISTORICAL_FREUD_UNBEHAGEN_1930","version_label":"Added 14 Oct 2026 · Run 14 Oct 2026 · gpt-5.6-terra / gpt-5.6-sol","version_revision":"01dde02f331acc70a871bdb3b4700fbc14cf87a91decddfc66f6316e8789c6cd","original_title":"Das Unbehagen in der Kultur (1930) · OCR review","title_language_code":"en","title_translation":{"schema":"care-title-heading-translation/1","language_code":"en","rendition_type":"machine","originals_preserved":true}},{"id":"WORK_MONAS_HIEROGLYPHICA_JOHN_DEE","slug":"beta-eb6edcaef3392c37","title":"Monas Hieroglyphica","author":"John Dee","edition":"","year":"1564","description":"","cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-eb6edcaef3392c37-df4a27ed9967941c.png","source_url":"","source_notices":{},"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","sources":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM","title":"Front matter","order":1,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_FROM","text":"[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 2]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 4]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 6]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 8]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 10]\n\n[illegible]\n\nn. 6.\n\n[illegible]\n\nL3\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 3, region 1]\n\nDigitized by the Internet Archive\nin 2010 with funding from\nResearch Library, The Getty Research Institute\n\nhttp://www.archive.org/details/monashieroglyphi00deej\n\nMONAS HIERO-\nGLYPHICA IOANNIS\nDEE, LONDINENSIS,\n\nAD\n\nMAXIMILIANVM, DEI\nGRATIA ROMANORVM, BO-\nHEMIÆ ET HVNGARIÆ RE-\nGEM SAPIENTISSIMVM.\n\nAVT TACEAT,\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 5, region 5]\n\nDe rore cæli, & pinguedine terræ, det tibi Deus.\n\nGeneſ. cap. 27.\n\nFRANCOFVRTI\n\nApud Ioannem Wechelum & Petrum\nFiſcherum conſortes,\n\nM D X C I.\n\n3\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 7, region 2]\n\nINCLYTI REGIS\nMAXIMILIANI EX-\nCELLENTISSIMÆ MAIESTA-\nTI IOANNES DEE, LONDI-\nnenſis Imperium optat Feli-\nciſſimum.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 7, region 4]\n\nQVÆ duæ cauſæ, meæ conditio-\nnis Hominem, REGEM tantum, tam exiguo donare Munere, animare poſſunt, hæ amba, nunc, me ad hoc faciendum impulſere. Benevolen-\ntiam imprimis erga veſtram Maiestatem meam maximam: & Muneris ipſius, licet parui, tum Raritas magna, tum Bonitas haud aſpernanda. Benevolentia vobis excitauere & conciliauere ſempiternam: Veſtræ admirandæ Virtutes: Quæ tantæ ſunt, ut, qui illas oculata non per-\nſpexerint fide, aliis quidem, vel medio-\ncriter credant, Rariſsima, de eisdem, li-\n\nA 2.\n\n14.\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\ncet veriſſima, narrantibus. Sed qui eaſdem diligenter accuratiusq; ſunt Con-\ntemplati Præſentes: Orationis, ſe, Di-\nctionisq; maxima laboraturos Inopia ac paupertate fatebuntur; quam primù Oratorie in earundem omnem ſe diffun-\ndere cupiant Amplitudinem. Huiusce rei cauſſas, Ego, proxime iam præterito Septembri, in Hungarici veſtri Regni Poſonio, aliquam trahens moram, lucu-\nlentiſſimas, easque variis exploratas modis, oculatus cognoui Teſtis.\n\nDe Muneris autem (mole quidem ipſa exigui) quod dicerem Raritate, ver-\nbis, quàm fieri poſſit, pauciſſimis; Mihi, Mentis indaganti conamine toto, Oc-\ncurrit Humanæ vitæ Duplex, inq; di-\nuerſas ſententias, Curſus (quorum alte-\nrum ingrediuntur Plerique omnes) iſtac conſiderandus ratione. Quam primum, Infantiæ confecto curriculo, Pueritiæ-\nque: Adoleſcentiam, Quod vitæ de-\n\ninceps\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n5\n\nincepſ ingredietur genus; Animum torquere incipiat Optio: Tunc, in ancipi-\ntis Judicii aliquantulum hæſitantes, Bi-\nvio: Statum tandem: Vel (Veritatis Eſſe quidem & virtutis Capti Amore) ad Philoſophandum, toto reliquo vitæ ſpacio, nervos contendendos omnes: Vel, (Illi certè, Mundanis irretiti Illecebris: aut Divitiarum flagrantes Cupiditate) delicatam Qvæſtuoſamve vitam duce-\nre, modis ſollicite laborandum omnibus. Et Iſtorum, Mille, profectò vel facillimè in venias: Vbi Illorum (ſinceriùs ſcilicet qui Philoſophiæ operam navant) vix Vnum monſtrare queas: Qui ipſa Phyſica, ſaltem prima veràque, deguſtarit fundamenta. At, Qui Cæleſtium virium & Actionum: Rerum aliarũ Ortus, Sta-\ntus, Obitusque, fuerit penitiùs pleniùsq; perſcrutatus Cauſſas: ne eorum quidem, qui ſe totos ad ſapientiæ ſtudia con-\nvertere, Milleſimum, in medium aſſer-\n\nA 3\n\n6\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nre, Reſp. Literaria poteſt. Quid ergo,\nQui, iſtis difficultatibus, ſuperatis o-\nmnibus, ad ſupercælestium Virtutum,\nMetaphyſicarumq; Influentialium Spe-\nculationem & comprehensionem Aſpi-\nrarit, VBI HVNC, in toto Terrarum\nOrbe (noſtris iſtis deploratiſſimis Tem-\nporibus) Magnanimum, vel VNV M,\neſſe ſperabimus HEROA? Cum iuxta\nprioris noſtræ (haud temere receptæ)\nMILLESIMÆ Proportionis Pro-\ngreſſu: EXCENTVM SINCERE\nPHILOSOPHANTIVM MYRIADIBVS:\nAT EX PROMISCVE HOMINVM SOR-\nTIS, CENTVM MYRIADVM MILLI-\nBVS, HVNC VNICVM FELICISSI-\nMVM FOETVM EXSPECTARE DEBE-\nMVS. Cuius ſic demonſtratæ RARITATIS\nHIEROGLYPHICVM Typum, ad\nPythagoricam (dictam) appingemus li-\nteram. Vbi, veſtræ Excellentiæ attenti-\nus intuenti, maiora eſſe (Conſideranda)\n\nofferre\n\nMAXIMILIANVM\n\n7\n\nofferre videbuntur, Myſteria: ex noſtris\nhoc modo deſcripta COSMOPOLI-\nTICIS Theoriis.\n\nΤΥΡΑΝΝΟΣ ΠΝΕΥΜΑΤΙΚΟΣ.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 11, region 5]\n\nIn quo nunc Triplicis iſtius (Philo-\nſophicæ) explicatæ Raritatis Gradus (Cle-\nmentiſſime REX) Optarem quidem hoc\nmeum Eſſe, Cenſeriq; Minus: Vel Ipſe,\nqui artium Maxim arum, Rerumq; Se-\ncretiſſimarum cognitione Excellis &\nabundas, facili poſſis aſſequi coniectura.\n\nA 4\n\n8\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\n1.\n\nAt in Inſimo, primoque Philoſophandi genere, ſtatuere: non id à me arroganter eſſe factum exiſtimo. Et ſi ab humo, alti-\nus interdù videatur Caput levare velle: Ex eodem ergo et BONITATIS Gra-\ndu, fructus uberes, de iſto meo Speran-\ndos Munere, Veſtræ Celſitudini polliceri, audeo. Et, hæc quoque Raritate præ-\nditum eſt, hoc noſtrũ Munus. Quod eo genere Scribendi, uſque ad extremum Orationis filũ, contextum eſt, quo, nunquam, ad hodiernum uſq; diem, aliquod fuiſſe abſolutum Opus, vel auditione ac-\ncipere potui, vel ex maiorum intelligere Monimentis.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\nHieroglyphicum etiam licet appel-\nlem, ſubeſſe tamen & Lumen & Robur\nquaſi Mathematicum. Qui penitius ex-\naminari, fatebitur: Quod in tam Raris\nfactitare rebus ſatis eſſe Rarum liquet.\n\n4.\n\nAn non hoc Rarum, quæſo, Astronomi-\ncos Vulgares Planetarum Characteres,\n\n(ex\n\nMAXIMILIANVM\n\n9\n\n(ex Mortuis aut Mutis, aut ſaltem quaſi Barbaris ad hanc horam Notis;) Iam, Vita imbui Immortali: & in omni Lingua & Natione, proprias ſuas eloquen-\ntiſſime explicare poſſe vires? Cui etiam ac cedit & iſtud valde Rarum: Externa eorundẽ Corpora, ad myſticas iam ſuas (optimis Argumentis Hieroglyphicis) eſſe revocata, reſtitutæve Symmetrias. Quasi, vel eædẽ fuiſſent olim, apud Sæ-\nclum prius: vel tales fore noſtri Optaſ-\nſent Maiores. In Ecliptica Dodecate-\nmoriorum Notis, quà novo, felicia, idem præſtare tentaverimus ſucceſſu, & id videre Vt eſt Rarum, ita novum prorſus. Et hæc omnia in Vnico, eoque MER-\nCVRII, Charactere Hieroglyphico (Acumine quodam præmunito) inclusi, eſt omnino Rariſſimum. Vere ergo, Ille, nobis totius Aſtronomiæ Reſtitutor & Inſtaurator nominari poteſt: & noſtri IEHOVÆ in hoc genere Nuncius, ut\n\n5.\n\n6.\n\n7.\n\n10.  PRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nSacrâ hanc Scriptiōnis Artem, vel NO-\nVAM Conderemus Primi : vel extin-\nEtiam prorſùs, & ex omni hominũ Me-\nmoriâ deletâ, eius Revocaremus Mont-\nis. Idque, à nobis, hoc eſt factum modo, ut placidiſſimè, & quaſi suâ ſponte, Hieroglyphicæ illæ interpretationes omnes, ſeſe in medio ponant : Violentum nil, vel Improprium quaſi per totum videri O-\npuſculum poteſt.\n\n8.\n\nEt hæc, Ita, LONDINENSI noſtro HERMETIS SIGILLO (ad ſempiternam Hominum memoriam) Con-\nſignari; Ut, in eodem, ne Superfluum Pun-\nctũ Vnũ; & ad hæc quæ diximus ſignifi-\ncanda, (longeque maiora) ne unum defi-\nciat Punctum; Omnes cogentur, maxime fateri Rarum. At præcæteris, Illi, qui in Philoſophiæ Sapientiæque pro-\nfundioribus Diſquiſitionibus, Nomen poſſunt profiteri ſuum. Sic enim Teſti-\n\nfica-\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n11\n\nſcabuntur Grammatici: dum rationes eſſe reddendas, de Literarum formis, Si-\ntu, Locis in Ordine Alphabetario, Ne-\nxibus variis, Valore Numerali, aliisq; plurimis (quæ circa Trium Linguarum Alphabeta Primaria conſiderari debent) hic admoneri ſe videbunt. Ut & alias, tam Rarè eſſe Grammatici, Qui Grãmatica, VNAM eſſe Scientiam, ab VNO di-\nſcendam Homine, exacte defendere poſſit: Quam Illum, quem Subrain Terris demonſtramus Rariſſimum: Apolo-\ngetice, olim diſſeruimus. Sed tanta debuys mihi conſtant Myſteria, quæ ſolidiſſima habent (tum iſtius Artis Grammatica-\ntum eorum quæ eiusdem eruantur au-\nxilio Myſteriorum) in Sacroſanctis\nDEI OMNIPOTENTIS\nScripturis, iacta Fundamenta; quan\nta nec Libro explicare magno queam;\nnec Locus iſte, iam requirere videtur.\n\nAnno\n1557.\nIn Spe-\nculo V-\nnitatis.\nſiue\nApolo-\ngia pro\nRoge-\nro Ba-\nchone\nAnglo.\n\n12\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nNeq; mireris, O Romanorum Rex in-\nclyte; Me, Alphabetaria Literaturam, magna continere Myſteria, nunc obi-\nter referre: Cum IPSE, qui omnium Myſteriorum, Author eſt SOLVS, ad Primam & Vltimam, SEIPSVM Comparauit Litera. (Quod nō in Græ-\nca ſolum eſſe intelligendum Lingua: ſed tum in Hebræa, tum in Latina, variis, ex arte iſta, demonſtrari poteſt viis.) O, Quanta, tum, debeant eſſe, Intermedi-\narum Myſteria? Et nō eſt mirum, hoc, in literis ſic conſtare: cum & Viſibilia & INVISIBILIA omnia: Manifeſta, & Occultiſſima (Natura vel Arte) ab ipſo Deo emanãtia, ad eius BONITA-\nTEM, SAPIENTIAM & POTENTIAM,\nprædicandam, celebrãdamq; à nobis, di-\nligentiſſima Indagine ſunt perluſtranda.\nInde, excuſatione omni carere HV-\nMANVM GENVS, docebat Pau-\nlus: Etiam ſi, nullum aliud de hijs habe-\n\nAd Rō.\ncap. 1.\n\nret\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n13\n\nret Scriptũ Maximum; Quam, quod ex CREATIONE, ipſo Digito DEI, in omnibus eſt exaratum Creaturis. At, hoc nunc non ago, Curioſus, vt iſta ab omnibus requirere velim Grammaticis: Sed ipſos, Qui Rerũ abdita eruere Myſteria Laborant: cum, Teſtes facere nos, RERVM quoddam in hoc Genere, (ex noſtra MONADE) demonstraſſe Exemplum: tum Amice admonere; Primas, Myſticasq;, Hebræorum, Græcorũ, & Latinorum literas: à Deo ſolo profectas, & Mortalibus Traditas. (Quicquid humanæ iactare ſolet Arrogantia) Ea-\nrumque omnium Figuras, ex Punctis, Re-\nctis Lineis & Circulorum peripheriis, (mirabili Sapientiſſimoq; diſpoſitis Artificio) prodiſſe. Et licet, omnem Moſa-\nice Legis ſenſum, vſq; ad Iodim & A-\npicum Impletionem omnium, conſidera-\ndi eſſe, nos docuit æterna Cæleſtis noſtri Patris Sapientia: quaſi in IOD & Chi-\n\nMatth.\ncap.5.\n\n14\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nreck ( ex quibus omnes Hebræorum Li-\nteræ, Vocalesque consurgunt ) ultima\nConſiderationis Legalis, facta Analyſi:\nNobis tamen non eſt id Contrarium,\n\nVNITATE APICIS CHIREK, IM-\nMOTA MANENTE: TRINITATEM\nMONADVM CONSVBSTANTIA-\nLIVM, INVNITATE IPSIVS IOD,\nCONSPICVAM, Amplectentibus: EX RECTA\nDESCENDENTE LINEA VNA ET\nDIVERSIS PERIPHERIÆ PARTI-\nBVS DVABVS, CONFORMA-\n\nTAM. Vnde satis enucleate, eodem la-\nbore detegimus: Primos Homines, tam\nStupendam Hebraicarum Literarum\n& Nekudoth Fabricam, ex tam My-\nsticis condere Principiis, ſine Præſentiſ-\nsimo Divini Numinis Afflatu, non Po-\ntuiſſe. Quæ etiamsi, Minima eorum\nſint, quæ vulgarium Grammaticorum\nponderentur Iudiciis: Dum tamen, quo\nſeſe ad omne Literarum & Nekudoth\nGenerationem, & quam mirabili ac-\n\ncom-\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n15\n\ncommodent Artificio, aptè à Sapien-\ntibus conſiderantur, Maxima, perplu-\nræque (abſolutiſſima Anagoga) illos\nedocent Myſteria. Sed diviniſſis, hoc\nmodo, Literarum iſtis, & Linguæ\nPhiloſophus; MATHEMATICOS\nmeos, Raritatis iſtius noſtri Muneris,\nadducam ſinceriſſimos Teſtes. A-\nRITHMETICVS, (non dico, LO-\nGISTA) an non mirabitur, Numeros\nſuos, quos à rebus Corporatis Abſtra-\nctos, & ſenſibilibus omnibus liberos;\nin Diænas recondet receptibus; ibi\nque, Mentis variis tractabat Actio-\nnibus: Eoſdem, hic, in noſtro Opere,\ntamquam Concretos & Corporeos o-\nſtendi, fierique: & eorundem Animas,\nFormalesq; vitas, ab eis, in noſtros ſecer-\nni uſus? An nô maxime mirabitur, Tã-\ntum videre MONADIS Fœtum: cui\nnec ulla Monas Alia, vel Numerus\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n16.\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nadditione accedit : Nec extrinſece ad ipſam Multiplicandam adhiberi poteſt: An ño admiratione afficietur maxima, in Rei & Cenſus Subtiliſſima Generali-\nque Regula: VNIVS REI, tanquã Chaos, propoſita, (ad omne diſſoluendũ Arithmeticũ Dubium, habilis) CEN-\nSVM ipſum, & valore, ſiue Æſtima-\ntionem (Potentiæ in ipſa RE Latentis) Hic Primo ſemper Examine, DENA-\nRIO explicari Numero? Accuratis Diuisionis & Æquationis operibus (vel ut illa Ars præſcribit) mediantibus prius? GEOMETRA (mi Rex) ſibi de Artis ſuæ vix ſatis plene conſtare Principiis (quod valde mirum eſt) incipiet hæſita-\nre: cum, hic, in Secreto, murmurari, In-\nnuique intelliget: QVADRATO, CIR-\nCVLARE, omnino Æquale, huius MONADIS Hieroglyphicæ Myſterio da-\nri. Archimedisque dictos SVD ORES, hic, excellentiſſimo cõpensari poſſe Fru-\n\nEti.\n\nPrinted page frame and horizontal rules.\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n17\n\nEtù: licet tentatum haud fuerit ipſe aſſe-\ncutus Problema. In Magnis Voluiſſe Sat eſt. MV SICVS, quo ſtupore ille poſſit iure affici meritiſſimo: cum ſine Motû & Sono, Inexplicabiles, Cæle-\nſtesque hic Intelliget HARMONI-\nAS? Et ASTRONOMVS, an non perpeſſus ſub Dio Algoris, vigiliarum et laborû pœnitebit ſe maxime, Cum, hic, ſine Aeris vlla perferenda Iniuria: Sub tecto, Clauſis vndique feneſtris Oſtiisq;, ad quodcunque datum Tempus, Cæleſtium Corporum Periphoras, oculis exactiſſime queat obſeruare? Et hoc quidem, ſine Mechanicis vllis, ex Ligno vel O-\nrichalco confectis Inſtrumentis? Et PERSPECTIVVS, ſui ingenii Stu-\npiditatem condemnabit: Qui, vt iuxta Parabolice Coni Sectionis Lineam (apte in gyrum circumactam) Speculum effi-\nceret, modis laborarit omnibus: quo pro-\npoſitam quamcunque (igni obnoxiam)\n\nB\n\n18\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nMateriam, incredibili ex Radiis Sola-\nribus vexaret Calore: Cum, hic, ex Te-\ntrahedri Sectione Trigonicâ, Linea ex-\nhiberetur; ex cuius Forma Circulata, fieri poteſt Speculum; Quod, (vel Nubi-\nbus Soli ſubductis) quoſcunque Lapides, Vel Metallum quodcunque, in Impalpa-\nbiles quaſi, vi Caloris (veriſſime maxi-\nmâ) redigere poteſt Pulueres. Et, qui\n\n7.\n\nPONDERVM ſubtili Speculationi toto vitæ Tempore inſudarit: Quàm bene, ſuos ille collocatos eſſe Labores, ſumptos-\nque indicabit: Cum, hic, Elementum Terræ ſupra Aquam natare poſſe, certiſ-\nſima experientia, MONADIS noſtræ docebit Magiſterium: Hanc ſecus, Qui\n\n8.\n\nRationes PLENI & VACVI (argu-\nmentum uſque ab ipſis Philoſophiæ In-\ncunabulis controuerſum) diligentissime\nventilarunt: Videruntque, ea Lege, &\nNaturâ (quaſi Indiſſolubili) vinculo,\n(à Deo Optimo & Max.) coordinatas,\n\ncon-\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n19\n\nconnexas, & Copulatas Elementorum proximum eſſe Superficies: Ut in Igne, Aere & Aqua, ſurſum deorſum, Hor-\nſum Illorſum, (ex eorum animi ſententia) ducendis impellendisve; hominibus Mi-\nranda confidentiſſime oſtendere poſſint (Variis & illi quidem Inventis Reip. ſunt utiles: Ut Hydraulicorum totum Artificium monſtrat, & reliqua He-\nronis Thaumopœetica; ut nunc placet illa nominare.) At, quod Terræ Elementum, Surſum, in Ignem, per Aqua, ulla Machina exaltare poſſit: Nul-\nlus ex illa Profeſſione, ſibi vendicabit. Nostratem MONADIS Theoriam, fieri id poſſe, demonſtrant. O Sapientiſſime Rex, Iſta in Mentis veſtræ, Me-\nmoriæq; reponatis Theſauris Secretiſſi-\nmis. Ad CABALISTAM iam venio He-\nbræu: Qui, ubi ſuam ſic dictã Geome-\nriã, Notariacon, & Tzyruph (Artis ſuæ tres quaſi præcipuas Claues) extra\n\n“\n“\n“\n“\n\n9.\n\nB 2\n\n20\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nSanctæ, Nuncupatæ Linguæ exerceri fines videbit: Immo undiquaque (ex ob-\nuiis quibusque, uiſibilibus & Inuiſibili-\nbus) huius, ( à Deo) Receptæ Traditio-\nnis Myſticæ Notas, Characteresq; cor-\nrogari, Vel, hanc quoque Artem, tum, uocabit SANCTAM: (veritate coa-\nctus; ſi Intelligat) Vel, non Iudæorum, tantum: Sed omnium Gentium, Natio-\nnum & Linguarum, ſine προσωποληψίας Eundem eſſe DEUM Benevolentissi-\nmum fatebitur: Nullumque Mortalẽ ſe Excuſare poſſe, de Sanctæ huius noſtræ Linguæ Imperitia. Quam, in noſtris ad Pariſienſes Aphorismis, REALEM nominaui CABALAM, ſiue τῷ ὄντι: Vt illam vulgarem alteram; Cabaliſti-\ncam nomino GRAMMATICAM ſiue τῷ λεγομένῳ; quæ notiſsimis Literis, ab Homine Scriptibilibus, inſiſtit. Hæc autem, quæ Creationis nobis eſt Nata Lege, (ut Paulus innuit) REALIS\n\nCA-\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n21\n\nCABALA GRAMMATICA quoque quædam Divinior eſt: cum Artium iſta ſit Inventrix Novarum, & Ab-\nſtruſiſsimarum fidelissima Explicatrix: Vt hoc noſtro alij tentare Exemplo, de cætero, poſsint. Non exhorreſces, bene ſcio, (OREX) Licet iam, in veſtra Re-\ngia Præſentia, MAGICAM hanc pro-\nponere audeam Parabolam. Terreſte quoddam Corpus, MONAS hæc noſtra Hieroglyphica, in Centro Centri, La-\ntens, poſsideret: Quod, Qua ſit ACTV-\nANDVM divina Potentia, ſine Ver-\nbis, ipſa docet: Cuius iam ACTVATO, Lunaris & Solaris eſt (Matrimonio per-\npetuo) COPVLANDA, Influential Gonetica: Licet, ante, in Cælo vel alibi, fuere ab EODEM Corpore SEPA-\nRATISSIMÆ. Hac (Dei Nutu) facta Gamæa, (Quam, Pariſienſibus, ſum Τῆς γαμῆς γάμον interpretatus: id eſt, Matrimonii Terram: ſive Influentialis\n\nB 3\n\n22\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nConiugii, Terreſtre Signum) Super ſuâ Naturam Terrâ, Eadem, ulterius Nu-\ntriri non poteſt, vel Irrigari, quam ad QVARTAM magnam vereq; Me-\ntaphyſicam Revolutionem Completam. Quo finitoProgreſſu: Qui aliut,in ME-\nTAMORPHOSIN, Primus Ipſe a-\nhibuit: Rariſsimeque, poſt, Mortalium conſpicietur oculis. Hæc, O Rex Optime, Vera eſt, toties decantata (Et ſine Scelere) MAGORVM INVISIBILI-\nTAS: Quæ (ut Poſteriomnes fatebuntur (Magi) noſtræ eſt MONADIS\n\n11.\nLib. Do.\nElement.\n\nconceſſa Theoriis. Expertisſimus ME-\nDICVS, etiam ex iisdem, facillime Hip-\npocratis Myſticam aſſequetur volunt a-\ntem. Sciet enim, QVID, CVI, AD-\nDENDVM ET AVFERENDVM\nſit: ut, ipſam Artem ſub maximo MO-\nNADIS noſtræ Compendio, & ME-\nDICINAM ipſam contineri, Lubens\ndeinde fateri Velit. BERYLLISTI-\n\nCVS,\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n23\n\nCVS, hîc, in Lamina Crystallina, omnia quæ ſub Cœlo LVNÆ, in Terra vel A-\nquis verſantur, exactiſsime videre poteſt: & in Carbunculo ſuæ ארץ Lapi-\nde, Aëream omnem & Igneam Regio-\nnem explorabit. Et, ſi VOARCHA-\nDVMICO, noſtræ Hieroglyphicæ MONADIS, Theoriam vigesimam primam, ſatis-\nfaciat; Ipſique, VOARH BETH ADV-\nMOTH, Speculandum miniſtret: Ad Indos vel Americos, non illi eſſe Philoſophandi gratia, peregrinandi, fatebitur.\n\n12.\n\n13.\n\nDeniq; de ADEPTIVO genere (quicquid vel ARIOTON ARS ſub-\nminiſtrare, vel polliceri poſſit: vel vigin-\nti Annorum maximi Hermetis labores ſunt aſſecuti) licet ad Pariſienſes, ſua MONADE peculiari (Anagogica Apo-\ndixi illuſtratũ) alias ſcripſerimus: Veſtræ tamè Maiestati Regiæ conſtanter aſſerim, ID OMNE, Analogico noſtræ MONADIS Hieroglyphica Opere, ita ad viuum\n\n14.\n\nAnno\n1613.\n\nB 4\n\n24\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nexprimi, vt Similius aliud Exemplum,\nhumano generi poſſet proponi. Quod,\nin ſeipſum, dupliciter, traducere debet:\nIpſum, Scilicet, Dignificatum Gloriæ\nOpus: & Operis Imitari Dignifica-\ntionem.\n\nNunc Satis à me; (Imo vereor ſi hæc hominum audiret Vulgus, ne plus ſatis;) de Raritate noſtri huiusce Muneris The oretici, eſſe dictum ( Triplicis Inclytiæ Diadematis honore) Concedas Rex O Maximiliane: Eiusdemque limitibus, e-\niusde definiri Bonitatem. Satis ergo ſit, (Regnum omnium Decus ſingulare) hoc noſtrum Munus, Dum, tam eſſe Rarū demonſtraverimus diligentius, Nemi-\nnem tamen (licet Inuidiæ Linguæ Petu-\nlantia Maledicentiſſimum quidem) A-\nnem eſſe Æſopican muſitare poſſe. Ta-\ntum profecto abeſſe, vt iuſte, illius Indi-\ngnitatem ferat Calumniæ; Modeſtiſ-\nſimi omnes Sapientiſſimique fatebuntur\n\nPhilo\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n25\n\nPhiloſophi: quod non dedignabuntur Illi quidem, una mecũ, Laudes & Ho-\nnorem illi Phœnici accingere, ex cuius Solis Misericordia Aliſ, Rariſſimas iſtas omnes cum Timore & Amore ex-\ntraxerimus Theoreticas Plumas: contra noſtram per Adamum introductam Nu-\nditatem: Vt eiſdem, Ignorantiæ aſperri-\nmis quibusdam frigoribus, multo reſiſte-\nremus alacrioreſ: & Errorum Turbitu-\ndinem, à Philoſophantium tegeremus oculis; Honeſtæ VERITATIS ſtudi-\noſiſſimi. Et quamuis Autoritate aliqua humana, nullo modo,hic ſumus freti; Si-\ncuti tamẽ, Antiquiſſimi aliqui Philoſophi, opportune poterat noſtro illuſtra-\nri Lumine, aliquot notabile dictum vel Scriptũ; ibi, illud amice noſtris exhibe-\nre Poſteris, non recuſauimus. Veluti in Hermetis, Oſtanis, Pythagoræ, Demo-\ncriti, & Anaxagoræ quibusdam My-\nſteriis: in quæ, ex noſtris Hieroglyphi-\n\n26\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\ncis deſcendimus Demonſtrationibus, non tanquam ab illis, fidem emendicantes in iſtis. Et iſtam tantam Raritatem, ita, ab ipſâ coniunctâ Comitatur Bonitas: ut Nihil, vel aperte vel tectè, in hoc libello à nobis eſſe poſitum, PROTESTEMVR, quod non Idem Honeſtum, ſincerum, Di-\ngnitati Humanæ aptum ſit: Pietatis per-\nfectiſſimæ, Religionisq; veræ ſtudio Vti-\nliſſimum. Et ut ΟΡΘΟΤΟΜΕΙΝ certe, in tam arduis Myſterijs non poteſt, niſi Ille, Qui, eorum perfectiſſimam habet omnem Amplitudinem: Sic Nemo citi-\nus Infantiam ſuam, Malitiam, vel Ar-\nrogantiam proderet, quà Ille, Qui, quic-\nquam eorum quæ hic Veſtræ Sapientiæ Commendauimus, vel tanquam Impium Condemnare, vel tanquam friuolum Re-\niicere auderet. Cuius rei, cum nullum, vel Iudicio Acutiorem; vel Vſu Exper-\ntiorem: vel Auctoritate Potentiorem: vel Sinceritate Fideliorẽ; adducere\n\nquis\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n27\n\nquis poſsit Teſtem, quàm Summus Ille\nRegum Rex Omnipotens, Regem fece-\nrit MAXIMILIANVM. Erit ergo\nmihi Veſtra Auguſta Maieſtas inſtar\naliorum Omnium. Cui, hæc noſtra, Pro-\nbata eſſe, haberiq́ue Rata; non ſolum\nTriobolarium multorum obturabit ora\nGrammaticastrorum: Sed etiam multo-\nrum Philoſophantium eriget animos: vel\nhumi, iam, propter tantorum Myſterio-\nrum proclamatam Incertitudinem, Ia-\ncentes. Vel propter Rerum Raritatem,\nImperitorum Superba timentes Iudi-\ncia. Qui bona cum Malis (temere,\npromiſcuèq́ue, ex nominis ſola Similitu-\ndine,) condemnare ſolent Studia. Cum\nmaximè deplorando (interdum) Opti-\nmorum librorum interitu. Q́uorum vi-\ntrumque, Reipublicæ Chriſtianæ, plu\nrimum, variis temporibus, attuliſſe\ndetrimenti, clariſſimè conſtare po-\nteſt. Apto nimirum ad tam\n\n28\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nmagna tractanda Capeſſendaq; Inge-\nnio, vel priori ratione perterrefacto. vel iam, quidem, cum Progreſſus haud me-\ndiocres fecerit, Ruſtice eiuſdem & Su-\nperbe, ab Imperitis Indicibus, univerſo tam nobili tamque divino Myſterio condemnato ſtudio. At alterius eſt loci, ſingulis Scientiis Honeſtis, ſuas compa-\nrare æmulas: falſas illas quidem, Umbra-\ntiles, Odioſas, Moleſtas, Hominumque Societati Inutiles. Quas Solas, & ea ratione qua vulgares capiunt homines & exercent: non Vulgari ſolum ſed ſapien-\ntiſſimi cuiuſq; Iudicio explodendas, con-\ndemnandasque, & fatemur: & ita diligentiſſime fieri, nos quoque, ſuademus. Sed, Qui, CORPORA illa, vel Eſſe neſciant, vel Vbi, vel Qualia ſint; Quorum iſta tenuiſſima ſunt Umbrae. Quo modo, Illi, Hominum non Vulgarium, non Vulgaria condemnare Studia, vel audent, vel ſaltem Iure poſſunt?\n\nFIAT\n\nFv\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n29\n\nIVSTITIA.\n\nVnicuiq; Quod Suum eſt, ſic, tribuatur, in iſtis Vulgaribus Sci olis, Artium Magnarum Vmbræ non ſectantibus ſolum, ſed eaſdem etiam ſce-\nleratiſſime ementientibus adulteranti-\nbusque: Nugas, Errorem, omnemque adſcribamus Impietatem: At in Bonis Solidisq; ſtudiis Projectionib. & honeſtis moribus tum confirmatis, tum ſua in-\ntegritate Clariſſimis: Vel, Vim (ob le-\nuem Vulgi Calumniam) inferre: Vel eorum in Odium vocare nomen, ſtudia-\nque: vel in diſcrimen, Vitam: non ſolum inhumanum id mihi (OREX) Sed In-\niuſtum & quaſi Impium videtur. Nam, ut Corporum quorumcunque, omnes v-\nbicumque Vmbræ, COMMVNES cum ipſis Corporib. TERMINOS habent: (Quod Mathematicis eſt notiſsi-\nmum) Eodem modo, & hic, Phraſes Lo-\nquendi, ſcribendique: Vmbris, Verisq; ipſis corporibus, Communes eſſe, Per-\n\n30 PRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nmittunt SOPHI. Vbi, Imperiti, Tem-\nrarii, & præſumptuoſi Simiæ, V M-\nBRAS Captant ſolas, nudas, & Inanes:\nDum Ipſi Sapientiores Philoſophi, COR-\nPORVM Solida fruantur Doctrina &\nfructu gratissimo.\n\nLuc. c.\n8.\n\nSicq; vere, Illud, vſu venire videmus: Vt Illis, Id quod ha-\nbere ſe putabant, (umbratile,) tanquam non Solidum & Sincerum, ex manibus eripiatur, iuſtiſsime: & Corpora ſta-\ntantibus, Vmbrarum omnis ſit concesſa honeſta legitimaq; Comprehenſio & Cognitio. ΟΡΘΟΤΟΜΕΙΝ igitur opor-\ntet, (O Rex,) inter VMBRAM & CORPVS: & utriuſq; distinguere fines, vires, & vſus, IVSTITIÆ Ille eſt Gla-\ndius, Regius, Imperatoriusq; cuius, vt alia multa, ita, & hoc, eſt præſtare Diu-\nnum Munus. Et Arte profecto qua-\ndam, interdum, Ipſi Sophi, VMBRA-\nTILES figuras, intra ipſorum Corporum Sinuoſos anfractus libenter admit-\n\ntunt:\n\nMAXIMILIANVM.\n\n31\n\ntunt: ne Aſinis in Heſperidum Hor-\ntos, ruditer irruentibus, electiſſimæ præ-\nbeantur Lactucæ, cum illis ſufficiant Cardui. Ignoſces mihi O Rex, Mun-\ndum, de Iniuſtitia (ex Chriſti Auctoritate) arguenti. Neque hæc, ullo modo, hoc loco, hiis Temporibus, Tuæ præſertim commemorata Sapientiæ, Pa-\nrerga cenſeri volo: immo ne Superflua quidem. Atque hæc hactenus. Hunc ergo meum MONADIS HIEROGLYPHICÆ Fœtum (Conceptione quidem Londinenſem, Natiuitate verò Antwerpenſem) Veſtræ Sereniſſimæ Maiestati, humillimè Offero: Obnixe à vobis contendens: vt eiuſdem non De-\ndignemini, nunc quidem, fieri Compa-\nrer: poſt verò, cùm erit & ætate gran-\ndior, & fide ſua Commendabilior, in Veſtra ſemper vobis vt ſeruire poſſit præſentia. Pro veſtro, deinceps Ego eundem haberi\n\n32\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM\n\nVolo, O Clementiſſime REX: Qui, vt mihi viſus eſt toto partus Tempore Blã-\ndiſſimo Aſpectu, ante oculos verſari meos: ita, ea ratione, facilem mihi expedi-\ntumque huius in Lucem editionis, Labo-\nrem feciſti. Nam quum Annos prius continuosᵃ Septem, Mente geſtaui mea, eũndẽ, incredibili veſtra ad tantũ inter-\nuallũ, Virtute Magnetica, duodecim ſo-\nlũ Dierũ ſpatio, in hanc cõmunem Aurã placidiſſime ſum Enixus. Quod, Felix, Fauſtumque eſſe, tum veſtræ Auguſtæ Celſitudini, tum ardentiſſimis meis ſin-\nceriſſimæ veritatis ſtudiis, Concedat illa Sacroſancta TRINITAS, Quæ in MONADIS Ineffabilis, Omnipotentia, ante omnia Sæcula fundata, vivit re-\ngnatque Sempiterna: Cui Soli, omnis Laus, Honor, Virtus & Gloria, ab omni ſemper exhibeatur, decanteturque Creatura. AMEN.\n\nVt ap\nparet in\nAphori-\nſmis\nnoſtris\nPropæ-\ndeu-\nmaticis, im-\npreſſis\nLondi-\nni, An.\n1558. ex\nAph.\n32.\n\nAntwerpiæ, Anno 1564-Ianuarii, 29.\n\nTYPO-\n\n33\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 37, region 2]\n\nTYPOGRAPHO\n\nGVLIELMO SILVIO\n\nAMICO SVO SINGVLARI,\n\nIoannes De Londinenſis\n\nS. D. P.\n\nV\n\nIDES Amice mi, Optime\nGulielme, Quam vnice\ncharus, Præclariſſimas habeam,\nIlluſtriſſimi Regis MAXIMI-\nLIANI Virtutes: Cui ex Cordis\nmei Scriniis, Rara, excellentiſſi-\nmeque communico Arcana: Ea-\nque ratione, illi communicanda\nCuraui, vt etiam Plures per Ter-\nrarum orbem, tum in eius Hono-\nrem, propter eximias ſuas, Regi-\naſque virtutes: tum vt Alii ex il-\nlo Sibi exemplum capiant: qui &\n\nC\n\n34\n\nAD TYPOGRAPHVM.\n\nRegius Sapientiſsime Vacare Re-\ngnorum Gubernaculis: & Philo-\nſophorum tamen, Sophorumque\nStupenda cumulate adiſcere\nMyſteria poteſt) Plures, inquam,\neiſdem frui: Veſtra Diligentia, &\nFide queant. Duo igitur ſunt,\nquæ mihi eſt orandus maxime:\nUnum, Ut ubique accuratam\nmeam, in Literarum Varietate,\nPunctis, Lineis, Diagrammati-\nbus, Schematibus, Numeris,\nalibiſque, Imitieris, (quantum poſ-\nſis) Diligentiam: Ne, Idem Ipſum,\nquod Ego (DEI NVTV) pepe-\nrier ex omni parte bene Formatum\nCorpus, Typographiæ Negligen-\ntia, vel Mutilum, vel Deforme\nprodeat in Lucem: indignum ſi-\nquidem, Rege tanto; Indignum\n\nVere\n\nAD TYPOGRAPHVM\n\n35\n\nuere Philoſophantium Studiis,\n& laboribus, quos in eo poenitiſſi-\nme, ſapiſſimeque examinando,\ncollocare volunt, Maximis. Ca-\nuere tamen ſatis, de iſto, mihi Vi-\ndeor, Infortunio, dum te elegi,\nIſtius nouiter Nati Operis Pa-\nrentem Typographicum: qui o-\nmnibus modis, nitidum, ſuiſque\nBene Compoſitum Membris, tua\nCuratura, emittere potes.\n\nS E C V N D V M,\n\nquod a te præ-\nſtari Optarem, haud eſt leue, id\nquidem: Nimirum, Promiſcuo\nut hominum generi, hoſce, nullo\nmodo, in manus des Libellos. Non\nquod illis ego hæc quidem, vel me-\nliora, inuideam: Sed hoc inde ori-\nturum mali Suſpicaſ: Non ſolum,\nquod ex iſto Labyrintho, Se, Mi-\n\nC 2\n\n36 A D  T Y P O G R A P H V M.\n\nſeri, nunquam extricare poſſunt:\n(Ingenium interea, Incredibili-\nbus Angentes modiſſimeque\nſuis proficiſcentes Rei familiaris\nnegotiis) ſed etiam, quod, Aliis\nquoque, (illis inuiſum) vel, ingredi\nſuadebit Iter: vel de eiuſdem, velut\nillis explorata, Certitudine, Sce-\nleratiſſime ementientur; Impo-\nſtores, Hominumque Laruae. Vel\nDenique, talia DER[illegible]AGNA-\nLIA, Eſſe, Negare. Aut meam,\nrapidiſſime accuſare Sincerita-\ntem audebunt: nunc tandem De-\nſperabundi; Ut, primo, hæc My-\nſteria, cum maxima Præſumptio-\nne aggreſſi ſunt Temerarii. At\nin hoc tanti Momenti negotio, Si\nte bene a multis iam annis noui\n(vel propter amicitiam noſtram:\n\nVel\n\nAD TYPOGRAPHVM.\n\n37\n\nvel Reip. Chriſtianæ Vtilitatem,\nvel ſaltem propter Ipſius Sapien-\ntiſſimi MAXIMILIANI He-\nroicas Virtutes, quæ nihil Commu-\nne cum Hominum Vulgari ha-\nbent Sorte) Canebis, Spero, ne Fi-\ndem tuam fruſtra requiſiſſe Vi-\ndear. Canebis tu quidem: &\nper te, Honeſtiſſimi omnes\nLibrorum Mercato-\nres. Valeas.\n\nEx Muſeo noſtro Antwerpiensi:\nAnno 1564. Ianuarii 30.\n\nC 3\n\n38\n\nMONAS\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 42, region 3]\n\nMONAS HIEROGLYPHI-\nCA IOANNIS DEE, LON-\nDINENSIS,\n\nMathematicè, Magicè, Cabaliſticè,\nAnagogiceque, explicata:\n\nAD\n\nSAPIENTIſſIMUM\n\nROMANORVM, BOHEMIÆ, ET\nHVNGARIÆ\nREGEM,\nMAXIMILIANVM.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0001","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 2]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0003","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0004","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 4]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0005","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0006","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 6]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0007","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0008","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 8]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0009","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0010","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 10]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0011","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0012","text":"n. 6.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0013","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0014","text":"L3","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0015","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0016","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 3, region 1]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0017","text":"Digitized by the Internet Archive\nin 2010 with funding from\nResearch Library, The Getty Research Institute","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0018","text":"http://www.archive.org/details/monashieroglyphi00deej","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0019","text":"MONAS HIERO-\nGLYPHICA IOANNIS\nDEE, LONDINENSIS,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0020","text":"AD","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0021","text":"MAXIMILIANVM, DEI\nGRATIA ROMANORVM, BO-\nHEMIÆ ET HVNGARIÆ RE-\nGEM SAPIENTISSIMVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0022","text":"AVT TACEAT,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0023","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 5, region 5]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0024","text":"De rore cæli, & pinguedine terræ, det tibi Deus.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0025","text":"Geneſ. cap. 27.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0026","text":"FRANCOFVRTI","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0027","text":"Apud Ioannem Wechelum & Petrum\nFiſcherum conſortes,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0028","text":"M D X C I.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0029","text":"3\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 7, region 2]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0030","text":"INCLYTI REGIS\nMAXIMILIANI EX-\nCELLENTISSIMÆ MAIESTA-\nTI IOANNES DEE, LONDI-\nnenſis Imperium optat Feli-\nciſſimum.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0031","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 7, region 4]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0032","text":"QVÆ duæ cauſæ, meæ conditio-\nnis Hominem, REGEM tantum, tam exiguo donare Munere, animare poſſunt, hæ amba, nunc, me ad hoc faciendum impulſere. Benevolen-\ntiam imprimis erga veſtram Maiestatem meam maximam: & Muneris ipſius, licet parui, tum Raritas magna, tum Bonitas haud aſpernanda. Benevolentia vobis excitauere & conciliauere ſempiternam: Veſtræ admirandæ Virtutes: Quæ tantæ ſunt, ut, qui illas oculata non per-\nſpexerint fide, aliis quidem, vel medio-\ncriter credant, Rariſsima, de eisdem, li-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0033","text":"A 2.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0034","text":"14.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0035","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0036","text":"cet veriſſima, narrantibus. Sed qui eaſdem diligenter accuratiusq; ſunt Con-\ntemplati Præſentes: Orationis, ſe, Di-\nctionisq; maxima laboraturos Inopia ac paupertate fatebuntur; quam primù Oratorie in earundem omnem ſe diffun-\ndere cupiant Amplitudinem. Huiusce rei cauſſas, Ego, proxime iam præterito Septembri, in Hungarici veſtri Regni Poſonio, aliquam trahens moram, lucu-\nlentiſſimas, easque variis exploratas modis, oculatus cognoui Teſtis.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0037","text":"De Muneris autem (mole quidem ipſa exigui) quod dicerem Raritate, ver-\nbis, quàm fieri poſſit, pauciſſimis; Mihi, Mentis indaganti conamine toto, Oc-\ncurrit Humanæ vitæ Duplex, inq; di-\nuerſas ſententias, Curſus (quorum alte-\nrum ingrediuntur Plerique omnes) iſtac conſiderandus ratione. Quam primum, Infantiæ confecto curriculo, Pueritiæ-\nque: Adoleſcentiam, Quod vitæ de-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0038","text":"inceps","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0039","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","text":"5\n\nincepſ ingredietur genus; Animum torquere incipiat Optio: Tunc, in ancipi-\ntis Judicii aliquantulum hæſitantes, Bi-\nvio: Statum tandem: Vel (Veritatis Eſſe quidem & virtutis Capti Amore) ad Philoſophandum, toto reliquo vitæ ſpacio, nervos contendendos omnes: Vel, (Illi certè, Mundanis irretiti Illecebris: aut Divitiarum flagrantes Cupiditate) delicatam Qvæſtuoſamve vitam duce-\nre, modis ſollicite laborandum omnibus. Et Iſtorum, Mille, profectò vel facillimè in venias: Vbi Illorum (ſinceriùs ſcilicet qui Philoſophiæ operam navant) vix Vnum monſtrare queas: Qui ipſa Phyſica, ſaltem prima veràque, deguſtarit fundamenta. At, Qui Cæleſtium virium & Actionum: Rerum aliarũ Ortus, Sta-\ntus, Obitusque, fuerit penitiùs pleniùsq; perſcrutatus Cauſſas: ne eorum quidem, qui ſe totos ad ſapientiæ ſtudia con-\nvertere, Milleſimum, in medium aſſer-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0041","text":"A 3","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0042","text":"6\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","text":"re, Reſp. Literaria poteſt. Quid ergo,\nQui, iſtis difficultatibus, ſuperatis o-\nmnibus, ad ſupercælestium Virtutum,\nMetaphyſicarumq; Influentialium Spe-\nculationem & comprehensionem Aſpi-\nrarit, VBI HVNC, in toto Terrarum\nOrbe (noſtris iſtis deploratiſſimis Tem-\nporibus) Magnanimum, vel VNV M,\neſſe ſperabimus HEROA? Cum iuxta\nprioris noſtræ (haud temere receptæ)\nMILLESIMÆ Proportionis Pro-\ngreſſu: EXCENTVM SINCERE\nPHILOSOPHANTIVM MYRIADIBVS:\nAT EX PROMISCVE HOMINVM SOR-\nTIS, CENTVM MYRIADVM MILLI-\nBVS, HVNC VNICVM FELICISSI-\nMVM FOETVM EXSPECTARE DEBE-\nMVS. Cuius ſic demonſtratæ RARITATIS\nHIEROGLYPHICVM Typum, ad\nPythagoricam (dictam) appingemus li-\nteram. Vbi, veſtræ Excellentiæ attenti-\nus intuenti, maiora eſſe (Conſideranda)","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0044","text":"offerre","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0045","text":"MAXIMILIANVM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0046","text":"7\n\nofferre videbuntur, Myſteria: ex noſtris\nhoc modo deſcripta COSMOPOLI-\nTICIS Theoriis.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0047","text":"ΤΥΡΑΝΝΟΣ ΠΝΕΥΜΑΤΙΚΟΣ.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0048","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 11, region 5]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0049","text":"In quo nunc Triplicis iſtius (Philo-\nſophicæ) explicatæ Raritatis Gradus (Cle-\nmentiſſime REX) Optarem quidem hoc\nmeum Eſſe, Cenſeriq; Minus: Vel Ipſe,\nqui artium Maxim arum, Rerumq; Se-\ncretiſſimarum cognitione Excellis &\nabundas, facili poſſis aſſequi coniectura.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0050","text":"A 4","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0051","text":"8\n\nPRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0052","text":"1.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0053","text":"At in Inſimo, primoque Philoſophandi genere, ſtatuere: non id à me arroganter eſſe factum exiſtimo. Et ſi ab humo, alti-\nus interdù videatur Caput levare velle: Ex eodem ergo et BONITATIS Gra-\ndu, fructus uberes, de iſto meo Speran-\ndos Munere, Veſtræ Celſitudini polliceri, audeo. Et, hæc quoque Raritate præ-\nditum eſt, hoc noſtrũ Munus. Quod eo genere Scribendi, uſque ad extremum Orationis filũ, contextum eſt, quo, nunquam, ad hodiernum uſq; diem, aliquod fuiſſe abſolutum Opus, vel auditione ac-\ncipere potui, vel ex maiorum intelligere Monimentis.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0054","text":"2.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0055","text":"3.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","text":"Hieroglyphicum etiam licet appel-\nlem, ſubeſſe tamen & Lumen & Robur\nquaſi Mathematicum. Qui penitius ex-\naminari, fatebitur: Quod in tam Raris\nfactitare rebus ſatis eſſe Rarum liquet.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0057","text":"4.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0058","text":"An non hoc Rarum, quæſo, Astronomi-\ncos Vulgares Planetarum Characteres,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0059","text":"(ex","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0060","text":"MAXIMILIANVM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","text":"9\n\n(ex Mortuis aut Mutis, aut ſaltem quaſi Barbaris ad hanc horam Notis;) Iam, Vita imbui Immortali: & in omni Lingua & Natione, proprias ſuas eloquen-\ntiſſime explicare poſſe vires? Cui etiam ac cedit & iſtud valde Rarum: Externa eorundẽ Corpora, ad myſticas iam ſuas (optimis Argumentis Hieroglyphicis) eſſe revocata, reſtitutæve Symmetrias. Quasi, vel eædẽ fuiſſent olim, apud Sæ-\nclum prius: vel tales fore noſtri Optaſ-\nſent Maiores. In Ecliptica Dodecate-\nmoriorum Notis, quà novo, felicia, idem præſtare tentaverimus ſucceſſu, & id videre Vt eſt Rarum, ita novum prorſus. Et hæc omnia in Vnico, eoque MER-\nCVRII, Charactere Hieroglyphico (Acumine quodam præmunito) inclusi, eſt omnino Rariſſimum. Vere ergo, Ille, nobis totius Aſtronomiæ Reſtitutor & Inſtaurator nominari poteſt: & noſtri IEHOVÆ in hoc genere Nuncius, ut","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0062","text":"5.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0063","text":"6.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0064","text":"7.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0065","text":"10.  PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","text":"Sacrâ hanc Scriptiōnis Artem, vel NO-\nVAM Conderemus Primi : vel extin-\nEtiam prorſùs, & ex omni hominũ Me-\nmoriâ deletâ, eius Revocaremus Mont-\nis. Idque, à nobis, hoc eſt factum modo, ut placidiſſimè, & quaſi suâ ſponte, Hieroglyphicæ illæ interpretationes omnes, ſeſe in medio ponant : Violentum nil, vel Improprium quaſi per totum videri O-\npuſculum poteſt.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0067","text":"8.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","text":"Et hæc, Ita, LONDINENSI noſtro HERMETIS SIGILLO (ad ſempiternam Hominum memoriam) Con-\nſignari; Ut, in eodem, ne Superfluum Pun-\nctũ Vnũ; & ad hæc quæ diximus ſignifi-\ncanda, (longeque maiora) ne unum defi-\nciat Punctum; Omnes cogentur, maxime fateri Rarum. At præcæteris, Illi, qui in Philoſophiæ Sapientiæque pro-\nfundioribus Diſquiſitionibus, Nomen poſſunt profiteri ſuum. Sic enim Teſti-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0069","text":"fica-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0070","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0071","text":"11","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0072","text":"ſcabuntur Grammatici: dum rationes eſſe reddendas, de Literarum formis, Si-\ntu, Locis in Ordine Alphabetario, Ne-\nxibus variis, Valore Numerali, aliisq; plurimis (quæ circa Trium Linguarum Alphabeta Primaria conſiderari debent) hic admoneri ſe videbunt. Ut & alias, tam Rarè eſſe Grammatici, Qui Grãmatica, VNAM eſſe Scientiam, ab VNO di-\nſcendam Homine, exacte defendere poſſit: Quam Illum, quem Subrain Terris demonſtramus Rariſſimum: Apolo-\ngetice, olim diſſeruimus. Sed tanta debuys mihi conſtant Myſteria, quæ ſolidiſſima habent (tum iſtius Artis Grammatica-\ntum eorum quæ eiusdem eruantur au-\nxilio Myſteriorum) in Sacroſanctis\nDEI OMNIPOTENTIS\nScripturis, iacta Fundamenta; quan\nta nec Libro explicare magno queam;\nnec Locus iſte, iam requirere videtur.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0073","text":"Anno\n1557.\nIn Spe-\nculo V-\nnitatis.\nſiue\nApolo-\ngia pro\nRoge-\nro Ba-\nchone\nAnglo.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0074","text":"12","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0075","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","text":"Neq; mireris, O Romanorum Rex in-\nclyte; Me, Alphabetaria Literaturam, magna continere Myſteria, nunc obi-\nter referre: Cum IPSE, qui omnium Myſteriorum, Author eſt SOLVS, ad Primam & Vltimam, SEIPSVM Comparauit Litera. (Quod nō in Græ-\nca ſolum eſſe intelligendum Lingua: ſed tum in Hebræa, tum in Latina, variis, ex arte iſta, demonſtrari poteſt viis.) O, Quanta, tum, debeant eſſe, Intermedi-\narum Myſteria? Et nō eſt mirum, hoc, in literis ſic conſtare: cum & Viſibilia & INVISIBILIA omnia: Manifeſta, & Occultiſſima (Natura vel Arte) ab ipſo Deo emanãtia, ad eius BONITA-\nTEM, SAPIENTIAM & POTENTIAM,\nprædicandam, celebrãdamq; à nobis, di-\nligentiſſima Indagine ſunt perluſtranda.\nInde, excuſatione omni carere HV-\nMANVM GENVS, docebat Pau-\nlus: Etiam ſi, nullum aliud de hijs habe-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0077","text":"Ad Rō.\ncap. 1.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0078","text":"ret","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0079","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0080","text":"13","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","text":"ret Scriptũ Maximum; Quam, quod ex CREATIONE, ipſo Digito DEI, in omnibus eſt exaratum Creaturis. At, hoc nunc non ago, Curioſus, vt iſta ab omnibus requirere velim Grammaticis: Sed ipſos, Qui Rerũ abdita eruere Myſteria Laborant: cum, Teſtes facere nos, RERVM quoddam in hoc Genere, (ex noſtra MONADE) demonstraſſe Exemplum: tum Amice admonere; Primas, Myſticasq;, Hebræorum, Græcorũ, & Latinorum literas: à Deo ſolo profectas, & Mortalibus Traditas. (Quicquid humanæ iactare ſolet Arrogantia) Ea-\nrumque omnium Figuras, ex Punctis, Re-\nctis Lineis & Circulorum peripheriis, (mirabili Sapientiſſimoq; diſpoſitis Artificio) prodiſſe. Et licet, omnem Moſa-\nice Legis ſenſum, vſq; ad Iodim & A-\npicum Impletionem omnium, conſidera-\ndi eſſe, nos docuit æterna Cæleſtis noſtri Patris Sapientia: quaſi in IOD & Chi-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0082","text":"Matth.\ncap.5.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0083","text":"14","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0084","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0085","text":"reck ( ex quibus omnes Hebræorum Li-\nteræ, Vocalesque consurgunt ) ultima\nConſiderationis Legalis, facta Analyſi:\nNobis tamen non eſt id Contrarium,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","text":"VNITATE APICIS CHIREK, IM-\nMOTA MANENTE: TRINITATEM\nMONADVM CONSVBSTANTIA-\nLIVM, INVNITATE IPSIVS IOD,\nCONSPICVAM, Amplectentibus: EX RECTA\nDESCENDENTE LINEA VNA ET\nDIVERSIS PERIPHERIÆ PARTI-\nBVS DVABVS, CONFORMA-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0087","text":"TAM. Vnde satis enucleate, eodem la-\nbore detegimus: Primos Homines, tam\nStupendam Hebraicarum Literarum\n& Nekudoth Fabricam, ex tam My-\nsticis condere Principiis, ſine Præſentiſ-\nsimo Divini Numinis Afflatu, non Po-\ntuiſſe. Quæ etiamsi, Minima eorum\nſint, quæ vulgarium Grammaticorum\nponderentur Iudiciis: Dum tamen, quo\nſeſe ad omne Literarum & Nekudoth\nGenerationem, & quam mirabili ac-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0088","text":"com-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0089","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0090","text":"15","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","text":"commodent Artificio, aptè à Sapien-\ntibus conſiderantur, Maxima, perplu-\nræque (abſolutiſſima Anagoga) illos\nedocent Myſteria. Sed diviniſſis, hoc\nmodo, Literarum iſtis, & Linguæ\nPhiloſophus; MATHEMATICOS\nmeos, Raritatis iſtius noſtri Muneris,\nadducam ſinceriſſimos Teſtes. A-\nRITHMETICVS, (non dico, LO-\nGISTA) an non mirabitur, Numeros\nſuos, quos à rebus Corporatis Abſtra-\nctos, & ſenſibilibus omnibus liberos;\nin Diænas recondet receptibus; ibi\nque, Mentis variis tractabat Actio-\nnibus: Eoſdem, hic, in noſtro Opere,\ntamquam Concretos & Corporeos o-\nſtendi, fierique: & eorundem Animas,\nFormalesq; vitas, ab eis, in noſtros ſecer-\nni uſus? An nô maxime mirabitur, Tã-\ntum videre MONADIS Fœtum: cui\nnec ulla Monas Alia, vel Numerus","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0092","text":"1.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0093","text":"2.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0094","text":"3.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0095","text":"16.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0096","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0097","text":"additione accedit : Nec extrinſece ad ipſam Multiplicandam adhiberi poteſt: An ño admiratione afficietur maxima, in Rei & Cenſus Subtiliſſima Generali-\nque Regula: VNIVS REI, tanquã Chaos, propoſita, (ad omne diſſoluendũ Arithmeticũ Dubium, habilis) CEN-\nSVM ipſum, & valore, ſiue Æſtima-\ntionem (Potentiæ in ipſa RE Latentis) Hic Primo ſemper Examine, DENA-\nRIO explicari Numero? Accuratis Diuisionis & Æquationis operibus (vel ut illa Ars præſcribit) mediantibus prius? GEOMETRA (mi Rex) ſibi de Artis ſuæ vix ſatis plene conſtare Principiis (quod valde mirum eſt) incipiet hæſita-\nre: cum, hic, in Secreto, murmurari, In-\nnuique intelliget: QVADRATO, CIR-\nCVLARE, omnino Æquale, huius MONADIS Hieroglyphicæ Myſterio da-\nri. Archimedisque dictos SVD ORES, hic, excellentiſſimo cõpensari poſſe Fru-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0098","text":"Eti.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0099","text":"Printed page frame and horizontal rules.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0100","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0101","text":"17","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","text":"Etù: licet tentatum haud fuerit ipſe aſſe-\ncutus Problema. In Magnis Voluiſſe Sat eſt. MV SICVS, quo ſtupore ille poſſit iure affici meritiſſimo: cum ſine Motû & Sono, Inexplicabiles, Cæle-\nſtesque hic Intelliget HARMONI-\nAS? Et ASTRONOMVS, an non perpeſſus ſub Dio Algoris, vigiliarum et laborû pœnitebit ſe maxime, Cum, hic, ſine Aeris vlla perferenda Iniuria: Sub tecto, Clauſis vndique feneſtris Oſtiisq;, ad quodcunque datum Tempus, Cæleſtium Corporum Periphoras, oculis exactiſſime queat obſeruare? Et hoc quidem, ſine Mechanicis vllis, ex Ligno vel O-\nrichalco confectis Inſtrumentis? Et PERSPECTIVVS, ſui ingenii Stu-\npiditatem condemnabit: Qui, vt iuxta Parabolice Coni Sectionis Lineam (apte in gyrum circumactam) Speculum effi-\nceret, modis laborarit omnibus: quo pro-\npoſitam quamcunque (igni obnoxiam)","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0103","text":"B\n\n18","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0104","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0105","text":"Materiam, incredibili ex Radiis Sola-\nribus vexaret Calore: Cum, hic, ex Te-\ntrahedri Sectione Trigonicâ, Linea ex-\nhiberetur; ex cuius Forma Circulata, fieri poteſt Speculum; Quod, (vel Nubi-\nbus Soli ſubductis) quoſcunque Lapides, Vel Metallum quodcunque, in Impalpa-\nbiles quaſi, vi Caloris (veriſſime maxi-\nmâ) redigere poteſt Pulueres. Et, qui","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0106","text":"7.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0107","text":"PONDERVM ſubtili Speculationi toto vitæ Tempore inſudarit: Quàm bene, ſuos ille collocatos eſſe Labores, ſumptos-\nque indicabit: Cum, hic, Elementum Terræ ſupra Aquam natare poſſe, certiſ-\nſima experientia, MONADIS noſtræ docebit Magiſterium: Hanc ſecus, Qui","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0108","text":"8.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0109","text":"Rationes PLENI & VACVI (argu-\nmentum uſque ab ipſis Philoſophiæ In-\ncunabulis controuerſum) diligentissime\nventilarunt: Videruntque, ea Lege, &\nNaturâ (quaſi Indiſſolubili) vinculo,\n(à Deo Optimo & Max.) coordinatas,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0110","text":"con-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0111","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0112","text":"19","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0113","text":"connexas, & Copulatas Elementorum proximum eſſe Superficies: Ut in Igne, Aere & Aqua, ſurſum deorſum, Hor-\nſum Illorſum, (ex eorum animi ſententia) ducendis impellendisve; hominibus Mi-\nranda confidentiſſime oſtendere poſſint (Variis & illi quidem Inventis Reip. ſunt utiles: Ut Hydraulicorum totum Artificium monſtrat, & reliqua He-\nronis Thaumopœetica; ut nunc placet illa nominare.) At, quod Terræ Elementum, Surſum, in Ignem, per Aqua, ulla Machina exaltare poſſit: Nul-\nlus ex illa Profeſſione, ſibi vendicabit. Nostratem MONADIS Theoriam, fieri id poſſe, demonſtrant. O Sapientiſſime Rex, Iſta in Mentis veſtræ, Me-\nmoriæq; reponatis Theſauris Secretiſſi-\nmis. Ad CABALISTAM iam venio He-\nbræu: Qui, ubi ſuam ſic dictã Geome-\nriã, Notariacon, & Tzyruph (Artis ſuæ tres quaſi præcipuas Claues) extra","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0114","text":"“\n“\n“\n“","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0115","text":"9.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0116","text":"B 2","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0117","text":"20","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0118","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","text":"Sanctæ, Nuncupatæ Linguæ exerceri fines videbit: Immo undiquaque (ex ob-\nuiis quibusque, uiſibilibus & Inuiſibili-\nbus) huius, ( à Deo) Receptæ Traditio-\nnis Myſticæ Notas, Characteresq; cor-\nrogari, Vel, hanc quoque Artem, tum, uocabit SANCTAM: (veritate coa-\nctus; ſi Intelligat) Vel, non Iudæorum, tantum: Sed omnium Gentium, Natio-\nnum & Linguarum, ſine προσωποληψίας Eundem eſſe DEUM Benevolentissi-\nmum fatebitur: Nullumque Mortalẽ ſe Excuſare poſſe, de Sanctæ huius noſtræ Linguæ Imperitia. Quam, in noſtris ad Pariſienſes Aphorismis, REALEM nominaui CABALAM, ſiue τῷ ὄντι: Vt illam vulgarem alteram; Cabaliſti-\ncam nomino GRAMMATICAM ſiue τῷ λεγομένῳ; quæ notiſsimis Literis, ab Homine Scriptibilibus, inſiſtit. Hæc autem, quæ Creationis nobis eſt Nata Lege, (ut Paulus innuit) REALIS","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0120","text":"CA-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0121","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0122","text":"21","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","text":"CABALA GRAMMATICA quoque quædam Divinior eſt: cum Artium iſta ſit Inventrix Novarum, & Ab-\nſtruſiſsimarum fidelissima Explicatrix: Vt hoc noſtro alij tentare Exemplo, de cætero, poſsint. Non exhorreſces, bene ſcio, (OREX) Licet iam, in veſtra Re-\ngia Præſentia, MAGICAM hanc pro-\nponere audeam Parabolam. Terreſte quoddam Corpus, MONAS hæc noſtra Hieroglyphica, in Centro Centri, La-\ntens, poſsideret: Quod, Qua ſit ACTV-\nANDVM divina Potentia, ſine Ver-\nbis, ipſa docet: Cuius iam ACTVATO, Lunaris & Solaris eſt (Matrimonio per-\npetuo) COPVLANDA, Influential Gonetica: Licet, ante, in Cælo vel alibi, fuere ab EODEM Corpore SEPA-\nRATISSIMÆ. Hac (Dei Nutu) facta Gamæa, (Quam, Pariſienſibus, ſum Τῆς γαμῆς γάμον interpretatus: id eſt, Matrimonii Terram: ſive Influentialis","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0124","text":"B 3","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0125","text":"22","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0126","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0127","text":"Coniugii, Terreſtre Signum) Super ſuâ Naturam Terrâ, Eadem, ulterius Nu-\ntriri non poteſt, vel Irrigari, quam ad QVARTAM magnam vereq; Me-\ntaphyſicam Revolutionem Completam. Quo finitoProgreſſu: Qui aliut,in ME-\nTAMORPHOSIN, Primus Ipſe a-\nhibuit: Rariſsimeque, poſt, Mortalium conſpicietur oculis. Hæc, O Rex Optime, Vera eſt, toties decantata (Et ſine Scelere) MAGORVM INVISIBILI-\nTAS: Quæ (ut Poſteriomnes fatebuntur (Magi) noſtræ eſt MONADIS","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0128","text":"11.\nLib. Do.\nElement.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","text":"conceſſa Theoriis. Expertisſimus ME-\nDICVS, etiam ex iisdem, facillime Hip-\npocratis Myſticam aſſequetur volunt a-\ntem. Sciet enim, QVID, CVI, AD-\nDENDVM ET AVFERENDVM\nſit: ut, ipſam Artem ſub maximo MO-\nNADIS noſtræ Compendio, & ME-\nDICINAM ipſam contineri, Lubens\ndeinde fateri Velit. BERYLLISTI-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0130","text":"CVS,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0131","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0132","text":"23","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0133","text":"CVS, hîc, in Lamina Crystallina, omnia quæ ſub Cœlo LVNÆ, in Terra vel A-\nquis verſantur, exactiſsime videre poteſt: & in Carbunculo ſuæ ארץ Lapi-\nde, Aëream omnem & Igneam Regio-\nnem explorabit. Et, ſi VOARCHA-\nDVMICO, noſtræ Hieroglyphicæ MONADIS, Theoriam vigesimam primam, ſatis-\nfaciat; Ipſique, VOARH BETH ADV-\nMOTH, Speculandum miniſtret: Ad Indos vel Americos, non illi eſſe Philoſophandi gratia, peregrinandi, fatebitur.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0134","text":"12.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0135","text":"13.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","text":"Deniq; de ADEPTIVO genere (quicquid vel ARIOTON ARS ſub-\nminiſtrare, vel polliceri poſſit: vel vigin-\nti Annorum maximi Hermetis labores ſunt aſſecuti) licet ad Pariſienſes, ſua MONADE peculiari (Anagogica Apo-\ndixi illuſtratũ) alias ſcripſerimus: Veſtræ tamè Maiestati Regiæ conſtanter aſſerim, ID OMNE, Analogico noſtræ MONADIS Hieroglyphica Opere, ita ad viuum","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0137","text":"14.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0138","text":"Anno\n1613.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0139","text":"B 4","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0140","text":"24","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0141","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0142","text":"exprimi, vt Similius aliud Exemplum,\nhumano generi poſſet proponi. Quod,\nin ſeipſum, dupliciter, traducere debet:\nIpſum, Scilicet, Dignificatum Gloriæ\nOpus: & Operis Imitari Dignifica-\ntionem.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0143","text":"Nunc Satis à me; (Imo vereor ſi hæc hominum audiret Vulgus, ne plus ſatis;) de Raritate noſtri huiusce Muneris The oretici, eſſe dictum ( Triplicis Inclytiæ Diadematis honore) Concedas Rex O Maximiliane: Eiusdemque limitibus, e-\niusde definiri Bonitatem. Satis ergo ſit, (Regnum omnium Decus ſingulare) hoc noſtrum Munus, Dum, tam eſſe Rarū demonſtraverimus diligentius, Nemi-\nnem tamen (licet Inuidiæ Linguæ Petu-\nlantia Maledicentiſſimum quidem) A-\nnem eſſe Æſopican muſitare poſſe. Ta-\ntum profecto abeſſe, vt iuſte, illius Indi-\ngnitatem ferat Calumniæ; Modeſtiſ-\nſimi omnes Sapientiſſimique fatebuntur","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0144","text":"Philo","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0145","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0146","text":"25","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","text":"Philoſophi: quod non dedignabuntur Illi quidem, una mecũ, Laudes & Ho-\nnorem illi Phœnici accingere, ex cuius Solis Misericordia Aliſ, Rariſſimas iſtas omnes cum Timore & Amore ex-\ntraxerimus Theoreticas Plumas: contra noſtram per Adamum introductam Nu-\nditatem: Vt eiſdem, Ignorantiæ aſperri-\nmis quibusdam frigoribus, multo reſiſte-\nremus alacrioreſ: & Errorum Turbitu-\ndinem, à Philoſophantium tegeremus oculis; Honeſtæ VERITATIS ſtudi-\noſiſſimi. Et quamuis Autoritate aliqua humana, nullo modo,hic ſumus freti; Si-\ncuti tamẽ, Antiquiſſimi aliqui Philoſophi, opportune poterat noſtro illuſtra-\nri Lumine, aliquot notabile dictum vel Scriptũ; ibi, illud amice noſtris exhibe-\nre Poſteris, non recuſauimus. Veluti in Hermetis, Oſtanis, Pythagoræ, Demo-\ncriti, & Anaxagoræ quibusdam My-\nſteriis: in quæ, ex noſtris Hieroglyphi-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0148","text":"26","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0149","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","text":"cis deſcendimus Demonſtrationibus, non tanquam ab illis, fidem emendicantes in iſtis. Et iſtam tantam Raritatem, ita, ab ipſâ coniunctâ Comitatur Bonitas: ut Nihil, vel aperte vel tectè, in hoc libello à nobis eſſe poſitum, PROTESTEMVR, quod non Idem Honeſtum, ſincerum, Di-\ngnitati Humanæ aptum ſit: Pietatis per-\nfectiſſimæ, Religionisq; veræ ſtudio Vti-\nliſſimum. Et ut ΟΡΘΟΤΟΜΕΙΝ certe, in tam arduis Myſterijs non poteſt, niſi Ille, Qui, eorum perfectiſſimam habet omnem Amplitudinem: Sic Nemo citi-\nus Infantiam ſuam, Malitiam, vel Ar-\nrogantiam proderet, quà Ille, Qui, quic-\nquam eorum quæ hic Veſtræ Sapientiæ Commendauimus, vel tanquam Impium Condemnare, vel tanquam friuolum Re-\niicere auderet. Cuius rei, cum nullum, vel Iudicio Acutiorem; vel Vſu Exper-\ntiorem: vel Auctoritate Potentiorem: vel Sinceritate Fideliorẽ; adducere","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0151","text":"quis","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0152","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0153","text":"27","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","text":"quis poſsit Teſtem, quàm Summus Ille\nRegum Rex Omnipotens, Regem fece-\nrit MAXIMILIANVM. Erit ergo\nmihi Veſtra Auguſta Maieſtas inſtar\naliorum Omnium. Cui, hæc noſtra, Pro-\nbata eſſe, haberiq́ue Rata; non ſolum\nTriobolarium multorum obturabit ora\nGrammaticastrorum: Sed etiam multo-\nrum Philoſophantium eriget animos: vel\nhumi, iam, propter tantorum Myſterio-\nrum proclamatam Incertitudinem, Ia-\ncentes. Vel propter Rerum Raritatem,\nImperitorum Superba timentes Iudi-\ncia. Qui bona cum Malis (temere,\npromiſcuèq́ue, ex nominis ſola Similitu-\ndine,) condemnare ſolent Studia. Cum\nmaximè deplorando (interdum) Opti-\nmorum librorum interitu. Q́uorum vi-\ntrumque, Reipublicæ Chriſtianæ, plu\nrimum, variis temporibus, attuliſſe\ndetrimenti, clariſſimè conſtare po-\nteſt. Apto nimirum ad tam","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0155","text":"28","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0156","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","text":"magna tractanda Capeſſendaq; Inge-\nnio, vel priori ratione perterrefacto. vel iam, quidem, cum Progreſſus haud me-\ndiocres fecerit, Ruſtice eiuſdem & Su-\nperbe, ab Imperitis Indicibus, univerſo tam nobili tamque divino Myſterio condemnato ſtudio. At alterius eſt loci, ſingulis Scientiis Honeſtis, ſuas compa-\nrare æmulas: falſas illas quidem, Umbra-\ntiles, Odioſas, Moleſtas, Hominumque Societati Inutiles. Quas Solas, & ea ratione qua vulgares capiunt homines & exercent: non Vulgari ſolum ſed ſapien-\ntiſſimi cuiuſq; Iudicio explodendas, con-\ndemnandasque, & fatemur: & ita diligentiſſime fieri, nos quoque, ſuademus. Sed, Qui, CORPORA illa, vel Eſſe neſciant, vel Vbi, vel Qualia ſint; Quorum iſta tenuiſſima ſunt Umbrae. Quo modo, Illi, Hominum non Vulgarium, non Vulgaria condemnare Studia, vel audent, vel ſaltem Iure poſſunt?","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0158","text":"FIAT","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0159","text":"Fv","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0160","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0161","text":"29","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0162","text":"IVSTITIA.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","text":"Vnicuiq; Quod Suum eſt, ſic, tribuatur, in iſtis Vulgaribus Sci olis, Artium Magnarum Vmbræ non ſectantibus ſolum, ſed eaſdem etiam ſce-\nleratiſſime ementientibus adulteranti-\nbusque: Nugas, Errorem, omnemque adſcribamus Impietatem: At in Bonis Solidisq; ſtudiis Projectionib. & honeſtis moribus tum confirmatis, tum ſua in-\ntegritate Clariſſimis: Vel, Vim (ob le-\nuem Vulgi Calumniam) inferre: Vel eorum in Odium vocare nomen, ſtudia-\nque: vel in diſcrimen, Vitam: non ſolum inhumanum id mihi (OREX) Sed In-\niuſtum & quaſi Impium videtur. Nam, ut Corporum quorumcunque, omnes v-\nbicumque Vmbræ, COMMVNES cum ipſis Corporib. TERMINOS habent: (Quod Mathematicis eſt notiſsi-\nmum) Eodem modo, & hic, Phraſes Lo-\nquendi, ſcribendique: Vmbris, Verisq; ipſis corporibus, Communes eſſe, Per-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0164","text":"30 PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","text":"mittunt SOPHI. Vbi, Imperiti, Tem-\nrarii, & præſumptuoſi Simiæ, V M-\nBRAS Captant ſolas, nudas, & Inanes:\nDum Ipſi Sapientiores Philoſophi, COR-\nPORVM Solida fruantur Doctrina &\nfructu gratissimo.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0166","text":"Luc. c.\n8.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","text":"Sicq; vere, Illud, vſu venire videmus: Vt Illis, Id quod ha-\nbere ſe putabant, (umbratile,) tanquam non Solidum & Sincerum, ex manibus eripiatur, iuſtiſsime: & Corpora ſta-\ntantibus, Vmbrarum omnis ſit concesſa honeſta legitimaq; Comprehenſio & Cognitio. ΟΡΘΟΤΟΜΕΙΝ igitur opor-\ntet, (O Rex,) inter VMBRAM & CORPVS: & utriuſq; distinguere fines, vires, & vſus, IVSTITIÆ Ille eſt Gla-\ndius, Regius, Imperatoriusq; cuius, vt alia multa, ita, & hoc, eſt præſtare Diu-\nnum Munus. Et Arte profecto qua-\ndam, interdum, Ipſi Sophi, VMBRA-\nTILES figuras, intra ipſorum Corporum Sinuoſos anfractus libenter admit-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0168","text":"tunt:","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0169","text":"MAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0170","text":"31","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","text":"tunt: ne Aſinis in Heſperidum Hor-\ntos, ruditer irruentibus, electiſſimæ præ-\nbeantur Lactucæ, cum illis ſufficiant Cardui. Ignoſces mihi O Rex, Mun-\ndum, de Iniuſtitia (ex Chriſti Auctoritate) arguenti. Neque hæc, ullo modo, hoc loco, hiis Temporibus, Tuæ præſertim commemorata Sapientiæ, Pa-\nrerga cenſeri volo: immo ne Superflua quidem. Atque hæc hactenus. Hunc ergo meum MONADIS HIEROGLYPHICÆ Fœtum (Conceptione quidem Londinenſem, Natiuitate verò Antwerpenſem) Veſtræ Sereniſſimæ Maiestati, humillimè Offero: Obnixe à vobis contendens: vt eiuſdem non De-\ndignemini, nunc quidem, fieri Compa-\nrer: poſt verò, cùm erit & ætate gran-\ndior, & fide ſua Commendabilior, in Veſtra ſemper vobis vt ſeruire poſſit præſentia. Pro veſtro, deinceps Ego eundem haberi","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0172","text":"32","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0173","text":"PRÆFATIO AD REGEM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174","text":"Volo, O Clementiſſime REX: Qui, vt mihi viſus eſt toto partus Tempore Blã-\ndiſſimo Aſpectu, ante oculos verſari meos: ita, ea ratione, facilem mihi expedi-\ntumque huius in Lucem editionis, Labo-\nrem feciſti. Nam quum Annos prius continuosᵃ Septem, Mente geſtaui mea, eũndẽ, incredibili veſtra ad tantũ inter-\nuallũ, Virtute Magnetica, duodecim ſo-\nlũ Dierũ ſpatio, in hanc cõmunem Aurã placidiſſime ſum Enixus. Quod, Felix, Fauſtumque eſſe, tum veſtræ Auguſtæ Celſitudini, tum ardentiſſimis meis ſin-\nceriſſimæ veritatis ſtudiis, Concedat illa Sacroſancta TRINITAS, Quæ in MONADIS Ineffabilis, Omnipotentia, ante omnia Sæcula fundata, vivit re-\ngnatque Sempiterna: Cui Soli, omnis Laus, Honor, Virtus & Gloria, ab omni ſemper exhibeatur, decanteturque Creatura. AMEN.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0175","text":"Vt ap\nparet in\nAphori-\nſmis\nnoſtris\nPropæ-\ndeu-\nmaticis, im-\npreſſis\nLondi-\nni, An.\n1558. ex\nAph.\n32.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0176","text":"Antwerpiæ, Anno 1564-Ianuarii, 29.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0177","text":"TYPO-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0178","text":"33","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0179","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 37, region 2]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0180","text":"TYPOGRAPHO","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0181","text":"GVLIELMO SILVIO","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0182","text":"AMICO SVO SINGVLARI,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0183","text":"Ioannes De Londinenſis","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0184","text":"S. D. P.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0185","text":"V\n\nIDES Amice mi, Optime\nGulielme, Quam vnice\ncharus, Præclariſſimas habeam,\nIlluſtriſſimi Regis MAXIMI-\nLIANI Virtutes: Cui ex Cordis\nmei Scriniis, Rara, excellentiſſi-\nmeque communico Arcana: Ea-\nque ratione, illi communicanda\nCuraui, vt etiam Plures per Ter-\nrarum orbem, tum in eius Hono-\nrem, propter eximias ſuas, Regi-\naſque virtutes: tum vt Alii ex il-\nlo Sibi exemplum capiant: qui &","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0186","text":"C\n\n34","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0187","text":"AD TYPOGRAPHVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","text":"Regius Sapientiſsime Vacare Re-\ngnorum Gubernaculis: & Philo-\nſophorum tamen, Sophorumque\nStupenda cumulate adiſcere\nMyſteria poteſt) Plures, inquam,\neiſdem frui: Veſtra Diligentia, &\nFide queant. Duo igitur ſunt,\nquæ mihi eſt orandus maxime:\nUnum, Ut ubique accuratam\nmeam, in Literarum Varietate,\nPunctis, Lineis, Diagrammati-\nbus, Schematibus, Numeris,\nalibiſque, Imitieris, (quantum poſ-\nſis) Diligentiam: Ne, Idem Ipſum,\nquod Ego (DEI NVTV) pepe-\nrier ex omni parte bene Formatum\nCorpus, Typographiæ Negligen-\ntia, vel Mutilum, vel Deforme\nprodeat in Lucem: indignum ſi-\nquidem, Rege tanto; Indignum","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0189","text":"Vere","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0190","text":"AD TYPOGRAPHVM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0191","text":"35","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0192","text":"uere Philoſophantium Studiis,\n& laboribus, quos in eo poenitiſſi-\nme, ſapiſſimeque examinando,\ncollocare volunt, Maximis. Ca-\nuere tamen ſatis, de iſto, mihi Vi-\ndeor, Infortunio, dum te elegi,\nIſtius nouiter Nati Operis Pa-\nrentem Typographicum: qui o-\nmnibus modis, nitidum, ſuiſque\nBene Compoſitum Membris, tua\nCuratura, emittere potes.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0193","text":"S E C V N D V M,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","text":"quod a te præ-\nſtari Optarem, haud eſt leue, id\nquidem: Nimirum, Promiſcuo\nut hominum generi, hoſce, nullo\nmodo, in manus des Libellos. Non\nquod illis ego hæc quidem, vel me-\nliora, inuideam: Sed hoc inde ori-\nturum mali Suſpicaſ: Non ſolum,\nquod ex iſto Labyrintho, Se, Mi-","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0195","text":"C 2","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0196","text":"36 A D  T Y P O G R A P H V M.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","text":"ſeri, nunquam extricare poſſunt:\n(Ingenium interea, Incredibili-\nbus Angentes modiſſimeque\nſuis proficiſcentes Rei familiaris\nnegotiis) ſed etiam, quod, Aliis\nquoque, (illis inuiſum) vel, ingredi\nſuadebit Iter: vel de eiuſdem, velut\nillis explorata, Certitudine, Sce-\nleratiſſime ementientur; Impo-\nſtores, Hominumque Laruae. Vel\nDenique, talia DER[illegible]AGNA-\nLIA, Eſſe, Negare. Aut meam,\nrapidiſſime accuſare Sincerita-\ntem audebunt: nunc tandem De-\nſperabundi; Ut, primo, hæc My-\nſteria, cum maxima Præſumptio-\nne aggreſſi ſunt Temerarii. At\nin hoc tanti Momenti negotio, Si\nte bene a multis iam annis noui\n(vel propter amicitiam noſtram:","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0198","text":"Vel","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0199","text":"AD TYPOGRAPHVM.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0200","text":"37","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0201","text":"vel Reip. Chriſtianæ Vtilitatem,\nvel ſaltem propter Ipſius Sapien-\ntiſſimi MAXIMILIANI He-\nroicas Virtutes, quæ nihil Commu-\nne cum Hominum Vulgari ha-\nbent Sorte) Canebis, Spero, ne Fi-\ndem tuam fruſtra requiſiſſe Vi-\ndear. Canebis tu quidem: &\nper te, Honeſtiſſimi omnes\nLibrorum Mercato-\nres. Valeas.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0202","text":"Ex Muſeo noſtro Antwerpiensi:\nAnno 1564. Ianuarii 30.","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0203","text":"C 3","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0204","text":"38","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0205","text":"MONAS","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0206","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 42, region 3]","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0207","text":"MONAS HIEROGLYPHI-\nCA IOANNIS DEE, LON-\nDINENSIS,","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0208","text":"Mathematicè, Magicè, Cabaliſticè,\nAnagogiceque, explicata:","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0209","text":"AD","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0210","text":"SAPIENTIſſIMUM","kind":"passage"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0211","text":"ROMANORVM, BOHEMIÆ, ET\nHVNGARIÆ\nREGEM,\nMAXIMILIANVM.","kind":"passage"}],"sha256":"bb28d37eb6644877af1d9f966b0d305454b32c35d84af5f52f14596cb838eb70","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231554895136Z_f0d89952","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Front matter","source_sha256":"bb28d37eb6644877af1d9f966b0d305454b32c35d84af5f52f14596cb838eb70","sha256":"b5b63d6e258f47ef0efbff543c0586eab1b7756f0235d2d68405869af8b1d3fd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:15:54.895341+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0001","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 2]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0003","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0004","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 4]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0005","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0006","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 6]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0007","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0008","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 8]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0009","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0010","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 1, region 10]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0011","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0012","text":"no. 6.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0013","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0014","text":"L3","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0015","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0016","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 3, region 1]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0017","text":"Digitized by the Internet Archive\nin 2010 with funding from\nResearch Library, The Getty Research Institute","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0018","text":"http://www.archive.org/details/monashieroglyphi00deej","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0019","text":"THE HIERO-\nGLYPHIC MONAD OF JOHN\nDEE, A LONDONER,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0020","text":"TO","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0021","text":"MAXIMILIAN, BY THE GRACE\nOF GOD THE MOST WISE KING OF THE ROMANS,\nBOHEMIA, AND HUNGARY.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0022","text":"OR LET HIM BE SILENT,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0023","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 5, region 5]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0024","text":"May God give thee of the dew of heaven, and of the fatness of the earth.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0025","text":"Genesis, chapter 27.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0026","text":"FRANKFURT","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0027","text":"At the press of Johann Wechel and Peter\nFischer, associates,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0028","text":"M D X C I.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0029","text":"3\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 7, region 2]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0030","text":"TO THE MOST ILLUSTRIOUS\nMAJESTY OF KING\nMAXIMILIAN, JOHN DEE, A LON-\ndoner, wishes a most happy\nreign.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0031","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 7, region 4]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0032","text":"THE two causes which can encourage a man of my condition to bestow so small a gift upon so great a KING, have both now impelled me to do this. First, my very great goodwill towards Your Majesty; and, secondly, both the great rarity and the not-to-be-despised goodness of the gift itself, though small. Your admirable virtues have aroused and secured for you my everlasting goodwill: they are so great that those who have not perceived them with eyewitness faith may indeed give moderate credence to others recounting the very rare—","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0033","text":"A 2.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0034","text":"14.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0035","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0036","text":"—albeit most true—things concerning them. But those who have been present and have contemplated these same things diligently and more exactly will confess that they shall labour under the greatest want and poverty of speech and expression, as soon as they desire, in an oratorical manner, to diffuse themselves over their entire magnitude. The most conspicuous causes of this matter, tested in various ways, I came to know as an eyewitness, when, in the September just past, I lingered for some time at Pressburg in your Hungarian kingdom.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0037","text":"But as to what I might say concerning the rarity of the gift (small indeed in its very bulk), in as few words as may be possible: as I search with the whole endeavour of my mind, there occurs to me a twofold course of human life, and one tending towards divergent judgments (one of which almost all enter upon), to be considered in this way. As soon as, the course of infancy and childhood having been completed, the race which thereafter proceeds through life reaches adolescence, Choice begins to torment the mind: then, hesitating somewhat at the parting of the ways, of uncertain judgment, it at last resolves upon a condition: either (captivated by love of Truth and Virtue indeed) that all its sinews must be strained in philosophizing throughout the remaining space of life; or (certainly ensnared by worldly allurements, or burning with desire for riches) that a life of luxury or gain must be pursued, with every means diligently exerted. And of the latter you will assuredly find a thousand, or even most easily; whereas of the former (that is, those who sincerely devote themselves to philosophy) you could scarcely point out one who has tasted the very first and true foundations of Physics. But among those who have more deeply and fully searched out the causes of the powers and actions of heavenly things, and of the origins, states, and deaths of other things, you will not produce even the thousandth of those who have turned themselves wholly to the studies of wisdom.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0038","text":"thereafter","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0039","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","text":"5\n\nthereafter the race shall enter upon; Choice begins to torment the mind. Then, hesitating somewhat at the parting of the ways, of uncertain judgment, it at last resolves upon a condition: either (captivated indeed by love of Truth and Virtue) that all its sinews must be strained in philosophizing throughout the remaining space of life; or (certainly ensnared by worldly allurements, or burning with desire for riches) that a life of luxury or gain must be pursued, with every means diligently exerted. And of the latter you will assuredly find a thousand, or even most easily; whereas of the former (that is, those who sincerely devote themselves to philosophy) you could scarcely point out one who has tasted the very first and true foundations of Physics. But among those who have more deeply and fully searched out the causes of the powers and actions of heavenly things, and of the origins, states, and deaths of other things, you will not produce even the thousandth of those who have turned themselves wholly to the studies of wisdom.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0041","text":"A 3","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0042","text":"6\n\nPREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","text":"The Republic of Letters, then, cannot bring forth even the thousandth part of these. What then of one who, having overcome all those difficulties, should aspire to the speculation and comprehension of the supercelestial virtues and of metaphysical Influentials—WHERE, in the whole circle of lands (in these our most deplorable times), shall we hope that there is even ONE high-minded HERO? Since, according to the progression of our former (not rashly adopted) PROPORTION OF ONE THOUSAND: FROM A HUNDRED MYRIADS OF THOSE PHILOSOPHIZING SINCERELY, BUT FROM THOUSANDS OF A HUNDRED MYRIADS OF THE COMMON SORT OF MEN, WE MUST EXPECT THIS ONE MOST HAPPY OFFSPRING. A HIEROGLYPHIC type of this RARITY, thus demonstrated, we shall append to the letter called Pythagorean. There, to one viewing more attentively, Your Excellency will seem to be offered greater Mysteries from our COSMOPOLITAN theories, described in this manner.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0044","text":"to offer","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0045","text":"MAXIMILIAN","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0046","text":"7\n\nto offer will seem greater\nMysteries: from our COSMOPOLI-\nTAN theories thus described.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0047","text":"THE SPIRITUAL TYRANT.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0048","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 11, region 5]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0049","text":"Now that the Degrees of that Threefold (Philo-\nsophical) Rarity have been set forth (Most Clement KING), I could indeed wish this work of mine to be mine, and to be judged less so: or You Yourself, who excel and abound in knowledge of the greatest arts and most secret matters, may readily attain [them] by conjecture.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0050","text":"A 4","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0051","text":"8\n\nPREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0052","text":"1.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0053","text":"But in placing [it] in the lowest and first kind of philosophizing, I deem that this has not been done arrogantly by me. And if, from the ground, it may sometimes seem to wish to raise its Head higher: from the same degree, therefore, of GOODNESS, I dare promise Your Highness abundant fruits to be hoped for from that offering of mine. And this our Offering too is endowed with Rarity: because it is woven, in that manner of Writing, to the very final thread of the Discourse, in which manner I have never been able, down to the present day, either to learn by report that any Work has been completed, or to understand [it] from the Memorials of our elders.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0054","text":"2.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0055","text":"3.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","text":"Though I may also call it Hieroglyphic, yet Light and Strength, as it were Mathematical, lie beneath. Whoever examines [it] more deeply will confess: that, in matters so Rare, to do such things is plainly sufficiently Rare.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0057","text":"4.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0058","text":"Is not this Rare, I pray, [that] the common Astronomical Characters of the Planets,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0059","text":"(from","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0060","text":"MAXIMILIAN","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","text":"9\n\n(from the Dead or Mute, or at least almost Barbarous, signs known unto this hour;) are now imbued with Immortal Life, and are able, in every Language and Nation, most eloquently to unfold their own proper powers? To which is also added this exceedingly Rare thing: that their external Bodies have now been recalled, or restored, to their mystical Symmetries (by the best Hieroglyphic Arguments). As though either they had once been the same, in an earlier Age; or our Ancestors had wished them to be such. In the Signs of the Ecliptic Dodecatemories, by what novel and fortunate success we have attempted to achieve the same thing, and to see this is, as it is Rare, so altogether new. And to have enclosed all these things in One—and that the Hieroglyphic Character of MER-\nCURY, furnished with a certain point—is utterly Most Rare. Therefore, he may truly be called by us the Restorer and Renewer of all Astronomy: and the Messenger of our JEHOVAH in this kind, so that","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0062","text":"5.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0063","text":"6.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0064","text":"7.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0065","text":"10.  PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","text":"we might be the first to establish this sacred Art of Writing as NEW: or, if utterly extinguished and erased from all memory of men, might recall its memorials. And this has been done by us in such a way that, most quietly, and as if of their own accord, all those Hieroglyphic interpretations set themselves forth in the midst: nothing violent, or as it were improper, can be seen throughout the whole little Work.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0067","text":"8.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","text":"And that these things should thus be Sealed with our LONDON SEAL OF HERMES (for the everlasting memory of Men); so that in it not One Point be superfluous; and, for signifying those things which we have said (and things far greater), not one Point be lacking: all will be compelled to confess [it] exceedingly Rare. But above all, those who can profess their name in the deeper Investigations of Philosophy and Wisdom. Thus Gram-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0069","text":"marians will bear witness:","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0070","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0071","text":"11","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0072","text":"marians, when they see themselves here admonished that accounts must be rendered concerning the forms of Letters, their Position, their Places in Alphabetical Order, their various Connections, their Numerical Value, and very many other things (which ought to be considered concerning the Primary Alphabets of Three Languages). As also, that Grammarians are as rare who can exactly defend that Grammar is ONE Science, to be learned by ONE Man, as that man whom we demonstrate Most Rare in Subrain Terris: we formerly discussed [this] apologetically. But such great Mysteries are known to me, which have their most solid Foundations laid in the most holy Scriptures of\nGOD ALMIGHTY—\nboth of that Grammatical Art and of those Mysteries which are elicited with its aid—that I could not set them forth even in a large Book; nor does this place now seem to require [them].","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0073","text":"In the year\n1557.\nIn the Mir-\nror of Tr-\nuth,\nor\nApolo-\ngy for\nRoger Ba-\ncon\nan Englishman.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0074","text":"12","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0075","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","text":"Nor should you wonder, O illustrious King of the Ro-\nmans, that I now briefly mention that Alphabetic Learning contains great Mysteries: since HE HIMSELF, who alone is the AUTHOR of all Mysteries, compared HIMSELF to the First and Last Letter. (Which is not to be understood only in the Greek tongue; but can be demonstrated in various ways, from that art, both in Hebrew and in Latin.) O, how great, then, ought the Mysteries of the intermediate [letters] to be? And it is not strange that this should be so established in letters: since all things both Visible and INVISIBLE, manifest and most hidden (by Nature or Art), emanating from God Himself, must be investigated with the most diligent inquiry, in order to proclaim and celebrate His GOOD-\nNESS, WISDOM, AND POWER.\nHence Paul taught that the HUMAN RACE is devoid of every excuse: even if it had no other [writing] concerning these things","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0077","text":"To the Ro-\nmans,\nch. 1.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0078","text":"than","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0079","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0080","text":"13","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","text":"than the greatest Writing; which, from the CREATION, is inscribed by the very Finger of GOD in all creatures. But I do not now concern myself, being curious, to wish to demand these things from all grammarians: but [I wish], both to make witnesses for us those who labour to bring forth the hidden Mysteries of Things, [that] we have demonstrated in this kind a certain example of THINGS (from our MONAD); and to admonish them as a friend: that the first and mystical letters of the Hebrews, Greeks, and Latins proceeded from God alone and were handed down to mortals (whatever human arrogance is wont to boast); and that the figures of them all arose from points, straight lines, and the circumferences of circles, by a marvellous and most wisely ordered artifice. And although the eternal Wisdom of our heavenly Father taught us that every sense of the Mosaic Law must be considered, even unto the fulfilment of every Iod and A-\npex: as though in IOD and Chi-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0082","text":"Matthew,\nch. 5.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0083","text":"14","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0084","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0085","text":"reck (from which arise all the letters and vowels of the He-\nbrews), the ultimate Analysis of Legal Consideration had been made:\nnevertheless this is not contrary to us,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","text":"THE UNITY OF THE APEX CHIREK\nREMAINING UN-\nMOVED: WHO EMBRACE THE TRINITY\nOF CONSUBSTANTIAL\nMONADS, MADE VISIBLE\nIN THE UNITY OF IOD ITSELF:\nCONFORMED FROM ONE DESCENDING\nSTRAIGHT LINE AND\nTWO DIVERSE PORTIONS OF THE\nCIRCUMFERENCE.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0087","text":"Whence, with sufficient clarity, by the same labour we discover that the first human beings could not, without the most present inspiration of the Divine Deity, have established so stupendous a fabric of Hebrew Letters and Nekudoth from such mystical principles. And although these things are the least among those weighed in the judgments of ordinary grammarians: nevertheless, when they are fittingly considered by the wise, in respect to how they apply themselves to every generation of Letters and Nekudoth, and by what wondrous adap-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0088","text":"ta-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0089","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0090","text":"15","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","text":"bility of artifice, they teach them very great and very many Mysteries, by a most perfect Anagogy. But to these most divine [matters] of Letters and Language, being a Philosopher, I shall bring my MATHEMATICIANS as most sincere witnesses of the rarity of this our Office. Will the ARITHMETICIAN (I do not say the LOGISTICIAN) not marvel that his numbers, which, abstracted from corporeal things and free from all sensible things, he had laid away in the recesses of the Goddess [Diana], and there handled by various operations of the mind—these same numbers are here, in our Work, shown and made as though concrete and corporeal; and that their souls and formal lives are separated by them for our uses? Will he not especially marvel to see so great an offspring of the MONAD: to which neither any other Monad nor Number","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0092","text":"1.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0093","text":"2.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0093"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0094","text":"3.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0094"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0095","text":"16.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0095"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0096","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0096"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0097","text":"by addition is added: Nor can it be applied extrinsically to the multiplicand itself: Will he not be affected with the greatest admiration, at the most subtle General Rule of Thing and Square,\nnamely: ONE THING, as it were Chaos, having been proposed, (fit for resolving every arithmetical doubt), the SQUARE itself, and the value, or Estimation (of the Power latent in the THING itself), here always, in the first examination, be explained by the number TEN? Accurate operations of Division and Equation (or as that Art prescribes) having first intervened? The GEOMETER (my King) will begin to hesitate that the principles of his own Art are scarcely sufficiently complete for him (which is very strange): when here, in secret, he will understand it murmured and intimated: that, by the mystery of this Hieroglyphic MONAD, A SQUARE is given altogether equal to a CIRCLE. And that the said SWEATS of Archimedes can here be compensated by a most excellent Fru-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0097"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0098","text":"And indeed.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0098"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0099","text":"Printed page frame and horizontal rules.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0099"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0100","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0100"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0101","text":"17","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0101"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","text":"And indeed: although he himself may not have attained the Problem attempted. In great matters, to have wished is enough. With what most deserved astonishment may the MUSICIAN be justly affected, when here, without Motion and Sound, he will understand inexplicable and celestial HARMONIES? And will not the ASTRONOMER, who has endured cold beneath the open sky, most greatly repent of his vigils and labours, when here, without any injury of air to be endured, under a roof, with windows and doors shut on every side, at whatever given time, he is able most exactly to observe with his eyes the revolutions of the heavenly bodies? And this indeed without any mechanical instruments made of wood or O-\nrichalcum? And the OPTICIAN will condemn the stupidity of his own ingenuity: who, that he might make a mirror according to the line of a parabolic section of a cone (aptly turned about in a circle), has laboured by every means: so that he might vex any proposed (liable to fire)","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0103","text":"B\n\n18","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0103"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0104","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0104"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0105","text":"material with incredible heat from the rays of the Sun: when here, from the trigonal section of a tetrahedron, a line would be exhibited; from whose circular form a mirror can be made; which (even when the Sun is withdrawn by clouds) can reduce whatsoever stones, or whatsoever metal, into almost impalpable powders by the force of heat (most truly the greatest). And he who","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0105"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0106","text":"7.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0106"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0107","text":"has toiled throughout the whole time of his life in subtle speculation upon WEIGHTS: how well he will declare his labours to have been bestowed and expended, when here, by most certain experience, the mastery of our MONAD will teach that the element of Earth can float above Water: Otherwise, those who","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0107"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0108","text":"8.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0108"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0109","text":"have most diligently debated the reasons of FULL and EMPTY (an argument disputed from the very cradle of Philosophy): and have seen that, by that law and nature, as if by an indissoluble bond, coordinated,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0109"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0110","text":"con-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0110"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0111","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0111"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0112","text":"19","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0112"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0113","text":"connected, and conjoined, are the nearest surfaces of the elements: so that, in Fire, Air, and Water, in leading or impelling them upward, downward, outward, inward, they may most confidently show men marvellous things (and indeed, by various inventions, they are useful to the Commonwealth: as the whole artifice of hydraulics shows, and the other wonder-working devices of Hero, as it now pleases to call them). But that any machine can raise the element of Earth upward into Fire, through Water: none of that profession will claim for himself. The theory of our MONAD demonstrates that this can be done. O most wise King, lay up these things in the most secret treasuries of your Mind and Memory. I now come to the Hebrew CABALIST: who, when he shall see his so-called Geome-\ntria, Notariacon, and Tzyruph (as it were the three chief Keys of his Art) exercised beyond the bounds of","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0113"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0114","text":"“\n“\n“\n“","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0114"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0115","text":"9.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0115"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0116","text":"B 2","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0116"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0117","text":"20","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0117"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0118","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0118"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","text":"the Language now called Holy: nay, that from everywhere (from all obvious things, visible and invisible) the signs and characters of this Mystical Tradition, received from God, are gathered together, he will then call this Art also HOLY (compelled by truth, if he understands); or he will confess that the same GOD is most benevolent, not only of the Jews, but of all Peoples, Nations, and Languages, without προσωποληψίας: and that no mortal can excuse himself on account of ignorance of this our Holy Language. In my Aphorisms to the Parisians, I called this the REAL CABALA, or τῷ ὄντι: just as I call that other, common one, CABALISTIC GRAMMAR, or τῷ λεγομένῳ; which rests upon the most familiar letters, capable of being written by man. But this, which has been born to us by the Law of Creation (as Paul hints), is REAL","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0120","text":"CA-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0120"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0121","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0121"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0122","text":"21","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0122"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","text":"CABALA grammar also is in a certain respect more Divine: since it is the Inventress of New Arts, and the most faithful Expounder of the most Abstruse ones: so that others may henceforth venture to attempt this by our example. You will not shudder, I well know, (OREX), although now, in your Royal Presence, I dare to set forth this MAGICAL Parable. This our Hieroglyphic MONAD would possess a certain earthly Body, lying hidden in the centre of the Centre: which, by what divine Power it is TO BE ACTUATED, itself teaches, without words: and when this has now been ACTUATED, its Lunar and Solar, by perpetual Marriage, Gonetic Influence is TO BE CONJOINED: although before, in Heaven or elsewhere, they had been MOST SEPARATE from THE SAME Body. This Gamæa having been made (which, for the Parisians, I have interpreted as Τῆς γαμῆς γάμον, that is, the Earth of Marriage: or of Influential","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0124","text":"B 3","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0124"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0125","text":"22","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0125"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0126","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0126"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0127","text":"Conjunction, an Earthly Sign) upon its Earth above Nature, the Same can no further be Nourished or Irrigated, than until the FOURTH great and truly Metaphysical Revolution has been completed. This Progress having been finished: He who first himself applied another [thing] to METAMORPHOSIS will very rarely afterwards be beheld by the eyes of mortals. This, O best King, is the true, so often celebrated (and without crime) INVISIBILITY OF THE MAGI: which (as all Magi of posterity will confess) has been granted to the Theories of our MONAD.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0127"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0128","text":"11.\nBook Do.\nElements.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0128"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","text":"The most experienced PHYSICIAN also, from these same things, will most easily attain the mystical intention of Hippocrates. For he will know WHAT, TO WHAT, IS TO BE ADDED AND TAKEN AWAY: so that he will then willingly acknowledge that the Art itself, under the greatest Compendium of our MONAD, and MEDICINE itself, are contained. THE BERYLLIST-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0130","text":"IC,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0130"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0131","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0131"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0132","text":"23","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0132"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0133","text":"IC, here, in a crystalline plate, can see with the greatest exactness all things which move beneath the Heaven of the MOON, on Earth or in the Waters: and in the Carbuncle of his ארץ Stone, he will explore the whole Aerial and Fiery Region. And, if he satisfies the twenty-first Theorem of the VOARCHADUMIC theory of our Hieroglyphic MONAD, and provides for himself VOARH BETH ADUMOTH for contemplation: he will confess that, for the sake of philosophizing, he has no need to travel to the Indies or the Americas.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0133"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0134","text":"12.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0134"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0135","text":"13.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0135"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","text":"Finally, concerning the ADEPTIVE kind (whatever the ART OF ARIOTON may be able to supply or promise, or the labours of the greatest Hermetist for twenty years have attained), although we have elsewhere written to the Parisians concerning their peculiar MONAD (which I showed forth as illuminated by an Anagogical Apodixis): nevertheless I constantly affirm to Your Royal Majesty, that ALL THIS, by the Analogical Hieroglyphic Work of our MONAD, is so expressed to the life","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0137","text":"14.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0137"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0138","text":"In the year\n1613.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0138"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0139","text":"B 4","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0139"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0140","text":"24","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0140"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0141","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0141"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0142","text":"that no other example more like it could be proposed to the human race. Which it ought to convey into itself in two ways: namely, the Work itself, dignified with Glory; and to imitate the Dignification of the Work.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0142"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0143","text":"Now enough has been said by me (indeed, I fear, if the common crowd of men heard these things, lest more than enough) concerning the Rarity of this our Theoretical Gift; grant, O King Maximilian, with the honour of the illustrious Diadem threefold, both its limits and its excellence to be defined. Let it therefore suffice, singular Glory of every kingdom, that, while we have more diligently demonstrated this our Gift to be so Rare, nevertheless no one (although the tongue of Envy be most insolently malicious indeed) may be able to mutter that it is an Aesopic ass. All the most modest and wisest will confess that it is so far from this that it may justly bear the indignity of that calumny.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0143"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0144","text":"Philo","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0144"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0145","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0145"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0146","text":"25","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0146"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","text":"Philosophers: for they indeed will not disdain, together with me, to array praises and honour upon that Phoenix, from whose sole Mercy we have drawn forth all those most rare theoretical feathers, with Fear and Love, against the Nakedness introduced into us through Adam: that we might resist more cheerfully certain most bitter chills of Ignorance; and might cover the Turbidity of Errors from the eyes of those philosophizing; being most zealous for honourable TRUTH. And although we have by no means relied here upon any human authority; nevertheless, whenever some saying or writing of certain most ancient Philosophers could aptly be illustrated by our Light, we have not refused there to set it forth kindly for our posterity. As in certain Mysteries of Hermes, Ostanes, Pythagoras, Democritus, and Anaxagoras: into which, from our Hieroglyphic","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0148","text":"26","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0148"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0149","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0149"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","text":"demonstrations, we descended, not as begging faith from them in these matters. And Goodness so attends upon this great Rarity itself conjoined [with it], that we PROTEST that nothing, either openly or covertly, has been placed by us in this little book which is not likewise honourable, sincere, suited to Human Dignity, and most useful for the pursuit of most perfect Piety and true Religion. And as certainly no one can ΟΡΘΟΤΟΜΕΙΝ in Mysteries so arduous, unless he who possesses their entire most perfect extent: so no one would sooner betray his own childishness, malice, or arrogance, than he who should dare either to condemn as impious, or reject as frivolous, anything among those things which here we have commended to Your Wisdom. Since, for this matter, no witness can be brought forward either keener in judgment, or more experienced in use, or more powerful in authority, or more faithful in sincerity,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0151","text":"who","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0151"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0152","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0152"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0153","text":"27","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0153"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","text":"who could be a witness, than that supreme omnipotent King of kings, who made MAXIMILIAN king. Therefore Your August Majesty shall be to me in place of all others. For these things of ours to be approved by You and held ratified will not only shut the mouths of many threepenny grammarians, but will also raise the spirits of many philosophers, now lying low either because of the proclaimed uncertainty of such great Mysteries, or through fear of the proud judgments of the unskilled because of the Rarity of the Things. For they are accustomed rashly and indiscriminately, from a mere similarity of name, to condemn good studies along with bad—sometimes with the most lamentable destruction of excellent books. That both of these have at various times brought very great harm upon the Christian Commonwealth may be most clearly established. For a genius suited to undertaking and pursuing such","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0155","text":"28","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0155"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0156","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0156"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","text":"great matters is either frightened off at the outset, or, after it has now made progress not undistinguished, the pursuit itself is rustically and proudly condemned by unskilled judges, together with the whole Mystery so noble and so divine. But it belongs elsewhere to compare to each honourable Science its rival arts: those false, shadowy, hateful, troublesome ones, and useless to the society of men. That these alone—and in that manner in which common men apprehend and practise them—should be driven out and condemned by the judgment not merely of the common sort but of every wisest man, we both admit and advise that it be done most diligently. But those who either do not know that those BODIES exist, or where or what sort they are, of which these are the thinnest Shadows—how do they dare, or even lawfully can they, condemn the studies, not common, of men who are not common?","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0158","text":"LET IT BE DONE","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0158"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0159","text":"Fv","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0159"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0160","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0160"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0161","text":"29","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0161"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0162","text":"JUSTICE.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0162"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","text":"Let to each be thus assigned what is his own. To those vulgar sciolists, who not only pursue the Shadows of the Great Arts but most wickedly counterfeit and adulterate them as well, let us ascribe trifles, error, and every impiety. But upon good and solid studies, upon projections and honourable manners, both confirmed and most illustrious in their integrity: either to inflict violence (because of the slight calumny of the crowd), or to call their name and studies into hatred, or their life into danger, seems to me not only inhuman (O King), but unjust and almost impious. For, as all Shadows everywhere of whatsoever Bodies have COMMON BOUNDARIES with the Bodies themselves (which is most well known to mathematicians), so likewise here the modes of speaking and writing are permitted by the WISE to be common to the Shadows and to the true Bodies themselves—","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0164","text":"30 PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0164"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","text":"whereas unskilled, rash, and presumptuous apes seize upon SHADOWS alone, naked and empty, while wiser Philosophers themselves enjoy the solid doctrine and most pleasing fruit of the BODIES.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0166","text":"Luke, ch.\n8.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0166"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","text":"And thus, truly, we see that that saying comes to pass: that from them, what they thought they possessed—something shadowy—is most justly snatched from their hands, as not solid and sincere; and that to those standing with the Bodies every honourable and lawful comprehension and knowledge of the Shadows is granted. Therefore one must ΟΡΘΟΤΟΜΕΙΝ, O King, between SHADOW and BODY, and distinguish the bounds, powers, and uses of each. That is the royal and imperial Sword of JUSTICE, whose divine office it is, among many other things, to perform this also. And indeed, by a certain art, the Wise themselves sometimes willingly admit SHADOWY figures within the winding recesses of their Bodies","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0168","text":"admit:","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0168"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0169","text":"MAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0169"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0170","text":"31","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0170"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","text":"they warn: lest, when asses rudely rush into the gardens of the Hesperides, the choicest lettuces be set before them, though thistles suffice for them. You will pardon me, O King, for accusing the World of Injustice (on Christ's authority). Nor do I wish these things, in any way, in this place, at this time, especially in view of your wisdom just mentioned, to be accounted incidental matters: indeed, not even superfluous ones. And thus far concerning these matters. Therefore I most humbly offer this my Offspring of the HIEROGLYPHIC MONAD (London-born indeed in conception, but Antwerp-born in nativity) to Your Most Serene Majesty: earnestly requesting of you that you do not deign it unworthy, for the present, to become its godfather; but afterwards, when it shall be both greater in age and more commendable in its fidelity, that it may always be able to serve you in your presence. Henceforth may I be accounted yours, the same","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0172","text":"32","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0172"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0173","text":"PREFACE TO THE KING","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0173"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174","text":"I wish, O Most Clement KING, that, as throughout the whole time of its birth you seemed to me to be before my eyes with a most kindly countenance, so by that means you have made easy and unimpeded for me the labour of bringing this into the light by publication. For whereas I bore the same in my mind for seven continuous yearsᵃ, by your incredible magnetic virtue, across so great an interval, I have most calmly brought it forth into this common air in the space of twelve days only. May that most sacred TRINITY grant that this be fortunate and auspicious, both to your august Highness and to my most ardent studies of most sincere truth: the TRINITY which, founded before all ages in the ineffable omnipotence of the MONAD, lives and reigns everlasting; to Whom alone may all praise, honour, power, and glory always be offered and sung by every creature. AMEN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0175","text":"As appears in our Propaedeutic Aphorisms, printed at London, in the year 1558, from Aphorism 32.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0175"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0176","text":"At Antwerp, 29 January, in the year 1564.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0176"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0177","text":"TYPO-","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0177"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0178","text":"33","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0178"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0179","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 37, region 2]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0179"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0180","text":"TO THE PRINTER","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0180"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0181","text":"GUILIELMUS SILVIUS","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0181"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0182","text":"HIS SINGULAR FRIEND,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0182"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0183","text":"John Dee of London","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0183"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0184","text":"Sends Many Greetings.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0184"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0185","text":"Y\n\nOU see, my friend, excellent Guilielmus, how uniquely dear I hold the most illustrious virtues of the most illustrious King MAXIMI-\nLIAN: to whom, from the innermost repositories of my heart, I communicate rare and most excellent secrets. And I have taken care that they be communicated to him in such a manner that still more persons throughout the circle of lands may, both in honour of him, on account of his exceptional and kingly virtues, and so that others may take from him an example for themselves—who, both","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0185"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0186","text":"C\n\n34","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0186"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0187","text":"TO THE PRINTER.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0187"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","text":"being most wisely royal, can be free for the helms of kingdoms, and yet abundantly learn the stupendous mysteries of philosophers and sages—may, I say, enjoy the same through your diligence and fidelity. There are therefore two things which I must especially request of you: one, that everywhere you imitate, as far as you can, my painstaking care in the variety of letters, points, lines, diagrams, figures, numbers, and elsewhere; lest that very thing which I (BY THE NOD OF GOD) have brought forth as a body well formed in every part should, through the negligence of typography, come forth into the light either mutilated or deformed: for it would be unworthy of so great a King; unworthy","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0189","text":"Truly","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0189"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0190","text":"TO THE PRINTER","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0190"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0191","text":"35","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0191"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0192","text":"truly of the studies and labours of philosophers, who wish to devote the greatest care to examining it most diligently and wisely. Yet I seem sufficiently to have guarded against that misfortune, when I chose you as the typographical parent of this newly born work: who can, by every means, send it forth fair and well composed in its members, under your care.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0192"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0193","text":"S E C O N D,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0193"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","text":"what I should wish to be afforded by you is indeed no slight thing: namely, that you should by no means put these little books into the hands of the promiscuous race of men. Not because I begrudge them these things, or even better things: but because you will suspect that this evil will arise therefrom: not only because from that Labyrinth they, wretched men, can never extricate themselves:","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0195","text":"C 2","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0195"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0196","text":"36 T O  T H E  P R I N T E R.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0196"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","text":"(while meanwhile they strain their intellects beyond belief and make the slightest progress in the affairs of their household) but also because they will persuade others too (a path hateful to them) either to enter upon the journey; or, concerning its certainty, as though it had been explored by them, they will most wickedly lie—impostors and spectres of men. Or finally they will deny that such DER[illegible]AGNALIA exist. Or they will dare most swiftly to accuse my sincerity: now at last despairing, just as at first, rash men, they approached these Mysteries with the greatest presumption. But in a matter of such great moment, if I have known you well for many years (whether on account of our friendship:","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0198","text":"Or","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0198"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0199","text":"TO THE PRINTER.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0199"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0200","text":"37","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0200"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0201","text":"or for the usefulness of the Christian Commonwealth, or at least on account of the heroic virtues of MAXIMILIAN himself, most wise, which have nothing in common with the vulgar lot of men), you will proclaim, I hope, that I do not seem to have sought your trust in vain. You indeed will proclaim it: and, through you, all most honourable booksellers. Farewell.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0201"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0202","text":"From our Antwerp study:\n30 January, in the year 1564.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0202"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0203","text":"C 3","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0203"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0204","text":"38","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0204"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0205","text":"MONAD","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0205"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0206","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 42, region 3]","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0206"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0207","text":"THE HIEROGLYPHIC\nMONAD OF JOHN DEE,\nLONDONER,","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0207"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0208","text":"explained mathematically, magically, cabalistically,\nand anagogically:","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0208"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0209","text":"TO","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0209"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0210","text":"THE MOST WISE","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0210"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0211","text":"KING\nOF THE ROMANS, BOHEMIA, AND\nHUNGARY,\nMAXIMILIAN.","kind":"passage","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_FROM:P0211"]}],"source_digest":"3981dd991db35587625e6cae546b0a14c672a9f8ccee5624907709b9ea6fe796","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Front matter"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Front matter","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI","title":"THEOREM I.","order":2,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_THEI","text":"THEOREMA I.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 42, region 10]\n\nPER Lineam rectam, Circu-\nlumque, Prima, Simpliciſſi-\nmaque fuit Rerum, tum, non\nexiſtentium, tum in Naturæ laten-\ntium Inuolucris, in Lucem Produ-\nctio, repræſentatioque.\n\nTHEO-\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n391","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREMA I.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 42, region 10]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0003","text":"PER Lineam rectam, Circu-\nlumque, Prima, Simpliciſſi-\nmaque fuit Rerum, tum, non\nexiſtentium, tum in Naturæ laten-\ntium Inuolucris, in Lucem Produ-\nctio, repræſentatioque.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0004","text":"THEO-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0005","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0006","text":"391","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"5c407fc33075eca45fba03d944b37f3e353597fd6e3cd7fd8a1c0fe0beb28f77","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231559103082Z_1c6612a8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM I.","source_sha256":"5c407fc33075eca45fba03d944b37f3e353597fd6e3cd7fd8a1c0fe0beb28f77","sha256":"ff124dafc9ea7b0ab66b2c77cf33c67f6fa756646ae3079fee9ccf1486ee4124","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:15:59.103133+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM I.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 42, region 10]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0003","text":"By means of the straight line and the circle, there was the first and simplest bringing forth into light and representation of things, both non-existent and lying hidden in the coverings of Nature.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0004","text":"THEO-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0005","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0006","text":"391","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEI:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"e593d419897d1c486557a74c35a5f7f2c64634a3a1b22e3eb91d0545cce5b6e3","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOREMA I."}],"original_title":"THEOREMA I.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2","title":"THEOREM II.","order":3,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_2","text":"THEOREMA II.\n\nAT nec ſine recta, Circulus; nec\nſine Puncto, Recta artificioſe fie-\nri poteſt. Puncti proinde, Monadíſq;\nratione, Res, & eſſe cœperunt primo:\nEt quæ peripheria ſunt affectæ, quam-\ntæcumque fuerint) Centralis Puncti\nnullo modo carere poſ-\nſunt Miniſterio.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 5]","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREMA II.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0002","text":"AT nec ſine recta, Circulus; nec\nſine Puncto, Recta artificioſe fie-\nri poteſt. Puncti proinde, Monadíſq;\nratione, Res, & eſſe cœperunt primo:\nEt quæ peripheria ſunt affectæ, quam-\ntæcumque fuerint) Centralis Puncti\nnullo modo carere poſ-\nſunt Miniſterio.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 5]","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"7fb7d099ab11be3db2df53f6af36bc5b7dd863ad1248efde948e0fed4908f3ab","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231601569637Z_311e41c4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM II.","source_sha256":"7fb7d099ab11be3db2df53f6af36bc5b7dd863ad1248efde948e0fed4908f3ab","sha256":"85f2efe21abda9d4aba02b4b1587f9db17cf50f1c04b66ccaf294b14c7d24a85","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:01.569724+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM II.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0002","text":"But neither can a Circle be made without a straight line, nor a Straight Line artfully made without a Point. Accordingly, things began first to have both the nature of a Point and of a Monad; and whatever things are affected by a circumference, however many they may have been, can by no means lack the service of a Central Point.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 5]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_2:DISPLAY-0003"]}],"source_digest":"d09706e9914b7c565021fdb6b09a82911f2034b749fecfd56f569486d4f8356e","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOREMA II."}],"original_title":"THEOREMA II.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3","title":"THEOREM III.","order":4,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_3","text":"THEOREMA III.\n\nMONADIS, Igitur, HIERO-\nGLYPHICÆ Conſpicui Cen-\ntrale Punctum, TERRAM refert;\ncirca quam, tum SOL tum LVNA,\nreliquique Planetæ ſuos conficiunt\nCurſus. Et in hoc munere, quia di-\ngnitatem SOL obtinet\nſummam, ipſum, (per\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 8]\n\nMONAS\nHIERO-\nGLYPHI-\nCA.\n\nexcellentiam,) Circu\nlo notamus Integro,\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 11]\n\nCentroque Viſibili.\n\nC 4\n\n40\nM O N A S","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREMA III.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0002","text":"MONADIS, Igitur, HIERO-\nGLYPHICÆ Conſpicui Cen-\ntrale Punctum, TERRAM refert;\ncirca quam, tum SOL tum LVNA,\nreliquique Planetæ ſuos conficiunt\nCurſus. Et in hoc munere, quia di-\ngnitatem SOL obtinet\nſummam, ipſum, (per","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 8]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0004","text":"MONAS\nHIERO-\nGLYPHI-\nCA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0005","text":"excellentiam,) Circu\nlo notamus Integro,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0006","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 11]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0007","text":"Centroque Viſibili.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0008","text":"C 4","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0009","text":"40\nM O N A S","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"d11075f56fd6b12eb1087405153a61f7029d05e7a1b044777d0ae612b4b47678","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231609852105Z_065c709d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM III.","source_sha256":"d11075f56fd6b12eb1087405153a61f7029d05e7a1b044777d0ae612b4b47678","sha256":"8684798c3c08699e0c20c3a99601f1268e1adf1908826609dd1a9f294c8e806c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:09.852266+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM III.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0002","text":"The visible central point, therefore, of the HIERO-\nGLYPHIC Monad signifies the EARTH;\naround which both the SUN and the MOON,\nand the remaining planets, complete their\ncourses. And in this office, since the\nSUN obtains the highest\ndignity,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 8]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIERO-\nGLYPHIC\nMONAD.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0005","text":"it itself, (by\nexcellence,) we denote by a\ncomplete circle,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0006","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 11]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0007","text":"and a visible centre.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0008","text":"C 4","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0009","text":"40\nM O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_3:DISPLAY-0009"]}],"source_digest":"cc3699a48e2ea0c4ca8580010c378689e0f7226798521329d93d964b7c94b13c","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOREMA III."}],"original_title":"THEOREMA III.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEO","title":"T H E O R E M IIII.","order":5,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_THEO","text":"T H E O R E M A  IIII.\n\nLunæ Hemicyclium, licet hic, So-\nlari ſit Circulo quaſi Superius\nPriusque: Tamen S O L E M tanquã\nDominum, Regemque ſuum ob-\nſervat: ejuſdem Forma ac vicinitate\nadeo gaudere videtur, vt & illam in\nSemidiametri æmuletur Magnitu-\ndine, (Vulgaribus apparente homi-\nnibus,) & ad eundem, ſemper ſuum\nconvertat Lumen: S O L A R I B V S Q.\nita tandem imbui Radiis appetat, vt\nin eundem quaſi transformata, toto\ndiſpareat Cælo: donec aliquot poſt\nDiebus, omnino hac qua depinxi-\nmus, appareat Corniculata figura.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEO:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M A  IIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEO:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Lunæ Hemicyclium, licet hic, So-\nlari ſit Circulo quaſi Superius\nPriusque: Tamen S O L E M tanquã\nDominum, Regemque ſuum ob-\nſervat: ejuſdem Forma ac vicinitate\nadeo gaudere videtur, vt & illam in\nSemidiametri æmuletur Magnitu-\ndine, (Vulgaribus apparente homi-\nnibus,) & ad eundem, ſemper ſuum\nconvertat Lumen: S O L A R I B V S Q.\nita tandem imbui Radiis appetat, vt\nin eundem quaſi transformata, toto\ndiſpareat Cælo: donec aliquot poſt\nDiebus, omnino hac qua depinxi-\nmus, appareat Corniculata figura.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"33355db32f1d1226f518f470c37f0f11204af1e3e330e320c783f0ad66d06aaa","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231617142999Z_77715e21","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R E M IIII.","source_sha256":"33355db32f1d1226f518f470c37f0f11204af1e3e330e320c783f0ad66d06aaa","sha256":"fd7c2f9b5d7eb5273042aa59d94f497c1337e6e77ef85d7c1faa747d6a45a928","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:17.143153+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEO:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M  IIII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEO:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEO:DISPLAY-0002","text":"The Moon’s semicircle, although here, in relation to the So-\nlar Circle, is as it were Higher\nand Prior: yet it observes the S U N as\nits Lord and King: and seems so greatly\nto delight in his Form and nearness, that it\nboth emulates that Form in the Magnitude\nof its Semidiameter (as appears to common\nmen), and always turns its own\nLight toward the same: and so desires at last\nto be imbued with S O L A R Rays, that,\nas if transformed into the same, it disappears\nfrom the whole Heaven: until, after some\nDays, it appears altogether in this horned\nfigure which we have depicted.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEO:DISPLAY-0002"]}],"source_digest":"0fbb50955bd9310b8aeda556670a281d237c1b74be7c18e9a6afb294a0308a15","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R E M A IIII."}],"original_title":"T H E O R E M A IIII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4","title":"T H E O R E M V.","order":6,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_4","text":"T H E O R E M A  V.\n\nET Lunari certe Semicirculo ad\nSolare complementum perducto:\nFactum eſt Veſpere & Mane Dies\nvnus. Sit ergo Primus, quo Lvx eſt\nfacta: Philoſophorum.\n\nT H E O-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n41","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M A  V.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0002","text":"ET Lunari certe Semicirculo ad\nSolare complementum perducto:\nFactum eſt Veſpere & Mane Dies\nvnus. Sit ergo Primus, quo Lvx eſt\nfacta: Philoſophorum.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0003","text":"T H E O-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0004","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0005","text":"41","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"92b9cdf6a3314ae5c7ed642f445af72356c06cb7a5dc7112edf335d32262467e","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231619719313Z_aa5db7c5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R E M V.","source_sha256":"92b9cdf6a3314ae5c7ed642f445af72356c06cb7a5dc7112edf335d32262467e","sha256":"901b43e3d83eb01e56637978c75618a6444a27502bf9a7aeecc1f2a4717d866b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:19.719369+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M  V.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0002","text":"And certainly, the Lunar Semicircle having been brought to its Solar complement:\nEvening and Morning, one day, came to pass.\nLet it therefore be the First, on which Light was\nmade: of the Philosophers.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0003","text":"T H E O-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0004","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0005","text":"41","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_4:DISPLAY-0005"]}],"source_digest":"99fa3bed40b48ed1ae86342e96a8b1859978f760abe8fb75ff0b5f2a0985d967","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R E M A V."}],"original_title":"T H E O R E M A V.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5","title":"T H E O R E M V I.","order":7,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_5","text":"T H E O R E M A  V I.\n\nS O L E M, L V N A M Q V E, Rectili-\nneæ Cruci, inniti, hîc videmus.\nQuæ, tum T E R N A R I V M, tum\nQ V A T E R N A R I V M, appoſite ſa-\ntis, ratione ſignificare Hieroglyphi-\nca poteſt. T E R N A R I V M quidem:\nex duabus Rectis, & Commu-\nni vtriſque, quaſi Copulatiuo\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 45, region 5]\n\nPuncto. Q V A T E R N A R I V M vero: ex 4. Rectis, includenti-\nbus 4. Angulos rectos. Singulis, bis, (adhoc) repetitis; (Sicque, ibidem, ſecretiſſime, etiam O C T O N A R I V S, ſe offert; quem, dubito an noſtri Præ-\ndeceſſores, Magi, vmquam conſpe-\nxerint: Notabisq. maxime.) Primo rum Patrum, & Sophorum T E R-\nN A R I V S, Magicus, C O R P O R E  S P I-\nR I T V, & A N I M A, conſtabat. Vnde,\nManifeſtum hîc Primarium habe-\nmus S E P T E N A R I V M. Ex dua-\n\n42\n\nM O N A S\n\nbus nimirum Rectis, ET Communi\nPuncto: Deinde ex 4. Rectis, AB\nVno Puncto, ſeſe, Separantibus.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M A  V I.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0002","text":"S O L E M, L V N A M Q V E, Rectili-\nneæ Cruci, inniti, hîc videmus.\nQuæ, tum T E R N A R I V M, tum\nQ V A T E R N A R I V M, appoſite ſa-\ntis, ratione ſignificare Hieroglyphi-\nca poteſt. T E R N A R I V M quidem:\nex duabus Rectis, & Commu-\nni vtriſque, quaſi Copulatiuo","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 45, region 5]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Puncto. Q V A T E R N A R I V M vero: ex 4. Rectis, includenti-\nbus 4. Angulos rectos. Singulis, bis, (adhoc) repetitis; (Sicque, ibidem, ſecretiſſime, etiam O C T O N A R I V S, ſe offert; quem, dubito an noſtri Præ-\ndeceſſores, Magi, vmquam conſpe-\nxerint: Notabisq. maxime.) Primo rum Patrum, & Sophorum T E R-\nN A R I V S, Magicus, C O R P O R E  S P I-\nR I T V, & A N I M A, conſtabat. Vnde,\nManifeſtum hîc Primarium habe-\nmus S E P T E N A R I V M. Ex dua-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0005","text":"42","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0006","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0007","text":"bus nimirum Rectis, ET Communi\nPuncto: Deinde ex 4. Rectis, AB\nVno Puncto, ſeſe, Separantibus.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"b9b6f0541d21b79f14aca2f3722dd406ab3ce9843a6e6560a992e5cfaaa6939f","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231631074441Z_fca27f2c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R E M V I.","source_sha256":"b9b6f0541d21b79f14aca2f3722dd406ab3ce9843a6e6560a992e5cfaaa6939f","sha256":"20474f24981c1dab18da3f08d3b892e254afff3fd16f7753a117c99e97b7cc94","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:31.074475+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M  V I.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Here we see the S U N and M O O N resting upon a straight-\nlined Cross.\nWhich can aptly enough signify, in a\nHieroglyphic manner, both the T E R N A R Y\nand the Q U A T E R N A R Y. The T E R N A R Y indeed:\nfrom two Straight Lines, and a Point\ncommon to both, as it were Copulative","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 45, region 5]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Point. But the Q U A T E R N A R Y: from 4 Straight Lines, enclosing\n4 right Angles. Each being twice (for this purpose) repeated; (and thus, in the same place, most secretly, also the O C T O N A R Y presents itself; whether, I doubt, our Pre-\ndecessors, the Magi, ever beheld it: and you will especially note this.) The magical T E R-\nN A R Y of the earliest Fathers and Sages consisted of B O D Y, S P I-\nR I T, and S O U L. Whence,\nhere we have the Primary S E P T E N A R Y. From two-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0005","text":"42","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0006","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0007","text":"namely, Straight Lines, A N D a common\nPoint: then from 4 Straight Lines, separating\nthemselves F R O M one Point.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_5:DISPLAY-0007"]}],"source_digest":"00353bf253c9a782b3b468c61ee8858c193908663a57cc6b201410829f8fbaeb","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R E M A V I."}],"original_title":"T H E O R E M A V I.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6","title":"T H E O R. V I I.","order":8,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_6","text":"T H E O R.  V I I.\n\nELementis, extra ſuas Sedes natu-\nrales, dimotis: Suos ad eaſdem\nreditus, naturaliter, per Rectas face-\nre lineas, Dislocatæ eorundem ho-\nmogeneæ Partes, experientem do-\ncebunt: Abſurdum igitur non erit,\nper 4. rectas, ab vnico Puncto, Indi-\nuiduoque in Contrarias excurrentes\npartes, QVATVOR ELEMENTO-\nRVM, (in quæ Elementata, ſingula,\ntandem reſolui poſſunt) innuere\nMyſterium. Hoc etiam notabilis dili-\ngẽter; Geometras docere, LINEAM\nEX PVNCTI FLVXV, produci.\nNos hic ſimili ratione, fieri mone-\nmus: Dum Elementares noſtræ Li-\nneæ, ex STILLAE, (tamquam Pun\n\ncti,\n\nHIER OGLYPHICA.\n\n43\n\nÆti, Phyſici) continuo Caſu, (quaſi\nFLVXV) in Mechanica noſtra pro-\nducantur Magia.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.  V I I.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0002","text":"ELementis, extra ſuas Sedes natu-\nrales, dimotis: Suos ad eaſdem\nreditus, naturaliter, per Rectas face-\nre lineas, Dislocatæ eorundem ho-\nmogeneæ Partes, experientem do-\ncebunt: Abſurdum igitur non erit,\nper 4. rectas, ab vnico Puncto, Indi-\nuiduoque in Contrarias excurrentes\npartes, QVATVOR ELEMENTO-\nRVM, (in quæ Elementata, ſingula,\ntandem reſolui poſſunt) innuere\nMyſterium. Hoc etiam notabilis dili-\ngẽter; Geometras docere, LINEAM\nEX PVNCTI FLVXV, produci.\nNos hic ſimili ratione, fieri mone-\nmus: Dum Elementares noſtræ Li-\nneæ, ex STILLAE, (tamquam Pun","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0003","text":"cti,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIER OGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0005","text":"43","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Æti, Phyſici) continuo Caſu, (quaſi\nFLVXV) in Mechanica noſtra pro-\nducantur Magia.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"3678eab90644d704997cde805f65352e924dc5256a6825d3e78dbe6fad4d7d2a","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231636404868Z_bc7933e6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. V I I.","source_sha256":"3678eab90644d704997cde805f65352e924dc5256a6825d3e78dbe6fad4d7d2a","sha256":"4721a93986fcd8a4c01a0864ba9564f0ec1102303f9e857eaa1d096e71a8ea4c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:36.404900+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M  V I I.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0002","text":"When the Elements, removed outside their natural Seats, experience the homogeneous Parts of those same [Elements], having been displaced, naturally make their returns to them by straight lines, they will teach: therefore it will not be absurd, by means of 4 straight [lines], running out from one single and indivisible Point toward contrary parts, to intimate the Mystery of the FOUR ELEMENTS (into which all compound things can at length be resolved). This too Geometers teach very notably and diligently: that A LINE IS PRODUCED FROM THE FLOWING OF A POINT.\n\nHere we admonish that it is done in a similar manner: while our elemental Lines, from a DROP (as though of a Poin","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0003","text":"t,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0004","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0005","text":"43","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0006","text":"t, in the opinion of Physicists), by continuous Fall (as if by FLOWING), are produced in our Mechanical Magic.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_6:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"6b09177dc24ea15bfc8fd9aaac13676cef019bd1480f2e9b44b58cd8474e4106","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. V I I."}],"original_title":"T H E O R. V I I.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV","title":"THEOR. VIII.","order":9,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_THEV","text":"THEOR. VIII.\n\nQVATERNARII, præterea Ex-\npanſio Cabaliſtica, ſecundum\nvſitatæ Numerationis Phraſin, (dum\ndicimus, Vnum, duo, tria, quatuor)\nDENARIVM, ſummatim exhibet.\nVt & ipſe Pythagoras dicere ſolebat:\nNam 1. 2. 3. & 4. decem conficiunt.\nNon temere ergo, CRVX Rectili-\nnea, (id eſt, Vigeſima & Prima Ro-\nman i Alphabeti litera) ex 4. fieri re-\nctis indicata, ad DENARIVM ſigni-\nficandum, ab Antiquiſſimis Latinis\nPhiloſophis eſt aſſumpta. Locus et-\ntiam illi eſt ibidem definitus, Vbi\nTERNARIVS, vim ſuam per SEPTE-\nNARIVM ducens, illum ſtatuit.\n\n44\n\nM O N A S","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. VIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0002","text":"QVATERNARII, præterea Ex-\npanſio Cabaliſtica, ſecundum\nvſitatæ Numerationis Phraſin, (dum\ndicimus, Vnum, duo, tria, quatuor)\nDENARIVM, ſummatim exhibet.\nVt & ipſe Pythagoras dicere ſolebat:\nNam 1. 2. 3. & 4. decem conficiunt.\nNon temere ergo, CRVX Rectili-\nnea, (id eſt, Vigeſima & Prima Ro-\nman i Alphabeti litera) ex 4. fieri re-\nctis indicata, ad DENARIVM ſigni-\nficandum, ab Antiquiſſimis Latinis\nPhiloſophis eſt aſſumpta. Locus et-\ntiam illi eſt ibidem definitus, Vbi\nTERNARIVS, vim ſuam per SEPTE-\nNARIVM ducens, illum ſtatuit.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0003","text":"44","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0004","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"ed9921924c1318bf736b32b630f7af0335cc8af5072ef87fe4a77c924c1bfcf7","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231643511851Z_f82ce848","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. VIII.","source_sha256":"ed9921924c1318bf736b32b630f7af0335cc8af5072ef87fe4a77c924c1bfcf7","sha256":"4d37581dcade09a9ddce1e7215c2f10108d64a4dd9c792b1ad6c1dc3591cf828","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:43.511941+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM VIII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0002","text":"The QUATERNARY, moreover, the Cabalistic Ex-\npansion, according to the phrase of\ncustomary Enumeration, (when\nwe say, One, two, three, four)\nexhibits the DENARY, in sum.\nAnd Pythagoras himself used to say:\nFor 1. 2. 3. & 4. make ten.\nNot without reason, therefore, was the Recti-\nlinear CROSS, (that is, the Twenty-first let-\nter of the Roman Alphabet) indicated as be-\ning made from 4. straight [lines], adopted by\nthe Most Ancient Latin Philosophers\nfor signifying the DENARY. A place also\nis there defined for it, Where\nthe TERNARY, conducting its force through the SEPTE-\nNARY, establishes it.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0003","text":"44","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0004","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEV:DISPLAY-0004"]}],"source_digest":"1bcdfedc910fa844012b4b1f8b7dfe6eb595a487157f978ac8992d35de2556cd","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. VIII."}],"original_title":"THEOR. VIII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_7","title":"T H E O R. I X.","order":10,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_7","text":"T H E O R.   I X.\n\nHOC autem noſtra MONADIS,\n   S O L I,   L V N Æ Q V E, optime\nconuenire videbitur: cum eorundé\nper 4. Elementorum Magiam, Exa-\nctiſſima in ſuas Lineas fuerit facta\nS E P A R A T I O: Deindeque, per ea-\nrundem Linearum Periphoras (Ad\nomnis enim datæ lineæ Magnitudi-\nnem, licet Circulum deſcribere: per\nGeometriæ leges) Circularis, in Co-\nplemento S O L A R I, fuerit facta\nC O N I V N C T I O. Tunc enim late-\nre non poteſt, quantum noſtræ MO-\nN A D I S, S O L I, L V N Æ Q V E, Cru-\ncis D E N A R I A inſeruiat Proportio.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_7:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.   I X.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_7:DISPLAY-0002","text":"HOC autem noſtra MONADIS,\n   S O L I,   L V N Æ Q V E, optime\nconuenire videbitur: cum eorundé\nper 4. Elementorum Magiam, Exa-\nctiſſima in ſuas Lineas fuerit facta\nS E P A R A T I O: Deindeque, per ea-\nrundem Linearum Periphoras (Ad\nomnis enim datæ lineæ Magnitudi-\nnem, licet Circulum deſcribere: per\nGeometriæ leges) Circularis, in Co-\nplemento S O L A R I, fuerit facta\nC O N I V N C T I O. Tunc enim late-\nre non poteſt, quantum noſtræ MO-\nN A D I S, S O L I, L V N Æ Q V E, Cru-\ncis D E N A R I A inſeruiat Proportio.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"e8d10c189ebefd1e8b28c4b39cb60b1592ca72bd2cd257f321610c9afc437d27","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231649879704Z_742313e3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. I X.","source_sha256":"e8d10c189ebefd1e8b28c4b39cb60b1592ca72bd2cd257f321610c9afc437d27","sha256":"df7664e0dcf076cf6da2a653f3579bf2cb134d2696d30799b05d8226d61ea271","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:16:49.879816+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_7:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.   I X.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_7:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_7:DISPLAY-0002","text":"But this would seem to agree exceedingly well with our MONAD,\n   S U N,   and M O O N: since, through the Magic of the 4 Elements, a most exact\nS E P A R A T I O N into their lines has been made; and thereafter, through the peripheries of those same lines (for, according to the laws of Geometry, it is permissible to describe a circle to the magnitude of every given line), a circular\nC O N J U N C T I O N has been made in the S O L A R complement. For then it cannot lie hidden how greatly the denary proportion of the Cross serves our MO-\nN A D, S U N, and M O O N.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_7:DISPLAY-0002"]}],"source_digest":"185073a4e30001bcbcfeb311a2e6d1c5ae7220c8c8b6e4758017a7ff55ac11b7","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. I X."}],"original_title":"T H E O R. I X.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8","title":"T H E O R. X.","order":11,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_8","text":"T H E O R.   X.\n\nDOdecætemorii Arietis, omnibus\n   eſt notiſſima, quæ eſt in Aſtro-\nnomorum vſu (quaſi Acioëdes, A-\ncuminataq; figura\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 48, region 7]\n\niſta: Vt &\n\nab\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n45\n\nab hoc cæli loco, Triplicitatis Igneæ,\nnotari Exordium coſtat. At ignis er-\ngo miniſterium (in huius Praxi MO-\nNADIS) requiri ſignificandum, Arie-\ntis adiecimus Aſtronomicam notâ.\nSicque breuiter, noſtræ MONADIS,\nvnam abſolui-\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 49, region 4]\n\nnus Conſidera-\ntionem Hiero-\nglyphicam: quâ\nſic volumus, V-\nnico Contextu Hieroglyphico pro-\nferri.\n\nMONADIS ISTIVS, LVNA ET SOL,\nSVA SEPARARI VOLVNT ELEMENTA, IN\nQVIBVS DENARIA VIGEBIT PROPORTIO;\nIDQVE IGNIS FIERI MINISTERIO.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.   X.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0002","text":"DOdecætemorii Arietis, omnibus\n   eſt notiſſima, quæ eſt in Aſtro-\nnomorum vſu (quaſi Acioëdes, A-\ncuminataq; figura","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 48, region 7]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0004","text":"iſta: Vt &","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0005","text":"ab","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0006","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0007","text":"45","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0008","text":"ab hoc cæli loco, Triplicitatis Igneæ,\nnotari Exordium coſtat. At ignis er-\ngo miniſterium (in huius Praxi MO-\nNADIS) requiri ſignificandum, Arie-\ntis adiecimus Aſtronomicam notâ.\nSicque breuiter, noſtræ MONADIS,\nvnam abſolui-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 49, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0010","text":"nus Conſidera-\ntionem Hiero-\nglyphicam: quâ\nſic volumus, V-\nnico Contextu Hieroglyphico pro-\nferri.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0011","text":"MONADIS ISTIVS, LVNA ET SOL,\nSVA SEPARARI VOLVNT ELEMENTA, IN\nQVIBVS DENARIA VIGEBIT PROPORTIO;\nIDQVE IGNIS FIERI MINISTERIO.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"6e8bc99d17f65c09672e654f7b2449ede107e9c7fbee628ba41d3c3e6d1de193","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231700442311Z_f484d4a1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. X.","source_sha256":"6e8bc99d17f65c09672e654f7b2449ede107e9c7fbee628ba41d3c3e6d1de193","sha256":"2829270cee8f2643dcbf135b67917c76042af13967c7e93590315f8ae4ba726e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:17:00.442367+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M   X.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0002","text":"THE dodecatemorion of Aries, most familiar to all, which is in the use of Astronomers (as though a pointed and sharpened figure","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 48, region 7]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0004","text":"this: As also","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0005","text":"from","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0006","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0007","text":"45","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0008","text":"from this place of heaven, it is established that the Beginning of the Fiery Triplicity is marked. Therefore, in order to signify that the ministry of fire is required (in the Practice of this MONAD), we have added the Astronomical sign of Aries. And thus briefly, we have brought one of our MONAD'S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 49, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Hieroglyphic Considerations to completion: which we wish thus to be set forth in a Single Hieroglyphic Context.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0011","text":"THE ELEMENTS OF THIS MONAD, THE MOON AND THE SUN, WISH TO BE SEPARATED, IN WHICH THE DENARY PROPORTION SHALL PREVAIL; AND THIS BY THE MINISTRY OF FIRE.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_8:DISPLAY-0011"]}],"source_digest":"67b3ceebafba5177ef6859a98053899165c9fa3126055109e2fb72a9b31b04e8","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. X."}],"original_title":"T H E O R. X.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX","title":"THEOR. XI.","order":12,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_THEX","text":"THEOR. XI.\n\nARietis Nota Myſtica, ex duobus\nSemicirculis, in communi Puncto\nconnexis, conſtituta Æquinoctialis\nNycthemeræ loco aptiſſime aſſigna-\n\n164\n\nM O N A S\n\ntur. Viginti enim & quatuor Hora-\nrum Tempus, Æquinoctii modo di-\ntributum, Secretiffimas noſtras de-\nnotat Proportiones. Noſtras dico,\nreſpectu Terræ.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XI.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0002","text":"ARietis Nota Myſtica, ex duobus\nSemicirculis, in communi Puncto\nconnexis, conſtituta Æquinoctialis\nNycthemeræ loco aptiſſime aſſigna-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0003","text":"164","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0004","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0005","text":"tur. Viginti enim & quatuor Hora-\nrum Tempus, Æquinoctii modo di-\ntributum, Secretiffimas noſtras de-\nnotat Proportiones. Noſtras dico,\nreſpectu Terræ.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"f29590ae95361ddf7c3ba122b06f3943df27ca45e9baf358958384f08743e32a","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231711080285Z_2a565370","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XI.","source_sha256":"f29590ae95361ddf7c3ba122b06f3943df27ca45e9baf358958384f08743e32a","sha256":"c59851a19fb45ba11570b06f51d02baeffbde9749b33e55186440c3f46bfd822","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:17:11.080416+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XI.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0002","text":"The Mystical Sign of Aries, constituted from two\nSemicircles, joined at a common Point,\nis most fittingly assign-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0003","text":"164","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0004","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0005","text":"ed to the place of an Equinoctial\nNychthemeron. For the space of twenty-\nfour Hours, divided in the manner of the\nEquinox, denotes our most secret\nProportions. I say ours,\nwith respect to the Earth.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THEX:DISPLAY-0005"]}],"source_digest":"5eadd4076ba47912910017589a569073cd6782902e9434d27661c90b89dea280","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XI."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XI.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9","title":"T H E O R. XII.","order":13,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_TH_9","text":"T H E O R.  XII.\n\nANtiquiſſimi Sapientes Magi, quin que Planetarum, nobis tradidere Notas Hieroglyphicas: Compoſitas quidem omnes, ex L V N Æ V E L S O L I S Characteribus: cum Elementorum aut Arietis Hieroglyphico Signo. Veluti iſtas, quas hîc videris figura-\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 50, region 6]\n\ntas. Quas ſingulas modo Hierogly-\nphico, ex noſtris prius iactis Funda-\nmentis, nō erit explicare difficile. At\nprimù, de iis quæ Lunæ habent Cha-\n\nracterem,\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n47\n\ntracterem,nos nunc Paraphrastice a-\ngemus:de Solaribus deinde. L V N A R I S noſtra Natura, dum per Elementorum ſcientiam, circa noſtram ſemel reuoluta Terram, S A T V R N V S myſti-\nce dicebatur. Et eadem de cauſa, I O V I S quoque; habebat nomen: iſtamq; reti-\nnebat figurâ ſecretiorè. Et Luna, ter-\ntia elementatâ vice, obſcurius ſic no-\ntabant.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 51, region 4]\n\nQuem, M E R C V R I V M\nvocare ſolent. Qui, quam ſit\nL V N A R I S, videris. Iſtum, Q V A R T A\nReuolutione produci, licet Quidam\nvelint Sophi: noſtro Secreto propo-\nſito tamen, non erit id contrarium;\nModo Spiritus Puriſſimus Magicus,\nloco Lunę, τῆς λευκώσεως administrabit\nOpus:& ſua virtute Spirituali,nobiſ-\ncum S O L V S, per Mediam quaſi Na-\nturalem diem ſine verbis, Hierogly-\nphice loquatur: in Puriſſimam Sim-\npliciſſimamq;, a nobis præparatam\n\n48\n\nMONAS\n\nTerram, Geogamicas, iſtas 4. intro-\nducens, IMPRIMENSQVE figuras; vel\nillarum\nlocō, il-\nlam al-\nteram.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 52, region 4]","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.  XII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0002","text":"ANtiquiſſimi Sapientes Magi, quin que Planetarum, nobis tradidere Notas Hieroglyphicas: Compoſitas quidem omnes, ex L V N Æ V E L S O L I S Characteribus: cum Elementorum aut Arietis Hieroglyphico Signo. Veluti iſtas, quas hîc videris figura-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 50, region 6]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0004","text":"tas. Quas ſingulas modo Hierogly-\nphico, ex noſtris prius iactis Funda-\nmentis, nō erit explicare difficile. At\nprimù, de iis quæ Lunæ habent Cha-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0005","text":"racterem,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0006","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0007","text":"47","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0008","text":"tracterem,nos nunc Paraphrastice a-\ngemus:de Solaribus deinde. L V N A R I S noſtra Natura, dum per Elementorum ſcientiam, circa noſtram ſemel reuoluta Terram, S A T V R N V S myſti-\nce dicebatur. Et eadem de cauſa, I O V I S quoque; habebat nomen: iſtamq; reti-\nnebat figurâ ſecretiorè. Et Luna, ter-\ntia elementatâ vice, obſcurius ſic no-\ntabant.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 51, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Quem, M E R C V R I V M\nvocare ſolent. Qui, quam ſit\nL V N A R I S, videris. Iſtum, Q V A R T A\nReuolutione produci, licet Quidam\nvelint Sophi: noſtro Secreto propo-\nſito tamen, non erit id contrarium;\nModo Spiritus Puriſſimus Magicus,\nloco Lunę, τῆς λευκώσεως administrabit\nOpus:& ſua virtute Spirituali,nobiſ-\ncum S O L V S, per Mediam quaſi Na-\nturalem diem ſine verbis, Hierogly-\nphice loquatur: in Puriſſimam Sim-\npliciſſimamq;, a nobis præparatam","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0011","text":"48","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0012","text":"MONAS","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0013","text":"Terram, Geogamicas, iſtas 4. intro-\nducens, IMPRIMENSQVE figuras; vel\nillarum\nlocō, il-\nlam al-\nteram.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0014","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 52, region 4]","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"94ac88acd82f528a9c9305d2fe8d671b1d83d9dbe96f183b50114222d383d1e7","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231727580074Z_b4be8fa5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. XII.","source_sha256":"94ac88acd82f528a9c9305d2fe8d671b1d83d9dbe96f183b50114222d383d1e7","sha256":"202fc006745d4290900c3457be01ec633b30c34b2c8f5b1446fb76e708c722e8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:17:27.580150+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.  XII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0002","text":"The most ancient wise Magi handed down to us the Hieroglyphic Marks of the five Planets: all indeed composed of the Characters of the M O O N or of the S U N, together with the hieroglyphic Sign of the Elements or of Aries. Such as those which here you will see figure-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 50, region 6]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0004","text":"d. It will not be difficult to explain each of these by the hieroglyphic method, from the Foundations previously laid by us. But first, concerning those which have the Cha-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0005","text":"racter,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0006","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0007","text":"47","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0008","text":"racter, we shall now deal in a paraphrastic manner: then with the solar ones. Our L U N A R Nature, while, through the knowledge of the Elements, it had once revolved about our Earth, was mystically called S A T U R N. And for the same reason it also had the name of J O V E; and retained it more secretly in its figure. And the Moon, at the third elemental turn, they thus marked more obscurely.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 51, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Whom they are accustomed to call M E R C U R Y. You will see how L U N A R he is. Although certain Sages may wish him to be produced by the F O U R T H Revolution, yet this will not be contrary to our proposed Secret; provided only that the Purest Magical Spirit, in place of the Moon, administer the Work of whitening, and, by its Spiritual power, alone with us, through, as it were, half a Natural day, speak hieroglyphically without words: into the Purest and Simplest, prepared by us","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0011","text":"48","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0012","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0013","text":"Earth, introducing and I M P R I N T I N G these 4 Geogamic figures; or, in their place, that other one.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0014","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 52, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_TH_9:DISPLAY-0014"]}],"source_digest":"a619806d9c40bac957389ce4a6f125a129230869734a7897f661395088981e29","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. XII."}],"original_title":"T H E O R. XII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10","title":"THEOR. XIII.","order":14,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_10","text":"THEOR. XIII.\n\nMARTIS ergo Character Myſti-\ncus, an non ex SOLIS & ARIE-\nTIS, Hieroglyphicis, eſt conflatus?\nelementali ( partim ) interueniente\nMagiſterio? Et VENERIS, quæſo, an\nnon ex SOLIS, & Elementorum\nPleniore Explicatione? Iſti ergo Pla-\nnetæ, SOLAREM reſpiciunt περιφο-\nράν, Opusque Ἀναζωπυρήσεως? In cuius\nprogreſſu fit tandẽ Conſpicuus\nMercurius ille alter: Prioris qui-\ndem Vterinus Frater. Lunari\nſcilicet Solariq; Elementorum Cõ-\npleta Magia, vt expreſſiſſime nobis i\npſe Hieroglyphicus loquitur Nun-\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 52, region 7]\n\ncius,\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n49\n\ncius, modo in illum oculos deſigere,\nauremque illi præbere attentiore ve-\nlinnus. Et, (NVT V DEI,)iſte eſt Phi-\nloſophorum MERCVRIVS, ille Ce-\nleberrimus MICROCOSMVS & A-\nDAM. At Solebát tunc Expertiffimi\nNonnulli, huius loco graduque SO-\nLEM ipſum ponere. Quod nos hac\nnoſtra ætate non poſſumus præſtare;\nniſi ANIMAM aliquam a CORPORE,\narte Pyronomica Separatam, huic\nOperi Χρυσοκολλίνῳ præficeremus.\nQuod & factu eſt difficile: & propter\nIgneos, Sulphureosque quos ſecum\naffert halitus, periculofiffimum. Sed\nilla, certe, ANIMA, mira præſtare\npoterit. Nimirum, tum ad LVNÆ,\nDiſcum, (Vel MERCVRII, ſaltem)\nLVCIFERVM; Immo & PYRO-\nENTA, Indiſſolubilibus Ligare vin-\nculis. Tum Tertio (vt volunt) loco,\n(ad SEPTENARIVM noſtrum Com-\n\nD\n\n50\n\nMONAS\n\nTOTIVS\nASTRO-\nNOMIÆ\nINFE-\nRIORIS,\nANATO-\nMIA MO\nNADICA,\nPRINCI-\nPALIS.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 54, region 4]\n\nplendum Nu-\nmerum) SO-\nLEM nobis\niſtum exhibe-\nre PHILOSO-\nPHORVM.\nIſtorum duo-\nrum Theore-\n\nmatum ARCANIS, ſignificandis:\nVidere quàm exacte, quàm apertè,\nnoſtræ MONADIS HIEROGLY-\nPHICÆ, reſpondeat ANATOMIA\niſta.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0002","text":"MARTIS ergo Character Myſti-\ncus, an non ex SOLIS & ARIE-\nTIS, Hieroglyphicis, eſt conflatus?\nelementali ( partim ) interueniente\nMagiſterio? Et VENERIS, quæſo, an\nnon ex SOLIS, & Elementorum\nPleniore Explicatione? Iſti ergo Pla-\nnetæ, SOLAREM reſpiciunt περιφο-\nράν, Opusque Ἀναζωπυρήσεως? In cuius\nprogreſſu fit tandẽ Conſpicuus\nMercurius ille alter: Prioris qui-\ndem Vterinus Frater. Lunari\nſcilicet Solariq; Elementorum Cõ-\npleta Magia, vt expreſſiſſime nobis i\npſe Hieroglyphicus loquitur Nun-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 52, region 7]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0004","text":"cius,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0005","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0006","text":"49","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0007","text":"cius, modo in illum oculos deſigere,\nauremque illi præbere attentiore ve-\nlinnus. Et, (NVT V DEI,)iſte eſt Phi-\nloſophorum MERCVRIVS, ille Ce-\nleberrimus MICROCOSMVS & A-\nDAM. At Solebát tunc Expertiffimi\nNonnulli, huius loco graduque SO-\nLEM ipſum ponere. Quod nos hac\nnoſtra ætate non poſſumus præſtare;\nniſi ANIMAM aliquam a CORPORE,\narte Pyronomica Separatam, huic\nOperi Χρυσοκολλίνῳ præficeremus.\nQuod & factu eſt difficile: & propter\nIgneos, Sulphureosque quos ſecum\naffert halitus, periculofiffimum. Sed\nilla, certe, ANIMA, mira præſtare\npoterit. Nimirum, tum ad LVNÆ,\nDiſcum, (Vel MERCVRII, ſaltem)\nLVCIFERVM; Immo & PYRO-\nENTA, Indiſſolubilibus Ligare vin-\nculis. Tum Tertio (vt volunt) loco,\n(ad SEPTENARIVM noſtrum Com-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0008","text":"D","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0009","text":"50","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0010","text":"MONAS","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0011","text":"TOTIVS\nASTRO-\nNOMIÆ\nINFE-\nRIORIS,\nANATO-\nMIA MO\nNADICA,\nPRINCI-\nPALIS.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0012","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 54, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0013","text":"plendum Nu-\nmerum) SO-\nLEM nobis\niſtum exhibe-\nre PHILOSO-\nPHORVM.\nIſtorum duo-\nrum Theore-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0014","text":"matum ARCANIS, ſignificandis:\nVidere quàm exacte, quàm apertè,\nnoſtræ MONADIS HIEROGLY-\nPHICÆ, reſpondeat ANATOMIA\niſta.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"3cc684cbd3a57b7fe02afe85f8fbac0b9672773f50863ac0a90e9390766a84b7","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231743102790Z_6b5c0866","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XIII.","source_sha256":"3cc684cbd3a57b7fe02afe85f8fbac0b9672773f50863ac0a90e9390766a84b7","sha256":"a1ea9c2268ee50e35b1a1eac4c2c72b44c721f116a8e86813cf6e78e1c783028","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:17:43.102882+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XIII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Is not, therefore, the Mystical Character of MARS compounded from the hieroglyphics of the SUN and ARIES, with elemental Mastery partly intervening? And that of VENUS, pray, is it not [compounded] from the SUN and a fuller Explication of the Elements? Therefore these Planets regard the SOLAR περιφορά, and the Work of Ἀναζωπύρησις? In the progress of which that other Mercury at length becomes visible: the uterine Brother, indeed, of the former. Namely, by the complete Magic of the lunar and solar Elements, as the Hieroglyphic Mes-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 52, region 7]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0004","text":"senger,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0005","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0006","text":"49","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0007","text":"senger, himself speaks to us most expressly, provided only that we fix our eyes upon him and lend him a more attentive ear. And, (BY THE WILL OF GOD,) this is the MERCURY of the Philosophers, that most celebrated MICROCOSM and ADAM. But at that time certain most experienced men used to place the SUN itself in this place and rank. Which in this our age we cannot accomplish, unless we should set over this Chrysocollinic Work some SOUL separated from a BODY by the Pyronomic art. This is both difficult to do and, on account of the fiery and sulphurous exhalations which it brings with it, most dangerous. But that SOUL, certainly, will be able to accomplish marvellous things. Namely, both to bind, with indissoluble bonds, the LIGHT-BRINGER to the Disk of the MOON (or at least of MERCURY); nay, also the FIERY [ones]. Then in the third place (as they wish), (for our sevenfold num-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231743102790Z_6b5c0866:DISPLAY-0008","text":"D\n\n50","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0008","RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0010","text":"MONAD","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0011","text":"OF THE ENTIRE\nINFERIOR\nASTRO-\nNOMY,\nTHE PRINCIPAL\nMONADIC\nANATOMY.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0012","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 54, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0013","text":"ber to be filled) to exhibit to us that SUN OF THE PHILOSOPHERS.\nOf the mysteries of these two theo-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0014","text":"rems, for signifying [them]: see how exactly, how openly, that Anatomy corresponds to our HIEROGLYPHIC MONAD.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_10:DISPLAY-0014"]}],"source_digest":"dcc9825e2743dab4f02865563a2149f1d1e569704f896d1b210ab5913c976e23","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XIII."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XIII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11","title":"THEOREM XIII.","order":15,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_11","text":"THEOREMA XIII.\n\nEX SOLE & LVNA, totum hoc\npendêre Magiſterium jam clarè\nconfirmatum eſt. Huius, etiam, Ter-\nmaximus ille Hermes, nos olim ad-\nmonuit: Eius Patrem SOLEM, eſſe,\naſſerens: LVNAM autem, Matrem:\nNutriti vero Scimus in TERRA LE-\nMNIA. Radiis nimirum LVNARI-\n\nBVS\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n51\n\nBVS & SOLARIBVS, Singularem\ncirca Eandem, exercentibus INFLV-\nENTIAM.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREMA XIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0002","text":"EX SOLE & LVNA, totum hoc\npendêre Magiſterium jam clarè\nconfirmatum eſt. Huius, etiam, Ter-\nmaximus ille Hermes, nos olim ad-\nmonuit: Eius Patrem SOLEM, eſſe,\naſſerens: LVNAM autem, Matrem:\nNutriti vero Scimus in TERRA LE-\nMNIA. Radiis nimirum LVNARI-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0003","text":"BVS","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0005","text":"51","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0006","text":"BVS & SOLARIBVS, Singularem\ncirca Eandem, exercentibus INFLV-\nENTIAM.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"a2cf0f2231b572ac02d1773cc4c01f168d1d3025620ac3a95d3e255aeddb49d3","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231752907645Z_968504ca","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM XIII.","source_sha256":"a2cf0f2231b572ac02d1773cc4c01f168d1d3025620ac3a95d3e255aeddb49d3","sha256":"5950e8ebb594c188ecd2e79e59d8bf6c5c69b499f57a1aa5095ba10b38c0b5e5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:17:52.907760+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XIII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0002","text":"FROM THE SUN & MOON, it has now been clearly established that this whole\nMagistery depends. Of this, moreover, that\nthrice-great Hermes formerly ad-\nmonished us: asserting that its Father is the SUN:\nbut the MOON, its Mother:\nwhile we know it to be nourished in LEMNIAN\nEARTH. Namely, by LUNAR-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0003","text":"RAYS","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIEROGLYPHIC.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0005","text":"51","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0006","text":"RAYS & SOLAR RAYS, exercising\na singular INFLU-\nENCE upon the Same.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_11:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"35ef94252f36b04ce384ec356f700e8a98cff004fb36cb8157634be1d871edb5","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOREMA XIII."}],"original_title":"THEOREMA XIII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12","title":"THEOR. XV.","order":16,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_12","text":"THEOR. XV.\n\nSOLIS proinde LVNÆQVE cir-\nca Terram Labores , Philoſophis\nproponimus Conſiderandos. Huius\nquidem , quo modo, dum in Ariete\nverſatur SOLARE Iubar: Ipſa tunc in\nProximo(ſcilicet Tauri)Signo, Lucis\nnouam recipiat Dignitatem : EX-\nALTETVRQVE Supra innatas ſibi\nvires. Quam(præ aliis notabilem ma-\ngis) LVMINARIVM, Vicinitatem,\nCharactere quodam myſtico expli-\ncabant veteres: TAVRI, inſignito\nNomine. Quam, quidem, LVNÆ eſſe\nEXALTATIONEM, vſque ab ipſa\nprima Hominum ætate(inter Aſtro-\nnomorum Placita, ) memoriæ eſſe\nproditum, notiſſimum eſt. At intel-\n\nD 2\n\n52\n\nM O N A S\n\nligunt Mysterium Illi ſoli, qui abſo-\nluti evaſere Mysteriorum Antiſtites. Ut & ſimili ratione, VENERIS eſſe DOMVM, dixere TAVRVM: Caſti ni-\nmirum Prolificique CONIVGALIS AMORIS: Sic enim φύσις, τῇ φύσει τέτα-\nκται: Ut Magnus ille OSTANES in Secre-\ntiſſimis ſuis Recondidit Mysterijs.\n\n2.\n\nSOLIS vero, qua ratione, Ipſe\npoſt Aliquas ſui Luminis, admiſſas\nEclipſes; MARTIVM Robur acci-\npit: & in eiusdem quoque DOMO\n(Noſtro ſcilicet Ariete) veluti in ſua\nTriumphare dicitur EXALTATIO.\nNE. Quæ ſecretiſſima Mysterîa, no-\nſtra etiam MONAS clarissime, per-\nfectiſſimeque demonſtrat: TAVRI\nquidem iſta quæ\nhic eſt depicta\nHieroglyphi-\nca figura: &\nilla MARTIS:\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 56, region 6]\n\nquam\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n53\n\nquam 12. & 13. Theoremate adduxi-\nmus: quæ S O L E M Rectam A R I E-\nT E M tendentem, indicat. Ex præ-\nſenti autem Theoria, Alia noſtra MO-\nN A D I S ſeſe offert Anatomia Caba-\nliſtica: cuius iſta eſt vera Artificioſa;\nexplicatio.   L V N Æ,   S O L I S Q V E\nE X A L T A T I O N E S,   M E D I A N T E\nE L E M E N T O R V M  S C I E N T I A.\n\nA N N O T A T I O.\n\nDuo hic maximopere notanda eſſe\nCenſeo: vnum, quod Tauri Hierogly-\nphica iſta figura, nobis Græcorum Di-\nphthongum ε, exacte repræſentet, Primæ\nDeclinationis, Genitivam ſemper ſin-\ngularem Terminationem. Secundo, ex-\napta Metatheſi Locali, dupliciter nobis\nA L P H A commonſtrat : Circulo &\nSemicirculo Tangentibus ſolum, vel ſe\nmutuo (vt hic) ſecantibus.\n\nD 3\n\n54\n\nM O N A S","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XV.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0002","text":"SOLIS proinde LVNÆQVE cir-\nca Terram Labores , Philoſophis\nproponimus Conſiderandos. Huius\nquidem , quo modo, dum in Ariete\nverſatur SOLARE Iubar: Ipſa tunc in\nProximo(ſcilicet Tauri)Signo, Lucis\nnouam recipiat Dignitatem : EX-\nALTETVRQVE Supra innatas ſibi\nvires. Quam(præ aliis notabilem ma-\ngis) LVMINARIVM, Vicinitatem,\nCharactere quodam myſtico expli-\ncabant veteres: TAVRI, inſignito\nNomine. Quam, quidem, LVNÆ eſſe\nEXALTATIONEM, vſque ab ipſa\nprima Hominum ætate(inter Aſtro-\nnomorum Placita, ) memoriæ eſſe\nproditum, notiſſimum eſt. At intel-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0003","text":"D 2","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0004","text":"52","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0005","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0006","text":"ligunt Mysterium Illi ſoli, qui abſo-\nluti evaſere Mysteriorum Antiſtites. Ut & ſimili ratione, VENERIS eſſe DOMVM, dixere TAVRVM: Caſti ni-\nmirum Prolificique CONIVGALIS AMORIS: Sic enim φύσις, τῇ φύσει τέτα-\nκται: Ut Magnus ille OSTANES in Secre-\ntiſſimis ſuis Recondidit Mysterijs.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0007","text":"2.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0008","text":"SOLIS vero, qua ratione, Ipſe\npoſt Aliquas ſui Luminis, admiſſas\nEclipſes; MARTIVM Robur acci-\npit: & in eiusdem quoque DOMO\n(Noſtro ſcilicet Ariete) veluti in ſua\nTriumphare dicitur EXALTATIO.\nNE. Quæ ſecretiſſima Mysterîa, no-\nſtra etiam MONAS clarissime, per-\nfectiſſimeque demonſtrat: TAVRI\nquidem iſta quæ\nhic eſt depicta\nHieroglyphi-\nca figura: &\nilla MARTIS:","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 56, region 6]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0010","text":"quam","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0011","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0012","text":"53","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0013","text":"quam 12. & 13. Theoremate adduxi-\nmus: quæ S O L E M Rectam A R I E-\nT E M tendentem, indicat. Ex præ-\nſenti autem Theoria, Alia noſtra MO-\nN A D I S ſeſe offert Anatomia Caba-\nliſtica: cuius iſta eſt vera Artificioſa;\nexplicatio.   L V N Æ,   S O L I S Q V E\nE X A L T A T I O N E S,   M E D I A N T E\nE L E M E N T O R V M  S C I E N T I A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0014","text":"A N N O T A T I O.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0015","text":"Duo hic maximopere notanda eſſe\nCenſeo: vnum, quod Tauri Hierogly-\nphica iſta figura, nobis Græcorum Di-\nphthongum ε, exacte repræſentet, Primæ\nDeclinationis, Genitivam ſemper ſin-\ngularem Terminationem. Secundo, ex-\napta Metatheſi Locali, dupliciter nobis\nA L P H A commonſtrat : Circulo &\nSemicirculo Tangentibus ſolum, vel ſe\nmutuo (vt hic) ſecantibus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0016","text":"D 3","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0017","text":"54","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0018","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"83f4749e65f7b205b1115ba6790f6aac52aa500888d6c1c72c1a2301d347a99e","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231808056656Z_217ee5b4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XV.","source_sha256":"83f4749e65f7b205b1115ba6790f6aac52aa500888d6c1c72c1a2301d347a99e","sha256":"59d1126f249776e2ea96da5d6eb532d2b99b5d746ec9fe8cc07ddbe1ee54b6b1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:18:08.056713+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XV.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Accordingly, we propose for the consideration of philosophers the Labours of the SUN and MOON around the Earth. Namely, in what manner, while the SOLAR radiance is situated in Aries, the Moon herself then, in the nearest Sign (that is, Taurus), receives a new Dignity of Light: AND IS EXALTED above her innate powers. This Neighbourhood of the LUMINARIES (more notable than the others), the ancients explained by a certain mystical Character, under the distinguished Name of TAURUS. That this, indeed, is the EXALTATION of the MOON, it is most well known to have been handed down in remembrance from the very first age of mankind (among the doctrines of astronomers). But they under-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0003","text":"D 2","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0004","text":"52","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0005","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0006","text":"stand the Mystery only, those who have become consummate Priests of the Mysteries. And by a similar reasoning, they declared TAURUS to be the HOUSE of VENUS: namely, of chaste and prolific CONJUGAL LOVE: for thus φύσις, τῇ φύσει τέτακται: as that great OSTANES concealed in his most secret Mysteries.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0007","text":"2.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0008","text":"But in what manner the SUN himself, after undergoing certain eclipses of his light, receives MARTIAL strength, and is said likewise to triumph in the same HOUSE (namely, in our Aries), as though in his own EXALTATIO.N. These most secret Mysteries our MONAS also demonstrates most clearly and most perfectly: those, indeed, of TAURUS by this Hieroglyphic figure which is depicted here: and those of MARS by that:","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 56, region 6]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0010","text":"which","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0011","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0012","text":"53","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0013","text":"we adduced in Theorems 12 and 13: which indicates the SUN tending directly toward ARIES. But from the present Theory another Cabalistic Anatomy of our MONAD offers itself; of which this is the true artificious explanation: THE EXALTATIONS OF THE MOON AND SUN, BY MEANS OF THE SCIENCE OF THE ELEMENTS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0014","text":"A N N O T A T I O N.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0015","text":"I judge that two things here are especially to be noted: first, that this Hieroglyphic figure of Taurus exactly represents for us the Greek diphthong ε, the termination always singular of the Genitive of the First Declension. Secondly, by an apt local transposition, it shows us ALPHA in two ways: by Circles and Semicircles either only touching, or mutually (as here) intersecting one another.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0016","text":"D 3","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0017","text":"54","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0018","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_12:DISPLAY-0018"]}],"source_digest":"67829005dbe8c319137d4d3cff553c9dba098479b0383ba947e90d9e40f19e3c","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XV."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XV.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13","title":"THEOR. XVI.","order":17,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_13","text":"THEOR. XVI.\n\nIam nobis de CRVCE, paucis, ad noſtrum propoſitum, eſt Philoſo-\nphandum. CRVX noſtra, licet ex duabus Rectis (vt diximus) & æqua-\nlibus illis quidem, confecta ſit: non ſe mutuo tamen in æquales diſſecant longitudines. Sed tum æquales, tum inæquales partes, in Myſtica noſtra Crucis diſtributione, haberi volu-\nmus. Innuentes, in Binarum ita ſe-\nctarum potestate (eo quod æqualis ſunt Magnitudinis) CRVCIS quoq; Æquilateræ, virtutem latêre. Gene-\nraliſſime enim, CRVCE, ex æquali-\nbus Rectis, fieri iuſſa; æquali profecto linearum Decuſſatione, eam fieri de-\nbere, NATVRÆ quædam requirit IVSTITIA. Secundum cuius Iu-\nſtitiæ Normâ, de Æquilatera CRVCE (qualis eſt Latini Alphabeti litera vigesima prima) hæc quæ ſequuntur,\n\nperpen-\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA\n\n55\n\nperpendenda proponemus. C R V-\nCIS, Rectilineæ Rectangulæ, & Æ-\nquilateræ, Si per commune ſectionis\npunctum, & Cōtrapolitos angulos,\nRecta vbicunque tranſire concipia-\ntur: Ex vtraque parte, ſic tranſeuntis\nRectæ, Crucis factæ partes, ſunt o-\nmnino ſimiles & æquales: Quarum\nfiguræ, eædem ſunt, cum illa Lati-\nnorum litera, quæ Vocalium eſſe\nQVINTA, recepta eſt, & ad QVINA-\nRIVM denotandum apud Antiquiſ-\nſimos Latinorum Philoſophos vſita-\ntiſſima erat: Idque haud abſurde ab\nillis eſſe factum Cenſeo; cum ſit De-\nnarii noſtri, Conformis Medietas.\nEx illius ergo figuræ, Sic\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 59, region 4]\n\nduplicatæ (ex hac Hypo\nthetica Crucis diuiſione)\nprouenientis, ea ratione,\nqua QVINARIVM vtraque repræ.\n\nD 4\n\n56\n\nM O N A S\n\nſentant ſcilicet erecta altera, Altera au-\ntem hic ſit euersa) Monemur, Radi-\ncum Quadratarum hic imitari Mul-\ntiplicationem Quadratatam: (quæ hic\nmirabiliter in NVMERVM CIRCV-\nLAREM incidit, ſcilicet QVINA-\nRIVM) Vnde produci certo conſtat,\nVIGINTI & QVINQVE: (ut & ipſa\nlitera , eſt vigesima : & vocalium\nQuinta.) Nunc vero alium ſitum\nipſius CRVCIS æquilateræ conſi-\nderabimus: iſtum nimirum: qui no-\nſtræ MONADICÆ CRV-\nCIS Situi eſt ſimilis: Simi-\nlem autem hic fieri Crucis\nDiuifionem bipartitam (ut\nſupra) ſupponimus. Vnde\nalterius literæ, Latini Alphabeti, ſe\nmonſtrat etiam geminata figura: e-\nrecta una; euersa, & auersa, altera:\nQuæ (ex Latinorum vetuſtiſſima co-\nſuetudine) ad QVINQVAGINTA\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 60, region 4]\n\nrepræ\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n57\n\nrepræſentandum,in vſu eſt. Iſtud,in-\nde mini primo ſtatutum videtur: Eo\nquod ſit & Iſta quidem QVINARII,\nNota; ex noſtro Crucis DENARIO,\neſſentialiter deſumpta: at eo ſitu LO-\ncatæ, quo, omnium Myſteriorum\nMaximi,ipſa Crux,eſt Conſumma-\ntiſſima, Hieroglyphica Nota: Vnde\nDENARII Poteſtatem,in ſua QVI-\nNARIA Virtute COMPLECTENS,\nQVINQVAGENARIO NVMERO\ntanquàm ſuo Partui, gratulatur. O,\nMIDEVS, QVANTA HÆC MY-\nSTERIA? & Nomen illi, EI. Immo\n& hac ratione quoque, ipſam Denaria\nCrucis virtutem reſpicere videtur;\nquod Medio Loco, inter primam\nAlphabeti Literam, & ipſum Crucis\nDenarium ſit conſtituta: & ab alter-\nutra,ipſa ſit, ordine,Decima. Et cum\nin CRVCE, duas ejuſmodi integra-\nles eſſe partes oſtendimus ( Numera-\n\n58\n\nM O N A S\n\nIſtem nunc ſolum earundem vim Co-\nſiderantes) CENTENARIVM inde\nexcreſcere apertiffimum eſt. At ſi, ex\nQuadratorum Lege, Mutuam pa-\ntiantur Multiplicationem, Bis Mille,\nQuingenta nobis reddent: Qui hu-\nius QVADRATVS, ad prioris Cir-\ncularis Numeri Quadratum, com-\nparatus: & eidem Applicatus, etiam\nCENTENARIVM, denuo reſti-\ntuet: vt & ipſa CRVX, ſecundum Sui\nDENARII Potentiam, ſe explicans,\nCENTVRIO eſſe agnoſcetur: Et ta-\nmen cum ſit niſi Vnicus ipſe CRV-\nCIS Character: Vnum quoq; repre-\nſentat. Hîc ergo (præter alia notatu\ndigniſſima) ab iſtis CRVCIS Theo-\nriis, Numerare, & Progredi iam ſu-\nmus edocti ad hûc modum: Vnum,\nDecem, Centum. DENARIA ſic\nnos evehente CRVCIS Proportio\nne.\n\nTHEO-\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n59","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XVI.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Iam nobis de CRVCE, paucis, ad noſtrum propoſitum, eſt Philoſo-\nphandum. CRVX noſtra, licet ex duabus Rectis (vt diximus) & æqua-\nlibus illis quidem, confecta ſit: non ſe mutuo tamen in æquales diſſecant longitudines. Sed tum æquales, tum inæquales partes, in Myſtica noſtra Crucis diſtributione, haberi volu-\nmus. Innuentes, in Binarum ita ſe-\nctarum potestate (eo quod æqualis ſunt Magnitudinis) CRVCIS quoq; Æquilateræ, virtutem latêre. Gene-\nraliſſime enim, CRVCE, ex æquali-\nbus Rectis, fieri iuſſa; æquali profecto linearum Decuſſatione, eam fieri de-\nbere, NATVRÆ quædam requirit IVSTITIA. Secundum cuius Iu-\nſtitiæ Normâ, de Æquilatera CRVCE (qualis eſt Latini Alphabeti litera vigesima prima) hæc quæ ſequuntur,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0003","text":"perpen-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0005","text":"55","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0006","text":"perpendenda proponemus. C R V-\nCIS, Rectilineæ Rectangulæ, & Æ-\nquilateræ, Si per commune ſectionis\npunctum, & Cōtrapolitos angulos,\nRecta vbicunque tranſire concipia-\ntur: Ex vtraque parte, ſic tranſeuntis\nRectæ, Crucis factæ partes, ſunt o-\nmnino ſimiles & æquales: Quarum\nfiguræ, eædem ſunt, cum illa Lati-\nnorum litera, quæ Vocalium eſſe\nQVINTA, recepta eſt, & ad QVINA-\nRIVM denotandum apud Antiquiſ-\nſimos Latinorum Philoſophos vſita-\ntiſſima erat: Idque haud abſurde ab\nillis eſſe factum Cenſeo; cum ſit De-\nnarii noſtri, Conformis Medietas.\nEx illius ergo figuræ, Sic","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0007","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 59, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0008","text":"duplicatæ (ex hac Hypo\nthetica Crucis diuiſione)\nprouenientis, ea ratione,\nqua QVINARIVM vtraque repræ.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0009","text":"D 4","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0010","text":"56","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0011","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0012","text":"ſentant ſcilicet erecta altera, Altera au-\ntem hic ſit euersa) Monemur, Radi-\ncum Quadratarum hic imitari Mul-\ntiplicationem Quadratatam: (quæ hic\nmirabiliter in NVMERVM CIRCV-\nLAREM incidit, ſcilicet QVINA-\nRIVM) Vnde produci certo conſtat,\nVIGINTI & QVINQVE: (ut & ipſa\nlitera , eſt vigesima : & vocalium\nQuinta.) Nunc vero alium ſitum\nipſius CRVCIS æquilateræ conſi-\nderabimus: iſtum nimirum: qui no-\nſtræ MONADICÆ CRV-\nCIS Situi eſt ſimilis: Simi-\nlem autem hic fieri Crucis\nDiuifionem bipartitam (ut\nſupra) ſupponimus. Vnde\nalterius literæ, Latini Alphabeti, ſe\nmonſtrat etiam geminata figura: e-\nrecta una; euersa, & auersa, altera:\nQuæ (ex Latinorum vetuſtiſſima co-\nſuetudine) ad QVINQVAGINTA","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0013","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 60, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0014","text":"repræ","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0015","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0016","text":"57","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0017","text":"repræſentandum,in vſu eſt. Iſtud,in-\nde mini primo ſtatutum videtur: Eo\nquod ſit & Iſta quidem QVINARII,\nNota; ex noſtro Crucis DENARIO,\neſſentialiter deſumpta: at eo ſitu LO-\ncatæ, quo, omnium Myſteriorum\nMaximi,ipſa Crux,eſt Conſumma-\ntiſſima, Hieroglyphica Nota: Vnde\nDENARII Poteſtatem,in ſua QVI-\nNARIA Virtute COMPLECTENS,\nQVINQVAGENARIO NVMERO\ntanquàm ſuo Partui, gratulatur. O,\nMIDEVS, QVANTA HÆC MY-\nSTERIA? & Nomen illi, EI. Immo\n& hac ratione quoque, ipſam Denaria\nCrucis virtutem reſpicere videtur;\nquod Medio Loco, inter primam\nAlphabeti Literam, & ipſum Crucis\nDenarium ſit conſtituta: & ab alter-\nutra,ipſa ſit, ordine,Decima. Et cum\nin CRVCE, duas ejuſmodi integra-\nles eſſe partes oſtendimus ( Numera-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0018","text":"58","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0019","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0020","text":"Iſtem nunc ſolum earundem vim Co-\nſiderantes) CENTENARIVM inde\nexcreſcere apertiffimum eſt. At ſi, ex\nQuadratorum Lege, Mutuam pa-\ntiantur Multiplicationem, Bis Mille,\nQuingenta nobis reddent: Qui hu-\nius QVADRATVS, ad prioris Cir-\ncularis Numeri Quadratum, com-\nparatus: & eidem Applicatus, etiam\nCENTENARIVM, denuo reſti-\ntuet: vt & ipſa CRVX, ſecundum Sui\nDENARII Potentiam, ſe explicans,\nCENTVRIO eſſe agnoſcetur: Et ta-\nmen cum ſit niſi Vnicus ipſe CRV-\nCIS Character: Vnum quoq; repre-\nſentat. Hîc ergo (præter alia notatu\ndigniſſima) ab iſtis CRVCIS Theo-\nriis, Numerare, & Progredi iam ſu-\nmus edocti ad hûc modum: Vnum,\nDecem, Centum. DENARIA ſic\nnos evehente CRVCIS Proportio\nne.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0021","text":"THEO-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0022","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0023","text":"59","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"0a4d4c46f2839bdaa3e7ba0adb0393f209469fd332565c9c57aedac373d89723","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231836103090Z_fde87403","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XVI.","source_sha256":"0a4d4c46f2839bdaa3e7ba0adb0393f209469fd332565c9c57aedac373d89723","sha256":"60793b926976cf0277c8b6eaeffa49990883d3ab54c03f36f3e0a72c96708c9c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:18:36.103311+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEORY XVI.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Now we must philosophize, briefly, concerning the CROSS, for our purpose. Our CROSS, although it is composed (as we have said) of two Straight [Lines], and indeed equal ones: nevertheless they do not mutually divide themselves into equal lengths. But we wish both equal and unequal parts to be had in our Mystical distribution of the Cross. Indicating that, in the power of two [lines] thus cut (because they are of equal Magnitude), the virtue also of the Equilateral CROSS lies hidden. For, most generally, when a CROSS is commanded to be made from equal Straight [Lines], a certain JUSTICE of NATURE requires that it should indeed be made by an equal decussation of the lines. According to the Rule of which Justice, concerning the Equilateral CROSS (such as is the twenty-first letter of the Latin Alphabet), we shall set forth the following things,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0003","text":"to be con-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0005","text":"55","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0006","text":"sidered. If, through the common point of intersection and the opposite angles, a Straight [Line] be conceived to pass anywhere through the Rectilinear, Right-angled, and Equilateral CROSS: the parts of the Cross made on either side of the Straight [Line] thus passing are altogether similar and equal. Their figures are the same as that Latin letter which is accepted as the FIFTH of the Vowels, and among the most ancient Latin Philosophers was very commonly used for denoting the QUINARY. And I judge that this was not done absurdly by them; since it is the conformable Half of our Denary. Therefore, from the figure of that [letter], thus","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0007","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 59, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0008","text":"doubled (arising from this hypothetical division of the Cross), in that manner whereby each [of them] repre-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0009","text":"D 4","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0010","text":"56","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0011","text":"MONAD","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0012","text":"sents the QUINARY—one, namely, being upright, but the other inverted here—we are admonished to imitate here the squared multiplication of square roots: (which here wonderfully falls into the CIRCULAR NUMBER, namely the QUINARY). Whence it is certainly evident that TWENTY-FIVE is produced: (as the letter itself is twentieth, and the fifth of the vowels.) But now we shall consider another position of the equilateral CROSS: namely, that which is similar to the position of our MONADIC CROSS. But we suppose that here a twofold division of the Cross is made (as above). Whence there also shows itself the doubled figure of another letter of the Latin Alphabet: one upright; the other inverted and turned away: which (from the most ancient custom of the Latins) is in use for representing FIFTY","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0013","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 60, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0014","text":"repre-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0015","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0016","text":"57","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0017","text":"sents. It seems to me that this was first established for the reason that it too is indeed a sign of the QUINARY, essentially derived from our DENARY of the Cross; but placed in that position in which, of all Mysteries the Greatest, the Cross itself is the most consummate Hieroglyphic Sign. Whence, EMBRACING the power of the DENARY in its QUINARY virtue, it congratulates the NUMBER FIFTY as though upon its offspring. O, MIDEVS, HOW GREAT ARE THESE MYSTERIES? And its name, EI. Indeed, also for this reason it seems to have regard to the Denary virtue of the Cross itself: because it is set in the middle place between the first Letter of the Alphabet and the Denary of the Cross itself; and is, in order, tenth from either. And since in the CROSS we have shown there to be two such integral parts (Num-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0018","text":"58","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0019","text":"MONAD","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0020","text":"Now considering only the force of the same [parts], it is most evident that a HUNDRED grows out of them. But if, according to the Law of Squares, they undergo mutual Multiplication, they will render us Two Thousand Five Hundred. The Square of this, compared with and applied to the Square of the former Circular Number, will also restore the HUNDRED anew: so that the CROSS itself, unfolding itself according to the Power of its DENARY, will be recognized as a CENTURION. And yet, since it is but the single Character of the CROSS, it also represents One. Here therefore (besides other things most worthy of note) we are now taught by these Theories of the CROSS to Number and to Proceed in this manner: One, Ten, One Hundred. Thus the DENARY Proportion of the CROSS raising us aloft.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0021","text":"THEO-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0022","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0023","text":"59","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_13:DISPLAY-0023"]}],"source_digest":"67655abd63e3c705f5c2048d9709b59403eb4c8b894fbab34a0d70ef658e61ca","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XVI."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XVI.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14","title":"THEOR. XVII.","order":18,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_14","text":"THEOR. XVII.\n\nVT ex Sexto Theoremate liquêre\npoteſt, in CRVCE noſtra QVA-\nTVOR rectos conſiderari, angulos:\nQuorum vnicuique, QVINARII at-\ntribuere ſignificationem, præcedens\ndoceret Theorema: Vno quidem lo\ncatis modo: At alterum obtinenti-\nbus Situm; Idem Theorema QVIN-\nQVAGENARII Numeri, fieri Hie-\nroglyphicas Notas admittit: Ita, eui\ndentiſſimum eſt, CRVCEM DE-\nNARIVM notare vulgariter: Tum\nin Latini Alphabeti ordine, literam\neſſe vigeſſimam primam: (Vnde eſt\nfactum, quod, Sophi, Mecubales, di-\ncti, viginti vnum, per eandem Signi-\nficabant Literam;) Denique, & Sim-\npliciſſime conſiderari poſſe: vt Vna\nNota, eſſe conſpicitur; qualemcunque,\n& quantamcunque aliam habet po\nteſtate. Ex quibus omnibus, optima\nDemonſtratione Cabaliſtica cõcludi\n\n60\n\nM O N A S\n\npoſſe videmus: C R V C E M noſtram,\nMyſtis, D V C E N T A, Q V I N Q V A-\nG I N T A D V O, mirabili Compendio\nSignificare poſſe. Q V A T E R enim\nQ V I N Q V E; Q V A T E R Q V I N Q V A-\nG I N T A; D E C E M: V I G I N T I V N V M;\n& V N V M: D V C E N T A Q V I N Q V A-\nG I N T A D V O efficiunt. Quem Nu-\nmerum, duabus adhuc aliis ratio-\nnibus.ex præmiſſis vt nos elicere poſ-\nſumus; ita Cabaliſticis Tyronibus, eundem commẽdamus eruendum: breuitati ſic Studentes: Eiuſdem ta-\nmen Magiſtralis Numeri, variâ პრო-\nductionem artificioſam, Philoſopho rum dignam Iudicantes Conſidera-\ntione. Nec vos, aliam, hic, Myſtago-\ngiam Celabo,Memorabilem. C R V-\nC E M noſtram in duas alias literas, ſe Diſtribui Paſſam, Videntes: Si, vt Numeralem earundẽ virtutem quo-\ndam modo perpendimus prius, ita\n\nviciſſim\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n61\n\nviciſſim nunc ILLARVM VERBA-\nLEM VIM, CVM IPSA CRVCE, CON-\nFEREMVS, quod inde Oriatur LVX:\nVERBVM, Finale & Magiſtrale(ex\nilla TERNARII, in Vnitate Verbi,\nConſpiratione & conſenſu ) cũ ſum-\nma Admiratione Intelligemus.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XVII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0002","text":"VT ex Sexto Theoremate liquêre\npoteſt, in CRVCE noſtra QVA-\nTVOR rectos conſiderari, angulos:\nQuorum vnicuique, QVINARII at-\ntribuere ſignificationem, præcedens\ndoceret Theorema: Vno quidem lo\ncatis modo: At alterum obtinenti-\nbus Situm; Idem Theorema QVIN-\nQVAGENARII Numeri, fieri Hie-\nroglyphicas Notas admittit: Ita, eui\ndentiſſimum eſt, CRVCEM DE-\nNARIVM notare vulgariter: Tum\nin Latini Alphabeti ordine, literam\neſſe vigeſſimam primam: (Vnde eſt\nfactum, quod, Sophi, Mecubales, di-\ncti, viginti vnum, per eandem Signi-\nficabant Literam;) Denique, & Sim-\npliciſſime conſiderari poſſe: vt Vna\nNota, eſſe conſpicitur; qualemcunque,\n& quantamcunque aliam habet po\nteſtate. Ex quibus omnibus, optima\nDemonſtratione Cabaliſtica cõcludi","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0003","text":"60","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0004","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0005","text":"poſſe videmus: C R V C E M noſtram,\nMyſtis, D V C E N T A, Q V I N Q V A-\nG I N T A D V O, mirabili Compendio\nSignificare poſſe. Q V A T E R enim\nQ V I N Q V E; Q V A T E R Q V I N Q V A-\nG I N T A; D E C E M: V I G I N T I V N V M;\n& V N V M: D V C E N T A Q V I N Q V A-\nG I N T A D V O efficiunt. Quem Nu-\nmerum, duabus adhuc aliis ratio-\nnibus.ex præmiſſis vt nos elicere poſ-\nſumus; ita Cabaliſticis Tyronibus, eundem commẽdamus eruendum: breuitati ſic Studentes: Eiuſdem ta-\nmen Magiſtralis Numeri, variâ პრო-\nductionem artificioſam, Philoſopho rum dignam Iudicantes Conſidera-\ntione. Nec vos, aliam, hic, Myſtago-\ngiam Celabo,Memorabilem. C R V-\nC E M noſtram in duas alias literas, ſe Diſtribui Paſſam, Videntes: Si, vt Numeralem earundẽ virtutem quo-\ndam modo perpendimus prius, ita","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0006","text":"viciſſim","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0007","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0008","text":"61","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0009","text":"viciſſim nunc ILLARVM VERBA-\nLEM VIM, CVM IPSA CRVCE, CON-\nFEREMVS, quod inde Oriatur LVX:\nVERBVM, Finale & Magiſtrale(ex\nilla TERNARII, in Vnitate Verbi,\nConſpiratione & conſenſu ) cũ ſum-\nma Admiratione Intelligemus.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"cbb1e31aac7e66867db58d111c60ac1c6319aa43c76722393e02d9243d81d61d","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231844891824Z_5edfb52a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XVII.","source_sha256":"cbb1e31aac7e66867db58d111c60ac1c6319aa43c76722393e02d9243d81d61d","sha256":"3d1c069f738b467442ca97011536648d600b99ccd3a9603dee78e4b9308bf5c0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:18:44.891992+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XVII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0002","text":"As may be clear from the Sixth Theorem, in our CROSS FOUR right angles may be considered: to each of which the preceding Theorem would teach that a QUINARY signification is to be attributed, when placed in one way indeed: but when the other assumes Position, the same Theorem admits of HIEROGLYPHIC marks of the number FIFTY: thus, it is most evident that the CROSS commonly denotes TEN: then, in the order of the Latin Alphabet, it is the twenty-first letter: (whence it has come about that the Sages, called Mecubales, signified twenty-one by the same Letter;) finally, it may also be considered most simply: as is seen, it is One Mark, having the power of whatsoever other [mark], and of however great [a one]. From all which things, by the best Cabalistic demonstration, [one may] conclude","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0003","text":"60","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0004","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0005","text":"we see that our CROSS can signify, for the Mystics, TWO HUNDRED AND FIFTY-TWO, by a wondrous compendium. For FOUR TIMES FIVE; FOUR TIMES FIFTY; TEN: TWENTY-ONE; and ONE: make TWO HUNDRED AND FIFTY-TWO. This Number, by two other methods still, from what has been set forth, as we are able to elicit, so we commend it to Cabalistic beginners, that they may elicit the same: thus attending to brevity: judging nevertheless the varied artful production of the same Masterly Number worthy of the Philosophers' consideration. Nor shall I conceal from you here another memorable Mystagogy. Seeing that our CROSS can be divided into two other letters: if, as we first weigh in some manner their numerical power, so","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0006","text":"in turn","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0007","text":"HIEROGLYPHIC.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0008","text":"61","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0009","text":"in turn we now COMPARE THEIR VERBAL POWER WITH THE CROSS ITSELF, we shall understand with the greatest admiration that from thence arise LIGHT: WORD, final and masterly (from that concord and agreement of the TERNARY in the Unity of the Word).","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_14:DISPLAY-0009"]}],"source_digest":"8f29058a108b31d4a5e6469e585710a351238780b1f2475e8f1a520e036b02c1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XVII."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XVII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15","title":"THEOR. XVIII.","order":19,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_15","text":"THEOR. XVIII.\n\nEX duodecimo & decimotertio\nTheorematibus noſtris colligi\npoteſt, Cæleſtem Aſtronomiam,\nINFERIORIS eſſe quaſi Parentem &\nMagiſtram. Suble-\n\nuatis ergo in Cælum\noculis Cabaliſticis(ex\nPrædictorum Myſte\nriorum Theorica Il-\nluminatis ) talem ad\namuſſim noſtræ Mo-\nNADIS, conſpiciemus\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 65, region 7]\n\nANATOMIAM: In NATVRÆ LVMINE,\nVITAQVE ſeſe ſic nobis ſemper o-\n\n62\n\nM O N A S\n\nſtendentem. Et ſuopte N V T V, Se-\ncretiſſima huiusce Phyſicæ A N A L Y-\nS E O S Myſteria, apertiffime dete­ge-\ntem. O V I autem figuram, iſti C O-\nO R D I N A T I O N I adhibere: Cæleſtis N V N C I I, dum Theoricos, Cæle-\nſteſque Geſtus, ſumus aliquando Contemplati, fuimus edocti. O V AL E M enim, Iſſum, in Æthere, ſuo Curſu Figurare Circuitionem, A-\nſtronomis eſt notiſſimum. Et, cum Dictum,Sapienti,Sat eſt debeat: En noſtras huius Cæleſtis Conſilii Inter-\npretationes (ſic Hieroglyphice pro-\npoſitas:) prædictis omnino Conſen-\ntaneas. H I N C Moniti, diſcat Miſe-\nrimi Alchimiſtæ, ſuos agnoſcere Er-\nrores variós: Quæ ſit Albuminis O-\nV O R V M A Q V A: Q V O D E X V I T E L-\nL I S O L E V M. Quæ O V O R V M C A L X:\nH I N C, Imperitiſſimi illi Impoſto-\nres, cum illorum Deſperatione, In-\n\ntelli-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n63\n\ntelligant: Aliaque his ſimilia, perſplu-\nra. Hic P R O P O R T I O N A T V M A\nN A T V R A, F E R E T O T V M H A-\nB E M V S. Hoc illud eſt Q V V M A-\nQ V I L I N V M, Quod S C A R A B E V S,\nolim diſſupit propter I N I V R I A M, quam Timidis Brutiſque Hominibus, Illius A V I S Violentia & Cru-\ndelitas intulit: Licet ad Scarabei An-\ntrum (Auxilii Implorandi Gratia) ali-\nquibus confugientibus, non inde tamẽ liberatis. Sed ipſe ſolus Scarabeus, hãc ſibi vindicandam I N I V R I A M, modis omnibus, exiſtimans: Vt erat alacri a-\nnimo, Conſtantique voluntate pa-\nratus, ita ad id præſtandum, nec Viribus carebat, nec Ingenio: Vnde variis Conatibus A Q V I L A M dum perſe-\nqueretur Scarabeus: Subtiliſſima F I M I Arte vſus, Illius tandem (vel in Iouis Gremio depoſitum) O V V M,\nin T E R R A M P R Æ C I P I T A R I\n\n64\n\nM O N A S\n\nadeoque DISRVMPI eſfecit. Et eā dem, aliave ratione Aquilinam tandem totam Speciem, e Terris dele-\nuiſſet Scarabeus, niſi, (malum tātum Præcauens,) Iupiter eſſeciſſet. Quo Anni tempore, Aquilæ ſuæ ſollicite curant OVA, Nulli vt circumuoli-\ntent SCARABEI. Illis tamen Con ſulerem, qui iſtius AVIS vexantur Crudelitate, ab ipſis Heliocantharis (qui ita certis Temporum Curricu-\nlis latitando viuunt) Vtiliſſimam ar-\ntem diſcere: Quibus, iam licet non faciant ipſi, eſſet tamen longe gratiſ-\nſimum, ſuis INDICIIS & Signis, de ſuo Inimico, Vindictam ſumi poſſe. Et hic (O Rex) non Æſopum conari me vt agam, Sed Oedipum, Fateren-\ntur, ſi adeſſent, illi, quorum Mentes, ita de Naturæ Summis Fabulari Myſteriis, primò ſubiuuit. Eſſe profecto quosdam noui qui SCARABEI AR-\n\nTIFI-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n65\n\nT I F I C I O, Si haberent D I S S O L V-\nT V M A Q V I L I N V M O V V M, C A L-\nCEM e iuſdem, cum Albumine puro, totoque T E M P E R A R E N T primo. Deinde illud T E M P E R A M E N T V M, V I T E L L I liquore toto, artificioſo ordine, oblinirent: voluendo, reuol-\nuendoque: Vt Scarabei ſuas conglo-\nmerant Pilas. Ita, magnā fieret O V I M E T A M O R P H O S I S: Iam ſcilicet\n\ndisparēret\n&qualin-\nuoluto AL\nB V M I N E\nipſo ( illis\nmultis ve-\nluti Heli-\ncis Reuo-\nlutionibus\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 69, region 5]\n\nfactis) in ipſo V I T E L L I N O S O L I-\nQ V O R E. Cuius Artificii, tale Hiero-\nglyphicum ſignum, N A T V R Æ haud\n\nE\n\n66\n\nM O N A S\n\ndiſplicebit Oeconomis. Sæculis prio-\nribus, multum eſſe a graviſſimis, & Antiquiſſimis celebratum Philoſo-\nphis, tale Artificium, legimus: certiſ-\nſimum & utiliſſimum. Anaxagoras certe, ex hoc Magiſterio, excellentiſ-\nſimam, Poſt, fecit Medicinam: ut in ſuo περὶ τῶν ἐκ προγόνων φυσικῶν libello videre licet. Nihil hic eſſe extra noſtræ Mo-\nN A D I S virtutem Hieroglyphicam, qui animum iſtis Myſteriis ſincerius applicat, clariſſime perſpiciet.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XVIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0002","text":"EX duodecimo & decimotertio\nTheorematibus noſtris colligi\npoteſt, Cæleſtem Aſtronomiam,\nINFERIORIS eſſe quaſi Parentem &\nMagiſtram. Suble-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0003","text":"uatis ergo in Cælum\noculis Cabaliſticis(ex\nPrædictorum Myſte\nriorum Theorica Il-\nluminatis ) talem ad\namuſſim noſtræ Mo-\nNADIS, conſpiciemus","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0004","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 65, region 7]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0005","text":"ANATOMIAM: In NATVRÆ LVMINE,\nVITAQVE ſeſe ſic nobis ſemper o-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0006","text":"62","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0007","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0008","text":"ſtendentem. Et ſuopte N V T V, Se-\ncretiſſima huiusce Phyſicæ A N A L Y-\nS E O S Myſteria, apertiffime dete­ge-\ntem. O V I autem figuram, iſti C O-\nO R D I N A T I O N I adhibere: Cæleſtis N V N C I I, dum Theoricos, Cæle-\nſteſque Geſtus, ſumus aliquando Contemplati, fuimus edocti. O V AL E M enim, Iſſum, in Æthere, ſuo Curſu Figurare Circuitionem, A-\nſtronomis eſt notiſſimum. Et, cum Dictum,Sapienti,Sat eſt debeat: En noſtras huius Cæleſtis Conſilii Inter-\npretationes (ſic Hieroglyphice pro-\npoſitas:) prædictis omnino Conſen-\ntaneas. H I N C Moniti, diſcat Miſe-\nrimi Alchimiſtæ, ſuos agnoſcere Er-\nrores variós: Quæ ſit Albuminis O-\nV O R V M A Q V A: Q V O D E X V I T E L-\nL I S O L E V M. Quæ O V O R V M C A L X:\nH I N C, Imperitiſſimi illi Impoſto-\nres, cum illorum Deſperatione, In-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0009","text":"telli-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0010","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0011","text":"63","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0012","text":"telligant: Aliaque his ſimilia, perſplu-\nra. Hic P R O P O R T I O N A T V M A\nN A T V R A, F E R E T O T V M H A-\nB E M V S. Hoc illud eſt Q V V M A-\nQ V I L I N V M, Quod S C A R A B E V S,\nolim diſſupit propter I N I V R I A M, quam Timidis Brutiſque Hominibus, Illius A V I S Violentia & Cru-\ndelitas intulit: Licet ad Scarabei An-\ntrum (Auxilii Implorandi Gratia) ali-\nquibus confugientibus, non inde tamẽ liberatis. Sed ipſe ſolus Scarabeus, hãc ſibi vindicandam I N I V R I A M, modis omnibus, exiſtimans: Vt erat alacri a-\nnimo, Conſtantique voluntate pa-\nratus, ita ad id præſtandum, nec Viribus carebat, nec Ingenio: Vnde variis Conatibus A Q V I L A M dum perſe-\nqueretur Scarabeus: Subtiliſſima F I M I Arte vſus, Illius tandem (vel in Iouis Gremio depoſitum) O V V M,\nin T E R R A M P R Æ C I P I T A R I","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0013","text":"64","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0014","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0015","text":"adeoque DISRVMPI eſfecit. Et eā dem, aliave ratione Aquilinam tandem totam Speciem, e Terris dele-\nuiſſet Scarabeus, niſi, (malum tātum Præcauens,) Iupiter eſſeciſſet. Quo Anni tempore, Aquilæ ſuæ ſollicite curant OVA, Nulli vt circumuoli-\ntent SCARABEI. Illis tamen Con ſulerem, qui iſtius AVIS vexantur Crudelitate, ab ipſis Heliocantharis (qui ita certis Temporum Curricu-\nlis latitando viuunt) Vtiliſſimam ar-\ntem diſcere: Quibus, iam licet non faciant ipſi, eſſet tamen longe gratiſ-\nſimum, ſuis INDICIIS & Signis, de ſuo Inimico, Vindictam ſumi poſſe. Et hic (O Rex) non Æſopum conari me vt agam, Sed Oedipum, Fateren-\ntur, ſi adeſſent, illi, quorum Mentes, ita de Naturæ Summis Fabulari Myſteriis, primò ſubiuuit. Eſſe profecto quosdam noui qui SCARABEI AR-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0016","text":"TIFI-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0017","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0018","text":"65","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0019","text":"T I F I C I O, Si haberent D I S S O L V-\nT V M A Q V I L I N V M O V V M, C A L-\nCEM e iuſdem, cum Albumine puro, totoque T E M P E R A R E N T primo. Deinde illud T E M P E R A M E N T V M, V I T E L L I liquore toto, artificioſo ordine, oblinirent: voluendo, reuol-\nuendoque: Vt Scarabei ſuas conglo-\nmerant Pilas. Ita, magnā fieret O V I M E T A M O R P H O S I S: Iam ſcilicet","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0020","text":"disparēret\n&qualin-\nuoluto AL\nB V M I N E\nipſo ( illis\nmultis ve-\nluti Heli-\ncis Reuo-\nlutionibus","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0021","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 69, region 5]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0022","text":"factis) in ipſo V I T E L L I N O S O L I-\nQ V O R E. Cuius Artificii, tale Hiero-\nglyphicum ſignum, N A T V R Æ haud","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0023","text":"E","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0024","text":"66","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0025","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0026","text":"diſplicebit Oeconomis. Sæculis prio-\nribus, multum eſſe a graviſſimis, & Antiquiſſimis celebratum Philoſo-\nphis, tale Artificium, legimus: certiſ-\nſimum & utiliſſimum. Anaxagoras certe, ex hoc Magiſterio, excellentiſ-\nſimam, Poſt, fecit Medicinam: ut in ſuo περὶ τῶν ἐκ προγόνων φυσικῶν libello videre licet. Nihil hic eſſe extra noſtræ Mo-\nN A D I S virtutem Hieroglyphicam, qui animum iſtis Myſteriis ſincerius applicat, clariſſime perſpiciet.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"27aced5ed7eff2a631ca521460b0a342c4ea53c388cc94b9efaeee06145e3e98","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231933210581Z_2a84ef76","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XVIII.","source_sha256":"27aced5ed7eff2a631ca521460b0a342c4ea53c388cc94b9efaeee06145e3e98","sha256":"2f4e38be7475ec66179220e78c52ca193ef462e20f8d519dfc0d1fd3efccea1c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:19:33.210715+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XVIII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0002","text":"FROM our twelfth and thirteenth\nTheorems it may be inferred that\nCelestial Astronomy is, as it were,\nthe Parent and Mistress of the\nINFERIOR [one]. Raised—","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0003","text":"therefore, into Heaven\nwith Cabalistic eyes (il-\nluminated from the The-\nory of the aforesaid Mys-\nteries), we shall behold an\nANATOMY precisely matching\nour MONAD:","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0004","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 65, region 7]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0005","text":"In NATURE'S LIGHT,\nAND LIFE, ever thus showing itself to us—","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0006","text":"62","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0007","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0008","text":"self. And, by its own NOD, most\nplainly unveiling the most secret mys-\nteries of this physical ANALY-\nSIS. But that the figure of the EGG is\nto be applied to this CO-\nORDINATION, we have been taught by the CELESTIAL MESSENGER, when at some time we have contemplated his theoretical and celestial gestures. For it is most well known to astronomers that HE traces an OVAL circuit in the Ether in his course. And, since it ought to be that what is said is enough for the wise: Behold our interpretations of this Celestial Counsel (thus set forth hieroglyphically), altogether consonant with the aforesaid matters. WARNED HENCE, let most wretched Alchemists learn to acknowledge their various errors: what is the WATER OF EGGS' ALBUMEN: THAT FROM YOLKS [IS] OIL. What is the LIME OF EGGS: HENCE, let those most unskilled impostors, together with their despair, under-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0009","text":"stand-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0010","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0011","text":"63","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0012","text":"stand: and very many other similar things. Here we have almost the whole [matter] PROPORTIONED BY NATURE. This is that EAGLE'S EGG which the SCARAB once destroyed on account of the INJURY which the violence and cruelty of that BIRD had inflicted upon timid and brutish men: although some, fleeing to the Scarab's cave in order to implore aid, were nevertheless not thereby saved. But the Scarab alone, deeming that this INJURY must by every means be avenged by him, as he was ready in spirit and steadfast will, so neither lacked strength nor ingenuity for accomplishing it. Whence, while the Scarab pursued the EAGLE by various attempts, employing the most subtle art of DUNG, he at last caused her EGG (even though deposited in Jupiter's lap) TO BE CAST DOWN TO THE EARTH","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0013","text":"64","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0014","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0015","text":"and thus caused it TO BURST. And by that, or some other means, the Scarab would at last have wiped out the whole species of Eagle from the earth, unless Jupiter, guarding against so great an evil, had caused it to be so. At that season of the year when they carefully tend their eggs, Eagles take care that no SCARABS fly about them. Yet I would advise those who are vexed by the cruelty of that BIRD to learn a most useful art from the Heliocanthari themselves (who live in hiding according to such fixed courses of times): although they themselves may now not do it, it would nevertheless be most agreeable that vengeance could be taken upon their enemy through their TOKENS and Signs. And here (O King), I would confess that I am attempting to play not Aesop, but Oedipus, if those were present whose minds he first aided thus to discourse concerning the lofty fabulous Mysteries of Nature. I know indeed that there are some who, by the SCARAB'S AR-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0016","text":"TI-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0017","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0018","text":"65","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0019","text":"FICE, if they had a DISSOLVED EAGLE'S EGG, would first TEMPER its LIME with pure Albumen, and the whole [of it]. Then they would coat that MIXTURE, in an artful order, with all the liquid of the YOLK: rolling and re-rolling it, as Scarabs compact their balls. Thus a great METAMORPHOSIS OF THE EGG would occur: namely, it would now","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0020","text":"disappear,\nand, as it\nwere, the AL-\nBUMEN itself\nhaving been\nrolled up (those\nmany, as it\nwere, spiral revo-\nlutions","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0021","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 69, region 5]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0022","text":"having been made), into the very VITELLINE SOLI-\nQUOR. Of which art, such a hiero-\nglyphic sign Nature by no means","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231933210581Z_2a84ef76:DISPLAY-0023","text":"E\n\n66","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0023","RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0025","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0026","text":"will displease the Economists. In earlier ages, we read that such an artifice was much celebrated by the most weighty and most ancient philosophers: as most certain and most useful. Anaxagoras indeed, from this Mastery, afterwards made the most excellent Medicine: as may be seen in his little book περὶ τῶν ἐκ προγόνων φυσικῶν. He who applies his mind more sincerely to those Mysteries will perceive most clearly that nothing here lies outside the Hieroglyphic power of our Monad.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_15:DISPLAY-0026"]}],"source_digest":"d8b2349059ec630660b08a8ee7fd7fdc9413b88b86e547822ccc22fdfa07455d","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XVIII."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XVIII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER","title":"T H E Ò R. X I X.","order":20,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_THER","text":"T H E Ò R.  X I X.\n\nQVod S O L & L V N A, omnibus\ncæteris Planetis, longe fortius, in\ninferiora cuncta Elementata Corpo-\nra, ſuas Corporales infundant Vires:\nOmnium rerum Corporatarum\nA N A L Y S I S  P Y R O N O M I C A, Effe-\nctu demonſtrat: L V N Æ dum refun-\ndunt Aqueum Humorem: S O L I S-\nQ V E Igneu Liquorem: quibus, Re-\n\nrum\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n67\n\nrum Mortalium Suſtentatur COR-\nPVLENTIA TERRESTRIS.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E Ò R.  X I X.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0002","text":"QVod S O L & L V N A, omnibus\ncæteris Planetis, longe fortius, in\ninferiora cuncta Elementata Corpo-\nra, ſuas Corporales infundant Vires:\nOmnium rerum Corporatarum\nA N A L Y S I S  P Y R O N O M I C A, Effe-\nctu demonſtrat: L V N Æ dum refun-\ndunt Aqueum Humorem: S O L I S-\nQ V E Igneu Liquorem: quibus, Re-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0003","text":"rum","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0004","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0005","text":"67","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0006","text":"rum Mortalium Suſtentatur COR-\nPVLENTIA TERRESTRIS.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"7dd544ce9b77aeb7b3214f99a1936d597f989f125bf798da0cfbf0241d213602","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T231937049697Z_72603521","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E Ò R. X I X.","source_sha256":"7dd544ce9b77aeb7b3214f99a1936d597f989f125bf798da0cfbf0241d213602","sha256":"b1cf95c1d887812c7392c4cc6c58283e0c5de347401e35d58bb167648ef54aba","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:19:37.049757+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M  X I X.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0002","text":"That the S U N and M O O N, far more powerfully than all the other Planets, pour their Corporeal Forces into all the lower Elementary Bodies: the P Y R O N O M I C Analysis of all Corporeal things demonstrates by its effect: while those of the M O O N pour back the Watery Humour, and those of the S U N the Igneous Liquid: by which, the—","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0003","text":"things","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0004","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0005","text":"67","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0006","text":"—Corporeity of mortal things is sustained.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_THER:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"b1677cfca766dfb7c45a00e82117bbd591f7ece8d51ffde181c96d7451942e08","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E Ò R. X I X."}],"original_title":"T H E Ò R. X I X.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16","title":"T H E O R. X X.","order":21,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_16","text":"T H E O R.  X X.\n\nLicet ſatis bona ratione Hierogly-\nphica , ſupra , demonſtrauimus,\nELEMENTA, per Lineas Rectas ſi-\ngnificari: Hic tamen de CRVCIS no-\nſtræ PVNCTO Quaſi CENTRALI,\nExactiſſimam dabimus Speculatio-\nnem. In TERNARII noſtri Conſide-\nratione, nullo modo, illud Abeſſe po-\nteſt: in eo noſtri BINARII Situ. Si e-\nnim abeſſe poſſe, Quis (Diuinæ Im-\nperitus Matheſeos) contenderet: Ab-\neſſe Supponat. Non erit ergo Reli-\nquus, BINARIVS noſter: Sed emer-\nget QVATERNARIVS: Puncti illius\nAblatione, Diſcontinuata Linearum\nvnitate. At Binarium eſſe Reliquum,\nvna nobiſcum Suppoſuit aduerſarius\nnoſter: Erit ergo & BINARIVS, idem,\n& QVATERNARIVS, eadem\n\nE  2\n\n68    M O N A S\n\nconſideratione. Quod ὡς ἀδύνατον eſſe, ſatis eſt Manifeſtum. Adeſſe ergo ex omni Neceſſitate, debet illud P V N C T V M, quod cum B I N A R I O, noſtrum Conſtituat T E R N A R I V M: nec Aliud quid eius loco S V B S T I-\nT V I poteſt. Non tamen eſt de Hy-\npoſtatica Proprietate, ipſius B I N A R I I: nec aliquo modo Pars. Quod non ſit Pars, hinc demonſtratur. Omnes Lineæ Partes, ſunt Lineæ. At illud eſſe P V N C T V M, hypotheſis confirmat. Non ergo B I N A R I I illius Pars ali-\nqua: Vnde multo minus de Hypo-\nſtatica Proprietate Binarii. Proinde N O T A N D V M eſt maxime, quod & Propriam Habeat H Y P O S T A S I M: Et nihilo minus tamen, in ipſis noſtri B I N A R I I Longitudinibus L IN E A R I B V S, contineatur. Et quia, Sic, V T R I S Q V E videtur eſſe C O M-\nM V N E, Q V A N D A M, & I P S V M,\n\nB I N A-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n69\n\nB I N A R I I,  S E C R E T A M  R E C I-\nP E R E  I M A G I N E M cenſeri. Vnde,\nQ V A T E R N A R I V M, Hîc, De-\nM O N S T R A M V S,  I N T E R N A R I O\nQ V I E S C E N T E M. Tu, mi Deus,\nmihi ignoſcas obſecro, Si erga tuam nunc Peccauerim Maiestatem, tan-\ntum, in Publicis, Scriptis, Reuelans, Myſterium. Sed Spero, quod, Soli, qui ſunt Digni illud vere Intelligent. Pergamus nunc ad noſtræ C R V C I S, illum, quem aſſignauimus Q V AT E R N A R I V M. Vbi an Abſeſſe illud P V N C T V M poteſt, quod I B I R C-\npræſentatur, perpendamus. Mathe-\nmatica profecto nos docet remoueri poſſe. Nam non Solum, E O S E P A-\nR A T O, R E L I Q V V S Eſt noſter Q V A-\nT E R N A R I V S: Sed cum D I S T I N-\nC T I O R longe tum C L A R I O R in o-\nmnium oculis erit F A C T V S. N V L-\nL A  S V Æ  S V B S T A N T I A L I S  P R O-\n\nE 3\n\n70\n\nM O N A S\n\nPORTIONIS RECEDENTE PAR-\nTE: SED SVPERFLVO, ET CON-\nFVSIONIS PVNCTO, SIG DA-\nMNATO, REIECTOQVE. O o-\nmnipotens Diuina Maieſtas, QVAN-\nTAM TVIS APICIBVS, ET IO-\nTIS, IN TVA DESCRIPTIS, DI-\nSPOSITISQVE LEGE INESSE\nSAPIENTIAM, ET INEFFABI-\nLIVM MYSTERIORVM INFINI-\nTATEM, CONFITERI COGIMVR\nMORTALES: SI MAXIMA TER-\nRENA SECRETA ET ARCANA,\nVNIVS ISTIVS PVNCTI, AME,\n(AT IN TVO LVMINE) LOCATI\nET EXAMINATI, INDICIO\nVARIO, EXPLICARI ET FI-\nDELISSIME DEMONSTRARI\nQVEANT; PVNCTI videlicet in\nTERNARIO diuino, nullo mo-\ndo SVPERFLVI: AT PVNCTI\nin QVATVOR ELEMENTO-\n\nRVM\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n71\n\nR V M   R E G N O, conſiderati, F Æ-\nC V L E N T I quidem, C O R R V-\nP T I B I L I S, T E N E B R I C O S I. O\nTerque, Quaterque Beatos illos, qui illud T E R N A R I I, (quaſi, C O R V-\nL A T I V V M) A D I P I S C I poſſunt\nP V N C T V M: & illud Q V A T E R-\nN A R I I, T E T R V M & S V P E R F L V-\nV M, A M A N D A R E Tenebrarumq;\nRelinquere Principi. Sic, ad C L A R I-\nT A T I S N I V E Æ, & A L B A R V M\nV E S T I V M Ornamenta perueniē-\nmus: O M A X I M I L I A N E,\nQuem, Deus, (iſta Myſtagogia, aut\nAuſtriacæ Familiæ aliquem) Maxi-\nmum, aliquando faciat (vel me qui-\ndem in Chriſto Dormiente) ad ſui\nTremendi Nominis Honorem: in\niſtis, Iſtis, (Punctis in T E R R I S S V-\nP E R F L V I,) abominandis Tene-\nbris; & vſterius, intolerabilibus.\nSed ne Ipſe iam Superflua ( non\n\nE 4\n\n72\n\nM O N A S\n\napto ſcilicet loco) profundam verba, intra Propoſiti mei Cancellos, actu-\ntum, nunc me recipiam. Et, quia, illis Sermonem iam abſoluerim, quorum Oculi in eorum Sedem Corde: Nunc mihi ad illos conuertenda Oratio eſt, quorum Corda in eorum adhuc pro-\nmineant oculis. Quæ hoc loco dixi-\nmus, En C R V C I S adſcripta figura, aliquo modo repræſentare poteſt. Primum, de P V N C T O, in Binis Æ-\nqualibus L I N E I S (æqualiter & ina-\nqualiter decuſſatis) N E C E S S A R I O; Veluti hic, ad A Deinde, ad B (quaſi quædam Puncti ſuperflui ablati, Va-\ncuitatem) diſtin-\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 76, region 4]\n\nctas videtis, QVA-\nTVOR rectas Li-\nneas: a P V N C T O,\nprius illis com-\nmuni, S E P A R A T A S: Illis, inde, nul-\nlo eueniente ſui detrimento. Iſta eſt\n\nvia,\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n75\n\nvia, per quam Noſtra M O N A S, per Binarium, T E R N A R I V M Q V E pro-\ngrediens, in Q V A T E R N A R I O Puri-\nficato, ſ i b i Vni reſtituatur, per Æ-\nqualitatis Proportionem. (Quodq; enim Totum, ſuis omnibus partibus eſt Æquale.) Hocque dum fiat, nihil interea Externarum admittit, Noſtra M O N A S, Vnitatum, Numero-\nrumve: Cum ipſa ſibi exactiſſime Sufficiat: Suis abſolutiſſima Nume-\nris omnibus. In quorum Amplitudi-\nnem, tum Magicis diffunditur mo-\ndis: tum non vulgari, poſt, Artificis Induſtria, & maximo ipſius Mona-\ndis Emolumento, (in Dignitate & Potentia) ad ſuam Primam Propria-\nque Reſtituitur M A T E R I A M: inte-\nrim, quæ ad genuinam hæreditaria-\nque ſuam non Spectant Proportionem, omni modo & diligentia, reſe-\nctis, reiectiſque in æternum Fæcibus.\n\n74\n\nMONAS","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.  X X.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Licet ſatis bona ratione Hierogly-\nphica , ſupra , demonſtrauimus,\nELEMENTA, per Lineas Rectas ſi-\ngnificari: Hic tamen de CRVCIS no-\nſtræ PVNCTO Quaſi CENTRALI,\nExactiſſimam dabimus Speculatio-\nnem. In TERNARII noſtri Conſide-\nratione, nullo modo, illud Abeſſe po-\nteſt: in eo noſtri BINARII Situ. Si e-\nnim abeſſe poſſe, Quis (Diuinæ Im-\nperitus Matheſeos) contenderet: Ab-\neſſe Supponat. Non erit ergo Reli-\nquus, BINARIVS noſter: Sed emer-\nget QVATERNARIVS: Puncti illius\nAblatione, Diſcontinuata Linearum\nvnitate. At Binarium eſſe Reliquum,\nvna nobiſcum Suppoſuit aduerſarius\nnoſter: Erit ergo & BINARIVS, idem,\n& QVATERNARIVS, eadem","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0003","text":"E  2","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0004","text":"68    M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0005","text":"conſideratione. Quod ὡς ἀδύνατον eſſe, ſatis eſt Manifeſtum. Adeſſe ergo ex omni Neceſſitate, debet illud P V N C T V M, quod cum B I N A R I O, noſtrum Conſtituat T E R N A R I V M: nec Aliud quid eius loco S V B S T I-\nT V I poteſt. Non tamen eſt de Hy-\npoſtatica Proprietate, ipſius B I N A R I I: nec aliquo modo Pars. Quod non ſit Pars, hinc demonſtratur. Omnes Lineæ Partes, ſunt Lineæ. At illud eſſe P V N C T V M, hypotheſis confirmat. Non ergo B I N A R I I illius Pars ali-\nqua: Vnde multo minus de Hypo-\nſtatica Proprietate Binarii. Proinde N O T A N D V M eſt maxime, quod & Propriam Habeat H Y P O S T A S I M: Et nihilo minus tamen, in ipſis noſtri B I N A R I I Longitudinibus L IN E A R I B V S, contineatur. Et quia, Sic, V T R I S Q V E videtur eſſe C O M-\nM V N E, Q V A N D A M, & I P S V M,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0006","text":"B I N A-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0007","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0008","text":"69","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0009","text":"B I N A R I I,  S E C R E T A M  R E C I-\nP E R E  I M A G I N E M cenſeri. Vnde,\nQ V A T E R N A R I V M, Hîc, De-\nM O N S T R A M V S,  I N T E R N A R I O\nQ V I E S C E N T E M. Tu, mi Deus,\nmihi ignoſcas obſecro, Si erga tuam nunc Peccauerim Maiestatem, tan-\ntum, in Publicis, Scriptis, Reuelans, Myſterium. Sed Spero, quod, Soli, qui ſunt Digni illud vere Intelligent. Pergamus nunc ad noſtræ C R V C I S, illum, quem aſſignauimus Q V AT E R N A R I V M. Vbi an Abſeſſe illud P V N C T V M poteſt, quod I B I R C-\npræſentatur, perpendamus. Mathe-\nmatica profecto nos docet remoueri poſſe. Nam non Solum, E O S E P A-\nR A T O, R E L I Q V V S Eſt noſter Q V A-\nT E R N A R I V S: Sed cum D I S T I N-\nC T I O R longe tum C L A R I O R in o-\nmnium oculis erit F A C T V S. N V L-\nL A  S V Æ  S V B S T A N T I A L I S  P R O-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0010","text":"E 3","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0011","text":"70","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0012","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0013","text":"PORTIONIS RECEDENTE PAR-\nTE: SED SVPERFLVO, ET CON-\nFVSIONIS PVNCTO, SIG DA-\nMNATO, REIECTOQVE. O o-\nmnipotens Diuina Maieſtas, QVAN-\nTAM TVIS APICIBVS, ET IO-\nTIS, IN TVA DESCRIPTIS, DI-\nSPOSITISQVE LEGE INESSE\nSAPIENTIAM, ET INEFFABI-\nLIVM MYSTERIORVM INFINI-\nTATEM, CONFITERI COGIMVR\nMORTALES: SI MAXIMA TER-\nRENA SECRETA ET ARCANA,\nVNIVS ISTIVS PVNCTI, AME,\n(AT IN TVO LVMINE) LOCATI\nET EXAMINATI, INDICIO\nVARIO, EXPLICARI ET FI-\nDELISSIME DEMONSTRARI\nQVEANT; PVNCTI videlicet in\nTERNARIO diuino, nullo mo-\ndo SVPERFLVI: AT PVNCTI\nin QVATVOR ELEMENTO-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0014","text":"RVM","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0015","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0016","text":"71","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0017","text":"R V M   R E G N O, conſiderati, F Æ-\nC V L E N T I quidem, C O R R V-\nP T I B I L I S, T E N E B R I C O S I. O\nTerque, Quaterque Beatos illos, qui illud T E R N A R I I, (quaſi, C O R V-\nL A T I V V M) A D I P I S C I poſſunt\nP V N C T V M: & illud Q V A T E R-\nN A R I I, T E T R V M & S V P E R F L V-\nV M, A M A N D A R E Tenebrarumq;\nRelinquere Principi. Sic, ad C L A R I-\nT A T I S N I V E Æ, & A L B A R V M\nV E S T I V M Ornamenta perueniē-\nmus: O M A X I M I L I A N E,\nQuem, Deus, (iſta Myſtagogia, aut\nAuſtriacæ Familiæ aliquem) Maxi-\nmum, aliquando faciat (vel me qui-\ndem in Chriſto Dormiente) ad ſui\nTremendi Nominis Honorem: in\niſtis, Iſtis, (Punctis in T E R R I S S V-\nP E R F L V I,) abominandis Tene-\nbris; & vſterius, intolerabilibus.\nSed ne Ipſe iam Superflua ( non","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0018","text":"E 4","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0019","text":"72","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0020","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0021","text":"apto ſcilicet loco) profundam verba, intra Propoſiti mei Cancellos, actu-\ntum, nunc me recipiam. Et, quia, illis Sermonem iam abſoluerim, quorum Oculi in eorum Sedem Corde: Nunc mihi ad illos conuertenda Oratio eſt, quorum Corda in eorum adhuc pro-\nmineant oculis. Quæ hoc loco dixi-\nmus, En C R V C I S adſcripta figura, aliquo modo repræſentare poteſt. Primum, de P V N C T O, in Binis Æ-\nqualibus L I N E I S (æqualiter & ina-\nqualiter decuſſatis) N E C E S S A R I O; Veluti hic, ad A Deinde, ad B (quaſi quædam Puncti ſuperflui ablati, Va-\ncuitatem) diſtin-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0022","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 76, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0023","text":"ctas videtis, QVA-\nTVOR rectas Li-\nneas: a P V N C T O,\nprius illis com-\nmuni, S E P A R A T A S: Illis, inde, nul-\nlo eueniente ſui detrimento. Iſta eſt","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0024","text":"via,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0025","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0026","text":"75","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0027","text":"via, per quam Noſtra M O N A S, per Binarium, T E R N A R I V M Q V E pro-\ngrediens, in Q V A T E R N A R I O Puri-\nficato, ſ i b i Vni reſtituatur, per Æ-\nqualitatis Proportionem. (Quodq; enim Totum, ſuis omnibus partibus eſt Æquale.) Hocque dum fiat, nihil interea Externarum admittit, Noſtra M O N A S, Vnitatum, Numero-\nrumve: Cum ipſa ſibi exactiſſime Sufficiat: Suis abſolutiſſima Nume-\nris omnibus. In quorum Amplitudi-\nnem, tum Magicis diffunditur mo-\ndis: tum non vulgari, poſt, Artificis Induſtria, & maximo ipſius Mona-\ndis Emolumento, (in Dignitate & Potentia) ad ſuam Primam Propria-\nque Reſtituitur M A T E R I A M: inte-\nrim, quæ ad genuinam hæreditaria-\nque ſuam non Spectant Proportionem, omni modo & diligentia, reſe-\nctis, reiectiſque in æternum Fæcibus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0028","text":"74","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0029","text":"MONAS","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"e5e9159b92a78674446c431aca0436d787ed75670943599802133ab62d5c4e07","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232005941871Z_caa8f529","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. X X.","source_sha256":"e5e9159b92a78674446c431aca0436d787ed75670943599802133ab62d5c4e07","sha256":"3ce1089458bfbce358466c15c8947784c2e2b415b49a9a60d391f424eec759a4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:20:05.941950+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M  X X.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Although above we have demonstrated, by sufficiently good hieroglyphic reasoning, that the ELEMENTS are signified by Straight Lines: yet here we shall give a most exact speculation concerning the POINT, as it were CENTRAL, of our CROSS. In the consideration of our TERNARY, it can by no means be absent: in the situation of our BINARY it is present. For if it could be absent, who (being unskilled in Divine Mathematics) would contend otherwise? Let him suppose it absent. Therefore our BINARY will not remain: but a QUATERNARY will emerge: through the removal of that Point, the unity of the Lines having been disrupted. But our adversary has supposed along with us that the Binary remains: therefore it will be both a BINARY, the same thing, and a QUATERNARY, in the same","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0003","text":"E  2","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0004","text":"68    M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0005","text":"consideration. That this is, ὡς ἀδύνατον, sufficiently manifest. Therefore that P O I N T must of all necessity be present, which, together with the B I N A R Y, constitutes our T E R N A R Y: nor can anything else be S U B S T I-\nT U T E D in its place. Yet it is not of the Hypostatic Property of that B I N A R Y: nor is it in any way a Part. That it is not a Part is demonstrated from this. All the Parts of Lines are Lines. But the hypothesis confirms that it is a P O I N T. Therefore it is no Part of that B I N A R Y: whence much less is it of the Hypostatic Property of the Binary. Accordingly it is most to be N O T E D, that it has its Own H Y P O S T A S I S: and nevertheless is contained in the L I N E A R Lengths themselves of our B I N A R Y. And because, thus, it seems to be, in a certain manner, C O M-\nM O N to B O T H, and the B I N A R Y itself,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0006","text":"B I N A-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0007","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0008","text":"69","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0009","text":"B I N A R Y, to receive a S E C R E T  I M A G E. Whence, here we D E M O N S T R A T E the Q U A T E R N A R Y R E S T I N G  I N  T H E  T E R N A R Y. Do Thou, my God, forgive me, I beseech Thee, if I have now sinned against Thy Majesty, by revealing so great a Mystery in public writings. But I hope that only those who are worthy truly understand it. Let us now proceed to that QUATERNARY of our C R O S S which we have assigned. Let us consider whether that P O I N T which is represented T H E R E by I B I R C can be absent. Mathematics indeed teaches us that it can be removed. For, not only does our Q U A-\nT E R N A R Y remain when I T  I S  S E P A-\nR A T E D: but it will become much more D I S T I N C T, and then C L E A R E R, in the eyes of all. N O  P A R T  O F  I T S  S U B S T A N T I A L  P R O-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0010","text":"E 3","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0011","text":"70","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0012","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0013","text":"PORTION HAVING RECEDED: BUT THE SUPERFLUOUS, AND THE POINT OF CONFUSION, HAVING BEEN DAMNED AND REJECTED. O omnipotent Divine Majesty, HOW GREAT A WISDOM, AND AN INFINITY OF INEFFABLE MYSTERIES, WE MORTALS ARE COMPELLED TO CONFESS TO INHERE IN THY TITTLES AND IOTAS, DESCRIBED AND DISPOSED IN THY LAW: IF THE GREATEST EARTHLY SECRETS AND ARCANA, OF THIS ONE POINT, PLACED AND EXAMINED BY ME (BUT IN THY LIGHT), MAY BE EXPLAINED BY VARIOUS INDICATION AND MOST FAITHFULLY DEMONSTRATED; namely, of the POINT in the divine TERNARY, by no means SUPERFLUOUS: BUT OF THE POINT in the KINGDOM OF THE FOUR ELEMENTS","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0014","text":"O F","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0015","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0016","text":"71","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0017","text":"C O N S I D E R E D, indeed F O U L, C O R R U P T I B L E, S H A D O W Y. O thrice and four times blessed are those who can A T T A I N that P O I N T of the T E R N A R Y, as it were C O R R E L A T I V E: and can C O N S I G N that T E T R O U S and S U P E R F L U O U S point of the Q U A T E R N A R Y, and leave it to the Prince of Darkness. Thus we shall attain the ornaments of S N O W Y  B R I G H T N E S S and W H I T E  G A R M E N T S: O M A X I M I L I A N, whom God may someday make Greatest (by this mystagogy, or by some one of the Austrian Family), to the honour of His Dread Name—even if I myself be sleeping in Christ—in these, those abominable Darknesses (the Points superfluous on E A R T H), and further, intolerable. But lest I myself now pour forth superfluous words (not","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0018","text":"E 4","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0019","text":"72","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0020","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0021","text":"namely, in a fitting place), let me now betake myself within the bounds of my purpose. And, since I have now finished my discourse for those whose Eyes are in the seat of their Heart: now I must turn my speech to those whose Hearts still protrude in their eyes. What we have said in this place, behold, the figure inscribed upon the C R O S S can in some manner represent. First, concerning the P O I N T, N E C E S S A R Y in Two Equal L I N E S (crossed equally and unequally), as here, at A. Then, at B, you see, as it were, a certain vacancy of the superfluous Point having been removed, distin-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0022","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 76, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0023","text":"ctly, F O U R straight Lines: S E P A R A T E D from the P O I N T formerly common to them: with no detriment to them resulting therefrom. This is the","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0023"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0024","text":"way,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0025","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0026","text":"75","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0026"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0027","text":"the way through which Our M O N A S, proceeding through the Binary and the T E R N A R Y,\nis restored to itself as One, in the Purified Q U A T E R N A R Y, through the Proportion of E-\nquality. (For every Whole is Equal to all its parts.) And while this is done, Our M O N A S meanwhile admits nothing of External Units or Num-\nbers: since it most exactly Suffices unto itself, by all its most absolute Num-\nbers. Into the Amplitude of which it is spread abroad, now by Magical modes: now, afterward, by the not common Industry of the Artificer, and to the greatest Emolument of the Monad itself (in Dignity and Power), it is Restored to its First and Proper M A T T E R: in the meantime, those things which do not pertain to its genuine and hereditary Proportion having by every means and diligence been cut away, and rejected for ever as Dregs.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0027"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0028","text":"74","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0028"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0029","text":"MONAS","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_16:DISPLAY-0029"]}],"source_digest":"1307540c8972759c8d765c3de4d4a3fcc7baebabb8a8804814d0b3909175066d","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. X X."}],"original_title":"T H E O R. X X.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17","title":"THEOR. XXI.","order":22,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_17","text":"THEOR. XXI.\n\nSI, Quod in noſtræ MONADIS Re-\nceſſibus , Interius Latebat Inuo-\nlutum, eſſet in Lucem erutum; com-\nmutatisque vicibus , eiuſdem Partes\nPrimæ , qualiſque Exteriores , Loco\nIncluderentur Medio , Qualis inde\nfieret MONADIS Philoſophica Trāſ-\nformatio , Superius Vidiſtis: Nunc\nvero , Myſticæ MONADIS , aliam\nvobis proponemus Localem Com-\nmutationem:Partibus illis,vnde SV-\nPERIORVM PLANETARVM, Cha\nracteres noſtri Hieroglyphici , ſeſe\nnobis obtulere prius,Surſum hic ere-\nctis: æque ratione,reliquis quidem\ndeinceps Planetis, eum ſingulis Sor-\ntientibus Situm,quem illis Plato ad\nſcribere ſere viſus eſt: Si rite ex\nPoſitione iſta deſumantur. In\nipſo enim Acuminé Arietino,\nCoueniunt Saturnus, Iupiter,\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 78, region 5]\n\nMars:\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n75\n\nMars: deinde deſcẽdendo, Crux Ve-\nneri Mercurioq; inſeruit. Sequuntur tandem ipſe Sol, & infima L V N A. Sed hæc alio ſunt ventilanda, loco: Noſtræ tamen M O N A D I S hoſce no-\nlui celare Theſauros Philoſophicos. Sicque unam rationem dare, cur ita M O N A D I S mutari Situm, conſultum duxîmus. Sed, alia, quæ in rem veſtrâ eſſe ſcio, Videte, Auditeq;, de hoc Si-\ntu, maiora: paucisq; explicanda. Di-\nſtribuamus igitur M O N A D E M, (hoc nouo modo Locatam) in Ana-\ntomica Membra B.D.C. Vbi, in illo nouo T E R N AR I O; ipſius D, & C, vel Ruſticis quidem, ſunt no-\ntæ F I G V R Æ. At ille T E R T I V S, qui per B deſignatur, non tam facile a Cunctis cognoſci poteſt. Nec illud\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 79, region 4]\n\n76\n\nM O N A S\n\nguidem leuiter eſt conſiderandum:\nillas tria notas FORMAS,D,&C; ſepa-\nratas diuerſasq; ab illo B, oſtendere\nESSENTIAS:Secundo,quod iſtius C,\ncornua, deorſum, quaſi TERRAM\nverſus conuerti conſpiciantur: Et,D\nillius,ea pars quæ ipſam C,illuminat.\nverſus terram, deorſum Scilicet, re-\nſpicit:in cuius ſolius Centro,eſt Viſi-\nbile PVNCTVM:vere TERRESTRE\nEt Quod vtraque Denique D & C,\nad Inferiora magis loca, hic ſuum\nHieroglyphicum faciunt Indicium,\nquam B. Terra autem, Hieroglyphi-\nce, STABILITATEM, & FIXIONEM\nnotare nobis poteſt. Qualia ergo\nſint D,&C,inde,concludendum re-\nlinquo. Vnde etiam Magnum nunc\nnotare SECRETVM, Quiſq; poteſt:\nde Priore SOLE&LVNA, quæ dixi-\nmus,quomodo hinc Interpretationẽ\npleniorem, & maxime neceſſariam,\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\nrecipe-\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n77\n\nrecipere poſſunt: Illis quidem, vſque\nin hunc locum, ſurſum poſitis: Luna-\nribuſque Cornibus ſurſum eleuatis.\nSed de hoc Satis. TERTII nunc il-\nlius, iuxta noſtrę Hieroglyphicę Ar-\ntis Fundamenta examinemus NA-\nTVRAM. Primo, in Capite geſtare\nvidetur L VNAM DVPLICEM. Vel\nArieté, noſtrum, (ſed inuersum My-\nſtice.) Deinde Elementorum habet\nannexum Hieroglyphicū Signum.\nQuantum ad L VNAM Duplicatam\nattinet: Sic (iuxta Materiam ſubiectā)\nexplicari poteſt: DVPLEX LVNÆ\nGRADVS. De gradibus loquimur il-\nlis,quales Phyſices Periti, QVATVOR\ntantum inter omnes poſſunt inueni-\nre Creatas NATVRAS. Nimirum\nESSE,VIVERE,SENTIRE,&INTEL-\nLIGERE. Primos ergo Duos iſtorum\nGradus, huic ineſſe, annotantes: Sic\ndicemus: LVNA EXISTENS, VIVA\n\n178\n\nM O N A S\n\nVitam vero Quidam per Motum\ndeſiniunt. MOTVS autem Sex ſunt\nnotiſſimæ Species. CRVX certe quę\nadiuncta eſt: Elementorum hic re-\nquiri Notat Artificium. Præterea, in\niſtis noſtris Theoriis, vt SEMICIR-\nCVLVM, LVNÆ eſſe Hierogly-\nphicum ſæpiſſime tradidimus: Ita &\nIntegrum Circulum, SOLEM ſigni-\nficare: hic autem, duo ſunt Semicir-\nculi; Sed SEPARATI (adcommu-\nne PVNCTVM Copulati tamen)\nqui, ſi apte coniungantur (vt arte\npoſſunt quidem) SOLAREM nobis\nCircularemq; referre poſſunt Pleni-\ntudinem. Ex iſtis ſimul conſideratis,\nſic Summatim, Hieroglyphicè, nos\nhanc proferre poſſe Sententiam pa-\ntet. LVNA EXISTENS VIVA, PER\nELEMENTORVM TRACTANDA\nMAGISTERIVM: HABENS PO-\nTENTIAM, VT SOLAREM REPRÆ-\n\nSENTET\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n79\n\nSENTET PLENITVDINEM, SVIS\nSIMVL ARTE CONNEXIS SEMI-\nCIRCULIS. Compleatur ergo: Fiatq; ille,(quem diximus) CIRCULVS: vt, per E literam, hic annotauimus. Me-\nmores ergo ſimus, primo hunc SOLAREM GRADVM, non Natura nobis fuiſſe obuium, ſed ARTIFICIA-\nLEM, FACTITIVMQVE iam eſſe: Et eum quidem, nobis ſe obtuliſſe primo aſpectu; & Natura ſua,(videlicet in B) ſuis Partibus Laxis,Fluxis,diſſo lutis; non SOLIDE in Solarem Spe-\nciem Compactis. Deinde horum Se-\nmicirculorum Semidiametrum, non eſſe æqualem Semidiametro D & C (nobis ita natorum,& omnibus No-\ntiſſimorum) ſed Minore multo. Vnde Clarum eſt: no eſſe tanta Ampli-\ntudinis, ipſu B, quantæ ſunt ipſa D, C. Et hoc bene nobis cõfirmat E ipſum: opere iſto Circulari,a B, in Specie E,\n\n80\nM O N A S\n\npromoto. Nam inde nobis emergit V E N E R I S solum Character. Aper-\ntum ergo iam fecimus, Hieroglyphi-\ncis iſtis Syllogiſmis: Ex B, non ſpera-\ndum nobis verum D. Nec fuiſſe primo veram C, in natura B: Vnde non fuit V E R A, L V N A, viua. De V I T A ergo & Motu quoque iam dubitare potes: an vere & Naturaliter, ſic ſe habeant: Erunt tamen, vt iam Pru-\ndentibus Elucidauimus, ad minus A N A L O G I C A quidem, O M N I A, quæ ſimili (de B) dicuntur Phraſi: vt & ſuperius, quæ de C, & D, perſtrin-\nximus breuiter, A N A L O G I C E: Ipſi B, cum ſuis E L E M E N T I S, Proprie conueniunt. Quæ de Arietis etiam Natura adduximus, huic debent ex-\nacte conuenire: cum eandem illius in ſuo capite (licet inuersam) geſtet Figuram: vt & Elementorum eandem Nota.Myſtica, ipſi B adiungitur.\n\nCum\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n81\n\nCum ex hac tamen Anatomia vi-\ndemus, quod ex vnico noſtræ MO-\nNADIS corpore ( tali diſſecto arte )\niſte nouus prodierit TERNARIVS.\nInde, dubitare non poſſumus, Eiuſ-\ncemodi MEMBRA, mutuam inter ſe\namplexura SYMPATHIAM: VNIO-\nNEMQVE MONADICAM ABSO-\nLVTISSIMAM, ſua quaſi ſponte, ad-\nmiſſura: Ita in iſtis MEMBRIS, MA-\nGNETICA virtus eſt vegeta.\n\nHoc denique annotare libuit, (a-\nnimi recreandi gratia:) Quod ipſum\nB, nobis, RVSTICAS, tot litteras ex-\npeditiſſime exhibet, quot Puncta,\nſurſum, conſpicienda in capi-\nte, & quaſi Fronte gerit: iſtas,\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 85, region 5]\n\nſcilicet tres: vt & alias quaſi ſex:(Summatim autem ter tria) RVDES valde & impolitas, fluxiles volubileſque: vt, ex Semicirculis, vno vel pluribus, eaſ-\ndem eſſe factas videatis. Sed, Expertorū\n\nF\n\n82\n\nM O N A S\n\nliterat orum; manibus ineſt firmior Stabiliorque I S T A S F O R M A N D I L I T E R A S Ratio. Myſteriorum in-\nfinítatem, hîc ante oculos habui: ſed volui cum hoc Ludicro, iſta abrum-\npere Theoriam. Haud parum tamẽ me quorundam promouit Cona-\ntus intelligo: Si (priori ſuo Myſtico Situi, reſtituta noſtra M O N A D E. Co-\npolitisq; Artificioſe ſingulis Membris) Saltem moneam eoſdem, horterque: accuratius, N V N C eruëre, Q V I S fuit\nI G N I S ille A R I E T I N V S, T R I P L I C I-\nT A T I S  P R I M Æ. Q V I S ille Æquino-\nctialis noſter. Q V I S in cauſa fuit, quod S O L E X A L T A R I poterat S V-\nP R A  V V L G A R E M  S V V M  G R A D V M:\nCæteraque priora, perplura, S E C V N-\nD I S  S A P I E N T I O R I B V S  P E R-\nC V R R E R E  M E D I T A T I O N I B V S.\nSed nos ad alia nunc properantes, di-\ngito tantum aliis iter indicare, (cui\n\ninſiſtere\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n83\n\ninſiſtere debeant) non amicè ſolum,\nſed etiam fideliſſime volumus: My-\nſteriorum (vt diximus) aliorum ta-\ncentes tamen infinitatem Conſpi-\ncuam.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XXI.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0002","text":"SI, Quod in noſtræ MONADIS Re-\nceſſibus , Interius Latebat Inuo-\nlutum, eſſet in Lucem erutum; com-\nmutatisque vicibus , eiuſdem Partes\nPrimæ , qualiſque Exteriores , Loco\nIncluderentur Medio , Qualis inde\nfieret MONADIS Philoſophica Trāſ-\nformatio , Superius Vidiſtis: Nunc\nvero , Myſticæ MONADIS , aliam\nvobis proponemus Localem Com-\nmutationem:Partibus illis,vnde SV-\nPERIORVM PLANETARVM, Cha\nracteres noſtri Hieroglyphici , ſeſe\nnobis obtulere prius,Surſum hic ere-\nctis: æque ratione,reliquis quidem\ndeinceps Planetis, eum ſingulis Sor-\ntientibus Situm,quem illis Plato ad\nſcribere ſere viſus eſt: Si rite ex\nPoſitione iſta deſumantur. In\nipſo enim Acuminé Arietino,\nCoueniunt Saturnus, Iupiter,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 78, region 5]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Mars:","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0005","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0006","text":"75","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0007","text":"Mars: deinde deſcẽdendo, Crux Ve-\nneri Mercurioq; inſeruit. Sequuntur tandem ipſe Sol, & infima L V N A. Sed hæc alio ſunt ventilanda, loco: Noſtræ tamen M O N A D I S hoſce no-\nlui celare Theſauros Philoſophicos. Sicque unam rationem dare, cur ita M O N A D I S mutari Situm, conſultum duxîmus. Sed, alia, quæ in rem veſtrâ eſſe ſcio, Videte, Auditeq;, de hoc Si-\ntu, maiora: paucisq; explicanda. Di-\nſtribuamus igitur M O N A D E M, (hoc nouo modo Locatam) in Ana-\ntomica Membra B.D.C. Vbi, in illo nouo T E R N AR I O; ipſius D, & C, vel Ruſticis quidem, ſunt no-\ntæ F I G V R Æ. At ille T E R T I V S, qui per B deſignatur, non tam facile a Cunctis cognoſci poteſt. Nec illud","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0008","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 79, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0009","text":"76","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0010","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0011","text":"guidem leuiter eſt conſiderandum:\nillas tria notas FORMAS,D,&C; ſepa-\nratas diuerſasq; ab illo B, oſtendere\nESSENTIAS:Secundo,quod iſtius C,\ncornua, deorſum, quaſi TERRAM\nverſus conuerti conſpiciantur: Et,D\nillius,ea pars quæ ipſam C,illuminat.\nverſus terram, deorſum Scilicet, re-\nſpicit:in cuius ſolius Centro,eſt Viſi-\nbile PVNCTVM:vere TERRESTRE\nEt Quod vtraque Denique D & C,\nad Inferiora magis loca, hic ſuum\nHieroglyphicum faciunt Indicium,\nquam B. Terra autem, Hieroglyphi-\nce, STABILITATEM, & FIXIONEM\nnotare nobis poteſt. Qualia ergo\nſint D,&C,inde,concludendum re-\nlinquo. Vnde etiam Magnum nunc\nnotare SECRETVM, Quiſq; poteſt:\nde Priore SOLE&LVNA, quæ dixi-\nmus,quomodo hinc Interpretationẽ\npleniorem, & maxime neceſſariam,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0012","text":"1.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0013","text":"2.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0014","text":"3.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0015","text":"4.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0016","text":"recipe-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0017","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0018","text":"77","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0019","text":"recipere poſſunt: Illis quidem, vſque\nin hunc locum, ſurſum poſitis: Luna-\nribuſque Cornibus ſurſum eleuatis.\nSed de hoc Satis. TERTII nunc il-\nlius, iuxta noſtrę Hieroglyphicę Ar-\ntis Fundamenta examinemus NA-\nTVRAM. Primo, in Capite geſtare\nvidetur L VNAM DVPLICEM. Vel\nArieté, noſtrum, (ſed inuersum My-\nſtice.) Deinde Elementorum habet\nannexum Hieroglyphicū Signum.\nQuantum ad L VNAM Duplicatam\nattinet: Sic (iuxta Materiam ſubiectā)\nexplicari poteſt: DVPLEX LVNÆ\nGRADVS. De gradibus loquimur il-\nlis,quales Phyſices Periti, QVATVOR\ntantum inter omnes poſſunt inueni-\nre Creatas NATVRAS. Nimirum\nESSE,VIVERE,SENTIRE,&INTEL-\nLIGERE. Primos ergo Duos iſtorum\nGradus, huic ineſſe, annotantes: Sic\ndicemus: LVNA EXISTENS, VIVA","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0020","text":"178","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0021","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0022","text":"Vitam vero Quidam per Motum\ndeſiniunt. MOTVS autem Sex ſunt\nnotiſſimæ Species. CRVX certe quę\nadiuncta eſt: Elementorum hic re-\nquiri Notat Artificium. Præterea, in\niſtis noſtris Theoriis, vt SEMICIR-\nCVLVM, LVNÆ eſſe Hierogly-\nphicum ſæpiſſime tradidimus: Ita &\nIntegrum Circulum, SOLEM ſigni-\nficare: hic autem, duo ſunt Semicir-\nculi; Sed SEPARATI (adcommu-\nne PVNCTVM Copulati tamen)\nqui, ſi apte coniungantur (vt arte\npoſſunt quidem) SOLAREM nobis\nCircularemq; referre poſſunt Pleni-\ntudinem. Ex iſtis ſimul conſideratis,\nſic Summatim, Hieroglyphicè, nos\nhanc proferre poſſe Sententiam pa-\ntet. LVNA EXISTENS VIVA, PER\nELEMENTORVM TRACTANDA\nMAGISTERIVM: HABENS PO-\nTENTIAM, VT SOLAREM REPRÆ-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0023","text":"SENTET","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0024","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0025","text":"79","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0026","text":"SENTET PLENITVDINEM, SVIS\nSIMVL ARTE CONNEXIS SEMI-\nCIRCULIS. Compleatur ergo: Fiatq; ille,(quem diximus) CIRCULVS: vt, per E literam, hic annotauimus. Me-\nmores ergo ſimus, primo hunc SOLAREM GRADVM, non Natura nobis fuiſſe obuium, ſed ARTIFICIA-\nLEM, FACTITIVMQVE iam eſſe: Et eum quidem, nobis ſe obtuliſſe primo aſpectu; & Natura ſua,(videlicet in B) ſuis Partibus Laxis,Fluxis,diſſo lutis; non SOLIDE in Solarem Spe-\nciem Compactis. Deinde horum Se-\nmicirculorum Semidiametrum, non eſſe æqualem Semidiametro D & C (nobis ita natorum,& omnibus No-\ntiſſimorum) ſed Minore multo. Vnde Clarum eſt: no eſſe tanta Ampli-\ntudinis, ipſu B, quantæ ſunt ipſa D, C. Et hoc bene nobis cõfirmat E ipſum: opere iſto Circulari,a B, in Specie E,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0027","text":"80\nM O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0028","text":"promoto. Nam inde nobis emergit V E N E R I S solum Character. Aper-\ntum ergo iam fecimus, Hieroglyphi-\ncis iſtis Syllogiſmis: Ex B, non ſpera-\ndum nobis verum D. Nec fuiſſe primo veram C, in natura B: Vnde non fuit V E R A, L V N A, viua. De V I T A ergo & Motu quoque iam dubitare potes: an vere & Naturaliter, ſic ſe habeant: Erunt tamen, vt iam Pru-\ndentibus Elucidauimus, ad minus A N A L O G I C A quidem, O M N I A, quæ ſimili (de B) dicuntur Phraſi: vt & ſuperius, quæ de C, & D, perſtrin-\nximus breuiter, A N A L O G I C E: Ipſi B, cum ſuis E L E M E N T I S, Proprie conueniunt. Quæ de Arietis etiam Natura adduximus, huic debent ex-\nacte conuenire: cum eandem illius in ſuo capite (licet inuersam) geſtet Figuram: vt & Elementorum eandem Nota.Myſtica, ipſi B adiungitur.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0029","text":"Cum","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0030","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0031","text":"81","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0032","text":"Cum ex hac tamen Anatomia vi-\ndemus, quod ex vnico noſtræ MO-\nNADIS corpore ( tali diſſecto arte )\niſte nouus prodierit TERNARIVS.\nInde, dubitare non poſſumus, Eiuſ-\ncemodi MEMBRA, mutuam inter ſe\namplexura SYMPATHIAM: VNIO-\nNEMQVE MONADICAM ABSO-\nLVTISSIMAM, ſua quaſi ſponte, ad-\nmiſſura: Ita in iſtis MEMBRIS, MA-\nGNETICA virtus eſt vegeta.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0033","text":"Hoc denique annotare libuit, (a-\nnimi recreandi gratia:) Quod ipſum\nB, nobis, RVSTICAS, tot litteras ex-\npeditiſſime exhibet, quot Puncta,\nſurſum, conſpicienda in capi-\nte, & quaſi Fronte gerit: iſtas,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 85, region 5]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0035","text":"ſcilicet tres: vt & alias quaſi ſex:(Summatim autem ter tria) RVDES valde & impolitas, fluxiles volubileſque: vt, ex Semicirculis, vno vel pluribus, eaſ-\ndem eſſe factas videatis. Sed, Expertorū","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0036","text":"F","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0037","text":"82","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0038","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0039","text":"literat orum; manibus ineſt firmior Stabiliorque I S T A S F O R M A N D I L I T E R A S Ratio. Myſteriorum in-\nfinítatem, hîc ante oculos habui: ſed volui cum hoc Ludicro, iſta abrum-\npere Theoriam. Haud parum tamẽ me quorundam promouit Cona-\ntus intelligo: Si (priori ſuo Myſtico Situi, reſtituta noſtra M O N A D E. Co-\npolitisq; Artificioſe ſingulis Membris) Saltem moneam eoſdem, horterque: accuratius, N V N C eruëre, Q V I S fuit\nI G N I S ille A R I E T I N V S, T R I P L I C I-\nT A T I S  P R I M Æ. Q V I S ille Æquino-\nctialis noſter. Q V I S in cauſa fuit, quod S O L E X A L T A R I poterat S V-\nP R A  V V L G A R E M  S V V M  G R A D V M:\nCæteraque priora, perplura, S E C V N-\nD I S  S A P I E N T I O R I B V S  P E R-\nC V R R E R E  M E D I T A T I O N I B V S.\nSed nos ad alia nunc properantes, di-\ngito tantum aliis iter indicare, (cui","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0040","text":"inſiſtere","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0041","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0042","text":"83","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0043","text":"inſiſtere debeant) non amicè ſolum,\nſed etiam fideliſſime volumus: My-\nſteriorum (vt diximus) aliorum ta-\ncentes tamen infinitatem Conſpi-\ncuam.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"6704f44150ac3eb627a1930d85bdebd9c60fbeefecfe72a431341035e47548df","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232048511786Z_7c08a05f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XXI.","source_sha256":"6704f44150ac3eb627a1930d85bdebd9c60fbeefecfe72a431341035e47548df","sha256":"9657b5b721b86b8d4685a1376b86b5df8286ab92c830f245fe01960bd7a9bce9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:20:48.511822+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEORY XXI.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0002","text":"IF that which, in the recesses of our MONAD, lay hidden inwardly, enfolded, were brought forth into the light; and, positions having been exchanged, its Primary Parts, such as were Exterior, were enclosed in the Middle Place, what Philosophical Transformation of the MONAD would thence result, ye have seen above: but now we shall propose to you another Local Transposition of the Mystical MONAD: those Parts from which the Characters of our Hieroglyphics of the SUPERIOR PLANETS first offered themselves to us, being here raised upward: and, by like reasoning, thereafter assigning to the remaining Planets severally that Position which Plato seems almost to ascribe to them: if they be rightly taken from that Position. For at the very Arietine Summit, Saturn, Jupiter,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0003","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 78, region 5]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Mars:","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0005","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0006","text":"75","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0007","text":"Mars: then, descending, the Cross is inserted for Venus and Mercury. Finally follow the Sun itself, and the lowest MOON. But these matters are to be discussed elsewhere: nevertheless, I did not wish to conceal these Philosophical Treasures of our MONAD. And thus we deemed it advisable to give one reason why the Position of the MONAD should be thus changed. But see and hear other and greater matters concerning this Position, which I know to be to your advantage, and which must be explained in few words. Let us therefore distribute the MONAD (placed in this new manner) into the Anatomical Members B. D. C. Where, in that new TERNARY, D and C themselves are familiar FIGURES, even to rustics. But that THIRD, which is denoted by B, cannot so easily be recognized by all. Nor indeed is that","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0008","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 79, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0009","text":"76","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0010","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0011","text":"to be considered lightly: that those three noted FORMS, D and C, separate and different from that B, show ESSENCES: secondly, that the horns of that C are seen to be turned downward, as though toward the EARTH: and that that part of D which illuminates C itself looks downward toward the earth; in the centre of which alone is the Visible POINT: truly TERRESTRIAL. And that, finally, both D and C make their Hieroglyphic indication here toward the lower places rather than does B. Now Earth, hieroglyphically, can denote STABILITY and FIXITY to us. What, therefore, D and C may be, I leave to be concluded thence. Whence anyone can now also note a great SECRET: concerning the former SUN and MOON, of which we have spoken, how they can hence receive a fuller, and most necessary, interpretation,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0012","text":"1.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0013","text":"2.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0014","text":"3.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0015","text":"4.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0016","text":"receive-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0017","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0018","text":"77","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0019","text":"can receive: those, indeed, up to this place having been placed upward, and with the Lunar Horns raised upward. But enough concerning this. Let us now examine the NATURE of that THIRD, according to the Foundations of our Hieroglyphic Art. First, it seems to bear a DOUBLE MOON upon its Head. Or our Aries, (but mystically inverted.) Next, it has attached the Hieroglyphic Sign of the Elements. So far as concerns the Doubled MOON, it can thus be explained (according to the subject matter): A DOUBLE DEGREE OF THE MOON. We speak of those degrees which experts in Natural Philosophy can find to be only four among all created NATURES. Namely, TO BE, TO LIVE, TO SENSE, and TO UNDERSTAND. Therefore, noting that the first Two of these Degrees are present in this, we shall say thus: THE MOON EXISTING, LIVING","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0020","text":"178","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0021","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0022","text":"But some define Life by Motion. Now there are six most well-known Species of MOTION. Certainly, the CROSS which is joined to it signifies that the Artifice of the Elements is here required. Moreover, in these our Theories, we have very often taught that the SEMICIRCLE is the Hieroglyphic of the MOON: so too, that the entire Circle signifies the SUN: but here there are two Semicircles; yet SEPARATE (nevertheless joined at a common POINT), which, if they be fittingly joined together (as indeed they can be by art), can represent to us a SOLAR and Circular Plenitude. From these things considered together, it is evident that we can thus set forth, summarily and hieroglyphically, this Proposition. THE MOON, EXISTING, LIVING, TO BE DEALT WITH THROUGH THE MASTERY OF THE ELEMENTS: HAVING THE POWER THAT IT MAY REPRE-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0023","text":"SENT","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0023"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0024","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0025","text":"79","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0026","text":"FEELS FULLNESS, with its semicircles\nat the same time connected by art. Let it therefore be completed: and let that (which we have called) CIRCLE come to be: as we have here marked it by the letter E. Let us therefore remember, first, that this SOLAR DEGREE was not encountered by us in Nature, but is now ARTIFICIAL AND MADE: and indeed, that it presented itself to us at first sight; and by its Nature (namely in B), with its Parts Loose, Fluid, dissolved; not COMPACTED SOLIDLY into a Solar Spe-\ncies. Secondly, that the Semidiameter of these Semicircles is not equal to the Semidiameter of D and C (born thus to us, and most well known to all), but much Smaller. Whence it is Clear: that B itself is not of so great an Extent as D and C themselves are. And E itself well confirms this to us: by that Circular operation, from B, advanced into the Species E,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0026"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0027","text":"80\nM O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0027"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0028","text":"there arises for us thence the Character of V E N U S alone. We have therefore now made plain, by these Hieroglyphic Syllogisms: From B, a true D is not to be hoped for. Nor was there at first a true C in the nature of B: whence there was not a T R U E, living M O O N. You may therefore now also doubt concerning L I F E and Motion: whether they are truly and Naturally so disposed: yet, as we have now elucidated for the Prudent, at the least, A N A L O G I C A L indeed are A L L things which are spoken in a similar phrase (concerning B): just as also those things which above we briefly touched upon concerning C and D, A N A L O G I C A L L Y, properly suit B itself with its E L E M E N T S. Those things also which we have adduced concerning the Nature of Aries ought exactly to agree with this: since it bears the same Figure of that one in its head (although inverted): and likewise the same Mystical Mark of the Elements is joined to B itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0028"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0029","text":"When","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0029"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0030","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0030"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0031","text":"81","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0031"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0032","text":"When nevertheless from this Anatomy we see that, from the single body of our M O N A D (thus dissected by art), this new T E R N A R Y has proceeded. Thence we cannot doubt that MEMBERS of this sort will embrace a mutual S Y M P A T H Y among themselves, and will, as it were of their own accord, admit a MOST ABSOLUTE MONADIC U N I O N: thus in these MEMBERS the M A G N E T I C virtue is vigorous.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0032"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0033","text":"Finally, I wished to note this (for the sake of refreshing the mind): that B itself most readily presents to us as many RUSTIC letters as it bears Points, to be beheld above, upon its head, and as it were its Forehead: namely,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0033"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 85, region 5]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0034"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0035","text":"those three: as also another, as it were six: (but in sum, thrice three) very ROUGH and unpolished, fluid and turning: so that you may see them to have been made from one or more Semicircles. But, of Experts","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0035"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232048511786Z_7c08a05f:DISPLAY-0036","text":"F\n\n82","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0036","RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0037"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0038","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0038"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0039","text":"in letters, a firmer and more stable method of F O R M I N G T H O S E L E T T E R S is in the hands. I had before my eyes an infinity of Mysteries here: but I wished to break off those matters with this Sportive Theory. Yet I understand that the endeavor of certain persons has advanced me not a little: If, our M O N A D restored to its former Mystical Position, and its individual Members artificially joined together, I should at least admonish and exhort those same persons to investigate more carefully, N O W, W H O that A R I E T I N E F I R E of the F I R S T T R I P L I C I T Y was. W H O that Equinoctial one of ours was. W H O was the cause that the S U N could be E X A L T E D A B O V E I T S C O M M O N D E G R E E: and to run through very many other preceding matters with S E C O N D, W I S E R M E D I T A T I O N S. But we, now hastening to other matters, wish only to point out the way to others with the finger (upon which","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0039"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0040","text":"they ought to tread","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0040"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0041","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0041"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0042","text":"83","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0042"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0043","text":"they ought to tread), not only amicably, but also most faithfully: nevertheless keeping silent, as we have said, concerning the conspicuous infinity of other Mysteries.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_17:DISPLAY-0043"]}],"source_digest":"a9f17ecba42f61fd3064a37474d18ab793612bfc62282c131d6ae715be96968b","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XXI."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XXI.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18","title":"THEOR. XXII.","order":23,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_18","text":"THEOR. XXII.\n\nNOndum noſtræ MONADIS eſſe\nexhauſta Myſteria, facile lique-\nbit. Si ſecretiora quædam ARTIS\nSANCTÆ Vaſa (omnino Cabali-\nſtica illa quidem) Solis Initiatis Re-\nuelanda; ex eiuſdem MONADIS\nofficina caute deſumpta, Veſtræ Se-\nrenitati Regiæ, nunc exhibuerim\nſpectanda. OMNI ergo NEXV\nnoſtræ MONADIS Sapienter DISSO-\nLVTO, ſingulis partibus (diſtinctionis\ngratia) literales addamus Notas: pro-\nut hic factû videris. Monemus ergo,\na, eſſe Vas quoddam Artificiale, ex A\n& B: cum vtriſque communi, & iam\n\nF 2\n\n84\n\nM O N A S\n\nManifeſtãdo\nSEMIDIAME-\nTRO ) ipſa\nquidem M,\nfactum: Et,\nab Alphabeti\nGræci, Prima,\nhac litera, ſo-\nla partium lo\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 88, region 4]\n\ncali Metatheſi, diverſum: vt Videtis.\nEx Recta enim, Circulo & Semicir-\nculo, Veram illius, Myſticamq; iam\nnos primi docemus, Symmetriam (ſi\ncet ſupra etiam monuimus, ex Circu-\nlo & Semicirculo eandem fieri poſſe:\nomnia tamen in idem recidunt pro-\npoſitum Myſticum) At, λ, & δ:\nPrimum quidem, aliorum ſunt Va-\nſorum quaſi imagines: (λ, quidem\nV I T R E I.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 88, region 6]\n\nautem, Terrei.) Sed, ſe-\ncundo in loco, λ, & δ, nos memores\nreddere poſſunt, cuiuſdam Piſtilli &\n\nMortarii,\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n85\n\nMortari,ex Materia (vetere) tali præ-\nparandorum,Vt cum iisdem Marga-\nritas Artificiales non perforatas, La-\nminas Cryſtallinas, Beryllinaſque:\nChryſolythos,Rubinos deinde pre-\ntioſos: Carbunculos & alios Rariſſi-\nmos Lapides Artificiales in Pulueres\nſubtiliſſimos Conteramus.Denique\nquod cum ω notatum videtis, Vaſ-\nculum eſt,Myſteriorum Pleniſſimum:\n& ab ipſa Vltima Alphabeti Græci li-\ntera, (ad ſuam primam inſtituta My-\nſtagogiam nunc reſtituta) vel ſola\npartium manifeſta Metatheſi locali\ndiſcrepans: ex duobus & illa quoque\nconſtante Semicirculis. De Vulgari-\nbus præterea Neceſſariis Vaſorum,\ntum figuris, tum (vnde fieri debent)\nMateriis,non eſt neceſſe hoc loco, vt\nverba faciamus. Hoc tamen erit co-\nſiderandum,ω, ſui Muneris obeundi\ncaptare Occaſionem, ex Secretiſſi-\n\nF\n3\n\n86\n\nM O N A S\n\nnobreuiſſimoque Spiraculi A R T I-\nF I C I O; Et ([illegible Hebrew])\n[illegible Hebrew] auro uinium [illegible Hebrew]\nTyronibus O P E R I S expeditiſſi-\nmum elíciet Primordiale Specimen;\nInterim dum S V B T I L I O R A Præ-\nparandi, artificioſior illis innoteſcat\nVia. At in λ, vitreo (In præcipui ſui\nofficii functione,) Aër omnis exter-\nnus , Ventuſve damnum adferret\nmagnum.\n\nω, autem, O M N I V M eſt H O R A R V M\nH O M O. Πόρισμα.\n\nΤῆς ἱερᾶς Τέχνης, Quis iam non potest\nſubodorari, ſuauiſſimos & ſalu-\nberrimos Fructus: vel ex iſtarum (di-\nco) duarum tantum literarum ena-\nſcentes Myſterio? Quorum aliquos\nquaſi in ſpeculo videndos, propius a-\nliquantulum ex noſtris H E S P E R I-\nD V M H O R T I S) adducemus: Nihil,\nextra noſtram M O N A D E M, in me-\n\ndium\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n87\n\ndiſſerentes. Ipſa enim quæ in Alpha\napparet Recta Linea, omologa illi eſt, ex\npoſtremæ Anatomia, Crucis parte ea,\nquæ Litera M, notatur: reliqua etiam,\ninde patere poteſt, vnde huc veniant.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 91, region 4]\n\nK 4\n\n88\n\nM O N A S\n\nHis paucis, tales me ſcio non ἀ-\nφορμὰς, ſolum, ſed Apodixes dare illis, quibus Igneus intus viget gliſcitque Vigor, & cœleſtis Origo: vt facile iam magno Democrito aurem præbeāt: τὸ τῆς Ψυχῆς prædicenti, ἅμα, ἢ πάντως μώ-\nχθῳ λυπηειον κατασκευάσαι βελομένοις, non Μυσικὸν eſſe hoc Dogma, ſed Μυστικὸν, & Arcanum: vt & illi, qui aſſerunt, quod λόγῳ δημιουργῷ κόσμῳ μεθοδοῦεται: ἵνα ὁ θεό-\nφρων ὁ θεωρητὴς ἄνθρωπος, διὰ τῆς εὐθείας ἐργα-\nσίας, τῇ μυστικῷ λόγῳ μάθῃ.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XXII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0002","text":"NOndum noſtræ MONADIS eſſe\nexhauſta Myſteria, facile lique-\nbit. Si ſecretiora quædam ARTIS\nSANCTÆ Vaſa (omnino Cabali-\nſtica illa quidem) Solis Initiatis Re-\nuelanda; ex eiuſdem MONADIS\nofficina caute deſumpta, Veſtræ Se-\nrenitati Regiæ, nunc exhibuerim\nſpectanda. OMNI ergo NEXV\nnoſtræ MONADIS Sapienter DISSO-\nLVTO, ſingulis partibus (diſtinctionis\ngratia) literales addamus Notas: pro-\nut hic factû videris. Monemus ergo,\na, eſſe Vas quoddam Artificiale, ex A\n& B: cum vtriſque communi, & iam","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0003","text":"F 2","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0004","text":"84","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0005","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Manifeſtãdo\nSEMIDIAME-\nTRO ) ipſa\nquidem M,\nfactum: Et,\nab Alphabeti\nGræci, Prima,\nhac litera, ſo-\nla partium lo","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0007","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 88, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0008","text":"cali Metatheſi, diverſum: vt Videtis.\nEx Recta enim, Circulo & Semicir-\nculo, Veram illius, Myſticamq; iam\nnos primi docemus, Symmetriam (ſi\ncet ſupra etiam monuimus, ex Circu-\nlo & Semicirculo eandem fieri poſſe:\nomnia tamen in idem recidunt pro-\npoſitum Myſticum) At, λ, & δ:\nPrimum quidem, aliorum ſunt Va-\nſorum quaſi imagines: (λ, quidem\nV I T R E I.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 88, region 6]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0010","text":"autem, Terrei.) Sed, ſe-\ncundo in loco, λ, & δ, nos memores\nreddere poſſunt, cuiuſdam Piſtilli &","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0011","text":"Mortarii,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0012","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0013","text":"85","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0014","text":"Mortari,ex Materia (vetere) tali præ-\nparandorum,Vt cum iisdem Marga-\nritas Artificiales non perforatas, La-\nminas Cryſtallinas, Beryllinaſque:\nChryſolythos,Rubinos deinde pre-\ntioſos: Carbunculos & alios Rariſſi-\nmos Lapides Artificiales in Pulueres\nſubtiliſſimos Conteramus.Denique\nquod cum ω notatum videtis, Vaſ-\nculum eſt,Myſteriorum Pleniſſimum:\n& ab ipſa Vltima Alphabeti Græci li-\ntera, (ad ſuam primam inſtituta My-\nſtagogiam nunc reſtituta) vel ſola\npartium manifeſta Metatheſi locali\ndiſcrepans: ex duobus & illa quoque\nconſtante Semicirculis. De Vulgari-\nbus præterea Neceſſariis Vaſorum,\ntum figuris, tum (vnde fieri debent)\nMateriis,non eſt neceſſe hoc loco, vt\nverba faciamus. Hoc tamen erit co-\nſiderandum,ω, ſui Muneris obeundi\ncaptare Occaſionem, ex Secretiſſi-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0015","text":"F\n3","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0016","text":"86","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0017","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0018","text":"nobreuiſſimoque Spiraculi A R T I-\nF I C I O; Et ([illegible Hebrew])\n[illegible Hebrew] auro uinium [illegible Hebrew]\nTyronibus O P E R I S expeditiſſi-\nmum elíciet Primordiale Specimen;\nInterim dum S V B T I L I O R A Præ-\nparandi, artificioſior illis innoteſcat\nVia. At in λ, vitreo (In præcipui ſui\nofficii functione,) Aër omnis exter-\nnus , Ventuſve damnum adferret\nmagnum.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0019","text":"ω, autem, O M N I V M eſt H O R A R V M\nH O M O. Πόρισμα.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0020","text":"Τῆς ἱερᾶς Τέχνης, Quis iam non potest\nſubodorari, ſuauiſſimos & ſalu-\nberrimos Fructus: vel ex iſtarum (di-\nco) duarum tantum literarum ena-\nſcentes Myſterio? Quorum aliquos\nquaſi in ſpeculo videndos, propius a-\nliquantulum ex noſtris H E S P E R I-\nD V M H O R T I S) adducemus: Nihil,\nextra noſtram M O N A D E M, in me-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0021","text":"dium","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0022","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0023","text":"87","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0024","text":"diſſerentes. Ipſa enim quæ in Alpha\napparet Recta Linea, omologa illi eſt, ex\npoſtremæ Anatomia, Crucis parte ea,\nquæ Litera M, notatur: reliqua etiam,\ninde patere poteſt, vnde huc veniant.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0025","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 91, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0026","text":"K 4","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0027","text":"88","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0028","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0029","text":"His paucis, tales me ſcio non ἀ-\nφορμὰς, ſolum, ſed Apodixes dare illis, quibus Igneus intus viget gliſcitque Vigor, & cœleſtis Origo: vt facile iam magno Democrito aurem præbeāt: τὸ τῆς Ψυχῆς prædicenti, ἅμα, ἢ πάντως μώ-\nχθῳ λυπηειον κατασκευάσαι βελομένοις, non Μυσικὸν eſſe hoc Dogma, ſed Μυστικὸν, & Arcanum: vt & illi, qui aſſerunt, quod λόγῳ δημιουργῷ κόσμῳ μεθοδοῦεται: ἵνα ὁ θεό-\nφρων ὁ θεωρητὴς ἄνθρωπος, διὰ τῆς εὐθείας ἐργα-\nσίας, τῇ μυστικῷ λόγῳ μάθῃ.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"c7da20880fce6956cd241ae59de38a718daafe414aeafbc2021d27d6832103d4","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232123855792Z_491a72c8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XXII.","source_sha256":"c7da20880fce6956cd241ae59de38a718daafe414aeafbc2021d27d6832103d4","sha256":"27f9321efd67e48f003241ad35bfef2394bcebf281a2700ab2bd03da2b909c12","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:21:23.855858+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOREM XXII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0002","text":"That the Mysteries of our MONAD have not yet been exhausted will readily be clear. If I should now exhibit for the contemplation of Your Royal Serenity certain more secret Vessels of the SACRED ART (indeed wholly Cabalistic ones), to be revealed only to the Initiated, cautiously taken from the workshop of the same MONAD. Therefore, when EVERY BOND of our MONAD has been Wisely DISSOLVED, let us add literal marks to the individual parts (for the sake of distinction): as you will see done here. We warn, therefore, that a is a certain artificial Vessel, from A and B: with what is common to both, and already","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0003","text":"F 2","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0004","text":"84","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0005","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0006","text":"by making manifest the SEMIDIAMETER) itself indeed made M, and differing from the first letter of the Greek Alphabet by this letter alone, through a local transposition of the parts: as you see.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0007","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 88, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0008","text":"For from a Straight Line, a Circle, and a Semicircle, we are the first now to teach its true and mystical Symmetry (although we also warned above that the same can be made from a Circle and a Semicircle: yet all things fall back upon the same mystical proposition). But λ and δ are, first indeed, as it were images of other Vessels: (λ, indeed, of GLASS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0009","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 88, region 6]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0010","text":"But δ, of Earth.) Yet, in the second place, λ and δ can remind us of a certain Pestle and","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0011","text":"Mortar,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0012","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0013","text":"85","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0014","text":"Mortar, for preparing such materials (of the old sort), so that with these we may grind into the most subtle powders artificial unperforated Pearls, crystalline and beryl-like Plates; then precious Chrysoliths and Rubies; Carbuncles and other very rare artificial Stones. Finally, that which you see marked with ω is a very small Vessel, most full of Mysteries; and differing from the very last letter of the Greek Alphabet (now restored to its first instituted mystagogy) solely through a manifest local transposition of its parts: it too consisting of two Semicircles. Moreover, concerning the ordinary necessities of Vessels, both their shapes and the Materials (from which they ought to be made), there is no need for us to speak here. Yet this must be considered: that ω may seize an opportunity of performing its Office, through the most secret and shortest contrivance of a little aperture,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0015","text":"F\n3","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0016","text":"86","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0017","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0018","text":"and ([illegible Hebrew])\n[illegible Hebrew] gold wine [illegible Hebrew]\nwill elicit a most ready Primary Specimen for Novices of the WORK; meanwhile, while a more ingenious Way of preparing the MORE SUBTLE things becomes known to them. But in the glass λ (in the performance of its chief office), all external Air, or Wind, would bring great damage.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0019","text":"But ω is the MAN FOR ALL HOURS. Corollary.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0020","text":"Of the sacred Art, who now cannot scent the most sweet and healthful Fruits, growing even from the Mystery, I say, of those two letters alone? We shall bring forward some of them, as it were to be viewed in a mirror, a little more closely from our GARDEN OF THE HESPERIDES; saying nothing, outside our MONAD, in the","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0021","text":"midst","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0022","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0023","text":"87","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0023"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0024","text":"The Straight Line itself which appears in Alpha is homologous to that part of the Cross, from the anatomy of the latter, which is marked with the letter M: the rest also can thence be clear, whence they come hither.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0025","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 91, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0026","text":"K 4","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0026"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0027","text":"88","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0027"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0028","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0028"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0029","text":"By these few things, I know that I give such persons not ἀφορμάς alone, but Apodixes, to those in whom an ardent Vigor flourishes and grows, and a heavenly Origin: so that they may now readily lend an ear to the great Democritus, proclaiming concerning the Soul, at once, or altogether, to those wishing to prepare a painful toil, that this Dogma is not μυσικόν, but μυστικόν, and Arcane: as also to those who assert that the cosmos is methodized by a demiurgic λόγος: in order that the god-minded contemplative man, through straight operation, may learn by the mystical λόγος.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_18:DISPLAY-0029"]}],"source_digest":"8590cabfd01a93981abca3502c5e0384e4493b704ec69e1deb676b2fcead63a9","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XXII."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XXII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19","title":"T H E O R. XXIII.","order":24,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_19","text":"T H E O R.  XXIII.\n\nSYmmetrias, iam, in noſtra MONADIS Conſtructione Hieroglyphica, a nobis obſeruatas: & ab illis, qui in Annulis, Sigillisve eandem geſta-\nre, vel aliter habere, gratum erit, ob-\nſeruandas: accurate annotatas hic ex-\nhibemus. In Nomine IESV CHRI-\nSTI, pro nobis CRVCI, affixi (cuius Spiritus celeriter hæc per me Scribe-\ntis, Calamum tantum, eſſe Me, &\n\nOpto,\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n89\n\nOpto, & Spero.) ExELEMENTO-\nRVM noſtra CRVCE, omnes iſtas\nnunc petemus Menſuras. Vel hæc\nquidem (iuxta PROPOSITI ANGV-\nMENTI MATERIAM) ratione:\nQuod, ſub Cælo LVNÆ, quidquid\nſuæ Generationis capit Exordium,\nvel ex QVATVOR Elementis eſt\ncoagmentatum: vel Elementaris ipſa\nquidem eſt ESSENTIA: Idq; mo-\ndis variis, non Vulgariter cognitis.\nEt quia in nulla re Creata, Elementa\nipſa, in Æquali ſunt Proportione, vel\nvirtute: Arte tamen ad Æqualitate,\nin quibusdam (vt Sophinorum) re-\nbus, reduci poſſunt: in CRVCE no-\nſtra, Æquales & non Æquales con-\nſtituimus partes. Quod, alia ratione,\nIdem & Diverſum: ſiue Vnum &\nPlura, nominare poſſumus. CRV-\nCIS æquilateræ, ( vt ſupra monui-\nmus ) in Secreto, admittentes Pro-\n\n90\n\nM O N A S\n\nProprietatem. At, Si SYMMETRI-\nARVM hîc poſitarum, rationes (quas\ntenemus) ſingulas, in medium ad-\nduceremus, vel aliter, quàm (Sapien-\ntibus) abundè ſatis, per totum ſeci-\nmus opuſculum, demonſtraremus\ncauſas; Propoſiti noſtri, Limites, no-\nbis, haud temere praeſcriptos, trans-\nliremus.\n\nAccepto,in plano,Puncto aliquo:\nVeluti A: per idem,vtrinq; duca-\ntur Recta ſatis longa: quæ ſit C,A,\nK. & ſuper lineam K,C,a Puncto A,\nerigatur Perpendicularis: Vtrinq; ad\nſufficientem producta Longitudine\n(in Infinitum,ſolent dicere Geome-\ntræ; bene,incommoda præcauentes)\nQuæ admittatur eſſe D A E. Jam\nin A K; accipiatur Punctum, vſili-\nbet; & ſit B. Habita proportionum nunc\nA,B,(noſtri ſcilicet operis commu-\nni Menſura) huius, Tripla capiatur, ab\n\nA ver-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n91\n\nA verſus C: & pona-\ntur eſſe AC. Ipſius A\nB, Dupla fiat AE. Et\nDupla ipſius AB, ſit\nAD. Ita quod tota\nDE, ſit ipſius AB,\nQuadrupla. Sic ergo\nnoſtram CRVCEM\nELEMENTALEM\nconſecimus. Ex AB,\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 95, region 4]\n\nAC AD, & AE. Linearum Scilicet QVATERNARIO. Nunc, ex BK, reſecetur recta, æqualis ipſi AD: & ſit BI. Centro I, & Interuallo IB, deſcribatur Circulus; qui ſit BR: ſecans rectam AK in puncto R. A puncto R, verſus K, reſcindatur recta æqualis ipſi AB; & ſit RK. Ad punctum K, educatur vtrinque, (ad angulos rectos, cum ipſa AK) Sufficientis lo-\ngitudinis lineæ rectæ: quæ ſit P, K, F. Ab ipſo K, puncto, verſus F, reſecetur\n\n92\n\nM O N A S\n\nrecta, ipſi A D æqualis: Et ſit K, F.\nCentro deinde K, & interuallo K F:\ndeſcribatur Semicirculus F, L, P, ita\nquod F, K, P, ſit eiusdem Diameter.\nTandem ad punctum C, ipſi recta\nA, C, ducatur Perpendicularis, vtrin-\nque, ad longitudinem ſufficientem\nextenſa: & ſit O, C, Q. Poſtea, ex linea\nC, Q, & ad punctum C, accipiatur\nRecta, æqualis A, B, lineæ: Et ſit C,\nM. Centro M, & interſtitio M, C, de-\nſcribatur Semicirculus C, H, O, cuius\nDiameter ſit C, M, O. Et ſimili deni-\nque ratione, ex C, Q, recta, & ad Pun-\nctum C, reſecetur linea æqualis ipſi\nA, B: & ſit C, N. Centro igitur N, &\nlongitudine N, C, fiat Semicirculus,\nC, G, Q. Cuius, C N Q ſit Diameter.\nIam Aſſertiones requisitas omnes, in\nnoſtra M O N A D E, S Y M M E T R I-\nA S, explicatas, deſcriptasque eſſe.\n    Monere tamen Mechanicum li-\n\nbet:\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n93\n\nbet: C,K, totam lineam, nouem eſſe\ntalium partium , qualium , noſtra\nF V N D A M E N T A L I S, A B, vna\neſt. Vnde alia via , ille ad hoc idem o-\npus abſoluendum accedere poteſt. Deinde Diametros, Semidiametroſ-\nque omnes, obſcuris hic ( vt loquun-\ntur Mechanici) lineis deſignari debe-\nre. Nec vllum viſibile relinquendum C E N T R V M: excepto Centro So-\nlari: quod, hic, litera I, notatum videt. Literas que adiungẽdas nullas, Tum ad Ornatum, (non Neceſſitatem ali-\nquam Myſticam a nobis ea ratione, iam conſiderandam) Peripheriæ So-\nlari, Latitudinem Superficialem (in-\ntrinſecus parallelo vno deſcripto) Me-\nchanicus adiicere poteſt. Parallelorũ vero diſtantia, per quartã quintamve partem, A, B, vel circiter, fieri poteſt. Lunari aute, illã tribuere Specie, qua ſolet Prima, poſt ſuã cum Sole Con-\n\niunctio-\n\n194\n\nM O N A S\n\niunctionem, in Cælo Appārere: vi-\ndelicet Corniculata admodù. Quod fiet, ſi a K puncto, verſus R, accipiatur illa, (quâ diximus) Quarta, quin-\ntæve pars lineæ A B: & ſuper eius lineæ fine, tanquam Centro, Semidia-\nmetro vero Lunari, trahatur iſta ſe-\ncunda Peripheriæ pars, ad vtrunque prioris Semicirculi contactum niti-\ndum. Simile quid ad M, & N, pun-\ncta, fieri poteſt: erectis ibi Perpendi-\ncularibus: in quibus pars, ipſius A B, ſexta, vel minor accipiatur: vbi, facto Centro, prioribus au-\ntem M, C, & N, C, Se-\nmidiametris, ducantur\nextrinſecus, illi ſecundi,\nquaſi Semicirculi. Per\nipſas denique, noſtræ\nCrucis Rectas, vtrinque\npoſſunt Parallelæ pro-\ntrahi, a mediis per octa-\nuam, vel decimam par-\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 98, region 4]\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n95\n\ntem ipſius A,B, diſtantes: Ita vt no-\nſtra CRVX, ex QVATVOR Super\nperficiebus quaſi Linearibus, ea ra-\ntione conficiatur: quarum latitudo,\nſit quarta vel quinta pars ipſius AB,\nrectæ. Hæc Ornamenta, appoſita fi-\ngura,volui aliquo modo adumbrare.\nQuæ omnia,vnuſquiſque, pro ſua a-\nnimi ſententia, facere poteſt: modo\ninterea, noſtris Myſticis SYMME-\nTRIIS, nulla (vel minima) inferatur\niniuria: Ne, ea quidem negligentia,\ntemporis tandem progreſſu, vera-\nrum iſtarum (& maxime neceſſaria-\nrum) Commenſurationum Hiero-\nglyphicarum perturbetur, pereatue\nDiſciplina noua: longe amplior Ma-\niorque quam hoc libello,eandem vel\npotuimus, vel voluimus quidem ex-\nplicare. Vt Temporis Filia, DEI NV-\nTV, docebit VERITAS.\n\n96\n\nM O N A S\n\nAT, quæ cuiuis eſſe obuia poſſunt, in iſtis neceſſariæ MONADIS Sym-\nmetriis ſeſe exercet, Methodice iam quædam, ob oculos ponemus. Pri-\nmum quidem ordientes, a noſtræ CRVCIS, Linearum QVATERNARIO: eo habito reſpectu, quo, QVATVOR eſſe Lineas, ſimpliciter enuntiare, quis poteſt. Deinde de Ea-\nrundem linearum QVATERNARIO prout peculiarem, Myſticamq́; alio modo habent partitionem, & rationem. Tertio, Numeris, quos vel iſto loco, vel ex aliis, per totum libellum, Theoriis, artificioſe elicuimus, vtilia quædam a Deo in NATVRA, eſſe deſtinata Oſficia, nonnullis mon-\nſtrabimus exemplis: aliaque oppor-\ntunis inferemus locis: quæ fructum haud exiguum ferent, probe in-\ntellecta: hæcque breuiſſime abſoluemus.\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n97\n\nQVATERNARII PYTHA-\nGORICI.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 101, region 4]\n\nOmnis poſ-\nſibilis Me-\ntacheſis, 24.\n\nSumma Py-\nthagorica,\n—— 10.\n\nOmnimo-\nda partium\nadditio, dat\n30.\n\nNoſter Matatheſeos Canon.\n\nNaturali ordine, a Prima Mona-\nde, deſcriptis quotcunque Nu-\nmeris: Si a Primo ad Vltimum, fiat\nContinuata multiplicatio: vt, Primi\nin Secundum producti in Tertium:\nilliuſque producti in Quartum: ſi-\nmilique modo ad vltimum: Produ-\nctum vltimum, omnem Poſſibilem\n\nG\n\n93\n\nM O N A S\n\nMetatheſin in illis tot locis, determi-\nnat. Pariſque ratione, in quibuſcun-\nque, tot diuersis rebus: Hanc ego O-\nperationem, tibi (Q R E X) pluri-\nmun Commendo; tum in omni\nNaturæ examinatione, tum in aliis\nReipubl. Negotiis vtiliſſimam. hac\n    ego in Hebræorum. Tziruph.\n    (ſiue Thmura) cum ma-\n        xima voluptate,\n            vti ſoleo.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 102, region 4]\n\nQVA-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n29\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 103, region 3]\n\nNon ſum Euclidem Neſcius, perplures a-\nlios, ex QVATERNARII, Arithmetica Virtute, & FORMALITATE, in lucem ad-\nſerri potuiſſe Numeros. Sed qui ISTIS, Naturæ euolui, illuſtrarique obſcuritatem ma-\ngnam, non deprehenderit: maiori eorum mul-\ntitudine, obtundi ſuum, non acuſſentiret in-\ngenium. Noſtris ergo Numeris (vt ſumus\n\nG 2\n\n100\n\nM O N A S\n\npolliciti) quantum inſit Auctorita-\ntis, in ELEMENTIS PONDERAN-\nDIS, in TEMPORVM MENSVRIS\ndeſiniendis, Denique in Rerum Po-\nteſtati & Virtuti, certis præſcriben-\ndis GRADIBVS, ex ſequen-\ntibus id perpendendum ex-\nhibemus Schema-\ntibus.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 104, region 4]\n\nNume-\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n101\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 105, region 3]\n\nG 3\n\n102\n\nM O N A S\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 106, region 3]\n\nEx.\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A. 103\n\nEX iſtis Schematibus, plura elici\npoſſunt: (ſi penitius conſideren-\ntur) quam apertis par eſt proferre ver-\nbis. Hoc tamen præ cæteris monendus\nſingulare vnum, (a nobis etiam pri-\nmis vna cum tota hac noua euulga-\ntum arte) Rationem hic in medio eſ-\nſe poſitam, ob quam, QVATERNAR-\nIVS, vel DENARIVS, Nu-\nmerationibus finem imponit quen-\ndam: eamque cauſam quam attulere\nMaiores noſtri, non fuiſſe abſolutam\nexactamque aſſerimus: ſed iſtam qua\nnunc narrabimus.\n\nPoſtquam iſta MONAS, eſt\nſibi integre, plenèque Phyſice-\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 4]\n\nque Reſtituta, (tum quidem eſt\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 6]\n\nMONAS, VNITISSIMA,\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 8]\n\nMagorumque iudicata VNITAS)\nneque in NATVRÆ, neque vllius\nARTIS eſt poteſtate, EANDEM\nSÆPIVS QVAM QVATER,\n\nper\n\nG 4\n\n104\n\nM O N A S\n\nSupercæleſtes Reuolutiones, ad Pro-\ngreſſum vllum, MOTVMVE facien-\ndum impellere:(Ac inde progignitur\nIlle, quem nos ob eminentiam\nſuam, ſic notari volumus,) Idq;\nea de cauſa, quod nec in Eleme-\ntali mundo, nec Cæleſti, nec Sv-\nPERCÆLESTI, ſit aliqua Potestas,\nCREATA INFLVENTIALIS: Qua,\ntunc, non fuerit abſolutiſſime Ditata\n& Dotata.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 108, region 4]\n\nCuius, hunc verum Effectum,\nQVATVOR ſimul (olim) Philoſo-\nphantes Clariſſimi Viri, Opere ſunt\nconſecuti: Vnde, diu, Maximo Rei\nMiraculo Attoniti, Tandem ad Dei\nOpt.Max. Canendas, prædicandaſq;\nLaudes, ſe totos, deinceps conuerte-\nbant. Qui, ea ratione, illis, tantam Sa-\npientiam, & ſuper CREATVRAS\ncæteras, Potentiam, Imperiumque\nfuiſſet Largitus ampliſſimum.\n\nTHEOR.\n\nHIEROGLYPHICA.\n\n109","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R.  XXIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0002","text":"SYmmetrias, iam, in noſtra MONADIS Conſtructione Hieroglyphica, a nobis obſeruatas: & ab illis, qui in Annulis, Sigillisve eandem geſta-\nre, vel aliter habere, gratum erit, ob-\nſeruandas: accurate annotatas hic ex-\nhibemus. In Nomine IESV CHRI-\nSTI, pro nobis CRVCI, affixi (cuius Spiritus celeriter hæc per me Scribe-\ntis, Calamum tantum, eſſe Me, &","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Opto,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0005","text":"89","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Opto, & Spero.) ExELEMENTO-\nRVM noſtra CRVCE, omnes iſtas\nnunc petemus Menſuras. Vel hæc\nquidem (iuxta PROPOSITI ANGV-\nMENTI MATERIAM) ratione:\nQuod, ſub Cælo LVNÆ, quidquid\nſuæ Generationis capit Exordium,\nvel ex QVATVOR Elementis eſt\ncoagmentatum: vel Elementaris ipſa\nquidem eſt ESSENTIA: Idq; mo-\ndis variis, non Vulgariter cognitis.\nEt quia in nulla re Creata, Elementa\nipſa, in Æquali ſunt Proportione, vel\nvirtute: Arte tamen ad Æqualitate,\nin quibusdam (vt Sophinorum) re-\nbus, reduci poſſunt: in CRVCE no-\nſtra, Æquales & non Æquales con-\nſtituimus partes. Quod, alia ratione,\nIdem & Diverſum: ſiue Vnum &\nPlura, nominare poſſumus. CRV-\nCIS æquilateræ, ( vt ſupra monui-\nmus ) in Secreto, admittentes Pro-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0007","text":"90","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0008","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0009","text":"Proprietatem. At, Si SYMMETRI-\nARVM hîc poſitarum, rationes (quas\ntenemus) ſingulas, in medium ad-\nduceremus, vel aliter, quàm (Sapien-\ntibus) abundè ſatis, per totum ſeci-\nmus opuſculum, demonſtraremus\ncauſas; Propoſiti noſtri, Limites, no-\nbis, haud temere praeſcriptos, trans-\nliremus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Accepto,in plano,Puncto aliquo:\nVeluti A: per idem,vtrinq; duca-\ntur Recta ſatis longa: quæ ſit C,A,\nK. & ſuper lineam K,C,a Puncto A,\nerigatur Perpendicularis: Vtrinq; ad\nſufficientem producta Longitudine\n(in Infinitum,ſolent dicere Geome-\ntræ; bene,incommoda præcauentes)\nQuæ admittatur eſſe D A E. Jam\nin A K; accipiatur Punctum, vſili-\nbet; & ſit B. Habita proportionum nunc\nA,B,(noſtri ſcilicet operis commu-\nni Menſura) huius, Tripla capiatur, ab","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0011","text":"A ver-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0012","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0013","text":"91","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0014","text":"A verſus C: & pona-\ntur eſſe AC. Ipſius A\nB, Dupla fiat AE. Et\nDupla ipſius AB, ſit\nAD. Ita quod tota\nDE, ſit ipſius AB,\nQuadrupla. Sic ergo\nnoſtram CRVCEM\nELEMENTALEM\nconſecimus. Ex AB,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0015","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 95, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0016","text":"AC AD, & AE. Linearum Scilicet QVATERNARIO. Nunc, ex BK, reſecetur recta, æqualis ipſi AD: & ſit BI. Centro I, & Interuallo IB, deſcribatur Circulus; qui ſit BR: ſecans rectam AK in puncto R. A puncto R, verſus K, reſcindatur recta æqualis ipſi AB; & ſit RK. Ad punctum K, educatur vtrinque, (ad angulos rectos, cum ipſa AK) Sufficientis lo-\ngitudinis lineæ rectæ: quæ ſit P, K, F. Ab ipſo K, puncto, verſus F, reſecetur","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0017","text":"92","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0018","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0019","text":"recta, ipſi A D æqualis: Et ſit K, F.\nCentro deinde K, & interuallo K F:\ndeſcribatur Semicirculus F, L, P, ita\nquod F, K, P, ſit eiusdem Diameter.\nTandem ad punctum C, ipſi recta\nA, C, ducatur Perpendicularis, vtrin-\nque, ad longitudinem ſufficientem\nextenſa: & ſit O, C, Q. Poſtea, ex linea\nC, Q, & ad punctum C, accipiatur\nRecta, æqualis A, B, lineæ: Et ſit C,\nM. Centro M, & interſtitio M, C, de-\nſcribatur Semicirculus C, H, O, cuius\nDiameter ſit C, M, O. Et ſimili deni-\nque ratione, ex C, Q, recta, & ad Pun-\nctum C, reſecetur linea æqualis ipſi\nA, B: & ſit C, N. Centro igitur N, &\nlongitudine N, C, fiat Semicirculus,\nC, G, Q. Cuius, C N Q ſit Diameter.\nIam Aſſertiones requisitas omnes, in\nnoſtra M O N A D E, S Y M M E T R I-\nA S, explicatas, deſcriptasque eſſe.\n    Monere tamen Mechanicum li-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0020","text":"bet:","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0021","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0022","text":"93","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0023","text":"bet: C,K, totam lineam, nouem eſſe\ntalium partium , qualium , noſtra\nF V N D A M E N T A L I S, A B, vna\neſt. Vnde alia via , ille ad hoc idem o-\npus abſoluendum accedere poteſt. Deinde Diametros, Semidiametroſ-\nque omnes, obſcuris hic ( vt loquun-\ntur Mechanici) lineis deſignari debe-\nre. Nec vllum viſibile relinquendum C E N T R V M: excepto Centro So-\nlari: quod, hic, litera I, notatum videt. Literas que adiungẽdas nullas, Tum ad Ornatum, (non Neceſſitatem ali-\nquam Myſticam a nobis ea ratione, iam conſiderandam) Peripheriæ So-\nlari, Latitudinem Superficialem (in-\ntrinſecus parallelo vno deſcripto) Me-\nchanicus adiicere poteſt. Parallelorũ vero diſtantia, per quartã quintamve partem, A, B, vel circiter, fieri poteſt. Lunari aute, illã tribuere Specie, qua ſolet Prima, poſt ſuã cum Sole Con-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0024","text":"iunctio-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0025","text":"194","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0026","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0027","text":"iunctionem, in Cælo Appārere: vi-\ndelicet Corniculata admodù. Quod fiet, ſi a K puncto, verſus R, accipiatur illa, (quâ diximus) Quarta, quin-\ntæve pars lineæ A B: & ſuper eius lineæ fine, tanquam Centro, Semidia-\nmetro vero Lunari, trahatur iſta ſe-\ncunda Peripheriæ pars, ad vtrunque prioris Semicirculi contactum niti-\ndum. Simile quid ad M, & N, pun-\ncta, fieri poteſt: erectis ibi Perpendi-\ncularibus: in quibus pars, ipſius A B, ſexta, vel minor accipiatur: vbi, facto Centro, prioribus au-\ntem M, C, & N, C, Se-\nmidiametris, ducantur\nextrinſecus, illi ſecundi,\nquaſi Semicirculi. Per\nipſas denique, noſtræ\nCrucis Rectas, vtrinque\npoſſunt Parallelæ pro-\ntrahi, a mediis per octa-\nuam, vel decimam par-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0028","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 98, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0029","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0030","text":"95","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0031","text":"tem ipſius A,B, diſtantes: Ita vt no-\nſtra CRVX, ex QVATVOR Super\nperficiebus quaſi Linearibus, ea ra-\ntione conficiatur: quarum latitudo,\nſit quarta vel quinta pars ipſius AB,\nrectæ. Hæc Ornamenta, appoſita fi-\ngura,volui aliquo modo adumbrare.\nQuæ omnia,vnuſquiſque, pro ſua a-\nnimi ſententia, facere poteſt: modo\ninterea, noſtris Myſticis SYMME-\nTRIIS, nulla (vel minima) inferatur\niniuria: Ne, ea quidem negligentia,\ntemporis tandem progreſſu, vera-\nrum iſtarum (& maxime neceſſaria-\nrum) Commenſurationum Hiero-\nglyphicarum perturbetur, pereatue\nDiſciplina noua: longe amplior Ma-\niorque quam hoc libello,eandem vel\npotuimus, vel voluimus quidem ex-\nplicare. Vt Temporis Filia, DEI NV-\nTV, docebit VERITAS.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0032","text":"96","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0033","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0034","text":"AT, quæ cuiuis eſſe obuia poſſunt, in iſtis neceſſariæ MONADIS Sym-\nmetriis ſeſe exercet, Methodice iam quædam, ob oculos ponemus. Pri-\nmum quidem ordientes, a noſtræ CRVCIS, Linearum QVATERNARIO: eo habito reſpectu, quo, QVATVOR eſſe Lineas, ſimpliciter enuntiare, quis poteſt. Deinde de Ea-\nrundem linearum QVATERNARIO prout peculiarem, Myſticamq́; alio modo habent partitionem, & rationem. Tertio, Numeris, quos vel iſto loco, vel ex aliis, per totum libellum, Theoriis, artificioſe elicuimus, vtilia quædam a Deo in NATVRA, eſſe deſtinata Oſficia, nonnullis mon-\nſtrabimus exemplis: aliaque oppor-\ntunis inferemus locis: quæ fructum haud exiguum ferent, probe in-\ntellecta: hæcque breuiſſime abſoluemus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0035","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0036","text":"97","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0037","text":"QVATERNARII PYTHA-\nGORICI.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0038","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 101, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0039","text":"Omnis poſ-\nſibilis Me-\ntacheſis, 24.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0040","text":"Summa Py-\nthagorica,\n—— 10.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0041","text":"Omnimo-\nda partium\nadditio, dat\n30.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0042","text":"Noſter Matatheſeos Canon.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0043","text":"Naturali ordine, a Prima Mona-\nde, deſcriptis quotcunque Nu-\nmeris: Si a Primo ad Vltimum, fiat\nContinuata multiplicatio: vt, Primi\nin Secundum producti in Tertium:\nilliuſque producti in Quartum: ſi-\nmilique modo ad vltimum: Produ-\nctum vltimum, omnem Poſſibilem","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0044","text":"G","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0045","text":"93","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0046","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0047","text":"Metatheſin in illis tot locis, determi-\nnat. Pariſque ratione, in quibuſcun-\nque, tot diuersis rebus: Hanc ego O-\nperationem, tibi (Q R E X) pluri-\nmun Commendo; tum in omni\nNaturæ examinatione, tum in aliis\nReipubl. Negotiis vtiliſſimam. hac\n    ego in Hebræorum. Tziruph.\n    (ſiue Thmura) cum ma-\n        xima voluptate,\n            vti ſoleo.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0048","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 102, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0049","text":"QVA-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0050","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0051","text":"29","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0052","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 103, region 3]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0053","text":"Non ſum Euclidem Neſcius, perplures a-\nlios, ex QVATERNARII, Arithmetica Virtute, & FORMALITATE, in lucem ad-\nſerri potuiſſe Numeros. Sed qui ISTIS, Naturæ euolui, illuſtrarique obſcuritatem ma-\ngnam, non deprehenderit: maiori eorum mul-\ntitudine, obtundi ſuum, non acuſſentiret in-\ngenium. Noſtris ergo Numeris (vt ſumus","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0054","text":"G 2","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0055","text":"100","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0056","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0057","text":"polliciti) quantum inſit Auctorita-\ntis, in ELEMENTIS PONDERAN-\nDIS, in TEMPORVM MENSVRIS\ndeſiniendis, Denique in Rerum Po-\nteſtati & Virtuti, certis præſcriben-\ndis GRADIBVS, ex ſequen-\ntibus id perpendendum ex-\nhibemus Schema-\ntibus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0058","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 104, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0059","text":"Nume-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0060","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0061","text":"101","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0062","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 105, region 3]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0063","text":"G 3","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0064","text":"102","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0065","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0066","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 106, region 3]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0067","text":"Ex.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0068","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A. 103","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0069","text":"EX iſtis Schematibus, plura elici\npoſſunt: (ſi penitius conſideren-\ntur) quam apertis par eſt proferre ver-\nbis. Hoc tamen præ cæteris monendus\nſingulare vnum, (a nobis etiam pri-\nmis vna cum tota hac noua euulga-\ntum arte) Rationem hic in medio eſ-\nſe poſitam, ob quam, QVATERNAR-\nIVS, vel DENARIVS, Nu-\nmerationibus finem imponit quen-\ndam: eamque cauſam quam attulere\nMaiores noſtri, non fuiſſe abſolutam\nexactamque aſſerimus: ſed iſtam qua\nnunc narrabimus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0070","text":"Poſtquam iſta MONAS, eſt\nſibi integre, plenèque Phyſice-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0071","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0072","text":"que Reſtituta, (tum quidem eſt","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0073","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 6]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0074","text":"MONAS, VNITISSIMA,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0075","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 8]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0076","text":"Magorumque iudicata VNITAS)\nneque in NATVRÆ, neque vllius\nARTIS eſt poteſtate, EANDEM\nSÆPIVS QVAM QVATER,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0077","text":"per","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0078","text":"G 4","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0079","text":"104","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0080","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0081","text":"Supercæleſtes Reuolutiones, ad Pro-\ngreſſum vllum, MOTVMVE facien-\ndum impellere:(Ac inde progignitur\nIlle, quem nos ob eminentiam\nſuam, ſic notari volumus,) Idq;\nea de cauſa, quod nec in Eleme-\ntali mundo, nec Cæleſti, nec Sv-\nPERCÆLESTI, ſit aliqua Potestas,\nCREATA INFLVENTIALIS: Qua,\ntunc, non fuerit abſolutiſſime Ditata\n& Dotata.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0082","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 108, region 4]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0083","text":"Cuius, hunc verum Effectum,\nQVATVOR ſimul (olim) Philoſo-\nphantes Clariſſimi Viri, Opere ſunt\nconſecuti: Vnde, diu, Maximo Rei\nMiraculo Attoniti, Tandem ad Dei\nOpt.Max. Canendas, prædicandaſq;\nLaudes, ſe totos, deinceps conuerte-\nbant. Qui, ea ratione, illis, tantam Sa-\npientiam, & ſuper CREATVRAS\ncæteras, Potentiam, Imperiumque\nfuiſſet Largitus ampliſſimum.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0084","text":"THEOR.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0085","text":"HIEROGLYPHICA.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0086","text":"109","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"653420c41a8c9e94376287048652e129f6d748ef6310890f20d95b51db24b350","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232223421278Z_081f5614","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. XXIII.","source_sha256":"653420c41a8c9e94376287048652e129f6d748ef6310890f20d95b51db24b350","sha256":"f979b377be278f5112e37d82cb77d1569b14b55723ba148f7bbf1b4325a443c5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:22:23.421340+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0001","text":"T H E O R E M.  XXIII.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0002","text":"The symmetries now observed by us in the Hieroglyphic Construction of our MONAD, and to be observed by those who will find it pleasing to carry the same in rings or seals, or otherwise to possess it, we here set forth accurately noted. In the Name of JESUS CHRIST, crucified for us (whose Spirit, swiftly, makes me who write these things through Him to be merely a pen, and","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0003","text":"I desire,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0004","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0005","text":"89","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0006","text":"I desire and hope.) From the CROSS of our ELEMENTS, we shall now seek all these Measures. Or indeed by this reasoning (according to the subject-matter of the proposed argument): Because, beneath the Heaven of the MOON, whatever takes the beginning of its Generation is either compacted from the FOUR Elements, or is itself an ELEMENTAL ESSENCE; and this in various modes not commonly known. And because in no created thing are the Elements themselves in equal proportion or power, yet by Art they can be reduced to equality in certain things (as in those of the Sophists): in our CROSS we establish equal and unequal parts. Which, by another reasoning, we may call the Same and the Different, or the One and the Many. Admitting in secret the Pro-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0007","text":"90","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0008","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0009","text":"perty of the equilateral CROSS (as we have noted above). But if we were to bring forward individually the reasons of the SYMMETRIES set down here (which we maintain), or otherwise demonstrate their causes than we have done sufficiently abundantly throughout this whole little work for the Wise, we should not without cause overstep the limits prescribed to us for our purpose.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Let some point be taken in a plane, for example A: through it let a sufficiently long straight line be drawn on both sides, namely C, A, K. And upon the line K, C, at point A, let a perpendicular be raised, extended on both sides to a sufficient length (Geometers customarily say, to infinity, prudently forestalling inconveniences), which may be admitted to be D, A, E. Now upon A, K let any point be taken, and let it be B. The proportion A, B (that is, the common measure of our work) having now been taken, let its triple be taken from","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0011","text":"from A to-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0012","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0013","text":"91","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0014","text":"ward C, and let it be set as AC. Let AE be made double AB. And let AD be double AB. Thus the whole DE is quadruple AB. Thus, therefore, we have made our ELEMENTAL CROSS, from AB, AC, AD, and AE: that is, from a QUATERNARY of lines. Now from BK let a straight line equal to AD itself be cut off, and let it be BI. With centre I and interval IB, let the circle BR be described, cutting the straight line AK at point R. From point R, toward K, let a straight line equal to AB itself be cut off, and let it be RK. At point K let straight lines of sufficient length be drawn on both sides (at right angles to AK itself), and let them be P, K, F. From that point K, toward F, let there be cut off","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0015","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 95, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0016","text":"a straight line equal to AD itself, and let it be K, F. Then, with centre K and interval KF, let the semicircle F, L, P be described, so that F, K, P is its diameter. Finally, at point C let a perpendicular be drawn to the straight line A, C, extended on both sides to a sufficient length, and let it be O, C, Q. Afterwards, from line C, Q and at point C, let a straight line equal to line A, B be taken, and let it be C, M. With centre M and interval M, C, let the semicircle C, H, O be described, of which C, M, O is the diameter. And finally, by a like method, from the straight line C, Q and at point C let a line equal to AB itself be cut off, and let it be C, N. Therefore, with centre N and length N, C, let the semicircle C, G, Q be made, of which C, N, Q is the diameter. I now assert that all the requisite SYMMETRIES in our M O N A D have been explained and described.\n    Yet it is fitting to warn the mechanic","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0017","text":"92","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0018","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0019","text":"that the entire line C, K consists of nine such parts as our FUNDAMENTAL A, B is one. Whence he may approach by another way to complete this same work. Next, all the diameters and semidiameters ought here to be marked with faint lines (as mechanics speak). Nor should any visible CENTRE be left, except the Solar Centre, which here he sees marked by the letter I. No letters are to be added; then, for ornament (not for any mystical necessity, to be considered by us now on that account), the mechanic may add to the Solar circumference a superficial breadth (one parallel having been drawn within). The distance of the parallels, however, may be made a fourth or fifth part of A, B, or thereabouts. But to the Lunar [circumference], let him assign that appearance which it customarily has first after its conjunction","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0020","text":"with-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0021","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0022","text":"93","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0023","text":"the Sun.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0023"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0024","text":"conjunction-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0025","text":"194","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0026","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0026"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0027","text":"junction, to appear in Heaven: namely, very horned. This will occur if, from point K, towards R, that fourth or fifth part of the line A B (of which we spoke) is taken; and, upon the end of that line, as centre, but with the lunar semidiameter, this second part of the circumference is drawn, tending towards either contact of the former semicircle. Something similar may be done at points M and N: perpendiculars having been raised there; in which a sixth part, or a smaller part, of A B itself is taken: where, a centre having been made, but with M, C, and N, C, as semidiameters, let those second, as it were semicircles, be drawn externally. Finally, through the straight lines of our Cross themselves, parallels may on either side be extended, distant from the middles by an eighth or a tenth part—","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0027"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0028","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 98, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0028"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0029","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0029"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0030","text":"95","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0030"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0031","text":"—of A, B itself: so that our CROSS may thus be composed, as it were, of FOUR linear surfaces, whose width is a fourth or fifth part of the straight line AB itself. I have wished, in the appended figure, to sketch these ornaments in some fashion. Each person may do all these things according to the judgment of his own mind: provided meanwhile that no injury (or the least possible) be inflicted upon our Mystical SYMMETRIES; lest, by that very negligence, in the progress of time, the Discipline of those true (and most necessary) Hieroglyphical Commensurations be disturbed and perish—a discipline far broader and greater than we either could, or indeed wished, to explain in this little book. As the Daughter of Time, by GOD'S NOD, TRUTH will teach.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0031"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0032","text":"96","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0032"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0033","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0033"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0034","text":"BUT we shall now methodically set before the eyes certain matters concerning those things which can be obvious to anyone in those necessary Symmetries of the MONAD. Beginning first, indeed, from the QUATERNARY of the Lines of our CROSS, with that respect in which anyone can simply declare that there are FOUR Lines. Then, concerning the QUATERNARY of those same lines, according as they have a particular and Mystical division and relation in another way. Thirdly, by some examples, we shall show to some persons that the Numbers which we have artfully elicited, whether in that place or from other Theories throughout the whole little book, have certain useful Offices appointed by God in NATURE; and we shall introduce other things in suitable places, which, if rightly understood, will bear no small fruit: and we shall dispatch these matters very briefly.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0034"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0035","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0035"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0036","text":"97","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0036"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0037","text":"OF THE PYTHA-\nGOREAN QUATERNARY.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0037"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0038","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 101, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0038"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0039","text":"Every pos-\nsible Meta-\nthesis, 24.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0039"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0040","text":"Pytha-\ngorean sum,\n—— 10.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0040"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0041","text":"The altogether\ncomplete addition\nof the parts gives\n30.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0041"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0042","text":"The Canon of our Matathesis.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0042"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0043","text":"With however many Numbers described in natural order from the First Monad: if, from the First to the Last, a continued multiplication be made—thus, the product of the First into the Second into the Third; and that product into the Fourth; and in like manner unto the last—the final product determines every Possible","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0043"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232223421278Z_081f5614:DISPLAY-0044","text":"G\n\n93","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0044","RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0045"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0046","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0046"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0047","text":"Metathesis in all those places. And by the same reasoning, in any number whatsoever of such diverse things. This Operation I most highly commend to thee, O KING, as most useful both in every examination of Nature and in other affairs of the Commonwealth. I am accustomed to use this in the Hebrew Tziruph (or Thmura) with the greatest delight.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0047"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0048","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 102, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0048"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0049","text":"QUA-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0049"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0050","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0050"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0051","text":"29","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0051"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0052","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 103, region 3]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0052"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0053","text":"I am not unaware that Euclid could have brought forth into light very many other Numbers from the Arithmetic Virtue and FORMALITY of the QUATERNARY. But he who has not perceived that by THESE a great obscurity of Nature is unfolded and illuminated, would not feel his own intellect blunted by their greater multitude. Therefore, in our Numbers (as we have promised)","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0053"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0054","text":"G 2","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0054"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0055","text":"100","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0055"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0056","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0056"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0057","text":"how much Authority resides, in WEIGHING THE ELEMENTS, in determining the MEASURES OF TIMES, and finally in prescribing certain DEGREES to the Power and Virtue of Things, we set forth to be weighed from the following Schemas.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0057"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0058","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 104, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0058"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0059","text":"Num-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0059"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0060","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0060"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0061","text":"101","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0061"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0062","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 105, region 3]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0062"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0063","text":"G 3","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0063"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0064","text":"102","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0064"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0065","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0065"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0066","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 106, region 3]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0066"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0067","text":"From.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0067"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0068","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S. 103","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0068"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0069","text":"From these Schemas, more can be drawn forth (if they are considered more deeply) than it is fitting to express in plain words. Yet, before the rest, one singular thing must be noted: that a Reason has here been set in the middle, on account of which the QUATERNARY, or the DENARY, imposes a certain limit upon Numerations; and we assert that the cause which our Elders adduced was not complete and exact, but rather this one which we shall now relate.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0069"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0070","text":"After that MONAD has been restored to itself wholly and fully, physically-","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0070"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0071","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0071"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0072","text":"and, (then indeed it is","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0072"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0073","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 6]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0073"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0074","text":"MONAD, MOST UNITARY,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0074"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0075","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 107, region 8]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0075"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0076","text":"and UNITY judged by the Magi)\nis neither in the power of NATURE, nor of any\nART, TO IMPEL THE SAME\nMORE OFTEN THAN FOUR TIMES,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0076"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0077","text":"through","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0077"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0078","text":"G 4","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0078"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0079","text":"104","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0079"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0080","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0080"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0081","text":"Supercelestial Revolutions, to impel [it]\nto make any Progress or MOTION:\n(And thence is begotten\nThat One, which, on account of its\neminence, we wish thus to be marked,)\nand for this reason, because neither in the Elemen-\ntal world, nor in the Celestial, nor in the SU-\nPERCÆLESTIAL, is there any POWER,\nCREATED AND INFLUENTIAL: Which,\nthen, shall not have been most absolutely Enriched\nand Endowed.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0081"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0082","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 108, region 4]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0082"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0083","text":"The true Effect of this [thing],\nFOUR most distinguished Men, philosophizing\ntogether (formerly), attained by their Work:\nWhence, for a long time, Astonished by the\nGreatest Miracle of the Thing, at length they\nturned themselves wholly thereafter to singing\nand proclaiming the Praises of God, Best and Greatest.\nWho, by that means, had bestowed upon them such\nWisdom, and, over the other CREATURES,\nPower and most ample Dominion.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0083"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0084","text":"THEORY.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0084"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0085","text":"HIEROGLYPHICS.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0085"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0086","text":"109","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_19:DISPLAY-0086"]}],"source_digest":"e2548247621022388f8fb047a3844fdad9981665592fabecfbd88e551770a1ed","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. XXIII."}],"original_title":"T H E O R. XXIII.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20","title":"THEOR. XXIIII.","order":25,"chapter_id":"CH_MHON_T_20","text":"THEOR. XXIIII.\n\nVT, noſtrum huius Libelli Exor-\ndium, a Puncto, Recta, Circulo-\nque Cœpimus: Sicque ex noſtro MO-\nNADICO PVNCTO, LINEAREM\nnoſtrorum ELEMENTORVM Eſ-\nfluxionem Extremam, in Circulum\nCircumduximus, Analogum fere,\nipſi Æquinoctiali; qui Horis 24, ſuam\nConficit Circuitionem: ITA, nunc\ntandem, QVATERNARII OMNI-\nMODAM METATHESIM; (Nume-\nro definitam, 24.) METAMORPHO-\nSIMQVE hac noſtra Vigeſima\nQVARTA Conſummabimus, Ter-\nminabimusque Theoria: Ad HONO-\nREM, GLORIAMQVE eius: QVI,\n(Teſte, Myſteriorum Diuinorum\nArchipræſule, Ioanne: in QVARTI\nApocalypſeos Capitis, parte QVAR-\nTA VLTIMAQVE) in Throno Se-\ndet: In Cuius MEDIO CIRCVIT-\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n106\n\nM O N A S\n\nVQVE, Animalia QVATVOR ſin,\ngula ALAS SEX habentia (Sine re-\nquie, DIE ac NOCTE, dicunt:\nSanctus, Sanctus, Sanctus Dominus\nDeus Omnipotens: QVI Erat: &,\nQVI Eſt: & QVI venturus Eſt:\nQVEM etiam, ex 24. Sedilibus, in\nCIRCVITV poſitis, SENIORES\n24, procidentes (AVREIS SVIS\nABIECTIS CORONIS) adorant;\ndicentes: Dignus es Domine accipe-\nre GLORIAM & HONOREM, &\nVIRTVTEM: QVIA, TV, CREA-\nSTI, OMNIA: Et propter VOLVN-\nTATEM TVAM SVNT: ET\nCREATA SVNT. AMEN,\n\n4\n\n5\n\nDICIT\n\nLITERA QVARTA,\n\nA.\n\nCui,\n\nH I E R O G L Y P H I C A.\n\n107\n\nCui, DEVS, Voluntatem Ha-\nbilitatemque dedit , Divinum\nhoc Myſterium, æternis Sic con-\nſignare Literarum Monimentis:\nLaboreſque hoſce Suos, placidiſ-\nſime abſoluere , Januarij\n25. die euſdem 13.\nInchoatos:\n\nAn. 1564. Antvverpiæ.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 111, region 5]\n\nVulgaris, Hic, Oculis\nCALIGABIT, DIFFIDETQVE\nplurimum.\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 115, region 1]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 116, region 1]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 118, region 1]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n[illegible]\n\nN°. 250\n\n10 Decᵇʳ. [illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 120, region 1]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]\n\n[illegible]","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEOR. XXIIII.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0002","text":"VT, noſtrum huius Libelli Exor-\ndium, a Puncto, Recta, Circulo-\nque Cœpimus: Sicque ex noſtro MO-\nNADICO PVNCTO, LINEAREM\nnoſtrorum ELEMENTORVM Eſ-\nfluxionem Extremam, in Circulum\nCircumduximus, Analogum fere,\nipſi Æquinoctiali; qui Horis 24, ſuam\nConficit Circuitionem: ITA, nunc\ntandem, QVATERNARII OMNI-\nMODAM METATHESIM; (Nume-\nro definitam, 24.) METAMORPHO-\nSIMQVE hac noſtra Vigeſima\nQVARTA Conſummabimus, Ter-\nminabimusque Theoria: Ad HONO-\nREM, GLORIAMQVE eius: QVI,\n(Teſte, Myſteriorum Diuinorum\nArchipræſule, Ioanne: in QVARTI\nApocalypſeos Capitis, parte QVAR-\nTA VLTIMAQVE) in Throno Se-\ndet: In Cuius MEDIO CIRCVIT-","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0003","text":"1.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0004","text":"2.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0005","text":"3.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0006","text":"106","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0007","text":"M O N A S","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0008","text":"VQVE, Animalia QVATVOR ſin,\ngula ALAS SEX habentia (Sine re-\nquie, DIE ac NOCTE, dicunt:\nSanctus, Sanctus, Sanctus Dominus\nDeus Omnipotens: QVI Erat: &,\nQVI Eſt: & QVI venturus Eſt:\nQVEM etiam, ex 24. Sedilibus, in\nCIRCVITV poſitis, SENIORES\n24, procidentes (AVREIS SVIS\nABIECTIS CORONIS) adorant;\ndicentes: Dignus es Domine accipe-\nre GLORIAM & HONOREM, &\nVIRTVTEM: QVIA, TV, CREA-\nSTI, OMNIA: Et propter VOLVN-\nTATEM TVAM SVNT: ET\nCREATA SVNT. AMEN,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0009","text":"4","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0010","text":"5","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0011","text":"DICIT","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0012","text":"LITERA QVARTA,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0013","text":"A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0014","text":"Cui,","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0015","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C A.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0016","text":"107","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0017","text":"Cui, DEVS, Voluntatem Ha-\nbilitatemque dedit , Divinum\nhoc Myſterium, æternis Sic con-\nſignare Literarum Monimentis:\nLaboreſque hoſce Suos, placidiſ-\nſime abſoluere , Januarij\n25. die euſdem 13.\nInchoatos:","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0018","text":"An. 1564. Antvverpiæ.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0019","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 111, region 5]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0020","text":"Vulgaris, Hic, Oculis\nCALIGABIT, DIFFIDETQVE\nplurimum.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0021","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0022","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0023","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0024","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 115, region 1]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0025","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 116, region 1]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0026","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 118, region 1]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0027","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0028","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0029","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0030","text":"[illegible]\n[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0031","text":"N°. 250","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0032","text":"10 Decᵇʳ. [illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0033","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 120, region 1]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0035","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0036","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0037","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0038","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"57df411f1730bce2066d5d7f7dfde5abc83d46a141567529bde2f0b9bf10dba9","language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232235834074Z_11bf6048","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XXIIII.","source_sha256":"57df411f1730bce2066d5d7f7dfde5abc83d46a141567529bde2f0b9bf10dba9","sha256":"c8025286559599578fc22966d2f7348a5fba343c43d0c2fa88e0ee160939a3f8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T23:22:35.834168+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0001","text":"THEORY XXIV.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0002","text":"AS we began the Exordium of this little Book of ours from a Point, a Straight Line, and a Circle: and thus from our MONADIC POINT drew out the extreme LINEAR efflux of our ELEMENTS into a Circle, nearly analogous to the Equinoctial itself, which completes its revolution in 24 hours: SO now at last we shall bring to completion, and shall terminate with this our Twenty-Fourth Theory, THE ALL-MODAL METATHESIS OF THE QUATERNARY (defined by the number 24), AND ITS METAMORPHOSIS: unto the HONOUR AND GLORY of Him WHO (as John, chief priest of the Divine Mysteries, testifies, in the FOURTH part, the LAST, of the FOURTH Chapter of the Apocalypse) sits upon the Throne: in the midst of whose CIRCUIT—","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0003","text":"1.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0004","text":"2.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0005","text":"3.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0006","text":"106","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0007","text":"M O N A D","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0008","text":"—ARE four living creatures, each having SIX WINGS, which, without rest, DAY and NIGHT, say:\nHoly, Holy, Holy, Lord God Almighty: WHO Was, and WHO Is, and WHO is to come:\nWHOM also the 24 ELDERS, falling down from the 24 seats set about in a CIRCUIT (CASTING DOWN THEIR GOLDEN CROWNS), worship, saying: Worthy art thou, O Lord, to receive GLORY and HONOUR and POWER: BECAUSE THOU HAST CREATED ALL THINGS: and because of THY WILL THEY ARE, AND WERE CREATED. AMEN.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261006T232235834074Z_11bf6048:DISPLAY-0009","text":"4\n\n5","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0009","RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0011","text":"SAYS","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0012","text":"THE FOURTH LETTER,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0013","text":"A.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0014","text":"To whom,","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0014"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0015","text":"H I E R O G L Y P H I C S.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0015"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0016","text":"107","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0016"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0017","text":"To whom God gave the will and ability to consign this Divine Mystery thus to the everlasting memorials of letters, and most peacefully to bring these his labours to completion, begun on the 25th day of January of the same 13th year:","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0017"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0018","text":"In the year 1564, at Antwerp.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0018"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0019","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 111, region 5]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0019"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0020","text":"The common man here will be dim-sighted, and will distrust exceedingly.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0020"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0021","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0021"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0022","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0022"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0023","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0023"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0024","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 115, region 1]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0024"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0025","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 116, region 1]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0025"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0026","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 118, region 1]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0026"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0027","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0027"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0028","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0028"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0029","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0029"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0030","text":"[illegible]\n[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0030"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0031","text":"No. 250","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0031"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0032","text":"10 Dec. [illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0032"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0033","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0033"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 120, region 1]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0034"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0035","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0035"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0036","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0036"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0037","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0037"]},{"id":"RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0038","text":"[illegible]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_MHON_T_20:DISPLAY-0038"]}],"source_digest":"5ae1c08e3af59a39f9c9ae546525b0c03267a1112c160661a932b413089477cf","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XXIIII."}],"original_title":"THEOR. XXIIII.","title_language_code":"en"}],"units":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM","layer":"CH","title":"Front matter","order":1,"parents":["RAW_MHON_FROM"],"revision":"CH_MHON_FROM@R001","sha256":"6a7575ad848515302ef0bc4ea504a6daf7a41a5dc22a79b948f0c0508fe106e9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS1","text":"Quaestio regens est quomodo unus character hieroglyphicus totius sapientiae compendium praebere atque publicationem simul exigere et restringere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0185","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS2","text":"Thesis principalis Monadem proponit ut formam exactam, mathematice roboratam et divinitus fundatam, quae litteras, numeros, figuras caelestes, naturam et mysteria metaphysica connectat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0208","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS3","text":"Argumentatio apologetica, reconstructiva, polemica et strategica est: artem restituit, eius legitimam naturam defendit, falsas similitudines excludit et condiciones transmissionis constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS4","text":"Motus incipit a raritate philosophi veri et per gradus physicos, caelestes atque supercaelestes ad raritatem muneris ascendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS5","text":"Raritas muneris per exactam compositionem characteris et per eius fecunditatem trans disciplinas comprobatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS6","text":"Defensio a distinctione inter corpora doctrinarum verarum et umbras imitationum falsarum pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS7","text":"Conclusio practica coniungit iudicium regium, reproductionem typographicam exactam et circulationem ad lectores idoneos restrictam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A1","text":"Omnia visibilia invisibiliaque a Deo emanant et eius bonitatem, sapientiam potentiamque significant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A2","text":"Creatio est scriptum divinum in creaturis exaratum atque humanae investigationi legibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A3","text":"Litterae mysticae primariae a Deo procedunt, earumque figurae ex punctis, lineis rectis et circulorum peripheriis componuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A4","text":"In forma Monadis nullum punctum superfluum aut semanticamente vacuum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A5","text":"Unitas immota pluralitatem consubstantialem et ordinate distinctam intra se continere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A6","text":"Character Monadis figuras astronomicas dispersas in unam formam symmetricam restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A7","text":"Interpretatio hieroglyphica lumen et robur mathematicum possidet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A8","text":"Eadem structura monadica per analogiam in pluribus artibus diversas potentias explicare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A9","text":"Cabala realis signa ex tota creatione, non ex una tantum lingua scripta, colligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A10","text":"Quo altior est gradus philosophiae, eo rarior est facultas eum sincere comprehendendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A11","text":"Iudicium validum de mysteriis perfectam amplitudinis eorum cognitionem praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A12","text":"Scientiae honestae sunt corpora solida, artes autem adulteratae earum umbrae inanes sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A13","text":"Corpora et umbrae terminis, figuris atque phrasibus communibus uti possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A14","text":"Demonstratio propria, non auctoritas humana, assensum philosophicum fundat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A15","text":"Bonitas muneris in fecunditate honesta, sincera, pia et dignitati humanae apta consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A16","text":"Receptio ab hominibus imperitis errorem, imposturam, negationem vel accusationem generare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A17","text":"Exactitudo typographica est condicio integritatis doctrinalis operis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A18","text":"Iustitia regia veras artes ab earum umbris discernere et contra iudicia imperitorum protegere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX1","text":"Monas non est character mortuus, mutus aut mere barbarus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX2","text":"Interpretatio hieroglyphica non est violenta, impropria aut formae extrinsecus imposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX3","text":"Cabala realis non terminatur litteris ab homine scribibilibus neque finibus unius linguae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX4","text":"Opus fidem suam ab Hermete, Pythagora aliisque antiquis non mendicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX5","text":"Magia vera non identificatur cum impietate, scelere aut superstitione vulgari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX6","text":"Similitudo nominis non sufficit ut studium honestum cum arte falsa condemnetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX7","text":"Mysteria non destinantur indiscriminatae multitudinis usui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX8","text":"Typographia non est medium semanticamente indifferens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX9","text":"Occultatio per figuras umbratiles non est necessario deceptio, si veritatem ab usu indigno protegit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D1","text":"Natura tota fit campus semioticus in quo res creatae simul obiecta et signa divinorum attributorum sunt.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A1","CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D2","text":"Geometria elementaris pontem constituit inter alphabetum, mathematicam et ordinem rerum.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A3","CH_MHON_FROM:A7","CH_MHON_FROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D3","text":"Monas operatur ut machina compressionis, qua unitas formaliter minima pluralitatem interpretationum ordinatarum generat.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A4","CH_MHON_FROM:A5","CH_MHON_FROM:A6","CH_MHON_FROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D4","text":"Concordia effectuum per multas disciplinas adductorum rarae fecunditatis atque bonitatis muneris testis efficitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A7","CH_MHON_FROM:A8","CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D5","text":"Cabala realis linguam sacram universalizat, quia idem Deus omnibus gentibus per creationem signa praebet.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A1","CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D6","text":"Corruptio umbratilis artis existentiam corporis veri non infirmat.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A12","CH_MHON_FROM:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D7","text":"Iudicium iustum usum, structuram et finem artis examinare debet potius quam vocabulum commune.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A12","CH_MHON_FROM:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D8","text":"Publicatio legitima reproductionem exactam cum delectu recipientium coniungere debet.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A4","CH_MHON_FROM:A16","CH_MHON_FROM:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D9","text":"Approbatio regia munus tutelae et discriminationis habet, non locum demonstrationis intrinsecae.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A14","CH_MHON_FROM:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D10","text":"Velamentum doctrinale fit instrumentum tutelae, quia communitas figurarum veritatem celare potest sine eius abolitione.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A13","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD1","text":"Disciplinae particulares reordinantur ut projectiones analogicae unius ordinis divini et monadici, non ut regiones penitus autonomae.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A1","CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A6","CH_MHON_FROM:A7","CH_MHON_FROM:A8","CH_MHON_FROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD2","text":"Accessus epistemicus simul gradualis et moralis est, quia altitudo obiecti, amplitudo cognitionis et sinceritas investigatoris inter se conectuntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A15","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD3","text":"Corpus materiale libri pars machinae conceptualis fit, quoniam corruptio puncti, lineae aut schematis doctrinam ipsam mutilat.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A4","CH_MHON_FROM:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD4","text":"Universalitas scripturae creationis non producit universalem aequalitatem accessus, sed publicum duplicem: omnes signis circumdantur, pauci ea recte interpretantur.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A9","CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD5","text":"Potestas regia tamquam ars distinctionis reconstituitur, cui competit corpora doctrinalia ab umbris homonymis separare.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A12","CH_MHON_FROM:A13","CH_MHON_FROM:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD6","text":"Repudiatio vulgi contra systema non necessario fit contra-testimonium, quia defectus comprehensionis ipsam repudiationem explicare potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet disciplinas absolutis finibus clausas neque ad commune principium reducibiles esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet signa esse mera instituta conventionalia rebus quas significant extrinseca.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet publicam accessibilitatem esse condicionem necessariam veritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet similitudinem vocabuli vel figurae identitatem rei probare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet auctoritatem, antiquitatem aut consensum per se demonstrationem constituere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet materiam typographicam sensui transmisso indifferentem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse oportet unitatem et pluralitatem ordinatam mutuo excludi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX8","text":"Falsum esse oportet abusus artis corpus verae artis tollere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX1","text":"Expositio omnino perspicua et indiscriminatim omnibus tradita habetur ut possibilitas epistemice et moraliter inadmissibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX2","text":"Tribunal externum, neutrum et a perfecta mysteriorum cognitione solutum, intra systema nullam competentiam ultimam obtinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX3","text":"Separatio absoluta inter characterem et rem significatam praecluditur, quia forma hieroglyphica vim realem et operativam continere ponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX4","text":"Divortium absolutum inter contemplationem sacram, scientiam naturalem et operationem technicam excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS1","text":"Deus → emanatio rerum → creatio ut scriptura → signa visibilia et invisibilia → inquisitio attributorum divinorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS2","text":"Signa dispersa → reductio ad punctum, lineam et circulum → compositio monadica exacta → validatio mathematica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS3","text":"Monas exacta → projectiones analogicae per disciplinas → testimonia concordantia → raritas fecunda → bonitas muneris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS4","text":"Communitas nominum et figurarum → confusio corporis cum umbra → cognitio integra → discretio iusta → tutela regia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS5","text":"Arcanum doctrinale → exemplar materialiter exactum → typographia fidelis → lector idoneus → cognitio legitima.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS6","text":"Typographia neglegens aut circulatio promiscua → mutilatio sensus → labyrinthus interpretativus → impostura, negatio vel accusatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AF1","text":"Raritas philosophi veri → raritas muneris → reductio signorum ad unitatem geometricam → fecunditas trans disciplinas → universalitas Cabalae realis → distinctio corporis et umbrae → iudicium regium → impressio exacta et circulatio selectiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME1","text":"Character astronomicus ex nota mortua in condensatum semanticum et operativum reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME2","text":"Grammatica ex disciplina litterarum humanarum in ontologiam signorum creationis dilatatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME3","text":"Disciplinae separatae in manifestationes analogicas unius ordinis monadici convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter scientiam et magiam substituitur distinctione inter corpus verum et umbram adulteratam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME5","text":"Typographia ex vehiculo externo in operationem constitutivam sensus mutatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME6","text":"Regnum ex patrocinio ornamentali in tribunal distinctionis et tutelam cognitionis reconfiguratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME7","text":"Publicum non amplius dividitur inter cognoscentes et omnino exclusos, sed inter eos qui signis communibus recte vel perperam utuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT1","text":"Surface — Praefatio raritatem, bonitatem et dignitatem Monadis defendit atque opus regi et typographo committit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT2","text":"Structural — Mechanismus consistit in reductione pluralitatis signorum ad formam geometricam exactam et in re-expansione eius per analogias disciplinarias.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Certamen de magia, Cabala et artibus occultis in quaestionem discriminationis inter corpora et umbras transfertur, simulque accessus et transmissio reguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas ut emanatio divina et scriptura legibilis ponitur, unitas pluralitatem continet, iar ars praesens simul ut nova constitutio et ut sapientiae priscae restitutio temporalis exhibetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem a scriptura creationis per compressionem monadicam ad tutelam transmissionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT2","text":"Demonstrationes particulares et nexus operativi inter characterem et effectus promissos in hac unitate nondum satis determinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT3","text":"Structura interne cohaeret quatenus forma exacta, analogia disciplinaris et discretio recipientium ex eodem principio significationis necessariae deducuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT4","text":"Firmissima commissura est coniunctio inter minutias formales, integritatem interpretationis et necessitatem typographiae fidelis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT5","text":"Clausura fragilis oritur ex regula qua nemo nisi amplitudinem mysteriorum iam comprehendens de eis valide iudicare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT6","text":"Universalitas Cabalae realis et inexcusabilitas generis humani cum prohibitione circulationis promiscuae in tensione manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT7","text":"Repudiatio auctoritatis humanae cum usu Maximiliani tamquam testis privilegiati et defensoris nondum plene conciliatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT8","text":"Ars inter primam constitutionem novam et revocationem traditionis extinctae ambigue collocatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT9","text":"Multa effecta disciplinaria vi enumerationis et promissionis potius quam demonstratione intra frontem materiae nituntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT10","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: raritas → unitas formalis → fecunditas universalis → discriminatio → transmissio custodita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222210699868Z_5ca0c930","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Front matter","source_sha256":"6a7575ad848515302ef0bc4ea504a6daf7a41a5dc22a79b948f0c0508fe106e9","sha256":"b05618955aa3421785fafd7f0bf0a97ff3c6bc3e890ba1af361349938399a427","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:22:10.700972+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS1","text":"The governing question is how a single hieroglyphic character can provide a compendium of all wisdom and simultaneously require and restrict publication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0185","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS2","text":"The principal thesis presents the Monad as an exact form, mathematically reinforced and divinely grounded, which connects letters, numbers, celestial figures, nature, and metaphysical mysteries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0208","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS3","text":"The argument is apologetic, reconstructive, polemical, and strategic: it restores the art, defends its legitimate nature, excludes false resemblances, and establishes the conditions of transmission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS4","text":"The movement begins from the rarity of the true philosopher and ascends through physical, celestial, and supercelestial degrees to the rarity of the gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS5","text":"The rarity of the gift is demonstrated through the exact composition of the character and through its fruitfulness across disciplines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS6","text":"The defense depends upon the distinction between bodies of true doctrines and the shadows of false imitations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AS7","text":"The practical conclusion joins royal judgment, exact typographical reproduction, and circulation restricted to suitable readers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A1","text":"All visible and invisible things emanate from God and signify His goodness, wisdom, and power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A2","text":"Creation is a divine writing inscribed in creatures and legible to human investigation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A3","text":"The primary mystical letters proceed from God, and their figures are composed of points, straight lines, and the circumferences of circles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A4","text":"In the form of the Monad, no point is superfluous or semantically empty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A5","text":"Immovable unity can contain within itself plurality that is consubstantial and orderly distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A6","text":"The character of the Monad restores dispersed astronomical figures into one symmetrical form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A7","text":"Hieroglyphic interpretation possesses mathematical illumination and strength.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A8","text":"The same monadic structure can, by analogy, explicate diverse powers in several arts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A9","text":"Real Cabala gathers signs from the whole of creation, not from only one written language.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A10","text":"The higher the degree of philosophy, the rarer is the capacity sincerely to comprehend it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A11","text":"A valid judgment concerning mysteries presupposes perfect knowledge of their scope.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A12","text":"Honest sciences are solid bodies, whereas adulterated arts are their empty shadows.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A13","text":"Bodies and shadows can employ common terms, figures, and phrases.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A14","text":"Proper demonstration, not human authority, grounds philosophical assent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A15","text":"The goodness of the gift consists in fruitfulness that is honest, sincere, pious, and suited to human dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A16","text":"Reception by unlearned persons can generate error, imposture, denial, or accusation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A17","text":"Typographical exactness is a condition of the work's doctrinal integrity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:A18","text":"Royal justice can distinguish true arts from their shadows and protect them against the judgments of the unlearned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX1","text":"The Monad is not a dead, mute, or merely barbarous character.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX2","text":"Hieroglyphic interpretation is not violent, improper, or imposed extrinsically upon the form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX3","text":"Real Cabala is not confined to letters writable by man or to the boundaries of one language.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX4","text":"The work does not beg its credibility from Hermes, Pythagoras, or other ancients.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX5","text":"True magic is not identified with impiety, crime, or vulgar superstition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX6","text":"Resemblance of name does not suffice for an honest study to be condemned together with a false art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX7","text":"Mysteries are not intended for the use of an indiscriminate multitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX8","text":"Typography is not a semantically indifferent medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:NX9","text":"Concealment through shadowy figures is not necessarily deception, if it protects truth from unworthy use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D1","text":"All nature becomes a semiotic field in which created things are at once objects and signs of divine attributes.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A1","CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D2","text":"Elementary geometry establishes a bridge between alphabet, mathematics, and the order of things.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A3","CH_MHON_FROM:A7","CH_MHON_FROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D3","text":"The Monad operates as a compression machine, by which formally minimal unity generates a plurality of ordered interpretations.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A4","CH_MHON_FROM:A5","CH_MHON_FROM:A6","CH_MHON_FROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D4","text":"The concordance of effects brought forth across many disciplines becomes a witness to the rare fruitfulness and goodness of the gift.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A7","CH_MHON_FROM:A8","CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D5","text":"Real Cabala universalizes sacred language, because the same God provides signs through creation to all peoples.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A1","CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D6","text":"The shadowy corruption of an art does not weaken the existence of a true body.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A12","CH_MHON_FROM:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D7","text":"Just judgment must examine the use, structure, and end of an art rather than a common term.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A12","CH_MHON_FROM:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D8","text":"Legitimate publication must join exact reproduction with the selection of recipients.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A4","CH_MHON_FROM:A16","CH_MHON_FROM:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D9","text":"Royal approval has a function of protection and discrimination, not the place of intrinsic demonstration.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A14","CH_MHON_FROM:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:D10","text":"The doctrinal veil becomes an instrument of protection, because the communality of figures can conceal truth without abolishing it.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A13","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD1","text":"Particular disciplines are reordered as analogical projections of one divine and monadic order, not as wholly autonomous regions.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A1","CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A6","CH_MHON_FROM:A7","CH_MHON_FROM:A8","CH_MHON_FROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD2","text":"The epistemic approach is at once gradual and moral, because the height of the object, the scope of knowledge, and the sincerity of the investigator are interconnected.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A15","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD3","text":"The material body of the book becomes part of the conceptual machine, since corruption of a point, line, or diagram mutilates the doctrine itself.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A4","CH_MHON_FROM:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD4","text":"The universality of the writing of creation does not produce universal equality of access, but a twofold public: all are surrounded by signs; few interpret them correctly.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A2","CH_MHON_FROM:A9","CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD5","text":"Royal power is reconstituted as an art of distinction, to which it belongs to separate doctrinal bodies from homonymous shadows.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A12","CH_MHON_FROM:A13","CH_MHON_FROM:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SD6","text":"Rejection by the vulgar against the system does not necessarily become counter-testimony, because failure of comprehension can explain the rejection itself.","refs":["CH_MHON_FROM:A10","CH_MHON_FROM:A11","CH_MHON_FROM:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX1","text":"It must be false that disciplines are closed within absolute boundaries and cannot be reduced to a common principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX2","text":"It must be false that signs are merely conventional institutions extrinsic to the things they signify.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX3","text":"It must be false that public accessibility is a necessary condition of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX4","text":"It must be false that similarity of word or figure proves identity of thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX5","text":"It must be false that authority, antiquity, or consensus in itself constitutes demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX6","text":"It must be false that typographical material is indifferent to the sense transmitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX7","text":"It must be false that unity and ordered plurality mutually exclude one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:DNX8","text":"It must be false that abuse of an art removes the body of the true art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX1","text":"An exposition wholly clear and delivered indiscriminately to all is regarded as an epistemically and morally inadmissible possibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX2","text":"An external and neutral tribunal, freed from perfect knowledge of the mysteries, obtains no ultimate competence within the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX3","text":"An absolute separation between the character and the thing signified is precluded, because the hieroglyphic form is posited to contain real and operative force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:SNX4","text":"An absolute divorce between sacred contemplation, natural science, and technical operation is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS1","text":"God → emanation of things → creation as writing → visible and invisible signs → inquiry into divine attributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS2","text":"Dispersed signs → reduction to point, line, and circle → exact monadic composition → mathematical validation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS3","text":"Exact Monad → analogical projections across disciplines → concordant testimonies → fruitful rarity → goodness of the gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS4","text":"Communality of names and figures → confusion of body with shadow → integral knowledge → just discrimination → royal protection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0163","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS5","text":"Doctrinal secret → materially exact exemplar → faithful typography → suitable reader → legitimate knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:FGS6","text":"Negligent typography or indiscriminate circulation → mutilation of sense → interpretive labyrinth → imposture, denial, or accusation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0197","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:AF1","text":"Rarity of the true philosopher → rarity of the gift → reduction of signs to geometric unity → fruitfulness across disciplines → universality of real Cabala → distinction of body and shadow → royal judgment → exact printing and selective circulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME1","text":"The astronomical character is reclassified from a dead sign into a semantic and operative condensate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME2","text":"Grammar is expanded from a discipline of humane letters into an ontology of the signs of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME3","text":"Separate disciplines are converted into analogical manifestations of one monadic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME4","text":"The opposition between science and magic is replaced by the distinction between true body and adulterated shadow.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME5","text":"Typography is transformed from an external vehicle into a constitutive operation of sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME6","text":"The kingdom is reconfigured from ornamental patronage into a tribunal of distinction and a protection of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0167","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ME7","text":"The public is no longer divided between those who know and those wholly excluded, but between those who use common signs rightly or wrongly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0165","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT1","text":"Surface — The preface defends the rarity, goodness, and dignity of the Monad and entrusts the work to the king and the printer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT2","text":"Structural — The mechanism consists in reducing a plurality of signs to an exact geometric form and re-expanding it through disciplinary analogies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The contest concerning magic, Cabala, and occult arts is transferred into a question of discrimination between bodies and shadows, while access and transmission are regulated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0123","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality is posited as divine emanation and legible writing; unity contains plurality; and the present art is exhibited at once as a new constitution and as a temporal restoration of ancient wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the sequence from the writing of creation through monadic compression to the protection of transmission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT2","text":"The particular demonstrations and operative links between the character and the promised effects are not yet sufficiently determined in this unit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT3","text":"The structure coheres internally insofar as exact form, disciplinary analogy, and discrimination of recipients are deduced from the same principle of necessary signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT4","text":"The strongest joint is the connection between formal minutiae, integrity of interpretation, and the necessity of faithful typography.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT5","text":"A fragile closure arises from the rule that no one can validly judge mysteries unless already comprehending their scope.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0150","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT6","text":"The universality of real Cabala and the inexcusability of the human race remain in tension with the prohibition of indiscriminate circulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0119","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT7","text":"The repudiation of human authority is not yet fully reconciled with the use of Maximilian as a privileged witness and defender.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0147","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0154","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0174","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT8","text":"The art is ambiguously situated between a first new constitution and the revival of an extinct tradition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT9","text":"Many disciplinary effects rest upon enumeration and promise rather than demonstration within the front matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0102","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_MHON_FROM:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: rarity → formal unity → universal fruitfulness → discrimination → guarded transmission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0157","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0188","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_MHON_FROM:P0194","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_FROM@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_FROM:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Front matter"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 01","title":"Front matter","context":"Chapter 01","original_title":"Front matter","original_context":"Chapter 01"},"original_title":"Front matter","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI","layer":"CH","title":"Theorem I.","order":2,"parents":["RAW_MHON_THEI"],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEI@R001","sha256":"ff62e886dd7024920a97e61c537d6f03da461dd1700c18704497f323a9dff26c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS1","text":"Prima rerum simplicissimae formae per lineam rectam et circulum constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS2","text":"Hae formae res existentes, res non existentes et ea quae in Naturae involucris latent comprehendunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS3","text":"Quod latet per simplicissimas formas in lucem producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS4","text":"Productio simul est repraesentatio eius quod antea occultum erat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS5","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructiva et ontologico-repraesentativa: a formis primis ad manifestationem rerum progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A1","text":"Linea recta est una ex formis rerum primis et simplicissimis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A2","text":"Circulus est una ex formis rerum primis et simplicissimis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A3","text":"Rerum natura continet non solum existentia, sed etiam non existentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A4","text":"In Natura quaedam res latent sub involucris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A5","text":"Forma simplicissima potest id quod latet in lucem producere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A6","text":"Productio rei et repraesentatio rei una operatione coniunguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX1","text":"Res primae non per formarum multitudinem, sed per lineam rectam et circulum simplicissime constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX2","text":"Manifestatio non limitatur ad res iam existentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX3","text":"Quod in Natura sub involucro latet non est extra ordinem rerum producibilium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX4","text":"Productio non est separabilis a repraesentatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX5","text":"Invisibile vel occultum non manet absolute indisponibile, si forma eius in lucem produci potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D1","text":"Forma prima simul habet munus ontologicum et repraesentativum.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A1","CH_MHON_THEI:A2","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D2","text":"Non-existentia et latentia sub eodem processu formativo tractantur ac existentia manifesta.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A3","CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D3","text":"Lux hic non tantum visibilitatem, sed transitum a latentia ad determinatam formam significat.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D4","text":"Repraesentatio non imitatur simpliciter rem iam constitutam, sed partem habet in eius productione ad manifestationem.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A5","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD1","text":"Ordo rerum a forma simplicissima incipit et per manifestationem ad cognitionem formabilem procedit.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A1","CH_MHON_THEI:A2","CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD2","text":"Distinctio inter ontologiam et repraesentationem structuram separatam non constituit; res producitur eo ipso quo repraesentatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A5","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD3","text":"Potestas formae extenditur ultra datum: etiam non-existentia et latentia intra campum productionis figurativae recipiuntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A3","CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD4","text":"Simplicitas formalis fit principium totalizationis, quia per paucas formas ad classes rerum diversas acceditur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A1","CH_MHON_THEI:A2","CH_MHON_THEI:A3","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet formas sensibiles tantum res iam completas repraesentare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet existentiam et repraesentabilitatem esse ordines penitus disiunctos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet latentia Naturae esse chaos informe quod nulla forma simplici comprehendi possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet non-existentia omnino carere quavis possibilitate manifestationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit ideam rei quae ante omnem formam et repraesentationem absolute inaccessibilis maneret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit divisionem ultimam inter producere et significare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit necessitatem multiplicis apparatus ad transitum a latentia ad lucem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX4","text":"Textus tacite praecludit realitatem quae neque existens, neque non existens, neque latens in forma aliqua comprehendi possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS1","text":"Linea recta + circulus → formae primae et simplicissimae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS2","text":"Formae primae → ordinatio rerum existentium, non-existentium et latentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS3","text":"Latentia sub Naturae involucris → productio in lucem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS4","text":"Productio in lucem → repraesentatio determinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS5","text":"Productio + repraesentatio → transitus communis ab occultatione ad manifestationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AF1","text":"Simplicissimae formae → comprehensio existentium et non-existentium → accessus ad latentia Naturae → productio in lucem → repraesentatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AF2","text":"Occultatio → forma prima → manifestatio → res repraesentabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME1","text":"Ager rerum reordinatur ita ut existentia, non-existentia et latentia sub una operatione formativa considerari possint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter productionem et repraesentationem corruit, quia utraque eodem actu manifestationis perficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME3","text":"Forma geometrica non iam est ornamentum descriptivum, sed instrumentum quo res ad lucem et cognitionem perveniunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME4","text":"Latentia Naturae fit status transitorius, non terminus ultimus rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT1","text":"Surface: linea recta et circulus tamquam formae primae et simplicissimae ponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT2","text":"Structural: formae simplices ordinant productionem rerum existentium, non-existentium et latentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: repraesentatio redefinitur ut operatio quae rem in lucem producit, non ut imitatio passiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: res a latentia ad manifestationem per transitum formativum procedit; distinctio inter esse constitutum et esse producendum aperitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam machinam: forma prima, latentia Naturae, productio et repraesentatio sunt eius nuclei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret, quia omnes termini ad unum transitum ab occulto ad manifestum referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT3","text":"Firmissimum est nexus inter simplicitatem formarum et productionem in lucem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT4","text":"Determinatio relationis inter res non existentes et res latentes nondum plene explicata manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT5","text":"Tensionem constituit quod productio simul rem efficere et rem repraesentare dicitur, sine distinctione ulteriore inter constitutionem et significationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum textus: a lineae rectae circuloque, tamquam formis primis, ad productionem et repraesentationem rerum occultarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222229155693Z_a2e45624","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM I.","source_sha256":"ff62e886dd7024920a97e61c537d6f03da461dd1700c18704497f323a9dff26c","sha256":"5171471e4ab2af86c248b5f8322c58774982094baf36eaab99f533b07b3be524","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:22:29.156702+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumentative Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS1","text":"The primary and simplest forms of things are constituted by the straight line and the circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS2","text":"These forms comprehend existing things, non-existing things, and those things that lie hidden in Nature's coverings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS3","text":"What lies hidden is brought into light through the simplest forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS4","text":"Production is at once the representation of that which was previously hidden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AS5","text":"The argumentation is reconstructive and ontological-representational: it proceeds from primary forms to the manifestation of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A1","text":"The straight line is one of the primary and simplest forms of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A2","text":"The circle is one of the primary and simplest forms of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A3","text":"The nature of things contains not only existents, but also non-existents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A4","text":"In Nature certain things lie hidden beneath coverings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A5","text":"The simplest form can bring into light that which lies hidden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:A6","text":"The production of a thing and the representation of a thing are conjoined in one operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX1","text":"Primary things are constituted most simply not through a multitude of forms, but through the straight line and the circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX2","text":"Manifestation is not limited to things already existing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX3","text":"That which lies hidden in Nature beneath a covering is not outside the order of producible things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX4","text":"Production is not separable from representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:NX5","text":"The invisible or hidden does not remain absolutely unavailable, if its form can be brought into light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D1","text":"The primary form at once has an ontological and a representational function.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A1","CH_MHON_THEI:A2","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D2","text":"Non-existence and hiddenness are treated under the same formative process as manifest existence.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A3","CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D3","text":"Here light signifies not only visibility, but the passage from hiddenness to determinate form.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:D4","text":"Representation does not simply imitate a thing already constituted, but takes part in its production toward manifestation.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A5","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD1","text":"The order of things begins from the simplest form and proceeds through manifestation to formable cognition.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A1","CH_MHON_THEI:A2","CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD2","text":"The distinction between ontology and representation does not constitute a separate structure; the thing is produced precisely insofar as it is represented.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A5","CH_MHON_THEI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD3","text":"The power of form extends beyond what is given: even non-existence and hiddenness are admitted within the field of figurative production.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A3","CH_MHON_THEI:A4","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SD4","text":"Formal simplicity becomes a principle of totalization, because through few forms one approaches diverse classes of things.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEI:A1","CH_MHON_THEI:A2","CH_MHON_THEI:A3","CH_MHON_THEI:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX1","text":"It must be false that sensible forms represent only things already complete.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX2","text":"It must be false that existence and representability are entirely disjoined orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX3","text":"It must be false that Nature's hiddenness is formless chaos that cannot be comprehended by any simple form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:DNX4","text":"It must be false that non-existents wholly lack any possibility of manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX1","text":"The text excludes the idea of a thing that would remain absolutely inaccessible prior to every form and representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX2","text":"The text excludes an ultimate division between producing and signifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX3","text":"The text excludes the necessity of a multiple apparatus for the passage from hiddenness to light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:SNX4","text":"The text silently precludes a reality that can be comprehended in no form as either existing, non-existing, or hidden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS1","text":"Straight line + circle → primary and simplest forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS2","text":"Primary forms → ordering of existing, non-existing, and hidden things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS3","text":"Hiddenness beneath Nature's coverings → production into light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS4","text":"Production into light → determinate representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:FGS5","text":"Production + representation → common passage from concealment to manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AF1","text":"Simplest forms → comprehension of existents and non-existents → access to Nature's hidden things → production into light → representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:AF2","text":"Concealment → primary form → manifestation → representable thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME1","text":"The field of things is reordered such that existence, non-existence, and hiddenness can be considered under one formative operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME2","text":"The opposition between production and representation collapses, because each is accomplished in the same act of manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME3","text":"Geometrical form is no longer a descriptive ornament, but an instrument by which things come to light and cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ME4","text":"Nature's hiddenness becomes a transitory state, not the ultimate end of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT1","text":"Surface: the straight line and the circle are posited as primary and simplest forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT2","text":"Structural: simple forms order the production of existing, non-existing, and hidden things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: representation is redefined as an operation that brings the thing into light, not as passive imitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: the thing proceeds from hiddenness to manifestation through a formative passage; the distinction between constituted being and being to be produced is opened.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the mechanism: primary form, Nature's hiddenness, production, and representation are its nuclei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally, because all terms refer to one passage from the hidden to the manifest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT3","text":"The strongest connection is that between the simplicity of forms and production into light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT4","text":"The determination of the relation between non-existing things and hidden things remains not yet fully explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT5","text":"It constitutes a tension that production is said at once to bring about the thing and to represent the thing, without a further distinction between constitution and signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEI:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text: from the straight line and circle, as primary forms, to the production and representation of hidden things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEI@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_THEI:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 02","title":"Theorem I.","context":"Chapter 02","original_title":"Theorema I.","original_context":"Chapter 02"},"original_title":"Theorema I.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2","layer":"CH","title":"Theorem II.","order":3,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_2"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_2@R001","sha256":"e1720521e8bb9c6e244a4d280525e194bc92facacb4804a7bbf8b1c04dd17701","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS1","text":"Geometrica quaestio est quomodo Circulus et Recta efficiantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS2","text":"Recta sine Puncto et Circulus sine Recta artificiose fieri non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS3","text":"Punctum, ratione Monadis, principium rerum et esse constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS4","text":"Omnis peripheria, quantaecumque sit, ministerio Puncti centralis indiget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS5","text":"Argumentatio geometrica transit in ordinem ontologicum: figura fundatur in centro, centrum in Puncto, Punctum in Monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","text":"Recta sine Puncto artificiose fieri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A2","text":"Circulus sine Recta artificiose fieri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","text":"Punctum ratione Monadis ad rerum exordium pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A4","text":"Punctum ratione Monadis ad exordium ipsius esse pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A5","text":"Circulus quaelibet peripheria est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","text":"Omnis peripheria centrum implicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A7","text":"Centrum per Punctum constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A8","text":"Ministerium centrale Puncti a magnitudine peripheriae non tollitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX1","text":"Recta non est figura Puncto carens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX2","text":"Circulus non est figura Recta carens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX3","text":"Peripheria nulla est a centro omnino separata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX4","text":"Magnitudo peripheriae centrum superfluum non reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX5","text":"Origo rerum non ponitur sine principio unitario Puncti vel Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D1","text":"Si Recta Puncto indiget et Circulus Recta indiget, Circulus mediate Puncto indiget.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","CH_MHON_TH_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D2","text":"Si omnis peripheria centrum implicat et centrum Punctum requirit, nulla peripheria sine Puncto centralis subsistit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D3","text":"Circulus non solum geometricum ambitum, sed seriem dependentiae a Recta ad Punctum exhibet.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A2","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D4","text":"Punctum fit terminus communis inter constructionem figurarum et originem rerum.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D5","text":"Primatus Monadis non est tantum temporalis, sed principium constitutivum relationis inter Punctum, centrum et figuram.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A4","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD1","text":"Geometrica figura hic demonstratur tamquam effectus ordinis ontologici, non tamquam compositio sine fundamento.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","CH_MHON_TH_2:A2","CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A4","CH_MHON_TH_2:A5","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7","CH_MHON_TH_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD2","text":"Unitas Monadis a centro per figuras diffunditur quin centrum in peripheriam dissolvatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD3","text":"Extensio quantitativa peripheriae principium eius qualitativum non mutat.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD4","text":"Textus constituit ordinem generativum in quo principium simplex necessitatem figurarum compositarum regit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX1","text":"Falsum est principia geometricorum esse figuras iam extensas potius quam Punctum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX2","text":"Falsum est peripheriam posse per se constitui sine relatione ad centrum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX3","text":"Falsum est magnitudinem principium unitatis superare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX4","text":"Falsum est originem ontologicam rerum a principio indivisibili separari posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX5","text":"Falsum est constructionem geometricam processum mere materialem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit mundum figurarum sine centro originario.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit pluralitatem absolutam quae ad unitatem Monadis non refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit peripheriam quae centrum tantum accidentaliter vel posterius recipiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX4","text":"Textus excludit conceptionem in qua esse et figura a principio communi seiunguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS1","text":"Monadis → Punctum → Centrum → Peripheria → Circulus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS2","text":"Puncti absentia → Rectae impossibilitas; Rectae absentia → Circuli impossibilitas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS3","text":"Punctum constituit Rectam; Recta mediat Circulum; centrum continet peripheriam; ergo Circulus Puncto centraliter dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS4","text":"Geometrica dependentia → ontologica interpretatio → universalis necessitas centri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AF1","text":"Impossibilitas constructionis sine fundamento → Puncti primatus → transitus a Puncto ad Monadem → constitutio centri → dependentia omnis peripheriae → universalizatio ministerii centralis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME1","text":"Punctum a minimo elemento geometrico ad principium rerum et esse reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME2","text":"Circulus et peripheria non amplius ut figurae autonomae, sed ut effectus ordinis centralis intelleguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter infinitam peripheriae magnitudinem et necessitatem Puncti dissolvitur: extensio variat, dependentia non variat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME4","text":"Relatio inter geometriae constructionem et ontologiam fit continua, quia eadem structura Puncti utrumque campum ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT1","text":"Surface: Recta, Circulus, Punctum et peripheria in ordine constructionis geometricae disponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT2","text":"Structural: Figurae constituuntur per relationem ordinatam inter Punctum, Rectam, centrum et peripheriam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Demonstratio geometrica adhibetur ad necessitatem principii centralis universalizandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Monas et Punctum ponuntur ut principia prima quibus Res et esse coeperunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam dependentiam Circuli a Recta, Rectae a Puncto et peripheriae a centro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT2","text":"Transitus a Puncto ad Monadem et ab geometrica constructione ad rerum esse textui necessarius est, quamvis modus huius identitatis non explicetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT3","text":"Structura interna cohaeret si Punctum simul geometricum principium et Monadis expressio ontologica accipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT4","text":"Firmissima est necessitas relationis inter centrum et peripheriam, quia textus eam a magnitudine peripheriae immunem declarat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT5","text":"Fragilis manet distinctio inter causam constructionis, principium ontologicum et ordinem temporalem in verbo “primo”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT6","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: ab impossibilitate figurarum sine fundamento ad universalitatem Puncti centralis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222355015043Z_758bb897","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM II.","source_sha256":"e1720521e8bb9c6e244a4d280525e194bc92facacb4804a7bbf8b1c04dd17701","sha256":"7c1cf8a4ba394a97a7bf9c4a0ddaab80d298e60ed3c50d7efa50682aebd60b07","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:23:55.017334+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS1","text":"The geometrical question is how a Circle and a Straight Line are produced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS2","text":"A Straight Line without a Point and a Circle without a Straight Line cannot be artificially produced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS3","text":"The Point, by reason of the Monad, constitutes the principle of things and of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS4","text":"Every circumference, however great it may be, requires the service of the central Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AS5","text":"The geometrical argument passes into the ontological order: figure is founded in the center, the center in the Point, and the Point in the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","text":"A Straight Line cannot be artificially produced without a Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A2","text":"A Circle cannot be artificially produced without a Straight Line.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","text":"The Point, by reason of the Monad, pertains to the beginning of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A4","text":"The Point, by reason of the Monad, pertains to the beginning of being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A5","text":"Every Circle is a circumference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","text":"Every circumference implies a center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A7","text":"The center is constituted through the Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:A8","text":"The central service of the Point is not removed by the magnitude of the circumference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX1","text":"A Straight Line is not a figure lacking a Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX2","text":"A Circle is not a figure lacking a Straight Line.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX3","text":"No circumference is wholly separated from its center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX4","text":"The magnitude of the circumference does not render the center superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:NX5","text":"The origin of things is not posited without the unitary principle of the Point or Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D1","text":"If a Straight Line requires a Point and a Circle requires a Straight Line, a Circle mediately requires a Point.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","CH_MHON_TH_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D2","text":"If every circumference implies a center and the center requires a Point, no circumference subsists without a central Point.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D3","text":"The Circle displays not only a geometrical circumference, but also a series of dependence from the Straight Line to the Point.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A2","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D4","text":"The Point becomes the common terminus between the construction of figures and the origin of things.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:D5","text":"The primacy of the Monad is not merely temporal, but is the constitutive principle of the relation among Point, center, and figure.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A4","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD1","text":"Geometrical figure is here demonstrated as an effect of ontological order, not as a composition without foundation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A1","CH_MHON_TH_2:A2","CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A4","CH_MHON_TH_2:A5","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7","CH_MHON_TH_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD2","text":"The unity of the Monad is diffused from the center through figures without the center being dissolved into the circumference.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD3","text":"The quantitative extension of the circumference does not alter its qualitative principle.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SD4","text":"The text establishes a generative order in which a simple principle governs the necessity of composite figures.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_2:A3","CH_MHON_TH_2:A6","CH_MHON_TH_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX1","text":"It is false that the principles of geometrical things are already extended figures rather than the Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX2","text":"It is false that a circumference can be constituted through itself without relation to a center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX3","text":"It is false that magnitude surpasses the principle of unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX4","text":"It is false that the ontological origin of things can be separated from an indivisible principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:DNX5","text":"It is false that geometrical construction is a merely material process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX1","text":"The text excludes a world of figures without an originating center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX2","text":"The text excludes an absolute plurality that is not referred to the unity of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX3","text":"The text excludes a circumference that receives the center only accidentally or subsequently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:SNX4","text":"The text excludes a conception in which being and figure are separated from a common principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS1","text":"Monad → Point → Center → Circumference → Circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS2","text":"Absence of the Point → impossibility of the Straight Line; absence of the Straight Line → impossibility of the Circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS3","text":"The Point constitutes the Straight Line; the Straight Line mediates the Circle; the center contains the circumference; therefore the Circle centrally depends on the Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:FGS4","text":"Geometrical dependence → ontological interpretation → universal necessity of the center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:AF1","text":"Impossibility of construction without a foundation → primacy of the Point → transition from the Point to the Monad → constitution of the center → dependence of every circumference → universalization of central service.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME1","text":"The Point is reclassified from the smallest geometrical element to the principle of things and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME2","text":"The Circle and circumference are understood no longer as autonomous figures, but as effects of central order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME3","text":"The opposition between the infinite magnitude of the circumference and the necessity of the Point is dissolved: extension varies, dependence does not vary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ME4","text":"The relation between geometrical construction and ontology becomes continuous, because the same structure of the Point orders both fields.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT1","text":"Surface: Straight Line, Circle, Point, and circumference are arranged in the order of geometrical construction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT2","text":"Structural: Figures are constituted through the ordered relation among Point, Straight Line, center, and circumference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Geometrical demonstration is employed to universalize the necessity of the central principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The Monad and the Point are posited as first principles by which things and being began.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the dependence of the Circle on the Straight Line, of the Straight Line on the Point, and of the circumference on the center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT2","text":"The transition from the Point to the Monad and from geometrical construction to the being of things is necessary to the text, although the manner of this identity is not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT3","text":"The internal structure coheres if the Point is understood simultaneously as a geometrical principle and an ontological expression of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT4","text":"The necessity of the relation between center and circumference is strongest, because the text declares it immune to the magnitude of the circumference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT5","text":"The distinction between the cause of construction, the ontological principle, and the temporal order in the word “first” remains fragile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_2:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: from the impossibility of figures without a foundation to the universality of the central Point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_2@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_2:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 03","title":"Theorem II.","context":"Chapter 03","original_title":"Theorema Ii.","original_context":"Chapter 03"},"original_title":"Theorema Ii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3","layer":"CH","title":"Theorem III.","order":4,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_3"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_3@R001","sha256":"472944e129356b2e5b727316b1f1043b40a8e3ee18233c2f726c1776f3e49e23","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo centrum conspicuum Monadis Hieroglyphicæ terram et ordinem corporum cælestium repraesentet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS2","text":"Figura ex puncto centrali ad circulum solarem et inde ad motus Lunæ procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS3","text":"Sol constituitur ut centrum dignitatis, dominus et rex Lunæ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS4","text":"Mutatio visibilis Lunæ explicatur per relationem eius ad formam, vicinitatem et radios Solis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS5","text":"Argumentatio est symbolica, cosmologica et reconstructiva: figura hieroglyphica ordinem cosmologicum per compositionem geometricam restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A1","text":"Punctum centrale conspicuum Monadis Hieroglyphicæ terram refert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A2","text":"Sol, Luna reliquique Planetæ circa terram suos cursus conficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","text":"Sol dignitatem summam obtinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A4","text":"Propter summam Solis dignitatem circulus integer Soli attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A5","text":"Circulus integer centro visibili notatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","text":"Hemicyclium Lunare circulo Solari subicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A7","text":"Luna Solem tamquam dominum et regem suum observat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A8","text":"Luna forma et vicinitate Solis afficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","text":"Luna lumen suum ad Solem convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A10","text":"Luna radiis solaribus imbuitur atque secundum relationem ad Solem variat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A11","text":"Luna, radiis solaribus imbuta, in cælo interdum quasi evanescit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A12","text":"Post aliquot dies Luna corniculata figura apparet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX1","text":"Centrum Monadis non est punctum abstractum sine referente cosmologico, sed terram refert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX2","text":"Circulus Solaris non est figura pura a centro separata, sed centro visibili constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX3","text":"Luna non est corpus a Sole autonomum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX4","text":"Lumen Lunare non exhibetur ut a Sole omnino independens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX5","text":"Mutatio Lunæ non definitur per formam stabilem et invariabilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX6","text":"Ordo astrorum non describitur ut distributio sine hierarchia dignitatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D1","text":"Terra fit centrum symbolicum circa quod cælestis ordo disponitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A1","CH_MHON_TH_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D2","text":"Sol fit mediatrix inter centrum terrestre et formas reliquorum corporum cælestium.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A2","CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D3","text":"Integritas circuli Solaris exprimit dignitatem eius superiorem.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A4","CH_MHON_TH_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D4","text":"Forma Lunæ explicatur ut effectus relationis Solaris potius quam ut proprietas isolata.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","CH_MHON_TH_3:A7","CH_MHON_TH_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D5","text":"Conversio Lunæ ad Solem coniungit ordinem motus cum dependentia luminis.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A7","CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","CH_MHON_TH_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D6","text":"Disparitio et reditus Lunæ efficiunt seriem temporalem inter formam occultam et formam corniculatam.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A10","CH_MHON_TH_3:A11","CH_MHON_TH_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD1","text":"Hieroglyphicum systema cosmologiam construit tamquam ordinem concentricum, in quo centrum terrestre et dignitas Solaris simul distributionem motuum determinant.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A1","CH_MHON_TH_3:A2","CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD2","text":"Forma Lunæ fit index relationis, quia eius visibilitas et configuratio ex gradu propinquitatis et irradiationis Solaris leguntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","CH_MHON_TH_3:A8","CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","CH_MHON_TH_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD3","text":"Hieroglyphicum temporalem mutationem in figura spatiali condensat: conversio, imminutio visibilitatis et corniculata apparentia unam seriem cosmicam efficiunt.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","CH_MHON_TH_3:A10","CH_MHON_TH_3:A11","CH_MHON_TH_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD4","text":"Dignitas politica, expressa nominibus domini et regis, structuram cosmologicam hierarchicam ordinat.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","CH_MHON_TH_3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX1","text":"Centrum geometricum sine cosmologica significatione tacite excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX2","text":"Corporum cælestium æqualitas functionalis excluditur, quia Sol dignitate præcellit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX3","text":"Luna ut principium luminis sui proprii et autonomi excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX4","text":"Forma ut status fixus excluditur; forma potius effectus relationis et temporis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX5","text":"Visibilitas ut simpliciter data et non-transformatibilis excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX6","text":"Motus astrorum ut processus materialis a symbolica hierarchia separabilis excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX1","text":"Impossibilis redditur cosmologia in qua centrum, dignitas et motus inter se disiunguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX2","text":"Præcluditur possibilitas Lunæ quæ Solem non respiciat nec ad eum lumen convertat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX3","text":"Præcluditur visio cæli ut campi uniformis, ubi nullum corpus principatum aut subordinationem obtinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX4","text":"Abest idea formæ cælestis a tempore separabilis; figura Lunæ tantum per mutationem relationis intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS1","text":"Punctum centrale → Terra → Ordo corporum circa centrum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS2","text":"Suprema dignitas Solis → Circulus integer → Centrum visibile → Figura Solaris privilegiata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS3","text":"Subordinatio Lunæ → Observatio Solis → Conversio luminis ad Solem → Imbutio radiis solaribus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS4","text":"Imbutio radiis → Mutatio formæ et visibilitatis → Disparitio quasi totalis → Reditus in figura corniculata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS5","text":"Centrum terrestre + principatus Solaris + dependentia Lunaris → Hieroglyphicum cosmologicum concentricum et temporale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AF1","text":"Punctum conspicuum → Terra ut centrum → Cursus planetarum circa centrum → Dignitas superior Solis → Circulus integer et centrum visibile → Subordinatio Lunæ → Conversio ad Solem → Mutatio luminis et formæ → Disparitio → Figura corniculata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME1","text":"Punctum centrale reclassificatur: ex elemento geometrico fit signum terræ et centrum ordinis cosmici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME2","text":"Circulus integer reclassificatur: ex figura abstracta fit signum dignitatis Solaris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME3","text":"Luna reclassificatur: ex corpus cæleste separatum fit forma relationalis a Sole definita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME4","text":"Mutatio visibilitatis reclassificatur: ex variatione isolata fit effectus irradiationis, conversionis et temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME5","text":"Oppositio inter motum et formam solvitur, quia forma Lunæ motum relationis Solaris visibilem reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT1","text":"Surface: Punctum, circulus, hemicyclium et figura corniculata referuntur ad terram, Solem et Lunam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT2","text":"Structural: Centrum terrestre, præcellentia Solaris et subordinatio Lunaris constituunt ordinem concentricum et hierarchicum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Hieroglyphicum transitum a figura ad cosmologiam instituit, ita ut geometria relationes dignitatis, motus et dependentiae legibiles reddat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Corpora cælestia constituuntur ut entia relationalia, quorum forma et visibilitas per ordinem Solaris irradiationis temporaliter mutantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendum motum a puncto centrali ad terram, a terra ad Solem et a Sole ad Lunam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT2","text":"Distinctio inter circulum integrum Solaris et hemicyclium Lunare est necessaria ad hierarchiam geometricam restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT3","text":"Dependentia luminis, conversio ad Solem et mutatio temporalis explicant seriem a visibilitate ad disparitionem et corniculatam formam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT4","text":"Relatio inter circulum Solaris et hemicyclium Lunare non omnibus geometricis terminis plene determinatur in textu tradito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT5","text":"Systema interne cohaeret quoad principatum Solis et dependentiam Lunæ, sed nexus exactus inter motum, formam et irradiationem partim symbolicus manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT6","text":"Firmitas argumenti in structura hierarchica et relationali consistit; eius fragilitas in transitu non demonstrato a figura geometrica ad causationem physicam apparet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222421075587Z_6d07cc50","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM III.","source_sha256":"472944e129356b2e5b727316b1f1043b40a8e3ee18233c2f726c1776f3e49e23","sha256":"c68e6e39727bcc81a5fccecc2b288a7765fcaaca7bd0f8137adbcec137e02b64","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:24:21.077440+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS1","text":"The central question is how the conspicuous center of the Hieroglyphic Monad represents the earth and the order of the celestial bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS2","text":"The figure proceeds from the central point to the solar circle and thence to the motions of the Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS3","text":"The Sun is established as the center of dignity, lord and king of the Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS4","text":"The visible change of the Moon is explained through its relation to the form, proximity, and rays of the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AS5","text":"The argumentation is symbolic, cosmological, and reconstructive: the hieroglyphic figure restores the cosmological order through geometric composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A1","text":"The conspicuous central point of the Hieroglyphic Monad refers to the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A2","text":"The Sun, Moon, and remaining Planets complete their courses around the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","text":"The Sun possesses the highest dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A4","text":"Because of the Sun's highest dignity, a complete circle is attributed to the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A5","text":"The complete circle is marked by a visible center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","text":"The lunar hemicycle is subjected to the solar circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A7","text":"The Moon observes the Sun as its lord and king.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A8","text":"The Moon is affected by the form and proximity of the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","text":"The Moon turns its light toward the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A10","text":"The Moon is imbued with solar rays and varies according to its relation to the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A11","text":"The Moon, imbued with solar rays, sometimes almost vanishes in the sky.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:A12","text":"After several days, the Moon appears in a horned figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX1","text":"The center of the Monad is not an abstract point without a cosmological referent, but refers to the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX2","text":"The Solar circle is not a pure figure separated from the center, but is constituted by a visible center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX3","text":"The Moon is not a body autonomous from the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX4","text":"Lunar light is not presented as wholly independent from the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX5","text":"The change of the Moon is not defined by a stable and invariable form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:NX6","text":"The order of the stars is not described as a distribution without a hierarchy of dignities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D1","text":"The earth becomes the symbolic center around which the celestial order is arranged.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A1","CH_MHON_TH_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D2","text":"The Sun becomes the mediator between the terrestrial center and the forms of the remaining celestial bodies.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A2","CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D3","text":"The wholeness of the Solar circle expresses its superior dignity.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A4","CH_MHON_TH_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D4","text":"The form of the Moon is explained as an effect of the Solar relation rather than as an isolated property.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","CH_MHON_TH_3:A7","CH_MHON_TH_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D5","text":"The Moon's turning toward the Sun joins the order of motion with the dependence of light.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A7","CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","CH_MHON_TH_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:D6","text":"The disappearance and return of the Moon produce a temporal series between hidden form and horned form.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A10","CH_MHON_TH_3:A11","CH_MHON_TH_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD1","text":"The hieroglyphic system constructs cosmology as a concentric order, in which the terrestrial center and Solar dignity together determine the distribution of motions.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A1","CH_MHON_TH_3:A2","CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD2","text":"The form of the Moon becomes an index of relation, because its visibility and configuration are read from the degree of Solar proximity and irradiation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","CH_MHON_TH_3:A8","CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","CH_MHON_TH_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD3","text":"The hieroglyphic condenses temporal change into a spatial figure: turning, diminution of visibility, and horned appearance produce one cosmic series.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A9","CH_MHON_TH_3:A10","CH_MHON_TH_3:A11","CH_MHON_TH_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SD4","text":"Political dignity, expressed by the names of lord and king, orders the hierarchical cosmological structure.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_3:A3","CH_MHON_TH_3:A6","CH_MHON_TH_3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX1","text":"A geometric center without cosmological significance is tacitly excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX2","text":"The functional equality of celestial bodies is excluded, because the Sun excels in dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX3","text":"The Moon as a principle of its own and autonomous light is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX4","text":"Form as a fixed state is excluded; rather, form is an effect of relation and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX5","text":"Visibility as simply given and non-transformable is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:DNX6","text":"The motion of the stars as a material process separable from symbolic hierarchy is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX1","text":"A cosmology in which center, dignity, and motion are disjoined from one another is rendered impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a Moon that does not regard the Sun nor turn its light toward it is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX3","text":"The vision of the sky as a uniform field, in which no body possesses primacy or subordination, is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:SNX4","text":"The idea of a celestial form separable from time is absent; the figure of the Moon is understood only through the change of relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS1","text":"Central point → Earth → Order of bodies around the center.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS2","text":"Supreme dignity of the Sun → Complete circle → Visible center → Privileged Solar figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS3","text":"Subordination of the Moon → Observation of the Sun → Turning of light toward the Sun → Imbuement with solar rays.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS4","text":"Imbuement with rays → Change of form and visibility → Almost total disappearance → Return in horned figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:FGS5","text":"Terrestrial center + Solar primacy + Lunar dependence → Concentric and temporal cosmological hieroglyphic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:AF1","text":"Conspicuous point → Earth as center → Courses of the planets around the center → Superior dignity of the Sun → Complete circle and visible center → Subordination of the Moon → Turning toward the Sun → Change of light and form → Disappearance → Horned figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME1","text":"The central point is reclassified: from a geometric element it becomes a sign of the earth and the center of cosmic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME2","text":"The complete circle is reclassified: from an abstract figure it becomes a sign of Solar dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME3","text":"The Moon is reclassified: from a separate celestial body it becomes a relational form defined by the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME4","text":"The change of visibility is reclassified: from an isolated variation it becomes an effect of irradiation, turning, and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ME5","text":"The opposition between motion and form is resolved, because the form of the Moon renders the motion of the Solar relation visible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT1","text":"Surface: Point, circle, hemicycle, and horned figure refer to the earth, Sun, and Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT2","text":"Structural: The terrestrial center, Solar preeminence, and Lunar subordination constitute a concentric and hierarchical order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The hieroglyphic institutes the transition from figure to cosmology, so that geometry renders relations of dignity, motion, and dependence legible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Celestial bodies are constituted as relational beings, whose form and visibility are temporally changed through the order of Solar irradiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the movement from the central point to the earth, from the earth to the Sun, and from the Sun to the Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT2","text":"The distinction between the complete Solar circle and the lunar hemicycle is necessary for restoring the geometric hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT3","text":"The dependence of light, turning toward the Sun, and temporal change explain the series from visibility to disappearance and horned form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT4","text":"The relation between the Solar circle and the lunar hemicycle is not fully determined in all geometric terms in the transmitted text.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT5","text":"The system is internally coherent with respect to the primacy of the Sun and the dependence of the Moon, but the exact nexus between motion, form, and irradiation remains partly symbolic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_3:MRT6","text":"The strength of the argument consists in its hierarchical and relational structure; its fragility appears in the undemonstrated transition from geometric figure to physical causation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_3@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_3:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 04","title":"Theorem III.","context":"Chapter 04","original_title":"Theorema Iii.","original_context":"Chapter 04"},"original_title":"Theorema Iii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R E M IIII.","order":5,"parents":["RAW_MHON_THEO"],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEO@R001","sha256":"cbf83757c1ff011cb328700a53af0294a50c1c71554b6863f332852c2247f666","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quomodo Lunæ hemicyclium, quamvis Solari Circulo quasi superius priusque videatur, ad Solem ordinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS2","text":"Nova constitutio ponit Lunam Solem tamquam Dominum Regemque suum observare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS3","text":"Fundamentum relationis est forma Solis et eius vicinitas, quibus Luna quasi assimilari videtur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS4","text":"Probatio procedit per conversionem luminis, irradiationem solarem et apparentem transformationem Lunæ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS5","text":"Motus concluditur per disparitionem Lunæ e caelo et eius post aliquot dies reditum in figuram corniculatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A1","text":"Lunæ hemicyclium Solari Circulo quasi superius priusque apparet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A2","text":"Sol Lunæ Dominus et Rex observatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A3","text":"Luna Solis formam et vicinitatem appetere ac diligere videtur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A4","text":"Luna magnitudinem Solis in semidiametro æmulatur, saltem vulgaribus apparentem hominibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A5","text":"Luna lumen suum semper ad Solem convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A6","text":"Luna radiis solaribus imbui appetit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A7","text":"Luna, quasi in Solem transformata, toto caelo disparere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A8","text":"Post aliquot dies Luna figura corniculata rursus apparet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A9","text":"Apparentia Lunæ per successionem figurarum et vicinitatum temporaliter determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX1","text":"Luna, quamvis quasi superior et prior appareat, non constituitur ut potestas a Sole independens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX2","text":"Lumen Lunæ non sistitur ut a Solis relatione separatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX3","text":"Luna non permanet in una eademque figura apparente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX4","text":"Transformativa assimilatio ad Solem non terminatur in perpetua praesentia Lunæ in caelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX5","text":"Disparitio Lunæ non est eius ultimus status, quia figura corniculata postea restituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX6","text":"Magnitudo hic non definitur ut mensura absoluta, sed ut magnitudo vulgaribus hominibus apparens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D1","text":"Apparens superioritas Lunæ non tollit eius ordinationem ad Solem.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A1","CH_MHON_THEO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D2","text":"Forma et vicinitas Solis efficiunt ut Luna non solum lumen recipere, sed etiam Soli assimilari videatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A2","CH_MHON_THEO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D3","text":"Conversio luminis ad Solem significat relationem directionalem, qua Luna per Solem visibiliter determinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D4","text":"Appetitus radiorum solarum ducit ad statum in quo distinctio apparens inter Lunam et Solem maxime attenuatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A6","CH_MHON_THEO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D5","text":"Disparitio caeli et reditus corniculatus constituunt unum motum periodicum potius quam conversionem irrevocabilem.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A7","CH_MHON_THEO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D6","text":"Figura corniculata post aliquot dies est effectus temporalis relationis Lunæ ad Solem.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A8","CH_MHON_THEO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD1","text":"Apparens hierarchia cosmica simul continet inversionem ordinum: Luna quasi superior apparet, sed causaliter et simbolice ad Solem subordinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A1","CH_MHON_THEO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD2","text":"Identitas Lunæ non ut substantia visualiter stabilis, sed ut series relationum ad Solem producitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A3","CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD3","text":"Lumen efficit medium transformationis: per irradiationem Luna a propria figura ad solaris similitudinis limen transit.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A4","CH_MHON_THEO:A6","CH_MHON_THEO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD4","text":"Tempus non tantum mutationem observat, sed formas Lunæ in circulum apparentiarum ordinat.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A7","CH_MHON_THEO:A8","CH_MHON_THEO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD5","text":"Relatio ad Solem simul est principium visibilitatis, assimilationis et disparitionis Lunæ.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A2","CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX1","text":"Systema tacite excludit Lunam cuius forma et lumen a relatione Solari plene explicarentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit oppositionem simplicem inter Lunam activam et Solem passivum, quia Luna ad Solem convertitur et ab eo formatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit identitatem quæ uno momento et una figura tota stabiliretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit distinctionem rigidam inter visibilitatem et transformationem, quia idem lumen Lunam ostendit et quasi abscondit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit temporalitatem rectilineam, in qua transformatio ad Solem sine reversione procederet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX1","text":"Textus circumit ideam luminis Lunaris absolute proprii, quia lumen in directione et radiis Solaribus explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX2","text":"Textus praecludit Lunam tamquam centrum ultimum ordinis cosmici, quamvis eius species momentanee quasi superior appareat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX3","text":"Textus relinquit indisponibilem ideam separationis absolutae inter corpora quæ per formam, vicinitatem et lumen definiuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX4","text":"Impossibilis fit figura Lunæ quæ extra vicissitudinem Solarem semel pro semper determinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX5","text":"Absentia constitutiva est autonomia Lunæ: eius apparentia semper aliquid extra Lunam, Solem, supponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS1","text":"Apparens superioritas Lunæ → recognitio Solis ut Domini et Regis → subordinatio relationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS2","text":"Forma et vicinitas Solis → æmulatio magnitudinis et conversio luminis → assimilatio Lunæ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS3","text":"Appetitus radiorum → quasi-transformătio in Solem → disparitio e caelo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS4","text":"Intervallum temporale → reapparitio figuræ corniculatæ → clausura circularis motus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS5","text":"Species initialis → relatio Solarizata → indistinctio apparens → absentia → species nova.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AF1","text":"Hemicyclium Lunæ quasi superius priusque → Solis auctoritas → assimilatio formæ et luminis → disparitio in solarizatione → reditus corniculatus post aliquot dies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AF2","text":"Apparentia Lunæ → relatio ad Solem → transformatio temporalis → restitutio alterius figuræ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME1","text":"Oppositio inter superioritatem Lunæ et dominationem Solis reclassificatur ut distinctio inter apparentem ordinem et relationalem dependentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME2","text":"Lumen non iam tantum proprietas visualis est, sed agens quod directionem, assimilationem et disparitionem coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME3","text":"Figura Lunæ mutatur a forma fixa in seriem statuum temporalium: hemicyclium, absentia, corniculata species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME4","text":"Disparitio non classificatur ut annihilatio, sed ut extrema forma assimilationis ad Solem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME5","text":"Vicinitas fit principium conceptuale quod hierarchiam, similitudinem et mutationem simul ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT1","text":"Surface: Luna variis figuris apparet, ad Solem lumen convertit, evanescit et postea corniculata redit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT2","text":"Structural: Forma Lunæ per vicinitatem, radios et relationem ad Solem determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Apparens superioritas ad subordinatam assimilationem convertitur; quod primo quasi prius apparet, postea a relatione ad Dominum explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Luna non ut ens visualiter immobile, sed ut corpus per periodicam transformationem et reversionem constitutum ponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam catenam a superioritate apparente ad dominationem Solis, assimilationem, disparitionem et reditum corniculatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia interna firma est in eo quod omnes mutationes ad relationem Solarem et ad successionem temporalem referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT3","text":"Determinatio astronomica exacta non satis stabilitur, quia textus describit apparentias et non explicat mechanismum geometricum completum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT4","text":"Verba «videtur», «apparente hominibus» et «quasi» limites epistemicos assertionibus imponunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT5","text":"Tensionalis commissura manet inter Lunæ quasi-superiorem positionem et eius statum Solariter subordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT6","text":"Altera tensio manet inter transformationem quasi irrevocabilem in Solem et reversionem ad figuram corniculatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum textus: ab apparentia formali ad relationem dominativam, inde ad solarizationem, absentiam et reappearance temporale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222248687561Z_0167a493","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R E M IIII.","source_sha256":"cbf83757c1ff011cb328700a53af0294a50c1c71554b6863f332852c2247f666","sha256":"f1d50a6f1464c0d8818e4dd634be223539af8d6112d2a02bb059ab8fe9d8cae1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:22:48.689977+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS1","text":"The question is how the Moon's semicircle, although it seems as though higher and prior to the Solar Circle, is ordered toward the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS2","text":"The new constitution holds that the Moon observes the Sun as its Lord and King.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS3","text":"The foundation of the relation is the form of the Sun and its proximity, by which the Moon seems as though to be assimilated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS4","text":"The proof proceeds through the turning of light, solar irradiation, and the apparent transformation of the Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AS5","text":"The movement is concluded through the Moon's disappearance from the sky and its return after some days in a horned figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A1","text":"The Moon's semicircle appears as though higher and prior to the Solar Circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A2","text":"The Sun is observed as the Moon's Lord and King.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A3","text":"The Moon seems to seek and cherish the Sun's form and proximity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A4","text":"The Moon emulates the Sun's magnitude in its semidiameter, at least as it appears to ordinary people.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A5","text":"The Moon always turns its light toward the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A6","text":"The Moon seeks to be imbued with solar rays.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A7","text":"The Moon, as though transformed into the Sun, can disappear from the whole sky.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A8","text":"After some days the Moon appears again in a horned figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:A9","text":"The Moon's appearance is temporally determined through a succession of figures and proximities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX1","text":"The Moon, although it appears as though superior and prior, is not constituted as a power independent of the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX2","text":"The Moon's light is not presented as separated from its relation to the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX3","text":"The Moon does not remain in one and the same apparent figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX4","text":"Transformative assimilation to the Sun does not end in the Moon's perpetual presence in the sky.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX5","text":"The Moon's disappearance is not its final state, because the horned figure is afterward restored.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:NX6","text":"Magnitude here is not defined as an absolute measure, but as a magnitude apparent to ordinary people.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D1","text":"The Moon's apparent superiority does not remove its ordering toward the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A1","CH_MHON_THEO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D2","text":"The form and proximity of the Sun bring it about that the Moon seems not only to receive light, but also to be assimilated to the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A2","CH_MHON_THEO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D3","text":"The turning of light toward the Sun signifies a directional relation by which the Moon is visibly determined through the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D4","text":"The seeking of solar rays leads to a state in which the apparent distinction between the Moon and the Sun is most attenuated.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A6","CH_MHON_THEO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D5","text":"Disappearance from the sky and horned return constitute one periodic movement rather than an irrevocable conversion.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A7","CH_MHON_THEO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:D6","text":"The horned figure after some days is a temporal effect of the Moon's relation to the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A8","CH_MHON_THEO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD1","text":"The apparent cosmic hierarchy simultaneously contains an inversion of orders: the Moon appears as though superior, but is causally and symbolically subordinated to the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A1","CH_MHON_THEO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD2","text":"The identity of the Moon is produced not as a visually stable substance, but as a series of relations to the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A3","CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD3","text":"Light effects a medium of transformation: through irradiation, the Moon passes from its own figure to the threshold of solar likeness.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A4","CH_MHON_THEO:A6","CH_MHON_THEO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD4","text":"Time not only observes change, but orders the Moon's forms into a circle of appearances.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A7","CH_MHON_THEO:A8","CH_MHON_THEO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SD5","text":"Relation to the Sun is at once the principle of the Moon's visibility, assimilation, and disappearance.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEO:A2","CH_MHON_THEO:A5","CH_MHON_THEO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX1","text":"The system tacitly excludes a Moon whose form and light would be fully explained apart from relation to the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a simple opposition between an active Moon and a passive Sun, because the Moon turns toward the Sun and is formed by it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an identity that would be wholly stabilized in one moment and one figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a rigid distinction between visibility and transformation, because the same light shows and as though conceals the Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a rectilinear temporality in which transformation toward the Sun would proceed without return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX1","text":"The text circumvents the idea of an absolutely proper lunar light, because light is explained in solar direction and rays.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX2","text":"The text precludes the Moon as the ultimate center of cosmic order, although its appearance momentarily seems as though superior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX3","text":"The text leaves unavailable the idea of absolute separation between bodies defined through form, proximity, and light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX4","text":"Impossible is a figure of the Moon that is once and for all determined outside solar vicissitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:SNX5","text":"The constitutive absence is the Moon's autonomy: its appearance always presupposes something outside the Moon, namely the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS1","text":"The Moon's apparent superiority → recognition of the Sun as Lord and King → subordination of the relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS2","text":"The Sun's form and proximity → emulation of magnitude and turning of light → assimilation of the Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS3","text":"Seeking of rays → quasi-transformation into the Sun → disappearance from the sky.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS4","text":"Temporal interval → reappearance of the horned figure → circular closure of the movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:FGS5","text":"Initial appearance → solarized relation → apparent indistinction → absence → new appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AF1","text":"The Moon's semicircle as though higher and prior → the Sun's authority → assimilation of form and light → disappearance in solarization → horned return after some days.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:AF2","text":"The Moon's appearance → relation to the Sun → temporal transformation → restoration of another figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME1","text":"The opposition between the Moon's superiority and the Sun's domination is reclassified as a distinction between apparent order and relational dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME2","text":"Light is no longer merely a visual property, but an agent that conjoins direction, assimilation, and disappearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME3","text":"The Moon's figure changes from a fixed form into a series of temporal states: semicircle, absence, horned appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME4","text":"Disappearance is not classified as annihilation, but as the extreme form of assimilation to the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ME5","text":"Proximity becomes a conceptual principle that simultaneously orders hierarchy, likeness, and change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT1","text":"Surface: The Moon appears in various figures, turns its light toward the Sun, vanishes, and later returns horned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT2","text":"Structural: The Moon's form is determined through proximity, rays, and relation to the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Apparent superiority is converted into subordinate assimilation; what first appears as though prior is afterward explained by relation to the Lord.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The Moon is posited not as a visually immobile being, but as a body constituted through periodic transformation and return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the chain from apparent superiority to the Sun's domination, assimilation, disappearance, and horned return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT2","text":"The internal coherence is firm in that all changes are referred to solar relation and temporal succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT3","text":"Exact astronomical determination is not sufficiently established, because the text describes appearances and does not explain the complete geometric mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT4","text":"The words «videtur», «apparente hominibus» and «quasi» impose epistemic limits upon the assertions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT5","text":"A tension remains between the Moon's quasi-superior position and its solar-subordinated state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT6","text":"Another tension remains between quasi-irrevocable transformation into the Sun and return to the horned figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEO:MRT7","text":"The restoration preserves the text's true movement: from formal appearance to dominative relation, thence to solarization, absence, and temporal reappearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEO@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_THEO:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R E M A IIII."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 05","title":"T H E O R E M IIII.","context":"Chapter 05","original_title":"T H E O R E M A Iiii.","original_context":"Chapter 05"},"original_title":"T H E O R E M A Iiii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R E M V.","order":6,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_4"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_4@R001","sha256":"61d74a10f78b4e927c2c54147a79c568930aadb07889cdadf46a9ba96ef8b5ac","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo relatio inter semicirculum Lunarem et complementum Solare diem constituat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS2","text":"Semicirculus Lunaris ad complementum Solare perductus unit vesperum et mane in unum diem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS3","text":"Haec unitas constituit diem primum, non simpliciter continuationem dierum iam datorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS4","text":"Dies primus definitur per productionem Lucis et ad ordinem Philosophorum refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis est: figura complementaria → unificatio temporalium → constitutio principii → designatio philosophica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A1","text":"Semicirculus Lunaris est figura partialis quae relatione ad aliud complementum determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A2","text":"Complementum Solare est terminus ad quem Semicirculus Lunaris perducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","text":"Perductio semicirculi ad complementum constituit relationem completivam inter Lunam et Solem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A4","text":"Vesper et mane in hac relatione ad unum diem pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A5","text":"Unus dies sic constitutus potest esse principium ordinis temporalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A6","text":"Dies primus est dies in quo Lux facta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A7","text":"Ordo hic ad designationem Philosophorum refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX1","text":"Dies non ex vespera vel mane solitarie constituitur, sed ex eorum coniunctione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX2","text":"Semicirculus Lunaris non ut figura plena aut iam completa tractatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX3","text":"Complementum Solare non est obiectum separatum a figura Lunari, sed eius terminatio constitutiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX4","text":"Primus dies non est unus dies inter alios, sed initium ordinis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX5","text":"Lux non ad eventum posteriorem diei reducitur, sed ad eius constitutionem primariam pertinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D1","text":"Per complementum Solare, partialitas Semicirculi Lunaris in unitatem ordinis convertitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A1","CH_MHON_TH_4:A2","CH_MHON_TH_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D2","text":"Si vesper et mane unum diem efficiunt, temporis divisio in formam unam ordinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D3","text":"Dies ex relatione complementaria oritur, non ex sola successione temporali.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D4","text":"Unitas diei primum locum obtinet quia ad productionem Lucis refertur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A5","CH_MHON_TH_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D5","text":"Designatio Philosophorum ponitur tamquam interpretatio ordinis primi diei.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A6","CH_MHON_TH_4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD1","text":"Principium temporale producitur per completionem relationis inter figuras, non per positionem unius termini isolati.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A1","CH_MHON_TH_4:A2","CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD2","text":"Oppositio inter vesperum et mane in unitatem constitutivam reordinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A4","CH_MHON_TH_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD3","text":"Lux fit principium ordinis, quia dies primus eam continet tamquam eventum originarium.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A5","CH_MHON_TH_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD4","text":"Philosophicum hic significat ordinem quo figurae cosmicae, tempora et Lux in unum principium legibile coniunguntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A6","CH_MHON_TH_4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet diem tamquam quantitatem mere mensurabilem sine figura et complemento constitui.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet Lunam et Solem ut terminos sine relatione mutua intelligi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet vesperum et mane duas unitates temporales independentes efficere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet originem Lucis a constitutione diei primigenii separari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet designationem Philosophorum ad nomen sine structura ordinis reduci.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit tempus quod ante omnem relationem figuralem iam plene constitutum esset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit complementum purum quod terminum suum partialem non transformaret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit principium quod a productione Lucis nullam vim ordinatingem acciperet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX4","text":"Textus tacite praecludit distinctionem inter sensum cosmologicum et sensum philosophicum tamquam duos ordines prorsus separatos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS1","text":"Semicirculus Lunaris partialis + complementum Solare → relatio completiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS2","text":"Relatio completiva → coniunctio vesperis et matutini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS3","text":"Coniunctio vesperis et matutini → unus dies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS4","text":"Unus dies → primus terminus ordinis temporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS5","text":"Primus dies + productio Lucis → principium originarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS6","text":"Principium originarium + relatio cosmica → designatio Philosophorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AF1","text":"Semicirculus Lunaris → complementum Solare → vesper et mane coniunguntur → unus dies constituitur → dies primus instituitur → Lux principium fit → ordo Philosophorum designatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME1","text":"Tempus fit visibile tamquam effectus relationis inter figuras cosmicas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME2","text":"Vesper et mane ex partibus oppositis in membra unius diei reclassificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME3","text":"Dies primus non amplius solum chronologicus, sed ontogeneticus apparet, quia cum productione Lucis coniungitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME4","text":"Relatio Lunaris-Solaris denuo describitur ut principium ordinis, non ut mera observatio astrorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME5","text":"Philosophicum collocatur in ipsa conversione figurae cosmicae in ordinem temporalem et lucis principium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** Semicirculus Lunaris ad complementum Solare perducitur, et vesper ac mane unum diem efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** Complementatio figurae mechanismum constitutivum diei praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** Textus quaestionem de figura cosmica in quaestionem de productione ordinis convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Dies primus et Lux tamquam origines ordinis temporalis constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem a semicirculo Lunari ad diem primum et Lucem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia interna constat ex motu a partialitate ad complementum, deinde ad unitatem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT3","text":"Relatio exacta inter verba «Philosophorum» et diem primum non plene determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT4","text":"Ambiguum manet utrum Philosophorum genitivus originem, proprietatem an interpretationem diei significet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT5","text":"Systema firmissimum est in unificatione vesperis et matutini per complementum; fragilius est in transitione ad designationem Philosophorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum textus, sed ultimam qualificationem philosophicam non ultra verba fontis determinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222437551241Z_5b4174ea","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R E M V.","source_sha256":"61d74a10f78b4e927c2c54147a79c568930aadb07889cdadf46a9ba96ef8b5ac","sha256":"eaee31179137380cef8e379ba802b8f68946744cef0c58626a700b3f7866fa86","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:24:37.553158+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS1","text":"The text asks how the relation between the Lunar semicircle and the Solar complement constitutes the day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS2","text":"The Lunar semicircle brought to the Solar complement unites evening and morning into one day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS3","text":"This unity constitutes the first day, not merely the continuation of days already given.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS4","text":"The first day is defined through the production of Light and is referred to the order of the Philosophers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument is: complementary figure → unification of temporal things → constitution of a principle → philosophical designation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A1","text":"The Lunar semicircle is a partial figure determined by its relation to another complement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A2","text":"The Solar complement is the term to which the Lunar semicircle is brought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","text":"The bringing of the semicircle to the complement constitutes a completing relation between the Moon and the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A4","text":"Evening and morning, in this relation, belong to one day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A5","text":"One day thus constituted can be the principle of the order of temporal things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A6","text":"The first day is the day on which Light was made.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:A7","text":"This order is referred to the designation of the Philosophers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX1","text":"The day is not constituted from evening or morning in isolation, but from their conjunction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX2","text":"The Lunar semicircle is not treated as a full or already completed figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX3","text":"The Solar complement is not an object separate from the Lunar figure, but its constitutive termination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX4","text":"The first day is not one day among others, but the beginning of the order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:NX5","text":"Light is not reduced to a later event of the day, but pertains to its primary constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D1","text":"Through the Solar complement, the partiality of the Lunar semicircle is converted into the unity of an order.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A1","CH_MHON_TH_4:A2","CH_MHON_TH_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D2","text":"If evening and morning make one day, the division of time is ordered into one form.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D3","text":"The day arises from a complementary relation, not from temporal succession alone.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D4","text":"The unity of the day holds the first place because it is referred to the production of Light.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A5","CH_MHON_TH_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:D5","text":"The designation of the Philosophers is posited as an interpretation of the order of the first day.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A6","CH_MHON_TH_4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD1","text":"A temporal principle is produced through the completion of the relation between figures, not through the positing of one isolated term.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A1","CH_MHON_TH_4:A2","CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD2","text":"The opposition between evening and morning is reordered into a constitutive unity.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A4","CH_MHON_TH_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD3","text":"Light becomes the principle of order because the first day contains it as an originating event.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A5","CH_MHON_TH_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SD4","text":"The philosophical here signifies the order by which cosmic figures, times, and Light are joined into one intelligible principle.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_4:A3","CH_MHON_TH_4:A6","CH_MHON_TH_4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX1","text":"It must be false that the day is constituted as a merely measurable quantity without figure and complement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the Moon and the Sun are understood as terms without mutual relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX3","text":"It must be false that evening and morning make two independent temporal unities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the origin of Light is separated from the constitution of the primordial day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the designation of the Philosophers is reduced to a name without a structure of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX1","text":"The text excludes a time that would already be fully constituted before every figural relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX2","text":"The text excludes a pure complement that would not transform its partial term.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX3","text":"The text excludes a principle that would receive no ordering force from the production of Light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:SNX4","text":"The text tacitly precludes the distinction between cosmological meaning and philosophical meaning as two altogether separate orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS1","text":"Partial Lunar semicircle + Solar complement → completing relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS2","text":"Completing relation → conjunction of evening and morning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS3","text":"Conjunction of evening and morning → one day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS4","text":"One day → first term of the temporal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS5","text":"First day + production of Light → originating principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:FGS6","text":"Originating principle + cosmic relation → designation of the Philosophers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:AF1","text":"Lunar semicircle → Solar complement → evening and morning are joined → one day is constituted → the first day is established → Light becomes principle → the order of the Philosophers is designated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME1","text":"Time becomes visible as the effect of a relation between cosmic figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME2","text":"Evening and morning are reclassified from opposed parts into members of one day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME3","text":"The first day appears no longer merely chronological, but ontogenetic, because it is joined with the production of Light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME4","text":"The Lunar-Solar relation is redescribed as a principle of order, not as a mere observation of the stars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ME5","text":"The philosophical is situated in the very conversion of the cosmic figure into temporal order and the principle of Light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** The Lunar semicircle is brought to the Solar complement, and evening and morning make one day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** The completion of the figure provides the constitutive mechanism of the day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** The text converts the question of cosmic figure into a question of the production of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** The first day and Light are constituted as origins of temporal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the sequence from the Lunar semicircle to the first day and Light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT2","text":"The internal coherence consists in the movement from partiality to complement, then to unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT3","text":"The exact relation between the word «Philosophorum» and the first day is not fully determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT4","text":"It remains ambiguous whether the genitive Philosophorum signifies the origin, property, or interpretation of the day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT5","text":"The system is strongest in the unification of evening and morning through complement; it is more fragile in the transition to the designation of the Philosophers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_4:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, but does not determine the final philosophical qualification beyond the words of the source.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_4@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_4:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 06","title":"T H E O R E M V.","context":"Chapter 06","original_title":"T H E O R E M A V.","original_context":"Chapter 06"},"original_title":"T H E O R E M A V.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R E M V I.","order":7,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_5"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_5@R001","sha256":"f55f0897d0864c8b25be8d0b983ee20ac0ccf9ac2e58c52491f359a41609b1ac","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quomodo Sol et Luna, Cruci Rectilineae innixi, formas Hieroglyphicas numeris significantes exhibeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS2","text":"Figura rectilinea ad ternarium et quaternarium significandum resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS3","text":"Ternarius ex duabus rectis et puncto communi, quaternarius ex quattuor rectis et quattuor angulis rectis constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS4","text":"Repetitio configurationum ad octonarium occulte producit, dum connexio ternarii et quaternarii ad septenarium primarium ducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS5","text":"Genus argumentationis est reconstructivum-symbolicum: a figura geometrica ad ordinationem numerorum et deinde ad significationem magicam procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","text":"Figura rectilinea potest rationes numericas Hieroglyphice significare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","text":"Duae rectae cum puncto communi ternarium constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A3","text":"Quattuor rectae quattuor angulos rectos includentes quaternarium constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A4","text":"Eadem elementa geometrica per repetitionem numerice multiplicari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A5","text":"Repetitio quaternarii ad octonarium pertinere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A6","text":"Ternarius apud Patres et Sophos magicus est compositio Corporis, Spiritus et Animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A7","text":"Ternarius et quaternarius simul rationem septenarii primarii constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A8","text":"Septenarius ex duabus rectis et puncto communi, deinde ex quattuor rectis ab uno puncto separantibus, intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A9","text":"Configuratio geometrica potest simul structuram numericam et significationem symbolicam sustinere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX1","text":"Ternarius non ex tribus rectis simpliciter, sed ex duabus rectis et puncto communi definitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX2","text":"Quaternarius non ad numerum quattuor nudum reducitur, sed quattuor rectas et quattuor angulos rectos requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX3","text":"Significatio Hieroglyphica non a figura qualibet, sed a ratione geometrica apposita procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX4","text":"Octonarius non ut forma primaria, sed ut effectus repetitionis occulte se offert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX5","text":"Septenarius non ut series numerica abstracta, sed ut compositio configurationum geometricarum instituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX6","text":"Auctor de praedecessoribus Magis non certitudinem, sed dubitationem profert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D1","text":"Si duae rectae puncto communi copulantur, figura eorum ternariam significationem accipit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D2","text":"Si quattuor rectae quattuor angulos rectos includunt, figura eorum quaternariam significationem accipit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D3","text":"Si configuratio quaternaria bis repetitur, octonarius ut effectus eiusdem ordinis manifestari potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A4","CH_MHON_TH_5:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D4","text":"Si ternarius magicus Corpus, Spiritum et Animam continet, numerus ternarius formam compositionis ontologicae accipit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D5","text":"Si ternarius et quaternarius coniunguntur, septenarius ut compositio primarium appellari potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D6","text":"Punctum commune primum copulationem, punctum unum cum rectis separantibus deinde divisionem contrariarum partium designat.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD1","text":"Numerus in hoc systemate non est quantitas separata a figura, sed relatio inter rectas, puncta, angulos et repetitiones.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A3","CH_MHON_TH_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD2","text":"Eadem figura potest plures ordines significationis generare, quia geometria simul numerum, compositionem et hieroglyphicum sustinet.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A6","CH_MHON_TH_5:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD3","text":"Ternarius et quaternarius in septenario non tantum numeri consecutivi, sed modi copulationis et separationis inter se fiunt.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A3","CH_MHON_TH_5:A7","CH_MHON_TH_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD4","text":"Repetitio structuram latentem producit quae in prima configuratione nondum tota conspicitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A4","CH_MHON_TH_5:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD5","text":"Significatio magica oritur cum relatio geometrica ad compositionem Corporis, Spiritus et Animae transfertur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A6","CH_MHON_TH_5:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX1","text":"Systema implicite negat numerum esse significatione carentem mensuram externam figurae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX2","text":"Systema implicite excludit separationem absolutam inter geometrice descriptum et symbolice significatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit interpretationem quae repetitionem mechanicam sine novo ordine numerico relinqueret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX4","text":"Systema non admittit ut copulatio et separatio sint operationes sine numerica aut hieroglyphica consequentia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX5","text":"Systema implicite negat primarium ordinem numerorum sine configuratione generatrice stabiliri posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX1","text":"Textus circumagit possibilitatem figurae purae, quae nec numerum nec significationem ontologicam generaret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio praecludit discretionem inter mathematicam formam et magicam interpretationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX3","text":"Absentia regulae completae de repetitione ostendit ordinem octonarii tamquam latentem, non plene formalizatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX4","text":"Impossibilis intra systema fit numerus qui a suis relationibus geometricis separari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS1","text":"Rectilinea Crux → relatio rectarum et punctorum → numerica significatio Hieroglyphica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS2","text":"Duae Rectae + Punctum Commune → Ternarius → Corpus / Spiritus / Anima.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS3","text":"Quattuor Rectae + Quattuor Anguli Recti → Quaternarius → repetitio configurationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS4","text":"Quaternarius × repetitio → Octonarius occultus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS5","text":"Ternarius + Quaternarius → Septenarius Primarius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS6","text":"Punctum Commune → Copulatio; Punctum Unum + Rectae Separantes → Contrariae Partes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS7","text":"Geometrica descriptio → relatio numerica → translatio magica → hieroglyphica clausura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AF1","text":"Sol et Luna super Cruce Rectilinea → quaestio de significatione figurae → distinctio ternarii et quaternarii → repetitio ad octonarium → compositio ternarii et quaternarii in septenario → connexio geometriae cum ternario magico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME1","text":"Figura rectilinea fit tabula in qua punctum, recta, angulus et repetitio simul legi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME2","text":"Numeri ternarius, quaternarius, septenarius et octonarius ex seriebus abstractis in configurationes visuales convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME3","text":"Ternarius a numero simplici in compositionem Corporis, Spiritus et Animae denuo classificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME4","text":"Quaternarius a collectione quattuor elementorum in structuram inclusivam quattuor angulorum rectangulorum mutatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME5","text":"Septenarius fit effectus coniunctionis inter copulationem ternariam et separationem quaternariam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME6","text":"Octonarius fit ordo latentis repetitionis, non prima species figurae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT1","text":"Surface: Sol et Luna Cruci Rectilineae innituntur, cui figurae geometricae attribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT2","text":"Structural: Rectae, puncta et anguli numeros per copulationem, inclusionem, separationem et repetitionem generant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Lectio figurae a descriptione geometrica ad ordinationem hieroglyphicam et magicam transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Ternarius Corpus, Spiritum et Animam componit; repetitio ordinem latentem posterius manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad motum principalem a Cruce Rectilinea ad ternarium, quaternarium, octonarium et septenarium restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT2","text":"Fundamentum significationis Solis et Lunae in figura non ulterius explicatur quam per innixionem Cruci.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT3","text":"Relatio formalis qua ternarius et quaternarius septenarium constituunt indicatur, sed non plene demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT4","text":"Status octonarii ambiguus manet, quia repetitio bis et eius exactus numericus effectus non omnino formalizantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT5","text":"Systema interne cohaeret, dum geometria tamquam generatrix numerorum et significationum assumitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT6","text":"Firmissimum est discrimen inter ternarium ex copulatione et quaternarium ex inclusione angulari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT7","text":"Restitutio verum textus motum servat, sed clausura numerica et interpretatio latentis octonarii partim vi synthetica nituntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222458447976Z_b5ea8d24","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R E M V I.","source_sha256":"f55f0897d0864c8b25be8d0b983ee20ac0ccf9ac2e58c52491f359a41609b1ac","sha256":"65fa90442f5eaa8ec6eac47ede53301eefb43e32a68cd41fb0f02b0861736315","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:24:58.450793+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS1","text":"The question is how the Sun and Moon, resting upon the Rectilinear Cross, display Hieroglyphic forms signifying numbers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS2","text":"The rectilinear figure is resolved into the signification of the ternary and the quaternary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS3","text":"The ternary is constituted from two straight lines and a common point, the quaternary from four straight lines and four right angles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS4","text":"The repetition of configurations covertly produces the octonary, while the connection of the ternary and quaternary leads to the primary septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AS5","text":"The kind of argumentation is reconstructive-symbolic: it proceeds from geometric figure to the ordering of numbers and then to magical signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","text":"A rectilinear figure can signify numerical relations hieroglyphically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","text":"Two straight lines with a common point constitute the ternary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A3","text":"Four straight lines enclosing four right angles constitute the quaternary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A4","text":"The same geometric elements can be numerically multiplied through repetition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A5","text":"The repetition of the quaternary can pertain to the octonary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A6","text":"Among the Fathers and the Wise, the magical ternary is the composition of Body, Spirit, and Soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A7","text":"The ternary and quaternary together constitute the ratio of the primary septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A8","text":"The septenary is understood from two straight lines and a common point, then from four straight lines separating from one point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:A9","text":"A geometric configuration can simultaneously sustain numerical structure and symbolic signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX1","text":"The ternary is defined not simply from three straight lines, but from two straight lines and a common point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX2","text":"The quaternary is not reduced to the bare number four, but requires four straight lines and four right angles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX3","text":"Hieroglyphic signification proceeds not from any figure whatsoever, but from an applied geometric ratio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX4","text":"The octonary presents itself not as a primary form, but covertly as an effect of repetition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX5","text":"The septenary is instituted not as an abstract numerical series, but as a composition of geometric configurations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:NX6","text":"Concerning the predecessor Magi, the author advances not certainty, but doubt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D1","text":"If two straight lines are joined by a common point, their figure receives ternary signification.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D2","text":"If four straight lines enclose four right angles, their figure receives quaternary signification.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D3","text":"If a quaternary configuration is repeated twice, the octonary can manifest as an effect of the same order.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A4","CH_MHON_TH_5:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D4","text":"If the magical ternary contains Body, Spirit, and Soul, the ternary number receives the form of an ontological composition.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D5","text":"If the ternary and quaternary are joined, the septenary can be called primary as a composition.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:D6","text":"The common point first signifies conjunction, then the one point with separating straight lines signifies the division of contrary parts.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD1","text":"Number in this system is not a quantity separate from figure, but a relation among straight lines, points, angles, and repetitions.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A3","CH_MHON_TH_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD2","text":"The same figure can generate several orders of signification, because geometry simultaneously sustains number, composition, and the hieroglyphic.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A1","CH_MHON_TH_5:A6","CH_MHON_TH_5:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD3","text":"In the septenary, the ternary and quaternary become not merely consecutive numbers, but modes of conjunction and separation in relation to one another.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A3","CH_MHON_TH_5:A7","CH_MHON_TH_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD4","text":"Repetition produces a latent structure that is not yet wholly visible in the first configuration.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A4","CH_MHON_TH_5:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SD5","text":"Magical signification arises when a geometric relation is transferred to the composition of Body, Spirit, and Soul.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_5:A2","CH_MHON_TH_5:A6","CH_MHON_TH_5:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX1","text":"The system implicitly denies that number is an external measure of figure devoid of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX2","text":"The system implicitly excludes an absolute separation between what is geometrically described and what is symbolically signified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an interpretation that would leave mechanical repetition without a new numerical order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX4","text":"The system does not admit that conjunction and separation are operations without numerical or hieroglyphic consequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:DNX5","text":"The system implicitly denies that the primary order of numbers can be established without a generative configuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX1","text":"The text circumscribes the possibility of a pure figure that would generate neither number nor ontological signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX2","text":"The argumentation precludes a distinction between mathematical form and magical interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX3","text":"The absence of a complete rule concerning repetition shows the order of the octonary as latent, not fully formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:SNX4","text":"Within the system, a number that could be separated from its geometric relations becomes impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS1","text":"Rectilinear Cross → relation of straight lines and points → numerical Hieroglyphic signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS2","text":"Two Straight Lines + Common Point → Ternary → Body / Spirit / Soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS3","text":"Four Straight Lines + Four Right Angles → Quaternary → repetition of configuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS4","text":"Quaternary × repetition → covert octonary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS5","text":"Ternary + Quaternary → Primary Septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS6","text":"Common Point → Conjunction; One Point + Separating Straight Lines → Contrary Parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:FGS7","text":"Geometric description → numerical relation → magical translation → hieroglyphic closure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:AF1","text":"Sun and Moon upon the Rectilinear Cross → question concerning the signification of the figure → distinction of ternary and quaternary → repetition to the octonary → composition of ternary and quaternary in the septenary → connection of geometry with the magical ternary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME1","text":"The rectilinear figure becomes a map in which point, straight line, angle, and repetition can be read simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME2","text":"The ternary, quaternary, septenary, and octonary numbers are converted from abstract series into visual configurations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME3","text":"The ternary is reclassified from a simple number into a composition of Body, Spirit, and Soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME4","text":"The quaternary is changed from a collection of four elements into an inclusive structure of four right angles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME5","text":"The septenary becomes the effect of a conjunction between ternary conjunction and quaternary separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ME6","text":"The octonary becomes an order of latent repetition, not the first appearance of the figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT1","text":"Surface: The Sun and Moon rest upon the Rectilinear Cross, to which geometric figure is attributed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT2","text":"Structural: Straight lines, points, and angles generate numbers through conjunction, inclusion, separation, and repetition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The reading of the figure is transferred from geometric description to hieroglyphic and magical ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The ternary composes Body, Spirit, and Soul; repetition subsequently manifests a latent order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement from the Rectilinear Cross to the ternary, quaternary, octonary, and septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT2","text":"The foundation of the signification of the Sun and Moon in the figure is not further explained than through their resting upon the Cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT3","text":"The formal relation by which the ternary and quaternary constitute the septenary is indicated, but not fully demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT4","text":"The status of the octonary remains ambiguous, because repetition twice and its exact numerical effect are not wholly formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT5","text":"The system coheres internally, provided that geometry is assumed as the generator of numbers and significations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT6","text":"Strongest is the distinction between the ternary from conjunction and the quaternary from angular inclusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_5:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, but numerical closure and the interpretation of the latent octonary rest partly upon synthetic force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_5@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_5:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 07","title":"T H E O R E M V I.","context":"Chapter 07","original_title":"T H E O R E M A V I.","original_context":"Chapter 07"},"original_title":"T H E O R E M A V I.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R. V I I.","order":8,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_6"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_6@R001","sha256":"be0131ee14c7db67ff6d4b986e97dac3ffebbbc61fa27b99d8e81737975dd43f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS1","text":"Dislocatio elementorum quaerit regulam reditus ad sedes naturales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS2","text":"Experientia reditus per rectas lineas homogenearum partium ostendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS3","text":"Ex uno puncto in quattuor contrarias partes ductae rectae mysterium quattuor elementorum innuunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS4","text":"Geometrica productio lineae ex puncti fluxu exemplar praebet productioni linearum elementarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS5","text":"Stilla, tamquam punctum physicum, per casum continuum fluxum mechanicis Magiae praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS6","text":"Numeratio quaternaria per summationem unitatum ad denarium extenditur et numerorum symbolicae structurae rationem aperit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS7","text":"Motus argumentationis est: dislocatio → reditus rectilineus → punctum et fluxus → elementa → numeratio → denarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","text":"Partes homogeneae, extra sedes naturales dimotae, ad easdem sedes naturaliter redeunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A2","text":"Reditus naturalis partium dislocatarum per rectas lineas fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","text":"Elementata singula tandem in quattuor elementa resolvi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A4","text":"Quattuor lineae ab uno puncto in contrarias partes excurrentes quattuor elementorum mysterium exprimere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","text":"Linea geometrica ex puncti fluxu producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","text":"Lineae elementares ex stilla, tamquam puncto physico, per casum continuum producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A7","text":"Casus continuus stillae in Mechanica Magia fluxui respondet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A8","text":"Numeratio quaternaria per unum, duo, tria et quattuor ad denarium summatim pervenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A9","text":"Quaternarius ad denarium referri potest per signa numerationis priscis philosophis attributa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A10","text":"Ternarius per relationem ad septenarium numerice determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX1","text":"Elementa extra sedes naturales non manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX2","text":"Dislocatarum partium reditus non est indeterminatus aut sine directione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX3","text":"Elementata non sunt ultima indivisibilia, quia in elementa resolvi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX4","text":"Linea non ut res puncto prorsus separata concipitur, sed ex puncti fluxu producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX5","text":"Stilla non est punctum mere geometricum, sed punctum physicum cui casus continuus accedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX6","text":"Quaternarius non clauditur in numero quattuor, sed ad denarium summatione extenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX7","text":"Numerorum significatio non reducitur ad appellationes ordinarias, sed per relationes doctrinales constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D1","text":"Si partes homogeneae ad sedes naturales per rectas redeunt, recta linea mechanismum restitutionis naturalis exhibet.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","CH_MHON_TH_6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D2","text":"Si elementata in quattuor elementa resolvuntur, quattuor directiones ex uno puncto structuram compositionis elementaris figurant.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","CH_MHON_TH_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D3","text":"Si linea ex puncti fluxu producitur, punctum principium staticum non est, sed origo cuiusdam productionis.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D4","text":"Si stilla est punctum physicum et casus eius continuus est, productio elementarium linearum est processus, non forma iam completa.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","CH_MHON_TH_6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D5","text":"Si unum, duo, tria et quattuor simul numerantur, quaternarius seriem constituit quae in denarium summatim clauditur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D6","text":"Si quaternarius ad denarium et ternarius ad septenarium referuntur, numeri nexum inter structuram simplicem et extensionem symbolicam efficiunt.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A9","CH_MHON_TH_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD1","text":"Natura restitutiva et Magia mechanica sub eadem productionis ratione coniunguntur: origo punctiformis per fluxum ordinatum ad figuras pervenit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","CH_MHON_TH_6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD2","text":"Elementorum unitas non simpliciter praesupponitur, sed ex dislocatione, resolutione et directione linearum generatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A2","CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","CH_MHON_TH_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD3","text":"Geometria fit translatio inter physicam observationem et structuram magicam.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","CH_MHON_TH_6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD4","text":"Numeratio fit forma ontologicae ordinationis: aggregatio unitatum ad denarium non tantum calculum, sed clausuram structurae indicat.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A8","CH_MHON_TH_6:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD5","text":"Punctum, stilla, linea, elementum et numerus in una serie generationis inter se convertuntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","CH_MHON_TH_6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet naturam ut ordinem corporum omnino inertem et sine reditu esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet lineam ut figuram a puncto et eius motu independentem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet elementa ut extrema et irreducibilia corpora sine compositione esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet casum ut mera perturbatio sine continua productione esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet numerum ut seriem clausam et a relationibus symbolicis separatam esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet physicam, geometriam et Magiam tres ordines omnino disiunctos constituere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit mundum in quo formae sine origine punctiformi et sine fluxu producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit materiam cui nulla sedes naturalis, nulla directio et nullus reditus competant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit numerum purum, cui nulla transformatio ontologica vel symbolica respondeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX4","text":"Textus excludit separationem principii mathematici a materia physica: punctum geometricum sine stilla physica machinam non absolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX5","text":"Textus tacite praecludit distinctionem inter productionem naturalem et operationem magicam, quam sub communi fluxus ratione ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS1","text":"Dislocatio partium → observatio reditus → restitutio per rectas → positio sedium naturalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS2","text":"Unum punctum → quattuor lineae contrariae → quattuor elementa → resolutio elementatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS3","text":"Punctum geometricum → fluxus → linea producta → analogia cum stilla physica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS4","text":"Stilla physica → casus continuus → lineae elementares → Mechanica Magia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS5","text":"Unum + duo + tria + quattuor → quaternarius aggregatus → denarius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS6","text":"Quaternarius et ternarius → numerationes doctrinales → relatio denarii et septenarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS7","text":"Motus universus: perturbatio apparens → ordo naturalis → figura geometrica → processus physicus → significatio magica → clausura numerica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF1","text":"Elementorum dislocatio → experientia reditus → recta ut via naturalis → quattuor directiones ex uno puncto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF2","text":"Quattuor directiones → resolutio elementatorum → mysterium quattuor elementorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF3","text":"Punctum → fluxus → linea → stilla physica → casus continuus → productio magica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF4","text":"Quaternarius numericus → summa unitatum → denarius → relatio ad antiquas doctrinas numericas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF5","text":"Structura quaternaria et ternaria → extensiones denaria et septenaria → ordo numericus symbolicus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME1","text":"Dislocatio, quae initio perturbatio videtur, denuo classificatur ut condicio restitutionis naturalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME2","text":"Recta linea non amplius est figura geometrica tantum, sed index reditus et instrumentum compositionis elementaris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME3","text":"Punctum transit ab unitate immobili ad principium fluxus et productionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME4","text":"Stilla physicam materiam et punctum geometricum coniungit sub una genealogia lineae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME5","text":"Quattuor elementa non ut inventarium separatum, sed ut quattuor directiones ex communi origine intelliguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME6","text":"Numeri quattuor, decem, tres et septem ordinantur ut transformationes inter diversas amplitudines structurae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME7","text":"Terminus «Mechanica Magia» agrum naturalis causationis et artis magicae in unam rationem fluxionalem redigit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT1","text":"Surface: Observantur partes homogeneae dislocatae, rectilineus earum reditus, stilla cadens et series numerica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT2","text":"Structural: Reditus, fluxus et resolutio constituunt mechanismum quo ex origine punctiformi formae et elementa producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Geometria et numeratio adhibentur ut media quibus observatio physica in mysterium magicum et doctrinam symbolicam convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Ens non ut forma fixa, sed ut productum fluxus continui, casus, resolutionis et aggregationis concipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam principalem machinam: dislocatio ad sedes redit, reditus per rectas fit, et recta ex puncti fluxu producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT2","text":"Additio stillae physicae et casus continui nexum inter geometriam et Mechanicam Magicam absolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT3","text":"Axiomata numerica quaternarium ad denarium referunt, sed vim exactam relationis ternarii ad septenarium non plene determinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT4","text":"Structura interne cohaeret in transitu punctum → fluxus → linea → elementum; cohaerentia minor est in transitu numerationis ad doctrinam philosophicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT5","text":"Firmissima est analogia inter reditum naturalem, lineam geometricam et productionem mechanicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT6","text":"Fragilior est transitus ab observatione experientiali ad «mysterium» quattuor elementorum, quia analogia sola probationem substituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT7","text":"Textus iterat inscriptionem «THEOR. VII» ante doctrinam numerorum; unitas inter duas expositiones formaliter non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT8","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus, dummodo nexus inter physicam, geometriam, Magiam et numerationem tamquam analogicus, non tamquam demonstratio stricte deductiva, intellegatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222520207092Z_97f43415","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R Y. V I I.","source_sha256":"be0131ee14c7db67ff6d4b986e97dac3ffebbbc61fa27b99d8e81737975dd43f","sha256":"18f997e89d1efae0e9e9e83ddca5c2efb8cf09fa3cb325aee76b85bec721f1da","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:25:20.208272+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS1","text":"The displacement of the elements seeks the rule of return to their natural places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS2","text":"Experience shows return through straight lines of homogeneous parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS3","text":"Straight lines drawn from one point into four opposite directions suggest the mystery of the four elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS4","text":"The geometrical production of a line from the flux of a point provides a model for the production of elementary lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS5","text":"A drop, as a physical point, through continuous falling provides flux to the mechanics of Magia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS6","text":"Quaternary counting is extended to ten through the summation of units and discloses the rationale of symbolic structures of numbers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AS7","text":"The movement of the argument is: displacement → rectilinear return → point and flux → elements → counting → ten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","text":"Homogeneous parts, removed outside their natural places, naturally return to those same places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A2","text":"The natural return of displaced parts occurs through straight lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","text":"Individual elementata can ultimately be resolved into four elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A4","text":"Four lines running out from one point into opposite directions can express the mystery of the four elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","text":"A geometrical line is produced from the flux of a point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","text":"Elementary lines are produced from a drop, as a physical point, through continuous falling.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A7","text":"The continuous falling of a drop corresponds to flux in Mechanica Magia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A8","text":"Quaternary counting, through one, two, three, and four, reaches ten by summation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A9","text":"The quaternary can be referred to ten through signs of counting attributed to ancient philosophers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:A10","text":"The ternary is numerically determined through relation to the septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX1","text":"The elements do not remain outside their natural places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX2","text":"The return of displaced parts is not indeterminate or without direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX3","text":"Elementata are not ultimate indivisibles, because they can be resolved into elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX4","text":"A line is not conceived as a thing wholly separate from a point, but is produced from the flux of a point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX5","text":"A drop is not a merely geometrical point, but a physical point to which continuous falling is added.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX6","text":"The quaternary is not enclosed within the number four, but is extended to ten by summation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:NX7","text":"The signification of numbers is not reduced to ordinary appellations, but is constituted through doctrinal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D1","text":"If homogeneous parts return to their natural places by straight lines, the straight line displays the mechanism of natural restoration.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","CH_MHON_TH_6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D2","text":"If elementata are resolved into four elements, four directions from one point figure the structure of elementary composition.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","CH_MHON_TH_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D3","text":"If a line is produced from the flux of a point, the point is not a static principle, but the origin of a certain production.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D4","text":"If a drop is a physical point and its falling is continuous, the production of elementary lines is a process, not an already completed form.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","CH_MHON_TH_6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D5","text":"If one, two, three, and four are counted together, the quaternary constitutes a series that is summatively closed in ten.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:D6","text":"If the quaternary is referred to ten and the ternary to seven, numbers effect a connection between simple structure and symbolic extension.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A9","CH_MHON_TH_6:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD1","text":"Restorative nature and mechanical Magia are joined under the same rationale of production: a point-like origin arrives at figures through ordered flux.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","CH_MHON_TH_6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD2","text":"The unity of the elements is not simply presupposed, but is generated from displacement, resolution, and the direction of lines.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A2","CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","CH_MHON_TH_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD3","text":"Geometry becomes a translation between physical observation and magical structure.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A1","CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","CH_MHON_TH_6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD4","text":"Counting becomes a form of ontological ordering: the aggregation of units to ten indicates not only calculation, but the closure of a structure.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A8","CH_MHON_TH_6:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SD5","text":"Point, drop, line, element, and number are mutually transformed within a single series of generation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_6:A3","CH_MHON_TH_6:A5","CH_MHON_TH_6:A6","CH_MHON_TH_6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX1","text":"It must be false that nature is an entirely inert order of bodies without return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX2","text":"It must be false that a line is a figure independent of a point and its motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the elements are ultimate and irreducible bodies without composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX4","text":"It must be false that falling is a mere disturbance without continuous production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX5","text":"It must be false that number is a closed series separated from symbolic relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:DNX6","text":"It must be false that physics, geometry, and Magia constitute three entirely disjoined orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX1","text":"The text excludes a world in which forms are produced without a point-like origin and without flux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX2","text":"The text excludes matter to which no natural place, no direction, and no return belong.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX3","text":"The text excludes pure number, to which no ontological or symbolic transformation corresponds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX4","text":"The text excludes the separation of mathematical principle from physical matter: a geometrical point without a physical drop does not complete the machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:SNX5","text":"The text tacitly precludes a distinction between natural production and magical operation, which it orders under a common rationale of flux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS1","text":"Displacement of parts → observation of return → restoration through straight lines → positing of natural places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS2","text":"One point → four opposite lines → four elements → resolution of elementata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS3","text":"Geometrical point → flux → produced line → analogy with a physical drop.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS4","text":"Physical drop → continuous falling → elementary lines → Mechanica Magia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS5","text":"One + two + three + four → aggregated quaternary → ten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS6","text":"Quaternary and ternary → doctrinal countings → relation of ten and seven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:FGS7","text":"Universal movement: apparent disturbance → natural order → geometrical figure → physical process → magical signification → numerical closure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF1","text":"Displacement of the elements → experience of return → straight line as natural path → four directions from one point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF2","text":"Four directions → resolution of elementata → mystery of the four elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF3","text":"Point → flux → line → physical drop → continuous falling → magical production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF4","text":"Numerical quaternary → sum of units → ten → relation to ancient numerical doctrines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:AF5","text":"Quaternary and ternary structure → denary and septenary extensions → symbolic numerical order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME1","text":"Displacement, which at first appears a disturbance, is reclassified as a condition of natural restoration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME2","text":"The straight line is no longer merely a geometrical figure, but an indication of return and an instrument of elementary composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME3","text":"The point passes from an immobile unit to a principle of flux and production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME4","text":"The drop joins physical matter and the geometrical point under one genealogy of the line.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME5","text":"The four elements are understood not as a separate inventory, but as four directions from a common origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME6","text":"The numbers four, ten, three, and seven are ordered as transformations among diverse magnitudes of structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ME7","text":"The term «Mechanica Magia» reduces the field of natural causation and magical art to a single fluxional rationale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT1","text":"Surface: Displaced homogeneous parts, their rectilinear return, a falling drop, and a numerical series are observed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT2","text":"Structural: Return, flux, and resolution constitute the mechanism by which forms and elements are produced from a point-like origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Geometry and counting are employed as means by which physical observation is converted into magical mystery and symbolic doctrine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Being is conceived not as a fixed form, but as the product of continuous flux, falling, resolution, and aggregation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal mechanism: displacement returns to places, return occurs through straight lines, and a straight line is produced from the flux of a point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT2","text":"The addition of the physical drop and continuous falling completes the connection between geometry and Mechanica Magia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT3","text":"The numerical axioms refer the quaternary to ten, but do not fully determine the exact force of the relation of the ternary to the septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT4","text":"The structure coheres internally in the transition point → flux → line → element; coherence is less in the transition from counting to philosophical doctrine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT5","text":"The analogy between natural return, geometrical line, and mechanical production is strongest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT6","text":"More fragile is the transition from experiential observation to the «mystery» of the four elements, because analogy alone substitutes for proof.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT7","text":"The text repeats the inscription «THEOR. VII» before the doctrine of numbers; the unity between the two expositions is not formally explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_6:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, provided that the connection among physics, geometry, Magia, and counting is understood as analogical, not as strictly deductive demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_6@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_6:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 08","title":"T H E O R. V I I.","context":"Chapter 08","original_title":"T H E O R. V I I.","original_context":"Chapter 08"},"original_title":"T H E O R. V I I.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. VIII.","order":9,"parents":["RAW_MHON_THEV"],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEV@R001","sha256":"e6d8ac6a6376139b1a16b152cedc65e5f8aee0f4e964def66ef4a2f4b4f94643","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo Quaternarius ad Denarium referatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS2","text":"Textus novam quaestionis constitutionem proponit, qua numeratio, figura litteralis et symbolum crucis in una serie considerantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS3","text":"Fundamentum est summa numerorum 1, 2, 3 et 4, quae denarium constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS4","text":"Probatio extenditur a structura numerica ad crucem rectilineam ex quattuor rectis compositam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS5","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructiva et symbolico-genealogica: numerus → figura → littera → Denarium → relatio ternarii ad septenarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A1","text":"Quaternarius, secundum expansionem cabalisticam et usitatam numerationis phrasin, Denarium summatim exhibet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A2","text":"Numeri unus, duo, tria et quatuor simul decem conficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A3","text":"Pythagorica auctoritas confirmat identitatem numerorum 1, 2, 3 et 4 cum Denario.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A4","text":"Crux rectilinea ex quattuor rectis indicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A5","text":"Crux rectilinea litterae vicesimae primae Romani alphabeti respondet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A6","text":"Crux rectilinea a philosophis Latinis antiquissimis ad Denarium significandum assumpta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A7","text":"Locus crucis in eadem serie definitur ubi Ternarius vim suam per Septenarium ducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A8","text":"Numeralis compositio et figura crucis in eodem ordine symbolico cohaerent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX1","text":"Relatio crucis ad Denarium non est temere constituta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX2","text":"Crux non tractatur ut figura sine numerali vel alphabetica determinatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX3","text":"Denarius non separatur a serie quae per Quaternarium, crucem, Ternarium et Septenarium ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX4","text":"Significatio crucis non reducitur ad eius formam geometricam nudam, sed terminatur in functione numerali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D1","text":"Quaternarius ad Denarium ducit per additionem graduum 1 + 2 + 3 + 4.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A1","CH_MHON_THEV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D2","text":"Figura quattuor rectarum potest esse vehiculum visibilis eiusdem relationis quam numerus quaternarius arithmeticus exhibet.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A2","CH_MHON_THEV:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D3","text":"Littera Romani alphabeti vicesima prima fit nexus inter figuram crucis et ordinem alphabeticum.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A4","CH_MHON_THEV:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D4","text":"Assumptio crucis a philosophis Latinis antiquis auctoritatem genealogicam significationi Denarii addit.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D5","text":"Positio crucis in serie non est tantum descriptiva, sed a transitu virtutis Ternarii per Septenarium ordinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SD1","text":"Numerus, littera et figura efficiunt systema conversionis in quo eadem unitas symbolica per modos arithmeticum, alphabeticum et geometricum producitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A1","CH_MHON_THEV:A4","CH_MHON_THEV:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SD2","text":"Significatio Denarii constituitur non per unum signum isolatum, sed per ordinem graduum et relationum inter Quaternarium, Ternarium et Septenarium.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A1","CH_MHON_THEV:A7","CH_MHON_THEV:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SD3","text":"Historia assumptionis a philosophis Latinis convertit correspondentiam numericam in traditionem doctrinalem atque legitimam.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A3","CH_MHON_THEV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX1","text":"Systema non admittit divisionem absolutam inter arithmeticam, alphabetum et geometriam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX2","text":"Forma visibilis non potest esse symbolice indifferens, quia quattuor rectae ad numeralem constitutionem referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX3","text":"Ordo numerorum non est mera enumeratio linearis, sed nexus graduum vim suam inter se transferentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX4","text":"Interpretatio non fundatur in arbitraria similitudine, sed in correspondentia inter compositionem numericam, formam et locum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SNX1","text":"Textus circumit possibilitatem signi cuius figura, numerus et locus inter se non respondeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SNX2","text":"Excluditur mundus in quo Denarius simpliciter summa arithmetica maneret sine manifestatione figurali et alphabetica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SNX3","text":"Indisponibilis fit interpretatio quae symbolum a serie ordinatrice Ternarii et Septenarii abstrahit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS1","text":"1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS2","text":"Quaternarius → Expansio cabalistica → Denarius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS3","text":"Quaternarius numericus → quattuor rectae → crux rectilinea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS4","text":"Crux rectilinea → littera vicesima prima Romani alphabeti → signum ordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS5","text":"Signum crucis → assumptio philosophica Latina → significatio Denarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS6","text":"Ternarius → Septenarius → locus definitus crucis in serie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS7","text":"Numerus + figura + littera + locus → unitas symbolica Denarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AF1","text":"Quaternarius → summa 1, 2, 3, 4 → Denarius → figura quattuor rectarum → crux rectilinea → littera vicesima prima → assumptio Latina → locus per Ternarium et Septenarium definitus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME1","text":"Quaternarius fit principium transitus inter numerum arithmeticum et signum figurale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME2","text":"Crux denuo classificatur ut nexus geometricus, alphabeticus et numeralis, non ut figura tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME3","text":"Denarius fit effectus ordinis compositi, non solum terminus additionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME4","text":"Relatio inter Ternarium et Septenarium constituit locum symboli intra seriem, ita ut positio ipsa vim significativam accipiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT1","text":"Surface: Quattuor numeri summati denarium efficiunt, et crux ex quattuor rectis componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT2","text":"Structural: Eadem quaternaria forma numerum, figuram crucis et litteram alphabeticam colligat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Interpretatio operatur per translationem inter ordines arithmeticum, geometricum, alphabeticum et doctrinalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Signum habet locum in ordine graduum, ubi vis Ternarii per Septenarium ad manifestationem crucis pervenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam productionem Denarii ex Quaternario et ad explicandam crucem ut eius signum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT2","text":"Nexus inter litteram vicesimam primam et numerum Denarium in textu affirmatur, sed eius mechanismus ulterior non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT3","text":"Relatio qua Ternarius vim suam per Septenarium ducit indicatur, non formaliter demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT4","text":"Systema interne cohaeret dum numerus, figura et locus eandem symbolicam seriem sustinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT5","text":"Firmitas maxima est in additione 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10; commissura fragilior est transitus ab arithmetica ad auctoritatem traditionis Latinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: a Quaternario numerico ad Denarium, a Denario ad crucem, et a cruce ad locum eius in serie symbolica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222324180453Z_ccf5eb2e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. VIII.","source_sha256":"e6d8ac6a6376139b1a16b152cedc65e5f8aee0f4e964def66ef4a2f4b4f94643","sha256":"f127fc82bf7a09dfcd9cc535bd1800903de19722e36e63ad154741bfd5de83cc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:23:24.182819+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS1","text":"The central question is how the Quaternary is related to the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS2","text":"The text proposes a new formulation of the question, in which numbering, literal figure, and the symbol of the cross are considered in a single series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS3","text":"The foundation is the sum of the numbers 1, 2, 3, and 4, which constitutes the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS4","text":"The proof extends from numerical structure to the rectilinear cross composed of four straight lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AS5","text":"The argumentation is reconstructive and symbolic-genealogical: number → figure → letter → Denary → relation of the Ternary to the Septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A1","text":"The Quaternary, according to the cabalistic expansion and the customary phrasing of numeration, summarily displays the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A2","text":"The numbers one, two, three, and four together make ten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A3","text":"Pythagorean authority confirms the identity of the numbers 1, 2, 3, and 4 with the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A4","text":"The rectilinear cross is indicated by four straight lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A5","text":"The rectilinear cross corresponds to the twenty-first letter of the Roman alphabet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A6","text":"The rectilinear cross was adopted by the most ancient Latin philosophers to signify the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A7","text":"The place of the cross in the same series is defined where the Ternary conducts its power through the Septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:A8","text":"Numerical composition and the figure of the cross cohere in the same symbolic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX1","text":"The relation of the cross to the Denary is not established at random.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX2","text":"The cross is not treated as a figure without numerical or alphabetical determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX3","text":"The Denary is not separated from the series ordered through the Quaternary, the cross, the Ternary, and the Septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:NX4","text":"The significance of the cross is not reduced to its bare geometrical form, but is delimited in numerical function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D1","text":"The Quaternary leads to the Denary through the addition of the degrees 1 + 2 + 3 + 4.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A1","CH_MHON_THEV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D2","text":"The figure of four straight lines can be the visible vehicle of the same relation that the arithmetical quaternary number displays.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A2","CH_MHON_THEV:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D3","text":"The twenty-first letter of the Roman alphabet becomes the link between the figure of the cross and alphabetical order.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A4","CH_MHON_THEV:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D4","text":"The adoption of the cross by ancient Latin philosophers adds genealogical authority to the significance of the Denary.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:D5","text":"The position of the cross in the series is not merely descriptive, but is ordered by the passage of the power of the Ternary through the Septenary.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SD1","text":"Number, letter, and figure produce a system of conversion in which the same symbolic unity is produced through arithmetical, alphabetical, and geometrical modes.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A1","CH_MHON_THEV:A4","CH_MHON_THEV:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SD2","text":"The significance of the Denary is constituted not by one isolated sign, but by an order of degrees and relations among the Quaternary, Ternary, and Septenary.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A1","CH_MHON_THEV:A7","CH_MHON_THEV:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SD3","text":"The history of adoption by Latin philosophers converts numerical correspondence into a doctrinal and legitimate tradition.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEV:A3","CH_MHON_THEV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX1","text":"The system does not admit an absolute division between arithmetic, alphabet, and geometry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX2","text":"Visible form cannot be symbolically indifferent, because four straight lines refer to numerical constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX3","text":"The order of numbers is not a mere linear enumeration, but a nexus of degrees transferring their power among themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:DNX4","text":"Interpretation is founded not on arbitrary resemblance, but on correspondence among numerical composition, form, and place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SNX1","text":"The text precludes the possibility of a sign whose figure, number, and place do not correspond to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SNX2","text":"A world is excluded in which the Denary would remain simply an arithmetical sum without figural and alphabetical manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:SNX3","text":"An interpretation that abstracts the symbol from the ordering series of the Ternary and Septenary becomes unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS1","text":"1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS2","text":"Quaternary → Cabalistic expansion → Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS3","text":"Numerical Quaternary → four straight lines → rectilinear cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS4","text":"Rectilinear cross → twenty-first letter of the Roman alphabet → ordered sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS5","text":"Sign of the cross → Latin philosophical adoption → significance of the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS6","text":"Ternary → Septenary → defined place of the cross in the series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:FGS7","text":"Number + figure + letter + place → symbolic unity of the Denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:AF1","text":"Quaternary → sum of 1, 2, 3, 4 → Denary → figure of four straight lines → rectilinear cross → twenty-first letter → Latin adoption → place defined through the Ternary and Septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME1","text":"The Quaternary becomes the principle of transition between arithmetical number and figural sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME2","text":"The cross is reclassified as a geometrical, alphabetical, and numerical nexus, not as a figure alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME3","text":"The Denary becomes the effect of a composite order, not merely the term of an addition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ME4","text":"The relation between the Ternary and the Septenary constitutes the place of the symbol within the series, such that position itself acquires significative force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT1","text":"Surface: Four numbers added together produce the Denary, and the cross is composed of four straight lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT2","text":"Structural: The same quaternary form binds together number, the figure of the cross, and the alphabetical letter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Interpretation operates through translation among arithmetical, geometrical, alphabetical, and doctrinal orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The sign has a place in an order of degrees, where the power of the Ternary reaches the manifestation of the cross through the Septenary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the production of the Denary from the Quaternary and to explain the cross as its sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT2","text":"The link between the twenty-first letter and the Denary number is affirmed in the text, but its further mechanism is not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT3","text":"The relation by which the Ternary conducts its power through the Septenary is indicated, not formally demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT4","text":"The system coheres internally so long as number, figure, and place sustain the same symbolic series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT5","text":"The greatest firmness lies in the addition 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10; the more fragile joint is the transition from arithmetic to the authority of Latin tradition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEV:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: from the numerical Quaternary to the Denary, from the Denary to the cross, and from the cross to its place in the symbolic series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEV@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_THEV:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. VIII."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 09","title":"Theor. VIII.","context":"Chapter 09","original_title":"Theor. Viii.","original_context":"Chapter 09"},"original_title":"Theor. Viii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R. I X.","order":10,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_7"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_7@R001","sha256":"943af30a106f922c145e83060c35784c59b255ee7f0c2904c7a30c94e831a863","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo MONAS, SOL et LVNA per separationem linearum et coniunctionem circularem inter se congruere possint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS2","text":"Textus proponit congruentiam horum terminorum per operationem geometricam elementorum Magiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS3","text":"Fundamentum operationis est separatio exactissima in proprias Lineas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS4","text":"Probatio procedit per circulos ex peripheriis linearum descriptos et in complemento SOLARI coniunctos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS5","text":"Argumentatio est demonstrativa-reconstructiva: separationem geometricam in coniunctionem proportionatam convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS6","text":"Conclusio est quod proportio Crucis DENARIA huiusmodi coniunctioni inserviat et quantitatem congruentiae patefaciat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","text":"MONAS, SOL et LVNA sunt termini quorum congruentia demonstranda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","text":"Quattuor Elementorum Magia materiam operationis geometricam praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","text":"Quaevis magnitudo data in Lineas separari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","text":"Lineae possunt per leges Geometriae in circulos describi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","text":"Peripheriae linearum ad coniunctionem circularem ordinari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","text":"Coniunctio circularis in complemento SOLARI institui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A7","text":"Separatio et coniunctio simul proportionem inter MONADEM, SOLEM et LVNAM constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","text":"Crux DENARIA est forma proportionis quae huic relationi inservit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A9","text":"Quantitas proportionis ex ipsa coniunctione circulari cognosci potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX1","text":"Congruentia MONADIS, SOLIS et LVNAE non per similitudinem indefinitam, sed per separationem in Lineas constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX2","text":"Separatio non est dissolutio sine ordine, sed separatio exactissima in partes determinatas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX3","text":"Coniunctio non praecedit separationem, sed post eam per peripherias linearum efficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX4","text":"Proportio non relinquitur absque mensura, quia per Crucem DENARIAM determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX5","text":"Operatio non excedit leges Geometriae, quia descriptio circuli eis explicite innititur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D1","text":"Si MONAS, SOL et LVNA per quattuor Elementorum Magiam in Lineas separantur et Linearum peripheriae circulos efficiunt, tunc eorum coniunctio circularis fieri potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D2","text":"Si coniunctio circularis in complemento SOLARI fit, tunc separatio linearum ad ordinem solarem refertur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D3","text":"Cum separatio et coniunctio in una operatione componantur, proportio MONADIS, SOLIS et LVNAE fit demonstrabilis.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D4","text":"Si Crux DENARIA huic coniunctioni inservit, proportio non solum exsistit sed etiam quantificari potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SD1","text":"Geometria hic non est mera descriptio formarum, sed medium quo separatio et coniunctio in unam proportionem convertuntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SD2","text":"Congruentia inter MONADEM, SOLEM et LVNAM producitur per seriem transformationum: materia Elementorum in Lineas, Lineae in circulos, circuli in coniunctionem solarem, coniunctio in proportionem denariam.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SD3","text":"Crux DENARIA obtinet munus clausurae formalis, quia relationem inter terminos post operationem geometricam stabilit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A7","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:DNX1","text":"Systema tacite excludit congruentiam quae sine separatione praevia aut sine mediis geometricis immediate assereretur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit oppositionem absolutam inter MONADEM, SOLEM et LVNAM, quia differentia eorum in ordinem coniunctionis transformatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit proportionem pure symbolicam quae a constructione circulari et a mensura DENARIA separata esset.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio impossibilem reddit statum in quo separatio et coniunctio sibi opponuntur ut operationes incompatibiles.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SNX2","text":"Argumentatio non admittit relationem inter MONADEM, SOLEM et LVNAM quae neque in circularem ordinem neque in proportionem formalem reduci possit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS1","text":"Quattuor Elementorum Magia → separatio exactissima in Lineas → determinatio partium ordinatarum.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS2","text":"Lineae datae → peripheriae linearum → circuli secundum leges Geometriae.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS3","text":"Circuli linearum → coniunctio circularis → complementum SOLARE.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS4","text":"Coniunctio circularis → proportio MONADIS, SOLIS et LVNAE → servitium Crucis DENARIAE.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A7","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS5","text":"Proportio constructa → quantitas congruentiae → cognitio ordinis inter tres terminos.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AF1","text":"Congruentia quaerenda → materia quattuor Elementorum → separatio in Lineas → circuli ex peripheriis → coniunctio in complemento SOLARI → proportio Crucis DENARIA → quantitas congruentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AF2","text":"Differentia inter MONADEM, SOLEM et LVNAM → ordinatio geometrica differentiae → coniunctio circularis → relatio proportionalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME1","text":"MONAS, SOL et LVNA e terminis separatis in seriem unius constructionis geometricae reclassificantur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME2","text":"Separatio et coniunctio apparent ut gradus complementarii eiusdem operationis, non ut processus contrarii.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME3","text":"Proportio fit obiectum constructibile et mensurabile, quia a Lineis, circulis et Cruce DENARIA derivatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME4","text":"Ager solaris non est tantum locus coniunctionis, sed complementum quod ordinem circularem recipit et stabilit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT1","text":"Surface: Textus separat MONADEM, SOLEM et LVNAM in Lineas earumque peripherias circulis describit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT2","text":"Structural: Separatio linearum et coniunctio circularis mechanismum constituunt quo termini diversi in proportionem communem rediguntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Argumentatio quaestionem de congruentia transfert ad quaestionem de ordine operationum geometricarum.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Relatio inter tres terminos tamquam processus successivus constituitur, in quo separatio praecedit coniunctionem et coniunctio proportionem efficit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam minimam machinam: separatio linearum, constructio circulorum, coniunctio solaris et proportio denaria.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret, quia omnis gradus posterior ex operatione priore pendet.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS1","CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS2","CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS3","CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT3","text":"Firmitas maxima est in transitu a Lineis ad circulos, quem leges Geometriae directe sustentant.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT4","text":"Minus determinatum manet quomodo singulae MONADIS, SOLIS et LVNAE Lineae construantur et quomodo Crux DENARIA exacte mensuretur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis est transitus a coniunctione circulari ad assertionem de quantitate proportionis, quia regula huius quantificationis non explicatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus, sed vim conclusionis de quantitate partim ex designatione Crucis DENARIAE, non ex demonstratione numerica explicita, accipit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222537152303Z_99bd6e0c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. I X.","source_sha256":"943af30a106f922c145e83060c35784c59b255ee7f0c2904c7a30c94e831a863","sha256":"6a83719bd94700ccc369af64e040dc2a3481a60e967c790c49369dbbef868993","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:25:37.154885+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS1","text":"The central question is how MONAS, SOL, and LVNA can correspond with one another through the separation of lines and circular conjunction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS2","text":"The text proposes the congruence of these terms through the geometric operation of the elements of Magic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS3","text":"The foundation of the operation is the most exact separation into proper Lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS4","text":"The proof proceeds through circles described from the peripheries of lines and joined in the SOLAR complement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS5","text":"The argumentation is demonstrative-reconstructive: it converts geometric separation into proportionate conjunction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AS6","text":"The conclusion is that the DENARY Cross serves such conjunction and discloses the quantity of congruence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","text":"MONAS, SOL, and LVNA are terms whose congruence is to be demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","text":"The Magic of the Four Elements supplies the geometric material of the operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","text":"Any given magnitude can be separated into Lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","text":"Lines can be described into circles according to the laws of Geometry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","text":"The peripheries of lines can be ordered toward circular conjunction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","text":"Circular conjunction can be instituted in the SOLAR complement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A7","text":"Separation and conjunction together establish the proportion among MONAS, SOL, and LVNA.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","text":"The DENARY Cross is a form of proportion that serves this relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:A9","text":"The quantity of proportion can be known from circular conjunction itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX1","text":"The congruence of MONAS, SOL, and LVNA is established not through indefinite similarity, but through separation into Lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX2","text":"Separation is not dissolution without order, but the most exact separation into determinate parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX3","text":"Conjunction does not precede separation, but is effected after it through the peripheries of lines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX4","text":"Proportion is not left without measure, because it is determined through the DENARY Cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:NX5","text":"The operation does not exceed the laws of Geometry, because the description of the circle explicitly rests upon them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D1","text":"If MONAS, SOL, and LVNA are separated into Lines through the Magic of the Four Elements, and the peripheries of the Lines produce circles, then their circular conjunction can occur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D2","text":"If circular conjunction occurs in the SOLAR complement, then the separation of lines is referred to solar order.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D3","text":"When separation and conjunction are combined in one operation, the proportion of MONAS, SOL, and LVNA becomes demonstrable.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:D4","text":"If the DENARY Cross serves this conjunction, proportion not only exists but can also be quantified.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SD1","text":"Geometry here is not a mere description of forms, but the means by which separation and conjunction are converted into one proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SD2","text":"Congruence among MONAS, SOL, and LVNA is produced through a series of transformations: the material of the Elements into Lines, Lines into circles, circles into solar conjunction, conjunction into denary proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SD3","text":"The DENARY Cross assumes the function of formal closure, because it stabilizes the relation among the terms after the geometric operation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A7","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:DNX1","text":"The system tacitly excludes a congruence that would be asserted immediately without prior separation or without geometric means.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:DNX2","text":"The system excludes absolute opposition among MONAS, SOL, and LVNA, because their difference is transformed into an order of conjunction.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a purely symbolic proportion that would be separated from circular construction and from DENARY measure.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SNX1","text":"The argumentation renders impossible a state in which separation and conjunction oppose one another as incompatible operations.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:SNX2","text":"The argumentation does not admit a relation among MONAS, SOL, and LVNA that could be reduced neither to circular order nor to formal proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS1","text":"Magic of the Four Elements → most exact separation into Lines → determination of ordered parts.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS2","text":"Given Lines → peripheries of lines → circles according to the laws of Geometry.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS3","text":"Circles of lines → circular conjunction → SOLAR complement.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS4","text":"Circular conjunction → proportion of MONAS, SOL, and LVNA → service of the DENARY Cross.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A7","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS5","text":"Constructed proportion → quantity of congruence → knowledge of the order among the three terms.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AF1","text":"Congruence to be sought → material of the four Elements → separation into Lines → circles from peripheries → conjunction in the SOLAR complement → proportion of the DENARY Cross → quantity of congruence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:AF2","text":"Difference among MONAS, SOL, and LVNA → geometric ordering of difference → circular conjunction → proportional relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME1","text":"MONAS, SOL, and LVNA are reclassified from separate terms into a series of one geometric construction.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME2","text":"Separation and conjunction appear as complementary stages of the same operation, not as contrary processes.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME3","text":"Proportion becomes a constructible and measurable object, because it is derived from Lines, circles, and the DENARY Cross.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ME4","text":"The solar field is not merely the place of conjunction, but the complement that receives and stabilizes circular order.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT1","text":"Surface: The text separates MONAS, SOL, and LVNA into Lines and describes their peripheries by circles.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A1","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT2","text":"Structural: The separation of lines and circular conjunction constitute the mechanism by which diverse terms are reduced to a common proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The argumentation transfers the question of congruence to the question of the order of geometric operations.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The relation among the three terms is established as a successive process, in which separation precedes conjunction and conjunction effects proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5","CH_MHON_TH_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the minimal mechanism: separation of lines, construction of circles, solar conjunction, and denary proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A2","CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally, because every later stage depends on the prior operation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS1","CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS2","CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS3","CH_MHON_TH_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT3","text":"The greatest firmness lies in the transition from Lines to circles, which the laws of Geometry directly support.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A4","CH_MHON_TH_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT4","text":"It remains less determined how the individual Lines of MONAS, SOL, and LVNA are constructed and how the DENARY Cross is exactly measured.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A3","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT5","text":"The fragile joint is the transition from circular conjunction to the assertion concerning the quantity of proportion, because the rule of this quantification is not explained.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A6","CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_7:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, but receives the force of the conclusion concerning quantity partly from the designation of the DENARY Cross, not from an explicit numerical demonstration.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_7:A8","CH_MHON_TH_7:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_7@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_7:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. I X."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 10","title":"T H E O R. I X.","context":"Chapter 10","original_title":"T H E O R. I X.","original_context":"Chapter 10"},"original_title":"T H E O R. I X.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R. X.","order":11,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_8"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_8@R001","sha256":"29518e2ab3ef73ddd012704618cb4873b7774793a040a34c6c21259b7212da69","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quomodo Aries, ut initium Triplicitatis Igneæ, in praxi MONADIS significationem habeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS2","text":"Signum astronomicum Arietis ad ministerium ignis intra praxim Monadis additur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS3","text":"MONAS per unum contextum hieroglyphicum comprehenditur, non per signa separatim dispersa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS4","text":"In hac Monade Luna et Sol elementa sua separare volunt, dum proportio denaria constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS5","text":"Separatio elementorum fit ministerio ignis, qui simul principium operativum et transitus inter partes est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","text":"Aries ex loco cæli designato exordium Triplicitatis Igneæ notat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","text":"Nota astronomica Arietis in praxi Monadis ad ministerium ignis significandum adhibetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","text":"Monadis una consideratio hieroglyphica per unum contextum hieroglyphicum proferri debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","text":"MONAS Luna et Solem tamquam elementa coniuncta continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","text":"Luna et Sol elementa sua separari volunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","text":"Separatio elementorum intra Monadem non est simplex dissolutio, sed operatio ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A7","text":"Proportio denaria in elementis separatis viget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A8","text":"Ignis ministerium separationis perficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A9","text":"Figura hieroglyphica relationes inter Lunam, Solem, elementa et ignem simul exhibet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A10","text":"Significatio Arietis derivatur ex coordinatione loci astronomici, ignis et structurae Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX1","text":"Monadis non tamquam compositio signorum independentium, sed tamquam unus contextus hieroglyphicus tractanda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX2","text":"Separatio Lunae et Solis non significat annihilationem eorum communis ordinis in Monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX3","text":"Proportio elementorum non relinquitur indefinita, sed denaria ratione circumscribitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX4","text":"Ignis non est elementum passive adiectum, sed ministerium eius separationem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX5","text":"Aries non est ornamentum graphicum sine munere, quia ad significationem ignis et exordii refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX6","text":"Figura non est mera imago astronomica, quia relationes operativas inter partes significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D1","text":"Aries locum initialem ignis intra ordinem Monadis designat.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D2","text":"Nota astronomica Arietis fit signum operationis, quia ministerium ignis per eam introducitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D3","text":"Unitas contextus hieroglyphici permittit ut Luna, Sol, elementa et ignis tamquam systema relationale legantur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D4","text":"Separatio elementorum necessario postulat proportionem quae relationem partium conservet.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D5","text":"Ignis est medium quo unitas Monadis in distinctiones ordinatas convertitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D6","text":"Significatio Monadis generatur ex simultanea retentione unitatis, separationis et proportionis.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD1","text":"Unitas Monadis non opponitur differentiationi, sed eam continet tamquam processum internum.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD2","text":"Separatio fit intelligibilis tantum si per proportionem et ministerium ignis in ordinem convertitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD3","text":"Astronomia, geometria symbolica et operatio alchemica in uno signo hieroglyphico coniunguntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7","CH_MHON_TH_8:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD4","text":"Ignis constituit transitum ontologicum a Monade indivisa ad elementa distincta sine ruptura totalis unitatis.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD5","text":"Exordium astronomicum simul initium processus transformationis internæ Monadis evadit.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit conceptionem Monadis ut unitatis omnino immobilis et sine differentiatione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit separationem quae sine proportione, mensura vel relatione fieret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit interpretationem ignis ut materiae tantum inter elementa collocatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit disiunctionem inter signum astronomicum et operationem hieroglyphicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit ideam quod sensus unius signi ex sola figura visibili sine contextu relationum oriatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX1","text":"Textus circumit possibilitatem ut unitas et divisio sint principia inter se absolute incompatibilia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX2","text":"Textus praecludit cosmologiam in qua partes separatae nullam proportionem communem retinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX3","text":"Textus tacite removet ordinem in quo ignis nihil intermedii vel transformativi efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX4","text":"Textus non admittit significationem quae inter astronomiam, symbolum et praxim nullum nexum causalem vel formativum agnoscat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS1","text":"Locus astronomicus Arietis → Exordium Triplicitatis Igneæ → Requisitio ministerii ignis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS2","text":"Nota astronomica Arietis + praxis Monadis → Significatio ignis ut operationis internæ.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS3","text":"MONAS una → Luna et Sol in communi contextu → Elementorum distinctio.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS4","text":"Elementorum distinctio + proportio denaria → Separatio ordinata.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS5","text":"Separatio ordinata + ministerium ignis → Contextus hieroglyphicus completus.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A8","CH_MHON_TH_8:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS6","text":"Contextus hieroglyphicus → Unitas quae differentiationem continet → Interpretatio Monadis tamquam processus.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:D6","CH_MHON_TH_8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF1","text":"Locus Arietis → Exordium ignis → Additio notæ astronomicæ → Praxi Monadis applicatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF2","text":"Unitas Monadis → Coniunctio Lunae et Solis → Voluntas separationis → Proportio denaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF3","text":"Proportio denaria → Ministerium ignis → Separatio ordinata → Unus contextus hieroglyphicus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF4","text":"Figura composita → Relatio astronomica, elementaris et operativa → Reconstitutio Monadis ut unitatis differentiantis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME1","text":"Aries fit non solum initium zodiacale, sed index processus quo ignis distinctionem internam Monadis producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME2","text":"Luna et Sol reclassificantur ab imaginibus caelestibus ad elementa intra operationem proportionatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME3","text":"Separatio et unitas desinunt esse oppositiones simplices, quia separatio tamquam actus internus unitatis describitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME4","text":"Ignis reponitur in categoria mediationis operativæ, non in categoria elementi tantum descripti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME5","text":"Figura hieroglyphica ordinat simul locum, substantias, proportionem et operationem, ita ut lectio linearis singulorum signorum insufficiens fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT1","text":"Surface: Aries, Luna, Sol, elementa et ignis in contextu hieroglyphico coniunguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT2","text":"Structural: Monadis unitas per separationem elementorum et proportionem denariam operatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Signum astronomicum convertitur in instrumentum quo relatio inter caelum, figuram et praxim legitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Exordium Arietis initium temporale simul et transitum ontologicum ab unitate ad distinctionem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam catenam ab Ariete et exordio ignis ad separationem Lunae et Solis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT2","text":"Unitas contextus, separatio elementorum, proportio denaria et ministerium ignis sunt nuclei sine quibus argumentatio deficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT3","text":"Structura interne cohaeret, quia divisio non extra Monadem ponitur, sed ab eius operatione generatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT4","text":"Relatio exacta proportionis denariae non plene determinatur: textus eam statuit, sed modum eius numerice explicatum non tradit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT5","text":"Status ignis inter elementum, signum et ministerium operativum non omnino disambiguatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT6","text":"Figura relationes principales exhibet, sed sola inspectio eius non sufficit ad omnem ordinem transformationis deducendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: locus astronomicus → ministerium ignis → separatio proportionata → contextus hieroglyphicus unificatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222558081660Z_350e3a7d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. X.","source_sha256":"29518e2ab3ef73ddd012704618cb4873b7774793a040a34c6c21259b7212da69","sha256":"b5a88d0d8e9df0573fbe88e7a305b80886d4cc1a552112f7e05e5dd831d76a36","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:25:58.084384+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS1","text":"The question is how Aries, as the beginning of the Fiery Triplicity, has significance in the practice of the MONAD.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS2","text":"The astronomical sign of Aries is added for the service of fire within the practice of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS3","text":"The MONAD is comprehended through one hieroglyphic context, not through signs separately scattered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS4","text":"In this Monad the Moon and the Sun wish to separate their elements, while a tenfold proportion is established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AS5","text":"The separation of the elements occurs through the service of fire, which is at once the operative principle and the passage between the parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","text":"Aries, from its designated place in heaven, marks the beginning of the Fiery Triplicity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","text":"The astronomical mark of Aries is employed in the practice of the Monad to signify the service of fire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","text":"A single hieroglyphic consideration of the Monad must be set forth through one hieroglyphic context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","text":"The MONAD contains the Moon and the Sun as conjoined elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","text":"The Moon and the Sun wish for their elements to be separated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","text":"The separation of the elements within the Monad is not a simple dissolution, but an ordered operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A7","text":"A tenfold proportion prevails in the separated elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A8","text":"Fire accomplishes the service of separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A9","text":"The hieroglyphic figure simultaneously displays the relations among the Moon, the Sun, the elements, and fire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:A10","text":"The significance of Aries is derived from the coordination of astronomical place, fire, and the structure of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX1","text":"The Monad is to be treated not as a composition of independent signs, but as one hieroglyphic context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX2","text":"The separation of the Moon and the Sun does not signify the annihilation of their common order in the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX3","text":"The proportion of the elements is not left indefinite, but is delimited by a tenfold ratio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX4","text":"Fire is not an element passively added, but its service constitutes separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX5","text":"Aries is not a graphic ornament without function, because it refers to the significance of fire and of beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:NX6","text":"The figure is not a mere astronomical image, because it signifies operative relations among the parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D1","text":"Aries designates the initial place of fire within the order of the Monad.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D2","text":"The astronomical mark of Aries becomes a sign of operation, because through it the service of fire is introduced.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D3","text":"The unity of the hieroglyphic context allows the Moon, the Sun, the elements, and fire to be read as a relational system.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D4","text":"The separation of the elements necessarily requires a proportion that preserves the relation of the parts.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D5","text":"Fire is the means by which the unity of the Monad is converted into ordered distinctions.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:D6","text":"The significance of the Monad is generated from the simultaneous retention of unity, separation, and proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD1","text":"The unity of the Monad is not opposed to differentiation, but contains it as an internal process.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD2","text":"Separation becomes intelligible only if it is converted into order through proportion and the service of fire.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD3","text":"Astronomy, symbolic geometry, and alchemical operation are joined in one hieroglyphic sign.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7","CH_MHON_TH_8:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD4","text":"Fire constitutes the ontological passage from the undivided Monad to distinct elements without rupture of total unity.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SD5","text":"The astronomical beginning simultaneously becomes the beginning of the process of the Monad's internal transformation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the conception of the Monad as a unity wholly immobile and without differentiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a separation that would occur without proportion, measure, or relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an interpretation of fire as merely matter placed among the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a disjunction between the astronomical sign and the hieroglyphic operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:DNX5","text":"The system excludes the idea that the meaning of one sign arises from visible figure alone, without a context of relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX1","text":"The text avoids the possibility that unity and division are principles absolutely incompatible with one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX2","text":"The text precludes a cosmology in which separated parts retain no common proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX3","text":"The text tacitly removes an order in which fire effects nothing intermediary or transformative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:SNX4","text":"The text does not admit a significance that acknowledges no causal or formative connection among astronomy, symbol, and practice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS1","text":"Astronomical place of Aries → Beginning of the Fiery Triplicity → Requirement of the service of fire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS2","text":"Astronomical mark of Aries + practice of the Monad → Significance of fire as an internal operation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A1","CH_MHON_TH_8:A2","CH_MHON_TH_8:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS3","text":"One MONAD → Moon and Sun in a common context → Distinction of the elements.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:A4","CH_MHON_TH_8:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS4","text":"Distinction of the elements + tenfold proportion → Ordered separation.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A6","CH_MHON_TH_8:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS5","text":"Ordered separation + service of fire → Complete hieroglyphic context.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A8","CH_MHON_TH_8:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:FGS6","text":"Hieroglyphic context → Unity that contains differentiation → Interpretation of the Monad as process.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_8:A3","CH_MHON_TH_8:D6","CH_MHON_TH_8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF1","text":"Place of Aries → Beginning of fire → Addition of the astronomical mark → Application to the practice of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF2","text":"Unity of the Monad → Conjunction of the Moon and the Sun → Will to separation → Tenfold proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF3","text":"Tenfold proportion → Service of fire → Ordered separation → One hieroglyphic context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:AF4","text":"Composite figure → Astronomical, elemental, and operative relation → Reconstitution of the Monad as differentiating unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME1","text":"Aries becomes not only a zodiacal beginning, but an index of the process by which fire produces the Monad's internal distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME2","text":"The Moon and the Sun are reclassified from celestial images into elements within a proportionate operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME3","text":"Separation and unity cease to be simple oppositions, because separation is described as an internal act of unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME4","text":"Fire is repositioned in the category of operative mediation, not in the category of a merely described element.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ME5","text":"The hieroglyphic figure orders place, substances, proportion, and operation simultaneously, so that a linear reading of individual signs becomes insufficient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT1","text":"Surface: Aries, the Moon, the Sun, the elements, and fire are joined in a hieroglyphic context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT2","text":"Structural: The unity of the Monad operates through the separation of the elements and tenfold proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The astronomical sign is converted into an instrument through which the relation among heaven, figure, and practice is read.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: The beginning of Aries constitutes at once a temporal beginning and an ontological passage from unity to distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the chain from Aries and the beginning of fire to the separation of the Moon and the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT2","text":"The unity of the context, the separation of the elements, tenfold proportion, and the service of fire are the nuclei without which the argument fails.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT3","text":"The structure coheres internally, because division is not placed outside the Monad, but is generated by its operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT4","text":"The exact relation of the tenfold proportion is not fully determined: the text establishes it, but does not provide its numerically explained mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT5","text":"The status of fire between element, sign, and operative service is not wholly disambiguated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT6","text":"The figure displays the principal relations, but inspection of it alone does not suffice to deduce the entire order of transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_8:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: astronomical place → service of fire → proportionate separation → unified hieroglyphic context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_8@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_8:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. X."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 11","title":"T H E O R. X.","context":"Chapter 11","original_title":"T H E O R. X.","original_context":"Chapter 11"},"original_title":"T H E O R. X.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. XI.","order":12,"parents":["RAW_MHON_THEX"],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEX@R001","sha256":"a5f39324c18e5262898cec21249fe3f509ea8be84e66c6a3de95d5ecc49b01d8","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo nota mystica Arietis in ordine nycthemerae collocanda sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS2","text":"Figura duobus semicirculis in puncto communi connexis constituta locum aequinoctialem nycthemerae aptissime significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS3","text":"Fundamentum probationis est analogia inter formam signi et distributionem temporis per viginti quattuor horas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS4","text":"Distributio aequinoctialis temporis occultas proportiones indicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS5","text":"Motus argumenti procedit a figura → ad locum temporalem → ad proportionem occultam → ad relationem cum Terra.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A1","text":"Nota mystica Arietis ex duobus semicirculis constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A2","text":"Semicirculi in puncto communi connexi sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A3","text":"Nota Arietis ad locum aequinoctialem nycthemerae assignatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A4","text":"Nycthemera tempus viginti quattuor horarum continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A5","text":"Tempus nycthemerae modo aequinoctiali distribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A6","text":"Distributio aequinoctialis occultas proportiones denotat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A7","text":"Proportiones dictae ad Terram referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX1","text":"Nota Arietis non ut figura libera, sed ut compositio duorum semicirculorum connexorum definitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX2","text":"Locus notae non extra ordinem aequinoctialem quaeritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX3","text":"Tempus nycthemerae non ut continuum indifferens, sed ut distributum et proportionale accipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX4","text":"Proportiones indicatae non ad caelum solum, sed ad Terram referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D1","text":"Figura duorum semicirculorum et puncti communis formam temporaliter divisam repraesentare potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A1","CH_MHON_THEX:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D2","text":"Assignatio ad locum aequinoctialem figuram in ordinem nycthemerae constituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D3","text":"Divisio aequinoctialis viginti quattuor horarum fit signum proportionis, non mera designatio temporis.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A5","CH_MHON_THEX:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D4","text":"Nota Arietis relationem symbolicam inter configurationem figurae, ordinem temporis et Terram instituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A1","CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A6","CH_MHON_THEX:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD1","text":"Significatio hieroglyphica ex analogia ordinum provenit: forma signi ordinem temporalem reddit, ordo temporalis proportionem occultam manifestat.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A1","CH_MHON_THEX:A5","CH_MHON_THEX:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD2","text":"Tempus terrestre intra symbolum caelesti specie constitutum theoretice ordinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD3","text":"Nota mystica non solum obiectum caeleste designat, sed proportionem inter signum, tempus et locum terrestre producit.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A6","CH_MHON_THEX:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD4","text":"Secretum signi in quantificabili distributione temporis positum est, quamquam ipsa proportio ulterius non determinatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A5","CH_MHON_THEX:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX1","text":"Systema non admittit significationem quae a forma materiali notae et ab eius connexione interna seiungatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX2","text":"Systema non admittit tempus sine partitione aequinoctiali tamquam fundamentum huius significationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX3","text":"Systema non admittit proportionem occultam quae a relatione ad Terram omnino abstrahatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX4","text":"Systema tacite excludit interpretationem quae notam Arietis ad unam rem isolatam reducat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio circumit, quin explicite constituat, quomodo figura geometrica horas singulas aut partes temporis repraesentet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX2","text":"Possibilitas signum esse meram conventionem arbitrariam praeclusa est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX3","text":"Absens manet definitio formalis vocis «proportiones»; haec absentia efficit ut secretum interpretationis retineatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX4","text":"Non datur schema explicitum quo relatio inter «nostras» proportiones et Terram verificari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS1","text":"Compositio duorum semicirculorum + connexio in puncto communi → unitas formalis notae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS2","text":"Unitas formalis + assignatio ad locum aequinoctialem → insertio notae in ordine nycthemerico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS3","text":"Nycthemera viginti quattuor horarum + distributio aequinoctialis → structura temporalis proportionata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS4","text":"Structura temporalis proportionata → denotatio proportionum occultarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS5","text":"Proportiones occultae + relatio ad Terram → significatio terrestris notae mysticae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AF1","text":"Figura connexa → locus aequinoctialis → nycthemera viginti quattuor horarum → distributio aequinoctialis → proportiones occultae → relatio ad Terram.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME1","text":"Nota Arietis ex figura isolata in nodum relationis inter formam, tempus et Terram reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME2","text":"Nycthemera fit tabula proportionum, non tantum mensura horarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME3","text":"Aequinoctium fit principium ordinationis quo figura hieroglyphica temporaliter legibilis redditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME4","text":"«Occultum» non extra ordinem numerabilem ponitur, sed in distributione temporis iam constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** Nota Arietis duobus semicirculis connexis describitur et ad locum aequinoctialem assignatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** Viginti quattuor horae per modum aequinoctialem distribuuntur et in proportiones convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** Lectio signi a designatione astrologica ad interpretationem hieroglyphicam relationum transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Tempus terrestre tamquam ordo occultas proportiones continens concipitur, non tamquam series neutra momentorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam transitionem a figura notae ad locum aequinoctialem et ad tempus distributum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT2","text":"Restitutio servat motum a forma ad proportionem et a proportione ad Terram.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT3","text":"Interna cohaerentia pendet ex aequatione implicita inter formam semicirculorum et distributionem temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT4","text":"Nondum satis determinatur quae proportiones «secretissimae» sint aut quomodo singulis partibus figurae respondeant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT5","text":"Relatio vocis «nostras» ad Terram ambigua manet et argumentationem non plene claudit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222339430358Z_af4c137d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOR. XI.","source_sha256":"a5f39324c18e5262898cec21249fe3f509ea8be84e66c6a3de95d5ecc49b01d8","sha256":"1eeb77fa551521871171d20154f569a47c498316936bdcd5450662b593e869d6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:23:39.432973+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS1","text":"The central question is how the mystical sign of Aries is to be situated within the order of the nycthemeron.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS2","text":"A figure constituted by two semicircles joined at a common point most fittingly signifies the equinoctial position of the nycthemeron.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS3","text":"The foundation of the proof is the analogy between the form of the sign and the distribution of time over twenty-four hours.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS4","text":"The equinoctial distribution of time indicates hidden proportions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from figure → to temporal position → to hidden proportion → to relation with the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A1","text":"The mystical sign of Aries is constituted from two semicircles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A2","text":"The semicircles are joined at a common point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A3","text":"The sign of Aries is assigned to the equinoctial position of the nycthemeron.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A4","text":"The nycthemeron contains a span of twenty-four hours.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A5","text":"The time of the nycthemeron is distributed in an equinoctial manner.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A6","text":"The equinoctial distribution denotes hidden proportions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:A7","text":"The stated proportions refer to the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX1","text":"The sign of Aries is defined not as a free figure, but as a composition of two connected semicircles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX2","text":"The position of the sign is not sought outside the equinoctial order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX3","text":"The time of the nycthemeron is understood not as an indifferent continuum, but as distributed and proportional.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:NX4","text":"The indicated proportions are referred not to heaven alone, but to the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D1","text":"The figure of two semicircles and a common point can represent a temporally divided form.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A1","CH_MHON_THEX:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D2","text":"Assignment to the equinoctial position places the figure within the order of the nycthemeron.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D3","text":"The equinoctial division of twenty-four hours becomes a sign of proportion, not a mere designation of time.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A5","CH_MHON_THEX:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:D4","text":"The sign of Aries establishes a symbolic relation between the configuration of the figure, the order of time, and the Earth.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A1","CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A6","CH_MHON_THEX:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD1","text":"Hieroglyphic significance arises from an analogy of orders: the form of the sign renders the temporal order, and the temporal order manifests hidden proportion.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A1","CH_MHON_THEX:A5","CH_MHON_THEX:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD2","text":"Terrestrial time is theoretically ordered within a symbol constituted under a celestial aspect.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD3","text":"The mystical sign not only designates a celestial object, but produces a proportion between sign, time, and terrestrial place.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A3","CH_MHON_THEX:A6","CH_MHON_THEX:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SD4","text":"The secret of the sign lies in the quantifiable distribution of time, although the proportion itself is not further determined.","refs":["CH_MHON_THEX:A4","CH_MHON_THEX:A5","CH_MHON_THEX:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX1","text":"The system does not admit a meaning that is separated from the material form of the sign and from its internal connection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX2","text":"The system does not admit time without equinoctial partition as the foundation of this meaning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX3","text":"The system does not admit a hidden proportion that is wholly abstracted from relation to the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:DNX4","text":"The system tacitly excludes an interpretation that reduces the sign of Aries to a single isolated thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX1","text":"The argument bypasses, without explicitly establishing, how the geometric figure represents individual hours or portions of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX2","text":"The possibility that the sign is a mere arbitrary convention is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX3","text":"A formal definition of the term «proportions» remains absent; this absence causes the secret of the interpretation to be retained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:SNX4","text":"No explicit schema is given by which the relation between «our» proportions and the Earth can be verified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS1","text":"Composition of two semicircles + connection at a common point → formal unity of the sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS2","text":"Formal unity + assignment to the equinoctial position → insertion of the sign into the order of the nycthemeron.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS3","text":"Nycthemeron of twenty-four hours + equinoctial distribution → proportioned temporal structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS4","text":"Proportioned temporal structure → denotation of hidden proportions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:FGS5","text":"Hidden proportions + relation to the Earth → terrestrial significance of the mystical sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:AF1","text":"Connected figure → equinoctial position → nycthemeron of twenty-four hours → equinoctial distribution → hidden proportions → relation to the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME1","text":"The sign of Aries is reclassified from an isolated figure into a node of relation among form, time, and the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME2","text":"The nycthemeron becomes a table of proportions, not merely a measure of hours.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME3","text":"The equinox becomes a principle of ordering through which the hieroglyphic figure is rendered temporally legible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ME4","text":"«Hidden» is not placed outside numerical order, but is already constituted in the distribution of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** The sign of Aries is described by two connected semicircles and assigned to the equinoctial position.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** Twenty-four hours are distributed in an equinoctial manner and converted into proportions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** The reading of the sign passes from astrological designation to a hieroglyphic interpretation of relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Terrestrial time is conceived as an order containing hidden proportions, not as a neutral series of moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the transition from the figure of the sign to the equinoctial position and to distributed time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement from form to proportion and from proportion to the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence depends on the implicit equation between the form of the semicircles and the distribution of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT4","text":"It is not yet sufficiently determined what the «most secret» proportions are or how they correspond to the individual parts of the figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_THEX:MRT5","text":"The relation of the word «our» to the Earth remains ambiguous and does not fully close the argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_THEX@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_THEX:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"THEOR. XI."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 12","title":"Theor. XI.","context":"Chapter 12","original_title":"Theor. Xi.","original_context":"Chapter 12"},"original_title":"Theor. Xi.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9","layer":"CH","title":"T H E O R. XII.","order":13,"parents":["RAW_MHON_TH_9"],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_9@R001","sha256":"0332e62ffbc19552cf9d2cf3f7e17c9790f2a30643ef79018d1baaf72c093f20","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quomodo Notae Hieroglyphicae planetarum ex characteribus Lunae vel Solis cum signo Elementorum aut Arietis componantur et explicentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS2","text":"Quaestio in structuram processualem convertitur, quia signum Lunare per successiones elementatas ac revolutiones naturae interpretandum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS3","text":"Fundamentum expositionis est systema prius iactis Fundamentis, quo singulae figurae hieroglyphicae explicabiles redduntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS4","text":"Probatio procedit a natura Lunari ad Saturnum, Iovem et Mercurium, deinde ad substitutionem operativam Spiritus Magici et Solis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis est: compositio signorum → interpretatio Lunaris → successiones elementatae → mediazione Spiritus et Solis → impressio figurarum in Terram praeparatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A1","text":"Notae Hieroglyphicae quinque Planetarum a Sapientibus Magis traditae sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A2","text":"Notae planetariae componuntur ex Characteribus Lunae vel Solis et signo Elementorum aut Arietis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A3","text":"Signorum compositio per fundamenta iam posita explicari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A4","text":"Natura Lunaris per scientiam Elementorum circa Terram revolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","text":"Eadem Natura Lunaris diversis gradibus vel vicibus elementatis sub nominibus Saturni, Iovis et Mercurii significatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A6","text":"Mercurius, quamvis Lunaris sit, quarta Revolutione produci potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A7","text":"Opus secretum non impugnatur si alii Sophi Mercurium quarta Revolutione productum esse volunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A8","text":"Spiritus Purissimus Magicus locum Lunae in opere λευκώσεως obtinere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A9","text":"Virtus spiritualis potest cum Solo per quandam Mediam Naturalem sine verbis hieroglyphice operari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A10","text":"Terra praeparata et simplicissima potest figuras geogamicas suscipere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A11","text":"Spiritus Magicus figuras in Terram introducit atque imprimit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A12","text":"Significatio planetaria non in nomine solo, sed in ordine compositivo et processu productionis figurarum consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX1","text":"Notae Hieroglyphicae non sunt characteres simplices, sed compositiones ex pluribus signis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX2","text":"Interpretatio signorum non separatur a fundamentis antea positis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX3","text":"Productio Mercurii quarta Revolutione non excluditur propter opinionem aliorum Sophorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX4","text":"Operatio spiritualis non requirit verba vocalia, quia Sol hieroglyphice per Mediam Naturalem loqui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX5","text":"Luna non est unica forma operativa operis, quia Spiritus Magicus eius locum administrare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D1","text":"Cum Notae ex Luna vel Sole et signo Elementorum componantur, figura hieroglyphica simul originem astralem et determinationem elementarem exhibet.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A1","CH_MHON_TH_9:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D2","text":"Cum Natura Lunaris per plures vicissitudines elementatas describatur, nomina Saturni, Iovis et Mercurii gradus eiusdem processualis indicant.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A4","CH_MHON_TH_9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D3","text":"Quarta Revolutio non delet ordinem Lunarem Mercurii, sed eum ad ulteriorem gradum productionis refert.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","CH_MHON_TH_9:A6","CH_MHON_TH_9:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D4","text":"Substitutio Lunae per Spiritum Magicum mutat medium operis, non finem eius, qui est administratio λευκώσεως.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D5","text":"Operatio Solis fit translatio spiritualis in medium naturale, quo signa sine locutione materiali exprimuntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D6","text":"Impressio figurarum in Terram facit ut hieroglyphicum non solum interpretetur, sed materialiter producatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A10","CH_MHON_TH_9:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD1","text":"Systema planetarium ordinatur tamquam series transformationum unius naturae, non tamquam collectio entitatum astralium separatarum.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A4","CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","CH_MHON_TH_9:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD2","text":"Hieroglyphicum fit machina transitus inter ordinem cosmologicum, processum magicum et inscriptionem materialem.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A2","CH_MHON_TH_9:A9","CH_MHON_TH_9:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD3","text":"Nomina planetarum funguntur ut indices occultorum graduum operationis, quorum sensus plene non datur nisi per successionem et compositionem.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","CH_MHON_TH_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD4","text":"Spiritus Magicus instituit mediatorem inter Lunam, Solem, Elementa et Terram, ita ut operis unitas per substitutionem servetur.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A8","CH_MHON_TH_9:A9","CH_MHON_TH_9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD5","text":"Auctoritas tradita et interpretatio operativa simul sustentant systema: traditio praebet formas, fundamenta praebent regulas productionis.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A1","CH_MHON_TH_9:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet hieroglyphicum signum esse meram designationem planetariae sine compositione elementorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet successiones Saturni, Iovis et Mercurii esse nominum disiunctas potius quam gradus unius Naturae Lunaris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet productionem magicam consistere in passiva receptione signorum, cum opus ad inscriptionem activam figurarum procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet substitutionem Lunae per Spiritum Magicum continuitatem operis tollere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet communicationem hieroglyphicam a voce, sermone vel locutione materiali pendere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX1","text":"Textus excludit chaos signorum in quo figurae sine ordine genealogico vel processuali exsisterent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX2","text":"Textus excludit dualismum absolutum inter operationem caelestem et operationem terrestrem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX3","text":"Textus excludit ideam unius instrumenti cosmici immutabilis, quia Luna per Spiritum Magicum substitui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX4","text":"Textus circumit sed plene non nominat regulam quae determinat quomodo singulae figurae ex quattuor vicibus elementatis producantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX5","text":"Textus tacite praecludit distinctionem inter significationem hieroglyphicam et efficaciam materialem: figura simul loquitur et agit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS1","text":"Character Lunae vel Solis + signum Elementorum aut Arietis → Nota Hieroglyphica composita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS2","text":"Nota Lunaris → Natura Lunaris → revolutio circa Terram → vicissitudines elementatae → indices Saturni, Iovis et Mercurii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS3","text":"Quarta Revolutio + admissio doctrinae Sophorum → productio Mercurii sine contradictione cum proposito secreto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS4","text":"Spiritus Purissimus Magicus pro Luna → administratio λευκώσεως → virtus spiritualis cum Solo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS5","text":"Sol + Media Naturalis + silentium verborum → locutio hieroglyphica → Terra pura et simplex → introductio et impressio figurarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AF1","text":"Notae planetariae compositae → explicabilitas per fundamenta priora → interpretatio signorum Lunarium → series revolutionum elementatarum → Mercurius quarta Revolutione → substitutio Lunae per Spiritum Magicum → actio Solis per Mediam Naturalem → impressio figurarum in Terram.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AF2","text":"Diversitas nominum planetariorum → unitas Naturae Lunaris → gradatio processualis → translatio cosmica in operationem magicam → materialis effectus hieroglyphicus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME1","text":"Signum planetarium fit obiectum quod simul secundum originem astralem, compositionem elementarem et gradum operationis classificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter Lunae et Solis characteres reordinatur tamquam differentia inter principium, medium et complementum operis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME3","text":"Nomina Saturni, Iovis et Mercurii reclassificantur ut stationes transformationis Naturae Lunaris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME4","text":"Terra non amplius apparet ut finis passivus, sed ut superficies receptiva et productiva figurarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME5","text":"Silentium verborum fit condicio communicationis hieroglyphicae, non defectus communicationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT1","text":"Surface — Signa Lunae vel Solis cum Elementorum aut Arietis signo componuntur et figurae in Terram imprimuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT2","text":"Structural — Una Natura Lunaris per revolutiones et vicissitudines elementatas in gradus Saturni, Iovis et Mercurii ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Interpretatio ex nominibus planetariis ad mechanismum productionis transfertur, ita ut controversia de quarta Revolutione systema non dissolvat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Res magicae constituuntur ut series transformationum inter Lunam, Spiritum, Solem, Elementa et Terram, quarum tempora per revolutiones definiuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam lineam principalem a compositione signorum ad inscriptionem figurarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret, quia substitutio Lunae per Spiritum Magicum explicatur ut mutatio medii intra idem opus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT3","text":"Firmitas maxima consistit in connexione inter compositionem signorum, successionem elementatam et effectum materialem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT4","text":"Determinatio exacta quattuor revolutionum et relationis inter singulas figuras in textu excerpto nondum plena est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT5","text":"Productio Mercurii quarta Revolutione admittitur, sed regula formalis huius productionis non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT6","text":"Restitutio nititur aliquantum in terminis arcanis et in transitione a figura visibili ad processum invisibilem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT7","text":"Schema servat verum motum textus: a forma composita ad ordinem processualem, inde ad mediationem spiritualem et ad effectum terrestre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222619085226Z_31281cd3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"T H E O R. XII.","source_sha256":"0332e62ffbc19552cf9d2cf3f7e17c9790f2a30643ef79018d1baaf72c093f20","sha256":"997d20f1cd627ba7882b8dcc2a6d98c0949b97dd11974dce4fd75e6baa5ae075","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:26:19.086125+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS1","text":"The question is how the Hieroglyphic Notes of the planets are composed from the characters of the Moon or the Sun together with the sign of the Elements or of Aries, and how they are to be explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS2","text":"The question is converted into a processual structure, because the Lunar sign must be interpreted through elemental successions and revolutions of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS3","text":"The foundation of the exposition is the system of Foundations previously laid down, by which the individual hieroglyphic figures are rendered explicable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS4","text":"The demonstration proceeds from Lunar nature to Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury, then to the operative substitution of the Magical Spirit and the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument is: composition of signs → Lunar interpretation → elemental successions → mediation of Spirit and Sun → impression of figures upon prepared Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A1","text":"The Hieroglyphic Notes of the five Planets were handed down by the Magi Sages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A2","text":"Planetary Notes are composed from the Characters of the Moon or the Sun and the sign of the Elements or of Aries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A3","text":"The composition of signs can be explained through foundations already laid down.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A4","text":"Lunar Nature revolves around the Earth through knowledge of the Elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","text":"The same Lunar Nature is signified at different elemental degrees or turns under the names of Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A6","text":"Mercury, although Lunar, can be produced by the fourth Revolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A7","text":"The secret work is not impugned if other Sages hold that Mercury is produced by the fourth Revolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A8","text":"The Most Pure Magical Spirit can occupy the place of the Moon in the work of λευκώσεως.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A9","text":"Spiritual power can operate hieroglyphically with the Sun through a certain Natural Medium without words.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A10","text":"Prepared and most simple Earth can receive geogamic figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A11","text":"The Magical Spirit introduces and impresses figures into the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:A12","text":"Planetary signification consists not in the name alone, but in the compositional order and the process of producing figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX1","text":"Hieroglyphic Notes are not simple characters, but compositions from several signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX2","text":"The interpretation of signs is not separated from the foundations previously laid down.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX3","text":"The production of Mercury by the fourth Revolution is not excluded on account of the opinion of other Sages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX4","text":"Spiritual operation does not require spoken words, because the Sun can speak hieroglyphically through the Natural Medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:NX5","text":"The Moon is not the sole operative form of the work, because the Magical Spirit can administer its place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D1","text":"Since the Notes are composed from the Moon or Sun and the sign of the Elements, the hieroglyphic figure displays at once an astral origin and an elemental determination.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A1","CH_MHON_TH_9:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D2","text":"Since Lunar Nature is described through several elemental vicissitudes, the names Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury indicate stages of the same process.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A4","CH_MHON_TH_9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D3","text":"The fourth Revolution does not erase Mercury's Lunar order, but refers it to a further stage of production.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","CH_MHON_TH_9:A6","CH_MHON_TH_9:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D4","text":"The substitution of the Moon by the Magical Spirit changes the medium of the work, not its end, which is the administration of λευκώσεως.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D5","text":"The operation of the Sun is a spiritual transmission into a natural medium, whereby signs are expressed without material utterance.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:D6","text":"The impression of figures upon Earth makes the hieroglyphic not only interpreted, but materially produced.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A10","CH_MHON_TH_9:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD1","text":"The planetary system is ordered as a series of transformations of one nature, not as a collection of separate astral entities.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A4","CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","CH_MHON_TH_9:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD2","text":"The hieroglyphic becomes a machine of passage between cosmological order, magical process, and material inscription.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A2","CH_MHON_TH_9:A9","CH_MHON_TH_9:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD3","text":"The names of the planets function as indices of hidden stages of operation, whose meaning is not fully given except through succession and composition.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A5","CH_MHON_TH_9:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD4","text":"The Magical Spirit establishes a mediator between Moon, Sun, Elements, and Earth, so that the unity of the work is preserved through substitution.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A8","CH_MHON_TH_9:A9","CH_MHON_TH_9:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SD5","text":"Handed-down authority and operative interpretation jointly sustain the system: tradition supplies the forms, the foundations supply the rules of production.","refs":["CH_MHON_TH_9:A1","CH_MHON_TH_9:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX1","text":"It must be false that a hieroglyphic sign is a mere designation of the planetary without a composition of elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the successions of Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury are disjoined names rather than stages of one Lunar Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX3","text":"It must be false that magical production consists in the passive reception of signs, since the work proceeds to the active inscription of figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the substitution of the Moon by the Magical Spirit removes the continuity of the work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:DNX5","text":"It must be false that hieroglyphic communication depends on voice, speech, or material utterance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX1","text":"The text excludes a chaos of signs in which figures would exist without genealogical or processual order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX2","text":"The text excludes an absolute dualism between celestial operation and terrestrial operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX3","text":"The text excludes the idea of one immutable cosmic instrument, because the Moon can be substituted by the Magical Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX4","text":"The text skirts around but does not fully name the rule that determines how individual figures are produced from four elemental turns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:SNX5","text":"The text tacitly forecloses the distinction between hieroglyphic signification and material efficacy: the figure speaks and acts simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS1","text":"Character of the Moon or Sun + sign of the Elements or of Aries → composite Hieroglyphic Note.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS2","text":"Lunar Note → Lunar Nature → revolution around the Earth → elemental vicissitudes → indices of Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS3","text":"Fourth Revolution + acceptance of the doctrine of the Sages → production of Mercury without contradiction with the secret purpose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS4","text":"Most Pure Magical Spirit in place of the Moon → administration of λευκώσεως → spiritual power with the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:FGS5","text":"Sun + Natural Medium + silence of words → hieroglyphic speech → pure and simple Earth → introduction and impression of figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AF1","text":"Composite planetary Notes → explicability through prior foundations → interpretation of Lunar signs → series of elemental revolutions → Mercury by the fourth Revolution → substitution of the Moon by the Magical Spirit → action of the Sun through the Natural Medium → impression of figures upon Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:AF2","text":"Diversity of planetary names → unity of Lunar Nature → processual gradation → cosmic translation into magical operation → material hieroglyphic effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME1","text":"The planetary sign becomes an object classified simultaneously according to astral origin, elemental composition, and stage of operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME2","text":"The opposition between the characters of the Moon and Sun is reordered as a difference between the principle, medium, and completion of the work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME3","text":"The names Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury are reclassified as stations of the transformation of Lunar Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME4","text":"Earth no longer appears as a passive end, but as a receptive and productive surface for figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ME5","text":"The silence of words becomes a condition of hieroglyphic communication, not a failure of communication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT1","text":"Surface — Signs of the Moon or Sun are composed with the sign of the Elements or of Aries, and figures are impressed upon Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT2","text":"Structural — One Lunar Nature is ordered through revolutions and elemental vicissitudes into the stages of Saturn, Jupiter, and Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Interpretation is transferred from planetary names to the mechanism of production, so that the controversy concerning the fourth Revolution does not dissolve the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Magical things are constituted as a series of transformations among Moon, Spirit, Sun, Elements, and Earth, whose times are defined by revolutions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal line from the composition of signs to the inscription of figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally, because the substitution of the Moon by the Magical Spirit is explained as a change of medium within the same work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT3","text":"Its greatest strength consists in the connection between the composition of signs, elemental succession, and material effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT4","text":"The exact determination of the four revolutions and of the relation among the individual figures is not yet complete in the excerpted text.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT5","text":"The production of Mercury by the fourth Revolution is admitted, but the formal rule of this production is not explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction relies to some extent on arcane terms and on the transition from visible figure to invisible process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_TH_9:MRT7","text":"The schema preserves the true movement of the text: from composite form to processual order, thence to spiritual mediation and terrestrial effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_TH_9@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_TH_9:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"T H E O R. XII."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 13","title":"T H E O R. XII.","context":"Chapter 13","original_title":"T H E O R. Xii.","original_context":"Chapter 13"},"original_title":"T H E O R. Xii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. XIII.","order":14,"parents":["RAW_MHON_T_10"],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_10@R001","sha256":"2278fa50b75841457100e651ac81fb6b010ceab94b688d3f5c112670e3aa4ff7","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est utrum character Martis ex Solis et Arietis hieroglyphicis, elementali magia interveniente, conflatus sit, atque utrum character Veneris ex Solis et pleniore Elementorum explicatione procedat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS2","text":"Quaestio ita constituitur ut planetae non simpliciter denotentur, sed motum Solaris περιφορά et opus Ἀναζωπυρήσεως exprimant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS3","text":"Fundamentum argumenti est progressus quo, perfecta lunari solarique Elementorum magia, Mercurius conspicuus emergit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS4","text":"Probatio fit per identificationem Mercurii cum Philosoporum Mercurio, Microcosmo et Adamo, atque per correspondentiam huius ordinis cum anatomia Monadis Hieroglyphicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis est: compositio hieroglyphica → circulatio Solaris → regeneratio → apparitio Mercurii → operatio animae separatae → ordinatio planetarum → confirmatio anatomiae Monadicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS6","text":"Genus argumentationis est reconstructivum, analogicum et alchemicum, quia signorum ordinem in processum cosmologicum et operativum restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A1","text":"Character hieroglyphicus potest ex aliis characteribus hieroglyphicis componi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A2","text":"Solis character principium constitutivum Martis et Veneris esse potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A3","text":"Elementale Magisterium compositionem hieroglyphicam mediat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A4","text":"Planetae ad Solaris περιφοράν respiciunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A5","text":"Opus Ἀναζωπυρήσεως motum transformationis planetariae constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A6","text":"Lunaris et Solaris Elementorum magia perfecta Mercurium conspicuum producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A7","text":"Mercurius Philosophorum est Microcosmus et Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A8","text":"Anima a corpore arte Pyronomica separata operi Χρυσοκολλίνῳ praefici potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A9","text":"Anima separata Lunam, vel saltem Mercurium, Luciferum et Pyroenta ligare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A10","text":"Sol Philosophorum potest tertius locus esse quo septenarius numerus completur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A11","text":"Anatomia Monadis Hieroglyphicae arcana duorum Theorematum exacte et aperte respondet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A12","text":"Correspondentia inter characteres planetarios et anatomiam Monadis potest significationem arcanorum exhibere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX1","text":"Mars non ut figura isolata, sed ut compositio Solis, Arietis et Magisterii elementalis accipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX2","text":"Venus non ad solam formam Solis reducitur, sed Elementorum pleniorem explicationem requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX3","text":"Mercurius hic non est tantum planeta astronomicus, sed Mercurius Philosophorum, Microcosmus et Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX4","text":"Sol non necessario locum Mercurii obtinet, quamvis quidam Expertissimi eum eodem gradu posuerint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX5","text":"Opus non fit sine mediatione animae, si Sol Philosophorum loco Mercurii substituatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX6","text":"Operatio animae separatae non est facilis neque sine periculo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX7","text":"Interpretatio non clauditur in singulis figuris, sed ad septenarii et totius anatomiae ordinem extenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D1","text":"Si Mars ex Sole et Ariete per Magisterium elementale componitur, character Martis Solaris ordinis effectus fit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A1","CH_MHON_T_10:A2","CH_MHON_T_10:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D2","text":"Si Venus Solis et Elementorum pleniorem explicationem coniungit, eius character gradum ampliorem explicationis magicae designat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A2","CH_MHON_T_10:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D3","text":"Si planetae Solaris περιφοράν respiciunt et opus Ἀναζωπυρήσεως efficiunt, eorum series processus transformationis potius quam catalogum corporum indicat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A4","CH_MHON_T_10:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D4","text":"Perfecta Elementorum magia, lunari solarique coniuncta, condicionem constituit qua Mercurius conspicuus appareat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D5","text":"Cum Mercurius Philosophorum Microcosmus et Adam sit, eius apparitio transitum ad hominis cosmici constitutionem significat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A6","CH_MHON_T_10:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D6","text":"Cum anima separata ad corpora planetaria vincula indissolubilia conferre possit, operatio planetaria ab animae mediatione pendet.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A8","CH_MHON_T_10:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D7","text":"Cum Sol Philosophorum tertium locum implere possit, septenarius planetarum per duplicem ordinationem Mercurii et Solis completur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D8","text":"Correspondentia Monadis cum duobus Theorematibus facit ut anatomia eius figurae non ornamentum, sed index arcanorum sit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A11","CH_MHON_T_10:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD1","text":"Signa planetaria in systema genealogicum convertuntur, in quo unum character ex altero per elementarem et solarem transformationem producitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A1","CH_MHON_T_10:A3","CH_MHON_T_10:A4","CH_MHON_T_10:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD2","text":"Cosmologia, alchimia et anthropologia in eodem processu coalescunt, quia Mercurius simul est planeta, operativum medium, Microcosmus et Adam.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A6","CH_MHON_T_10:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD3","text":"Anima separata fit nexus ontologicus inter corpus, planetas et opus alchemicum.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A8","CH_MHON_T_10:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD4","text":"Septenarius non ex sola numeratione planetarum, sed ex gradibus transformationis et substitutionis constituitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A9","CH_MHON_T_10:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD5","text":"Anatomia Monadis Hieroglyphicae se praebet ut compendium internum ordinis cosmici, non ut descriptionem externam figurae.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A11","CH_MHON_T_10:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit notionem characterum planetariorum ut signorum arbitrariorum et inter se independentium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit separationem rigidam inter astronomiam, alchemiam et anthropologiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit regenerationem ut eventum puramente naturalem sine arte, magia et mediatione animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit Microcosmum ut imaginem passivam mundi; Microcosmus hic est effectus transformationis operativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit univocam identitatem Solis et Mercurii, quia utriusque locus variari potest secundum ordinem interpretativum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX6","text":"Systema excludit operationem omnino tutam et immediatam, cum halitus ignei sulphureique periculum constituant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX1","text":"Impossibilis fit interpretatio quae symbolum a processu formationis separat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX2","text":"Indisponibilis fit cognitio quae ad visum superficiei hieroglyphicae sistit nec eius correspondentias operativas quaerit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX3","text":"Praecluditur mundus in quo anima, elementa et planetae ordines prorsus heterogenei sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX4","text":"Vetatur clausura uniuscuiusque signi in identitate fixa, quia characteres per circulationem, compositionem et substitutionem definiuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX5","text":"Abest distinctio absoluta inter opus cosmologicum et opus humanum: idem processus a planetis ad animam et a figura ad anatomiam transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS1","text":"Character Solar principium → Character Martis et Arietis → Magisterium elementale → compositio Martis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS2","text":"Sol + Elementorum explicatio plenior → character Veneris → gradus ampliatus magicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS3","text":"Circulatio Solaris → Opus Ἀναζωπυρήσεως → perfectio magia lunaris et Solaris → Mercurius conspicuus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS4","text":"Mercurius conspicuus → Mercurius Philosophorum → Microcosmus et Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS5","text":"Anima a corpore separata → praefectura operis Χρυσοκολλίνου → ligatio Lunae, Mercurii, Luciferi et Pyroentae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS6","text":"Locus tertius Solis → completio septenarii → translatio ordinis planetarii in ordinem Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS7","text":"Duo Theoremata → arcana significata → correspondentia cum anatomia Monadis Hieroglyphicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF1","text":"Compositio Martis et Veneris → Solaris ordo planetarum → Ἀναζωπύρησις → Mercurius conspicuus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF2","text":"Mercurius conspicuus → Mercurius Philosophorum → Microcosmus et Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF3","text":"Limitatio substitutionis Solis → necessitas animae separatae → operatio difficilis et periculosa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF4","text":"Anima operans → ligatio corporum planetariorum → completio septenarii per Solis locum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF5","text":"Completio ordinis planetarii → arcana duorum Theorematum → confirmatio anatomiae Monadis Hieroglyphicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME1","text":"Characteres planetarii e signis separatis in seriem geneticam et transformativam reordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME2","text":"Mercurius denuo classificatur ut nodus communis cosmologiae, alchemiae et anthropologiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME3","text":"Anima separata fit obiectum operativum quod corpora planetaria coniungere potest, non tantum principium cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME4","text":"Sol et Mercurius non amplius oppositionem simplicem constituunt, sed loca alternantia intra eundem ordinem septenarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME5","text":"Anatomia Monadis fit tabula compressionis qua ordo planetarius et arcana Theorematum simul leguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME6","text":"Oppositio inter figuram et operationem corruit: figura ipsa processus magici et cosmici vestigium fit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT1","text":"Surface: Characteres Martis, Veneris, Solis, Arietis, Lunae et Mercurii ut figurae hieroglyphicae inter se componuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT2","text":"Structural: Elementale Magisterium, Solaris περιφορά et Ἀναζωπύρησις ordinem compositionis et regenerationis instituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Lectio signorum mutatur in restitutionem ordinis quo planetae, anima et Monadis anatomia eandem machinam explicant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Realitas exhibetur ut processus graduum, substitutionum et transformationum, in quo Microcosmus per perfectam Elementorum magiam emergit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam principalem catenam a compositione characterum ad correspondentiam Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret dum signa planetaria ut gradus unius processus transformativi tractat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT3","text":"Relatio inter duas formas Mercurii, Mercurium conspicuum et Mercurium Philosophorum, non omnino formaliter determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT4","text":"Substitutio Solis pro Mercurio manet conditionalis, quia textus eam quibusdam Expertissimis attribuit et auctoris aetati negat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT5","text":"Status animae separatae inter instrumentum, principium operativum et subiectum ontologicum oscillat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT6","text":"Vis argumenti firmissima est in correspondentia inter ordinem planetarium et anatomiam Monadis; fragilior est in probatione ipsius correspondentiae, quae praecipue ex assertione exactae et apertae responsionis pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum fontis, sed non aufert eius quaestionalem et conditionalem formam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222648289937Z_13f9a198","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM XIII.","source_sha256":"2278fa50b75841457100e651ac81fb6b010ceab94b688d3f5c112670e3aa4ff7","sha256":"8c89075009680c57b9da773ec7a4c7419bcd81bd64b8b2d8712acee60c627108","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:26:48.296275+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS1","text":"The central question is whether the character of Mars was compounded from the hieroglyphics of the Sun and Aries, with elemental magic intervening, and whether the character of Venus proceeds from the Sun and a fuller explication of the Elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS2","text":"The question is thus framed so that the planets are not simply denoted, but express the Solar περιφορά and the work of Ἀναζωπυρήσεως.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS3","text":"The foundation of the argument is the progression by which, lunar and solar magic of the Elements having been perfected, conspicuous Mercury emerges.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS4","text":"The proof is made through the identification of Mercury with the Mercury of the Philosophers, the Microcosm, and Adam, and through the correspondence of this order with the anatomy of the Hieroglyphic Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument is: hieroglyphic composition → Solar circulation → regeneration → appearance of Mercury → operation of the separated soul → ordering of the planets → confirmation of the Monadic anatomy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AS6","text":"The kind of argumentation is reconstructive, analogical, and alchemical, because it restores the order of signs to a cosmological and operative process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A1","text":"A hieroglyphic character can be composed from other hieroglyphic characters.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A2","text":"The character of the Sun can be the constitutive principle of Mars and Venus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A3","text":"The Elemental Magisterium mediates hieroglyphic composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A4","text":"The planets refer to the Solar περιφορά.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A5","text":"The work of Ἀναζωπυρήσεως constitutes the movement of planetary transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A6","text":"Perfected lunar and solar magic of the Elements produces conspicuous Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A7","text":"The Mercury of the Philosophers is the Microcosm and Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A8","text":"A soul separated from the body by the Pyronomic art can be set over the Χρυσοκολλίνῳ work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A9","text":"The separated soul can bind the Moon, or at least Mercury, Lucifer, and Pyroenta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A10","text":"The Sun of the Philosophers can be the third place by which the septenary number is completed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A11","text":"The anatomy of the Hieroglyphic Monad corresponds exactly and openly to the arcana of the two Theorems.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:A12","text":"The correspondence between planetary characters and the anatomy of the Monad can display the meaning of the arcana.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX1","text":"Mars is understood not as an isolated figure, but as a composition of the Sun, Aries, and the elemental Magisterium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX2","text":"Venus is not reduced to the form of the Sun alone, but requires a fuller explication of the Elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX3","text":"Mercury here is not merely an astronomical planet, but the Mercury of the Philosophers, the Microcosm, and Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX4","text":"The Sun does not necessarily occupy the place of Mercury, although certain most expert persons have placed it at the same rank.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX5","text":"The work is not accomplished without the mediation of the soul, if the Sun of the Philosophers is substituted in place of Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX6","text":"The operation of the separated soul is neither easy nor without danger.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:NX7","text":"The interpretation is not enclosed within individual figures, but extends to the order of the septenary and of the whole anatomy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D1","text":"If Mars is composed from the Sun and Aries through the elemental Magisterium, the character of Mars becomes an effect of the Solar order.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A1","CH_MHON_T_10:A2","CH_MHON_T_10:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D2","text":"If Venus joins the Sun and a fuller explication of the Elements, its character designates a more extensive degree of magical explication.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A2","CH_MHON_T_10:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D3","text":"If the planets refer to the Solar περιφορά and effect the work of Ἀναζωπυρήσεως, their series indicates a process of transformation rather than a catalogue of bodies.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A4","CH_MHON_T_10:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D4","text":"Perfected magic of the Elements, conjoined with the lunar and solar, constitutes the condition under which conspicuous Mercury may appear.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D5","text":"Since the Mercury of the Philosophers is the Microcosm and Adam, its appearance signifies a transition to the constitution of the cosmic human being.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A6","CH_MHON_T_10:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D6","text":"Since the separated soul can confer indissoluble bonds upon planetary bodies, planetary operation depends upon the mediation of the soul.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A8","CH_MHON_T_10:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D7","text":"Since the Sun of the Philosophers can fill the third place, the planetary septenary is completed through the double ordering of Mercury and the Sun.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:D8","text":"The correspondence of the Monad with the two Theorems makes the anatomy of its figure not an ornament, but an index of arcana.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A11","CH_MHON_T_10:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD1","text":"Planetary signs are converted into a genealogical system, in which one character is produced from another through elemental and solar transformation.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A1","CH_MHON_T_10:A3","CH_MHON_T_10:A4","CH_MHON_T_10:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD2","text":"Cosmology, alchemy, and anthropology coalesce in the same process, because Mercury is simultaneously a planet, an operative medium, the Microcosm, and Adam.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A6","CH_MHON_T_10:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD3","text":"The separated soul becomes an ontological nexus between body, planets, and the alchemical work.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A8","CH_MHON_T_10:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD4","text":"The septenary is constituted not by the enumeration of planets alone, but by degrees of transformation and substitution.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A9","CH_MHON_T_10:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SD5","text":"The anatomy of the Hieroglyphic Monad presents itself as an internal compendium of the cosmic order, not as an external description of the figure.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_10:A11","CH_MHON_T_10:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the notion of planetary characters as arbitrary and mutually independent signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a rigid separation between astronomy, alchemy, and anthropology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX3","text":"The system excludes regeneration as a purely natural event without art, magic, and the mediation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the Microcosm as a passive image of the world; the Microcosm here is the effect of operative transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a univocal identity of the Sun and Mercury, because the place of each can vary according to the interpretive order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:DNX6","text":"The system excludes an operation wholly safe and immediate, since fiery and sulphurous vapours constitute a danger.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX1","text":"An interpretation that separates the symbol from the process of formation becomes impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX2","text":"Knowledge that halts at the sight of the hieroglyphic surface and does not seek its operative correspondences becomes unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX3","text":"A world is precluded in which soul, elements, and planets are orders wholly heterogeneous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX4","text":"The confinement of each sign within a fixed identity is forbidden, because characters are defined through circulation, composition, and substitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:SNX5","text":"The absolute distinction between cosmic work and human work is absent: the same process passes from planets to soul and from figure to anatomy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS1","text":"Solar character as principle → character of Mars and Aries → elemental Magisterium → composition of Mars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS2","text":"Sun + fuller explication of the Elements → character of Venus → expanded degree of magic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS3","text":"Solar circulation → Work of Ἀναζωπυρήσεως → perfection of lunar and solar magic → conspicuous Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS4","text":"Conspicuous Mercury → Mercury of the Philosophers → Microcosm and Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS5","text":"Soul separated from the body → superintendence of the Χρυσοκολλίνου work → binding of the Moon, Mercury, Lucifer, and Pyroenta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS6","text":"Third place of the Sun → completion of the septenary → transfer of the planetary order into the order of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:FGS7","text":"Two Theorems → signified arcana → correspondence with the anatomy of the Hieroglyphic Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF1","text":"Composition of Mars and Venus → Solar order of the planets → Ἀναζωπύρησις → conspicuous Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF2","text":"Conspicuous Mercury → Mercury of the Philosophers → Microcosm and Adam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF3","text":"Limitation of the substitution of the Sun → necessity of the separated soul → difficult and dangerous operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF4","text":"Operating soul → binding of planetary bodies → completion of the septenary through the place of the Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:AF5","text":"Completion of the planetary order → arcana of the two Theorems → confirmation of the anatomy of the Hieroglyphic Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME1","text":"Planetary characters are reordered from separate signs into a genetic and transformative series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME2","text":"Mercury is reclassified as a common node of cosmology, alchemy, and anthropology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME3","text":"The separated soul becomes an operative object that can join planetary bodies, not merely a principle of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME4","text":"The Sun and Mercury no longer constitute a simple opposition, but alternating places within the same septenary order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME5","text":"The anatomy of the Monad becomes a compression map by which the planetary order and the arcana of the Theorems are read together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ME6","text":"The opposition between figure and operation collapses: the figure itself becomes a trace of the magical and cosmic process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT1","text":"Surface: The characters of Mars, Venus, the Sun, Aries, the Moon, and Mercury are composed together as hieroglyphic figures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT2","text":"Structural: The Elemental Magisterium, Solar περιφορά, and Ἀναζωπύρησις establish the order of composition and regeneration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The reading of signs is transformed into a restoration of the order by which the planets, the soul, and the anatomy of the Monad explicate the same machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Reality is presented as a process of degrees, substitutions, and transformations, in which the Microcosm emerges through perfected magic of the Elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the principal chain from the composition of characters to the correspondence of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally while it treats planetary signs as stages of a single transformative process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT3","text":"The relation between the two forms of Mercury, conspicuous Mercury and the Mercury of the Philosophers, is not wholly formally determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT4","text":"The substitution of the Sun for Mercury remains conditional, because the text attributes it to certain most expert persons and denies it to the author's age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT5","text":"The status of the separated soul oscillates between instrument, operative principle, and ontological subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT6","text":"The force of the argument is strongest in the correspondence between the planetary order and the anatomy of the Monad; it is weaker in the proof of the correspondence itself, which depends chiefly on the assertion of an exact and open correspondence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_10:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the source, but does not remove its interrogative and conditional form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_10@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_T_10:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 14","title":"Theor. XIII.","context":"Chapter 14","original_title":"Theor. Xiii.","original_context":"Chapter 14"},"original_title":"Theor. Xiii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11","layer":"CH","title":"Theorem XIII.","order":15,"parents":["RAW_MHON_T_11"],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_11@R001","sha256":"d2fcacaa840edc1c776593ea7868e41795b80b09429e6de0ba9d9d8c87ca5e83","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est unde totum Magisterium pendeat et quomodo eius influxus constituatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS2","text":"Textus quaestionem in structuram triadicam Solis, Lunae et Terrae Lemniae constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS3","text":"Assertio principalis est Magisterium ex Sole et Luna pendere, Terra Lemnia autem eius nutrimentum praebere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS4","text":"Auctoritatem huius structurae per testimonium Hermetis et per operationem radiorum Solarium ac Lunarium firmat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS5","text":"Motus argumentationis est: dependentia → genealogia symbolica → receptaculum terrestre → influxus radialis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A1","text":"Totum hoc Magisterium ex Sole et Luna pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A2","text":"Sol principium paternum Magisterii est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A3","text":"Luna principium maternum Magisterii est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A4","text":"Terra Lemnia locum nutritionis Magisterii praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A5","text":"Radii Lunares et Solares circa Terram Lemniam singularem Influentiam exercent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A6","text":"Hermes hanc relationem genealogicam auctoritate sua confirmat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A7","text":"Magisterium non ex uno tantum principio, sed ex coniunctione principiorum caelestium et receptaculi terrestris constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX1","text":"Magisterium non est principium autonomum a Sole et Luna separatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX2","text":"Terra Lemnia non est pater aut mater Magisterii, sed eius locus nutritionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX3","text":"Sol et Luna non ad meram praesentiam staticam reducuntur, quia radii eorum Influentiam exercent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX4","text":"Magisterium non definitur per originem caelestem sine mediatione terrestri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX5","text":"Testimonium de origine non ab auctoritate Hermetis seiungitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D1","text":"Magisterium formatur per relationem inter generationem caelestem et nutritionem terrestrem.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A1","CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D2","text":"Sol et Luna efficiunt principia activa, Terra Lemnia autem efficit condicionem receptivam et nutritivam.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D3","text":"Influentialis vis Magisterii transit per radios, non per causalitatem abstractam a corporibus caelestibus.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A1","CH_MHON_T_11:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D4","text":"Triadica dispositio patris, matris et terrae ordinem generationis, recept receptionis et nutritionis constituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D5","text":"Confirmatio Hermetica relationem caelestem-terrestrem in ordinem doctrinaliter legitimatum transfert.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A5","CH_MHON_T_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD1","text":"Magisterium est effectus circulationis inter fontes caelestes et materiam terrestrem, non res uno loco clausa.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A1","CH_MHON_T_11:A4","CH_MHON_T_11:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD2","text":"Distinctio inter originem et nutritionem duas causalitatis formas separat: caelestis constituit, terrestris sustentat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD3","text":"Radii efficiunt medium quo genealogia symbolica Solis et Lunae in operationem physicam vel cosmologicam convertitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD4","text":"Auctoritas Hermetica et relatio radialis simul faciunt ut Magisterium tamquam ordo traditus et influxus operativus intelligatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A5","CH_MHON_T_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX1","text":"Systema tacite excludit notionem Magisterii quod sine influxu caelesti aut sine fundamento materiali subsisteret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit causalitatem univocam, sive caelestem tantum sive terrestrem tantum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX3","text":"Paternitas et maternitas hic non designant personas humanas, sed functiones distinctas intra generationem cosmologicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX4","text":"Terra Lemnia non est materia passiva prorsus separata ab influxu, sed condicio sine qua nutritio Magisterii non explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX5","text":"Auctoritas antiqua sola non sufficeret ad systema constituendum, nisi influxus radialis ei mechanismum adderet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX1","text":"Textus circumit conceptionem Magisterii ut artificii hominis autonomi, quia eius originem extra humanam actionem collocat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX2","text":"Praecluditur possibilitas ut caelum et terra sint tantum imagines metaphoricae sine efficacia influxiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX3","text":"Praecluditur separatio absoluta inter symbolicam genealogiam et operationem naturalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX4","text":"Systema indisponibilem facit originem unicam et simplicem: Magisterium tantum ex Soli, tantum ex Luna, aut tantum ex Terra derivari non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS1","text":"Sol + Luna → principia paternum et maternum → dependentia constitutiva Magisterii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS2","text":"Terra Lemnia → receptio et nutritio → continuatio terrestris eius quod caelitus constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS3","text":"Radii Lunares + radii Solares → influxus singularis circa Terram Lemniam → operatio coniuncta Magisterii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS4","text":"Testimonium Hermeticum + ordo influxus → legitimatio genealogica et cosmologica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS5","text":"Coniunctio caelestis et terrestris → Magisterium ut processus dependens, nutritus et influxus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AF1","text":"Dependentia Magisterii → constitutio Solis et Lunae ut parentum → Terra Lemnia ut nutrimentum → radii ut medium influxus → unitas operativa trium terminorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME1","text":"Origo Magisterii reclassificatur a fonte singulari ad relationem inter duo principia caelestia et unum locum terrestrem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME2","text":"Terra Lemnia fit non finis materialis, sed nodus receptivus ubi influxus Solis et Lunae operantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME3","text":"Paternitas, maternitas et nutritio ordinantur ut functiones causales distinctae, non ut vocabula mere poetica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME4","text":"Radii reordinantur ut medium commune quo symbolum Hermeticum in mechanismum influxus transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME5","text":"Oppositio caelum/terra dissolvitur in schema circulationis: caelum influit, terra recipit et nutrit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT1","text":"Surface — Magisterium a Sole, Luna et Terra Lemnia dependere asseritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT2","text":"Structural — Systema distribuit functiones inter principia generativa caelestia, receptaculum terrestre et radios mediantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Auctoritas Hermetica et influxus radialis coniunguntur ut genealogia symbolica vim doctrinalem et operativam obtineat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Realitas Magisterii est processus generationis, receptionis et nutritionis sub influxu corporum caelestium; non est substantia immobilis neque origo simpliciter localis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam machinam minimam: duo principia caelestia, unum receptaculum terrestre, influxus radialis et confirmatio Hermetica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT2","text":"Textus interne cohaeret quoad ordinem patris, matris, nutritionis et influxus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT3","text":"Firmitas maxima est in structura triadica et in oppositione inter originem caelestem ac nutritionem terrestrem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT4","text":"Determinatio manet incompleta circa sensum exactum Magisterii, Terrae Lemniae et singularis Influentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis est transitus a testimonio Hermetico ad efficaciam radialem: auctoritas confirmat relationem, sed mechanismum eius non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT6","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus, quamquam causalitas radiorum et status ontologicus Terrae Lemniae in fonte amplius demonstrari non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222704651299Z_c5c95870","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM XIII.","source_sha256":"d2fcacaa840edc1c776593ea7868e41795b80b09429e6de0ba9d9d8c87ca5e83","sha256":"e219042920abb82a4969bc05b5a367be9445b747f2dd991afe0ade1bdce86a3f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:27:04.653778+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS1","text":"The central question is on what the whole Magisterium depends and how its influence is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS2","text":"The text frames the question within a triadic structure of the Sun, Moon, and Lemnian Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS3","text":"The principal assertion is that the Magisterium depends on the Sun and Moon, while Lemnian Earth provides its nourishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS4","text":"It establishes the authority of this structure through the testimony of Hermes and through the operation of Solar and Lunar rays.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument is: dependence → symbolic genealogy → terrestrial receptacle → radial influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A1","text":"This whole Magisterium depends on the Sun and Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A2","text":"The Sun is the paternal principle of the Magisterium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A3","text":"The Moon is the maternal principle of the Magisterium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A4","text":"Lemnian Earth provides the place of nourishment for the Magisterium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A5","text":"Lunar and Solar rays exert a singular Influence around Lemnian Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A6","text":"Hermes confirms this genealogical relation by his authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:A7","text":"The Magisterium is constituted not from one principle alone, but from the conjunction of celestial principles and a terrestrial receptacle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX1","text":"The Magisterium is not an autonomous principle separated from the Sun and Moon.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX2","text":"Lemnian Earth is not the father or mother of the Magisterium, but the place of its nourishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX3","text":"The Sun and Moon are not reduced to mere static presence, because their rays exert Influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX4","text":"The Magisterium is not defined by celestial origin without terrestrial mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:NX5","text":"Testimony concerning origin is not separated from the authority of Hermes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D1","text":"The Magisterium is formed through the relation between celestial generation and terrestrial nourishment.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A1","CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D2","text":"The Sun and Moon constitute active principles, whereas Lemnian Earth constitutes a receptive and nutritive condition.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D3","text":"The influential force of the Magisterium passes through rays, not through causality abstracted from the celestial bodies.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A1","CH_MHON_T_11:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D4","text":"The triadic arrangement of father, mother, and earth establishes an order of generation, reception, and nourishment.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:D5","text":"Hermetic confirmation transfers the celestial-terrestrial relation into a doctrinally legitimized order.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A5","CH_MHON_T_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD1","text":"The Magisterium is the effect of a circulation between celestial sources and terrestrial matter, not a thing enclosed in one place.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A1","CH_MHON_T_11:A4","CH_MHON_T_11:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD2","text":"The distinction between origin and nourishment separates two forms of causality: the celestial constitutes, the terrestrial sustains.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD3","text":"Rays constitute the medium through which the symbolic genealogy of the Sun and Moon is converted into physical or cosmological operation.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A2","CH_MHON_T_11:A3","CH_MHON_T_11:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SD4","text":"Hermetic authority and radial relation together cause the Magisterium to be understood as both a transmitted order and an operative influence.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_11:A5","CH_MHON_T_11:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX1","text":"The system tacitly excludes the notion of a Magisterium that could subsist without celestial influence or without a material foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX2","text":"The system excludes univocal causality, whether solely celestial or solely terrestrial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX3","text":"Paternity and maternity here designate not human persons, but distinct functions within cosmological generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX4","text":"Lemnian Earth is not passive matter wholly separated from influence, but a condition without which the nourishment of the Magisterium cannot be explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:DNX5","text":"Ancient authority alone would not suffice to constitute the system unless radial influence added a mechanism to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX1","text":"The text avoids the conception of the Magisterium as the contrivance of an autonomous human being, because it locates its origin outside human action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX2","text":"The possibility that heaven and earth are merely metaphorical images without influential efficacy is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX3","text":"The absolute separation between symbolic genealogy and natural operation is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:SNX4","text":"The system renders unavailable a single and simple origin: the Magisterium cannot be derived solely from the Sun, solely from the Moon, or solely from the Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS1","text":"Sun + Moon → paternal and maternal principles → constitutive dependence of the Magisterium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS2","text":"Lemnian Earth → reception and nourishment → terrestrial continuation of that which is constituted celestially.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS3","text":"Lunar rays + Solar rays → singular influence around Lemnian Earth → conjoint operation of the Magisterium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS4","text":"Hermetic testimony + order of influence → genealogical and cosmological legitimation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:FGS5","text":"Celestial and terrestrial conjunction → the Magisterium as a dependent, nourished, and influential process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:AF1","text":"Dependence of the Magisterium → constitution of the Sun and Moon as parents → Lemnian Earth as nourishment → rays as the medium of influence → operative unity of the three terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME1","text":"The origin of the Magisterium is reclassified from a singular source to a relation between two celestial principles and one terrestrial place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME2","text":"Lemnian Earth becomes not a material end, but a receptive node where the influences of the Sun and Moon operate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME3","text":"Paternity, maternity, and nourishment are ordered as distinct causal functions, not as merely poetic terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME4","text":"Rays are reordered as the common medium through which the Hermetic symbol passes into a mechanism of influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ME5","text":"The heaven/earth opposition is dissolved into a schema of circulation: heaven influences; earth receives and nourishes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT1","text":"Surface — The Magisterium is asserted to depend on the Sun, Moon, and Lemnian Earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT2","text":"Structural — The system distributes functions among celestial generative principles, a terrestrial receptacle, and mediating rays.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Hermetic authority and radial influence are conjoined so that symbolic genealogy acquires doctrinal and operative force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The reality of the Magisterium is a process of generation, reception, and nourishment under the influence of celestial bodies; it is neither an immobile substance nor an origin simply local.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the minimal mechanism: two celestial principles, one terrestrial receptacle, radial influence, and Hermetic confirmation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT2","text":"The text is internally coherent with respect to the order of father, mother, nourishment, and influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT3","text":"The greatest firmness lies in the triadic structure and in the opposition between celestial origin and terrestrial nourishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT4","text":"Determination remains incomplete concerning the exact sense of the Magisterium, Lemnian Earth, and singular Influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT5","text":"The fragile juncture is the transition from Hermetic testimony to radial efficacy: authority confirms the relation, but does not explain its mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_11:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text, although the causality of the rays and the ontological status of Lemnian Earth can no longer be further demonstrated in the source.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_11@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_T_11:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 15","title":"Theorem XIII.","context":"Chapter 15","original_title":"Theorema Xiii.","original_context":"Chapter 15"},"original_title":"Theorema Xiii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. XV.","order":16,"parents":["RAW_MHON_T_12"],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_12@R001","sha256":"f18bc228e1f84fa39ed402259cf97ed25868d984b5c28587af73014e7b73cb71","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS1","text":"Labores Solis Lunaeque circa Terram ad considerationem philosophicam proponuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS2","text":"Quaestio constituitur ex modo quo Sol in Ariete versans Lunae in proximo signo, Tauro, novam lucis dignitatem tribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS3","text":"Exaltatio Lunae et robur Martis per domos astrologicas et relationes inter signa explicantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS4","text":"Hieroglyphica figura Tauro adiuncta has relationes non modo significat, sed demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS5","text":"Monas ex astrologica dispositione ad anatomiam cabalisticam et ad scientiam elementorum transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS6","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructiva et demonstrativa: dispositio cosmica → figura hieroglyphica → relatio grammatica et geometrica → explicatio cabalistica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A1","text":"Sol in Ariete versans Lunam in Tauro proximo signo constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A2","text":"Proximitas signi ad Luminare eius dignitatem augere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A3","text":"Luna in Tauro exaltationem habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A4","text":"Taurus domus Veneris est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A5","text":"Venus in Tauro castum, prolificum et coniugalem amorem significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A6","text":"Sol post eclipses quasdam robur Martis accipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A7","text":"Aries domus Martis est et locus eius exaltationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A8","text":"Monas hieroglyphica relationes Solis, Lunae, Martis, Tauri, Arietis et elementi in una figura colligere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A9","text":"Figura hieroglyphica Tauri diphthongum Graecorum ε exacte repraesentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A10","text":"Metathesis localis figurae Tauri duplicem formam Alphae per circulum et semicirculum manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A11","text":"Exaltationes Lunae et Solis mediantibus scientia elementorum cabalisticam explicationem accipiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A12","text":"Intelligentia mysteriorum huius ordinis ad eos restringitur qui mysteriorum antistites absoluti evaserunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX1","text":"Mysterium astrologicum non omnibus spectatoribus per se intelligibile est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX2","text":"Exaltatio non ad vires innatas Luminarium reducitur, sed ex situ et proximitate signorum determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX3","text":"Domus astrologica non est mera locatio, sed relatio qualitativa inter planetam et virtutem eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX4","text":"Figura hieroglyphica non est ornamentum separatum ab doctrina, sed pars ipsius demonstrationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX5","text":"Scientia elementorum a cabalistica anatomia non excluditur, sed eius medium constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX6","text":"Significatio Tauri non ad nomen mythicum solum restringitur, quia figura etiam operationes litterarias et geometricas continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D1","text":"Lunae exaltatio ex coniunctione proximitatis Solis et loci Tauri constituitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A1","CH_MHON_T_12:A2","CH_MHON_T_12:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D2","text":"Taurus simul locum exaltationis Lunae et domum Veneris constituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A3","CH_MHON_T_12:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D3","text":"Venus in Tauro coniunctionem inter proximitatem, fecunditatem et amorem coniugalem instituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A4","CH_MHON_T_12:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D4","text":"Solis relatio ad Martem per transitum ab Ariete ad eiusdem domus exaltationem figuratur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A6","CH_MHON_T_12:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D5","text":"Figura Tauri relationem Lunae ad Solis radium et elementorum ordinem simul exhibet.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A1","CH_MHON_T_12:A3","CH_MHON_T_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D6","text":"Eadem figura ex forma grafica ad ordinem linguae Graecae transit, quia Taurus ε repraesentat et per metathesin Alphae formas ostendit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A9","CH_MHON_T_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D7","text":"Astrologica dispositio in anatomiam cabalisticam convertitur cum exaltationes per scientiam elementorum explicantur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A8","CH_MHON_T_12:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD1","text":"Monas ordines astrologicum, mythicum, linguisticum, geometricum et elementalem tamquam manifestationes unius structurae connectit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:D2","CH_MHON_T_12:D5","CH_MHON_T_12:D6","CH_MHON_T_12:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD2","text":"Exaltatio fit operatio transmutativa qua vis astralis per locum, figuram et elementum in dignitatem intelligibilem convertitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A2","CH_MHON_T_12:A8","CH_MHON_T_12:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD3","text":"Figura hieroglyphica efficit ut relatio cosmica non solum significetur, sed in forma visuali, grammatica et geometrica iterari possit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:D5","CH_MHON_T_12:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD4","text":"Cabalistica explicatio caelestem ordinem ad scientiam mediatam reducit, ita ut signorum sensus per elementa structuram corporalem et operativam accipiat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:D7","CH_MHON_T_12:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD5","text":"Auctoritas mysterii ex communi traditione ad regimen interpretum initiatorum transfertur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A12","CH_MHON_T_12:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX1","text":"Systema falsum haberetur si caelestia signa tantum res physicae sine ordine symbolico essent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX2","text":"Systema non admittit separationem inter astrologiam, linguam, geometriam et cabalam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX3","text":"Exaltatio ut mera superioritas quantitativa tacite reicitur; ipsa relatio ordinata dignitatem producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX4","text":"Figura non potest esse arbitraria imitatio, quia eius vis demonstrationis ab exacta repraesentatione ε et Alphae pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX5","text":"Scientia non distribuitur aequaliter, cum intellectus mysteriorum ad initiatos reservetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX6","text":"Elementum non est terminus infimus vel materialis tantum, sed condicio conversionis inter ordines symbolicos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX1","text":"Argumentatio excludit mundum in quo signa nihil aliud quam nomina vel picturae decorativae sint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX2","text":"Excluditur possibilitas unius disciplinae autonomae quae totum sensum Monadis continere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX3","text":"Excluditur immediata accessibilitas mysterii, quia veritas eius sine initiatione indisponibilis manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX4","text":"Excluditur oppositio simplex inter naturalem causationem et significationem symbolicam; utrumque in scientia elementorum coniungitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX5","text":"Excluditur indifferentia loci, quia ordo signorum et domorum sine mutatione localis vim suam amitteret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS1","text":"Sol in Ariete → Luna in Tauro proximo loco → nova Lunae lucis dignitas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS2","text":"Lunae exaltatio in Tauro → domus Veneris → amor castus, prolificus et coniugalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS3","text":"Solis eclipses → acquisitio roboris Martis → Aries ut domus et locus exaltationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS4","text":"Relatio astralis → figura Tauri et Arietis → visibilis demonstratio Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS5","text":"Forma Tauri → ε Graecum → metathesis localis → duplex ostensio Alphae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS6","text":"Exaltationes Solis et Lunae → scientia elementorum → anatomia cabalistica Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS7","text":"Structura cosmica → translatio symbolica → demonstratio hieroglyphica → interpretatio cabalistica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AF1","text":"Labores Solis Lunaeque → quaestio de dignitate luminarium → proximitas signorum et domus → exaltatio Lunae et Solis → figura hieroglyphica ut demonstratio → translatio grammatica et geometrica → anatomia cabalistica per elementa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME1","text":"Caeleste spatium fit tabula relationum in qua proximitas, domus et exaltatio inter se classificatae sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME2","text":"Figura Taurus non amplius ad zodiacum tantum pertinet, sed simul ad litteram, numerum implicite constitutum, geometriam et doctrinam cabalisticam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter mythum et demonstrationem corruit, quia mythica nomina per formas et relationes verificabiles ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter caeleste et terrestre reclassificatur per scientiam elementorum, quae utrumque ordinem mediat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME5","text":"Interpretatio fit operatio structurale translatans: signum astrale → figura → littera → forma geometrica → essentia cabalistica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT1","text":"Surface: Sol, Luna, Mars, Taurus et Aries per exaltationes, domos et proximitates ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT2","text":"Structural: Dignitas luminarium producitur per situm relatum, et figura hieroglyphica has relationes componit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Monas disciplinarum diversas non iuxta materiam separat, sed eas ut gradus unius interpretationis disponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Realitas caelestis ut ordo dynamice transmutans concipitur, in quo transitio, vicinitas et mediatio virtutes efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam catenam a dispositione Solis et Lunae ad exaltationes astrologicas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de figura, ε, Alpha et elementis sufficiunt ad transitum ab astrologia ad hieroglyphicam et cabalam restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT3","text":"Structura interne cohaeret dum exaltatio intellegitur tamquam effectus relationis, non tamquam proprietas isolata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT4","text":"Firmissima est connexio inter situm astralem, figuram Tauri et duplicationem ordinum symbolici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT5","text":"Minus determinatum manet quomodo scientia elementorum singulas Lunae et Solis exaltationes causaliter explicet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT6","text":"Demonstratio figurae praesupponit interpretationes astrologicas et cabalisticas quas non omnia gradus formaliter probant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: ex relatis caelestibus ad ordinem hieroglyphicum, deinde ad articulationem cabalisticam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222726349139Z_f1764032","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEORY XV.","source_sha256":"f18bc228e1f84fa39ed402259cf97ed25868d984b5c28587af73014e7b73cb71","sha256":"73b8ed22ff1e61a0daa0f544816676f41dc821455e76b31c8d8fc515ec1ee583","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:27:26.351921+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS1","text":"The labors of the Sun and Moon around the Earth are proposed for philosophical consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS2","text":"The question is constituted by the manner in which the Sun, situated in Aries, confers upon the Moon in the neighboring sign, Taurus, a new dignity of light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS3","text":"The exaltation of the Moon and the strength of Mars are explained through astrological houses and relations among the signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS4","text":"The hieroglyphic figure joined to Taurus not only signifies these relations, but demonstrates them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS5","text":"The Monad passes from astrological disposition to cabalistic anatomy and to the science of the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AS6","text":"The argumentation is reconstructive and demonstrative: cosmic disposition → hieroglyphic figure → grammatical and geometrical relation → cabalistic explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A1","text":"The Sun, situated in Aries, places the Moon in Taurus, the neighboring sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A2","text":"The proximity of a sign to its Luminary can increase its dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A3","text":"The Moon has its exaltation in Taurus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A4","text":"Taurus is the house of Venus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A5","text":"Venus in Taurus signifies chaste, prolific, and conjugal love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A6","text":"After certain eclipses, the Sun receives the strength of Mars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A7","text":"Aries is the house of Mars and the place of its exaltation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A8","text":"The hieroglyphic Monad can gather the relations of the Sun, Moon, Mars, Taurus, Aries, and the element into one figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A9","text":"The hieroglyphic figure of Taurus exactly represents the Greek diphthong ε.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A10","text":"The local metathesis of the figure of Taurus manifests the double form of Alpha through the circle and semicircle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A11","text":"The exaltations of the Moon and Sun receive a cabalistic explanation by means of the science of the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:A12","text":"Understanding of the mysteries of this order is restricted to those who have become accomplished initiates of the mysteries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX1","text":"The astrological mystery is not intelligible in itself to all spectators.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX2","text":"Exaltation is not reduced to the innate powers of the Luminaries, but is determined by the position and proximity of the signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX3","text":"An astrological house is not a mere location, but a qualitative relation between a planet and its power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX4","text":"The hieroglyphic figure is not an ornament separate from doctrine, but a part of the demonstration itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX5","text":"The science of the elements is not excluded from cabalistic anatomy, but constitutes its medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:NX6","text":"The significance of Taurus is not restricted to the mythical name alone, because the figure also contains literal and geometrical operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D1","text":"The exaltation of the Moon is constituted from the conjunction of the Sun's proximity and the place of Taurus.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A1","CH_MHON_T_12:A2","CH_MHON_T_12:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D2","text":"Taurus simultaneously constitutes the place of the Moon's exaltation and the house of Venus.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A3","CH_MHON_T_12:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D3","text":"Venus in Taurus establishes a conjunction between proximity, fertility, and conjugal love.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A4","CH_MHON_T_12:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D4","text":"The relation of the Sun to Mars is figured through the passage from Aries to the exaltation of the same house.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A6","CH_MHON_T_12:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D5","text":"The figure of Taurus simultaneously displays the relation of the Moon to the Sun's ray and the order of the elements.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A1","CH_MHON_T_12:A3","CH_MHON_T_12:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D6","text":"The same figure passes from graphic form to the order of the Greek language, because Taurus represents ε and, through metathesis, shows the forms of Alpha.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A9","CH_MHON_T_12:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:D7","text":"The astrological disposition is converted into cabalistic anatomy when the exaltations are explained through the science of the elements.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A8","CH_MHON_T_12:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD1","text":"The Monad connects the astrological, mythical, linguistic, geometrical, and elemental orders as manifestations of one structure.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:D2","CH_MHON_T_12:D5","CH_MHON_T_12:D6","CH_MHON_T_12:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD2","text":"Exaltation becomes a transmutative operation by which astral force is converted through place, figure, and element into intelligible dignity.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A2","CH_MHON_T_12:A8","CH_MHON_T_12:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD3","text":"The hieroglyphic figure makes it possible for the cosmic relation not only to be signified, but also to be repeated in visual, grammatical, and geometrical form.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:D5","CH_MHON_T_12:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD4","text":"The cabalistic explanation reduces the celestial order to mediated knowledge, so that the sense of the signs receives a corporeal and operative structure through the elements.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:D7","CH_MHON_T_12:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SD5","text":"The authority of mystery is transferred from common tradition to the governance of initiated interpreters.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_12:A12","CH_MHON_T_12:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX1","text":"The system would be considered false if celestial signs were only physical things without symbolic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX2","text":"The system does not admit a separation between astrology, language, geometry, and cabala.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX3","text":"Exaltation as mere quantitative superiority is tacitly rejected; the ordered relation itself produces dignity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX4","text":"The figure cannot be an arbitrary imitation, because its demonstrative force depends upon the exact representation of ε and Alpha.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX5","text":"Knowledge is not distributed equally, since understanding of the mysteries is reserved for the initiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:DNX6","text":"The element is not the lowest or merely material term, but the condition of conversion between symbolic orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX1","text":"The argumentation excludes a world in which signs are nothing other than names or decorative pictures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a single autonomous discipline capable of containing the whole meaning of the Monad is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX3","text":"The immediate accessibility of the mystery is excluded, because its truth remains unavailable without initiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX4","text":"The simple opposition between natural causation and symbolic signification is excluded; both are joined in the science of the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:SNX5","text":"Indifference of place is excluded, because the order of signs and houses would lose its force without local change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS1","text":"Sun in Aries → Moon in Taurus in the neighboring place → new dignity of the Moon's light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS2","text":"Exaltation of the Moon in Taurus → house of Venus → chaste, prolific, and conjugal love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS3","text":"Eclipses of the Sun → acquisition of the strength of Mars → Aries as house and place of exaltation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS4","text":"Astral relation → figure of Taurus and Aries → visible demonstration of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS5","text":"Form of Taurus → Greek ε → local metathesis → double showing of Alpha.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS6","text":"Exaltations of the Sun and Moon → science of the elements → cabalistic anatomy of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:FGS7","text":"Cosmic structure → symbolic translation → hieroglyphic demonstration → cabalistic interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:AF1","text":"Labors of the Sun and Moon → question concerning the dignity of the luminaries → proximity of signs and houses → exaltation of the Moon and Sun → hieroglyphic figure as demonstration → grammatical and geometrical translation → cabalistic anatomy through the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME1","text":"Celestial space becomes a map of relations in which proximity, house, and exaltation are classified in relation to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME2","text":"The figure Taurus no longer pertains only to the zodiac, but simultaneously to the letter, the implicitly constituted number, geometry, and cabalistic doctrine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME3","text":"The opposition between myth and demonstration collapses, because mythical names are ordered through verifiable forms and relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME4","text":"The opposition between celestial and terrestrial is reclassified through the science of the elements, which mediates both orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ME5","text":"Interpretation becomes a structurally translating operation: astral sign → figure → letter → geometrical form → cabalistic essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT1","text":"Surface: Sun, Moon, Mars, Taurus, and Aries are ordered through exaltations, houses, and proximities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT2","text":"Structural: The dignity of the luminaries is produced through relational position, and the hieroglyphic figure composes these relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: The Monad does not separate diverse disciplines according to their subject matter, but arranges them as stages of one interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Celestial reality is conceived as a dynamically transmuting order, in which transition, neighborhood, and mediation produce powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the chain from the disposition of the Sun and Moon to astrological exaltations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning the figure, ε, Alpha, and the elements suffice to restore the transition from astrology to hieroglyphics and cabala.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT3","text":"The structure coheres internally so long as exaltation is understood as an effect of relation, not as an isolated property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT4","text":"Strongest is the connection between astral position, the figure of Taurus, and the duplication of symbolic orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT5","text":"It remains less determined how the science of the elements causally explains the individual exaltations of the Moon and Sun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT6","text":"The demonstration of the figure presupposes astrological and cabalistic interpretations that not all stages formally prove.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_12:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: from celestial relations to hieroglyphic order, then to cabalistic articulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_12@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_T_12:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 16","title":"Theor. XV.","context":"Chapter 16","original_title":"Theor. Xv.","original_context":"Chapter 16"},"original_title":"Theor. Xv.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. XVI.","order":17,"parents":["RAW_MHON_T_13"],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_13@R001","sha256":"e10a874fc81c4d57da48b227f28e0943aab945753b53ee7d97762e4bc19020a9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS1","text":"Quaestio est quomodo CRVX ex aequalibus rectis, per sectionem et situm, vim numericam occultam exhibeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS2","text":"CRVX non ut figura geometrica tantum, sed ut nota hieroglyphica secundum normam iustitiae naturae consideratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS3","text":"Fundamentum argumenti est transitus a partibus crucis ad litteras, a litteris ad numeros, et a numeris ad multiplicationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS4","text":"Prima divisio figuram ad QVINARIVM et VIGINTI QVINQVE refert; altera situs figurae ad QVINQVAGINTA.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS5","text":"Duarum partium vis ad CENTENARIVM, per legem quadratorum ad BIS MILLE QVINGENTA, et per proportionem denariam ad VNVм, DECEM, CENTVM progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS6","text":"Genus argumentationis est metaphysicum, arithmologicum et reconstructivum: figura, littera et numerus in unam machinam generatricem rediguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A1","text":"CRVX ex duabus rectis aequalibus conficitur, sed hae rectae non necessario se mutuo in longitudines aequales dissecant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A2","text":"In distributione mystica crucis admittuntur simul partes aequales et inaequales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A3","text":"Aequalitas magnitudinis in binis partibus virtutem CRVCIS ÆQVILATERÆ occultam continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A4","text":"Natura aequalem linearum decussationem ex aequalibus rectis tamquam iustitiae normam requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A5","text":"Recta per commune sectionis punctum et angulos oppositos transiens partes crucis ex utraque parte similes et aequales reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A6","text":"Figurae sic productae cum littera Latina quinta vocalium et ad QVINARIVM significandum adhibita congruunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A7","text":"Geminatio et conversio situs figurae eam in signum numerale transformant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A8","text":"Prima figura geminata QVINARIVM repraesentat et per multiplicationem quadratam VIGINTI QVINQVE producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A9","text":"Similis divisio in situ crucis monadicae alteram litteram geminatam producit, quae ad QVINQVAGINTA significandum adhibetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A10","text":"Altera figura essentialiter ex virtute denaria crucis et ex virtute quinaria eius sumitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A11","text":"Duae partes integrae crucis, secundum vim earum numeratam, CENTENARIVM efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A12","text":"Lex quadratorum permittit mutuam multiplicationem, quae BIS MILLE QVINGENTA producit et, comparatione ad priorem numerum circularem, CENTENARIVM denuo restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A13","text":"CRVX, quamvis unus character sit et VNVМ repraesentet, secundum potentiam denariam CENTVRIO agnosci potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX1","text":"Aequalitas duarum rectarum non definit aequalitatem omnium longitudinum quas divisio producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX2","text":"Distributio crucis non restringitur ad partes omnes aequales neque ad partes omnes inaequales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX3","text":"CRVX non ad figuram geometricam nudam reducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX4","text":"Sensus numeralis non ex uno situ fixo crucis constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX5","text":"Unitas characteris non excludit multiplicationem, expansionem aut centenariam eius potentiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX6","text":"Progressio numerica non est simplex enumeratio linearis, sed proportionem denariam et operationes quadratas includit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D1","text":"Aequalitas linearum, decussatio aequalis et divisio per commune punctum faciunt ut symmetria geometrica vim symbolicam recipiat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A3","CH_MHON_T_13:A4","CH_MHON_T_13:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D2","text":"Partes similes crucis in figuram litteralem convertuntur, ita ut figura idem tempus signum geometricum et signum QVINARII sit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A5","CH_MHON_T_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D3","text":"Geminatio et conversio primae figurae efficiunt ut QVINARIVM per multiplicationem quadratam in VIGINTI QVINQVE transeat.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A7","CH_MHON_T_13:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D4","text":"Altera divisio, quia eundem modum bipartitionis in alio situ repetit, alteram litteram numeralem et significationem QVINQVAGINTA constituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A7","CH_MHON_T_13:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D5","text":"Signum QVINQVAGINTA denariam potestatem in quinaria virtute complectitur, quia ex denario crucis et ex quinario eius essentialiter sumitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A9","CH_MHON_T_13:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D6","text":"Numeratio duarum partium integralium crucis ad CENTENARIVM pervenit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D7","text":"Mutua partium quadratura BIS MILLE QVINGENTA producit, sed relatio ad priorem numerum circularem CENTENARIVM iterum restituit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D8","text":"Ex potentia denaria crucis ordo VNVМ → DECEM → CENTVM generatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A12","CH_MHON_T_13:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD1","text":"Figura geometrica in operationem numericam vertitur: divisio, situs et conversio non describunt tantum, sed numeros generant.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D1","CH_MHON_T_13:D3","CH_MHON_T_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD2","text":"Identitas signi non a forma sola, sed a relatione inter figuram, situm, litteram et numerum constituitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D2","CH_MHON_T_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD3","text":"Systema unum continuum construit ex unitate, quinario, denario, quinquagenario et centenario.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D3","CH_MHON_T_13:D5","CH_MHON_T_13:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD4","text":"CRVX simul ut character simplex et ut vis multiplicativa operatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A13","CH_MHON_T_13:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD5","text":"Progressio non a signo extrinseco imponitur, sed ex compositione partium, quadratura et comparatione interna producitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D6","CH_MHON_T_13:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD6","text":"Cognitio numeralis hic pendet ex translatione inter tres ordines: geometriae, alphabeti et arithmeticae.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D2","CH_MHON_T_13:D4","CH_MHON_T_13:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX1","text":"Lectura pure Euclidea, quae CRVCEM a litteris et numeris separat, systema destruere debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX2","text":"Figurae sensus non potest esse invariabilis ab omni situ et conversione independens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX3","text":"Littera non potest esse signum linguisticum sine simul habita potentia numerali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX4","text":"Numerus non potest apparere tamquam quantitas a figura et partitione prorsus separata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX5","text":"Progressio non potest explicari per additionem simplicem, quia quadratura et multiplicatio eius structuram determinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX6","text":"Significatio numerorum non nititur demonstratione arithmetica sola, sed etiam analogia situs et auctoritate consuetudinis antiquae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX1","text":"Systema excludit possibilitatem termini neutralis inter figuram, litteram et numerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX2","text":"Excluditur conceptio CRVCIS quae eam in unam mensuram stabilem et non-generativam clauderet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX3","text":"Excluditur distinctio absoluta inter signum quod unum repraesentat et potentiam quae centum producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX4","text":"Excluditur progressio quae extra crucem initium et finem haberet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX5","text":"Excluditur lectio in qua figurae alphabeticae tantum memoriam conventionis, non ordinem cosmicum vel numericum, servent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS1","text":"Rectae aequales + decussatio communis + divisio per angulos oppositos → partes similes et aequales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS2","text":"Partes similes → figura litteralis → signum QVINARII.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS3","text":"Signum QVINARII duplicatum et inversum → multiplicatio quadrata → VIGINTI QVINQVE.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS4","text":"Eadem bipartitio in alio situ → figura litteralis geminata → signum QVINQVAGINTA.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS5","text":"QVINQVAGINTA → complexio denariae potestatis et quinariae virtutis → relatio ad CENTENARIVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS6","text":"Duae partes integrae → CENTENARIVM; mutua quadratura → BIS MILLE QVINGENTA; comparatio circularis → CENTENARIVM denuo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS7","text":"Character unus + potentia denaria → VNVМ → DECEM → CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF1","text":"CRVX ex aequalibus rectis → norma aequalis decussationis → divisio per commune punctum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF2","text":"Divisio crucis → partes similes → figura litteralis → QVINARIVM et VIGINTI QVINQVE.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF3","text":"Mutatus situs crucis → altera figura geminata → QVINQVAGINTA → denaria potestas quinaria inclusa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF4","text":"Numeratio duarum partium → CENTENARIVM → quadratura reciproca → BIS MILLE QVINGENTA → restitutio CENTENARII.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF5","text":"Potentia crucis explicata → transitus a VNVМ ad DECEM et CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME1","text":"Tabula conceptualis CRVCEM ex obiecto geometricum in operatorium transformationis numeralis reclassificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME2","text":"Litterae alphabeticae fiunt nodi in serie numerica, non signa linguistica isolata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter formam et numerum corruit, quia forma ipsa multiplicationem et progressionem continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME4","text":"Unitas, quinarium, denarium, quinquagenarium et centenarium in unam hierarchiam generativam componuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME5","text":"BIS MILLE QVINGENTA non finem progressionis constituunt, sed per comparationem ad numerum circularem in CENTENARIVM rediguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME6","text":"Alphabetum, geometria et arithmetica in eundem campum hieroglyphicum transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Obiectum immediatum est CRVX aequilatera eiusque partes per sectionem distributae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Mechanismus internus constat ex aequalitate, bipartitione, conversione situs, multiplicatione quadrata et comparatione numerorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Textus lectorem docet non tantum figuram aspicere, sed per eam numerare, multiplicare et progredi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Natura tamquam ordinem iustitiae continens praesupponitur, in quo una figura potest esse simul character, unitas et potentia numerorum superiorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem a figura crucis ad VNVМ, DECEM et CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT2","text":"Systema interne cohaeret ubi divisio, situs et quadratura ut operationes eiusdem signi agunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT3","text":"Firmissimum est argumentum in transitu a duabus partibus ad CENTENARIVM et in proportione denaria finali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT4","text":"Fragilior est transitus a formis geometricis ad significationes litterarum et a consuetudine antiqua ad necessitatem symbolicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT5","text":"Manet tensio inter assertionem partium aequalium et inaequalium et privilegium partium similium in demonstratione principali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT6","text":"Manet etiam tensio inter VNVМ ut characterem unicum et CENTVRIONEM ut eius potentiam expansam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT7","text":"Reductio BIS MILLE QVINGENTORVM ad CENTENARIVМ per comparationem ad numerum circularem formaliter minus explicata manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: geometria → littera → numerus → multiplicatio → progressio denaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222753630007Z_04012b32","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEORY XVI.","source_sha256":"e10a874fc81c4d57da48b227f28e0943aab945753b53ee7d97762e4bc19020a9","sha256":"535b1a985653bb77a800383606dd4d75f2a52d69eb3c54a7887d4fd46a92a29f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:27:53.632441+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS1","text":"The question is how CRVX, from equal straight lines, through division and position, displays a hidden numerical power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS2","text":"CRVX is considered not merely as a geometric figure, but as a hieroglyphic sign according to the norm of nature's justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS3","text":"The foundation of the argument is the passage from the parts of the cross to letters, from letters to numbers, and from numbers to multiplication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS4","text":"The first division refers the figure to QVINARIVM and VIGINTI QVINQVE; the second, the position of the figure to QVINQVAGINTA.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS5","text":"The power of the two parts advances to CENTENARIVM, through the law of squares to BIS MILLE QVINGENTA, and through the decimal proportion to VNVм, DECEM, CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AS6","text":"The kind of argumentation is metaphysical, arithmological, and reconstructive: figure, letter, and number are reduced to one generative machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A1","text":"CRVX is composed of two equal straight lines, but these lines do not necessarily cut one another into equal lengths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A2","text":"In the mystical distribution of the cross, equal and unequal parts are admitted together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A3","text":"Equality of magnitude in the two parts contains the hidden power of CRVCIS ÆQVILATERÆ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A4","text":"Nature requires the equal decussation of lines from equal straight lines as a norm of justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A5","text":"A straight line passing through the common point of intersection and opposite angles renders the parts of the cross similar and equal on either side.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A6","text":"The figures thus produced correspond with the fifth Latin vowel and with that used to signify QVINARIVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A7","text":"Doubling and reversal of the figure's position transform it into a numerical sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A8","text":"The first doubled figure represents QVINARIVM and through square multiplication produces VIGINTI QVINQVE.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A9","text":"A similar division in the position of the monadic cross produces another doubled letter, which is used to signify QVINQVAGINTA.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A10","text":"The other figure is essentially derived from the decimal power of the cross and from its quinary power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A11","text":"The two integral parts of the cross, according to their counted power, produce CENTENARIVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A12","text":"The law of squares permits mutual multiplication, which produces BIS MILLE QVINGENTA and, by comparison with the preceding circular number, restores CENTENARIVM anew.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:A13","text":"CRVX, although it is one character and represents VNVМ, may be recognized as CENTVRIO according to its decimal power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX1","text":"The equality of two straight lines does not define the equality of all the lengths produced by division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX2","text":"The distribution of the cross is restricted neither to parts all equal nor to parts all unequal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX3","text":"CRVX is not reduced to a bare geometric figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX4","text":"Numerical meaning is not constituted from one fixed position of the cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX5","text":"The unity of the character does not exclude its multiplication, expansion, or centenary power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:NX6","text":"Numerical progression is not a simple linear enumeration, but includes decimal proportion and square operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D1","text":"The equality of lines, equal decussation, and division through a common point cause geometric symmetry to receive symbolic power.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A3","CH_MHON_T_13:A4","CH_MHON_T_13:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D2","text":"The similar parts of the cross are converted into a literal figure, so that the figure is at once a geometric sign and a sign of QVINARIVM.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A5","CH_MHON_T_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D3","text":"Doubling and reversal of the first figure cause QVINARIVM to pass through square multiplication into VIGINTI QVINQVE.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A7","CH_MHON_T_13:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D4","text":"The other division, because it repeats the same mode of bipartition in another position, establishes another numerical letter and the signification of QVINQVAGINTA.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A7","CH_MHON_T_13:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D5","text":"The sign of QVINQVAGINTA comprises decimal power within quinary power, because it is essentially derived from the decimality of the cross and its quinarity.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A9","CH_MHON_T_13:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D6","text":"The enumeration of the two integral parts of the cross arrives at CENTENARIVM.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D7","text":"The mutual squaring of the parts produces BIS MILLE QVINGENTA, but the relation to the preceding circular number restores CENTENARIVM again.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:D8","text":"From the decimal power of the cross, the order VNVМ → DECEM → CENTVM is generated.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A12","CH_MHON_T_13:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD1","text":"The geometric figure is turned into a numerical operation: division, position, and reversal do not merely describe, but generate numbers.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D1","CH_MHON_T_13:D3","CH_MHON_T_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD2","text":"The identity of the sign is constituted not by form alone, but by the relation among figure, position, letter, and number.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D2","CH_MHON_T_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD3","text":"One continuous system is constructed from unity, the quinary, the decimal, the quinquagenary, and the centenary.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D3","CH_MHON_T_13:D5","CH_MHON_T_13:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD4","text":"CRVX operates simultaneously as a simple character and as a multiplicative power.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:A13","CH_MHON_T_13:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD5","text":"The progression is not imposed from an extrinsic sign, but is produced from the composition of parts, squaring, and internal comparison.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D6","CH_MHON_T_13:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SD6","text":"Numerical knowledge here depends on translation among three orders: geometry, alphabet, and arithmetic.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_13:D2","CH_MHON_T_13:D4","CH_MHON_T_13:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX1","text":"A purely Euclidean reading, which separates CRVX from letters and numbers, must destroy the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX2","text":"The sense of the figure cannot be invariable and independent of every position and reversal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX3","text":"A letter cannot be a linguistic sign without at the same time possessing numerical power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX4","text":"A number cannot appear as a quantity wholly separated from figure and partition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX5","text":"The progression cannot be explained by simple addition, because squaring and multiplication determine its structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:DNX6","text":"The meaning of numbers rests not on arithmetical demonstration alone, but also on analogy of position and the authority of ancient custom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility of a neutral term between figure, letter, and number.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX2","text":"Excluded is a conception of CRVX that would confine it to one stable and non-generative measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX3","text":"Excluded is an absolute distinction between the sign that represents one and the power that produces one hundred.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX4","text":"Excluded is a progression that would have its beginning and end outside the cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:SNX5","text":"Excluded is a reading in which alphabetic figures preserve only the memory of convention, not cosmic or numerical order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS1","text":"Equal straight lines + common decussation + division through opposite angles → similar and equal parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS2","text":"Similar parts → literal figure → sign of QVINARIVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS3","text":"The sign of QVINARIVM doubled and inverted → square multiplication → VIGINTI QVINQVE.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS4","text":"The same bipartition in another position → doubled literal figure → sign of QVINQVAGINTA.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS5","text":"QVINQVAGINTA → combination of decimal power and quinary power → relation to CENTENARIVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS6","text":"Two integral parts → CENTENARIVM; mutual squaring → BIS MILLE QVINGENTA; circular comparison → CENTENARIVM anew.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:FGS7","text":"One character + decimal power → VNVМ → DECEM → CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF1","text":"CRVX from equal straight lines → norm of equal decussation → division through a common point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF2","text":"Division of the cross → similar parts → literal figure → QVINARIVM and VIGINTI QVINQVE.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF3","text":"Changed position of the cross → another doubled figure → QVINQVAGINTA → decimal power included in quinary power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF4","text":"Enumeration of two parts → CENTENARIVM → reciprocal squaring → BIS MILLE QVINGENTA → restoration of CENTENARIVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:AF5","text":"The power of the cross unfolded → passage from VNVМ to DECEM and CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME1","text":"The conceptual map reclassifies CRVX from a geometric object into an operator of numerical transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME2","text":"Alphabetic letters become nodes in a numerical series, not isolated linguistic signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME3","text":"The opposition between form and number collapses, because form itself contains multiplication and progression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME4","text":"Unity, the quinary, the decimal, the quinquagenary, and the centenary are composed into one generative hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME5","text":"BIS MILLE QVINGENTA do not constitute the end of the progression, but are reduced to CENTENARIVM through comparison with the circular number.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ME6","text":"Alphabet, geometry, and arithmetic are transferred into the same hieroglyphic field.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The immediate object is the equilateral CRVX and its parts distributed by section.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The internal mechanism consists of equality, bipartition, reversal of position, square multiplication, and comparison of numbers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text teaches the reader not merely to look at the figure, but to count, multiply, and progress through it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Nature is presupposed as containing an order of justice, in which one figure can be simultaneously a character, a unity, and the power of higher numbers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the series from the figure of the cross to VNVМ, DECEM, and CENTVM.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT2","text":"The system coheres internally where division, position, and squaring act as operations of the same sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT3","text":"The argument is strongest in the passage from two parts to CENTENARIVM and in the final decimal proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT4","text":"More fragile is the passage from geometric forms to the significations of letters and from ancient custom to symbolic necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT5","text":"There remains a tension between the assertion of equal and unequal parts and the privileging of similar parts in the principal demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT6","text":"There also remains a tension between VNVМ as a unique character and CENTVRIONEM as its expanded power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT7","text":"The reduction of BIS MILLE QVINGENTORVM to CENTENARIVМ through comparison with the circular number remains formally less explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_13:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: geometry → letter → number → multiplication → decimal progression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_13@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_T_13:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 17","title":"Theor. XVI.","context":"Chapter 17","original_title":"Theor. Xvi.","original_context":"Chapter 17"},"original_title":"Theor. Xvi.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. XVII.","order":18,"parents":["RAW_MHON_T_14"],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_14@R001","sha256":"03fbd1edeae05fe05365cb47ea0bb2bbdc9ef9a9f0950d17a6779d6060c09426","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS1","text":"Ex Sexto Theoremate crux tamquam figura quattuor angulorum rectorum constituitur, quorum singulis significatio quinarialis attribui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS2","text":"Eadem structura numerorum quinquagenariorum, denariorum, alphabeticorum et unitariorum ad notas hieroglyphicas converti potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS3","text":"Per has conversiones crux simul numerum, litteram et notam cuiuslibet potestatis significare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS4","text":"Ex compositione harum significationum numerus 252 elicitur, quem crux mystis compendiose significare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS5","text":"Crux in duas litteras distributa et cum vi earum verbali collata efficit ut Lux et Verbum finale ac magistrale intelligantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A1","text":"Crux nostra quattuor angulos rectos continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A2","text":"Singulis angulis significatio quinarialis attribui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A3","text":"Situs angulorum significationem eorum determinare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A4","text":"Eadem theorematis ratio numeros quinquagenarios in notas hieroglyphicas converti sinit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A5","text":"Crux denarium vulgariter notare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A6","text":"Crux, secundum ordinem Latini alphabeti, litteram vicesimam primam significare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A7","text":"Una nota potestatem quamcumque et quantamcumque aliam habere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A8","text":"Quattuor quinque, quattuor quinquaginta, decem, viginti unum et unum in unum numerum componi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A9","text":"Numerus sic compositus est 252.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A10","text":"Crux in duas alias litteras distribui potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A11","text":"Vis numeralis litterarum et vis verbalis earundem separatim aestimari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A12","text":"Conspiratio et consensus ternarii in unitate Verbi ad significationem magistralem ducere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX1","text":"Crux ad unam tantum significationem numericam non restringitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX2","text":"Significatio crucis non ex una sola dispositione angulorum definitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX3","text":"Crux non est tantum figura geometrica, quia etiam numerum, litteram et notam significare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX4","text":"Nota non est ad unam potestatem aut ad unam quantitatem limitata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX5","text":"Numerus 252 non est unica via qua significatio crucis constituitur, quia duae aliae rationes praetermissae commemorantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX6","text":"Verbum finale non ad numeralem vim solam reducitur, sed ex vi numerali et verbali simul oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D1","text":"Quattuor anguli crucis, singulis quinariali significatione affectis, seriem compositionum numericorum producunt.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A1","CH_MHON_T_14:A2","CH_MHON_T_14:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D2","text":"Crux eadem operatione potest denarium, litteram vicesimam primam et potestatem generalem significare.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A4","CH_MHON_T_14:A5","CH_MHON_T_14:A6","CH_MHON_T_14:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D3","text":"Compositio quattuor quinariorum, quattuor quinquagenariorum, denarii, viginti unius et unitatis producit 252.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A8","CH_MHON_T_14:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D4","text":"Numerus 252 fit compendium in quo plures ordines significationis crucis simul servantur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D2","CH_MHON_T_14:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D5","text":"Divisio crucis in duas litteras transfert analysim a figura integra ad elementa verba constituentia.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D6","text":"Comparatio virium numeralis et verbalis litterarum producit significationem lucis.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D7","text":"Lux cum unitate Verbi et consensu ternarii coniuncta efficit Verbum finale ac magistrale.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A12","CH_MHON_T_14:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD1","text":"Crux fit machina translationis inter geometriam, arithmeticam, alphabetum, verbum et theologiam hieroglyphicam.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A1","CH_MHON_T_14:A4","CH_MHON_T_14:A6","CH_MHON_T_14:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD2","text":"Identitas signi non ab uno codice, sed ab superpositione plurium ordinum interpretativorum constituitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D2","CH_MHON_T_14:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD3","text":"Numerus 252 non claudit interpretationem, sed eam ad productiones ulteriores et ad lectionem magistralem aperit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D3","CH_MHON_T_14:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD4","text":"Unitas Verbi ex diversarum potentiarum coordinatione, non ex simplici identitate unius elementi, generatur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A11","CH_MHON_T_14:A12","CH_MHON_T_14:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD5","text":"Hieroglyphica cognitio transit a calculo signi ad productionem ontologico-verbalem lucis et Verbi.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D4","CH_MHON_T_14:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX1","text":"Figura geometrica isolata non sufficit ad sensum crucis explicandum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX2","text":"Signum non habet propriam vim univocam quae omnes eius significationes exhauriat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX3","text":"Numeralis reductio non potest viam verbalem et magistralem abolere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX4","text":"Littera separata a vi numerali suae significationis plenitudinem non retinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX5","text":"Interpretatio non potest sisti ad primam derivationem si eadem figura plures rationes productionis admittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX1","text":"Impossibilis habetur clausura signi intra unum genus, sive geometricum sive numericum sive alphabeticum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX2","text":"Praecluditur oppositio inter figuram materialem et Verbum, quia figura ipsa ad Verbum transfigurari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX3","text":"Abest idea significationis quae sine conversione, compositione et consensu obtineatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX4","text":"Inaccessibilis manet explicatio quae unitatem Verbi a pluralitate formarum separat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS1","text":"Figura crucis → quattuor anguli recti → distributio significationum quinarialium.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A1","CH_MHON_T_14:A2","CH_MHON_T_14:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS2","text":"Significationes angulorum → series numerorum et notarum → translatio hieroglyphica.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A4","CH_MHON_T_14:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS3","text":"Crux → denarius + littera vicesima prima + nota generalis → multiplicitas potentiarum significandi.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A5","CH_MHON_T_14:A6","CH_MHON_T_14:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS4","text":"Quattuor quinque + quattuor quinquaginta + decem + viginti unum + unum → 252 → compendium cabalisticum.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A8","CH_MHON_T_14:A9","CH_MHON_T_14:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS5","text":"Crux integra → divisio in duas litteras → collatio numeralis et verbalis.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A10","CH_MHON_T_14:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS6","text":"Collatio litterarum → Lux → Verbum finale et magistrale → unitas per ternarium, conspirationem et consensum.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A12","CH_MHON_T_14:D6","CH_MHON_T_14:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF1","text":"Theorema praecedens de angulis et significatione quinariali → crux ut quattuor-angulata constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF2","text":"Crux quattuor-angulata → numeri quinquagenarii et notae hieroglyphicae derivantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF3","text":"Nota hieroglyphica → denarius, littera vicesima prima et potestas generalis coalescunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF4","text":"Compositiones numerales → 252 ut compendium magistrale producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF5","text":"Compendium numericum → divisio in duas litteras → vis numeralis et verbalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF6","text":"Vis litterarum → Lux → Verbum finale et magistrale in unitate ternarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME1","text":"Crux ex figura contemplanda fit nexus inter quattuor ordines: spatium, numerum, alphabetum et verbum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME2","text":"Numerus et littera non amplius agunt ut systemata separata, sed ut conversiones eiusdem notae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME3","text":"Multiplicitas significationum non confunditur cum errore, sed ordinatur per compositionem hieroglyphicam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME4","text":"Numerus 252 transfert punctum gravitatis ab una voce ad structuram productionis quae plures vias admittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME5","text":"Divisio crucis in litteras reclassificat sensum ut processum a potentia numerali ad lucem verbalem procedentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME6","text":"Verbum finale apparet effectus coordinationis, non initium immediatum interpretationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT1","text":"Surface — Crux quattuor angulos rectos continet et varias notationes numerales atque alphabeticas recipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT2","text":"Structural — Figura per situm, numerum, litteram et divisionem in elementa significationes successive generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Interpretatio ab una lectione ad plures rationes productionis movetur, ita ut compendium numericum ad lectionem verbalem transitus fiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Verbum, Lux et Unitas non tamquam data immediata quam tamquam terminus compositionis, conspirationis et consensus producuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT1","text":"Axiomata de quattuor angulis, significatione quinariali et conversione hieroglyphica sufficiunt ad primam machinam derivationis restituendam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT2","text":"Axiomata de denario, littera vicesima prima et potestate generali sufficiunt ad multiplicem identitatem crucis explicandam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT3","text":"Axiomata compositionis numericae sufficiunt ad 252 producendum, sed duas alias rationes a textu promissas non determinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT4","text":"Transitus a divisione in duas litteras ad Lux et Verbum formaliter minus explicitus manet quam transitus numericus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT5","text":"Systema interne cohaeret quatenus omnes gradus ad conversionem unius signi referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT6","text":"Firmissimum est in compositione numerorum et in pluralitate notarum; fragilius est in identitate litterarum et in necessitate conclusionis verbalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT7","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum: figura → numerus → nota → littera → Lux → Verbum, quamquam clausura magistralis innititur praemissis non plene explicatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222815038134Z_e64e9b49","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM XVII.","source_sha256":"03fbd1edeae05fe05365cb47ea0bb2bbdc9ef9a9f0950d17a6779d6060c09426","sha256":"f80b05aff4603858cfa8404393630f480f1cb261bf652211a6c18f256dd61d50","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:28:15.040593+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS1","text":"From the Sixth Theorem, the cross is constituted as a figure of four right angles, to each of which a quinary signification can be attributed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS2","text":"The same structure of quinquagenary, denary, alphabetic, and unitary numbers can be converted into hieroglyphic signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS3","text":"Through these conversions, the cross can simultaneously signify number, letter, and a sign of any power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS4","text":"From the composition of these significations, the number 252 is elicited, which the cross can signify compendiously to the initiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AS5","text":"The cross, distributed into two letters and compared with their verbal force, brings it about that Light and the final and masterful Word are understood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A1","text":"Our cross contains four right angles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A2","text":"A quinary signification can be attributed to each angle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A3","text":"The position of the angles can determine their signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A4","text":"The same rationale of the theorem permits quinquagenary numbers to be converted into hieroglyphic signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A5","text":"The cross can commonly denote the denary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A6","text":"The cross, according to the order of the Latin alphabet, can signify the twenty-first letter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A7","text":"One sign can have any and however great power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A8","text":"Four fives, four fifties, ten, twenty-one, and one can be composed into one number.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A9","text":"The number thus composed is 252.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A10","text":"The cross can be distributed into two other letters.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A11","text":"The numerical force of letters and their verbal force can be assessed separately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:A12","text":"The conspiring and agreement of the ternary in the unity of the Word can lead to a masterful signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX1","text":"The cross is not restricted to only one numerical signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX2","text":"The signification of the cross is not defined by one disposition of the angles alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX3","text":"The cross is not merely a geometric figure, because it can also signify number, letter, and sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX4","text":"A sign is not limited to one power or to one quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX5","text":"The number 252 is not the sole way by which the signification of the cross is constituted, because two other omitted methods are mentioned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:NX6","text":"The final Word is not reduced to numerical force alone, but arises from numerical and verbal force together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D1","text":"The four angles of the cross, each endowed with quinary signification, produce a series of numerical compositions.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A1","CH_MHON_T_14:A2","CH_MHON_T_14:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D2","text":"By the same operation, the cross can signify the denary, the twenty-first letter, and general power.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A4","CH_MHON_T_14:A5","CH_MHON_T_14:A6","CH_MHON_T_14:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D3","text":"The composition of four fives, four fifties, the denary, twenty-one, and unity produces 252.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A8","CH_MHON_T_14:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D4","text":"The number 252 becomes a compendium in which several orders of the signification of the cross are simultaneously preserved.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D2","CH_MHON_T_14:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D5","text":"The division of the cross into two letters transfers the analysis from the whole figure to the elements constituting the word.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D6","text":"The comparison of the numerical and verbal forces of letters produces the signification of light.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:D7","text":"Light, joined with the unity of the Word and the agreement of the ternary, brings about the final and masterful Word.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A12","CH_MHON_T_14:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD1","text":"The cross becomes a machine of translation among geometry, arithmetic, alphabet, word, and hieroglyphic theology.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A1","CH_MHON_T_14:A4","CH_MHON_T_14:A6","CH_MHON_T_14:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD2","text":"The identity of the sign is constituted not by one code, but by the superposition of several interpretative orders.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D2","CH_MHON_T_14:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD3","text":"The number 252 does not close interpretation, but opens it to further productions and to masterful reading.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D3","CH_MHON_T_14:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD4","text":"The unity of the Word is generated from the coordination of diverse powers, not from the simple identity of one element.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A11","CH_MHON_T_14:A12","CH_MHON_T_14:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SD5","text":"Hieroglyphic cognition passes from the calculation of the sign to the ontological-verbal production of Light and Word.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:D4","CH_MHON_T_14:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX1","text":"An isolated geometric figure is not sufficient to explain the meaning of the cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX2","text":"The sign does not possess a proper univocal force that exhausts all its significations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX3","text":"Numerical reduction cannot abolish the verbal and masterful path.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX4","text":"A letter separated from its numerical force does not retain the fullness of its signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:DNX5","text":"Interpretation cannot stop at the first derivation if the same figure admits several modes of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX1","text":"The closure of the sign within one genus, whether geometric, numerical, or alphabetic, is held to be impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX2","text":"The opposition between material figure and Word is precluded, because the figure itself can be transfigured into the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX3","text":"There is absent an idea of signification obtained without conversion, composition, and agreement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:SNX4","text":"An explanation that separates the unity of the Word from the plurality of forms remains inaccessible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS1","text":"Figure of the cross → four right angles → distribution of quinary significations.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A1","CH_MHON_T_14:A2","CH_MHON_T_14:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS2","text":"Significations of the angles → series of numbers and signs → hieroglyphic translation.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A4","CH_MHON_T_14:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS3","text":"Cross → denary + twenty-first letter + general sign → multiplicity of powers of signifying.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A5","CH_MHON_T_14:A6","CH_MHON_T_14:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS4","text":"Four fives + four fifties + ten + twenty-one + one → 252 → cabalistic compendium.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A8","CH_MHON_T_14:A9","CH_MHON_T_14:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS5","text":"Whole cross → division into two letters → numerical and verbal comparison.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A10","CH_MHON_T_14:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:FGS6","text":"Comparison of letters → Light → final and masterful Word → unity through ternary, conspiring, and agreement.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_14:A12","CH_MHON_T_14:D6","CH_MHON_T_14:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF1","text":"The preceding theorem concerning angles and quinary signification → the cross is constituted as four-angled.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF2","text":"Four-angled cross → quinquagenary numbers and hieroglyphic signs are derived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF3","text":"Hieroglyphic sign → the denary, the twenty-first letter, and general power coalesce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF4","text":"Numerical compositions → 252 is produced as a masterful compendium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF5","text":"Numerical compendium → division into two letters → numerical and verbal force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:AF6","text":"Force of letters → Light → final and masterful Word in the unity of the ternary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME1","text":"From a figure to be contemplated, the cross becomes a nexus among four orders: space, number, alphabet, and word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME2","text":"Number and letter no longer act as separate systems, but as conversions of the same sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME3","text":"The multiplicity of significations is not confused with error, but is ordered through hieroglyphic composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME4","text":"The number 252 transfers the center of gravity from one utterance to a structure of production that admits several paths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME5","text":"The division of the cross into letters reclassifies meaning as a process proceeding from numerical power to verbal light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ME6","text":"The final Word appears as an effect of coordination, not as the immediate beginning of interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT1","text":"Surface — The cross contains four right angles and admits various numerical and alphabetic notations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT2","text":"Structural — Through position, number, letter, and division into elements, the figure successively generates significations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Interpretation moves from one reading to several modes of production, so that the numerical compendium becomes a transition to verbal reading.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Word, Light, and Unity are produced not as immediate givens so much as as the terminus of composition, conspiring, and agreement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning four angles, quinary signification, and hieroglyphic conversion suffice to reconstruct the first machine of derivation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning the denary, the twenty-first letter, and general power suffice to explain the multiple identity of the cross.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT3","text":"The axioms of numerical composition suffice to produce 252, but do not determine the two other methods promised by the text.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT4","text":"The transition from division into two letters to Light and Word remains formally less explicit than the numerical transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT5","text":"The system coheres internally insofar as all stages are referred to the conversion of one sign.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT6","text":"It is strongest in the composition of numbers and in the plurality of signs; it is more fragile in the identity of letters and in the necessity of the verbal conclusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_14:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: figure → number → sign → letter → Light → Word, although the masterful closure rests on premises not fully explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_14@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_MHON_T_14:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 18","title":"Theor. XVII.","context":"Chapter 18","original_title":"Theor. Xvii.","original_context":"Chapter 18"},"original_title":"Theor. Xvii.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15","layer":"CH","title":"Theor. XVIII.","order":19,"parents":["RAW_MHON_T_15"],"revision":"CH_MHON_T_15@R001","sha256":"6f09003c1d58c545f43cd2da4b5e18734752419ecebff171bed85aada12c8e10","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo caelestis astronomia structuram et anatomiam Monadis in natura manifestet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS2","text":"Quaestio a descriptione corporum caelestium ad interpretationem hieroglyphicam relationis inter caelum, naturam et artem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS3","text":"Ex Theorematibus XII et XIII caelestis astronomia inferioris quasi Parens et Magistra constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS4","text":"Contemplatio caelestium motuum et figurae ovalis praebet formam qua proportio naturalis et anatomia ovi legi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS5","text":"Haec structura ab ovo aquilino et conflictu Scarabei cum Aquila ad operationem artificialem et metamorphosin ovi derivatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS6","text":"Argumentatio est hieroglyphice analogica, reconstructiva et polemica: fabula naturae in schema physicum, alchymicum et medicinale convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A1","text":"Theoremata XII et XIII caelestem Astronomiam quasi Parentem et Magistram inferioris constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A2","text":"Oculi Cabalistici, praedictorum mysteriorum theorica illuminati, anatomiam Monadis in lumine Naturae et Vitae percipere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A3","text":"Contemplatio caelestium nunciorum et gestuum doctrinam de forma et ordine caelesti praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A4","text":"Cursus corporis caelestis figuram ovalem et circuitionem repraesentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A5","text":"Interpretationes hieroglyphicae consilium caeleste cum praedictis theorematibus consentaneum reddunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A6","text":"Natura proportiones ordinatas continet quae fere totum ordinem rei naturalis comprehendunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A7","text":"In ovo albumen aquae, vitellus olei et calx ovi correspondent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A8","text":"Aquila hominibus timidis et brutis violentiam infert, qua iniuria vindictam Scarabei motivat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A9","text":"Scarabeus per vim et subtilissimam artem ovum aquilinum in terram praecipitat atque disrumpit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A10","text":"Iupiter, malum tantum praecavens, impedit ne Scarabeus totam Aquilinam speciem e terris deleat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A11","text":"Textus Heliocantharos certis temporum curriculis latitantes ponit, quorum indicia contra inimicum adhiberi possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A12","text":"Quidam, quos auctor se nosse dicit, ovum aquilinum dissolutum calce et albumine temperant, deinde temperamento liquorem vitelli ordine artificioso superinducunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A13","text":"Volutatio et revolutio artificiosa, ad modum Scarabei pilas conglomerantis, metamorphosin ovi producunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A14","text":"In metamorphosi albumen evanescit et in ipso vitellinoso liquore absorbetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A15","text":"Tale artificium a gravissimis et antiquissimis philosophis celebratum atque certissimum et utilissimum traditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A16","text":"Anaxagoras ex hoc magisterio medicinam excellentissimam fecisse affirmatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A17","text":"Nihil horum extra virtutem hieroglyphicam Monadis ponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX1","text":"Anatomia Monadis non per simplicem visum, sed per oculos Cabalisticos et theorica mysteriorum illuminatos apprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX2","text":"Textus se non Aesopum, sed Oedipum agere declarat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX3","text":"Fabulari superficialiter de summis Naturae mysteriis non sufficit ad eorum intellectum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX4","text":"Confugium ad antrum Scarabei auxilium petentibus liberationem non praestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX5","text":"Vindicta Scarabei non ad solam vim brutam reducitur, sed subtili arte efficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX6","text":"Metamorphosis artificialis non per mixtionem indeterminatam, sed per temperationem et ordinem operationum procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX7","text":"Virtus hieroglyphica Monadis extra hunc ordinem caelestem, naturalem et artificialem non extenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D1","text":"Motus caelestis formam formalem praebet qua processus physicus describi potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A1","CH_MHON_T_15:A3","CH_MHON_T_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D2","text":"Circulatio ovalis a figura astronomica in principium coordinationis naturae et operationis artificialis convertitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A2","CH_MHON_T_15:A4","CH_MHON_T_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D3","text":"Ovum constituitur microstructura proportionata cuius partes materiales significationes hieroglyphicas suscipiunt.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A6","CH_MHON_T_15:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D4","text":"Certamen inter Scarabeum et Aquilam in processum materialem iniuriae, disruptionis et restitutionis transponitur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A8","CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:NX2","CH_MHON_T_15:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D5","text":"Tempus, latitatio et indicia animalium antagonisticorum in cognitionem strategicam convertuntur.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A10","CH_MHON_T_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D6","text":"Operatio artificialis motum Scarabei imitatur, ita ut volutatio ipsa fiat instrumentum metamorphoseos.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:A12","CH_MHON_T_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D7","text":"Disruptio ovi non in annihilatione terminatur, sed in transpositione albuminis ad liquorem vitellinum.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:A13","CH_MHON_T_15:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D8","text":"Praecedens philosophicum et medicinale operationem alchymicam intra ordinem scientiae legitimat, quamvis textus hanc auctoritate tradita affirmet.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A15","CH_MHON_T_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD1","text":"Signum hieroglyphicum fit mediatio unica inter ordinem caelestem, anatomiam naturalem et artem operativam.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:D1","CH_MHON_T_15:D2","CH_MHON_T_15:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD2","text":"Natura et ars non constituunt ordines oppositos, quia ars motus et proportionem naturae imitari potest.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A6","CH_MHON_T_15:A12","CH_MHON_T_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD3","text":"Fabula animalium, processus physicus et operatio alchymica sunt tres gradus eiusdem structurae hieroglyphicae.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:D4","CH_MHON_T_15:D6","CH_MHON_T_15:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD4","text":"Destructio in hoc systemate formam mutationis habet, quia dissolutio materiam in novum ordinem disponit.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:A13","CH_MHON_T_15:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD5","text":"Cognitio non consistit in observatione separata, sed in interpretatione signorum, motuum et temporum.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A2","CH_MHON_T_15:A3","CH_MHON_T_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD6","text":"Monas totalizat astronomiam, physicam, mythum, alchymiam et medicinam sub una virtute hieroglyphica.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A1","CH_MHON_T_15:A7","CH_MHON_T_15:A15","CH_MHON_T_15:A16","CH_MHON_T_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX1","text":"Systema excludit separationem absolutam inter caelum et naturam inferiorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit naturam quae formis, proportionibus et signis non iam ordinetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit mythum qui ad fabulam moralem vel ad narrationem sine physico mysterio reducatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit oppositionem simplicem inter artificium et Naturam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX5","text":"Systema excludit destructionem tamquam terminum ultimum, quia disruptio ad metamorphosin transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX6","text":"Systema excludit cognitionem quae a signis, motibus et temporalibus circulis seiungi possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX7","text":"Systema excludit materiam isolatam, cuius partes sine proportione et correspondence inter se intelligantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX1","text":"Textus praecludit possibilitatem ordinis naturalis qui extra analogiam caelestem et hieroglyphicam maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX2","text":"Textus circumit possibilitatem sermonis neutri qui naturam sine figura, signo aut interpretatione describat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX3","text":"Textus praecludit eventum naturalem omnino fortuitum et significatione carentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX4","text":"Textus praecludit abolitionem totalem ordinis aquilini, quia interventus Iovis extinctionem universalem impedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX5","text":"Textus praecludit aliquod magisterium alchymicum quod extra virtutem hieroglyphicam Monadis subsistat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS1","text":"Theoremata XII et XIII → Astronomia caelestis ut Parens et Magistra → oculi Cabalistici → anatomia Monadis in Natura et Vita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS2","text":"Contemplatio nunciorum et gestuum caelestium → cursus ovalis → figura circuitionis → concordantia interpretationum hieroglyphicarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS3","text":"Proportio a Natura → ovum ut microstructura → albumen/aqua, vitellus/oleum, calx → materia apta ad hieroglyphicam translationem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS4","text":"Iniuria Aquilae → vindicta Scarabei → praecipitatio ovi → disruptio → imminens deletio speciei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS5","text":"Interventus Iovis → conservatio limitata Aquilae → cura ovorum certis anni temporibus → indicia Heliocantharorum → possibilitas responsionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS6","text":"Ovum dissolutum + calx + albumen → temperatio → liquor vitelli → oblitio ordinata → volutatio et revolutio → metamorphosis ovi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS7","text":"Metamorphosis → transitus albuminis in liquorem vitellinum → signum hieroglyphicum Naturae → auctoritas philosophica et medicina → clausura in virtute Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AF1","text":"Theoremata XII–XIII → Astronomia ut Parens et Magistra → visus Cabalisticus → motus ovalis → concordantia hieroglyphica → proportio Naturae → anatomia ovi → antagonismus Aquilae et Scarabei → metamorphosis artificialis → inclusio in virtute Monadis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AF2","text":"Caelum ↔ figura → figura ↔ natura → natura ↔ fabula animalis → fabula ↔ operatio alchymica → operatio ↔ medicina philosophica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME1","text":"Argumentatio caelum, naturam et artem in unam tabulam continuorum ordinum reponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME2","text":"Ovum, motus ovalis, Scarabeus et Aquila non amplius ut res separatae, sed ut variantes eiusdem formae proportionatae classificari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME3","text":"Oppositio inter naturale et artificiale corruit, quia artificium motum naturalem repetendo metamorphosin producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter destructionem et generationem denuo classificatur: disruptio fit conditio mutationis materiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME5","text":"Tempus et signa animalium ex circumstantia narrativa in instrumenta cognitionis et responsionis convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME6","text":"Monas fit tabula totalizans in qua astronomia, physica, mythus, alchymia et medicina eadem structura hieroglyphica participant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME7","text":"Figurae adiunctae motum caelestem per formam ovalem et dispositiones circulares ostendunt, quamvis singulae correspondentiae signorum non plene glossentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** Textus ovum aquilinum, Scarabeum, Aquilam, Iovem et operationem temperationis proponit ut obiecta immediata significationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** Haec obiecta in ordinem proportionis, circuitionis, compositionis et dissolutionis materialis ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** Interpretatio hieroglyphica certamen inter adversarios et cognitionem alchymicam denuo constituit, ita ut indicia et motus ad responsionem adhiberi possint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Caelum, natura, ars et mythus unum continuum realitatis formant, cuius motus per circulos, tempora et metamorphoses ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad motum principalem a theorematibus caelestibus ad anatomiam ovi et metamorphosin artificialem restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia firmissima est ubi circulatio caelestis, volutatio Scarabei et revolutio artificialis eandem formam motus repetunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT3","text":"Transitus a Theorematibus XII et XIII ad compositionem ovi nititur potius concordantia hieroglyphica quam demonstratione formali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT4","text":"Correspondentiae inter albumen, vitellum, calcem, caelestes figuras et virtutem Monadis non omnibus gradibus explicite determinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT5","text":"Textus inter historiam animalium, fabulam hieroglyphicam et instructionem alchymicam transit, sed regulas translationis inter hos gradus non plene formalizat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT6","text":"Interventus Iovis limitat potentiam totalizantem Scarabei et in systemate tensionem inter vindictam, conservationem et deletionem relinquit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT7","text":"Auctoritas Anaxagorae et philosophorum antiquorum operationem confirmat testimonialiter, non per probationem internam eius efficaciae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT8","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus, sed exacta relatio inter signa figurarum adiunctarum et omnia elementa doctrinalia ex sola expositione non prorsus determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261006T222843638015Z_f413c01e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THEOREM XVIII.","source_sha256":"6f09003c1d58c545f43cd2da4b5e18734752419ecebff171bed85aada12c8e10","sha256":"3659fe2ea0239399ff5b944139db782bf1d5504d91631ca4e8854439004bcdb5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-06T22:28:43.639925+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS1","text":"The text asks how celestial astronomy manifests the structure and anatomy of the Monad in nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS2","text":"The question is transferred from the description of celestial bodies to the hieroglyphic interpretation of the relation among heaven, nature, and art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS3","text":"From Theorems XII and XIII, celestial astronomy is established as the Parent and Mistress, as it were, of the lower realm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS4","text":"Contemplation of celestial motions and of the oval figure provides the form by which natural proportion and the anatomy of the egg can be read.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS5","text":"This structure is derived from the eagle's egg and from the conflict of Scarabeus with Aquila to artificial operation and the metamorphosis of the egg.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AS6","text":"The argumentation is hieroglyphically analogical, reconstructive, and polemical: the fable of nature is converted into a physical, alchemical, and medical schema.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A1","text":"Theorems XII and XIII establish celestial Astronomy as the Parent and Mistress, as it were, of the lower realm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A2","text":"Cabalistic eyes, illuminated by the theory of the aforesaid mysteries, can perceive the anatomy of the Monad in the light of Nature and Life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A3","text":"Contemplation of celestial messengers and gestures provides doctrine concerning celestial form and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A4","text":"The course of a celestial body represents an oval figure and circulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A5","text":"Hieroglyphic interpretations render the celestial design consonant with the aforesaid theorems.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A6","text":"Nature contains ordered proportions which encompass almost the whole order of the natural thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A7","text":"In the egg, albumen, yolk, and eggshell correspond respectively to water, oil, and lime.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A8","text":"Aquila inflicts violence upon timid and brutish human beings, by which injury the vengeance of Scarabeus is motivated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A9","text":"By force and most subtle art, Scarabeus casts the eagle's egg to the ground and breaks it apart.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A10","text":"Iupiter, guarding against so great an evil, prevents Scarabeus from destroying the entire Aquiline species from the earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A11","text":"The text places Heliocanthari in hiding during certain courses of time, whose signs may be employed against the enemy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A12","text":"Certain persons, whom the author says he knows, temper a dissolved eagle's egg with lime and albumen, then by tempering lay the liquid of the yolk over it in an artificial order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A13","text":"Artificial rolling and revolving, after the manner of Scarabeus conglomerating balls, produce the metamorphosis of the egg.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A14","text":"In the metamorphosis, the albumen vanishes and is absorbed into the very yolk-liquid.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A15","text":"Such an artifice is celebrated by the most weighty and most ancient philosophers and is handed down as most certain and most useful.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A16","text":"Anaxagoras is affirmed to have made an exceptionally excellent medicine from this teaching.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:A17","text":"None of these things is placed outside the hieroglyphic virtue of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX1","text":"The anatomy of the Monad is apprehended not through simple sight, but through Cabalistic eyes illuminated by the theory of the mysteries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX2","text":"The text declares that it plays not Aesop, but Oedipus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX3","text":"To speak fabulously in a superficial manner about the highest mysteries of Nature does not suffice for their understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX4","text":"Flight to the cave of Scarabeus does not provide liberation to those seeking aid.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX5","text":"The vengeance of Scarabeus is not reduced to brute force alone, but is effected by subtle art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX6","text":"Artificial metamorphosis proceeds not through indeterminate mixture, but through tempering and the order of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:NX7","text":"The hieroglyphic virtue of the Monad does not extend outside this celestial, natural, and artificial order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D1","text":"Celestial motion provides a formal form by which a physical process can be described.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A1","CH_MHON_T_15:A3","CH_MHON_T_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D2","text":"Oval circulation is converted from an astronomical figure into a principle of coordinating nature and artificial operation.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A2","CH_MHON_T_15:A4","CH_MHON_T_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D3","text":"The egg consists as a proportioned microstructure whose material parts assume hieroglyphic significations.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A6","CH_MHON_T_15:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D4","text":"The contest between Scarabeus and Aquila is transposed into a material process of injury, disruption, and restoration.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A8","CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:NX2","CH_MHON_T_15:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D5","text":"Time, concealment, and the signs of antagonistic animals are converted into strategic knowledge.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A10","CH_MHON_T_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D6","text":"Artificial operation imitates the motion of Scarabeus, such that rolling itself becomes an instrument of metamorphosis.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:A12","CH_MHON_T_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D7","text":"The disruption of the egg ends not in annihilation, but in the transposition of albumen into yolk-liquid.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:A13","CH_MHON_T_15:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:D8","text":"Philosophical and medical precedent legitimates the alchemical operation within the order of knowledge, although the text affirms this by received authority.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A15","CH_MHON_T_15:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD1","text":"The hieroglyphic sign becomes the sole mediation between celestial order, natural anatomy, and operative art.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:D1","CH_MHON_T_15:D2","CH_MHON_T_15:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD2","text":"Nature and art do not constitute opposed orders, because art can imitate the motion and proportion of nature.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A6","CH_MHON_T_15:A12","CH_MHON_T_15:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD3","text":"The fable of animals, the physical process, and the alchemical operation are three levels of the same hieroglyphic structure.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:D4","CH_MHON_T_15:D6","CH_MHON_T_15:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD4","text":"Destruction in this system has the form of change, because dissolution disposes matter into a new order.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A9","CH_MHON_T_15:A13","CH_MHON_T_15:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD5","text":"Knowledge consists not in separate observation, but in the interpretation of signs, motions, and times.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A2","CH_MHON_T_15:A3","CH_MHON_T_15:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SD6","text":"The Monad totalizes astronomy, physics, myth, alchemy, and medicine under one hieroglyphic virtue.","refs":["CH_MHON_T_15:A1","CH_MHON_T_15:A7","CH_MHON_T_15:A15","CH_MHON_T_15:A16","CH_MHON_T_15:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an absolute separation between heaven and lower nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a nature no longer ordered by forms, proportions, and signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a myth reduced to a moral fable or to a narrative without physical mystery.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a simple opposition between artifice and Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX5","text":"The system excludes destruction as an ultimate end, because disruption passes into metamorphosis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX6","text":"The system excludes knowledge that could be separated from signs, motions, and temporal cycles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:DNX7","text":"The system excludes isolated matter, whose parts are understood without proportion and correspondence among themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX1","text":"The text forecloses the possibility of a natural order that remains outside celestial and hieroglyphic analogy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX2","text":"The text circumvents the possibility of a neutral discourse that describes nature without figure, sign, or interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX3","text":"The text forecloses a natural event wholly accidental and lacking signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX4","text":"The text forecloses the total abolition of the Aquiline order, because the intervention of Iupiter prevents universal extinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:SNX5","text":"The text forecloses any alchemical teaching that subsists outside the hieroglyphic virtue of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS1","text":"Theorems XII and XIII → celestial Astronomy as Parent and Mistress → Cabalistic eyes → anatomy of the Monad in Nature and Life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS2","text":"Contemplation of celestial messengers and gestures → oval course → figure of circulation → concordance of hieroglyphic interpretations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS3","text":"Proportion from Nature → egg as microstructure → albumen/water, yolk/oil, lime → matter suited to hieroglyphic translation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS4","text":"Injury by Aquila → vengeance of Scarabeus → casting down of the egg → disruption → impending destruction of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS5","text":"Intervention of Iupiter → limited preservation of Aquila → care for eggs at certain times of the year → signs of Heliocanthari → possibility of response.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS6","text":"Dissolved egg + lime + albumen → tempering → liquid of yolk → ordered coating → rolling and revolving → metamorphosis of the egg.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:FGS7","text":"Metamorphosis → passage of albumen into yolk-liquid → hieroglyphic sign of Nature → philosophical authority and medicine → closure in the virtue of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AF1","text":"Theorems XII–XIII → Astronomy as Parent and Mistress → Cabalistic vision → oval motion → hieroglyphic concordance → proportion of Nature → anatomy of the egg → antagonism of Aquila and Scarabeus → artificial metamorphosis → inclusion in the virtue of the Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:AF2","text":"Heaven ↔ figure → figure ↔ nature → nature ↔ animal fable → fable ↔ alchemical operation → operation ↔ philosophical medicine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME1","text":"The argumentation places heaven, nature, and art upon a single map of continuous orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME2","text":"The egg, oval motion, Scarabeus, and Aquila can no longer be classified as separate things, but as variants of the same proportioned form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME3","text":"The opposition between the natural and the artificial collapses, because artifice produces metamorphosis by repeating natural motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME4","text":"The opposition between destruction and generation is reclassified: disruption becomes the condition of the change of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME5","text":"Time and animal signs are converted from narrative circumstance into instruments of knowledge and response.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME6","text":"The Monad becomes a totalizing map in which astronomy, physics, myth, alchemy, and medicine participate in the same hieroglyphic structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ME7","text":"The accompanying figures display celestial motion through the oval form and circular dispositions, although the individual correspondences of the signs are not fully glossed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** The text presents the eagle's egg, Scarabeus, Aquila, Iupiter, and the operation of tempering as immediate objects of signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** These objects are ordered into an order of proportion, circulation, composition, and material dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** Hieroglyphic interpretation reconstitutes the contest between adversaries and alchemical knowledge, such that signs and motions can be employed for response.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Heaven, nature, art, and myth form one continuum of reality, whose motions are ordered through cycles, times, and metamorphoses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement from the celestial theorems to the anatomy of the egg and artificial metamorphosis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT2","text":"The strongest coherence is where celestial circulation, the rolling of Scarabeus, and artificial revolution repeat the same form of motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT3","text":"The transition from Theorems XII and XIII to the composition of the egg rests more upon hieroglyphic concordance than upon formal demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT4","text":"The correspondences among albumen, yolk, lime, celestial figures, and the virtue of the Monad are not explicitly determined at every level.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT5","text":"The text passes among animal history, hieroglyphic fable, and alchemical instruction, but does not fully formalize the rules of translation among these levels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_MHON_T_15:MRT6","text":"The intervention of Iupiter limits the totalizing power of Scarabeus and lea